Q[150900]={p="你又得到更多的奥术魔典了吗，<name>？",pEN="Have you obtained any more arcane tomes, <name>?",c="这本魔典中蕴含的力量极为庞大。不过，头脑清明之人能轻易将它凝练成一枚符文。",cEN="The power contained in this tome is tremendous. Yet it is easily condensed into a single rune by one with a clear mind."}
Q[150901]={p="你最近碰到过什么邪能武器装备吗？让圣光发挥作用吧，<name>。别让这些污秽之物留在世上。",pEN="Have you run into any fel armaments lately? Let the Light do its work, <name>. Do not allow these foul objects to remain in this world.",c="邪能材料已从此世清除。只剩下圣光的残余。",cEN="The fel materials are removed from this world. Only the Light's residue remains."}
Q[150902]={p="你又得到更多的奥术魔典了吗，<name>？",pEN="Have you obtained any more arcane tomes, <name>?",c="这本魔典中蕴含的力量极为庞大。不过，头脑清明之人能轻易将它凝练成一枚符文。",cEN="The power contained in this tome is tremendous. Yet it is easily condensed into a single rune by one with a clear mind."}
Q[150903]={p="你最近碰到过什么邪能武器装备吗？让圣光发挥作用吧，<name>。别让这些污秽之物留在世上。",pEN="Have you run into any fel armaments lately? Let the Light do its work, <name>. Do not allow these foul objects to remain in this world.",c="邪能材料已从此世清除。只剩下圣光的残余。",cEN="The fel materials are removed from this world. Only the Light's residue remains."}
Q[170000]={d="号召所有战士\n\n在艾尔文森林翠绿的山丘之间坐落着人类王国暴风城！突袭暴风城，杀死现任人类领袖伯瓦尔·弗塔根！",dEN="Calling all Warriors\n\nWithin the green hills of the Elwynn Forest lies the human nation of Stormwind! Raid Stormwind and slay the current leader of the humans Bolvar Fordragon!",o="在暴风城杀死伯瓦尔·弗塔根。",oEN="Slay Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind.",p="敌方领袖仍在顽抗。攻陷他们的要塞，将他们击溃。",pEN="The enemy leaders still stand defiant. Storm their stronghold and lay them low.",c="敌方首领已被击毙！这是对我们事业的决定性一击。街道被我们敌人的鲜血染红。胜利！",cEN="The enemy's leadership has been struck down! A decisive blow for our cause. The streets run red with the blood of our foes. Victory!"}
Q[170001]={d="在丹莫罗寒冷群山的深处住着矮人。他们地下的城市名为铁炉堡。围攻铁炉堡，杀死矮人领袖麦格尼·铜须！",dEN="Deep down in the frosty mountains of Dun Morogh is where the dwarves live. Their city below the surface is called Ironforge. Lay siege to Ironforge and slay the dwarven Leader Magni Bronzebeard!",o="在铁炉堡杀死麦格尼·铜须和大工匠梅卡托克。",oEN="Slay Magni Bronzebeard and High Tinker Mekkatorque in Ironforge.",p="敌方领袖仍在顽抗。攻陷他们的要塞，将他们击溃。",pEN="The enemy leaders still stand defiant. Storm their stronghold and lay them low.",c="敌方首领已被击毙！这是对我们事业的决定性一击。街道被我们敌人的鲜血染红。胜利！",cEN="The enemy's leadership has been struck down! A decisive blow for our cause. The streets run red with the blood of our foes. Victory!"}
Q[170002]={d="在卡利姆多西北部、迷雾之海之中矗立着世界之树泰达希尔。在它的树冠中隐藏着暗夜精灵的家园达纳苏斯。攀上泰达希尔，进入达纳苏斯，杀死暗夜精灵领袖泰兰德·语风！",dEN="In the north west of Kalimdor inside the Veiled Sea stands the world tree Teldrassil. Hidden within it's crown lies Darnassus the home of the night elves. Climb Teldrassil, enter Darnassus and slay the leader of the night elves Tyrande Whisperwind!",p="敌方领袖仍在顽抗。攻陷他们的要塞，将他们击溃。",pEN="The enemy leaders still stand defiant. Storm their stronghold and lay them low.",c="敌方首领已被击毙！这是对我们事业的决定性一击。街道被我们敌人的鲜血染红。胜利！",cEN="The enemy's leadership has been struck down! A decisive blow for our cause. The streets run red with the blood of our foes. Victory!"}
Q[170004]={d="在如今被称为杜隆塔尔的红色荒漠中，兽人建起了一座坚固的城市。围攻奥格瑞玛，击败兽人领袖萨尔。",dEN="In the red deserts now known as Durotar the orcs have built themselves a formidable city. Lay Siege to Orgrimmar and take down the orcish leader Thrall.",p="敌方领袖仍在顽抗。攻陷他们的要塞，将他们击溃。",pEN="The enemy leaders still stand defiant. Storm their stronghold and lay them low.",c="敌方首领已被击毙！这是对我们事业的决定性一击。街道被我们敌人的鲜血染红。胜利！",cEN="The enemy's leadership has been struck down! A decisive blow for our cause. The streets run red with the blood of our foes. Victory!"}
Q[170005]={d="在洛丹伦废墟的深处坐落着幽暗城。这里是摆脱了巫妖王影响的亡者的家园。攻击幽暗城，杀死亡者领袖希尔瓦娜斯·风行者！",dEN="Deep within the ruins of Loraderon lies the Undercity. Home to the undead that have freed themselves of the influence of the Lichking. Attack Undercity and kill the leader of the undead Sylvanas Windrunner!",o="杀死幽暗城的希尔瓦娜斯·风行者。",oEN="Slay Sylvanas Windrunner in Undercity.",p="敌方领袖仍在顽抗。攻陷他们的要塞，将他们击溃。",pEN="The enemy leaders still stand defiant. Storm their stronghold and lay them low.",c="敌方首领已被击毙！这是对我们事业的决定性一击。街道被我们敌人的鲜血染红。胜利！",cEN="The enemy's leadership has been struck down! A decisive blow for our cause. The streets run red with the blood of our foes. Victory!"}
Q[170006]={d="在莫高雷山谷最陡峭的石柱之上，牛头人建起了他们的家园。雷霆崖是一座独一无二的城市。烧毁它，并杀死牛头人领袖凯恩·血蹄。",dEN="On top of the steepest pillars in the valley of Mulgore is where the tauren have built their home. Thunder Bluff is a city like no other. Burn it down and slay the leader of the tauren Cairne Bloodhoof.",o="在雷霆崖杀死凯恩·血蹄。",oEN="Slay Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.",p="敌方领袖仍在顽抗。攻陷他们的要塞，将他们击溃。",pEN="The enemy leaders still stand defiant. Storm their stronghold and lay them low.",c="敌方首领已被击毙！这是对我们事业的决定性一击。街道被我们敌人的鲜血染红。胜利！",cEN="The enemy's leadership has been struck down! A decisive blow for our cause. The streets run red with the blood of our foes. Victory!"}
Q[170010]={d="艾泽拉斯的全体英雄注意：自我们记事起，其拉虫人便一直在侵扰艾泽拉斯。\n\n近来，他们开始利用希利苏斯阿努比萨斯的力量。阿努比萨斯是由活石驱动的巨像，拥有怪异的力量。其中一个名为塞提斯的阿努比萨斯化身，一直在祸害驻扎在希利苏斯的塞纳里奥议会的高贵成员。\n\n集结你的力量，摧毁塞提斯。",dEN="Attention all Heroes of Azeroth: the Qiraji have been infesting Azeroth for as long as we can remember.\n\nRecently, we they have begun utilizing the powers of the Anubisath in Silithus. The Abunisath are animated giants of living stone that possess strange powers. One particular incarnation of the Abunisath known as Setis has been causing havoc for the noble members of the Cenarion Circle located in Silithus,\n\nGather your forces to destroy Setis.",o="摧毁塞提斯！",oEN="Destroy Setis!",p="对艾泽拉斯的威胁依然存在。等你杀死那头危及我们所有人的野兽后再回来。",pEN="The threat to Azeroth persists. Return when you have slain the beast that endangers us all.",c="一个强大的敌人已被击败！知道有你这样的勇士随时待命，艾泽拉斯也能更安心地呼吸了。领取你应得的奖励吧。",cEN="A mighty foe has been vanquished! Azeroth breathes easier knowing champions like you stand ready. Claim your well-earned reward."}
Q[170011]={d="艾泽拉斯的全体英雄注意：有报告称，一个名为卡扎克的强大恶魔在荒芜之地现身。卡扎克又称基尔加丹的右手、末日守卫恶魔领主，在第三次大战期间曾被认为是阿克蒙德最信任的副官之一。他是燃烧军团中一位强大而可怕的恶魔。\n卡扎克手持阿克蒙德的传奇之刃，最后一次被人看见是在荒芜之地的腐痕谷。\n\n集结你的英雄同伴，从燃烧军团手中拯救艾泽拉斯世界。",dEN="Attention all Heroes of Azeroth: There have been reports of a formidable demon known as Kazzak spotted in the Blasted Lands. Also known as Kil'jaeden's Right Hand and Lord of the Doomguard demons, Kazzak was known as one of Archimonde's most trusted lieutenants during the Third War. He is a formidable and powerful demon of the Burning Legion\nKazzak, wielding the fabled blade of Archimonde, was last seen in the Blasted Lands at the Tainted Scar.\n\nRally together your fellow heroes to save the world of Azeroth from the Burning Legion.",o="击败卡扎克领主！",oEN="Defeat Lord Kazzak!",p="对艾泽拉斯的威胁依然存在。等你杀死那头危及我们所有人的野兽后再回来。",pEN="The threat to Azeroth persists. Return when you have slain the beast that endangers us all.",c="一个强大的敌人已被击败！知道有你这样的勇士随时待命，艾泽拉斯也能更安心地呼吸了。领取你应得的奖励吧。",cEN="A mighty foe has been vanquished! Azeroth breathes easier knowing champions like you stand ready. Claim your well-earned reward."}
Q[170012]={d="艾泽拉斯的全体英雄注意：\n\n在大分裂之前，暗夜精灵城市埃达拉斯曾繁荣于如今被称为艾萨拉的土地上。一条名为艾索雷葛斯的蓝龙一直在该地区漫无目的地游荡。有人认为，在那座昔日强大要塞的废墟中，或许能找到许多古老而强大的高等精灵神器。无数世代以来，蓝龙军团一直守护着强大的神器与魔法知识，确保它们不会落入凡人之手。蓝龙艾索雷葛斯的出现，似乎表明艾萨拉的荒野中可能存在极其重要的物品，也许就是传说中的永恒之瓶。无论艾索雷葛斯在寻找什么，有一点是确定的：艾索雷葛斯是艾泽拉斯的威胁，必须被消灭。",dEN="Attention all Heroes of Azeroth:\n\nBefore the Great Sundering, the night elf city of Eldarath flourished in the land that is now known as Azshara. A blueflight dragon known as Azuregos has been aimlessly wandering the region. Some believebelieved that many ancient and powerful Highborne artifacts may be found among the ruins of the once-mighty stronghold. For countless generations, the Blue Dragon Flight has safeguarded powerful artifacts and magical lore, ensuring that they do not fall into mortal hands. The presence of Azuregos, the blue dragon, seems to suggest that items of extreme significance, perhaps the fabled Vials of Eternity themselves, may be found in the wilderness of Azshara. Whatever Azuregos seeks, one thing is certain: Azuregos is a threat to Azeroth and must be slain.",o="杀死艾索雷葛斯！",oEN="Slay Azuregos!",p="对艾泽拉斯的威胁依然存在。等你杀死那头危及我们所有人的野兽后再回来。",pEN="The threat to Azeroth persists. Return when you have slain the beast that endangers us all.",c="一个强大的敌人已被击败！知道有你这样的勇士随时待命，艾泽拉斯也能更安心地呼吸了。领取你应得的奖励吧。",cEN="A mighty foe has been vanquished! Azeroth breathes easier knowing champions like you stand ready. Claim your well-earned reward."}
Q[171000]={d="所有联盟的战士，听令！\n\n部落与亡命徒正计划入侵我们的城市，我们需要一位像你这样的英雄相助，<name>。我认为我们应当重整防御，为即将到来的进攻做好准备！",dEN="Calling every warrior of the Alliance!\n\nThe Horde and Outlaws are planning an invasion into our city and we need the help of a hero like you, <name> I believe we should band up the defenses and prepare for an incoming attack!",o="保卫你的城市！",oEN="Defend Your City!",p="你的任务尚未完成。等你履行完契约再回到告示板。",pEN="Your task is not yet complete. Return to the board when you have fulfilled the contract."}
Q[171004]={d="所有部落的战士，听令！\n\n联盟与亡命徒正计划入侵我们的城市，我们需要一位像你这样的英雄相助，<name>。我认为我们应当重整防御，为即将到来的进攻做好准备！",dEN="Calling every warrior of the Horde!\n\nThe Alliance and Outlaws are planning an invasion into our city and we need the help of a hero like you, <name> I believe we should band up the defenses and prepare for an incoming attack!",o="保卫你的城市！",oEN="Defend Your City!",p="你的任务尚未完成。等你履行完契约再回到告示板。",pEN="Your task is not yet complete. Return to the board when you have fulfilled the contract."}
Q[172000]={d="审判官卡莱拉斯、塞鲁林将军与战争使者戈德拉克，是玛里苟斯最忠诚、最强大的副官之列，被派去守护汇聚于魔枢的魔网。他们确保蓝龙军团对世界魔法能量的统治，推进其主人的毁灭计划。\n\n英雄，艾泽拉斯的根本正岌岌可危。深入考达拉，击败审判官卡莱拉斯、塞鲁林将军与战争使者戈德拉克。击败这些守卫，你就能削弱玛里苟斯对魔网的控制，帮助维护维系我们世界的魔法平衡。",dEN="Inquisitor Caleras, General Cerulean, and Warbringer Goredrak are among Malygos's most loyal and formidable lieutenants, assigned to safeguard the ley lines converging at the Nexus. They ensure the blue dragonflight's dominance over the world's magical energies, furthering their master's destructive plan.\n\nHero, Azeroth's very essence is at stake. Journey into the depths of Coldarra and vanquish Inquisitor Caleras, General Cerulean, and Warbringer Goredrak. By defeating these guardians, you will weaken Malygos's control over the ley lines and aid in preserving the delicate balance of magic that sustains our world.",o="在考达拉击败审判官卡莱拉斯、塞鲁林将军与战争使者戈德拉克，以打断玛里苟斯对魔网的控制，守护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。",oEN="Defeat Inquisitor Caleras, General Cerulean, and Warbringer Goredrak in Coldarra to disrupt Malygos's control over the ley lines and safeguard the balance of magic in Azeroth.",c="英雄，你英勇的努力已对玛里苟斯控制魔网的企图造成重大打击，确保魔法平衡不受扰乱。为表彰你对艾泽拉斯的贡献，你的坚定付出将得到回报。",cEN="Hero, your valiant efforts have struck a significant blow against Malygos's control over the ley lines, ensuring the balance of magic remains undisturbed. In recognition of your service to Azeroth, you will be rewarded for your unwavering dedication."}
Q[172001]={d="近来，魔枢内的奥术能量开始溢出到周边地区，使现实的结构本身发生错位与扭曲。由此诞生了一种强大而不稳定的实体，被称为奥术巨蛇——一条灌注了原始奥术力量的魔法巨蛇。\n\n英雄，这些巨蛇失控的能量严重威胁着魔网的稳定与艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。前往考达拉，直面这种不稳定的生物。消灭奥术巨蛇，你就能帮助恢复魔网的完整，防止更大的灾难。",dEN="Recently, the arcane energy within the Nexus has begun to spill over into the surrounding area, causing the very fabric of reality to shift and warp. This has given birth to a powerful and unstable entity known as Arcane Serpents, a magical serpent infused with raw arcane power.\n\nHero, the unchecked energies of these Serpents pose a grave threat to the stability of the ley lines and the magical balance of Azeroth. Travel to Coldarra and confront this volatile creature. By vanquishing Arcane Serpents, you will help restore the integrity of the ley lines and prevent further catastrophe.",o="在考达拉杀死奥术巨蛇，阻止失控的奥术能量破坏魔网稳定、进一步损害艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。",oEN="Slay Arcane Serpents in Coldarra to prevent the unchecked arcane energies from destabilizing the ley lines and causing further harm to the magical balance of Azeroth.",c="英雄，你战胜奥术巨蛇，帮助恢复了魔网的均衡，避免了一场潜在的灾难。为感谢你守护艾泽拉斯魔法平衡的坚定奉献，你的英勇付出将得到回报。",cEN="Hero, your victory over the Arcane Serpents has helped restore the equilibrium of the ley lines and averted a potential disaster. In gratitude for your unwavering devotion to preserving the balance of magic in Azeroth, you will be rewarded for your courageous efforts."}
Q[172002]={d="为维持对魔网与魔枢的控制，玛里苟斯在整个考达拉布下了一支魔枢守护者军团。这些警觉的生物负责看守魔网，并消灭任何胆敢挑战蓝龙军团统治的入侵者。\n\n英雄，魔枢守护者是玛里苟斯控制艾泽拉斯奥术能量的重要一环。前往考达拉击败魔枢守护者，削弱玛里苟斯对魔网的掌控，帮助维护对我们世界至关重要的魔法平衡。",dEN="To maintain control over the ley lines and the Nexus, Malygos has stationed a legion of Nexus Watchers throughout Coldarra. These vigilant creatures are charged with the task of guarding the ley lines and eliminating any intruders who dare to challenge the blue dragonflight's dominance.\n\nHero, the Nexus Watchers are a vital component of Malygos's control over the arcane energies in Azeroth. Travel to Coldarra and defeat the Nexus Watchers to weaken Malygos's grip on the ley lines and aid in preserving the balance of magic that is vital to our world.",o="在考达拉杀死魔枢守护者，打断玛里苟斯对魔网的控制，保护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。",oEN="Slay Nexus Watchers in Coldarra to disrupt Malygos's control over the ley lines and protect the balance of magic in Azeroth.",c="英雄，你战胜魔枢守护者，已对玛里苟斯掌控魔网造成重大打击，确保魔法平衡安然无虞。为表彰你对艾泽拉斯的贡献，你的坚定付出与勇气将得到回报。",cEN="Hero, your triumph over the Nexus Watchers has dealt a significant blow to Malygos's hold over the ley lines, ensuring the balance of magic remains secure. In recognition of your service to Azeroth, you will be rewarded for your unwavering dedication and valor."}
Q[172003]={d="在考达拉的中心，织法者玛里苟斯仍在追寻夺取艾泽拉斯奥术能量的目标。他的钴蓝龙人军团是他的步兵，为他支配魔网效力。\n这些钴蓝龙人身上附魔的鳞片蕴含着强大的奥术能量，可用于抵销玛里苟斯对魔网的影响。若能善用这些能量，艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡或许得以保全。\n\n英雄，深入考达拉冰封的荒野，从钴蓝龙人身上取得钴蓝龙鳞。如此一来，你将帮助天平向我们倾斜，确保维系我们世界的魔法平衡。",dEN="In the heart of Coldarra, Malygos, the Spell-Weaver, continues his quest to seize control of Azeroth's arcane energies. His legion of Cobalt Wyrmkins serve as foot soldiers in his efforts to dominate the ley lines.\nThe enchanted scales of these Cobalt Wyrmkins contain powerful arcane energies that can be used to counteract Malygos's influence over the ley lines. If these energies can be harnessed, the balance of magic in Azeroth may be preserved.\n\nHero, venture into the frozen wilds of Coldarra and obtain Cobalt Dragon Scales from the Cobalt Wyrmkin. By doing so, you will help tip the scales in our favor and secure the magical balance that sustains our world.",o="在考达拉从钴蓝龙人身上收集钴蓝龙鳞，帮助抵销玛里苟斯对魔网的控制，保护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。",oEN="Collect Cobalt Dragon Scales from Cobalt Wyrmkin in Coldarra to help counteract Malygos's control over the ley lines and protect the balance of magic in Azeroth.",p="从考达拉阵亡的钴蓝鳞须者、钴蓝织法者和钴蓝剃刀者身上收集钴蓝龙鳞。这些附魔鳞片蕴含强大的奥术能量，可用于抵销玛里苟斯对魔网的影响。",pEN="Collect Cobalt Dragon Scales from the fallen Cobalt Scalebanes, Cobalt Mageweavers, and Cobalt Razors in Coldarra. These enchanted scales contain powerful arcane energies that can be used to counteract Malygos's influence over the ley lines.",c="英雄，你成功取得钴蓝龙鳞，为我们提供了抵销玛里苟斯对魔网影响的手段。艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡离安稳又近了一步。为感谢你的坚定奉献与付出，你的英勇努力将得到回报。",cEN="Hero, your success in obtaining the Cobalt Dragon Scales has provided us with the means to counteract Malygos's influence over the ley lines. The balance of magic in Azeroth is one step closer to being secure. In gratitude for your unwavering dedication and service, you will be rewarded for your valiant efforts."}
Q[172004]={d="考达拉的奥术能量蕴含着巨大的潜力，是造福还是为祸，取决于谁掌控它们。为保护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡，我们必须研究并理解织法者玛里苟斯试图操纵的力量。\n为了解更多关于考达拉魔法能量的信息，我们需要你收集散落在岛上的四件特定物品。寻找并收集一条魔枢龙、一份强效结晶法力、一块缚魔古树皮和一份地质报告。这些物品包含宝贵的信息与强大的能量，能帮助我们制定对抗玛里苟斯计划的策略。\n\n英雄，你的任务至关重要，因为艾泽拉斯魔法平衡的未来悬于一线。收集这些物品，帮助我们揭开魔网的奥秘以及考达拉境内奥术力量的真相。",dEN="The arcane energies of Coldarra hold great potential for both good and ill, depending on who controls them. To protect the balance of magic in Azeroth, it is crucial that we study and understand the forces that Malygos, the Spell-Weaver, seeks to manipulate.\nIn order to learn more about the magical energies of Coldarra, we need you to gather four specific items scattered across the island. Seek out and collect a Nexus Dragon, a Potent Crystalized Mana, a Magic-bound Ancient Bark, and a Geological Report. These items contain valuable information and potent energies that can help us devise a strategy to counteract Malygos's plans.\n\nHero, your mission is of great importance, as the future of Azeroth's magical balance hangs in the balance. Gather these items and help us unravel the mysteries of the ley lines and the arcane forces that lie within Coldarra.",o="在考达拉地区寻找并拾取魔枢龙、强效结晶法力、缚魔古树皮和地质报告，帮助我们更好地理解此地的奥术力量，保护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。",oEN="Find and loot the Nexus Dragon, Potent Crystalized Mana, Magic-bound Ancient Bark, and Geological Report in the Coldarra area to help us better understand the arcane forces at play and protect the balance of magic in Azeroth.",p="英雄，你成功取得这些关键物品，为我们提供了关于考达拉奥术力量的宝贵知识。有了这些情报，我们现在可以采取措施守护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。为表彰你的坚定奉献与付出，你的高尚努力将得到回报。",pEN="Hero, your success in obtaining these crucial items has provided us with invaluable knowledge about the arcane forces within Coldarra. Armed with this information, we can now take steps to safeguard the balance of magic in Azeroth. In recognition of your unwavering dedication and service, you will be rewarded for your noble efforts.",c="英雄，你成功取得这些关键物品，为我们提供了关于考达拉奥术力量的宝贵知识。有了这些情报，我们现在可以采取措施守护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。为表彰你的坚定奉献与付出，你的高尚努力将得到回报。",cEN="Hero, your success in obtaining these crucial items has provided us with invaluable knowledge about the arcane forces within Coldarra. Armed with this information, we can now take steps to safeguard the balance of magic in Azeroth. In recognition of your unwavering dedication and service, you will be rewarded for your noble efforts."}
Q[172005]={d="英雄，一些故障机器人已经失控，正在间歇泉平原制造混乱与破坏。这些机器人原本是为采矿作业设计的，但该地区的能量中断导致它们发生故障。我们需要你的帮助，消灭这些失控的机器人，确保当地社区和我们采矿作业的安全。你愿意响应号召、终结这些失控的机器人吗？",dEN="Hero, malfunctioning robots have gone rogue and are causing chaos and destruction in the Geyser Fields. These robots were originally designed for mining operations, but the energy disruption in the area has caused them to malfunction. We need your help to eliminate the rogue robots and ensure the safety of the local communities and our mining operations. Will you heed the call to arms and bring an end to the rogue robots?",o="故障机器人占据了间歇泉平原，正在造成破坏。我们必须派一位英雄去消除威胁，确保该地区的安全。",oEN="Malfunctioning robots have taken over the Geyser Fields and are causing destruction. We need to send a Hero to eliminate the threat and ensure the safety of the area.",c="干得好，英雄。你在间歇泉平原消灭失控机器人的努力，为该地区带回了和平与安定。当地社区和我们的采矿作业如今可以不必担心危险地运转了。谢谢你响应号召，拯救了这一天。",cEN="Well done, Hero. Your efforts in eliminating the rogue robots in the Geyser Fields have brought peace and stability back to the area. The local communities and our mining operations can now operate without fear of danger. Thank you for answering the call to arms and saving the day."}
Q[172006]={d="英雄，我们最近截获了关于菲兹克兰机械侏儒在北风苔原间歇泉平原进行实验的情报。我们的消息来源认为他们发现了一种新技术，若留在他们手中可能相当危险。我们必须确保这类知识不会落入错误之手，或被用来对付我们。",dEN="Hero, we have recently intercepted information about the Fizzcrank Mechagnomes conducting experiments in the Geyser Fields of the Borean Tundra. Our sources believe they have uncovered a new technology that could be potentially dangerous if left in their hands. We must ensure that such knowledge does not fall into the wrong hands or be used against us.",o="从间歇泉平原的菲兹克兰机械侏儒身上拾取奇怪的图纸。",oEN="Loot Strange Schematics from Fizzcrank Mechagnomes in the Geyser Fields.",p="干得漂亮，英雄！你成功从菲兹克兰机械侏儒手中取得了奇怪的图纸。有了它，我们现在可以分析并对抗他们的技术可能带来的任何潜在威胁。",pEN="Amazing work, Hero! You've managed to acquire the Strange Schematics from the Fizzcrank Mechagnomes. With this in our possession, we can now analyze and counteract any potential threats their technology may pose.",c="你干得非常出色，英雄。你取回的奇怪图纸对保护我们的人民免受菲兹克兰机械侏儒及其阴险阴谋的侵害，将是无价之宝。你不仅展现了极大的勇气与本领，还守护了我们的未来。我们永远感激你的付出，并会确保你的努力得到应有的回报。",cEN="You have done an outstanding job, Hero. The Strange Schematics you retrieved will be invaluable in protecting our people from the Fizzcrank Mechagnomes and their sinister machinations. You have not only displayed great courage and skill but also safeguarded our future. We are forever grateful for your service, and we will ensure that your efforts are aptly rewarded."}
Q[172007]={d="英雄，北风苔原的间歇泉平原最近显露出一种独特的资源，引起了我们技艺精湛的工程师们的兴趣。\n\n在这一地区发现的浸油盐晶拥有非凡的特性，可用于驱动和强化我们的科技装置与武器。\n\n它们可以在北风苔原间歇泉平原的哨兵机器人 57-K 处找到。",dEN="Hero, the Geyser Fields of the Borean Tundra have recently revealed a unique resource that has piqued the interest of our skilled engineers.\n\nOil-Infused Salt Crystals found in this area possess remarkable properties that can be harnessed to power and enhance our technological devices and weaponry.\n\nThey can be found at Sentry-bot 57-K at the Geyser Fields of the Borean Tundra.",o="从间歇泉平原的哨兵机器人 57-K 处收集 12 块浸油盐晶。",oEN="Collect 12 Oil-Infused Salt Crystals from Sentry-bot 57-K at the Geyser Fields.",p="干得漂亮，英雄！你成功收集了 10 块浸油盐晶。这些资源对于我们开发先进技术、加强防御的努力将是无价之宝。",pEN="Outstanding work, Hero! You have successfully collected 10 Oil-Infused Salt Crystals. These resources will be invaluable in our efforts to develop advanced technology and reinforce our defenses.",c="你的努力确实产生了影响，英雄。有了你收集的浸油盐晶，我们的工程师如今可以探索创新的方式，利用这些资源开发突破性技术，帮助我们对黑暗势力作战。你的奉献与勇敢不会被遗忘，你对大业的贡献将得到应有的回报。",cEN="Your efforts have truly made an impact, Hero. With the Oil-Infused Salt Crystals you've collected, our engineers can now explore innovative ways to utilize these resources in developing groundbreaking technology to aid us in our battle against the forces of darkness. Your dedication and bravery will not be forgotten, and you will be duly rewarded for your contribution to our cause."}
Q[172008]={d="英雄，我们在北风苔原的间歇泉平原面临日益增长的威胁。尼鲁布'ar 吐毒者、尼鲁布'ar 战士和尼鲁布'ar 掘地者已在该地区肆虐，对我们的人民构成重大危险，也扰乱了我们获取宝贵资源的行动。",dEN="Hero, we have a growing threat in the Geyser Fields of the Borean Tundra. The Nerub'ar Venomspitter, Nerub'ar Warrior, and Nerub'ar Tunneler have infested the area, posing a significant danger to our people and disrupting our efforts to secure valuable resources.",o="在间歇泉平原杀死尼鲁布'ar 吐毒者、尼鲁布'ar 战士和尼鲁布'ar 掘地者。",oEN="Kill Nerub'ar Venomspitter, Nerub'ar Warrior, and Nerub'ar Tunneler in the Geyser Fields.",c="你在战斗中展现了高超的本领，英雄。尼鲁布'ar 吐毒者、尼鲁布'ar 战士和尼鲁布'ar 掘地者都不是你力量的对手。这些生物被清除后，间歇泉平原对我们的人民来说又安全了。在保护我们土地的努力中，你的决心与勇气被证明是无价之宝。请放心，你的功绩不会被忽视，应得的奖励正等着你。",cEN="You have shown great prowess in battle, Hero. The Nerub'ar Venomspitter, Nerub'ar Warrior, and Nerub'ar Tunneler were no match for your might. With these creatures eradicated, the Geyser Fields are once again safe for our people. Your determination and courage have proven invaluable in our efforts to protect our lands. Rest assured that your deeds will not go unnoticed, and your just rewards await you."}
Q[172009]={d="英雄，我们收到令人警觉的报告，称北风苔原间歇泉平原的尼鲁布'ar 数量大幅增加。我们的斥候已确认该地区散布着尼鲁布'ar 卵囊，若不加以控制，它们的数量将激增到无法收拾的地步。",dEN="Hero, we have received alarming reports about a significant increase in the number of Nerub'ar in the Geyser Fields of the Borean Tundra. Our scouts have identified Nerub'ar Egg Sacs scattered across the area, which, if left unchecked, will lead to an uncontrollable surge in their population.",o="摧毁间歇泉平原的尼鲁布'ar 卵囊。",oEN="Destroy Nerub'ar Egg Sacs in the Geyser Fields.",c="你的果断行动带来了改变，英雄。摧毁尼鲁布'ar 卵囊，你阻止了一场可能淹没间歇泉平原、让我们的人民陷入严重危险的虫害。你的机敏与坚定再次被证明对保护我们的土地无比珍贵。请放心，你的勇敢与付出将得到应有的认可，奖励正等着你。",cEN="Your decisive action has made a difference, Hero. By destroying the Nerub'ar Egg Sacs, you have prevented a potential infestation that could have overwhelmed the Geyser Fields and put our people in grave danger. Your quick thinking and unwavering determination have once again proven invaluable in protecting our lands. Rest assured that your bravery and efforts will be duly recognized, and your rewards await you."}
Q[172010]={d="英雄，我们的研究员一直在研究天灾对北风苔原 \"垂死兽穴\" 附近野生动物造成的毁灭性影响。我们相信，通过检验天灾猛犸象的肉和染疫猛犸人的血液样本，我们能查明关于天灾感染与腐化方法的关键情报。这些知识在我们对抗亡灵、治愈这片土地的努力中将是无价之宝。\n\n我们需要你深入垂死兽穴附近的危险地带，从天灾猛犸象身上收集天灾之肉，从染疫猛犸人身上收集天灾血液样本。你的勇敢与奉献，将是我们持续研究与对抗天灾的关键。",dEN="Hero, our researchers have been studying the Scourge's devastating impact on the wildlife near \"The Dens of Dying\" in the Borean Tundra. We believe that by examining Scourged Mammoth meat and Plagued Magnataur blood samples, we can uncover crucial information about the Scourge's methods of infection and corruption. This knowledge will be invaluable in our fight against the undead and our efforts to heal the land.\n\nWe need you to venture into the dangerous territory near The Dens of Dying and collect Scourge Meat from the Scourged Mammoths and Scourge Blood Samples from the Plagued Magnataurs. Your bravery and dedication will be instrumental in our continued research and battle against the Scourge.",o="在垂死兽穴附近，从天灾猛犸象身上收集天灾之肉，从染疫猛犸人身上收集天灾血液样本。",oEN="Collect Scourge Meat from Scourged Mammoths and Scourge Blood Samples from Plagued Magnataurs near The Dens of Dying.",p="干得漂亮，英雄！你成功收集了天灾猛犸象的天灾之肉和染疫猛犸人的天灾血液样本。这些样本将帮助我们加深对天灾及其阴险腐化手段的理解。",pEN="Incredible work, Hero! You have successfully gathered the Scourge Meat from the Scourged Mammoths and the Scourge Blood Samples from the Plagued Magnataurs. These samples will help us further our understanding of the Scourge and their insidious methods of corruption.",c="多亏你勇敢的努力，英雄，我们的研究员如今可以深入研究天灾对当地野生动物的影响。在我们持续对抗亡灵、努力恢复北风苔原平衡的过程中，你的贡献至关重要。你再次证明了自己的勇气与对大业的忠诚，应得的奖励正等着你。",cEN="Thanks to your courageous efforts, Hero, our researchers can now delve deeper into the study of the Scourge's effects on the local wildlife. Your contribution is vital in our ongoing battle against the undead and in our efforts to restore balance to the Borean Tundra. You have once again proven your valor and commitment to our cause, and your well-earned rewards await you."}
Q[172011]={d="英雄，北风苔原的塔拉玛斯地区已成为天灾的据点。白骨战士、塔拉玛斯憎恶和溃烂食尸鬼如今在该地区肆虐，威胁着把它们邪恶的影响进一步扩散到整个区域。\n\n你的任务是深入塔拉玛斯的敌方领地，消灭这些怪物，阻止天灾的扩张。我们绝不能让天灾继续对我们土地发动无情的进攻。坚守阵地，英雄，把这些可憎的生物从塔拉玛斯彻底清除。",dEN="Hero, the area of Talramas in the Borean Tundra has become a stronghold for the Scourge. Bone Warriors, Talramas Abominations, and Festering Ghouls now infest the area, threatening to spread their vile influence further into the region.\n\nYour task is to venture into the enemy territory of Talramas and eliminate these monstrosities to halt the Scourge's expansion. We must not allow the Scourge to continue their unrelenting assault on our lands. Stand strong, Hero, and eradicate these abhorrent creatures from Talramas.",o="在塔拉玛斯杀死白骨战士、塔拉玛斯憎恶和溃烂食尸鬼。",oEN="Kill Bone Warriors, Talramas Abominations, and Festering Ghouls in Talramas.",c="你为我们的大业立下了大功，英雄。击败白骨战士、塔拉玛斯憎恶和溃烂食尸鬼，你遏制了天灾向北风苔原推进的浪潮。你在战斗中的本领与勇敢，对削弱天灾在塔拉玛斯的立足点起了关键作用。因此，我们现在可以集中精力巩固防御，为与天灾的持续斗争做准备。请放心，你的付出会得到回报，你的名字将被铭记在最伟大的英雄之列。",cEN="You have done a great service to our cause, Hero. By vanquishing the Bone Warriors, Talramas Abominations, and Festering Ghouls, you have stemmed the tide of the Scourge's advance into the Borean Tundra. Your skill and bravery in battle have been instrumental in weakening the Scourge's foothold in Talramas. As a result, we can now focus our efforts on fortifying our defenses and preparing for the ongoing struggle against the Scourge. Rest assured that your efforts will be rewarded, and your name will be remembered among the greatest heroes."}
Q[172012]={d="英雄，我们得到消息，北风苔原的塔拉玛斯与恩基拉赫神殿城中藏有四本强大的亡灵法术魔典。这些书记载着关于天灾如何复活死者、控制其亡灵大军的关键情报。\n\n你的任务是潜入这些敌方要塞，找到这四本书：\"复活死者：死灵法师指挥亡者大军指南\"、\"尸体制作的艺术：将死者转化为强大仆从\"、\"死灵法师的学徒：亡者召唤世界之旅\"，以及\"死灵之书：禁忌法术与咒语合集\"，并把它们带回来给我们。这些知识在我们对抗天灾的斗争中将是无价之宝，也许能为我们提供削弱其力量的关键。",dEN="Hero, we have received word of four powerful necromantic tomes hidden within Talramas and the Temple City of En'kilah in the Borean Tundra. These books contain vital information about the Scourge's methods for raising the dead and controlling their undead armies.\n\nYour mission is to infiltrate these enemy strongholds, locate the four books - \"Raising the Dead: A Necromancer's Guide to Commanding an Undead Army,\" \"The Art of Corpse Crafting: Transforming the Dead into Powerful Servants,\" \"The Necromancer's Apprentice: A Journey into the World of Undead Summoning,\" and \"The Necrotic Tome: A Collection of Forbidden Spells and Incantations\" - and return them to us. This knowledge will be invaluable in our fight against the Scourge and could provide us with the key to weakening their forces.",o="从塔拉玛斯和恩基拉赫神殿城收集四本死灵法术魔典。",oEN="Collect the four necromantic tomes from Talramas and the Temple City of En'kilah.",p="英雄，你成功取得四本亡灵法术魔典：\"复活死者：死灵法师指挥亡者大军指南\"、\"尸体制作的艺术：将死者转化为强大仆从\"、\"死灵法师的学徒：亡者召唤世界之旅\"，以及\"死灵之书：禁忌法术与咒语合集\"。你勇敢的行动为我们在对抗天灾的斗争中提供了至关重要的情报。",pEN="Hero, you have successfully acquired the four necromantic tomes: \"Raising the Dead: A Necromancer's Guide to Commanding an Undead Army,\" \"The Art of Corpse Crafting: Transforming the Dead into Powerful Servants,\" \"The Necromancer's Apprentice: A Journey into the World of Undead Summoning,\" and \"The Necrotic Tome: A Collection of Forbidden Spells and Incantations.\" Your brave actions have granted us vital information in our struggle against the Scourge.",c="有了这些禁忌魔典在手，我们现在可以研究天灾的黑暗法术，并制定削弱其力量的对策。英雄，你的勇气与机智在这一努力中发挥了关键作用。多亏你坚定不移的付出，我们离胜利又近了一步。你赢得了属于你的奖励，你的名字将被铭记在那些英勇对抗天灾的英雄之列。",cEN="With these forbidden tomes in our possession, we can now study the Scourge's dark arts and develop countermeasures to weaken their forces. Your courage and resourcefulness have played a vital role in this endeavor, Hero. We are one step closer to victory, thanks to your unwavering commitment. You have earned your rewards, and your name will be remembered among the heroes who have fought valiantly against the Scourge."}
Q[172013]={d="英雄，北风苔原的恩基拉赫神殿城是天灾的据点，充斥着强大的亡灵生物。天灾一直把恩基拉赫当作行动基地，向附近定居点发动袭击，危及许多无辜者的生命。\n\n我们需要一位像你这样勇敢的英雄深入恩基拉赫的中心，消灭潜伏在其墙内的最危险敌人。你的目标是恩基拉赫憎恶、恩基拉赫地穴恶魔、恩基拉赫石像鬼和恩基拉赫食尸鬼。\n\n削减他们的数量，我们就能削弱天灾对该地区的控制，为我们的部队争取宝贵时间来准备一次更具决定性的进攻。",dEN="Hero, the Temple City of En'kilah in the Borean Tundra is a stronghold of the Scourge, teeming with powerful undead creatures. The Scourge has been using En'kilah as a staging ground to launch attacks against nearby settlements, putting the lives of many innocent people at risk.\n\nWe need a courageous hero like yourself to venture into the heart of En'kilah and eliminate some of the most dangerous foes lurking within its walls. Your targets are En'kilah Abominations, En'kilah Crypt Fiends, En'kilah Gargoyles, and En'kilah Ghouls.\n\nBy thinning their ranks, we can weaken the Scourge's grip on the area and buy precious time for our forces to prepare for a more decisive assault.",o="在恩基拉赫神殿城杀死恩基拉赫憎恶、恩基拉赫地穴恶魔、恩基拉赫石像鬼和恩基拉赫食尸鬼。",oEN="Slay En'kilah Abominations, En'kilah Crypt Fiends, En'kilah Gargoyles, and En'kilah Ghouls in the Temple City of En'kilah.",c="英雄，你的勇气与本领对恩基拉赫神殿城中的天灾部队造成了重大打击。消灭这些危险的敌人，你削弱了天灾对该地区的控制，也为那些对抗巫妖王爪牙的人带回了希望。你赢得了属于你的奖励，你的行动不会被遗忘。",cEN="Your valor and skill have dealt a significant blow to the Scourge's forces within the Temple City of En'kilah, Hero. By eliminating these dangerous foes, you have weakened the Scourge's hold on the area and provided hope to those who are fighting against the Lich King's minions. You have earned your reward, and your actions will not be forgotten."}
Q[172014]={d="英雄，我们的情报报告显示，塔拉玛斯与恩基拉赫神殿城的教派瘟疫使者与恩基拉赫死灵法师正准备举行黑暗仪式，向北风苔原释放更强大的亡灵生物。\n\n这些邪恶的施法者是瘟疫计划中增强其军队的关键一环。\n\n我们需要一位像你这样的英雄去打断他们的仪式，阻止他们邪恶的计划得逞。你的任务是消灭塔拉玛斯与恩基拉赫神殿城的教派瘟疫使者与恩基拉赫死灵法师。如此一来，你将削弱天灾对该地区的掌控，给我们的部队一战之力。",dEN="Hero, our intelligence reports indicate that the Cult Plaguebringers and En'kilah Necromancers in Talramas and the Temple City of En'kilah are preparing dark rituals to unleash more potent undead creatures upon the Borean Tundra. These vile spellcasters are key components of the Scourge's plans to bolster their forces.\n\nWe need a hero like you to disrupt their rituals and prevent their nefarious plans from coming to fruition. Your mission is to eliminate Cult Plaguebringers and En'kilah Necromancers in Talramas and the Temple City of En'kilah. By doing so, you will weaken the Scourge's grasp on the region and give our forces a fighting chance.",o="在塔拉玛斯与恩基拉赫神殿城杀死教派瘟疫使者与恩基拉赫死灵法师。",oEN="Slay Cult Plaguebringers and En'kilah Necromancers in Talramas and the Temple City of En'kilah.",c="英雄，你的英勇行动对瘟疫的计划造成了重大打击。消灭教派瘟疫使者与恩基拉赫死灵法师，你打乱了他们的黑暗仪式，阻止了更强大亡灵生物的召唤。你的功绩无疑拯救了无数生命，也为对抗天灾的人们带回了希望。你的奖励当之无愧，你的勇气将被铭记。",cEN="Your heroic actions have dealt a significant blow to the Scourge's plans, Hero. By eliminating the Cult Plaguebringers and En'kilah Necromancers, you have disrupted their dark rituals and prevented the summoning of more powerful undead creatures. Your deeds have undoubtedly saved countless lives and provided hope to those battling the Scourge. Your reward is well-deserved, and your courage will be remembered."}
Q[172015]={d="英雄，我们收到报告称，埃尔德拉纳斯废墟、沸腾之池与焦痕高地一带的元素生物出现了异动。看来不同元素力量之间的平衡已被打破，它们失控的狂怒正在该地区肆虐。\n\n狂怒风暴、沸腾之灵和狂暴沸煮者变得格外具有攻击性，对我们的部队和周边环境构成重大威胁。我们需要你的帮助来恢复元素之间的平衡。\n\n前往埃尔德拉纳斯废墟、沸腾之池与焦痕高地，消灭狂怒风暴、沸腾之灵和狂暴沸煮者。你的行动将有助于让该地区重归和谐，防止更大的破坏。",dEN="Hero, we've received reports of a disturbance among the elementals in the Ruins of Eldra'nath, Boiling Pool, and Charred Rise. It seems that the balance between the different elemental forces has been disrupted, and their unchecked fury is wreaking havoc on the region.\n\nThe Enraged Tempests, Boiling Spirits, and Raging Boilers have become particularly aggressive, posing a significant threat to our forces and the surrounding environment. We need your help to restore the balance between the elements.\n\nVenture to the Ruins of Eldra'nath, Boiling Pool, and Charred Rise, and eliminate the Enraged Tempests, Boiling Spirits, and Raging Boilers. Your actions will help bring harmony back to the region and prevent further destruction.",o="在埃尔德拉纳斯废墟、沸腾之池与焦痕高地杀死狂怒风暴、沸腾之灵和狂暴沸煮者，恢复元素的平衡。",oEN="Slay Enraged Tempests, Boiling Spirits, and Raging Boilers in the Ruins of Eldra'nath, Boiling Pool, and Charred Rise to restore balance to the elements.",c="英雄，你的努力对恢复埃尔德拉纳斯废墟、沸腾之池与焦痕高地的元素平衡产生了重大影响。消灭狂怒风暴、沸腾之灵和狂暴沸煮者，你帮助平息了它们的破坏力量，防止了该地区遭受更多损害。你为维护世界和谐所作出的奉献令人钦佩，你的奖励当之无愧。",cEN="Hero, your efforts have made a significant impact on restoring balance to the elements in the Ruins of Eldra'nath, Boiling Pool, and Charred Rise. By eliminating the Enraged Tempests, Boiling Spirits, and Raging Boilers, you have helped to calm their destructive forces and prevented further harm to the region. Your dedication to preserving the harmony of the world is admirable, and your reward is well-earned."}
Q[172016]={d="埃尔德拉纳斯废墟、沸腾之池与焦痕高地的元素力量已变得危险地不稳定。为恢复平衡，我们必须从该地区最强大的元素生物——狂怒风暴、沸腾之灵和狂暴沸煮者——身上收集强效的元素精华。收集狂怒元素之空气、沸腾元素之水和狂暴元素之火，你将帮助确保这一地区的安全，防止混乱进一步蔓延。你的努力对维持元素力量之间的和谐至关重要。",dEN="The elemental forces in the Ruins of Eldra'nath, Boiling Pool, and Charred Rise have become dangerously unstable. In order to restore balance, we must gather potent elemental essences from the most powerful elementals in the area: Enraged Tempests, Boiling Spirits, and Raging Boilers. By collecting Enraged Elemental Air, Boiling Elemental Water, and Raging Elemental Fire, you will help ensure the safety of this region and prevent further chaos from spreading. Your efforts are crucial in maintaining harmony amongst the elemental forces.",o="从埃尔德拉纳斯废墟、沸腾之池与焦痕高地的元素生物身上收集狂怒元素之空气、沸腾元素之水和狂暴元素之火。",oEN="Collect Enraged Elemental Air, Boiling Elemental Water, and Raging Elemental Fire from the elementals in the Ruins of Eldra'nath, Boiling Pool, and Charred Rise.",p="干得好，英雄！你成功从狂怒风暴身上收集了狂怒元素之空气，从沸腾之灵身上收集了沸腾元素之水，从狂暴沸煮者身上收集了狂暴元素之火。这些强效的元素精华将极大帮助我们恢复该地区自然力量的平衡。你英勇的努力在我们对抗狂暴元素的持续斗争中产生了重大影响。",pEN="Well done, Hero! You've managed to collect the Enraged Elemental Air from the Enraged Tempest, Boiling Elemental Water from the Boiling Spirit, and Raging Elemental Fire from the Raging Boiler. These potent elemental essences will greatly assist us in restoring balance to the forces of nature in the region. Your valiant efforts have made a significant impact on our ongoing struggle against the volatile elements.",c="干得好，英雄！有了这些元素，我们就能恢复该地区的平衡，确保北风苔原的安全。你今天的努力对保护这片土地的自然和谐产生了重大影响。感谢你坚定不移的奉献。",cEN="Well done, Hero! With these elements in hand, we can restore balance to the area and ensure the safety of the Borean Tundra. Your efforts today have made a significant impact on preserving the natural harmony of the land. Thank you for your unwavering dedication."}
Q[172017]={d="熔岩巨蛾碾压者一直在熔岩巨蛾地区肆虐，破坏该地区的平衡，威胁当地居民。我们必须终结它们破坏性的行径，以恢复秩序、确保该地区的安全。你的任务是直面并击败熔岩巨蛾碾压者，削弱它们的影响，制止它们的暴行。",dEN="The Magmoth Crushers have been causing havoc in Magmoth, disrupting the balance of the area and posing a threat to its inhabitants. We must put an end to their destructive ways to restore order and ensure the safety of the region. Your task is to confront and defeat the Magmoth Crushers, weakening their influence and halting their rampage.",o="在熔岩巨蛾地区击败熔岩巨蛾碾压者。",oEN="Defeat Magmoth Crushers in the Magmoth area.",c="消灭熔岩巨蛾碾压者，你已对它们的破坏力量造成重大打击，帮助恢复了熔岩巨蛾地区的秩序。你的行动为该地区带回了和平与安定，我们感激你英勇的努力。",cEN="By eliminating the Magmoth Crushers, you have dealt a significant blow to their destructive force, helping to restore order in Magmoth. Your actions have brought peace and stability back to the area, and we are grateful for your valiant efforts."}
Q[172018]={d="熔岩巨蛾萨满和熔岩巨蛾觅食者一直在用熄灭的蜡烛举行黑暗仪式，威胁着熔岩巨蛾地区的权力平衡。夺回这些熄灭的蜡烛，我们就能打断他们的仪式，削弱他们对该地区的影响。任务就落在你身上：从熔岩巨蛾萨满和熔岩巨蛾觅食者手中收集那些熄灭的蜡烛。",dEN="The Magmoth Shaman and Magmoth Foragers have been using extinguished candles in their dark rituals, threatening the balance of power in Magmoth. By reclaiming these extinguished candles, we can disrupt their ceremonies and weaken their influence on the area. The task falls upon you to collect the extinguished candles from the clutches of the Magmoth Shaman and Magmoth Foragers.",o="在熔岩巨蛾地区从熔岩巨蛾萨满和熔岩巨蛾觅食者身上收集 5 支熄灭的蜡烛。",oEN="Collect 5 Extinguished Candles from Magmoth Shaman and Magmoth Foragers in Magmoth.",p="从熔岩巨蛾萨满和熔岩巨蛾觅食者那里取回 5 支熄灭的蜡烛。",pEN="Recover 5 Extinguished Candles from the Magmoth Shaman and Magmoth Foragers.",c="收集熄灭的蜡烛，你打乱了熔岩巨蛾萨满和熔岩巨蛾觅食者的黑暗仪式。它们对该地区的影响已被削弱，熔岩巨蛾地区的权力平衡得以恢复。你的努力为该地区带来了安定，我们感激你勇敢的行动。",cEN="By collecting the extinguished candles, you have disrupted the dark rituals of the Magmoth Shaman and Magmoth Foragers. Their influence on the area is weakened, and the balance of power in Magmoth has been restored. Your efforts have brought stability to the region, and we are grateful for your courageous actions."}
Q[172019]={d="在北风苔原北部地区的战斗与冲突中，重要的补给品遗失并散落在各处。这些补给对我们维持该地区立足点至关重要。赶在它们落入敌手或被自然环境毁坏之前找回这些丢失的补给，极为重要。勇敢的冒险者，去寻找这些失落的补给，把它们带回来给我们。",dEN="In the chaos of battles and skirmishes throughout the northern area of Borean Tundra, vital supplies have been lost and scattered across the landscape. These supplies are crucial for our efforts to maintain a foothold in the region. It is of utmost importance that we recover these lost supplies before they fall into enemy hands or are lost to the elements. Brave adventurer, seek out the lost supplies and return them to us.",o="在北风苔原北部地区收集 10 份失落的补给。",oEN="Collect 10 Lost Supplies in the northern area of Borean Tundra.",p="找回散落在北风苔原北部地区的 10 份失落的补给。",pEN="Recover 10 Lost Supplies scattered throughout the northern area of Borean Tundra.",c="找回失落的补给，你为我们北风苔原的行动作出了重大贡献。你的机智与奉献并未被忽视。多亏你的行动，我们现在可以巩固阵地，更好地支援这片严酷地区的部队。",cEN="With the recovery of the lost supplies, you have made a significant contribution to our efforts in the Borean Tundra. Your resourcefulness and dedication have not gone unnoticed. Thanks to your actions, we can now reinforce our position and better support our troops in this harsh region."}
Q[172020]={d="在神秘的洪泛平原，被称为蒸汽蛙的两栖生物受到了该地区奇异能量的影响。它们独特的生理结构使其吸收了潜在的力量，体内灌注了异常强效的精华。这种精华在制作强效药水和药剂时可能价值非凡。在洪泛平原从蒸汽蛙身上收集 5 只蒸制蛙，让它们的精华能为我们的大业所用。",dEN="In the mysterious Flood Plains, the amphibious creatures known as Steam Frogs have been affected by the strange energies in the area. Their unique biology has caused them to absorb the latent power, imbuing their bodies with an unusually potent essence. This essence could prove invaluable in crafting powerful potions and elixirs. Collect 5 Steamed Frogs from the Steam Frogs in the Flood Plains so that their essence can be harnessed for our cause.",o="在洪泛平原从蒸汽蛙身上收集 5 只蒸制蛙。",oEN="Collect 5 Steamed Frogs from Steam Frogs in the Flood Plains.",p="你收集了 5 只蒸制蛙。它们的精华脉动着能量，暗示着它们在强效药剂中的潜力。",pEN="You have collected 5 Steamed Frogs. Their essence pulses with energy, hinting at their potential in powerful concoctions.",c="多亏你的努力，我们现在有了一份宝贵的资源来强化药水和药剂。你收集的蒸制蛙体内的精华，在未来的战斗中无疑将价值非凡。你为我们的大业立下了大功。",cEN="Thanks to your efforts, we now have a valuable resource to enhance our potions and elixirs. The essence within the Steamed Frogs you've collected will no doubt prove invaluable in the battles to come. You have done a great service for our cause."}
Q[172022]={d="居住在洪泛平原的 Gorloc 部族对附近定居点变得越来越敌视和具有攻击性。Gorloc 蹒跚者、Gorloc 呓语者和 Gorloc 喷汽者不断的侵袭与领地侵占，让当地人的生活苦不堪言。我们需要一位有能力的英雄介入，终结这一威胁。杀死这些 Gorloc，为洪泛平原带回和平。",dEN="The Gorloc tribes inhabiting the Flood Plains have grown increasingly hostile and aggressive towards nearby settlements. The constant raids and territorial encroachments by the Gorloc Waddlers, Gorloc Gibberers, and Gorloc Steam Belchers have made life unbearable for the locals. We need a capable Hero to step in and put an end to this threat. Slay the Gorlocs to bring peace to the Flood Plains.",o="在洪泛平原击败 Gorloc 蹒跚者、Gorloc 呓语者和 Gorloc 喷汽者。",oEN="Defeat Gorloc Waddlers, Gorloc Gibberers, and Gorloc Steam Belchers in the Flood Plains.",c="多亏你们英勇的努力，洪泛平原的 Gorloc 威胁已被压制。附近定居点的居民如今可以安居乐业，不必再惧怕 Gorloc 的怒火。你们的行动为该地区带来了亟需的安定，你们的名字将被那些被你们拯救的人铭记。",cEN="Thanks to your valiant efforts, the Gorloc threat in the Flood Plains has been subdued. The inhabitants of the nearby settlements can now live in peace, knowing that they no longer need to fear the wrath of the Gorlocs. Your actions have brought much-needed stability to the region, and your name will be remembered by those whose lives you've saved."}
Q[172023]={d="卡斯卡拉的海象人一直处在科瓦迪尔劫掠者的持续威胁之下，后者在该地区四处劫掠、制造恐慌。这些来自深渊的邪恶生物给该地区带来了恐惧与混乱，是时候终结它们的暴行了。击败 15 名科瓦迪尔劫掠者，保护卡斯卡拉，为海象人带回希望。",dEN="The Tuskarr of Kaskala have been under constant threat from the Kvaldir Raiders, who have been pillaging and terrorizing the area. These vile beings from the depths have brought fear and chaos to the region, and it's time we put an end to their rampage. Defeat 15 Kvaldir Raiders to protect Kaskala and bring hope back to the Tuskarr.",o="在卡斯卡拉击败 15 名科瓦迪尔劫掠者。",oEN="Defeat 15 Kvaldir Raiders in Kaskala.",c="消灭科瓦迪尔劫掠者，你不仅为卡斯卡拉带回了和平，也证明了自己是真正的勇士。多亏你们的勇敢与决心，这里的海象人如今可以不再恐惧地生活。你们的行动对把这里称作家园的人们产生了重大影响。",cEN="By eliminating the Kvaldir Raiders, you have not only brought peace to Kaskala but also proven yourself as a true champion. The Tuskarr here can now live without fear, thanks to your bravery and determination. Your actions have made a significant impact on the lives of those who call this place home."}
Q[172503]={d="去当个大英雄，杀掉大怪物，拿到战利品",dEN="Go be big hero kill big monster get loot",o="杀死 LR 生物",oEN="Kill LR Creatures",p="《巫妖王之怒》日常占位文本",pEN="Wrath Daily Placeholder Text",c="《巫妖王之怒》日常占位文本",cEN="WotlK Daily Placeholder Text"}
Q[172504]={d="考达拉的奥术能量蕴含着巨大的潜力，是造福还是为祸，取决于谁掌控它们。为保护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡，我们必须研究并理解织法者玛里苟斯试图操纵的力量。\n为了解更多关于考达拉魔法能量的信息，我们需要你收集散落在岛上的四件特定物品。寻找并收集一条魔枢龙、一份强效结晶法力、一块缚魔古树皮和一份地质报告。这些物品包含宝贵的信息与强大的能量，能帮助我们制定对抗玛里苟斯计划的策略。\n\n英雄，你的任务至关重要，因为艾泽拉斯魔法平衡的未来悬于一线。收集这些物品，帮助我们揭开魔网的奥秘以及考达拉境内奥术力量的真相。",dEN="The arcane energies of Coldarra hold great potential for both good and ill, depending on who controls them. To protect the balance of magic in Azeroth, it is crucial that we study and understand the forces that Malygos, the Spell-Weaver, seeks to manipulate.\nIn order to learn more about the magical energies of Coldarra, we need you to gather four specific items scattered across the island. Seek out and collect a Nexus Dragon, a Potent Crystalized Mana, a Magic-bound Ancient Bark, and a Geological Report. These items contain valuable information and potent energies that can help us devise a strategy to counteract Malygos's plans.\n\nHero, your mission is of great importance, as the future of Azeroth's magical balance hangs in the balance. Gather these items and help us unravel the mysteries of the ley lines and the arcane forces that lie within Coldarra.",o="在考达拉地区寻找并拾取魔枢龙、强效结晶法力、缚魔古树皮和地质报告，帮助我们更好地理解此地的奥术力量，保护艾泽拉斯的魔法平衡。",oEN="Find and loot the Nexus Dragon, Potent Crystalized Mana, Magic-bound Ancient Bark, and Geological Report in the Coldarra area to help us better understand the arcane forces at play and protect the balance of magic in Azeroth.",p="《巫妖王之怒》日常占位文本",pEN="Wrath Daily Placeholder Text",c="《巫妖王之怒》日常占位文本",cEN="WotlK Daily Placeholder Text"}
Q[175000]={d="你是要前往苍白之境吗？\n\n我的主人塞文·达伦加尔大人吩咐我在这些土地上招募一切能招募的帮手。从你的样子看，你会是个极好的补充。\n\n你看，我主人的家乡斯卡德尔德省正面临最黑暗的时刻：霜鬃巨魔从山间涌下，强盗在光天化日之下劫掠旅人……当然，还有野蛮的艾尔迪尔。他们是最糟的一群。\n\n到暴风要塞的贵族区、回廊庭院下方的贵族议院向达伦加尔大人报到。\n\n告诉他是我派你来的。\n\n凡你能提供的帮助，他都会给予丰厚的回报。",dEN="Are you bound for the Pale Reach?\n\nMy lord, Lord Servin Darengar, charged me with recruiting all the help I could find in these lands. And judging by your appearance, you could make a splendid addition.\n\nYou see, my lord's homeland, the province of Scadeald, is facing its darkest hour: Frostmane trolls descending from the mountains, bandits waylaying travelers in broad daylight... and the savage Ealdir, of course. The worst of the bunch.\n\nReport to Lord Darengar in the House of Nobles, within Stormwind Keep, beneath the cloister courtyard. Tell him I sent you.\n\nHe will amply reward any aid you can provide.",o="在暴风要塞庭院找到楼梯，前往请愿厅与塞文·达伦加尔大人交谈。",oEN="Find the stairs in the Stormwind Keep courtyard and speak with Lord Servin Darengar in the Petitioner's Chamber.",c="\n你说是我手下某位骑士派你来的？\n\n很好。在这类事情上，我更信任他们的判断，而非我自己的。我接受你的效劳，作为……侍从？还是雇佣兵？\n\n<塞文·达伦加尔挥了挥手，仿佛不愿计较头衔的问题。>\n\n请原谅，我很难理清思绪。我在这里被关了好几个钟头，试图说服贵族议院派兵前往斯卡德尔德……收效甚微。",cEN="Sent by one of my knights, you say?\n\nVery well. In these matters, I trust their judgment more than my own. I accept your services as... a squire? A mercenary?\n\n<Servin Darengar waves a hand, as if dismissing the matter of titles.>\n\nForgive me, I find it difficult to think clearly. I've been shut in here for hours, trying to convince the House of Nobles to send the army to Scadeald... with little success."}
Q[175001]={d="<钟声在贵族议院中回荡。塞文·达伦加尔叹了口气，在不舒服的座位上挺直了背。>\n\n看来我们的喘息结束了。\n\n请先站到一旁，等我们这些贵族把挚爱省份的命运辩论完。\n\n观察，聆听，然后评判。之后你就会明白我的绝望。",dEN="<The tolling of bells echoes through the House of Nobles. Lord Servin Darengar responds with a sigh, straightening his back in his uncomfortable seat.>\n\nIt seems our respite is at an end.\n\nStand aside for a moment, while we nobles finish debating the fate of my beloved province.\n\nObserve, listen, and judge. Then you shall understand my despair.",o="出席贵族的集会。",oEN="Attend the gathering of the nobles.",p="跟这些人打交道既乏味又累人……",pEN="Dealing with these people is tedious and wearying...",c="<你能从老人湿润的眼中清楚地看到挫败。>\n\n要想说服这群懦夫哪怕一次主动出手，恐怕得靠奇迹。你也亲耳听到了：只要塞雷妮娅·冷湖女士——她那姓氏的最后一人——拒绝正式求援（而她永远不会这么做），贵族议院就不会介入。\n\n我族人的血会染在他们的手上，而不是我的手上。我不会袖手旁观，看着斯卡德尔德枯萎凋零。",cEN="<You can see defeat written clearly in the old man's watery eyes.>\n\nIt would have taken a miracle to convince this lot of cowards to take the initiative for once. You heard it yourself: as long as Lady Serenya Coldmere, last of her name, refuses to formally request aid, which she never will, the House of Nobles will not intervene.\n\nThe blood of my people will stain their hands, but not mine. I will not sit idly by while Scadeald withers away."}
Q[175002]={d="如果暴风城那些金贵的法律让贵族议院束手无策，那就随它去吧。他们并非我唯一的出路；据我所知，没有什么禁止我以私人身份招募雇佣兵和冒险者。\n\n那我就这么做。就当你是 \"受雇\" 了。\n\n拿着我的印章。我的儿子阿拉松留在斯卡德尔德，试图缓解该省的疾苦。去向他报到，向他提供你的效劳。我会尽快设法派出更多人手；眼下，只能靠你了。",dEN="If Stormwind's precious laws condemn the House of Nobles to inaction, then so be it. They were not my only recourse; as far as I am aware, nothing forbids me from recruiting the aid of mercenaries and adventurers in a private capacity.\n\nAnd so, I shall. Consider yourself 'hired.'\n\nTake my seal. My son, Arathon, remained in Scadeald to try and alleviate the province's woes. Present yourself to him. Offer him your services. I will endeavor to send more men as soon as possible; for now, you will have to suffice.",o="到斯卡德尔德达伦加尔庄园向阿拉松·达伦加尔报到。",oEN="Report to Arathon Darengar at the Darengar Estate in Scadeald.",p="欢迎来到达伦加尔家族的庄园。",pEN="Welcome to the Darengar Family Estate.",c="<女仆攥紧围裙，指节发白。>\n\n你是为我主阿拉松来的？\n\n那你来晚了。灰天镇那帮蛮子，是塞雷妮娅女士那只喜鹊派来的，几小时前就把他抓走了。他们连让他穿靴子的功夫都不肯给。\n\n现在他们正把宅子翻个底朝天！你信吗？他们指控达伦加尔家族犯下叛国重罪！",cEN="<The handmaid clenches her fists against her apron, her knuckles white.>\n\nAre you here for my lord Arathon?\n\nYou are too late, then. Those brutes from Graysky, sent by that magpie Lady Serenya, arrested him hours ago. They wouldn't even let him put on his boots.\n\nAnd now they are turning the manor upside down! Can you believe it? They have accused the Darengar family of high treason!"}
Q[175003]={d="<卡德米拉擦了擦眼泪，眼中燃起一股突如其来的决心。>\n\n你带着塞文大人的印章。这说明你得到了他的信任。所以，仔细听好：\n\n我需要你在灰天镇那些打手找到之前，把阿拉松的日记带给我。要是那些纸页落到塞雷妮娅女士手里，天亮之前她就能拿到他的死刑令。\n\n快去！我会设法在门口拖住那位队长。",dEN="<Cadmilla dabs at her eyes. A sudden determination burns within them.>\n\nYou carry Lord Servin's seal. That means you have his trust. So, listen closely:\n\nI need you to bring me Arathon's journal before those Graysky thugs find it. If those pages fall into Lady Serenya's hands, she will have his death warrant signed before dawn.\n\nGo! I shall try to distract the captain at the entrance.",o="在达伦加尔庄园内找到阿拉松的日记。",oEN="Find Arathon's Journal inside the Darengar Estate.",p="阿拉松的房间在楼上。",pEN="Arathon's room is upstairs.",c="这是……\n\n<翻看日记的纸页时，卡德米拉的表情从悲伤转为困惑。>\n\n我完全看不懂这些。\n\n<卡德米拉摇了摇头。>\n\n这是阿拉松大人的笔迹，毫无疑问。哦，天哪！他怎么能……？",cEN="This is...\n\n<As she flips through the pages of the journal, Cadmilla's expression shifts from sorrow to confusion.>\n\nI don't understand any of this.\n\n<Cadmilla shakes her head.>\n\nIt is Lord Arathon's handwriting, there is no doubt of that. Oh, oh dear! How could he...?"}
Q[175004]={d="<卡德米拉啪地合上日记。>\n\n这么说，是真的了。我主阿拉松一直在与艾尔迪尔勾结。\n\n你听说过他们吗？他们自称是这片土地原住民的子孙。是一群渴望独立的异教徒与叛教者。简而言之，就是野蛮人。\n\n我哥哥多年前就死于艾尔迪尔的伏击。\n\n日记里提到庄园下方有个洞穴，还提到那口井。我猜我们能在下面找到答案。你介意去查一查吗？",dEN="<Cadmilla snaps the journal shut.>\n\nIt is true, then. My lord Arathon was conspiring with the Ealdir.\n\nHave you heard of them? They claim to be descendants of this land's original inhabitants. Pagans and heretics who crave independence. Savages, in short.\n\nMy brother died years ago in an Ealdir ambush.\n\nThe journal mentions a cave beneath the manor and something about the well. I suspect we might find answers down there. Would you mind looking into it?",o="下到达伦加尔庄园的井中，调查里面隐藏着什么。",oEN="Descend into the well at the Darengar Estate and investigate what lies hidden within.",p="<破碎的箱子，上面印着联盟的徽记。>",pEN="<Shattered crates with the Alliance seal.>",c="<带有联盟徽记的裂开的箱子。看来它们是被人从井口匆忙扔下的。坠落摔碎了好几个，暴风城的钢材散落在洞穴潮湿的地面上。>\n\n<这不是垃圾。这是一座军械库。>",cEN="<Splintered crates bearing the seal of the Alliance. It appears they were tossed from the top of the well with criminal haste. The fall shattered several, scattering Stormwind steel across the damp floor of the cave.>\n\n<This isn't refuse. It's an arsenal.>"}
Q[175005]={d="<检查箱子时，一阵寒意顺着你的脊背爬上来：几乎所有武器都已被掠走。四周的脚印轨迹显示出一种令人不安的混合——沉重的靴子与赤裸的双脚。>\n\n<看来这是真的了：阿拉松·达伦加尔与艾尔迪尔勾结。>\n\n<你该寻找更多情报，揭露他们的阴谋。>",dEN="<As you inspect the crates, a chill runs down your spine: nearly all the weapons have been plundered. The trail of footprints surrounding them reveals an unsettling mix of heavy boots and bare feet.>\n\n<It seems it is true, then: Arathon Darengar was in league with the Ealdir.>\n\n<You should seek more information to bring their plans to light.>",o="消除艾尔迪尔的威胁，揭开他们在达伦加尔庄园井中策划的阴谋。",oEN="Eliminate the Ealdir threat and uncover the plot they were hatching within the well of the Darengar Estate.",p="<自从你抵达庄园，那位队长就一直在密切注视着你。>",pEN="<The Captain has been watching you closely since you arrived at the estate.>",c="<队长在远处朝你示意，做了个严峻的手势。>\n\n女仆把一切都告诉我了。\n\n我们早就严重怀疑达伦加尔家族在密谋反对灰天镇政府，但没想到他们竟敢做到这种地步……\n\n他们在武装艾尔迪尔！我猜他们的意图是加深斯卡德尔德面临的危机，进一步动摇塞雷妮娅女士的统治。",cEN="<The captain beckons you from a distance with a grim gesture.>\n\nThe handmaid has told me everything.\n\nWe had grave suspicions that the Darengars were conspiring against the government of Graysky, but to think they would dare go this far...\n\nThey were arming the Ealdir! I imagine their intent was to deepen the crisis facing Scadeald, further undermining Lady Serenya's rule."}
Q[175006]={d="我怀疑这座宅邸里还有许多秘密有待发掘。达伦加尔家族多年来一直在冷湖家族背后密谋；我们不过触及了他们阴谋的皮毛。\n\n至于你，你展现了勤勉与可靠的判断力。如果你要前往灰天镇，我有一项任务交给你；这是最高的荣誉：\n\n去觐见我的女士塞雷妮娅·冷湖，向她禀报我们今日在此的发现：阿拉松大人叛国的全部规模，以及艾尔迪尔的阴险计划。",dEN="I suspect there are yet many secrets to be unearthed in this manor. The Darengars have been conspiring behind House Coldmere's back for years; we have only scratched the surface of their intrigues.\n\nAs for you, you have shown diligence and sound judgment. If you are bound for Graysky, I have a task for you; the highest of honors:\n\nPresent yourself to my lady, Serenya Coldmere, and apprise her of what we have uncovered here today: the sheer scope of Lord Arathon's treason and the Ealdir's grim plot.",o="到灰天镇向塞雷妮娅·冷湖女士复命。",oEN="Report to Lady Serenya Coldmere in Graysky.",c="<即便隔着遮住塞雷妮娅面庞的纱幕，你也能感到她目光的冰冷，如双箭穿心。>\n\n这倒真是达伦加尔家族该有的结局。我会亲自确保历史记住他们的名字，让它成为背叛的同义词。\n\n至于你的参与，你赢得了斯卡德尔德的感激。像你这样的人才，能为本省做出很大贡献。",cEN="<Even through the veil obscuring Serenya's face, you feel the coldness of her eyes, piercing through you like twin arrows.>\n\nA turn of events worthy of House Darengar. I shall personally see to it that history remembers their name as a synonym for betrayal.\n\nAs for your involvement, you have the gratitude of Scadeald. Someone of your caliber could be of great service to this province."}
Q[175007]={d="达伦加尔家族的背叛虽然阴险，却不过是肆虐本省的灾祸之海中的一滴水。\n\n我们早已习惯艾尔迪尔的存在，就像病人习惯了自身的病痛。他们是这片土地上的一块陈年顽疾，若非霜鬃巨魔入侵，我早就将其清除。\n\n<塞雷妮娅女士长时间凝视着你。>\n\n我相信你有这个本事。如果你也这么认为，就去王座厅向灰天镇卫队指挥官德拉温爵士报到。他会告诉你如何帮我们击溃敌人、恢复秩序。",dEN="The Darengars' treachery, insidious as it was, is but a drop in the ocean of calamities ravaging this province.\n\nWe have grown accustomed to the Ealdir as a sick man grows accustomed to his ailment. They are a chronic blight upon these lands, one I would have already purged were it not for the Frostmane troll invasion.\n\n<Lady Serenya fixes you with a long, steady gaze.>\n\nI believe you have what it takes. If you believe so too, report to Sir Draewyn, Commander of the Graysky Guard, in the throne room. He will tell you how to help us crush our enemies and restore order.",o="到灰天镇王座厅向德拉温爵士复命。",oEN="Report to Sir Draewyn in the Graysky throne room.",c="是塞雷妮娅女士推荐你来的，是吗？\n\n<德拉温给你的印象是那种不必提高嗓门就能赢得尊重的人。他灰色的眼睛把你从头到脚打量了一遍。>\n\n斯卡德尔德在两件事上很慷慨：雨水和麻烦。圣光知道我们需要每一个能召集到的人手。很好！你看起来能干。勤勉。这已经比这里大多数人都强了！",cEN="You come recommended by Lady Serenya, do you?\n\n<Draewyn strikes you as one of those men who need not raise their voice to command respect. His gray eyes size you up from head to toe.>\n\nScadeald is generous in two things: rain and trouble. The Light knows we need every soul we can muster. Very well! You look competent. Diligent. That's already more than I can say for most here!"}
Q[175008]={d="你！对，就是你！耽误你一会儿！\n\n你看起来像是个能照顾好自己的人。你是要前往斯卡德尔德省吗？我丈夫德尔盖恩在灰天镇的宫廷里，我需要有人把这些货物送给他。\n\n我想你已经听说了：连接暴风城和铁炉堡的国王大道已被巨魔侵占，贸易彻底停摆。斯卡德尔德不再安全了！就目前的情况，我可不敢亲自跑一趟灰天镇。\n\n我需要一个信使。你说呢？报酬绝对值得，我保证；我丈夫一向比我阔绰。",dEN="You! Yes, you! A moment of your time!\n\nYou look like someone who knows how to handle themselves. Were you headed for the province of Scadeald? My husband, Durghain, is at the court of Graysky, and I need someone to deliver these goods to him.\n\nYou've heard by now, I imagine: the Kingsway, connecting Stormwind and Ironforge, has been overrun by trolls, and trade has ground to a halt. Scadeald is no longer safe! And I wouldn't dare make the trek to Graysky given how things stand.\n\nI need a courier. What do you say? The pay will be worth your while, I assure you; my husband has always been more lavish than I.",o="前往灰天镇，把货物交给德尔盖恩。",oEN="Travel to Graysky and deliver the goods to Durghain.",p="<德尔盖恩仔细打量着你的包裹，然后把目光移到你脸上。>",pEN="<Durghain scrutinizes the bags you're carrying before shifting his gaze to your face.>",c="是，是，不用说了。是希尔玛派你来的。\n\n你是这个月第四个了。她明明雇得起护卫亲自过来，但自从我们上次吵架，她就宁愿保持距离。这是她惩罚我的方式。\n\n不管怎样，这不是你的错。拿着，这是你应得的报酬。\n\n<德尔盖恩礼貌地低下头。>\n\n对斯卡德尔德来说，对我也一样，都是艰难的日子；我没法给你工作。但卫队总是急于招募新血。如果你有打仗的胃口，我建议你去向卫队指挥官德拉温爵士报到。",cEN="Yes, yes, don't tell me. Hilma sent you.\n\nYou're the fourth this month. She could afford an escort and come herself, but since our last spat, she prefers to keep her distance. It's her way of punishing me.\n\nRegardless, you are not to blame. Here, take this; the payment for your services.\n\n<Durghain bows his head politely.>\n\nThese are lean times for Scadeald, and for my pockets as well; I cannot offer you work. But the guard is always eager to recruit new blood. If you have the stomach for war, I suggest you report to Sir Draewyn, Commander of the Guard."}
Q[175009]={d="我收到了来自邓郡的令人不安的报告，而我抽不出人手去援助那个村庄。\n\n这类事务通常由当地贵族处理，但邓郡属于达伦加尔家族的领地。而迄今为止，达伦加尔家族只会让本就糟糕的局面雪上加霜。\n\n我需要你作为灰天镇的特使前往邓郡。与阿姆罗斯·达戈尔队长谈谈，看看村民们需要什么帮助。",dEN="Troubling reports have reached me from Dunshire, and I lack the men to spare for the village's aid.\n\nThe local nobility usually handles such matters, but Dunshire belongs to the Darengar domain. And thus far, the Darengars have served only to make a bad situation worse.\n\nI need you to go to Dunshire as an envoy of Graysky. Speak with Captain Amros Dhagor and see what help the villagers require.",o="到邓郡向阿姆罗斯·达戈尔队长报到。",oEN="Report to Captain Amros Dhagor in Dunshire.",c="所以，他们终于肯派人来了！我想，迟到总比不到好；哪怕你只是个雇佣剑客。\n\n请原谅我把火气撒在你身上。自从我把报告呈给德拉温爵士，已经过去两周了，从那以后灰天镇那边只有沉默。\n\n我知道卫队因为艾尔迪尔和霜鬃巨魔已经捉襟见肘，但这村子里发生的事，理应比路边的一次伏击更让我们担忧。",cEN="So, they finally deigned to send someone! Better late than never, I suppose; even if you are just a sellsword.\n\nForgive me for taking my frustration out on you. It's been a fortnight since I dispatched my report to Sir Draewyn, and I've had naught but silence from Graysky ever since.\n\nI know the guard is stretched thin with the Ealdir and the Frostmane trolls, but something has happened in this village that should worry us far more than a roadside ambush."}
Q[175010]={d="温德海姆中士正在前线指挥作战，但我们对抗霜鬃巨魔的进展甚微。敌人仍控制着国王大道，我们每杀死一个巨魔，就有两个顶上来。\n\n在威胁斯卡德尔德完整的所有危险中，没有比这更紧迫的了。\n\n去向温德海姆报到。在我统领灰天镇卫队的岁月里，我学到的一点是：战争并不总是只靠军队取胜。哪怕最卑微的士兵也能扭转战局。",dEN="Sergeant Windhelm is leading the war effort at the front, but we have made little headway against the Frostmane trolls. The enemy still holds the Kingsway, and for every troll we slay, two more rise to take their place.\n\nOf all the threats to the integrity of Scadeald, none is as pressing as this.\n\nReport to Windhelm. If there is one thing I've learned during my time leading the Graysky Guard, it is that wars are not always won by armies alone. Even the lowliest soldier can turn the tide of battle.",o="到国王大道的灰天镇前哨站向温德海姆中士报到。",oEN="Report to Sergeant Windhelm at the Graysky Outpost on the Kingsway.",c="新兵？\n\n既然总指挥官认为多一双手就能让天平向我们倾斜，那你一定非比寻常。\n\n你对霜鬃巨魔了解多少？你知道自己正踏进什么吗？砍翻几个强盗，或者对付几个围腰布的野人，那是一回事。战场则完全是另一回事。\n\n而霜鬃巨魔是毫不留情的敌人。",cEN="A new recruit?\n\nYou must be something exceptional, if the Lord Commander believes one more pair of hands will tip the scales in our favor.\n\nWhat do you know of the Frostmane trolls? Do you have any idea what you're stepping into? Cutting down bandits or dealing with savages in loincloths is one thing. The battlefield is another entirely.\n\nAnd the Frostmane trolls are implacable foes."}
Q[175011]={d="我刚收到克雷斯特海恩的埃洛尔斯神父的来信。看来他们正面临某种……不太正统的麻烦，可以这么说。和那些墓穴有关。无疑是艾尔迪尔的黑暗魔法。\n\n克雷斯特海恩是本省第二大定居点，仅次于灰天镇。然而，它的位置使它成为最容易遭受艾尔迪尔暴行的地点之一。\n\n作为灰天镇的特使去向埃洛尔斯神父报到，尽你所能缓解克雷斯特海恩的苦难。",dEN="I have just received a missive from Father Elorth, a priest in Cresthairn. It seems they are facing troubles of an... unorthodox nature, shall we say. Something about the crypts. Ealdir dark magic, no doubt.\n\nCresthairn is the second-largest settlement in the province, surpassed only by Graysky. However, its location makes it one of the places most prone to Ealdir violence.\n\nPresent yourself to Father Elroth as an envoy of Graysky, and provide whatever aid you can to alleviate Cresthairn's woes.",o="到克雷斯特海恩向埃洛尔斯神父报到。",oEN="Report to Father Elroth in Cresthairn.",c="是德拉温爵士派你来的，是吗？\n\n好，好。我知道灰天镇的情况不妙。巨魔的威胁，国王大道被切断……\n\n<神父发出一声疲惫而紧张的叹息。>\n\n那些墓穴。我就墓穴的事写信给总指挥官了，但最好还是你亲眼去看看。",cEN="Sent by Sir Draewyn, are you?\n\nGood, good. I know things are not going well in Graysky. The troll threat, the Kingsway being cut off...\n\n<The priest heaves a weary, nervous sigh.>\n\nThe crypts. I wrote to the Lord Commander regarding the crypts, but it would be best if you saw them with your own eyes."}
Q[175012]={d="这里人人都把国王大道说成是本省的脐带。他们错了。早在灰天镇的第一块石头奠基之前，教会就已在斯卡德尔德立足。\n\n圣风悬空修道院是其利益的长子；本省最古老、最高贵的建筑。然而战争搅乱了棋局。如今我担心这座城市的当权者已经忽视了他们对修道院的职责。\n\n去吧，去向阿姆罗德神父报到，告诉他灰天镇仍记得自己的誓约。教会绝不能倒下。",dEN="Everyone here speaks of the Kingsway as if it were the province's umbilical cord. They are mistaken. Long before the first stone of Graysky was ever laid, the Church already held a presence in Scadeald.\n\nThe Hallow Wind Hanging Abbey is the firstborn of its interests; the oldest and noblest edifice in the province. War, however, has upended the board. And now I fear the authorities of this city have neglected their duty toward the abbey.\n\nGo, present yourself to Father Amrod, and tell him that Graysky still remembers its vows. The Church must not fall.",o="到圣风悬空修道院向阿姆罗德神父报到。",oEN="Present yourself to Father Amrod at the Hallow Wind Hanging Abbey.",c="所以，是灰天镇的随军牧师派你来的。那人叫什么来着？森西斯？康蒂斯？昆提尔？呸！\n\n说实话，灰天镇卫队在修道院这里只会碍手碍脚。我们维持现状更好。\n\n不过既然你来了，我倒有一两件事你可以帮忙。",cEN="So, the chaplain from Graysky sends you. What was that man's name? Centhis? Contis? Cuntir? Bah!\n\nTruth be told, the Graysky Guard would do little more than get in the way here at the abbey. We are better off as we are.\n\nBut since you are here, I can think of a thing or two you might help with."}
Q[175013]={d="修道院是学习与沉思的圣殿，是凡人与神明之间的帷幕最薄的地方。透明。\n\n这看似是一种恩赐，但作为交换，它要求绝对的纪律与虔诚。你明白「绝对」这个词的含义吗？很好，因为这里并非人人都懂。\n\n有些见习者难以将它付诸实践。有几个甚至在考虑离开修道院。\n\n去和他们谈谈。向他们发起决斗挑战。让他们记起圣风的等级秩序……以及背弃誓言的下场。",dEN="Abbeys are temples of learning and reflection, places where the veil between the human and the divine is at its thinnest. Transparent.\n\nIt may seem like a blessing, but in exchange, it demands discipline and absolute devotion. Do you understand the meaning of that word, 'absolute'? Good, because not everyone here does.\n\nSome initiates are struggling to put it into practice. A few are even considering abandoning the abbey.\n\nSpeak with them. Challenge them to a duel. Remind them of the Hallow Wind hierarchy... and the consequences of failing their oath.",o="向那些信仰动摇的见习者发起决斗挑战，让他们记起圣风的等级秩序。",oEN="Challenge the initiates experiencing a crisis of faith to a duel to remind them of the Hallow Wind hierarchy.",p="软弱也是一种罪。",pEN="Weakness is also a sin.",c="圣光在此显现，在布道与祈祷之中。但它也显现在你挑战过的那些见习者的尖叫、鲜血与泪水之中。\n\n你帮了他们一个忙。\"棍棒之下出孝子\"，我父亲过去常说。他说过很多话，大多是胡扯，但在这件事上……在这件事上，他说得对。",cEN="The Light is present here, in the sermons and the prayers. But it was also present in the screams, the blood, and the tears of the initiates you challenged.\n\nYou have done them a favor. 'Spare the rod, spoil the child,' my father used to say. He used to say many things, mostly nonsense, but in this... In this, he was right."}
Q[175014]={d="如今我明白，随军牧师不过是圣光旨意的工具，回应了我们的祈祷。我祈求一个奇迹，而你就站在这里。\n\n容我向你说明情况：在修道院以东的群山中，不到十个朔月之前，我们发现了那些异教种族之一的巢穴——他们的存在本身就是对人类尊严的侮辱。\n\n我说的是穴居人。\n\n虽然我派出了几名最得力的手下前去处理，但在心底深处，我一直怀疑我是在送他们去死。也许你能证明我的直觉是错的？",dEN="Now I see that the Chaplain was but an instrument of the Light's will, answering our prayers. I pleaded for a miracle, and here you are.\n\nLet me apprise you of the situation: to the east of the abbey, in the hills, we discovered not ten moons ago the burrow of one of those pagan races whose very existence is an insult to human dignity.\n\nI speak of the Troggs.\n\nThough I sent some of my best men to deal with them, in my heart of hearts, I have always suspected I was sending them to their deaths. Perhaps you can prove my intuition false?",o="寻找阿姆罗德神父派去处理穴居人的十字军战士。",oEN="Find the crusaders that Father Amrod sent to deal with the Troggs.",p="<这位矮人十字军战士的状况很严重。>",pEN="<The dwarf crusader's condition is serious.>",c="是阿姆罗德神父派你来的……？啊！\n\n<迪亚洛斯失血过多，似乎几乎察觉不到周围的情况。>\n\n这些穴居人和其他同类不一样。他们伏击了我们。一个陷阱。全都是。\n\n我是唯一活下来的……",cEN="Father Amrod sent...? Agh!\n\n<Diallos has lost too much blood. He seems barely conscious of his surroundings.>\n\nThese troggs are not like the others. They ambushed us. A trap. All of it.\n\nI am the only one left alive..."}
Q[175015]={d="穴居人的巢穴在结冰的河对岸，过桥就是。\n\n<一股狂热的决心攫住了迪亚洛斯。>\n\n尽量多杀。把他们灭绝。砸碎他们的头骨！用你的刀把他们串起来！用你的——！\n\n<一阵咳嗽打断了迪亚洛斯的激愤。他吐在雪地上的痰带着血丝。>\n\n给他们看看他们对我战友所施的同样的仁慈。",dEN="The trogg den is on the other side of the frozen river, across the bridge.\n\n<A feverish determination takes hold of Diallos.>\n\nKill as many as you can. Exterminate them. Crush their skulls! Skewer them with your blade! Pulverize them with your—!\n\n<A fit of coughing puts an end to Diallos's vehemence. The sputum he spits onto the snow is stained with blood.>\n\nShow them the same mercy they showed my comrades.",o="击败污坑的穴居人。",oEN="Defeat the troggs of Grimepit.",p="愿圣光指引十字军战士，无论他们身在何处。你找到他们了吗？",pEN="May the Light guide the crusaders wherever they are. Have you managed to find them?",c="穴居人的污秽已成往事。很好。\n\n别让他们的死比你派去处理他们的十字军战士的死更让你内疚——那些死同样压在我的良心上。\n\n一方面，穴居人没有灵魂。另一方面，十字军战士曾宣誓为侍奉圣光而牺牲生命。",cEN="The trogg filth is history. Good.\n\nDo not let their deaths weigh on you any more than the deaths of the crusaders I sent to deal with them weigh on my conscience.\n\nOn one hand, troggs lack souls. And on the other, the crusaders swore to sacrifice their lives in service to the Light."}
Q[175016]={d="<穴居人神器。它散发着奇异的绿色荧光，仿佛被辐射浸透。>\n\n<如果这尊偶像与这些穴居人的信仰存在某种关联，那么它的源头无疑在诺莫瑞根。摧毁这些偶像应当能削弱他们。>\n\n<你该把这件神器带到圣风悬空修道院去，以便接受检查。>",dEN="<Trogg artifact. It emits a strange green luminescence, as if it were bathed in radiation.>\n\n<If this idol correlates in any way with the faith of these troggs, then its origin lies, without a doubt, in Gnomeregan. Destroying these idols should weaken them.>\n\n<You should take this artifact to the Hallow Wind Hanging Abbey so that it may be examined.>",o="摧毁污坑中穴居人信仰的偶像。",oEN="Destroy idols of the Trogg faith in Grimepit.",p="<在成堆的卷轴和书籍之间，学者恩哈隆眯着一只眼、挑着眉毛看着你。>\n\n你打扰我有什么事？",pEN="<Among piles of scrolls and books, Scholar Enharon watches you with one eye narrowed and an arched eyebrow.>\n\nWhat is the reason for your interruption?",c="我们这儿有什么？\n\n<恩哈隆检视着神器，目光中好奇与厌恶各半。>\n\n那些可憎的东西！我从没想到它们竟会有自己的宗教；竟有足够的智力。真是可恨。一种与诺莫瑞根辐射相关的信仰，真是的。\n\n这不可能是巧合。没有任何东西在诺莫瑞根幸存而不发生改变。如果我的猜测没错，那么辐射使这些穴居人产生了突变：赋予了他们一定程度的智力。\n\n杀掉他们真是件痛快事。",cEN="What have we here?\n\n<Enharon inspects the artifact with a gaze that is equal parts curiosity and repulsion.>\n\nThose abominations! I never imagined they could possess a religion of their own; that they would have sufficient intelligence. This is detestable. A faith bound to the radiation of Gnomeregan, no less.\n\nIt cannot be a coincidence. Nothing survived Gnomeregan unchanged. If my suspicions are correct, then the radiation mutated these troggs: it granted them a certain degree of intellect.\n\nKilling them was an indulgence."}
Q[175017]={d="里面的穴居人不是普通的穴居人……他们是士兵。有人在领导他们。他们听从命令。\n\n命令……<迪亚洛斯的呼吸紊乱。他每说一个词都是一阵剧痛。> 有命令，就有首领。而有首领，就有机会。\n\n找到他，杀了他。要杀死一条蛇，只有一个办法，就是砍掉它的头。",dEN="The troggs in there are no ordinary troggs... they are soldiers. Someone is leading them. They follow orders.\n\nOrders... <Diallos's breathing is erratic. Every word he speaks is a stab of pain.> Where there are orders, there is a leader. And where there is a leader, there is an opportunity.\n\nFind him and kill him. There is only one way to kill a snake, and that is to cut off its head.",p="<阿姆罗德的诵念让他的周身笼罩在一层冰冷的光芒中。>",pEN="<The prayer recited by Father Amrod envelops his presence in a cold light.>",c="一个国王？<阿姆罗德神父放声大笑，笑声洪亮而嘲弄。>\n\n那些畜生。它们连呼吸的空气都不配。一个国王。一个国王！接下来是什么？公主？游吟诗人？祭司？\n\n<他的语气一变，变得冷硬。脸色阴沉下来。>\n\n对付那些野兽，死亡是唯一有效的药方。",cEN="A king? <Father Amrod laughs heartily, a loud, mocking roar.>\n\nThose animals. They don't even deserve the air they breathe. A king. A king! What will be next? Princesses? Troubadours? Priests?\n\n<His tone changes, hardening. His countenance turns dark.>\n\nDeath is the only remedy that works on those beasts."}
Q[175018]={d="<商人的额头渗出汗珠，他艰难地寻找着措辞。他的手腕上有被紧紧捆绑的痕迹；显然他曾被俘虏。>\n\n我的货车……我的货物……我可怜的驴子蒂托……全毁了。真是场灾难……\n\n感谢圣光，卫兵及时赶到，在那些恶棍把我弄成蒂托那样之前把他们吓跑了。\n\n<商人望着被洗劫的货车，肩膀耷拉下来。>\n\n我没法从这场打击中恢复过来……我把所有的一切都投进了这批货物。求你，帮帮我！找到那些恶棍的藏身处，把我被抢走的东西拿回来。",dEN="<Sweat beads on the merchant's brow as he struggles to find the words. His wrists bear marks from being bound tightly; he has clearly been held captive.>\n\nMy wagon... my wares... my poor donkey, Tito... All ruined. What a disaster...\n\nThank the Light the guard arrived in time and managed to scare off those scoundrels before they left me in the same state as Tito.\n\n<The merchant gazes at his looted wagon, his shoulders slumped.>\n\nI won't be able to recover from this... I invested everything I had into these goods. Please, help me! Find the hideout of those thugs and recover the items they stole from me.",o="在艾尔文森林北部深处的深石洞穴中找回被偷的货物。",oEN="Recover the stolen merchandise in Northern Elwynn, inside the Deepstone Cave.",p="快告诉我你找回了我的一部分货物！",pEN="Tell me you managed to recover some of my wares!",c="哦，谢谢你，太感谢你了！你找回的比我敢指望的还多；至少够我免于破产了。\n\n我会试着修好货车，等蒂托一康复，我就重新踏上前往灰天镇的旅程。\n\n我不知道该怎么报答你，但我永远欠你一份情。",cEN="Oh, thank you, thank you so much! You've recovered more than I dared hope for; enough to save me from ruin, at least.\n\nI'll try to repair the wagon, and as soon as Tito recovers, I'll resume my journey toward Graysky.\n\nI don't know how I can ever pay you back, but I am forever in your debt."}
Q[175019]={d="国王大道从来就谈不上安全，但自从南方的省份牵扯了我们的注意力——该死的迪菲亚——它就变得比以往更危险了。\n\n城市这一侧我们的士兵太少了，本地强盗对此心知肚明。\n\n你愿意帮我们一把吗？总得有人去猎杀那些袭击商人的匪徒。为了王国的利益。",dEN="The Kingsway has never been truly safe, but with the southern provinces hogging our attention, damn those Defias, it has become more dangerous than ever.\n\nThere are far too few of us soldiers on this side of the city, and the local bandits know it well.\n\nWould you be willing to lend us a hand? Someone must hunt down the brigands who assaulted that merchant. For the good of the kingdom.",o="击败藏在深石洞穴中的艾尔文森林北部强盗。",oEN="Defeat the bandits in Northern Elwynn hiding within the Deepstone Cave.",p="那些罪犯藏身的洞穴应该不远了……你找到了吗？",pEN="La cueva donde se ocultan esos criminales no debe estar lejos... ¿has dado ya con ella?",c="你回来时满身血红。很好。\n\n多亏了你，这片树林稍微安全了一些。暴风城卫队致力于保护这一带；即便如此，如果你打算继续前往斯卡德尔德，还是请谨慎行事。\n\n我们收到了灰天镇卫队的报告，警告我们要提防艾尔迪尔。看来他们的袭击正变得越来越频繁。",cEN="You return stained in red. Good.\n\nThese woods are a little safer thanks to you. The Stormwind Guard is committed to keeping this area protected; even so, proceed with caution if you plan to continue your journey toward Scadeald.\n\nReports have reached us from the Graysky Guard, warning about the Ealdir. It seems their attacks are becoming increasingly frequent."}
Q[175020]={d="我确信影井河的源头出了什么事。鱼人不停地涌向这个湖的岸边，鱼根本不可能这样上钩。\n\n把你在这一带发现的鱼人清掉，别让它们的数量多到我们应付不了。\n\n这也许不能从根本上解决问题，但至少能让暴风城的家庭今天餐桌上有鱼。",dEN="I am certain something is happening at the source of the Shadewell River. Murlocs won't stop coming down to the shores of this lake, and there's no way for the fish to bite like this.\n\nWipe out the murlocs you find around here before their numbers become more than we can handle.\n\nThis might not solve the problem at its root, but at least it will allow Stormwind's families to have fish on the table today.",o="击败艾尔文森林北部兰登湖的鱼人。",oEN="Defeat the murlocs at the lake Landen in Northern Elwynn.",p="只要湖里还有鱼人，我甩多少次竿都没用……你把那些害虫解决了吗？",pEN="As long as there are murlocs in the lake, it doesn't matter how many times I cast my line... have you finished off those pests yet?",c="有鱼咬钩了！我敢肯定这是托你的福。\n\n非常感谢你的帮助。我没什么可给的，但请收下这个，聊表谢意。",cEN="A bite! I'm sure it's thanks to you.\n\nThank you very much for your help. I don't have much to offer, but please accept this as a token of my gratitude."}
Q[175021]={d="那些该死的鱼人……我迟早要报仇！\n\n<渔夫的伤口是新的。虽然看起来不致命，但在情况恶化之前他需要治疗。>\n\n一个鱼人伏击了我，抢走了我好不容易钓到的一点渔获。虽然我还能活着讲述这事算是走运，但我几乎站不住了。我觉得它的武器有毒……\n\n这个湖里长着一种植物，我们渔夫常用来处理毒鱼造成的伤口。我们叫它钩草。帮我采一些嫩芽好吗？",dEN="Those damned murlocs... I'll have my revenge yet!\n\n<The fisherman's wounds are fresh. Though they do not seem fatal, he needs medical attention before his condition worsens.>\n\nA murloc ambushed me and made off with the little catch I had managed to land. While I'm lucky to be alive to tell the tale, I can barely stand. I think its weapon was poisoned...\n\nA plant grows in this lake that we fishermen often use to treat wounds from venomous fish. Hookweed, we call it. Help me gather a few sprouts, would you?",o="在兰登湖采集钩草，并把它们交给受伤的渔夫。",oEN="Collect Hookweed plants at Lake Landen and deliver them to the wounded fisherman.",p="啊……求你别去太久。你拿到那些植物了吗？",pEN="Aagh... please don't take too long. Do you have the plants already?",c="<渔夫接过植物，开始在两手之间揉搓。等它们变成糊状后，他直接敷在伤口上。>\n\n啊啊啊！你不知道这有多刺痛……但要是刺得疼，那就是在愈合……\n\n太感谢你了。我已经能感觉到知觉在恢复。我想接下来我自己能应付，但你走之前，收下这个，谢谢你的帮助。",cEN="<The fisherman takes the plants and begins to rub them between his hands. Once they reach a paste-like consistency, he applies it directly to his wounds.>\n\nAgggh! You've no idea how it stings... but if it nips, it heals...\n\nThank you so much. I can already feel the sensation returning. I think I can manage on my own from here, but before you go, take this in thanks for your help."}
Q[175022]={d="呃……那个……你好。\n\n我没在搞什么鬼，好吗？\n\n只是……有人交给我一个任务，而……说实话，我没自己想的那么勇敢。我觉得我会搞砸。我总是什么都搞砸……\n\n嗯？你……你愿意帮我？真的？让我想想……你得这么做：\n\n<男孩开始一项项列举任务，掰着他小小的手指。这么做时，你注意到他缺了小指。>\n\n一：溜进城堡。二：到达请愿厅。三：打开这个小瓶。四：回到塞……回到小保罗那里！\n\n很简单……对吧？你会帮我吗？",dEN="Uh... er... hello.\n\nI'm not up to anything, okay?\n\nIt's just... I was given a task and... the truth is, I'm not as brave as I thought. I feel like I'm going to mess it up. I always mess things up...\n\nHuh? You... you would help me? Really? Let's see... you have to do this:\n\n<The boy begins to list the tasks, lifting his tiny fingers one by one. As he does, you notice that his pinky finger is missing.>\n\nOne: Sneak into the castle. Two: Reach the Petitioner's Chamber. Three: Open this flask. Four: Return to Cer... Return to Little Paul!\n\nIt's easy... right? Will you help me?",o="潜入暴风要塞的请愿厅，打开小米奇的小瓶。",oEN="Venture into the Petitioner's Chamber within Stormwind Keep and open Little Mickey's flask.",p="像这样的任务对你这种人来说是小菜一碟……对吧？",pEN="A task like this is a piece of cake for someone like you... isn't it?",c="你……你做到了？！哇啊啊！\n\n真希望我长大以后能像你一样勇敢。太谢谢你了！\n\n给，这个你留着吧。在下水道里……我用不着它。",cEN="You... you did it!? Woooaaah!\n\nI wish I could be as brave as you when I grow up. Thank you so much!\n\nHere, keep this. In the sewers... I won't be needing it."}
Q[175023]={d="邓郡首先是个矿业小镇。四处看看吧。你注意到什么奇怪的地方了吗？没有？那我告诉你：这里几乎没剩下什么男人了。\n\n几周前出了事，一件我完全无法解释的事：\n\n一群豺狼人在一个班次中途袭击了矿场。可是……它们是从哪儿来的？为什么它们还盘踞在坑道里？\n\n我猜矿工们把自己封在里面了，若真如此，他们剩下的时间不多了。我本指望德拉温爵士多派些士兵来，但现在只能靠你了：去矿场。解决那些豺狼人，救出矿工。",dEN="Dunshire is, first and foremost, a mining town. Take a look around. Do you notice anything strange? No? I'll tell you: there are hardly any men left.\n\nSomething happened a few weeks ago, something for which I can find no explanation:\n\nA gnoll pack attacked the mine in the middle of a shift. But... where did they come from? And why do they still haunt its tunnels?\n\nI suspect the miners barricaded themselves in, in which case they don't have much time left. I was hoping Sir Draewyn would send more soldiers, but you'll have to suffice: head to the mine. Deal with the gnolls and save the miners.",o="击败铁枝矿场的豺狼人，并探索坑道寻找失踪的矿工。",oEN="Defeat the gnolls at the Ironbough Mine and explore its tunnels in search of the missing miners.",p="<尽管它做出了常见的咬紧牙关的动作，但这只豺狼人全身紧绷的肌肉表明，它绝非寻常之辈。>",pEN="<Despite the common gesture of clenching his jaws, the tension running through the rest of the gnoll’s body reveals that he is no ordinary one.>",c="<尽管外表如此，你面前的这只生物眼中仍残留着一丝人性，让人很难完全把它当作怪物看待。>\n\n等等！等等。我。我和别人不一样。还能思考。会说话。我们说话？好吗？\n\n矿工。挖矿。洞穴。是吧？塌方！石头和死人。矿工被困。饿。很饿。我们吃死人。然后……然后长出爪子。长出毛发。长出牙齿。\n\n变成怪物！很多失去了心智。有些没有。有些像我。有些害怕。",cEN="<Despite appearances, the creature before you retains a vestige of humanity in its eyes that makes it difficult to perceive it entirely as a monster.>\n\nWait! Wait. I. I not like others. Still think. Speak. We speak? Yes?\n\nMiners. Mining. Cave. Yes? Cave-in! Rocks and dead. Miners trapped. Hunger. Bad hunger. We eat dead. Then... then claws grow. Hair grow. Teeth grow.\n\nTurn into monsters! Many lose mind. Others no. Others like me. Others scared."}
Q[175024]={d="<你注意到这只豺狼人在艰难地寻找合适的措辞时流露出的绝望。>\n\n附近有女巫。林子里的小屋。她能做到点什么。这是诅咒。黑暗魔法的诅咒。女巫擅长黑暗魔法。\n\n是女巫诅咒我们？\n\n你去和她谈。恳求。倾听。找到治愈身体和心智的办法！",dEN="<You notice the gnoll's desperation as he struggles to articulate the right words.>\n\nWitch nearby. Shack in the woods. She can do something. This be curse. Curse dark magic. Witch be expert in dark magic.\n\nWitch curse us?\n\nYou talk to her. Plead. Listen. Find way to heal body and mind!",o="找到住在邓郡上方峭壁、孤屋中的女巫，请她帮忙解除矿工身上的诅咒。",oEN="Seek out the witch who lives in the crags above Dunshire, at the Lonely Shack, and ask for her help to reverse the miners' curse.",c="新面孔，而且这回你没带着干草叉和火把。开头不错。说吧，你找我什么事？\n\n<你讲述了奥托·比尔伯格的事，以及矿工们似乎遭受的诅咒——把他们变成了豺狼人。>\n\n典型。他们又怕又瞧不起你，直到某天突然需要你。可这些年来，我一直活在「异类」之中，被邓郡人的蔑视和时时猜疑所困。\n\n我凭什么要帮他们？",cEN="A new face, and you aren't carrying pitchforks and torches, for a change. Not a bad start. Tell me, what brings you to me?\n\n<You recount the story of Alto Bilberg and the curse the miners seem to have suffered, transforming them into gnolls.>\n\nTypical. They fear and despise you until the day they suddenly need you. But for all these years, I have lived in 'otherness,' condemned to the contempt and constant suspicion of the people of Dunshire.\n\nWhy should I help them?"}
Q[175025]={d="利益。说到底就是这个词。\n\n我提个交易：我会配一剂解除诅咒的药水，但作为交换，我要你帮我弄到一样材料：\n\n妖精之尘。\n\n我的药水都需要它，包括这一剂；而我自己越来越难弄到它了。因为……嗯。它是从邓郡一带出没的小妖精身上采集的，它们是一群让人受不了的小东西，相信我，一个个滑溜得很。\n\n杀几只小妖精，给我带足够的妖精之尘来，我就帮你。",dEN="Interest. It all comes down to that.\n\nI propose a deal: I will brew a potion to reverse the curse, but in exchange, I want you to help me acquire an ingredient:\n\nFey Dust.\n\nI need it for my potions, this one included; and it's becoming increasingly difficult for me to obtain it on my own. Because... well. It is harvested from the sprites that haunt Dunshire, and they are unbearable little creatures, believe me, as slippery as they come.\n\nKill a few sprites, bring me enough fey dust, and I will help you.",o="从邓郡一带游荡的小妖精身上获取妖精之尘。摇动被施了魔法的花朵来召唤它们。",oEN="Obtain Fey Dust from the sprites wandering around Dunshire. Shake the enchanted flowers to summon them.",p="你有仙灵之尘吗？",pEN="Do you have the fey dust?",c="<贝尔德雷德把她那鹰钩鼻凑近仙灵之尘，深深吸了一口那四溢的魔法。有那么一瞬间，她的眼睛翻白了。>\n\n啊！很好。我满意了，是的。这够我用好几个月。\n\n可别说贝尔德雷德不守信用！你还在从那些娇小尸体上抖落灰尘的时候，我就已经动手开始熬药了。\n\n我只需要一点时间把它完成。",cEN="<Beldred brings her aquiline nose close to the fey dust and breathes in the radiating magic deeply. For a moment, her eyes roll back.>\n\nAh! Good. I am satisfied, yes. This will last me for several months.\n\nLet it not be said that Beldred fails to keep her word! While you were shaking the dust off their dainty little corpses, I went ahead and began brewing the potion.\n\nI just need a moment to finish it."}
Q[175026]={d="这个……<贝尔德雷德递给你一个装着橙色物质、宛如液态琥珀的瓶子。>这应该够了。我想。\n\n回到矿坑去，在一个受诅咒影响的矿工身上试试这瓶药。要挑敌对的那种；就是那些已经变成无脑豺狼人的家伙。你知道的，以防万一它效果不完美。\n\n<一声短笑暴露了贝尔德雷德促狭的幽默感。>",dEN="This... <Beldred offers you a flask containing an orange substance, like liquid amber.> This should be enough. I think.\n\nReturn to the mine and test the potion on one of the miners affected by the curse. One of the hostile ones; those who have turned into mindless gnolls. You know, just in case it doesn't work perfectly.\n\n<A short chuckle betrays Beldred's mischievous humor.>",o="在矿坑里的豺狼人身上试验贝尔德雷德的药水。你得先把它们打虚弱。",oEN="Test Beldred's potion on the gnolls in the mine. You will need to weaken them first.",p="成功了吗？",pEN="Did it work?",c="没成功，对吧？我从你脸上看出来了。\n\n<贝尔德雷德把脸扭成一个嫌恶的鬼脸。这似乎是真心的。>\n\n恐怕我再也无能为力了。我本想请教我的女巫集会，但她们远在天边，正忙着跟灰天打一场毫无意义的战争。况且，她们为帮忙开出的价码也远远超出你的能力。\n\n不过……",cEN="It didn't work, did it? I can see it on your face.\n\n<Beldred twists her face into a grimace of disgust. It seems to be a genuine sentiment.>\n\nI'm afraid there is nothing more I can do, then. I would consult my coven, but they are far away and busy fighting a pointless war against Graysky. And in any case, the price they would demand for their help is far beyond your means.\n\nAlthough..."}
Q[175027]={d="在这些峭壁的另一边，河水冲刷出一条山谷，如今成了高等精灵的家园。他们的领袖——如果这个头衔适用的话——是一位拥有可怕力量的巫女。我相信她是整个斯卡德尔德最强大的人。\n\n从这里进入山谷的唯一途径是穿过邓希尔的一处洞穴。然而，那里有精灵的附魔守护，凡不把精灵视为朋友者都无法通过。\n\n去调查洞穴附近的情况。如果你找到穿越屏障的办法，就以最快的速度赶往精灵圣地，向巫女阿玛兰瑟陈述你的请求。如果有人能为矿工们做些什么，那就是她。",dEN="On the other side of these crags, the water carved out a valley that now serves as a home to the High Elves. Their leader, if such a title applies, is a sorceress of terrible power. The most powerful in all of Scadeald, I believe.\n\nThe only way to access the valley from here is through a cave in Dunshire. However, it is protected by elven enchantments that bar the way to those who do not count the elves as friends.\n\nInvestigate the vicinity of the cave. If you find a way to cross the barrier, head with the utmost haste to the elven sanctuary and present your case to the sorceress Amaranthe. If anyone can do anything for the miners, it is her.",o="找到穿越魔法屏障的办法，抵达鎏金谷。到了那里，与阿玛兰瑟·奈米尔女士交谈。",oEN="Find a way to cross the magical barrier and reach the Gilded Vale. Once there, speak with Lady Amaranthe Naemyl.",p="<精灵的目光落在天边的某一点上，越过环抱山谷的白色山峰。>",pEN="<The elf's gaze rests on some point upon the horizon, beyond the white peaks that cradle the valley.>",c="<阿玛兰瑟的目光带着某种赤裸感。她的双眼是两泓深沉的记忆之井。>\n\n士兵的重担，是一颗比剑更沉重的心。我知道是什么把你带到我面前。你的努力高尚，你的意图纯粹。\n\n但我帮不了你。\n\n鎏金谷正经历黑暗的日子，我的力量也随着森林的生机一同衰退。\n\n恐怕我无能为力。除非我们挫败笼罩在所有人头上的威胁。",cEN="<Amaranthe's gaze carries a certain sense of nakedness. Her eyes are two wells of deep memory.>\n\nA soldier's burden is a heart heavier than their sword. I know what brings you before me. Your effort is noble, and your intentions pure.\n\nBut I cannot help you.\n\nThe Gilded Vale endures dark days, and my power wanes alongside the vitality of the forest.\n\nI'm afraid I cannot be of assistance. Not until we thwart the threat that looms over us all."}
Q[175028]={d="抱歉，我今天忙得不可开交，不再接新订单了。你改天再——\n\n<面包师抬起头看了一眼。>\n\n哎呀呀呀……这是什么？一个真正的甜食爱好者！\n\n你肯定是来尝我的拿手好戏的。举世闻名的邓希尔馅饼！灰天、冠发、碎岩、影井甚至敦卡扎德的人都专程为它而来……而且他们总会再来！\n\n是的，你流口水了。别担心，我会给你做一个，但作为交换，我需要你帮我干今天的活。先去农田收割小麦。收齐之后，把它送给磨坊主。",dEN="I'm sorry, I'm up to my neck today and I'm not taking any more orders. Come back some other tim—\n\n<The baker looks up for a moment.>\n\nWell, well, well... what do we have here? A true sweet tooth!\n\nYou're here because you want to taste my specialty, surely. The world-famous Dunshire Pie! People from Graysky, Cresthairn, Rockrend, Shadewell, and even Dun Kazad come just for it... and they always come back!\n\nYes, your mouth is watering. I'll make one for you, don't worry, but in exchange, I need you to lend me a hand with today's work. Start by harvesting the wheat from the crop fields. Once you have it all, take it to the miller.",o="收集制作著名邓希尔馅饼所需的小麦。",oEN="Gather the wheat needed to prepare the famous Dunshire Pie.",p="只要风车还在转，一切就都好。\n\n哦……你需要什么吗？",pEN="As long as the sails keep turning, everything will be fine.\n\nOh... do you need something?",c="今天没风……你得等我们把现有的都磨完。\n\n然后你才能磨你的小麦。",cEN="The wind isn't blowing today... You'll have to wait until we finish grinding what we already have.\n\nThen you can grind your wheat."}
Q[175029]={d="面粉生产不能停，而今天风力根本不足以完成这些订单……\n\n<你向磨坊主解释，你只需要磨一点小麦，为面包师跑一趟腿。>\n\n邓希尔馅饼？！你早说啊！把小麦给我，我亲自帮你！\n\n我把麦子倒进料斗；你使劲摇那曲柄。今天风不帮忙，想要真正的馅饼，就得磨出细面粉。",dEN="Flour production cannot stop, and the wind isn't blowing nearly hard enough today to get through all these orders...\n\n<You explain to the miller that you only need to grind a little wheat for the baker's errand.>\n\nA Dunshire Pie!? You should have said so sooner! Give me the wheat, I'll help you myself!\n\nI'll set the grain in the hopper; you give that crank a good turn. The wind isn't helping us today, and we need a fine flour if we want a proper pie.",o="启动风车，磨出制作著名邓希尔馅饼所需的面粉。",oEN="Activate the windmill to produce the flour needed for the famous Dunshire Pie.",p="面包师的主要原料是面粉。你拿到了吗，小馋鬼？",pEN="The baker's main ingredient is flour. Do you have it yet, you sweet tooth?",c="看看这个！你带回了这么多面粉，太好了。\n\n对著名的邓希尔馅饼来说，又少了一样要操心的原料。",cEN="Look at that! You've brought plenty of flour, fantastic.\n\nThat's one less ingredient to worry about for the famous Dunshire Pie."}
Q[175030]={d="邓希尔馅饼的配方需要好几种原料。大部分我这里都有，但你还得再添两样，小馋鬼。\n\n出去给我弄来邓希尔母鸡下的最好的蛋。\n\n还有……嗯……我可以让你爬上山去，但你去旅店买两升他们从山顶带下来的极品风掠牛奶会更省事。",dEN="The recipe for Dunshire Pie requires several ingredients. I have most of what's needed right here, but you still have to provide a couple more, you sweet tooth.\n\nGet out there and bring me the best eggs from the Dunshire hens.\n\nAnd... hmmm... I could make you climb the mountain, but it'll be easier if you go to the inn and buy a couple of liters of that Exquisite Windswept Milk they bring down from the summit.",o="从邓希尔酒馆取得邓希尔鸡蛋和极品风掠牛奶。",oEN="Obtain Dunshire eggs and Exquisite Windswept Milk from the Dunshire tavern.",p="你给我带来的货物必须新鲜，这很重要。",pEN="It's important that the goods you bring me are fresh.",c="我们什么都不缺了！\n\n你想让我现在就动手做，还是你还没饿，小馋鬼？\n\n呸，这问的什么话……香气一飘出来，你就该流口水了！",cEN="We have everything!\n\nDo you want me to start preparing it now, or has your hunger not kicked in yet, you sweet tooth?\n\nBah, what a question... as soon as the smell hits you, your mouth will be watering!"}
Q[175031]={d="现在轮到我了。我或许不懂得驾驭元素，也不会召唤奥术，更不会你们冒险者会的那些东西……但等你尝过邓希尔馅饼，你就无法否认我离做出同样惊艳的成就只差一点点。\n\n大师需要时间。给我几分钟，让我用配得上的用心把它做成形，再让烤炉的热力发挥作用。\n\n所以过一会儿再来吧，小馋鬼。",dEN="Now it's my turn. I may not know how to master the elements, or conjure the arcane, or any of those things adventurers like you do... but once you taste the Dunshire Pie, you won't deny that I come pretty close to achieving something just as spectacular.\n\nA master needs time. Give me a few minutes to shape it with the care it deserves and let the heat of the oven do its work.\n\nSo come back in a bit, you sweet tooth.",o="等待面包师做完著名的邓希尔馅饼。",oEN="Wait for the Baker to finish preparing the famous Dunshire Pie.",p="耐心……这辈子做任何事，最主要的原料永远是耐心。",pEN="Patience... the main ingredient for anything in this life is always patience.",c="此刻，你是整个斯卡德尔德羡慕的对象。说真的，你知道有多少人愿意处在你的位置吗？第一次品尝邓希尔馅饼……\n\n细细品味这一刻。慢慢吃。填饱肚子。那一口你永远不会忘记！",cEN="Right now, you are the envy of all Scadeald. Seriously; do you have any idea how many people would love to be in your shoes? Tasting the Dunshire Pie for the very first time...\n\nSavor the moment. Eat without haste. Fill your belly. You never forget that first bite!"}
Q[175032]={d="你！对，就是你。你没在这附近见过一枚徽章吧？\n\n<看到你摇头，达隆德的肩膀垮了下来。>\n\n我是这个村子的搬运工，也是精灵们的\"朋友\"。我丢失的那枚徽章，是我穿过洞穴中魔法屏障的护身符。没有它，我就干不了活；精灵们时不时会需要我的效力。\n\n这次就是其中之一。而我已经把到处都找遍了。\n\n能麻烦你帮我一把吗？",dEN="You! Yes, you. You haven't seen a medallion around here, have you?\n\n<Darond's shoulders slump as he sees you shake your head.>\n\nI am the porter of this village, and a 'friend' to the elves. The medallion I've lost is my safeguard to pass through the enchanted barrier in the cave. Without it, I cannot do my job; every now and then, the elves require my services.\n\nThis is one of those times. And I have already searched for the amulet everywhere.\n\nWould you mind lending me a hand?",o="找到属于邓希尔搬运工达隆德的魔法护符。",oEN="Find the magic amulet belonging to Darond, the Dunshire porter.",p="运气如何？我的生计就靠那枚徽章了……",pEN="Any luck? My livelihood depends on that medallion...",c="护符，你找到了！\n\n你不知道你把我从多么窘迫的处境里解救出来。现在我可以专心备货了。而且换个说法，我晚上也能睡个安稳觉了。\n\n等一切准备妥当我会通知你，如果你愿意的话。我想你已经赢得了亲眼看看鎏金谷的权利。",cEN="The amulet, you found it!\n\nYou have no idea what a tight spot you've gotten me out of. Now I can focus on preparing the shipment. And I'll be able to get some sleep at night, for a change.\n\nI'll let you know when everything is ready, if you're willing. I believe you've earned the right to see the Gilded Vale with your own eyes."}
Q[175033]={d="你来了。很好。我已经把交付的东西都准备好了。拿着这枚徽章。你需要它来穿过洞穴的魔法屏障。\n\n背起包裹，前往纳玛里安圣所。到达目的地后，去找哈尔丁·绿歌。他是圣所的商人，也是你即将送达的那批订货的下单人。\n\n报酬你留着。这是你帮我所得。不过，如果我没弄错，一旦你亲眼见到鎏金谷，就会觉得任何其他奖赏都黯然失色。",dEN="You're here. Good. I have everything ready for the delivery. Take the medallion. You'll need it to pass through the magical barrier in the cave.\n\nShoulder the pack and head to the Namarien Sanctuary. Once you reach your destination, look for Haldin Greensong. He is the Sanctuary's merchant and the elf who placed the order you're about to deliver.\n\nKeep the payment. You've earned it for the help you've given me. Though, if I'm not mistaken, once you see the Gilded Vale with your own eyes, you'll feel that any other reward pales in comparison.",o="从达隆德那里取走货物，穿过洞穴抵达鎏金谷。到了那里，前往纳玛里安圣所寻找哈尔丁·绿歌。",oEN="Pick up Darond's merchandise and pass through the cave to the Gilded Vale. Once there, head to the Namarien Sanctuary and find Haldin Greensong.",p="什么事？",pEN="Yes?",c="一张新面孔。嗯。看你背上的包裹，我猜你带来了我的订货。那么是达隆德派你来的。\n\n好吧，朋友，深吸一口气，放宽心。你在这圣所里找不到任何不是你随身带来的邪恶。",cEN="A new face. Hm. Judging by the pack upon your back, I take it you carry my order. Darond sent you, then.\n\nWell, friend, take a breath and set your mind at ease. You will find no evil in this Sanctuary that you did not bring with you."}
Q[175034]={d="熊正在成为一个麻烦，而这全怪艾尔迪尔。整天把森林和灵魂挂在嘴边……伪君子！他们占据熊的洞穴，打断它们的冬眠周期……\n\n如今那些野兽在林中怒不可遏地游荡，在村庄附近出没，袭击我们的农场。必须结束这一切！\n\n短期内唯一的解决办法就是猎杀它们。成年熊、幼崽……我们不能破例。\n\n能杀多少就杀多少，把它们的皮带给我，让它们的死不至于全然白费。",dEN="The bears are becoming a problem, and it is all the fault of the Ealdir. All that talk of the forest and the spirits... Hypocrites! They occupy the bears' caves, they disrupt their hibernation cycles...\n\nAnd now the beasts wander the woods in a rage, prowling near the villages and attacking our farms. It must end!\n\nThe only short-term solution is to hunt them down. Adults, cubs... we cannot make exceptions.\n\nKill as many as you find out there and bring me their pelts, so that their deaths are not entirely in vain.",o="杀死斯卡德尔德熊，把它们的皮带给约南·萨洛尔。",oEN="Kill the Scadeald Bears and bring their pelts to Jornan Thalor.",p="你有那些皮子吗？",pEN="Do you have the pelts?",c="冠发的人民感谢你。\n\n这些熊的死将为这一带带来和平，它们的毛皮会在丹莫罗的寒风刮起时提供温暖。",cEN="The people of Cresthairn thank you.\n\nThe death of these bears will bring peace to the region, and their furs will provide warmth when the winds of Dun Morogh blow."}
Q[175035]={d="你……你不是本地人。也许你有我儿子的消息？\n\n阿贝隆是红头发，留着长胡子，一头乱蓬蓬的长发。凯恩是金发，胡子刮得干干净净，蓝眼睛，短发。\n\n他们几天前离开了村子。阿贝隆铁了心要……这么说吧，他想法很复杂：他想加入艾尔迪尔，就像他兄弟凯恩加入了冠发民兵那样。\n\n他们吵了起来。动了手。阿贝隆逃走，凯恩追了上去。他们的眼神，哦，那眼神！我当时就知道他们什么都做得出来。甚至互相残杀。\n\n日子一天天过去，我担心最坏的情况。如果你查到他们的消息，如果你在旅途中遇到他们……求你，告诉他们，他们的母亲非常想念他们。",dEN="You... you are not from around here. Perhaps you have news of my sons?\n\nAbellon is a redhead, with a long beard and a disheveled mane. Cairn is blond, clean-shaven, with blue eyes and short hair.\n\nThey left the village a few days ago. Abellon was determined to... well, he has complicated ideas: he wanted to join the Ealdir, just as his brother, Cairn, had joined the Cresthairn militia.\n\nThey argued. Blows were exchanged. Abellon fled, and Cairn went after him. Their eyes, oh, those eyes! I knew then they were prepared for anything. Even to kill one another.\n\nDays have passed, and I fear the worst. If you find out anything about them, if you cross paths with them in your travels... please, tell them their mother misses them dearly.",o="寻找追踪阿贝隆和凯恩的线索，查明他们的下落。",oEN="Find clues to track Abellon and Cairn to discover what has become of them.",p="呃……！那些艾尔迪尔真该死。疼得像鬼一样……",pEN="Gah...! Curse those Ealdir. It hurts like hell...",c="别动。蹲下，不然我们俩都会没命。前面就是艾尔德梅因洞穴，地地道道的艾尔迪尔巢穴。\n\n在灰天，有人出一大笔钱买艾尔德梅因首领的人头。我一想到就流口水。\n\n<兰德克咬紧牙关，压住一声痛哼。他膝盖上插着一支箭。>\n\n该死。",cEN="Stop. Get down, or you'll get us both killed. Up ahead are the Ealdmaine caverns, an Ealdir den if ever there was one.\n\nIn Graysky, they were offering a handsome sum for the head of the Ealdmaine leader. My mouth started watering at the thought.\n\n<Randec clenches his teeth to stifle a groan of pain. An arrow is buried in his knee.>\n\nDammit."}
Q[175036]={d="看来你懂得自保。也许我们可以互相帮个忙。\n\n看见这个人了吗？<兰德克毫不客气地晃了晃右边那团东西。看衣着是个艾尔迪尔。>\n\n我本打算剥了他的衣服，用他的装束混进艾尔德梅因洞穴。显然，这对我已经不可能了。\n\n但你……你刚才提到什么兄弟，对吧？既然你反正要去洞穴，用这身伪装是明智之举。要是你进去后找到这伙渣滓的首领……把他的头带给我。灰天开出的赏金我们对半分。\n\n你说呢？",dEN="You look like you know how to handle yourself. Maybe we can do each other a favor.\n\nSee this man? <Randec shakes the bundle to his right without much ceremony. An Ealdir, by the looks of his clothes.>\n\nI was planning to strip him and use his clothes to sneak into the Ealdmaine caverns. Obviously, that's off the table for me now.\n\nBut you... you said something about some brothers, right? Since you were heading to the caverns anyway, it would be wise to use the disguise. And if once inside you find the leader of this rabble... bring me his head. We'll split the reward they're offering in Graysky, fifty-fifty.\n\nWhat do you say?",o="检查兰德克身旁的尸体，伪装成艾尔迪尔潜入艾尔德梅因洞穴。",oEN="Inspect the corpse next to Randec to disguise yourself as an Ealdir and infiltrate the Ealdmaine Caverns.",p="怎么样？",pEN="Well?",c="你。\n\n<雷格·安拉莫尔叫住你，一只手搭在你肩上。紧接着，他把鼻子凑近你伪装上偷来的毛皮。他的脸皱成一团。>\n\n你浑身散发着死亡的气味。但我不认识你的脸。艾尔德梅因洞穴可不是你出生那个可怜的小村子。真正的艾尔迪尔才会来这里。那些有战士之心的人。来训练。来杀戮。",cEN="You.\n\n<Raigh Anramor stops you, placing a hand on your shoulder. Immediately after, he brings his nose close to the stolen furs of your disguise. His face wrinkles into a grimace.>\n\nYou reek of death. But I do not know your face. The Ealdmaine caverns are not the pathetic little village where you were born. Real Ealdir come here. Those with the hearts of warriors. To train. To kill."}
Q[175037]={d="你有那份本事吗？你愿意为事业赴死吗？愿意为斯卡德尔德的自由而杀戮吗？\n\n那就向我证明你的价值。\n\n洞穴这第一段里还有别的像你这样的新兵，急着留下自己的印记。去挑战他们。给我一场好戏。让我看看你是什么料子。\n\n然后，也许，我会把你当回事。",dEN="Do you have what it takes? Would you be willing to die for the cause? To kill for the freedom of Scadeald?\n\nThen prove your worth to me.\n\nThere are other recruits like you in this first stretch of the cavern, eager to make their mark. Challenge them. Give me a good show. Show me what you're made of.\n\nAnd then, perhaps, I will take you seriously.",o="挑战一名埃尔德新兵并击败对方。",oEN="Challenge Ealdir Aspirant to a duel and defeat them.",p="向一名艾尔迪尔见习者发起决斗并击败对方。",pEN="Todavía estoy esperando ese espectáculo. ¿O eres pura palabrería?",c="真了不起！何况你才刚刚到这里。\n\n要是每个埃尔德都像你这样能打，我们眨眼之间就能赢下这场战争。\n\n你已经赢得了留在这里的资格。从今往后，就把埃尔德梅因洞穴当成你的新家吧。我们还有很多事要做。",cEN="Impressive! And you've only just arrived.\n\nIf every Ealdir fought like you, we would win this war in the blink of an eye.\n\nYou have earned the right to be here. Consider the Ealdmaine Caverns your new home from now on. We have much to do."}
Q[175038]={d="<你成功进入了埃尔德梅因洞穴。现在，正如外面那名受伤的雇佣兵兰德克告诉你的，剩下的就是找到首领并取他首级。>\n\n<这帮人的首领想必就在洞穴最深处。>",dEN="<You have managed to gain access to the Ealdmaine Caverns. Now, just as the wounded mercenary outside, Randec, told you, all that remains is to find the leader and take his head.>\n\n<It is to be expected that the leader of this group would be found in the deepest part of the cave.>",o="在埃尔德梅因矿坑中杀死首领克拉加恩，并把他的首级带给兰德克。",oEN="Kill Chieftain Cragarn in the Ealdmaine mines and bring his head to Randec.",p="杀死艾尔德梅因矿坑的首领克拉加恩，把他的头带给兰德克。",pEN="Please tell me you have his head.",c="你杀了他。该死，你真的杀了他。我甚至不知道自己能不能打败他。\n\n但交易就是交易。我们约好把报酬平分的。\n\n拿着，这个给你。你赢得了提前领取你那份额的权利。看我这副样子，光是走到灰空就得花上好几天吧。",cEN="You killed him. Dammit, you actually killed him. I don't even know if I would have been able to best him myself.\n\nBut a deal is a deal. And we agreed to split the reward in two.\n\nHere, take this. You've earned the right to collect your share in advance. It'll take me a few days just to reach Graysky in this state, I reckon."}
Q[175039]={d="「又怎么了？他们派你来拷问我吗？我已经说过了：我不会让你享受到听我惨叫的乐趣。」\n\n<你认出这名俘虏正是冠羽镇那个女人描述的、她两个儿子之一：金发、短发、胡子刮得干干净净。这一定就是凯恩。>\n\n<你于是告诉他，是他的母亲派你来的。>\n\n赞美圣光！我还以为我会烂死在这个笼子里。你必须把我弄出去。用什么办法都行。去找笼子的钥匙。有一个埃尔德拿着它。杀了他。把他们全杀光。这些野人没有一个无辜！",dEN="What now? Have they sent you to torture me? I've already told you—I won't give you the satisfaction of hearing me scream.\n\n<You recognize in the prisoner the description given by the woman from Cresthairn regarding one of her two sons: blond, short hair, clean-shaven. This must be Cairn.>\n\n<You proceed to tell him that his mother sent you.>\n\nPraise the Light! I thought I would rot in this cage. You have to get me out of here. By any means. Find the key to the cage. One of the Ealdir has it. Kill him. Kill them all. None of these savages are innocent!",o="找到能打开凯恩笼子的钥匙。为此，击败附近的埃尔德。",oEN="Find the key that opens Cairn's cage. To do so, defeat the Ealdir nearby.",p="找到打开凯恩笼子的钥匙。为此，击败附近的艾尔迪尔。",pEN="Have you found the key?",c="你干得很好。不止是好。要是冠羽镇的民兵都像你这样，这场内战几年前就该结束了。\n\n你选对了阵营，朋友。不像我弟弟。我试着让他回心转意，相信我。但毫无办法。\n\n我做了我该做的事。是的，先生。我做了唯一明智的事。",cEN="You've done well. More than well. If all the Cresthairn militiamen were like you, this civil war would have ended years ago.\n\nYou've chosen the right side, friend. Not like my brother. I tried to make him see reason, believe me. But there was no way.\n\nI did what I had to do. Yes, sir. I did the only sensible thing."}
Q[175040]={d="「我还能怎么办？我弟弟满脑子都是些不切实际的念头。他鼓吹某些主张……他同情埃尔德！他甚至想加入他们。\n\n我们对上了。兄弟对兄弟。男人对男人。而我杀了他。是的。我杀了他。因为那是我的职责。我身为士兵的职责。我身为兄长的职责：守护我们家族姓氏的荣耀。\n\n我明白母亲不会这么看。但父亲，相信我……如果父亲还活着，他自己也会杀了他的。\n\n给你。阿贝隆的项链。我不知道我被俘之后埃尔德对他的遗体做了什么，但母亲总得有个东西下葬，哪怕只是象征性的。拿着吧。」",dEN="What else could I do? My brother had his head in the clouds. He defended certain ideas... he sympathized with the Ealdir! He even wanted to join them.\n\nWe faced each other. Brother against brother. Man against man. And I killed him. Yes. I killed him. Because it was my duty. My duty as a soldier. My duty as a brother; to protect the honor of our family name.\n\nI understand that Mother will not see it that way. But Father, believe me... if Father were still alive, he would have killed him himself.\n\nHere. Abellon's necklace. I don't know what the Ealdir did with his body after they captured me, but Mother will want something to bury, even if it's only symbolic. Take it.",o="回到冠羽镇，把你就她两个儿子的下落所查明的一切告诉阿拉利亚。",oEN="Return to Aralia in Cresthairn and tell her what you have discovered about the fate of her sons.",p="回到冠发的阿拉利亚那里，把你查到的关于她两个儿子命运的事告诉她。",pEN="Tell me you bring good news, please...",c="<阿拉利亚的脸就是痛苦、毁灭与崩溃的化身。在她那双和善的眼睛后面，有什么东西碎裂了。某种永远不会愈合的东西。永远。这辈子不会，下辈子不会，任何一世都不会。>\n\n我……为什么？为什么是我？为什么是我的儿子们？\n\n阿贝隆。哦，阿贝隆。死了。死在自己兄弟手里。\n\n我做错了什么？",cEN="<Aralia's face is the very image of pain, devastation, and ruin. Something breaks inside her, behind her kind eyes. Something that will never heal. Never. Not in this life, nor in the next, nor in any other.>\n\nI... Why? Why me? Why my sons?\n\nAbellon. Oh, Abellon. Dead. Dead at the hands of his own brother.\n\nWhat did I do wrong?"}
Q[175041]={d="<阿拉利亚的脸就是痛苦、毁灭与崩溃的化身。在她那双和善的眼睛后面，有什么东西碎裂了。某种永远不会愈合的东西。永远。这辈子不会，下辈子不会，任何一世都不会。>\n\n我……为什么？为什么是我？为什么是我的儿子们？\n\n阿贝隆。哦，阿贝隆。死了。死在自己兄弟手里。\n\n我做错了什么？",dEN="<Aralia's weeping lasts for several painful minutes. Then, without warning, the storm passes, and a strange, unsettling calm takes hold of her.>\n\nWe should bury the necklace. I want a grave for my son. Even if I don't have his body. I don't care; I will find him. I will.\n\nI will.\n\nYou... I don't have the strength to leave this house. And I don't want anyone in the village to see me like this. Take the necklace. Go to the cemetery and find the grave of my husband, Noghan Dolmen. Bury it in the niche to his left.",o="在冠羽镇墓园中，将阿贝隆的遗物埋葬在诺甘·多尔门的墓旁。",oEN="Bury Abellon's keepsake next to the grave of Noghan Dolmen at the Cresthairn cemetery.",p="把阿贝隆的遗物埋在冠发墓园诺格汉·多尔门的墓旁。",pEN="Is it done? Is my son... resting now?",c="你办好了吗？\n\n<尽管遭遇如此，阿拉利亚还是勉强露出一丝微弱的感激微笑>\n\n我付不起你为我所做的一切。就算我是全省最富有的女人，也付不起。",cEN="Have you done it?\n\n<Despite the circumstances, Aralia manages to offer a faint, tiny smile of gratitude.>\n\nI cannot pay you for what you have done for me. I could not, even if I were the wealthiest woman in the province."}
Q[175042]={d="我已闩上门、祝福了门槛。我不知道还能做什么。\n\n教堂之下有什么东西在蠢动。\n\n黑暗魔法，而且是最污秽的那一种。死者正离开自己的坟墓，在墓穴的走廊里游荡。\n\n<埃尔斯罗神父用手比了个手势，像是在为自己祝福。>\n\n必须有人让他们安息。而且要快，赶在他们逃出墓穴、让整个村子陷入恐慌之前。",dEN="I have barred the doors and blessed the threshold. I knew not what else to do.\n\nSomething is stirring beneath the church.\n\nDark magic, and of the foulest kind. The dead are forsaking their graves and wandering the halls of the crypt.\n\n<Father Elroth makes a gesture with his hand, as if to bless himself.>\n\nSomeone must grant them rest. And quickly, before they escape the crypts and sow terror throughout the village.",o="击败在冠羽镇教堂墓穴中游荡的亡灵。",oEN="Defeat the undead prowling the crypts of the Cresthairn church.",p="击败在冠发教堂墓穴中游荡的亡灵。",pEN="Please... grant them all rest.",c="那些亡灵你处理掉了吗？\n\n感谢圣光！也感谢领主指挥官派你过来！当然，还要谢谢你动手办事。\n\n我还是不明白这事怎么会发生。那些女巫究竟施了什么法术，竟能亵渎那些坟墓的神圣，让安息其中的人化为亡灵复苏？",cEN="Have you dealt with the undead?\n\nThank the Light! And thanks to the Lord Commander for sending you! And to you, of course, for doing the deed.\n\nI still do not understand how this could have happened. What manner of spell must those witches have conjured to profane the sanctity of those graves and raise their guests as undead?"}
Q[175043]={d="<在一具男尸旁发现的日记。>\n\n\"我最亲爱的阿兰娜。没有你的笑容，日子都在枯萎。我常常回想起我们如何让不可能成为可能；一个埃尔德与一名十字军，无可救药地相爱。准备好迎接一切。甘愿违抗我们自己人：圣光，还有林中的诸神。\n\n你很了解我，阿兰娜。所以你知道我打算做什么。既然我们曾让不可能成为可能，为什么不再试一次？\n\n这是我的承诺：\n\n我会把你带回来，无论代价如何。而我知道该从何处着手：\n\n你故事里的三姐妹。\"",dEN="<Journal found beside a man's body.>\n\n“My dearest Alanna. The days wither away without your smile. Often, I find myself remembering how we made the impossible possible; an Ealdir and a Crusader, hopelessly in love. Ready for anything. Willing to defy our own; the Light, the gods of the woods.\n\nYou know me well, Alanna. So you know what I intend to do. If we made the impossible possible once before, why not try again?\n\nThis is my promise:\n\nI will bring you back, no matter the cost. And I know where to begin:\n\nThe Three Sisters from your stories.”",o="在冠羽镇教堂的墓穴中找到阿兰娜的墓。",oEN="Find Alanna's tomb within the crypts of the Cresthairn Church.",p="在冠发教堂的墓穴中找到阿兰娜的墓。",pEN="<The creature's gaze rests upon a point infinitely far away.>",c="<La criatura te dirige una mirada afligida y suplicante>\n\n你……必须……帮帮我们……\n\n我的丈夫……他做了些什么……\n\n圣光……被腐化了……\n\n我们……没法……死去……",cEN="<The creature turns an afflicted, pleading gaze upon you.>\n\nYou... must... help us...\n\nMy husband... he did something...\n\nThe Light... Tainted...\n\nWe... cannot... die..."}
Q[175044]={d="卡登想把我带回来……\n\n他做到了……把我带了回来。把我们所有人都带了回来……\n\n<每一个字都是一阵刺痛。存在的每一秒，都是折磨。>\n\n现在我们死不了……我们什么都试过了……\n\n别告诉埃尔斯罗神父……谁都别说！酒馆里的艾丝琳……去找她。她会知道去哪儿找三姐妹。\n\n求你了……只有她们能帮我。只有她们能纠正这桩逆理之事。",dEN="Carden wanted to bring me back...\n\nHe succeeded... With me. With all of us...\n\n<Every word is a stab of pain. Every second of existence, a torment.>\n\nNow we cannot die... We have tried everything...\n\nDo not tell Father Elroth... No one! Aisling, at the tavern... Find her. She will know where to find the Three Sisters.\n\nPlease... Only they can help me. Only they can correct this perversion.",o="到冠羽镇的旅店去找艾丝琳。",oEN="Seek out Aisling at Cresthairn's inn.",p="在冠发的旅店里寻找艾丝琳。",pEN="<Aisling seems to be resting her throat between songs. She is the bard of this inn, if appearances can be trusted.>",c="所以阿兰娜相信只有三姐妹能救她。\n\n<艾丝琳掂量着其中的含义，神情变得凝重>\n\n那三位胃口无常。她们可能帮你，也可能因为你胆敢找上门来而惩罚你的无礼。\n\n不管怎样，她们怎么处置你都不关我的事。要是你愿意冒险站到她们面前，我就帮你。",cEN="So Alanna believes only the Three Sisters can save her.\n\n<Aisling's expression grows grave as she weighs the implications.>\n\nThose three have fickle appetites. They may help you, or punish your insolence for coming to them at all.\n\nEither way, whatever they do with you is not my problem. If you're willing to risk standing before them, I'll help you."}
Q[175045]={d="这么说阿兰娜认为只有三姐妹能救她。\n\n<艾丝琳的表情变得凝重，权衡着其中的含义。>\n\n那三位欲望无常。她们可能帮你，也可能因你竟敢找上门来而惩罚你的无礼。\n\n不管怎样，她们怎么处置你都不关我的事。如果你愿意冒险站到她们面前，我就帮你。",dEN="Tradition holds that the Three Sisters dwell in the waterfalls of the Swiftwater. But passage requires a safe-conduct:\n\nThe blessing of three different witches.\n\nThat would have been simple enough once. These days, however, nearly every witch in Scadeald has sworn loyalty to Morgwena, and they would attack you on sight.\n\nI'll give you my blessing, of course, but mine alone won't be enough. It falls to you to find two other witches willing to help.",o="取得三位斯凯德尔女巫的祝福。",oEN="Gain the blessing of three Scadeald witches.",p="获得三位斯卡德尔德女巫的祝福。",pEN="What? Do we have a problem, you and I?",c="你说艾丝琳派你来的？\n\n<卡萨尔嗅了嗅空气，仿佛能凭你的气味分辨真话与谎言。>\n\n很好。从灰空有一条路能抵达三姐妹，但你得仔细听好：",cEN="You say Aisling sent you?\n\n<Cathal sniffs the air, as if he could tell truth from lies by your scent.>\n\nVery well. There is a way to reach the Three Sisters from Graysky, but you'll need to listen closely:"}
Q[175046]={d="你说艾丝琳派你来的？\n\n<卡萨尔嗅了嗅空气，仿佛能靠你的气味分辨真话与谎言。>\n\n很好。从灰天有一条路能到三姐妹那里，但你得仔细听：",dEN="Oh! Thank the Light; a traveler! And an intrepid one, by the looks of it! Could I ask you a favor?\n\nIt wasn't even a day ago that the Ealdir ambushed some travelers on this very bridge. Look at the state of things! The guards advise me not to leave the path, but the trout I sell won't climb up the ravine to my stall on their own. And I simply don't dare to wander off.\n\nCould you catch a few trout for me? I'll pay you for them, of course; better safe than sorry!",o="为店主默塞尔钓取斯凯德尔鳟鱼。",oEN="Catch Scadeald Trout for Shopkeeper Mercel.",p="为店主默塞尔钓斯卡德尔德鳟鱼。",pEN="Those trout can resist even the finest fisherman... have you caught them?",c="你收来的货色真不错！甚至比我期望的还多！\n\n承诺就是承诺，拿着吧。对了……要是哪天你想给一个卑微的小店主干活，就回来找我。",cEN="Fine stock you've gathered! Even more than I expected!\n\nA promise is a promise, so here you go. And hey... if you ever want to work for a humble shopkeeper, come back around."}
Q[175047]={d="我们追踪到昨夜袭击大桥的埃尔德，一路追到了附近的一处洞穴。\n\n我们不能就这样丢下岗位，也等不到灰空的援军；守备队都分散去处理王路那边的冲突了。你知道的……那些霜鬃巨魔。\n\n你要是愿意，这活儿可以交给你。我会把洞穴的位置标在你的地图上。进去，把里面的埃尔德清干净。恐怕那些野人只懂得以眼还眼。\n\n你知道么？我们也一样。",dEN="We've tracked the Ealdir who attacked the bridge last night to a cave near here.\n\nWe can't simply abandon our post, and we aren't expecting reinforcements from Graysky either; the guard is spread thin dealing with the conflict at the Kingsway. You know... the Frostmane trolls.\n\nIf you're willing, this could be a task for you. I'll mark the cave's location on your map. Go inside and eliminate the Ealdir you find within. Those savages only understand an eye for an eye, I fear.\n\nAnd you know what? So do we.",o="消灭锯齿洞穴中的埃尔德。",oEN="Eliminate the Ealdir within Jagged Cave.",p="消灭锯齿洞穴里的艾尔迪尔。",pEN="Can I assume the area is safe once more?",c="死狗不咬人……我们是这么说的。不过我不确定这句老话对这些杂种管用。迟早会有更多埃尔德冒出来占下这个洞穴。\n\n他们总是这样。\n\n不管怎么说，你赢得了斯凯德尔省的感激。托你的福，这段路会安稳上一阵子。",cEN="Dead dogs don't bite... or so we say. Though I'm not sure that old proverb applies to these bastards. Sooner or later, more Ealdir will show up to occupy the cave.\n\nThey always do.\n\nOne way or another, you have the gratitude of the province of Scadeald. This stretch of the road will be safer for a while thanks to you."}
Q[175048]={d="退后……退后，不然我就用最后一口气诅咒你……\n\n<一阵剧咳让霍尔加痛得弯下腰。等她缓过劲来，眼里再没有半点倔强。>\n\n他们派我们来对付那些长角者……封住仪式撕开的裂隙。可是……已经太迟了。他们都死了。\n\n别往前。里面只有死亡……",dEN="Back... Stay back, or I will lay a curse upon you with my final breath...\n\n<A coughing fit causes Holga to double over in pain. When she recovers, there is no trace of defiance left in her eyes.>\n\nThey sent us to deal with the Horned Ones... to close the rifts opened by the ritual. But... it is already too late. They are all dead.\n\nStay back. You will only find death inside...",o="深入织夜洞穴，击败长角者，并封印黑林的裂隙。",oEN="Venture into Nightweave Cave, defeat the Horned Ones, and close the Blackwood Rifts.",p="深入织夜洞穴，击败带角者并关闭黑林裂隙。",pEN="Those creatures are the spawn of the Rooted Shadow. They are not of this world...",c="那些生物……那些裂隙……\n\n你是怎么……？\n\n<霍尔加低声问出这最后一句话，随即失去了知觉。>",cEN="The creatures... the rifts...\n\nHow did you...?\n\n<Holga loses consciousness as she whispers that final question.>"}
Q[175049]={d="别傻站着！\n\n你是来搭把手的，还是打算袖手旁观，看着你的同胞在雪地里流干血？\n\n在急救物资里找一卷厚绷带，去照料伤员。他们正在用命保护这个省和整个王国。也是你的王国！\n\n快去，快点！",dEN="Don't just stand there!\n\nHave you come to lend a hand, or to stand idly by while your compatriots bleed out on the snow?\n\nFind a roll of thick bandage among the first-aid supplies and tend to the wounded. They are laying down their lives to protect the province and the kingdom. Your kingdom, too!\n\nMove, quickly!",o="在急救物资中找出厚绷带，并照料伤员。",oEN="Search for thick bandages among the first-aid supplies and tend to the wounded.",p="在急救物资中寻找厚绷带，照料伤员。",pEN="Have you tended to them? Any help is vital right now.",c="<索林的目光里透出一丝羞愧。>\n\n你干得好。原谅我刚才那样粗鲁地对你说话。这场战争、那些巨魔、这么多的死亡……我快撑不住了。而我常常把气撒在无辜的人身上。\n\n收下这个，就当是我的谢意；至少能让我少羞愧一点。",cEN="<Soryn's gaze betrays a sense of shame.>\n\nYou've done well. Forgive me for earlier, for speaking to you so curtly. The war, the trolls, all this death... I am overwhelmed. And I often take it out on the wrong person.\n\nAccept this as my thanks; at the very least, it might make me feel a little less ashamed."}
Q[175050]={d="<索林的目光流露出羞愧。>\n\n你做得很好。原谅我刚才那样粗暴地跟你说话。战争、巨魔、这一切死亡……我快撑不住了。而我常常把气撒在不相干的人身上。\n\n收下这个，作为我的谢意；至少，这能让我少一点羞愧。",dEN="The troll ambush, and the battle that followed, stained the snow red. Hundreds perished; friends, comrades. Compatriots.\n\nWe haven't been able to recover their bodies yet. Hell, we've done nothing but gift corpses to the snow since then.\n\nDo me a favor: I won't ask you to shoulder any bodies, but recover their insignias, at least. Something we can pay homage to when this nightmare ends; when the last Frostmane troll has fallen.",o="在霜鬃伏击地附近找回阵亡士兵的徽记。",oEN="Recover the insignias of the fallen soldiers in the surroundings of Frostmane Ambush.",p="在霜鬃伏击地附近找回阵亡士兵的徽记。",pEN="Once you bring the insignias, we can properly honor the brave.",c="<徽记挂着的链子叮当作响，从你手中交到埃德里克手里。>\n\n你找回了不少。\n\n<埃德里克把徽记按在胸甲上，正好压在心口。>\n\n这比你想象的更珍贵。",cEN="<The chains from which the insignias hang jingle as they pass from your hands to Edrik's.>\n\nYou've managed to recover a fair few.\n\n<Edrik presses the insignias against his breastplate, right over his heart.>\n\nThis is worth more than you know."}
Q[175051]={d="<串着徽记的链条叮当作响，从你手中转到埃德里克手中。>\n\n你收回了相当多。\n\n<埃德里克把徽记按在胸甲上，正对着心脏。>\n\n这比你想象的更珍贵。",dEN="Look at them. Vermin. <Windhelm jerks his head toward the trees, a gesture steeped in hatred.>\n\nSince the first ambush, weeks ago, the skirmishes for control of the Kingsway have been ceaseless. Our situation is precarious: for every troll we kill, two more take its place. And the same cannot be said for our own losses.\n\nBut the Lord Commander sent you. That means he saw something in you. Something it is time to put to the test.\n\nVenture into the forest and eliminate any Frostmane Ambushers prowling the Kingsway. Then, report to the forward party near the bridge that crosses the river.",o="杀死在王路一带游荡的霜鬃伏击者。",oEN="Slay the Frostmane Ambushers that wander the Kingsway.",p="杀死在王路游荡的霜鬃伏击者。",pEN="<The lieutenant is deep in thought, studying the troll ruins, and remains unaware of your presence.>",c="哎哟，哎哟！中士一定是手头宽裕了；距他上次给我们派援兵已经过去好几天了。\n\n让我好好看看你。<中尉带着戏谑嘲弄的眼神打量着你。最后，他友好地拍了拍你的肩膀。>\n\n看来你来的路上顺手砍了几颗脑袋。干得不错，确实不错。\n\n保持这股劲头！",cEN="Well, well! The Sergeant must be feeling generous; it's been a couple of days since he last sent us any reinforcements.\n\nLet me get a proper look at you. <The lieutenant inspects you with an amused, mocking gaze. Finally, he gives you a friendly slap on the shoulder.>\n\nAnd it looks like you lopped off a few heads on your way here. Good work, indeed. Good work.\n\nKeep that attitude up!"}
Q[175052]={d="哎哟，哎哟！中士一定很大方；距他上次给我们派援兵已经过去好几天了。\n\n让我好好打量打量你。<中尉带着戏谑嘲弄的目光审视你。最后，他在你肩上友好地拍了一下。>\n\n看来你一路上砍了几颗脑袋。干得好，确实好。干得好。\n\n保持这股劲头！",dEN="Let the trail of troll corpses you've left behind serve as a warning to the rest. Forget the forest; the true peril lies just ahead.\n\n<Frieren's gloved hand points toward the ruins before you with an energetic sweep.>\n\nZuramunda. Our scouts believe the Frostmane trolls are coordinating their war effort from within. The cave is vast, and it will be teeming with enemies. Which, judging by your look, sounds like an invitation.\n\nFine, I expected no less! Venture into the ruins and strike down every cold-blooded bastard that crosses your path. Go. Go!",o="杀死祖拉蒙达废墟与洞穴中的霜鬃巨魔。",oEN="Kill the Frostmane trolls within the ruins and cave of Zuramunda.",p="杀死祖拉蒙达废墟与洞穴中的霜鬃巨魔。",pEN="Did that help you get it off your chest?",c="对。<一抹残忍的笑容在中尉脸上绽开。>他们的惨叫从这里都能听见。\n\n早就该让那些杂种懂得什么叫恐惧了。",cEN="Yes. <A cruel smile spreads across the lieutenant's face.> Their screams could be heard even from here.\n\nIt was about time those bastards learned the meaning of fear."}
Q[175053]={d="当你面对一个霜鬃巨魔时，会发生三种情况之一：你把他放倒，你成了他的下一顿饭，或者你被拖到祖拉蒙达的废墟里去。\n\n那地方塞满了巨魔俘虏；大多是我军战斗中负伤的士兵。我不知道他们打算拿这些人怎么办，但我宁愿永远不知道。\n\n你一路杀穿洞穴时，能放多少就放多少。我在外面等着，确保他们被送到安全的地方。",dEN="When you face a Frostmane troll, one of three things can happen: you strike him down, you become his next meal, or you find yourself hauled away to the ruins of Zuramunda.\n\nThat place is overflowing with troll prisoners; mostly soldiers from our army who were wounded in combat. I don't know what they plan to do with them, but I'd rather not find out.\n\nFree as many as you can as you fight your way through the cave. I'll wait out here and see to it that they're brought to safety.",o="取得万能钥匙，解救祖拉蒙达洞穴中的人质。",oEN="Obtain the master key and free the hostages within the Zuramunda cave.",p="取得万能钥匙，解救祖拉蒙达洞穴里的人质。",pEN="The safety of the hostages is our priority.",c="人质安全了。\n\n身体状况好一些的人决定冒险穿过森林前往灰空。其余的人躲进了那座旧瞭望塔。\n\n干得好，<class>。",cEN="The hostages are safe.\n\nThose in better condition have decided to risk the trek through the forest toward Graysky. The rest have taken refuge in the old watchtower.\n\nGood work, <class>."}
Q[175054]={d="感谢圣光……我还以为再也见不到一张友善的脸了。\n\n我不知道自己在这里躲了多少天。我设法从笼子里溜了出来，但没跑多远。从那以后，我就一直在等机会除掉……他。\n\n阿格拉莫。\n\n<人质的表情阴沉下来。>\n\n没错。这些巨魔的首领是个兽人。看样子，是部落的一名指挥官。\n\n你跟我不同。你能杀了他。你必须杀了他。\n\n灰空守备队必须知道这件事。这场战争背后是部落在撑腰……",dEN="Thank the Light... I thought I'd never see a friendly face again.\n\nI don't know how many days I've spent hiding here. I managed to slip out of my cage, but I didn't get far. Since then, I've been waiting for the chance to finish... him.\n\nAgramor.\n\n<The hostage's expression darkens.>\n\nYes. The leader of these trolls is an orc. A commander of the Horde, it seems.\n\nYou are not like me. You can kill him. You must kill him.\n\nThe Graysky Guard must know. That the Horde is behind this war...",o="把阿格拉莫的首级交给弗里伦中尉。",oEN="Deliver Agramor's head to Lieutenant Frieren.",p="把阿格拉莫尔的头交给弗里伦中尉。",pEN="You seem uneasy... Do you know something I don't?",c="<弗里伦狐疑地看着那个袋子。一查看里面的东西，他脸上的表情便由厌恶转为激愤。>\n\n一个兽人？在这里？\n\n<有那么一瞬间，那袋子仿佛要从他手中滑落。>\n\n那么部落和霜鬃巨魔结盟了。那次伏击、这场战争……没有一件事是巧合。\n我们得通知灰空。但首先，我要你去办最后一件事。",cEN="<Frieren looks at the sack with suspicion. Upon checking its contents, the expression on his face shifts from disgust to agitation.>\n\nAn orc? Here?\n\n<For a fleeting moment, the sack seems as if it might slip through his fingers.>\n\nThen the Horde is allied with the Frostmane trolls. The ambush, the war... none of it was by chance.\nWe must inform Graysky. But first, I want you to see to one last thing."}
Q[175055]={d="你在里面干得很出色。比我手下任何人都强。<弗里伦咂了咂舌，压低声音补充道：>换我自己也做不到更好。\n\n你从祖拉蒙达救出的一些人质躲进了河对岸的那座旧瞭望塔。我在这边恢复秩序，你过去看看他们，确保他们安全。\n\n他们当中有一位女祭司。人们叫她莎拉。去跟她谈谈。有了这点助力，再加上最后一搏，我们或许就能重新控制王路。",dEN="You've done a fine job in there. Better than any of my men. <Frieren clicks his tongue and adds in a low voice:> I couldn't have done better myself.\n\nSome of the hostages you rescued from Zuramunda have taken refuge in the old watchtower, just across the river. While I restore order on this side, go to them and ensure they are safe.\n\nA certain priestess is with them. Sarah, they call her. Speak with her. With a little help, and one final push, we might just regain control of the Kingsway.",o="到旧瞭望塔联络莎拉修女。",oEN="Contact Sister Sarah at the old watchtower.",c="你也受伤了吗？\n\n<女祭司用满含怜悯的目光打量着你。随后，她的神情松弛下来。>\n\n没有。你一定就是大家都在谈论的那个人。那个救了无数性命的人。\n\n我本想说\"愿圣光祝福你\"，但我想它已经这么做了。而且借由你，它祝福了我们所有人。",cEN="Are you injured as well?\n\n<The priestess scans you with eyes full of compassion. Then, her expression relaxes.>\n\nNo. You must be the one everyone is talking about. The one who has saved so many lives.\n\nI would say 'May the Light bless you,' but I believe it already has. And through you, it has blessed us all."}
Q[175056]={d="你也受伤了吗？\n\n<女祭司用充满怜悯的眼睛打量你。随后，她的表情放松了。>\n\n不。你一定就是大家都在谈论的那个人。那个救了这么多人的人。\n\n我本想说“愿圣光祝福你”，但我相信它已经祝福了你。并通过你，祝福了我们所有人。",dEN="Whether or not you are a devotee of the Light, there is no doubt you are its instrument.\n\nWould you share a brief prayer with me? The wounded would appreciate a few words of comfort. And your warrior's heart, I believe, would appreciate a rest from such violence.\n\nAnd one last thing. You need to warm yourself. Stay by the bonfire for a while, and toss a few logs in to stoke the flames.\n\nIt is the least we can offer, after all you have done for Scadeald...",o="向圣光祈祷以抚慰伤员，并投掷木柴添旺篝火。",oEN="Pray to the Light to bring comfort to the wounded and feed the bonfire by tossing in wooden logs.",p="向圣光祈祷以安慰伤员，并投掷木柴添旺篝火。",pEN="The fire, much like the wounded, requires tending.",c="你的精神为这座瞭望塔带来了温暖。\n\n你想在火边待多久就待多久。",cEN="Your spirit has brought warmth to this watchtower.\n\nStay as long as you need by the fire."}
Q[175057]={d="<尽管篝火暖热，那名士兵的腿却一直在抖。不是冷的缘故。是恐惧。>\n\n我所属的营当时在守卡拉多尔大桥。我们顶住了第一波攻势，还有第二波……有一阵子，我们真以为能守住阵线。\n\n可就在那时，他来了。\n\n一个高大的巨魔，比我见过的任何巨魔都要庞大。他骑着一头可怕的野兽。\n\n莎拉修女坚持要我们休息，可每当我闭上眼，就看见他的脸和那些死者的脸，这叫人怎么休息？\n\n你必须想办法杀了他。",dEN="<Despite the warmth of the bonfire, the soldier's leg has not stopped trembling. It isn't the cold. It is fear.>\n\nThe battalion I belonged to was defending the Kharadol Bridge. We held through the first assault, and the second... and for a time, we truly believed we could hold the line.\n\nBut then, he arrived.\n\nA towering troll, larger than any I have ever seen. He rode a terrible beast.\n\nSister Sarah insists that we rest, but how can one rest when I see his face and the faces of the dead every time I close my eyes?\n\nYou must find a way to kill him.",o="在卡拉多尔大桥杀死飞升者阿尔塔辛。",oEN="Slay Alta'zin the Ascended at the Kharadol Bridge.",p="杀死哈拉多尔大桥的飞升者阿尔塔津。",pEN="¿Has matado a ese monstruo?",c="那个巨魔。那头野兽……都死了吗？\n\n<士兵闭上眼，许久以来第一次感到某种近乎\"安宁\"的东西。>\n\n没人能把我阵亡的战友还给我。连圣光也做不到。但你给了我某种接近它的东西。\n\n我没什么能拿来酬谢你，但我真心想这么做。请你收下。",cEN="The troll. The beast... Are they dead?\n\n<The soldier closes his eyes and, for the first time in a long while, he feels something akin to 'peace'.>\n\nNo one can return my fallen comrades to me. Not even the Light. But you have given me something that comes close.\n\nI have little with which to reward you, but I wish to do so. Please, accept this."}
Q[175058]={d="莎拉修女的心比我们任何人都大，但并非所有的伤痛都能靠祈祷治愈。\n\n我们的干净绷带用完了，消毒酒精昨天也见了底。更别提我们手无寸铁这件事。\n\n真是讽刺。我们需要的一切都在卡拉多尔大桥的地窖里。\n\n<鲁尔文咬紧牙关低吼。他的颤抖一直没停过。>\n\n如果你能一路杀到大桥，就把能搬的箱子都带回来：医疗物资、武器、弹药……迟早我们得回灰空去……最好还是带着武器回去。",dEN="Sister Sarah has a heart larger than any of us, but not every ill can be mended with prayer.\n\nWe've run out of clean bandages here, and the disinfecting alcohol was spent yesterday. Not to mention the fact that we are utterly defenseless.\n\nIronic. Everything we need is in the cellar of the Kharadol Bridge.\n\n<Rulven grunts through gritted teeth. He has not stopped trembling.>\n\nIf you can fight your way to the bridge, bring back every crate you can carry: medical supplies, weapons, ammunition... Sooner or later, we'll have to return to Graysky... and it would be best to do so armed.",o="收集卡拉多尔大桥内的医疗箱、武器和弹药。",oEN="Collect the medical crates, weapons, and ammunition inside Kharadol Bridge.",p="收集哈拉多尔大桥内的医疗箱、武器和弹药。",pEN="The ammunition, weapons, and medicine should be inside the Kharadol Bridge. Have you found it all?",c="武器和弹药由我亲自分发。\n\n莎拉修女管医疗物资比我强。不过先拿着这个：迟早你会用得上。你从来不停下来，是吧？！\n\n别推辞；有了你带回来的这些东西，够我们救治三场战争的伤员了。",cEN="I'll distribute the weapons and ammunition myself.\n\nSister Sarah will know how to manage the medical supplies better than I. But first, take this: sooner or later, you'll have need of it. You never stop, do you!\n\nDon't refuse it; with what you've brought back, we could treat the wounded of three wars."}
Q[175059]={d="你为斯凯德尔做了这么多……你洒下的所有血。你自己流下的所有血。我们不能再要求你什么了。\n\n回灰空去吧。走吧。好好休息。你需要力气，因为这事远没有结束。如果部落真和霜鬃巨魔结成了同盟……这不过是一场更漫长战争的黎明。\n\n直接去见领主指挥官德雷温爵士。关于部落的警告，不能因为要经手中间人而耽搁。\n\n我相信他知道该如何奖赏你在王路立下的功绩。",dEN="After all you have done for Scadeald... All the blood you have spilled. All you have bled yourself. We can ask no more of you.\n\nGo back to Graysky. Go on. And rest. You will need your strength, for this is far from over. If the Horde is in league with the Frostmane trolls... this is but the dawn of a much longer war.\n\nReport directly to Sir Draewyn, the Lord Commander. A warning regarding the Horde cannot be delayed by intermediaries.\n\nI am certain he will know how to reward the deeds you have achieved here on the Kingsway.",o="向德雷温爵士禀报事情的始末。",oEN="Inform Sir Draewyn of all that has transpired.",c="<领主指挥官的脸像一副面具，不泄露丝毫情绪。可他的眼睛……哦，他的眼睛在预言战争。那份笃定令人胆寒。>\n\n部落。\n\n那么，一切都更简单了。同时也更复杂了。\n\n<接着是一段漫长的沉默。然后，他补充道：>\n\n你超出了我的期望。这并不常见。我会确保你得到应有的奖赏。眼下，只要我还是领主指挥官，就把这座城堡当成你的家。",cEN="<The Lord Commander's face is a mask that betrays no emotion. But his eyes... Oh, his eyes prophesy war. With a certainty that is terrifying.>\n\nThe Horde.\n\nEverything is simpler, then. And more complicated at the same time.\n\n<An eternal silence follows. Then, he adds:>\n\nYou have exceeded my expectations. That does not happen often. I shall see to it that you are rewarded accordingly. For now, as long as I remain Lord Commander, consider this castle your home."}
Q[175060]={d="<领主指挥官的脸是一张不泄露任何情绪的假面。但他的眼睛……哦，他的眼睛预言着战争。带着一种令人恐惧的确信。>\n\n部落。\n\n那一切就简单多了。同时也更复杂了。\n\n<随之而来的是永恒的沉默。然后，他补充道：>\n\n你超出了我的期望。这并不常见。我会确保你得到应有的奖赏。眼下，只要我还是领主指挥官，就把这座城堡当作你的家。",dEN="They devour them. What a grotesque sight.\n\nThose cannibals... have you seen them? They regenerate like lizards after feasting upon our own. Even their own kind. I had only seen such a thing when I was stationed in the north...\n\nThe task I have for you is not a pleasant one: set the corpses ablaze; save them from the trolls' appetite.\n\nTake this torch.<Jorvik presses a hand to his stomach; his expression anticipates a retching gag.>\n\nTake advantage now, while the wind is blowing against them...",o="焚烧王路一带的人类与巨魔尸体。",oEN="Set fire to the human and troll corpses around the Kingsway.",p="点燃王路一带的人类与巨魔尸体。",pEN="<Lieutenant Frieren wrinkles his nose.>",c="<中尉深吸一口气；闻到空气中烧焦血肉的刺鼻气味，他眯起了眼睛。>\n\n我知道这不容易……做正确的事向来不易。",cEN="<The Lieutenant takes a deep breath; as he notices the acrid scent of burning flesh in the air, he narrows his eyes.>\n\nI know it isn't easy... Doing the right thing rarely is."}
Q[175061]={d="野蛮的埃尔德，本省的敌人、王国的叛徒，在离城不远处、三姐妹瀑布之上扎下了营地。\n\n他们称之为斯凯德恩村，这是令人无法容忍的挑衅，也是对我们和平的直接威胁。\n\n通缉：\n斯凯德恩首领的首级，以及将其埃尔德追随者斩尽杀绝。",dEN="The savage Ealdir, enemies of the province and traitors to the realm, have established a camp but a short distance from the city, perched above the Three Sisters Fall.\n\nScaidern Village, as they call it, is an intolerable provocation and a direct threat to our peace.\n\nWANTED:\nThe head of the Scaidern chieftain and the annihilation of his Ealdir followers.",o="找到斯凯德恩村，清除埃尔德势力，并将其首领的首级交给德雷温爵士。",oEN="Locate Scaidern Village, eliminate the Ealdir presence, and deliver their leader's head to Sir Draewyn.",p="找到斯凯德恩村，清除艾尔迪尔的势力，把其首领的首级交给德雷温爵士。",pEN="Word from Scaidern Village, then? Speak.",c="死了。\n\n可惜这么多人会被这种念头蛊惑。如果埃尔德退回到森林里、停止争取分离的斗争，斯凯德尔会强大得多。",cEN="Dead.\n\nA pity so many allow themselves to be seduced by such notions. Scadeald would be far stronger if the Ealdir withdrew to the forests and ceased their struggle for secession."}
Q[175062]={d="<手写的命令。你读到以下内容：>\n\n急流渡口是一处地理上的瓶颈。如果那座旧桥消失……斯凯德尔的大片土地将脱离暴风城的掌控。\n\n换句话说：我们将孤立灰空。\n\n到斯凯德恩村去，我的兄弟们，去见拉格首领。在你们执行这些命令期间，他会给你们庇护：\n\n唤醒河流。将它从冰封的桎梏中解放。召来千年未见的洪水。让整个斯凯德尔都见证三姐妹的怒吼。伟大的母亲如此下令。\n\n<一个名叫卡斯巴德的人签署了这份羊皮卷。>",dEN="<Handwritten orders. You read the following:>\n\nThe Rushwater Crossing is a geographical bottleneck. If that old bridge were to vanish... a vast portion of Scadeald would fall beyond the grasp of Stormwind.\n\nIn other words: we would isolate Graysky.\n\nGo to Scaidern Village, my brothers, and present yourselves before Chieftain Rallagh. He shall grant you shelter while you carry out these orders:\n\nAwaken the river. Release it from its icy yoke. Invoke a flood the likes of which has not been seen in millennia. Let all of Scadeald witness the cry of the Three Sisters. So commands the Great Mother.\n\n<One Cathbad signs the parchment.>",o="击败在斯凯德恩村附近河畔潜伏的黑暗德鲁伊。",oEN="Defeat the Dark Druids lurking by the river near Scaidern Village.",p="击败在斯凯德恩村附近河畔潜伏的黑暗德鲁伊。",pEN="Yes?",c="这是什么？\n\n<查看羊皮卷时，阿尔卡里安的眉毛从一条直线拧成了陡峭的斜线。等他终于抬起头，眼里满是纯粹的惊慌。>\n\n你是说，你挫败了这件事？你杀了那些德鲁伊？\n\n<一声如释重负的叹息。他一手按住胸口。>\n\n好。呼。对。你来找我做对了。对。对！我会组织一次调查！就这么办！我保证查个水落石出。",cEN="What is this?\n\n<As he inspects the parchment, Alcarian's eyebrows shift from a flat line to a sharp diagonal. When he finally looks up, his eyes betray sheer panic.>\n\nAnd you say you've thwarted it? You killed the druids?\n\n<A sigh of relief. He presses a hand to his chest.>\n\nGood. Phew. Yes. You did well coming to me. Yes. Yes! I shall organize an investigation! That's it! I promise to get to the root of this matter."}
Q[175063]={d="野蛮的埃尔德，本省的敌人、王国的叛徒，在道莫尔峰的山坡上扎下了营地。\n\n他们称之为加尔达恩村，这对整个地区的完整构成威胁。\n\n通缉：\n加尔达恩首领的首级，以及将其埃尔德追随者斩尽杀绝。",dEN="The savage Ealdir, enemies of the province and traitors to the realm, have established a camp upon the slopes of Daumor Peak.\n\nThey call it Galdaern Village, and it stands as a threat to the very integrity of the region.\n\nWANTED:\nThe head of the Galdaern chieftain and the annihilation of his Ealdir followers.",o="找到加尔达恩村，清除埃尔德势力，并将其首领的首级交给德雷温爵士。",oEN="Locate Galdaern Village, eliminate the Ealdir presence, and deliver their leader's head to Sir Draewyn.",p="找到加尔达恩村，清除艾尔迪尔的势力，把其首领的首级交给德雷温爵士。",pEN="Word from Galdearn Village, then? Speak.",c="又一个营地被端掉了。\n\n<德雷温的呼吸很重。气息尖锐而断续。>\n\n至少这一次，我们的人没有再送命。\n\n感谢你的效力。",cEN="Another camp liquidated.\n\n<Draewyn's breathing is heavy. His breath, sharp and ragged.>\n\nAt least none of our own had to die this time.\n\nThank you for your service."}
Q[175064]={d="你是我几个星期以来见到的第一个人。你不是灰空派来的吧？不是？好吧，不是。\n\n<布罗姆利沮丧地低下头。>\n\n也许你照样能帮我。道莫尔峰。你知道这名字什么意思吗？「道莫尔」在矮人语里是「野猪」；我相信你一定注意到了，它们在这座山上泛滥成灾。\n\n你看着就像这辈子杀过不少野猪的人，也许这活儿会让你觉得「无聊」。可我那些长羽毛的朋友得填饱肚子，而野猪正好是它们的主要食物。\n\n去猎几头回来，行吗？把你能背的肉都带回来。拜托了！",dEN="You're the first person I've seen in weeks. You wouldn't happen to be sent from Graysky, would you? No? Right, no.\n\n<Bromli hangs his head in defeat.>\n\nMaybe you can help me regardless. Daumor Peak. You know what that means? 'Daumor' is Dwarven for 'Boar'; and I'm sure you've noticed they're a plague on this mountain.\n\nYou look like the type who's killed many a boar in your time, and perhaps the task 'bores' you. But my feathered friends need to fill their bellies, and it turns out boars are their main source of food.\n\nHunt a few of them down, would you? And bring back all the meat you can carry. Please!",o="在道莫尔峰收集野猪肉。",oEN="Collect boar meat from Daumor Peak.",p="在道莫尔峰收集野猪肉。",pEN="Do you have the boar meat?",c="你弄到多少肉了？\n\n<布罗姆利飞快地瞥了一眼。>\n\n好，好。这些够当开胃菜了。没错，一道\"开胃菜\"。别那样看我：我跟你说过，它们吃得比你能想象的还多！",cEN="How much meat did you manage to get?\n\n<Bromli takes a quick glance.>\n\nGood, good. This will do for an appetizer. Yes, an 'appetizer'. Don't look at me like that: I told you they eat more than you can imagine!"}
Q[175065]={d="你弄到了多少肉？\n\n<布罗姆利飞快地瞥了一眼。>\n\n好，好。这够当开胃菜了。是的，一道“开胃菜”。别那样看我：我告诉过你，它们吃得比你想象的还多！",dEN="Would you mind lending me a hand again? Sometimes the gryphons bring back... 'peculiar' items to their nests, and it's best to clear them out before someone gets hurt.\n\nNow that you have the meat, toss them a good chunk so they can fill their bellies and stay calm. Only then should you go anywhere near the nests.\n\nOh! And if you find any fallen feathers, don't go tossing them in the trash; they have more uses than you'd imagine. Bring me all you find!",o="清理道莫尔峰的狮鹫巢穴，并收集掉落的羽毛。",oEN="Clean the gryphon nests at Daumor Peak and collect the fallen feathers.",p="清理道莫尔峰的狮鹫巢，收集掉落的羽毛。",pEN="Are you done? Did you bring the feathers?",c="干干净净，正合我意！不然它们怎么休息？再说，谁愿意在脏兮兮的巢里下蛋？\n\n咱俩私下说，我一直觉得挺别扭：它们长着鹰的头、狮子的身子，可……居然……还是下蛋。",cEN="Spotless, just the way I like 'em! How else are they supposed to rest? Besides, who'd want to lay eggs in a filthy nest?\n\nBetween you and me, it's always given me a bit of a turn that they have the head of an eagle, the body of a lion, and... yet... they still lay eggs."}
Q[175066]={d="是啊。我想是的。有何不可？毕竟你为我们做了这么多。你该得到一份像样的奖赏。\n\n告诉我，你想不想骑上一头狮鹫的背？\n\n时候到了！我心里已经有一头完美的狮鹫。亲人。温顺。但好奇心重。自从你成了这儿的新面孔，它就喜欢上你了。我想它会让你骑的。",dEN="Aye. I think so. And why not? After all, you've done a great deal for us. You deserve a proper reward.\n\nTell me, how would you like to ride upon the back of a gryphon?\n\nThe time has come! And I have the perfect gryphon in mind. Affectionate. Docile. But curious. He's taken a shine to you since you're the new face around here. I reckon he'll let you mount up.",o="在道莫尔峰骑上狮鹫达恩，飞越斯凯德尔。",oEN="Mount Daarn the gryphon at Daumor Peak and fly over Scadeald.",p="在道莫尔峰骑上狮鹫达恩，飞越斯卡德尔德。",pEN="One never forgets their first flight...",c="挺难忘的体验，是吧？\n\n风扑在脸上。山间的寒气。斯凯德尔的景色在脚下铺展开来……\n\n啊！不用谢我。跟你干的活儿比起来，这已经是我能拿出的最微薄的回报了。\n\n要是哪天路把你带回道莫尔峰，请过来打个招呼。",cEN="Quite the experience, eh?\n\nThe wind in your face. The mountain chill. The landscape of Scadeald stretching out below...\n\nAh! No need to thank me. This is the least I could offer in exchange for the work you've done.\n\nIf the road ever brings you back to Daumor Peak, please, stop by and say hello."}
Q[175067]={d="相当难忘的体验，嗯？\n\n风拂过脸颊。山间的寒意。斯卡德尔德的景色在脚下铺展开来……\n\n啊！不用谢我。这是我为你所做的工作最起码能给的回报。\n\n如果路把你带回道莫尔峰，请过来打个招呼。",dEN="She is always in my prayers. Ralda, that poor woman... Do you hear the wailing? It must be one of those days. Her dark days. Half the flow of the Shadewell is made of her tears.\n\nThere is no remedy for it; losing a daughter... it is not natural. To make matters worse, shortly after what happened to her girl, they stationed her husband at Windswept Watch, where he keeps guard day and night. And she, so very alone...\n\nWould you do me a kindness? Could you take her something to eat? She never has an appetite, poor soul, and sometimes she forgets to eat altogether.\n\nShe lives in the lonely house at our feet, by the shores of the lake.",o="去暗影井湖畔那座孤零零的房子找拉尔达谈谈。",oEN="Speak with Ralda at the lonely house by Shadewell Lake.",p="与影井湖畔孤屋中的拉尔达交谈。",pEN="Dorothy...?",c="多萝西……？哦……\n\n<看到那包食物，你眼见着她眼中的希望熄灭>\n\n是费尔纳德派你来的。我……多谢了，我想。可我没胃口。女儿下落不明，我没法袖手旁观。\n\n我必须找到她！",cEN="Dorothy...? Oh...\n\n<Upon seeing the bundle of food, you watch as the hope dies in her eyes.>\n\nFernad sent you. I... Thank you, I suppose. But I have no appetite. I cannot sit idly by while my daughter is missing.\n\nI must find her!"}
Q[175068]={d="是鱼人干的，你知道吗？他们掳走了我的小多萝西！\n\n「他们从不上来这么远」，他们这么跟我说。「他们从没给我们惹过麻烦」。信人就得遭报应！那些怪物抢走了我的孩子，就因为镇上没人觉得他们算得上威胁。\n\n可你是外乡人。所以你懂这世道是怎么运转的。你早就把眼罩摘下来了。\n\n我也是。<说出这句话时，拉尔达的声音碎了。>\n\n求你了。去瀑布那边，能杀多少鱼人就杀多少。也许……也许你能找到多萝西？",dEN="It was the murlocs, you know? They took my little Dorothy!\n\n'They never come this far up,' they told me. 'They've never caused us any trouble.' Trust and be damned! Those monsters snatched my girl because no one in town thought they could be a threat.\n\nBut you're an outsider. You know how the world works, then. You've taken the blindfold off.\n\nSo have I. <Ralda's voice breaks as she says it.>\n\nPlease. Go down the falls and slaughter as many murlocs as you can. Maybe... Maybe you'll find Dorothy?",o="杀死 9 名暗影井鱼人战士和 5 名暗影井鱼人占卜者。",oEN="Slay 9 Shadewell Murloc Warriors and 5 Shadewell Murloc Augurs.",p="杀死9名影井鱼人战士和5名影井鱼人占卜者。",pEN="The murlocs took Dorothy...",c="你把他们杀了……对吧？\n\n也许你该杀得更多。直到一个鱼人都不剩。\n\n多萝西不该遭这个罪。我也不该失去她……\n\n他们把她抢走了。让他们把多萝西还回来。\n\n<拉尔达失声痛哭。>",cEN="You killed them... didn't you?\n\nMaybe you should kill more. Until not a single murloc is left.\n\nDorothy didn't deserve this. I didn't deserve to lose her...\n\nThey took her from me. Make them give Dorothy back.\n\n<Ralda breaks into tears.>"}
Q[175069]={d="你杀了他们……对吧？\n\n也许你该再多杀一些。直到一个鱼人都不剩。\n\n多萝西不该遭这个罪。我不该失去她……\n\n他们把她从我身边夺走了。让他们把多萝西还回来。\n\n<拉尔达失声痛哭。>",dEN="Dorothy disappeared while she was playing near the shore. I always warned her to be careful... Always. Always.\n\nBut one lapse is all it takes... Something surged from the water. They grabbed her by the ankle. They dragged her toward the falls and...\n\n<Ralda shudders.>\n\nI don't want to imagine how she must feel right now... imprisoned, lost, alone.\n\nPlease, look for any clue as to where the murlocs have taken her.",o="在暗影井瀑布寻找多萝西下落的线索。",oEN="Search for clues regarding Dorothy's whereabouts at the Shadewell Falls.",p="在影井瀑布寻找关于多萝西下落的线索。",pEN="I still hold onto hope that nothing irreparable has happened to my poor girl... Help me.",c="你说你们什么都没找到是什么意思？可那些鱼人……多萝西……\n\n<拉尔达的目光阴沉下来。>\n\n你是不是在瞒着我什么？你不敢的！就算多萝西不在……要是她……<她艰难地咽了口唾沫。喉咙里的结始终没散。>我宁愿知道真相，也不想活在悬而未决里。\n\n那就告诉我。你一定找到了什么。\n\n她还活着吗？求你了！\n\n<拉尔达失声痛哭。>",cEN="What do you mean you found nothing? But the murlocs... Dorothy...\n\n<Ralda's gaze darkens.>\n\nAre you hiding something from me? You wouldn't dare! Even if Dorothy weren't... If she... <She swallows hard. The lump in her throat remains.> I would rather know than live with the uncertainty.\n\nSo tell me. Because you must have found something.\n\nIs she still alive? Please!\n\n<Ralda breaks down into tears.>"}
Q[175070]={d="如果多萝西不在鱼人那里，那还能是谁……？\n\n<拉尔达擦去眼泪，一股突如其来的决绝在她眼中燃起。>\n\n狗头人……！当然，一定是他们。他们把我的孩子关起来，让她凿石头，或者在黑暗里点蜡烛。\n\n我女儿很乖。非常非常乖，很听话。他们不会愿意放她走。那我们只好逼他们放。\n\n他们住在这附近的一个洞穴里。我见过他们！扯掉他们的尾巴。他们的胡须。他们肮脏的脑袋。把他们全杀了。一个活口都别留！",dEN="If Dorothy wasn't with the murlocs, then who could have...?\n\n<Ralda wipes away her tears as a sudden determination burns in her eyes.>\n\nThe kobolds...! Of course, it had to be them. They have my little one locked away, picking at stone or lighting candles in the dark.\n\nMy daughter is good. Very, very good, and obedient. They won't want to let her go. We'll have to force them.\n\nThey live in a cave, near here. I've seen them! Rip off their tails. Their whiskers. Their filthy heads. Kill them all. Leave not a single one alive!",o="解决暗影井一带的狗头人威胁。",oEN="Deal with the kobold threat in the vicinity of Shadewell.",p="解决影井一带的狗头人威胁。",pEN="It had to be the kobolds who took Dorothy...",c="他们死了吗？受苦了吗？疼得叫喊了吗？\n\n<仇恨在拉尔达眼中烧得如此炽烈，她的泪水几乎像是在蒸发。>\n\n我敢肯定，还不够。",cEN="Are they dead? Did they suffer? Did they scream in pain?\n\n<The hatred burns so intensely in Ralda's eyes that it almost seems as if her tears are evaporating.>\n\nNot enough, I'm sure."}
Q[175071]={d="<拉尔达泪光朦胧的眼神里，透出一连串狂乱焦灼的念头。>\n\n村里的父母，我们总是吓唬自家孩子……我们说，要是他们不乖，狗头人就会把他们抓去凿石头当惩罚……\n\n也许我丈夫对我女儿就是这么做的。也许这就是他再也不来这儿的原因……\n\n<拉尔达从恍惚中醒来，转向你。>\n\n狗头人抓着她。我敢肯定。\n\n到他们洞穴深处去，找出任何能说明她被关在哪里的线索。快点。求你了！",dEN="<Ralda's watery gaze betrays a frantic sequence of feverish thoughts.>\n\nThe parents in the village, we always threaten our little ones... we tell them that if they don't behave, the kobolds will take them away to pick at stone as punishment...\n\nMaybe my husband did that to my daughter. Maybe that's why he doesn't come around here anymore...\n\n<Ralda snaps out of her trance and turns to you.>\n\nThe kobolds have her. I'm certain of it.\n\nGo deep into their cave and look for any clue as to where they are holding her. Hurry. Please!",o="在暗影井洞穴中寻找多萝西下落的线索。",oEN="Search for clues regarding Dorothy's whereabouts within the Shadewell Cave.",p="在影井洞穴中寻找关于多萝西下落的线索。",pEN="<Ralda has a vacant stare.>",c="你说你们什么都没找到是什么意思？你确定？多萝西一点踪迹都没有？不可能……不可能……不可能！\n\n她父亲惩罚她，把她带去矿坑交给狗头人了。她一定在那儿！\n\n你们找得不够仔细……你们得回去再仔细找。她一定在那儿……在某个地方。",cEN="What do you mean you found nothing? Are you sure? Not a single trace of Dorothy? Impossible... Impossible... Impossible!\n\nHer father punished her and took her to the mine with the kobolds. She has to be there!\n\nYou didn't look well enough... You have to go back and search harder. She has to be there... somewhere."}
Q[175072]={d="多萝西的父亲……罗斯弗斯。\n\n他会不会把她带到那座受诅咒的塔里去了？当然，他想让我远离我的女儿……他比鱼人和狗头人还要禽兽！我真是太瞎了。太瞎了……！\n\n<她说着，攥紧拳头，指节发白。>\n\n去风啸岗找他。逼他说出他把她藏在哪儿。告诉他，把她还给我……\n\n<痛楚与怒火哽住了她的声音。>\n\n我不在乎他。我只想要我的女儿。我只想让多萝西回来……",dEN="Dorothy's father... Rothfuss.\n\nCould he have taken her with him to that cursed tower? Of course, he wants to keep me away from my daughter... He's a monster even worse than the murlocs and the kobolds! How blind I've been. How blind...!\n\n<As she speaks, she clenches her fists until her knuckles turn white.>\n\nGo find him at Windswept Watch. Make him tell you where he's hiding her. Tell him to give her back to me...\n\n<Pain and rage strangle her voice.>\n\nI don't care about him. I only want my daughter. I just want Dorothy back...",o="在风啸岗与多萝西的父亲罗斯弗斯当面对质。",oEN="Confront Rothfuss, Dorothy's father, at Windswept Watch.",p="在风掠哨塔与多萝西的父亲罗斯弗斯对质。",pEN="<Rothfuss watches you without a word, steady but visibly weary.>",c="收下这个，虽然微薄，就当是赔你的辛苦。\n\n谢谢你照顾我的女儿——愿圣光护佑她——也谢谢你照顾我可怜的夫人。",cEN="Take this, small as it may be, as compensation for your trouble.\n\nThank you for caring for my daughter, may the Light keep her, and for my poor wife."}
Q[175073]={d="你大概注意到了，我这旅店里最让人吃不腻的，就是风啸的奶酪。可按他们消耗的速度，我一眨眼就要断货了。\n\n往常我会派侄子去补货，可斯凯德尔是这副光景……而暗影井又那么远！\n\n你就不一样了……<多尔克雷斯特上下打量你，点了点头。>旅途把你磨炼出来了。你这身板更结实。\n\n去暗影井，找大奶酪师阿尔莫，订一批精选奶酪。我会重重酬谢你，别弄错了。",dEN="You've likely noticed that if there's one thing folks can't get enough of in my inn, it's the cheeses from Windswept. But at the rate they're being devoured, I'll be out of stock in a heartbeat.\n\nNormally, I'd send my nephew for more, but with Scadeald in such a state... and Shadewell being so far away!\n\nYou, on the other hand... <Dolcrest looks you up and down and nods.> Your travels have seasoned you. You're made of sturdier stuff.\n\nHead to Shadewell, find Grand Cheesemonger Almo, and order a fine assortment of cheeses. I'll pay you handsomely for it, make no mistake.",o="与暗影井村的奶酪大师阿尔莫交谈。",oEN="Speak with Cheese Master Almo in Shadewell Village.",c="你说你是从灰空来的？多尔克雷斯特那个老吝啬鬼……要是由着他的性子，他会把我最后一块奶酪都囤走。\n\n告诉他不必担心：我转眼就能备好他的订单。\n\n说实话，我的名声大半要归功于灰空人。南方各省在些贵族的压力下，净给我们出口使绊子。\n\n你知道么？那是他们的损失。我们的奶酪是暴风城王国最好的。",cEN="From Graysky, you say? That old skinflint Dolcrest... if it were up to him, he'd hoard every last one of my cheeses.\n\nTell him not to worry: I'll have his order ready in two shakes of a lamb's tail.\n\nTo be honest, I owe much of my reputation to the people of Graysky. The southern provinces do nothing but hinder exports due to pressure from certain nobles.\n\nYou know what? It's their loss. Our cheeses are the finest in the Kingdom of Stormwind."}
Q[175074]={d="从灰天来的，你说？多尔克雷斯特那个老吝啬鬼……要是由着他，他会把我最后一块奶酪都囤走。\n\n告诉他别担心：我转眼就能备好他的订单。\n\n说实话，我的名声大半要归功于灰天的人们。南方各省因为有某些贵族施压，只会给出口设障碍。\n\n你知道吗？那是他们的损失。我们的奶酪是暴风城王国最好的。",dEN="Shadewell cheeses don't just appear by magic. Have you had the chance to visit the beautiful meadows of Windswept?\n\nOur cows graze upon the summit. A local breed that roams free in some of the most fertile pastures in the kingdom. There's no other secret to it!\n\nRight now, several cows are waiting to be milked. Unfortunately, there are few hands left in the village; many were conscripted to defend the Fortress of Andraste from the Blackrock orcs, while others are giving their lives to protect the Kingsway from the trolls.\n\nWould you help me? I just need you to fill a few buckets with milk. I'll pay you well!",o="用风啸奶牛的新鲜乳汁装满奶桶。",oEN="Fill buckets with fresh milk from the Windswept cows.",p="把风掠奶牛的鲜奶装满奶桶。",pEN="If it were up to me to determine the value of things, a bucket of fresh Windswept milk would be worth more than one filled with gold.",c="瞧瞧这色泽！闻起来也棒极了！丝般柔滑、浓郁香甜，还带着一股清新气息，让人想起风啸的翠绿草甸……\n\n没有什么，绝对没有什么，能跟我们这些牛的奶相比。",cEN="Look at that color! And it smells wonderful! Smooth as silk, creamy, sweet, and with a fresh aroma that brings to mind the green meadows of Windswept...\n\nNothing, absolutely nothing, compares to the milk from our cows."}
Q[175075]={d="除了牛奶，还有另一种配料让我的奶酪如此特别。\n\n霉菌！\n\n没有它，那绵密的口感、那香气、那风味……全都毁了。这是个漫长的过程，相信我，需要耐心和极细致的功夫。不过话说回来，我能当上大奶酪师，总是有原因的。\n\n而且不是随便什么霉菌都行。我要的是长在某个特定洞穴里的那一种。我会把它标在你的地图上。\n\n能麻烦你去那里采一些回来吗？",dEN="Besides the milk, there is another ingredient that makes my cheeses so special.\n\nMold!\n\nWithout it, the creamy texture, the aromas, the flavors... the whole thing would be ruined. It's a long process, believe me, one that requires patience and a great deal of finesse. But there's a reason I'm a grand cheesemonger, after all.\n\nBesides, not just any mold will do. I need the variety that grows in one specific cave. I'll mark it on your map.\n\nWould you mind heading over there to gather some?",o="从风啸洞穴采集新鲜霉菌。",oEN="Gather Fresh Mold from the Windswept Cave.",p="从风掠洞穴采集新鲜霉菌。",pEN="The clouds that break against the mountains of Scadeald create the perfect conditions for the mold to grow.",c="嗯，这些应该够维持好一阵子的奶酪生产了。\n\n谢谢你。",cEN="Yes, this should be enough to keep the cheese production going for quite some time.\n\nThank you."}
Q[175076]={d="哎呀！你好啊，年轻的<man/woman>！看见这些漂亮家伙了吗？这些羊该剪毛了！\n\n愿意搭把手吗？\n\n拿着。抄起剪子，卷起袖子，像没有明天一样剪下去。剪完把羊毛带给我，别担心，我会让你觉得值当！这些羊的羊毛贵比黄金；难不成你以为只有它们的奶才值钱？",dEN="Opa! Hello there, young <man/woman>! Have you seen these beauties? These sheep are ripe for the shear'n!\n\nCare to lend a hand?\n\nHere. Grab the shears, roll up your sleeves, and get to shearing like there's no tomorrow. Bring me the wool when you're through, and don't you worry, I'll make it worth your while! The wool from these sheep is worth its weight in gold; or did you think only their milk was of any value?",o="给风啸的绵羊剪毛，并收集成捆的羊毛。",oEN="Shear the Windswept sheep and collect bundles of wool.",p="给风掠羊剪毛，收集成捆的羊毛。",pEN="If one goes out looking for wool, they'd best make sure they don't come back shorn.",c="你把它们打理得漂亮极了！也瘦了，没错，<sir/ma'am>。干得非常好。要是我掉几斤肉也能这么容易就好了……\n\n多谢你帮忙。想看看风啸的羊毛有多好吗？拿上我这顶帽子。我用你带来的这些羊毛再给自己做一顶。",cEN="You've left 'em lookin' right handsome! And lean, too, yes <sir/ma'am>. Very well done. If only I could shed a few pounds that easily...\n\nMany thanks for the help. Want to see just how good Windswept wool is? Take my hat. I'll just make myself a new one with all the wool you've brought me."}
Q[175077]={d="你对这些羊有感情了，是吧？\n\n它们每一只都有名字。而我一个都不会忘；就连那些早就走了的，名字我也记得……\n\n我们风啸的牧场主一向把狼群挡在外面，可最近它们成了实打实的祸害。\n\n我已经因为它们的饥肠辘辘损失了太多羊。\n\n杀掉狼群的头狼，顺手再多清掉几头。没了首领、数量又减了，剩下的再想回来就得掂量掂量了。你说呢？",dEN="You've grown fond of the sheep, haven't you?\n\nEach and every one of 'em has a name. And I never forget a single one; not even the names of those who're long gone...\n\nWe ranchers of Windswept have always kept the wolves at bay, but lately they've become a real problem.\n\nAnd I've already lost far too many sheep to their hunger.\n\nKill the pack's alpha and get rid of a few more wolves while you're at it. Without their leader and with their numbers thinned, the rest will think twice before coming back. What do you say?",o="杀死高风的狼群和它们的头狼裂空之口。",oEN="Slay the Highwind wolves and their alpha, Skymaw.",p="杀死高风狼群及其首领天颚。",pEN="The pack alpha dictates the behavior of all the rest.",c="狼群首领决定其余所有狼的行为。",cEN="Well done! Many thanks on behalf of Shadewell and Windswept. This wolf has caused us more headaches than any other."}
Q[175078]={d="沿山路往下走，你会找到安德拉斯特要塞。它被黑石兽人围困已有一段时间了。\n\n你能走到这儿，说明你就是那种总想找点事做的人。那好；这座塔里没什么动静，但地下室通着一处洞穴，而那洞穴的出口就在土堤脚下。\n\n我们有几个人在下面扎了营。他们正准备袭击围困要塞的黑石兽人的后方。\n\n去找阿拉塞尔。我相信他有活儿给你干。",dEN="Following the path down the mountain, you'll find the Fortress of Andraste. It's been under siege by the Blackrock orcs for some time now.\n\nIf you've made it this far, it's because you're the type who's always looking for something to do. Well then; not much is moving in this tower, but the basement leads to a cave, and that cave opens up at the foot of the embankment.\n\nA few of our men have set up a camp down there. They're preparing to strike the rear of the Blackrock orcs besieging the fortress.\n\nHead to Arathel. I'm sure he'll have work for you.",o="前往土堤上、塔脚下的阿拉塞尔营地。",oEN="Visit Arathel's camp at the foot of the tower, on the embankment.",p="拜访塔脚下土堤上阿拉瑟尔的营地。",pEN="Yes?",c="你是什么人，雇佣兵？我无所谓；就算你是个披着<class>皮囊的鱼人我也不在乎。事实是，我需要有胆气、不会轻易退缩的人。\n\n这不是灰空这几周打的那种小打小闹。这是战争。真正的战争。要是安德拉斯特要塞陷落，黑石兽人就会像瘟疫一样蔓延整个省。",cEN="What are you, a mercenary? Fine by me; you could be a murloc in a <class> disguise for all I care. Fact is, I need people with grit, those who don't flinch easily.\n\nThis isn't some skirmish like the ones Graysky has been fighting these past few weeks. This is war. Real war. And if the Fortress of Andraste falls, the Blackrock orcs will spread through the province like a plague."}
Q[175079]={d="敌军——如果「军队」这个词用得上——没料到会遭到后方袭击。他们最精锐的战士都在前线，与要塞的士兵交战。\n\n你知道这意味着什么吗？意味着进攻的时候到了。\n\n你看着很急躁，而你能走到这儿，说明你巴不得打一场。告诉我，想不想带头冲锋？\n\n干掉一些黑石士兵。我和我的人收拾剩下的。完事之后，去向摩尔指挥官报到。",dEN="The enemy army, if the word 'army' even applies, isn't expecting an attack from the rear. Their finest warriors are at the front, locked in combat with the fortress soldiers.\n\nDo you know what that means? It means the time has come to strike.\n\nYou look impatient, and if you've come this far, it's because you're itching for a fight. Tell me, would you like to lead the charge?\n\nCut down a few of those Blackrock soldiers. My men and I will handle the rest. When you're finished, report to Commander Moore.",o="击败从后方围困安德拉斯特要塞的黑石兽人战士。",oEN="Defeat the Blackrock orc warriors besieging the Fortress of Andraste from the rear.",p="击败从背后围攻安德拉斯特要塞的黑石兽人战士。",pEN="<The Commander is far too busy barking orders and coordinating the defense.>",c="<指挥官正忙着下令、协调防御，无暇分身。>",cEN="Are you with Arathel's lot? Hm. Good. You fought well down there."}
Q[175080]={d="兽人的技术再粗糙，投石车终究是投石车。而一块足够大、足够快的石头，造成的破坏不亚于一门大炮。\n\n我们得把它们除掉。\n\n拿着。炸药。靠近时安放在底座上，把那些东西炸飞几个。完事之后向摩尔指挥官报到。",dEN="Rudimentary as orc technology may be, a catapult is still a catapult. And a rock that's big enough and fast enough can do just as much damage as a cannon.\n\nWe need to get rid of them.\n\nHere. Explosives. Place them at the base when you get close, and blow a few of those things sky-high. Report to Commander Moore when you're through.",o="摧毁黑石兽人的攻城器械。",oEN="Destroy the Blackrock orc siege engines.",p="摧毁黑石兽人的攻城器械。",pEN="Soldier?",c="黑石的投石车越来越成问题，我的士兵又没法足够快地穿过他们的阵列去够到那些投石车。\n\n你立了大功，<class>。",cEN="The Blackrock catapults were becoming quite the problem, and my soldiers weren't advancing through their ranks fast enough to reach them.\n\nYou have rendered a fine service, <class>."}
Q[175081]={d="我可能犯了个算错，需要你帮忙纠正。\n\n我们的狩猎大师凯瑟里克·萨德森没法及时填饱要塞的肚子。而打完这样一场仗，我的人需要的不只是一碗稀薄的蔬菜汤才能撑下去。\n\n去森林里找凯瑟里克，尽力帮他。光是来到这座要塞、站到我面前，你就已经比大多数人更有胆识了。我觉得这件事非你莫属。\n\n去吧。",dEN="It is possible I have made a miscalculation, and I need your help to set it right.\n\nOur Master of the Hunt, Ketheric Sadson, will not be able to fill the stronghold's bellies in time. And after a battle like this, my men will need more than a meager vegetable soup to keep them going.\n\nFind Ketheric in the woods and assist him however you can. You have already shown more courage than most just by coming to this fortress and standing before me. I believe you are the right person for this task.\n\nGo.",o="在附近的林地中寻找安德拉斯特要塞的狩猎大师凯瑟里克·萨德森。",oEN="Look for Ketheric Sadson, the Master of the Hunt of Andraste's Stronghold, in the nearby woodlands.",c="是摩尔派你来的？知道指挥官还记得我，挺好。\n\n依我的经验，我告诉你：战斗让人胃里发紧、肠子发松。可胜利……胜利之后总是跟着饿狼般的饥饿。而我一个人没法给整座要塞供肉。\n\n想派上用场，就准备好弄脏你的手。",cEN="Moore sent you? It's good to know the Commander still remembers me.\n\nIn my experience, I'll tell you this: battle tightens the stomach and loosens the bowels. But victory... victory is always followed by a ravenous hunger. And I cannot provide meat for an entire stronghold on my own.\n\nIf you want to be of use, prepare to get your hands dirty."}
Q[175082]={d="首先，我们得弄到足够的肉。算我们走运，大自然自有供给。\n\n<凯瑟里克做了个夸张的手势，像是在指四周的树林。>\n\n每年这个时候，牦牛都会从霜林丘陵下来找食找水。虽然对杜恩卡扎德的矮人来说这是个敏感话题，但牦牛肉最能填饱人。而我们正在打仗。\n\n去猎几头，把肉带给我。我们比它们更需要这些肉。",dEN="First, we must secure enough meat. Fortunately for us, nature provides.\n\n<Ketheric makes a theatrical gesture, as if to point at the surrounding woods.>\n\nAt this time of year, the yaks descend from the Waldfrost Foothills in search of food and water. Although it's a sore subject for the dwarves of Dun Kazad, their meat nourishes like no other. And we are at war.\n\nHunt a few of them and bring me their meat. We're going to need it more than they do.",o="在曲丘森林收集牦牛肉，以供要塞的士兵食用。",oEN="Collect yak meat from the forest of the Crooked Hills to feed the soldiers of the stronghold.",p="在弯曲丘陵的森林中为要塞的士兵收集牦牛肉。",pEN="Did you have a good time on the hunt? To be honest, I find little joy in it myself.",c="<凯瑟里克带着一副又傻又饿的笑容摸着那些肉。>\n\n这些够了。没错。肉的料理我亲自来。\n\n每个士兵都会分到自己的口粮。而他们会清楚该谢谁。",cEN="<Ketheric feels the meat with a silly, hungry grin.>\n\nThis will be enough. Yes. I'll see to the preparation of the meat myself.\n\nEvery soldier shall have their ration. And they'll know exactly who to thank."}
Q[175083]={d="我在这儿备口粮，你却抱着胳膊站在那儿，我看着难受。再来跑最后一趟怎么样？\n\n春之精灵就在附近；非常守礼，非常客气，但别搞错了：他们的和善是一面盾牌，他们的谨慎只是远离我们麻烦的借口。\n\n也许你跟他们打交道会比我顺利。\n\n去拜访他们一趟，行吗？为我们的伤员向他们讨些那珍贵泉水的魔法之水。他们把那个地方护得极紧，可也该像我们其他人一样出把力了。",dEN="It sits poorly with me, seeing you stand there with folded arms while I prepare the rations. How about one last errand?\n\nThe Elves of the Spring are nearby; very proper, very cordial, but make no mistake: their kindness is a shield, their caution an excuse to stay clear of our troubles.\n\nPerhaps you'll have better luck with them than I did.\n\nPay them a visit, will you? Ask for enchanted water from their precious spring, for our wounded. They guard that place with fierce zeal, but it's high time they put their shoulder to the wheel like the rest of us.",o="找到泉边的高等精灵，确保获得魔法之水的供应。",oEN="Locate the High Elves at the spring and secure a supply of enchanted water.",c="一张友善的面孔。近来我们很少见到这样的人。这世界仿佛已被阴影填满。\n\n过来告诉我们：是什么把你带到这儿来的？\n\n<那精灵的目光剥开了你的意图。他点点头，仿佛了然于心。>\n\n啊，是猎人派你来的。我知道安德拉斯特那边怎么说我们！别向精灵讨主意，因为他们既会说「行」，也会说「不行」。\n\n<他笑了。>\n\n可忠告是件危险的礼物，即便在智者之间也是如此，而所有的路都可能走岔。\n\n尽管如此，我们还是尽力帮你。",cEN="A friendly face. We welcome few of those, lately. It seems as though the world has filled with shadows.\n\nCome and tell us: what brings you here?\n\n<The elf's gaze strips away your intentions. He nods, as if understanding.>\n\nAh, the hunter sent you. I know what they say of us in Andraste! Ask not the elves for advice, because they will tell you both 'yes' and 'no'.\n\n<He laughs.>\n\nBut advice is a dangerous gift, even from the wise to the wise, and all courses may run ill.\n\nStill, we shall endeavor to help you."}
Q[175084]={d="这处泉水是一份我们很少与圣所之外的人分享的礼物。\n\n<萨纳德利尔的眼神警惕了一瞬，随即露出微笑。>\n\n但你们的事业是高尚的。在安德拉斯特洒下的血汗，帮着维系了我们山谷的安宁；我们出手相助也是应该的。\n\n拿上这只水罐，浸入泉水之中。守护泉水的灵魂会抗拒；它总是这样，那个坏脾气的老家伙。你得……安抚它。",dEN="The water from this spring is a gift we rarely share with those from outside the Sanctuary.\n\n<Sanadriel's eyes grow wary for a moment before he smiles.>\n\nBut your cause is noble. The blood and sweat shed at Andraste help maintain the peace of our valley; it is only right that we assist.\n\nTake the amphora and submerge yourself in the waters. The spirit that guards the spring will resist; he always does, the grumpy old thing. You will have to... soothe him.",o="用水罐盛满魔法之水，击败泉水的守护之灵，再把它带回安德拉斯特要塞救治受伤的士兵。",oEN="Fill the amphora with enchanted water, defeat the spring's guardian spirit, and carry it back to Andraste's Stronghold to heal the wounded soldiers.",p="把陶罐装满附魔之水，击败泉水守护精魂，再把它带回安德拉斯特要塞治疗受伤的士兵。",pEN="You've come from speaking with the High Elves, I see.",c="要不是亲眼所见，我绝不会相信。就算是十个圣骑士，也做不到那罐魔法之水为这些人做到的事。\n\n我知道山谷里的精灵是强大的盟友，但鉴于他们内敛的性情，我一直宁愿让他们置身这场战争之外。\n\n也许我该重新考虑。",cEN="I wouldn't believe it if I hadn't seen it with my own eyes. Not even ten paladins could have done for these men what the enchanted water from that amphora has achieved.\n\nI knew the elves of the valley were powerful allies, but I always preferred to keep them out of this war, given their reserved nature.\n\nPerhaps I should reconsider."}
Q[175085]={d="前天夜里来了一批北郡、金镇和湖畔镇的士兵。这本该是好消息——要不是「士兵」这个词放在他们身上这么不合适的话。\n\n他们几乎毫无战斗经验。\n\n去跟他们谈谈，帮他们训练。他们很有干劲，这已经比大多数人强了，但他们需要来点务实的教训。\n\n我是说，一场硬碰硬的较量。把那些不切实际的念头从他们脑子里打出去。",dEN="The other night, a contingent of soldiers arrived from Northshire, Goldshire, and Lakeshire. It would be good news, if only the word 'soldier' didn't fit them so poorly.\n\nThey have barely any combat experience.\n\nSpeak with them and help them with their training. They are motivated, which is more than most can say, but they need a dose of pragmatism.\n\nA good fight, I mean. To knock the fancy ideas right out of their heads.",o="在安德拉斯特要塞向新来的新兵发起决斗挑战。",oEN="Challenge the newly arrived recruits at Andraste's Stronghold to a duel.",p="在安德拉斯特要塞向新来的新兵发起决斗挑战。",pEN="Are you finished with them?",c="他们当中不止一个掉了眼泪。可怜的家伙。\n\n我们这世道很残酷。但要是还没撕下他们眼前的遮布就把他们送上战场，那才更残酷。",cEN="More than one of them shed tears. Poor devils.\n\nIt's a cruel world, ours. But it would be far crueler to send them to the battlefield before tearing the blindfolds from their eyes."}
Q[175086]={d="关于我们的敌人，你知道些什么？\n\n我们面对的兽人打着黑石的旗号，但我认为他们听命于自己的一位大酋长。也许是个叛党，而且闹得很凶。\n\n我已经数不清我们挨了多少次进攻了。是时候把战火引向兽人了。\n\n去找我们部署在他们堡垒附近的军情七处特工。阿伦多尔会告诉你行动的细节。",dEN="What do you know about our enemies?\n\nThe orcs we face fly the banner of the Blackrock, but I believe they answer to a Warchief of their own. A rebel, perhaps, and a noisy one at that.\n\nI have already lost count of the assaults we have endured. The time has come to take the war to the orcs.\n\nFind the SI:7 agents we deployed near their fort. Arendor will provide you with the details of the operation.",o="在克雷博堡外围找到军情七处特工。",oEN="Locate the SI:7 agents in the outskirts of Fort Kerebor.",p="在克雷博尔堡外围找到军情七处特工。",pEN="Sh...",c="<阿伦多尔把一根手指压在唇上，另一只手示意你保持安静。>\n\n光是走到这儿，你就已经闹出够大的动静了。",cEN="<Arendor presses a finger to his lips, using his other hand to signal for you to remain calm.>\n\nYou've already caused enough of a racket just getting here."}
Q[175087]={d="<阿伦多尔最后环视一圈，继续咬着牙说话。>\n\n克雷博。这里曾是人类的堡垒。如今成了兽人滋生的鼠洞。我们跟踪他们好些天了，已经拔掉了几个关键目标；上一次围攻安德拉斯特就是他们的报复。\n\n但如果你想帮军情七处，克雷博还有活儿要干。我这儿有一份名单：\n\n威维尔，马厩主管。\n\n屠夫艾格，在瞭望塔上。\n\n术士卡雷戈，在堡垒后方。\n\n解决掉他们之后，去桥对面向萨玛拉报到。",dEN="<Arendor takes one last look around, continuing to speak through gritted teeth.>\n\nKerebor. Once a human stronghold. Now, an orc-infested rathole. We've been tailing them for days and have already neutralized several key targets; that last siege on Andraste was their retaliation.\n\nBut there is still work to be done in Kerebor, if you're looking to help the SI:7. And I have a list of names:\n\nWeevil, the Stable Master.\n\nButcher Eigor, at the lookout tower.\n\nWarlock Karegor, behind the bastion.\n\nReport to Samara, across the bridge, once you are finished with them.",o="潜入克雷博堡，除掉马厩主管威维尔、屠夫艾格和术士卡雷戈。",oEN="Slip into Fort Kerebor and eliminate Stable Master Weevil, Butcher Eigor, and Warlock Karegor.",p="潜入克雷博尔堡，除掉马厩主管维维尔、屠夫艾格尔和术士卡雷戈尔。",pEN="Arendor sent you, didn't he?",c="我明白了……干得好。顺便说一句，你迟到了；不过迟来总比不来好。\n\n重要的是你来了。",cEN="I see... Well done. Late, by the way; but better late than never.\n\nWhat matters is that you're here."}
Q[175088]={d="兽人的军事策略通常可以概括为「冲上去杀」，但他们的首领——勇士库尔干——扮演的角色远比吼叫命令重要得多：他是把其余人黏合在一起的那层胶。\n\n而我们把他研究得很透。这个时辰，他应该待在指挥室里。几乎独自一人。\n\n别放过这个杀他的机会。哦！还有，记住，我们是军情七处；凡是详细记载他们营地计划的文件，都收起来。\n\n把它们交给桥对面的萨玛拉。",dEN="While orcish military strategy can usually be summed up as 'go and kill,' their leader, Champion Kurgan, serves a far more vital role than simply barking orders: he is the glue that holds the rest of them together.\n\nAnd we've studied him well. At this hour, he should be in the command room. Mostly alone.\n\nDo not let this chance to kill him slip away. Oh! And remember, we are SI:7; gather any documents you find detailing their battalion's plans.\n\nDeliver them to Samara, across the bridge.",o="在克雷博堡的堡垒中杀死黑石勇士库尔干。",oEN="Kill the Blackrock Champion Kurgan in the bastion of Fort Kerebor.",p="在克雷博尔堡的堡垒中杀死黑石勇士库尔干。",pEN="What is that you're carrying? Is it for me?",c="<萨玛拉急切地接过文件。直到读完，她才重新迎上你的目光。她的神情严峻。>\n\n库尔干的死讯我乐于听闻。但这事还没完。远远没完。",cEN="<Samara takes the documents with an anxious gesture. She does not meet your gaze again until she has finished reading them. Her expression is grim.>\n\nI welcome the news of Kurgan's death. But this is not over. Not by a long shot."}
Q[175089]={d="该死。\n\n我们本就怀疑库尔干是听命于他人，这些文件证实了这一点。我们低估了敌人。\n\n库尔干的目的就是尽可能闹出大动静；围攻安德拉斯特要塞，同时让另一队人马打穿暗影井、直扑艾尔文。\n\n伏击者。他们会先扑向北郡谷，然后是金镇，像刽子手的斧头一样落下。\n\n我们得趁还来得及，削减他们的人数。",dEN="Dammit.\n\nWe suspected Kurgan was following someone else's orders, and these documents confirm it. We have underestimated the enemy.\n\nKurgan's objective was to make as much noise as possible; to lay siege to Andraste's Stronghold while another group carved a path through Shadewell toward Elwynn.\n\nAmbushers. They will fall upon Northshire first, and Goldshire next, like a headsman's axe.\n\nWe must thin their ranks before it is too late.",o="击败潜伏在暗影井的黑石伏击者。",oEN="Defeat the Blackrock ambushers lurking within the Shadewell.",p="击败潜伏在影井的黑石伏击者。",pEN="Is it done? I hope you left a few for me.",c="好。这会拖慢他们。至少够我们的警告及时传到北郡了。\n\n这么多暴力……<萨玛拉疲惫地揉着太阳穴。>但它自有其意义：\n\n我们战斗、流血、流汗，是为了让别人不必见识战争的恐怖。是为了让暴风城的人民能安宁地生活。",cEN="Good. That will slow them down. Long enough, at least, for our warning to reach Northshire in time.\n\nSo much violence… <Samara rubs her temples with a weary gesture.> But it serves a purpose:\n\nWe fight, we bleed, and we sweat so that others do not have to know the horrors of war. So that the people of Stormwind may live in peace."}
Q[175090]={d="好。这会拖慢他们。至少能拖到我们的警告及时送到北郡。\n\n这么多暴力……<萨玛拉带着疲惫的神情揉着太阳穴。>但它有其目的：\n\n我们战斗、流血、流汗，是为了让其他人不必经历战争的恐怖。为了让暴风城的人民能安居乐业。",dEN="Like the cockroaches they are, no matter how many orcs we exterminate, more will rise to take their place.\n\nIn any case, a victory is a victory, however modest.\n\nReturn to Andraste. Report to the Commander. I will finish the work on this side of the bridge.",o="回到安德拉斯特要塞向摩尔指挥官复命。",oEN="Return to Commander Moore at Andraste's Fortress.",c="<尽管每隔几秒就要喊叫下令，摩尔指挥官还是专心地听完了你的报告。>\n\n所以他们是要去北郡。\n\n我明白了。\n\n你为我们争取到了时间，<name>。足以避免一场惨剧。\n\n这座要塞感激你。",cEN="<Despite the shouts and orders he barks every few seconds, Commander Moore listens to your report attentively.>\n\nSo they were headed for Northshire.\n\nI see.\n\nYou have bought us time, <name>. Enough to avert a tragedy.\n\nYou have the gratitude of this fortress."}
Q[175091]={d="你好。打扰一下。我叫萨芙莉娜，是要塞里两名书记员之一。我的同僚是个叫达文的矮人。兽人进攻时，他正好出去查看城墙外的废墟了。\n\n而他到现在还没回来。\n\n这里人人都忙得不可开交，外面的黑石攻城器械又……我知道现在不是去找他的好时机，可是……如果您能去，如果您不介意……求您了！\n\n把达文平安带回来给我。",dEN="Hello. Excuse me. My name is Safrina; I'm one of the two scribes here at the fortress. My colleague is a dwarf named Darvin. He had gone out to inspect the ruins beyond the walls when the orcs attacked.\n\nAnd he hasn't returned yet.\n\nEveryone here is far too busy, and with the Blackrock siege engines out there... I know it's not the best time to go looking for him, but... if you can, if you wouldn't mind... Please!\n\nBring Darvin back to me, safe and sound.",o="在要塞城墙外的废墟中寻找达文。",oEN="Find Darvin in the ruins outside the walls of the stronghold.",p="在要塞城墙外的废墟中寻找达文。",pEN="<The dwarf has been hiding here for hours. His face, with wide eyes and a feverish gaze, bears witness to his exhaustion.>",c="你……你不是兽人，对吧？\n\n<达文发出一声震天的叹息，仿佛已经屏住呼吸好几个小时了。>\n\n以我祖先的胡子起誓！我从没这么害怕过！当石头开始乱飞、那些战争号角响起时……我以为他们肯定会找到我。",cEN="You're... you're not an orc, are you?\n\n<Darvin lets out a thunderous sigh, as if he'd been holding his breath for hours.>\n\nBy the beards of my ancestors! I've never been so terrified! When the stones started flying and those war horns sounded... I thought for sure they'd find me."}
Q[175092]={d="听我说。我知道黑石兽人是眼下的威胁，但安德拉斯特不会只面对这一个麻烦太久。\n\n我说的是黑铁矮人。\n\n我不知道他们在谋划什么，但他们以前从未冒险靠得这么近。而且……好吧。您看看四周就知道了。\n\n兽人是可怕的敌人，但这座火山、这一片废墟……都是黑铁的杰作。\n\n想象一下他们还能干出什么。",dEN="Listen. I know the Blackrock orcs are the immediate threat, but they won't be the only problem Andraste faces for much longer.\n\nI'm talking about the Dark Iron dwarves.\n\nI don't know what they're up to, but they've never ventured this close before. And... well. Just look around you.\n\nThe orcs are fearsome foes, but this volcano, all this destruction... that's the handiwork of the Dark Iron.\n\nImagine what they are capable of.",o="击败安德拉斯特要塞附近的黑铁矮人，查明他们的图谋。收集他们的笔记，再拼合起来破译他们的计划。",oEN="Defeat the Dark Iron dwarves near Andraste's Stronghold and uncover their plans. Collect their notes, then piece them together to decipher their plans.",p="击败安德拉斯特要塞附近的黑铁矮人并查明他们的计划。收集他们的笔记，然后拼凑起来破译他们的计划。",pEN="Have you managed to find anything out?",c="这是什么？\n\n达文的目光扫过那些黑铁密信，眉头因愈发担忧而紧锁。\n\n公会。他们自称燃影公会。这么说，他们不是寻常的黑铁。\n\n而这……<La mirada del enano se ensombrece>.\n\n这很令人担忧。",cEN="What have we here?\n\n<Darvin's eyes scan the Dark Iron missives, his brow furrowing with growing concern.>\n\nThe Guild. They call themselves the Shadowburn Guild. So, they aren't your typical Dark Iron, then.\n\nAnd this…<The dwarf's gaze darkens.>\n\nThis is troubling."}
Q[175093]={d="他们是狂信徒。一个教派。而根据我从你带来的文件中整理出的内容，他们信奉危险的念头。\n\n他们想借暗影来束缚火焰。这就像想用添柴来扑灭篝火！\n\n我们得发出警报。得警告摩尔指挥官；不，我在说什么？我们得通知杜恩卡扎德的矮人！\n\n去吧。直接向领主禀报。我和萨芙莉娜回要塞去，把我们查明的这一切都告诉摩尔指挥官。",dEN="They are fanatics. A cult. And from what I've gathered in the documents you brought me, they possess dangerous ideas.\n\nThey seek to bind Fire through Shadow. That is like trying to extinguish a bonfire by tossing more wood onto it!\n\nWe must sound the alarm. Commander Moore must be warned; no, what am I saying? We must alert the dwarves of Dun Kazad!\n\nGo. Inform the Thane directly. I shall return to the fortress with Safrina to explain everything we have uncovered to Commander Moore.",o="向杜恩卡扎德的领主阿扎加·石歌禀报。",oEN="Inform the Thane of Dun Kazad, Azaghal Stonesong.",c="<杜恩卡扎德的领主听你讲述，是耐心还是漠然，无从分辨。>\"\n\n嗯。\n\n在我看来，他们不是我们的问题。一个黑铁教派，妄想把他们氏族从火焰之王的桎梏中解放出来？这股味儿就是内战。\n\n我说，让他们自相残杀去。",cEN="<The Thane of Dun Kazad listens to your tale with either patience or indifference. It is impossible to tell.>\"\n\nHm.\n\nAs I see it, they are not our problem. A Dark Iron cult aspiring to liberate their clan from the Firelord's yoke? It reeks of civil war.\n\nI say let them kill each other."}
Q[175094]={d="<敦卡扎德的族长听你讲述时，态度是耐心还是漠然，无从分辨。>\n\n嗯。\n\n在我看来，他们不是我们的麻烦。一个黑铁矮人教派，妄想把他们氏族从火焰之王的枷锁下解放出来？这闻起来就是内战。\n\n我说，让他们自相残杀去吧。",dEN="Your face is unknown to me, friend. You have chosen dark times to visit us, but perhaps it is no coincidence.\n\nI see the fire of war in your eyes. That word had no place in this valley until very recently. But now, we have need of people like you.\n\nMy dear friend, Meredyl Sunheart, set out into the valley to gather medicinal plants and should have returned by now. The valley has become filled with dangers of late, and I fear the Treants, who have lost their minds for reasons we do not yet understand, may have attacked her.\n\nCould you search for Meredyl? Would you do this favor for us?",o="到鎏金谷寻找梅瑞迪尔·阳心，确保她安然无恙。",oEN="Find Meredyl Sunheart in the Gilded Vale and ensure she is safe.",c="谢谢。我觉得没看上去那么严重。不过是一道抓伤，可疼得像有人把匕首扎进我身体里。\n\n愿圣光赐福埃伦德尔，是他派你来找我。也愿它赐福于你，感谢你伸出援手。\n\n这些小精灵……哎哟！",cEN="Thank you. It's not as bad as it looks, I think. It was barely a scratch, but it hurts as if a dagger had been driven into me.\n\nMay the Light bless Erendel for sending you to find me. And bless you as well, for lending your aid.\n\nThese sprites... Ow!"}
Q[175095]={d="谢谢你。我想没看上去那么糟。只是一道划伤，可疼得像有人把匕首捅进我身体里。\n\n愿圣光祝福派你来找我的埃伦德尔。也祝福你，感谢你伸出援手。\n\n这些鬼灵……哎哟！",dEN="I was gathering medicinal herbs by the river. This valley has always been a haven of peace; a small island of calm in an ocean of death and war. The sprites are usually playful, mischievous at most. But never violent.\n\nI won't be able to gather the remaining herbs in this state. Would you be willing to help me?\n\nThe herb I need only grows in this valley. I named it myself: Belorite. Bring me a generous handful; I will need quite a few to heal the venom in my wound and make the journey back to the Sanctuary.",o="在鎏金谷为梅瑞迪尔·阳心采集贝洛瑞特花。",oEN="Gather Belorite flowers for Meredyl Sunheart in the Gilded Vale.",p="在鎏金谷为梅瑞迪尔·阳心采集贝洛莱特花。",pEN="Do you have the herbs? The venom... it's beginning to spread.",c="你有药草吗？毒……已经开始扩散了。谢谢你，朋友。\n\n别为我担心。我会用你带来的贝洛莱特调制一副膏药，虽然要花点时间。无论如何，我已无性命之忧。\n\n请继续赶你的路吧。别徒劳地留在这里陪我。你帮我的已经超过我能道谢的了。",cEN="This should be more than enough. I thank you, friend.\n\nDo not worry about me. I will prepare a poultice with the Belorite you've brought, though it will take me a while. In any case, I am no longer in danger.\n\nGo on your way, please. Do not linger here uselessly with me. You have already helped me more than I can ever thank you for."}
Q[175096]={d="鎏金谷。在我们的语言里，它另有一个名字：奈恩阿拉。\n\n<阿玛兰瑟呼吸着白色山峰间涌出的清新空气。>\n\n它的美是海市蜃楼：森林正在躁动、不安。它心脏的某处正在变暗。曾经友善的树人变得狂暴而具攻击性。而我的心告诉我，这只是开始。\n\n如果你愿意帮忙，就下到林中去，协助我们安抚在林间小径上游荡的狂怒树人。然后，去寻找考拉诺斯，林地的守护者。他睿智而可敬；如果有人能认出折磨森林的病症，那就是他。",dEN="The Gilded Vale. In our tongue, we know it by another name: Nen'alah.\n\n<Amaranthe breathes in the fresh air exhaled from the white peaks.>\n\nIts beauty is a mirage: the forest is stirring, restless. Something is darkening at its heart. The Treants, once friendly, have become violent and aggressive. And my heart tells me this is only the beginning.\n\nIf you wish to help, descend into the woods and aid us in pacifying the Furious Treants that prowl our paths. Then, seek out Cauranos, Guardian of the Grove. He is wise and venerable; if anyone can recognize the sickness afflicting the forest, it is he.",o="使用纳玛里安水晶安抚狂怒树人，然后寻找考拉诺斯。",oEN="Use the Namarien Crystal to pacify Furious Treants and then find Cauranos.",p="树木的精魂在呼喊。你给它们带来安宁了吗？",pEN="The spirits of the trees are crying out. Have you brought them peace?",c="这么说你来自圣所。阿玛兰瑟女士的直觉没错：森林正在躁动。\n\n血精灵就是原因。他们对山谷魔法的肆意攫取扰乱了平衡。他们带来了那些邪恶的水晶，用它抽干森林的生机。\n\n于是森林反抗了。\n\n危险比你猜想的更大。因为这片森林不只是一片森林。",cEN="So, you come from the Sanctuary. Lady Amaranthe's intuition is correct: the forest is growing restless.\n\nThe Blood Elves are the reason. Their irresponsible consumption of the valley's magic disturbs the balance. They have brought those vile crystals with them and are using them to drain the very life from the woods.\n\nAnd the forest rebels.\n\nThe danger is greater than you suspect. For this forest is not just a forest."}
Q[175097]={d="只要血精灵还在抽取森林的生机，这座山谷就得不到安宁。它的生灵也会充满恶意。不可能有别的结果。\n\n有时，确保和平的唯一方式就是流血。我绝不会向圣所的精灵提出这种要求，但你……你和他们不同。你习惯了暴力。\n\n我就直说了：森林要求那些魔导师去死。他们欠下的债只能用性命来偿还……还有毁掉他们的水晶。",dEN="As long as the Blood Elves continue to drain the vitality of the woods, this valley will know no peace. And its creatures will be filled with malice. It could be no other way.\n\nSometimes, the only way to ensure peace is through the shedding of blood. I would never ask this of the Sanctuary elves, but you... you are different from them. You are accustomed to violence.\n\nI shall be frank: the forest demands the death of the Magisters. They have incurred a debt that can only be paid with their lives... and the destruction of their crystals.",o="杀死血精灵魔导师，摧毁他们在鎏金谷的恶魔水晶。",oEN="Slay the Blood Elf Magisters and destroy their Demonic Crystals in the Gilded Vale.",p="债还清了吗？森林还在流血吗？",pEN="Has the debt been paid? Does the forest still bleed?",c="你感觉到了吗？从峰顶落下的微风，在树间低语。河流奔涌而下的旋律。鸟儿的歌唱。\n\n森林用众声与百音说话。而在每一个声音里，它都在感谢你。",cEN="Do you feel that? The breeze falling from the peaks, whispering through the trees. The melody of the river as it flows downstream. The song of the birds.\n\nThe forest speaks with a chorus of voices and sounds. And in every one of them, it thanks you."}
Q[175098]={d="最先响应森林召唤的，是树妖。她们像山间飞雪般扑向魔导师，却敌不过他们那淫邪的巫术。\n\n许多树妖死了，但有一些仅剩一线生机地逃了出来。我已尽力治愈了能救的，可我的力量不足以帮到所有人。\n\n拿着。<这位庞大的守护者递给你一件形似琥珀水滴的水晶状物件。>用它来治愈你找到的受伤树妖。它会引导森林生机的一小部分；足以把死亡的秃鹫挡在门外。",dEN="Among the first to answer the call of the forest were the Dryads. They fell upon the Magisters like the snow from the mountains, but they were no match for their obscene sorcery.\n\nMany died, but some managed to escape with but a thread of life remaining. I have healed as many as I could, but my powers do not reach far enough to help them all.\n\nHere. <The immense guardian offers you a crystal-like object, resembling a drop of amber.> Use it to heal the wounded Dryads you find. It will channel a fraction of the forest's vitality; it shall be enough to keep death's vultures at bay.",o="使用德鲁伊琥珀治愈鎏金谷中受伤的树妖。",oEN="Use the Druidic Amber to heal the wounded Dryads in the Gilded Vale.",p="树妖们正在消散……你修补好她们的精魂了吗？",pEN="The Dryads are fading... have you managed to mend their spirits?",c="一切生命都珍贵，你救下的每一位树妖都有意义。\n\n你拥有我永恒的感激，<race>。",cEN="All life is precious, and every Dryad you have saved counts.\n\nYou have my immortal gratitude, <race>."}
Q[175099]={d="假以时日，血精灵留下的伤口会结疤，森林会重归平静与沉思般的安宁。\n\n但是……我怀疑这不过是一场牵制。那些魔导师鲁莽、冲动。这很不符合他们那一族的作风。\n\n你看：这片森林不只是一片森林。树木在地下手牵着手；数千年来，它们织成的网络一直隔绝着沉睡在这片土地之下的黑暗。\n\n去吧，跟阿玛兰瑟女士谈谈。把一切都告诉她，并把我的忧虑与她分享。",dEN="In time, the wound left by the Blood Elves will scar over, and the forest will return to peace and contemplative calm.\n\nBut... I suspect this has been nothing more than a distraction. The Magisters have been reckless, impulsive. Something quite unbecoming of their kind.\n\nYou see: this forest is more than just a forest. The trees clasp hands beneath the earth; for millennia, the network they weave has isolated the darkness that slumbers beneath these lands.\n\nGo, speak with Lady Amaranthe. Explain everything, and share my fears with her.",o="回到阿玛兰瑟·奈米尔女士那里，向她警示森林之下的威胁。",oEN="Return to Lady Amaranthe Naemyl and warn her about the threat beneath the forest.",p="在圣所与阿玛兰瑟·奈米尔女士交谈",pEN="Speak with Lady Amaranthe Naemyl at the Sanctuary",c="恐怕考拉诺斯的警告来得太迟了。就在片刻之前，血精灵成功打碎了封印埃尔达亚密室的那些防护法印。\n\n我已派出我最精锐的战士，圣所的精英。但他们还不够。\n\n我们需要你。",cEN="Cauranos's warning comes too late, I fear. Moments ago, the Blood Elves succeeded in shattering the protective sigils that sealed the Chambers of Erdaya.\n\nI have sent my finest warriors, the elite of the Sanctuary. But they will not be enough.\n\nWe need you."}
Q[175100]={d="埃尔达亚密室是万古之前由如今连尘埃都不如的双手开凿出来的。它们像迷宫一样在森林之下延伸；实际上，它们只是一座庞大得多的泰坦建筑的表面。\n\n一个黑暗难以名状的生物的牢狱。\n\n圣所脚下的湖泊藏着唯一的入口。我们需要你的帮助。如果血精灵冒了这么大的风险，那说明他们的野心同样巨大。他们没安好心。\n\n找到那处水下入口，深入埃尔达亚密室。",dEN="The Chambers of Erdaya were excavated eons ago by hands that are less than dust. They stretch out like a labyrinth beneath the forest; in truth, they are but the surface of a much vaster Titanic complex.\n\nThe prison of a creature of unspeakable darkness.\n\nThe lake at the foot of the Sanctuary hides the only entrance. We need your help. If the Blood Elves have risked so much, it is because their ambitions were equally grand. They are up to no good.\n\nFind the submerged entrance and venture into the Chambers of Erdaya.",o="潜入圣殿下方的湖泊，找到水下的入口，进入 Erdaya 之厅。",oEN="Dive into the lake beneath the Sanctuary, find the submerged entrance, and enter the Chambers of Erdaya.",p="他们……他们到处都是……",pEN="They... they were everywhere...",c="那是个陷阱。他们杀光了所有人……怎么可能有这么多混进外交随行人员里？我早该察觉的。我早该……！\n\n<一阵剧烈的咳嗽打断了这位黑暗游侠。她胸口的伤口渗出一种黑色的液体，看上去极为污秽。>\n\n他们是一个邪教。我记得他们自称The Family。我试图阻止他们，但差点落得和你的圣殿女主人派来的那些战士一样的下场。和其他所有人一样的下场……",cEN="It was a trap. They killed everyone... How could so many have infiltrated the diplomatic retinue? I should have realized. I should have...!\n\n<A coughing fit interrupts the Dark Ranger. The wound on her chest bleeds a black liquid that looks very foul indeed.>\n\nThey are a cult. They call themselves The Family, I believe. I tried to stop them, but I nearly suffered the same fate as the warriors sent by your Sanctuary's lady. The same fate as all the others..."}
Q[175101]={d="仔细听我说。\n\n<那位黑暗游侠在呻吟与喘息间断断续续地说着。她剩下的时间不多了。>\n\n那些疯子……我不知道他们在图谋什么，我也不需要知道。必须阻止他们。\n\n<她咬紧牙关。双眼像两颗残酷的宝石般燃烧。>\n\n若我还有力气，我会亲手处理他们。总得有人为他们的罪行付出代价。他们背叛了部落。背叛了他们的王国。他们杀光了营地里的所有人。大使。他的随从。护卫。全都死了……\n\n以眼还眼，我说。趁还来得及，把他们全杀了。",dEN="Listen to me carefully.\n\n<The Dark Ranger speaks through grunts and gasps. She hasn't much time left.>\n\nThose lunatics... I don't know what they are after, and I don't need to. They must be stopped.\n\n<She clenches her teeth. Her eyes burn like two cruel jewels.>\n\nI would deal with them myself if I had the strength. Someone must make them pay for their crimes. They have betrayed the Horde. Their kingdom. They killed everyone in the camp. The ambassador. His assistants. The escort. All dead...\n\nAn eye for an eye, I say. Kill them all before it is too late.",o="杀死 Erdaya 之厅内 The Family 的邪教徒。",oEN="Slay the cultists of The Family within the Chambers of Erdaya.",p="结束了吗？空气里是否弥漫着他们失败的恶臭？",pEN="Is it done? Is the air thick with the scent of their failure?",c="我听见了他们的惨叫。\n\n我听见了他们的惨叫……",cEN="I heard them scream.\n\nI heard them scream..."}
Q[175102]={d="这场骚乱的首领是一个叫 Tharion 的人。我至今仍难以相信；就在几天前，他还假装自己只是另一个书记员。那是他的伪装。\n\n他究竟在密谋什么并不重要。必须阻止他。若在别的情况下，我会亲自加入追捕。我会确保将他活捉，严刑拷打，榨出最后一丝情报。\n\n但我们没有时间。\n\n杀了他就够了。\n\n不过……让他受尽折磨。",dEN="The leader of this rabble is a man named Tharion. I still find it hard to believe; until a few days ago, he feigned being just another scribe. It was his cover.\n\nIt doesn't matter what exactly he is plotting. He must be stopped. In other circumstances, I would join the hunt myself. I would make sure to capture him alive and torture him to extract every last drop of information.\n\nBut we have no time.\n\nKilling him will suffice.\n\nHowever... make him suffer.",o="在 Erdaya 之厅的深处迎战族长 Tharion，终结他的疯狂。",oEN="Confront Patriarch Tharion in the depths of the Chambers of Erdaya and end his madness.",p="这个地方的阴影终于消散了吗？",pEN="Is the shadow finally lifted from this place?",c="所以那是个邪教。真可惜。这会让我国与血精灵的关系变得复杂。而且，毫无疑问会同时引起部落和联盟的猜疑。\n\nNen'alah 从未见过这样的暴行。我们也从未为如此多的同胞哀悼过。\n\n但危险已经过去，山谷重获生机。假以时日，森林会痊愈；我们也会痊愈。而 Namarien 圣殿将再次听到欢笑与歌声。",cEN="So, it was a cult. A pity. This will complicate our relations with the Blood Elves. And certainly, it will rouse the suspicion of both the Horde and the Alliance.\n\nNen'alah has never seen such violence. And we have never had to mourn so many of our own.\n\nBut the danger has passed, and the valley breathes. In time, the forest will heal; we will heal. And the Namarien Sanctuary will hear laughter and songs once more."}
Q[175103]={d="把你引到这里的那件事，降临在那个人类村庄矿工身上的诅咒，我并没有忘记。\n\n山谷正在痊愈，我的力量也在增长。你对我们的帮助比你能想象的更多。我理应回报这份恩情。\n\n收下这份礼物。\n\n<精灵把一粒种子放进你手中，它看起来就像一块金锭。>\n\n这是我故乡 Quel'Thalas 的纪念物；是一朵曾生长在如今已失落的 Sunwell 旁的花的种子，它至今仍保留着微光。把它交给那些矿工；叫他们把它种在矿场附近。\n\n当它绽放时，诅咒便会消散。",dEN="The matter that brought you here, the curse that fell upon the miners of that human village, I have not forgotten it.\n\nThe valley heals, and my power grows. You have helped us more than you imagine. It is only right that I return the favor.\n\nAccept this gift.\n\n<The elf places a seed in your hand that resembles a golden nugget.>\n\nA memento of my homeland, Quel'Thalas; the seed of a flower that grew near the now-lost Sunwell, and it still retains its glow. Deliver it to the miners; tell them to bury it near the mine.\n\nWhen it blooms, the curse will fade.",o="把受祝福的金色种子带到采矿村庄的 Alto Bilberg，并把它种在矿场附近。",oEN="Take the Blessed Golden Seed to Alto Bilberg in the mining village and plant it near the mine.",p="<Alto Bilberg 嗅了嗅你。>\n\n药？你……带药来？好久……好久没见了！",pEN="<Alto Bilberg sniffs you.>\n\nMedicine? You… bring medicine? Much time has passed!",c="你！你，来这里！\n\n这是什么？\n\n<Alto Bilberg 嗅了嗅那粒种子。起初那股气味似乎令他退避，接着他的瞳孔却放大了。>\n\n种下？这个治病？不是巫术。别的魔法。更强。\n\n花……我喜欢花。",cEN="You. You here!\n\nWhat be this?\n\n<Alto Bilberg sniffs the seed. Though the scent seems to repel him at first, his pupils dilate.>\n\nWe plant? This heal? Not witch magic. Different magic. Stronger.\n\nFlower... Me like flowers."}
Q[175104]={d="失去 Sunwell 之后随之而来的魔法之渴是一种可怕的命运。血精灵采取了绝望的手段；在我们看来，那在道德上是错误的。而我们高等精灵……嗯，我们想出了无数种补救之法。\n\n对一些人而言，答案在于冥想与自律。对另一些人而言，答案则是与森林建立一种共生的关系。\n\n这是一片特别的森林，你知道吗？从中涌出的力量能包裹并升华灵魂。我们从不多取森林未曾自愿给予之物；我只不过是从落在地上的松果里提取魔法。\n\n如果你在树林间漫步，就采些松果带给我吧。",dEN="The thirst for magic that followed the fall of the Sunwell is a terrible fate. The Blood Elves took desperate measures; morally wrong, in our judgment. We, the High Elves... well, we have developed a myriad of remedies.\n\nFor some, the answer lies in meditation and discipline. For others, the solution involves a symbiotic relationship with the forest.\n\nIt is a special forest, you know? A power emanates from it that envelops and uplifts the spirit. We never take more than what the forest gives freely; I limit myself to extracting magic from the pinecones that fall to the ground.\n\nIf you wander among the trees, gather a few pinecones and bring them to me, please.",o="在金色山谷的森林地面上采集附魔松果，并带给 Celedorn。",oEN="Gather Enchanted Pinecones from the forest floor in the Gilded Vale and bring them to Celedorn.",p="你找到什么了吗？",pEN="Were you able to find any?",c="你感觉得到吗？虽然很微弱，但每一颗松果都像心脏一样跳动，里面蕴含着森林沉睡的魔法。\n\n要从它们内部提取魔法，需要耐心、细心和极为精细的手法。\n\n给我一点时间，我演示给你看。",cEN="Do you feel it? Though subtle, each pinecone pulses like a heart with the latent magic of the forest.\n\nIt requires patience, care, and a great deal of finesse to extract the magic they hold within.\n\nGive me a moment and I shall show you."}
Q[175105]={d="拿着。看好了。\n\n<Celedorn 用双手操纵着一簇能量火花。片刻之后，他把那股能量倾倒在桌上的面包上。>\n\n只需一口，就足以安抚灵魂，让人重获新生。当然，也能满足更实际意义上的饥饿。\n\n你愿意行行好，把它分给圣殿的居民们吗？",dEN="Here. Observe.\n\n<Celedorn manipulates a spark of energy with his hands. A moment later, he pours that energy over the bread on the table.>\n\nA single bite is enough to soothe the spirit and breathe new life into one. And to satisfy hunger in a more physical sense, of course.\n\nWould you be so kind as to distribute it among the inhabitants of the sanctuary?",o="把 Celedorn 的附魔面包分发给 Namarien 圣殿的居民。",oEN="Distribute Celedorn's Enchanted Bread to the inhabitants of Namarien Sanctuary.",p="大家都吃过了吗？希望这面包能给他们带来些许慰藉。",pEN="Has everyone been fed? I hope the bread brought them some comfort.",c="你拥有我的感激，以及整个圣殿的感激。\n\n请收下这个，作为给你添麻烦的补偿。并请放心离去：Namarien 圣殿永远欢迎你。",cEN="You have my gratitude, and that of the sanctuary.\n\nPlease, accept this as compensation for your trouble. And depart with the certainty that you will always be welcome in Namarien Sanctuary."}
Q[175106]={d="你和别人不一样。我是说，和这座圣殿里的精灵不一样。\n\n我来自 Graysky。一项正式任务，由 Draewyn 爵士亲自签署。也许你能帮上忙？\n\n最近我们得知，在这座圣殿以北、Kharadol 桥下，有一个 Ealdir 营地。Ealdir 是一场瘟疫，考虑到 Graysky 正与巨魔们纠缠不清，他们只会让事情变得更棘手。\n\n把那个营地清干净，好吗？你知道我说\"清干净\"是什么意思，对吧？\n\n报酬不会让你失望。",dEN="You aren't like the others. Like the elves of this sanctuary, I mean.\n\nI come from Graysky. An official mission, signed by Sir Draewyn himself. Perhaps you can help?\n\nRecently, we've learned of an Ealdir camp located north of this sanctuary, beneath Kharadol Bridge. The Ealdir are a plague, and considering the troubles Graysky is facing with the trolls, they are only making things more difficult.\n\nClear the camp, will you? You know what I mean by 'clear,' right?\n\nThe reward will be worth it.",o="清剿圣殿以北 Kharadol 桥下的 Ealdir 营地。",oEN="Clear the Ealdir camp located beneath Kharadol Bridge, north of the Sanctuary.",p="告诉我活儿干完了。",pEN="Tell me the job is done.",c="他们全都……？你懂的。<Daendor 用拇指在脖子上一划，然后发出一个滑稽的声音，把舌头伸向一边。>\n\n好，好。没错。啊……\n\n<一阵突如其来的悲伤攫住了他。他的肩膀塌了下来。>\n\n不，不。我没事。只是……既然你已经解决了 Ealdir，我就没有理由再留下了。而我不想离开 Namarien 圣殿。我不想回 Graysky。",cEN="Are they all...? You know. <Daendor makes a gesture with his thumb across his neck. Then he makes a funny sound and sticks his tongue out to the side.>\n\nGood, good. Yes. Ah...\n\n<A sudden sadness washes over him. His shoulders slump.>\n\nNo, no. I'm fine. It's just that... now that you've dealt with the Ealdir, I have no reason to stay. And I don't want to leave Namarien Sanctuary. I don't want to go back to Graysky."}
Q[175107]={d="<Draewyn 爵士朝你点头致意，随后指向桌上那堆文件。>\n\n报告。你的名字出现在其中大多数里。你赢得了我的尊敬。甚至还有我的信任。\n\n我还有最后一项任务交给你。\n\n<Draewyn 爵士压低了声音。>\n\n几天前，Rockrend 村遭到 Ealdir 的残暴袭击。我们正在调查，但看来他们没有留下任何活口。我要你去那里看看，替我观察并打探当地的动静。\n\n去找游侠 Thandel 报到。尽你所能协助他。",dEN="<Sir Draewyn greets you with a nod. Then, he gestures toward the pile of documents resting on the table.>\n\nReports. Your name appears in most of them. You have earned my respect. My trust, even.\n\nI have one last mission for you.\n\n<Sir Draewyn lowers his voice.>\n\nA few days ago, the village of Rockrend fell victim to a brutal Ealdir attack. We are investigating it, but it doesn't seem they left anyone alive. I want you to visit the site and be my eyes and ears in the area.\n\nReport to Ranger Thandel. Help him in any way you can.",o="前往 Rockrend 的废墟，向游侠 Thandel 报到，一同调查 Ealdir 的袭击。",oEN="Travel to the ruins of Rockrend and report to Ranger Thandel to investigate the Ealdir attack.",c="你就是 Draewyn 爵士信任的<man/woman>吧？\n\n欢迎来到 Rockrend，我想。灾祸降临之前，我来过这个村子不止一次。他们总给我居家恋乡的印象。",cEN="You're Sir Draewyn's trusted <man/woman>, aren't you?\n\nWelcome to Rockrend, I suppose. I visited this village more than once before misfortune befell it. They always seemed like homebody folk to me."}
Q[175108]={d="村子成了鬼村。我的士兵？被屠戮殆尽。但原本住在这里的人……啊，问题就在这儿。他们怎么样了？\n\n我告诉你我的看法：Ealdir 尽可能多地掳走了人。目的为何，我不知道，但我的人发现了一条通往矿场的踪迹。而且我怀疑，Ealdir 打过来时，不止一个灵魂试图躲进那些坑道。\n\n彻底搜一遍。从地面到地底。每一条矿脉、每一个竖井、每一道该死的裂缝。我拿我的胡子打赌，里面还有活人。",dEN="The village is a ghost town. My soldiers? Butchered. But the folk who lived here... ah, there's the rub. What has become of them?\n\nI'll tell you what I believe: the Ealdir abducted as many people as they could. To what end, I do not know, but my men have found a trail leading to the mine. And I suspect more than one soul tried to go to ground in those tunnels when the Ealdir came knocking.\n\nScour it. From top to bottom. Every vein, every shaft, every gods-forsaken crevice. I'll stake my beard there's still a survivor left inside.",o="在矿场深处搜寻任何可能从 Ealdir 袭击中幸存下来的村民。",oEN="Search the depths of the mine for any villagers who might have survived the Ealdir onslaught.",p="退后！",pEN="Stay back!",c="你不是他们的人……感谢众灵！\n\n我们就是仅剩的人了；都是跑得够快、从 Ealdir 指缝里溜出来的人。\n\n现在……现在离开安全吗？",cEN="You're not one of them... Spirits be praised!\n\nWe're all that's left; those of us quick enough to slip through the Ealdir's fingers.\n\nIs it... Is it safe to leave now?"}
Q[175109]={d="通往矿场的那条踪迹是单向的；换句话说，进去的人从没出来过。\n\n幸存者？那正是我的希望。但他们是被猎杀的，这一点我确信。而且在我看来，当时紧咬他们脚跟的那些生物仍在那些坑道里游荡。\n\n我不知道你会在里面遇到什么，但做好最坏的准备。任何挡在你面前的东西……都送它下地狱。",dEN="The trail leading to the mine is one-way; in other words, whoever went in never came out.\n\nSurvivors? That is my hope. But they were hunted, of that I am certain. And it seems to me that the creatures snapping at their heels are still prowling those tunnels.\n\nI do not know what you will find in there, but prepare for the worst. And whatever crosses your path... send it to hell.",o="在矿场中搜寻幸存者，并消灭你遇到的一切威胁。",oEN="Investigate the mine for survivors and eliminate any threats you encounter.",p="现在……现在离开安全吗？",pEN="Is it... Is it safe to leave now?",c="<那个女人形销骨立：头发乱成一团，衣服破烂不堪；双脚发黑，血迹斑斑。她看上去几乎就像个 Ealdir。>\n\n你把那些怪物解决掉了吗？那我们就该比怕他们更怕你。你……你是站在我们这边的，对吧？",cEN="<The woman cuts a haggard figure: her hair is a tangled mess, her clothes tattered and torn; her feet are blackened and bloodied. She almost looks like an Ealdir herself.>\n\nHave you finished off those monsters? Then we should fear you even more than them. Are you... you are on our side, right?"}
Q[175110]={d="我……我希望能帮上更多忙。Ealdir 是夜里来的。他们像山上的落石一样砸向我们。他们带走了所有人。到处是惨叫。他们屠杀了士兵。也杀了一些村民……\n\n我没时间思考。我只是跑。我拼命地跑，能多快就多快。其他人跟着我。接着那些生物就扑了上来。\n\n但他们不敢深入矿场。他们不敢追我追到这里。\n\nEaldir 在密谋什么。一件大事。否则，他们不会费这么大力气活捉我们。",dEN="I... I wish I could be of more help. The Ealdir came by night. They fell upon us like a rockslide from the mountains. They took everyone. There were screams. They slaughtered the soldiers. Some of the villagers, too...\n\nI had no time to think. I just ran. I ran as far as I could, as fast as I could. Others followed me. And then those creatures were upon us.\n\nBut they didn't dare venture so deep into the mine. They didn't dare follow me this far.\n\nThe Ealdir are plotting something. Something big. Otherwise, they wouldn't have gone to such lengths to take us alive.",o="向 Thandel 报告矿场里发生的事。",oEN="Report what happened in the mine to Thandel.",c="正如我怀疑的。你说有多少人躲在矿场里？\n\n<Thandel 眯起眼睛，缓缓摇头，眉头紧锁。>\n\n这么少。太少了。就算我们能救回他们掳走的每一个灵魂，这个村子也永远无法从这样的打击中恢复。",cEN="As I suspected, then. How many did you say were hiding in the mine?\n\n<Thandel narrows his eyes and shakes his head slowly, his brow furrowed.>\n\nSo few. Far too few. This village will never recover from such a blow, even if we manage to save every soul they abducted."}
Q[175111]={d="现在不是绝望的时候。如果 Ealdir 需要这些人活着，那我们还来得及。我们还能行动。\n\n我会确保这个消息传到 Graysky。但在我的人侦察完村子之前，我要你出发去找 Laurelin 和 Telperion 的营地。\n\n他们是我们最优秀的。和我一样，他们被派来调查 Rockrend 的失踪案，但他们深入了森林更深处。到这时候，我敢打赌他们已经查到了有用的东西。\n\n我会在地图上标出他们的位置。",dEN="Now is no time to lose hope. If the Ealdir needed these people alive, then we still have time. We can still act.\n\nI will see that this information reaches Graysky. But while my men finish scouting the village, I want you to head out and find Laurelin and Telperion's camp.\n\nThey are our best. Like me, they were tasked with investigating the disappearances at Rockrend, but they pushed further into the woods. By now, I'll wager they've turned up something useful.\n\nI'll mark their location on your map.",o="在森林中寻找 Laurelin 和 Telperion 的营地。",oEN="Find Laurelin and Telperion's camp within the woods.",c="啊，一张友善的面孔！圣光作证，要是再和 Telperion 待上一天，我非掐死他不可，哪怕只为让他那张脸松弛一回；他一整天都皱着眉。\n\n说说，你叫什么名字？是那个矮个子派你来的，对吧？你在 Rockrend 查到什么了吗？\n\n恐怕我们没什么进展。我们完全不知道俘虏被带去了哪里，也不知道为什么。",cEN="Ah, a friendly face! Light knows, one more day with Telperion and I'd have strangled him, if only to get him to relax his face for once; he's been scowling all day.\n\nTell me, what's your name? The short one sent you, didn't he? Have you turned up anything in Rockrend?\n\nI'm afraid we haven't made much headway. We've no idea where the captives were taken, nor why."}
Q[175112]={d="这一带，也就是 Scadeald 冢岩，是 Ealdir 领地的核心。他们的村庄还很远，但要开出一条通往那里的路，我们得先解决在 Braicag Heights 一带游荡的 Ealdir。\n\n少一个 Ealdir，就少一个要操心的敌人。\n\n沿着盘山小径走上去，削减他们的数量。为了 Graysky！为了 Scadeald！也为了他们所有人。",dEN="This region, the Scadeald Barrow-Crags, is the heart of Ealdir territory. Their villages are still a long way off, but to carve a path to them, we must first deal with the Ealdir prowling Braicag Heights.\n\nOne less Ealdir is one less enemy to worry about.\n\nFollow the path that winds up the mountainside and thin their ranks. For Graysky! For Scadeald! And all that lot.",o="在 Braicag Heights 击败 Ealdir。",oEN="Defeat the Ealdir at Braicag Heights.",p="清剿进行得怎么样？",pEN="How is the cull coming along?",c="希望你已经让几颗丑陋的脑袋搬了家。\n\n很好。Ealdir 会学会畏惧你——如果他们还不曾畏惧的话。",cEN="I hope you've sent a few of those ugly heads rolling.\n\nGood. The Ealdir will learn to fear you, if they don't already."}
Q[175113]={d="尽管 Ealdir 比任何人都了解这些森林，但若没有驻扎在 Braicag Heights 瞭望塔上的哨兵，他们也无法守住冢岩的边界。\n\n如果有人说，比如，把那座塔炸上天……那我们其余人推进 Ealdir 领地、处理剩下的事就会容易得多。\n\n我说的是\"有人\"，但显然，我心里想的是像你这样的人。\n\n拿着这些炸药。把它们安放在塔基处。然后在引爆之前，用你双腿能跑出的最快速度跑远。",dEN="Though the Ealdir know these woods better than anyone, they couldn't secure the borders of the Barrow-Crags without the lookouts stationed at the Braicag Heights watchtower.\n\nIf someone were to, say, blow that tower to kingdom come... it would be much easier for the rest of us to push into Ealdir territory and handle the rest.\n\nI said 'someone,' but obviously, I had you in mind.\n\nTake these explosive charges. Plant them at the base of the tower. And get away as fast as your legs can carry you before they go off.",o="使用 Laurelin 的炸药摧毁 Braicag Heights 的瞭望塔。",oEN="Use Laurelin's Explosive Charges to destroy the Braicag Heights watchtower.",p="喜欢烟花，是吧？",pEN="Fond of fireworks, are you?",c="我们从这儿就听到了爆炸声。你还能看见烟雾从树梢间升起。\n\n干得好。",cEN="We heard the blast from here. You can still see the smoke rising through the trees.\n\nFine work."}
Q[175114]={d="根据 Telperion 和我查到的消息，Braicag Heights 的 Ealdir 听命于一个叫酋长 Saidarn 的暴君。\n\n杀几个 Ealdir 对一个赢得过 Draewyn 爵士尊敬的人来说算不了什么挑战；炸一座瞭望塔也一样。可是击败冢岩最血腥的首领之一……没错，那似乎更合你的胃口。\n\n杀了酋长 Saidarn。他的死会给所有追随他的 Ealdir，以及其他部族的酋长，传递一个明确的信号。",dEN="From what Telperion and I have gathered, the Ealdir of Braicag Heights answer to a despot known as Chieftain Saidarn.\n\nSlaying a few Ealdir won't be much of a challenge for someone who has earned Sir Draewyn's respect; nor will blowing a watchtower. Defeating one of the bloodiest leaders in the Barrow-Crags, however... Yes, that seems more your speed.\n\nKill Chieftain Saidarn. His death will send a clear message to all the Ealdir who followed him, and to the chieftains of the other tribes.",o="在 Braicag Heights 击败酋长 Saidarn",oEN="Defeat Chieftain Saidarn in Braicag Heights",p="那个混蛋断气了吗？",pEN="Has the bastard ceased to breath?",c="你杀了他？圣光在上，你真的杀了他！\n\n<Laurelin 热情地拥抱了你。>\n\n他死了之后，Braicag Heights 的 Ealdir 就再也不会对我们的人构成威胁了。你知道他们怎么说：死狗……\n\n不咬人。",cEN="You killed him? By the Light, you actually killed him!\n\n<Laurelin embraces you enthusiastically.>\n\nWith him gone, the Ealdir of Braicag Heights will no longer pose a threat to our men. You know what they say: dead dogs...\n\nCan't bite."}
Q[175115]={d="Thandel。Rockrend。对，我全都听说了。\n\n既然你已经来了，我有件事需要帮忙：Ealdir 修习的魔法，与我们卡多雷数千年来修习的德鲁伊之道有许多共通之处。然而，Ealdir 融入了某种黑暗的元素；一个打破自然和谐的不谐之音。\n\n我必须研究它，理解它。就从他们的符文开始。\n\n在 Cair Cragg 村附近，大地裂开成一道峡谷，Ealdir 在那里刻下了许多巨石碑。找到并带给我那些刻有符文的碎石，好让我研究它们散发的魔法。",dEN="Thandel. Rockrend. Yes, I have heard it all.\n\nSince you are already here, I require assistance with something: the magic practiced by the Ealdir shares much with the druidism we Kaldorei have practiced for millennia. Yet, the Ealdir incorporate a dark element; a note of discord that shatters the natural harmony.\n\nI must study it, understand it. Starting with their runes.\n\nNear the village of Cair Cragg, the earth splits into a canyon where the Ealdir have carved numerous monoliths. Find and bring me the pebbles inscribed with runes, so that I may study the magic they exude.",o="在 Cair Cragg 附近的巨石碑上收集符文碎石。",oEN="Gather runic pebbles from the monoliths near Cair Cragg.",p="你已经取回那些石头了吗？",pEN="Have you recovered the stones yet?",c="Ealdir 的符文起着锚点的作用。通过它们，他们引导从自己土地上自然流淌而出的魔法。一种黑暗的、被污染的魔法。\n\n答案长期以来一直躲着我，但我相信，通过研究你带来的这些符文石，我会对这道阴影的本质获得不止一点洞见。\n\n你拥有我的感激。",cEN="The runes of the Ealdir act as anchors. Through them, they channel the magic that flows naturally from their land. A dark magic, tainted.\n\nThe answer has eluded me for a long time, but I believe I shall gain more than one insight into the nature of this shadow by studying the runestones you have brought me.\n\nYou have my gratitude."}
Q[175116]={d="在我们所在位置的东南方，深藏于森林的岩壁之间，坐落着 Ealdir 的村庄 Cair Cragg，那里是女巫 Bagga Darma 的家。\n\n我已经与她的魔法周旋了一段时间。她派出害虫、诅咒和阴影来折磨我们。我尽我所能地防御，呼唤森林的力量与女神的庇佑。\n\n你的援助或许能让天平向我们倾斜。\n\n去找到 Cair Cragg，找到 Bagga Darma。你很可能会发现她已被自己邪恶的巫术吞噬。利用这一点；出其不意，终结她可悲的存在。",dEN="To the southeast of our position, tucked away among the crags deep within the forest, lies the Ealdir village of Cair Cragg, home to the witch Bagga Darma.\n\nI have been contending with her magic for some time now. She sends vermin, curses, and shadows to torment us. I defend us as best I can, invoking the power of the forest and the protection of the Goddess.\n\nYour aid could tip the scales in our favor.\n\nSeek out Cair Cragg and find Bagga Darma. You will likely find her consumed by her vile sorcery. Use that to your advantage; take her by surprise and put an end to her wretched existence.",o="在 Cair Cragg 村找到并击败女巫 Bagga Darma。",oEN="Find and defeat the witch Bagga Darma in the village of Cair Cragg.",p="Bagga Darma 必须死。",pEN="Bagga Darma must die.",c="女巫死了。对，我感觉到了；就像一副重担变轻了，或者一种疼痛变得更容易忍受了。\n\n不再有噩梦了。不再有夜惊。不再有偏执妄想。\n\n我终于可以专注于我真正来这里要做的事了。",cEN="The witch is dead. Yes, I felt it; like a burden becoming lighter, or a pain made easier to bear.\n\nNo more nightmares, then. No more night-terrors. No more paranoia.\n\nAt last, I can focus on what I truly came here to do."}
Q[175117]={d="随着 Braicag Heights 的 Ealdir 被击溃、他们的酋长被杀、Cair Cragg 的女巫被处以刀剑，通往冢岩主村 Baile Escada 的道路已经敞开。\n\n仔细听好：\n\n如果说有哪个地方能让你查出 Ealdir 如何处置 Rockrend 的俘虏，那就是那里。\n\n我亲手给这枚护身符施了变形术。激活它，它会把你变成一只猫，让你溜进 Baile Escada，在居民之间徘徊而不引起怀疑。尽可能了解他们的谋划。最重要的是，查明他们打算如何处置那些被掳走的人。",dEN="With the Ealdir of Braicag Heights routed, their chieftain slain, and the witch of Cair Cragg put to the sword, the path to Baile Escada, the primary village of the Barrow-Crags, lies open.\n\nListen closely:\n\nIf there is one place where you might uncover what the Ealdir have done with the captives of Rockrend, it is there.\n\nI have enchanted this amulet myself with a metamorphosis dweomer. Activate it, and it shall transform you into a cat, allowing you to slip into Baile Escada and prowl among its inhabitants without raising suspicion. Learn all you can of their designs. And above all, find out what they intend for those they have abducted.",o="使用 Telperion 的猫形护身符潜入 Baile Escada，查明 Ealdir 的计划。",oEN="Use Telperion's Feline Amulet to infiltrate Baile Escada and uncover the Ealdir's plans.",p="<Deirdre 似乎忙着自己的事，连看都懒得看你一眼。>",pEN="<Deirdre seems far too busy with her own business to spare you a glance.>",c="<Deirdre 长着长得不可思议的指甲的双手抓了抓你的肋侧，又抚过你的额头。>\n\n乖猫，对，就是这样。多漂亮的小猫咪。\n\n是什么把你带到我的小屋来的，嗯？让我猜猜！你想让我吐露我们的计划？我们最黑暗、最美味的秘密。你会喜欢的，对吧，小花瓣？\n\n<Deirdre 发出一阵残酷的大笑。>\n\n愚蠢的<boy/girl>。你以为这么粗糙的咒语能骗得了我？来吧，别演戏了。你我面对面地谈谈。",cEN="<Deirdre's hands, tipped with impossibly long nails, scratch your flank and caress your brow.>\n\nGood cat, yes indeed. Such a fine little puss.\n\nWhat has brought you to my shack, hm? Let me guess! You want me to spill our plans? Our darkest, most delicious secrets. You'd like that, wouldn't you, petal?\n\n<Deirdre cackles with cruel laughter.>\n\nFoolish <boy/girl>. Did you think such a crude spell could deceive me? Come now, let's dispense with the theatrics. Let us speak face to face, you and I."}
Q[175118]={d="当 Rockrend 出事的传言传到我耳中时，我就知道冲突叩响 Baile Escada 的大门只是时间问题。因为你是来查那些绑架案的，对吧？\n\n是的，我知道 Rockrend 的人被关在哪里。我也确切知道我的亲族打算怎么处置他们。\n\n仔细听好，亲爱的；也许你还来得及救他们。",dEN="When rumors of the happenings in Rockrend reached my ears, I knew it was only a matter of time before the conflict came knocking at the gates of Baile Escada. For you've come to sniff out those abductions, haven't you?\n\nYes, I know where the folk of Rockrend are being kept. And I know exactly what my kin intend to do with them.\n\nListen closely, darling; it may be that you're still in time to save them.",o="与 Deirdre 交谈，查明 Rockrend 那些人的命运。",oEN="Speak with Deirdre to discover the fate of the people of Rockrend.",p="听好了，听好了。",pEN="Listen, listen.",c="根植之影。光是大声说出它的名字，就会让阳光枯萎。\n\n我会帮你把那些可怜的灵魂从献祭祭坛上救下来。但如果我们要阻止 Morgwena，我们自己也得准备好牺牲一切、赌上一切。",cEN="The Rooted Shadow. Merely speaking its name aloud makes the very sunlight wither.\n\nI shall help you save those poor souls from the sacrificial altar. But, if we are to stop Morgwena, we too must be prepared to sacrifice, and to risk, everything."}
Q[175119]={d="Ealdir 追随 Morgwena，是出于习惯与恐惧。但若有人能证明她的魔法并非万无一失，这一点或许就会改变。\n\n在 Baile Escada 附近，也就是我们上方的那座山丘上，Morgwena 留下了一些她的Hushed；那些因违抗而付出代价、被变成无心智傀儡的 Ealdir。\n\n去面对他们。击碎他们的面具，打破禁锢他们的附魔。他们的解放，将像几块小石头的滚落引发山间雪崩。",dEN="The Ealdir follow Morgwena out of habit and fear. But that might change if someone were to prove that her magic is fallible.\n\nNear Baile Escada, on the hill above us, Morgwena left behind some of her 'Hushed'; Ealdir who paid the price of disobedience by being turned into mindless puppets.\n\nFace them. Shatter their masks and break the enchantment that holds them prisoner. Their liberation will be like the falling of small stones that starts an avalanche in the mountains.",o="在 Baile Escada 上方的山丘上击碎面具，解放 Morgwena 的 Hushed。",oEN="Free Morgwena's Hushed by shattering their masks on the hill above Baile Escada.",p=" 你已经把那面具砸得粉碎了，还是看到它们就吓破了胆？",pEN="Have you smashed those masks to bits yet, or did you lose your nerve at the sight of them?",c="我们是怎样破除压在那些 Ealdir 身上的诅咒的，消息已经传开了。他们看见你从我的小屋里出来，所以他们认为那是我们干的：我的魔法加上你的蛮力。\n\n要是他们知道只要砸碎面具就够了……不过我更喜欢这样；让他们怕我们。",cEN="Word has spread of how we broke the curse weighing upon those Ealdir. They saw you leave my shack, so they believe it was our doing: my magic and your brawn.\n\nIf only they knew that shattering the masks was enough... But I like it better this way; let them fear us."}
Q[175120]={d="要活着通过守护 Morgwena 小屋的附魔，我们需要两样东西：\n\n<Deirdre 把一枚骨制护身符放进你手中。>\n\n这个。还有巨鹿的祝福。\n\n曾经，巨鹿是 Morgwena 的守护神，但很久以前她背弃了对他的崇拜，转而投向根植之影。\n\n去山丘顶上的祭坛，向图腾致以敬意。在 Morgwena 对他所做的一切之后，我猜巨鹿之灵会非常乐意赐予我们他的恩惠。",dEN="To survive the enchantment guarding Morgwena's hut, we shall require two things:\n\n<Deirdre places a bone amulet in your hand.>\n\nThis. And the blessing of the Great Stag.\n\nOnce, the Great Stag was Morgwena's tutelary deity, but she turned her back on his cult long ago in favor of the Rooted Shadow.\n\nVisit his altar atop the hill and pay your respects to the totem. After what Morgwena did to him, I suspect the spirit of the Great Stag will be more than willing to grant us his favor.",o="前往巨鹿祭坛，献上骨制护身符以获得他的祝福。",oEN="Visit the Altar of the Great Stag and offer the bone amulet to obtain his blessing.",p="那么？",pEN="Well?",c="你拿到巨鹿的祝福了吗？\n\n拿到了。即使从这里我也能感觉到它从你身上散发出来。\n\n很好。",cEN="Have you secured the Great Stag's blessing?\n\nYes. I can feel it radiating from you even from here.\n\nGood."}
Q[175121]={d="我已经准备好一切，可以开始反咒了，但是……啊，总有个但是，对吧？\n\n我们得先让天平平衡。违抗大母让我冒了很大的风险；在继续之前，我也要你付出牺牲。\n\n一命换一命。Morgwena 换 Serenya Coldmere。\n\n只要他们俩还有一个活着，Ealdir 与 Graysky 之间就不可能有和平。别告诉我你觉得意外！和平之树必须用鲜血浇灌。\n\n拿着这瓶毒药。把它交给城堡厨房里的 Hagrond Doroth。他是我们的人之一。就这样。没别的了。就这么简单。",dEN="I have everything I need to begin the counter-spell, but... ah, there's always a 'but,' isn't there?\n\nWe must balance the scales first. I am risking much by defying the Grand Mother; before we proceed, I want a sacrifice from you as well.\n\nA life for a life. Morgwena for Serenya Coldmere.\n\nThere will be no peace between the Ealdir and Graysky as long as either of them draws breath. Don't tell me you're surprised! The tree of peace must be watered with blood.\n\nTake this poison. Deliver it to Hagrond Doroth in the castle kitchens. He is one of our agents. And that's it. Nothing more. Simple as that.",o="把 Deirdre 的毒药交给 Graysky 城堡厨房里的 Hagrond Doroth。",oEN="Deliver Deirdre's poison to Hagrond Doroth in the Graysky Castle kitchens.",p="<Coldmere 要塞最后一位厨师全神贯注于自己的活儿，没注意到你闯进了他的厨房。>",pEN="<The last cook of Coldmere Keep is too absorbed in his duties to notice your intrusion into his kitchen.>",c="我很忙，你没看出来吗！到底是什么鬼——？\n\n<当你把毒药小瓶给他看时，厨师话说到一半停住了，声音立刻降成耳语。>\n\n所以他们派了你来。行吧。为什么不呢？不是说事不过三吗？我正好快把面包做好了。Serenya 女士喜欢配着一杯葡萄酒享用。",cEN="I'm busy, in case you hadn't noticed! What the dev—?\n\n<The cook cuts himself short when you show him the vial of poison, his voice dropping to a whisper at once.>\n\nSo, they sent you. Fine then. Why not? Isn't it they say, third time's a charm? I was just finishing the bread. Lady Serenya does enjoy a glass of wine to wash it down."}
Q[175122]={d="<Hagrond Doroth 用一把巨大的刀切开一条刚出炉的厚实面包。然后，他把 Deirdre 交给你的毒药倒进一只盛了半杯的酒杯里。>\n\n拿去。端给她。确保她一滴不剩地喝下去。药效几乎是即时的：先是困倦，然后神志昏乱，最后是深度昏睡。几个小时内，她就会死。\n\n而 Scadeald 将获得自由。或者说，我们一直被告知如此……",dEN="<Hagrond Doroth uses a massive knife to slice a generous loaf of freshly baked bread. He then pours the poison Deirdre gave you into a wine glass he has filled halfway.>\n\nHere. Take it to her. And make sure she swallows every last drop. The effect should be near-instant; drowsiness first, then confusion, and finally a deep lethargy. Within a few hours, she will be dead.\n\nAnd Scadeald will be free. Or so we've been taught...",o="把有毒的点心送到 Serenya 女士的私人起居室。",oEN="Deliver the poisoned snack to Lady Serenya in her private chambers.",p="这是什么？啊，我的点心。太客气了。",pEN="What have we here? Ah, my refreshment. Most kind.",c="<Serenya 女士从酒杯里小小地啜了一口。她皱起眉头。她用奇怪的眼神看了你一眼。她再次把杯沿凑到唇边，一口气饮尽了杯中物。>\n\n<她的双眼虽藏在面纱之后，却似乎向你投来挑衅的目光。>",cEN="<Lady Serenya takes a timid sip from the wine glass. She frowns. She gives you a strange look. She brings the rim of the glass to her lips once more and drains the contents in one long draught.>\n\n<Her eyes, though hidden behind her veil, seem to cast a defiant gaze upon you.>"}
Q[175123]={d=" 我该叫卫兵来吗？我可以下令处决你，这座城市里连一个眨眼的人都不会有。\n\n但我不会那样做。放轻松。我知道你为什么在这里，也知道你为什么选择做你做过的事。请坐。放松。\n\n我只是想……谈谈。",dEN="Should I call for the guards? I could have you executed, and not a soul in this city would so much as blink.\n\nBut I shall do no such thing. Be at ease. I know why you are here, and I know why you chose to do what you've done. Sit, please. Relax.\n\nI only wish... to talk.",o="听 Serenya Coldmere 女士的忏悔。",oEN="Listen to Lady Serenya Coldmere's confession.",p="<Serenya Coldmere 女士注视着你。她的目光比先前更加空洞……>",pEN="<Lady Serenya Coldmere watches you. Her gaze is emptier than before...>",c="我的心很久以前就停止了跳动。这些年来，我从未停止向圣光祈求一个答案：\n\n为什么是我？\n\n我的丈夫曾是 Scadeald 的领主，而我能想到的纪念他的唯一方式，唯一能让我这可怖的存在获得意义的方式，就是统治这个省。保护它。\n\n但现在我清楚地看到，圣光对我的真正安排是什么。\n\n这是唯一剩下的路。",cEN="My heart ceased its beating long ago. In all these years, I have never stopped imploring the Light for an answer:\n\n'Why me?'\n\nMy husband was the Lord of Scadeald, and the only way I could think of to honor him, the only way to give meaning to my grotesque existence, was by ruling this province. By protecting it.\n\nBut now I see with clarity what the Light's design for me truly was.\n\nThis is the only path left to take."}
Q[175124]={d="拿走我的戒指。把它交给 Deirdre，作为我已死的凭证。虽然这消息迟早会以某种方式传到她耳中。\n\n我会等你离开，然后一动不动。下一个走进这间起居室的人，看到的只会是一具尸体。\n\n会举行一场弥撒。我会被安葬。到那时，我对 Scadeald 的承诺便已期满，我就可以自由地在真正的死亡……与走自己的路之间做出选择。",dEN="Take my ring. Bring it to Deirdre as proof of my passing. Though the news will reach her ears soon enough, one way or another.\n\nI shall wait for you to depart, and then I will remain very still. The next person to enter these chambers will see nothing but a corpse.\n\nA mass will be held. I will be buried. And then, my commitment to Scadeald will have expired, and I shall be free to choose between true death... or following a path of my own.",o="把 Serenya 女士的戒指交给 Baile Escada 的 Deirdre。",oEN="Deliver Lady Serenya's ring to Deirdre in Baile Escada.",p="你做了吗？",pEN="Did you do it?",c="这是……\n\n<Deirdre 带着近乎贪婪的神情端详着 Serenya 女士的戒指。这枚戒指是一件你前所未见的工艺杰作；单是嵌在其中的蓝宝石，就比 Ealdir 所有珠宝加在一起还值钱。>\n\n那么你杀了她。消息传开用不了多久。\n\n好。太好了！既然 Serenya 已经出局，就只剩下 Morgwena 了。",cEN="This is...\n\n<Deirdre inspects Lady Serenya's ring with something akin to greed. The ring is a masterpiece of craftsmanship unlike any you have seen; the sapphire set within it alone is worth more than all the Ealdir's jewels combined.>\n\nYou killed her, then. It won't be long before the word spreads.\n\nGood. Good! Now that Serenya is off the board, only Morgwena remains."}
Q[175125]={d="在你处理 Serenya 的时候，我一直在辛苦钻研反咒。并不容易，但有了这枚护身符和巨鹿的祝福，我相信我找到了穿透守护 Morgwena 小屋的魔法屏障的办法。\n\n拿着。\n\n<Deirdre 把先前给你的护身符还给你，但它已经变了。摸起来感觉不同；从骨头中散发的能量令人陶醉。>\n\n如果有必要，就把那小屋翻个底朝天。那本魔法书里藏着 Morgwena 正在进行的仪式的秘密……也是阻止她的关键。",dEN="While you were seeing to Serenya, I've been toiling away at the counter-spell. It hasn't been easy, but with the amulet and the Great Stag's blessing, I believe I've found a way to pierce the magical barrier guarding Morgwena's hut.\n\nHere.\n\n<Deirdre returns the amulet she gave you earlier, but it has changed. It feels different to the touch; the energy radiating from the bone is intoxicating.>\n\nTurn the hut upside down if you must. Within that grimoire lie the secrets of the ritual Morgwena is performing... and the key to stopping her.",o="进入 Morgwena 的小屋，取回她的魔法书。",oEN="Enter Morgwena's hut and recover her grimoire.",p="那本该死的书在哪儿？",pEN="Where is that blasted book?",c="Morgwena 的魔法书！数个世纪的知识发酵成了最黑暗的仪式与咒术。\n\n她正在进行的仪式的细节，必定就在这些书页之中。\n\n我需要时间来仔细研究它。",cEN="Morgwena's grimoire! Centuries of knowledge fermented in rituals and spells of the darkest nature.\n\nThe particulars of the ritual she is conducting must be contained within these pages.\n\nI shall require time to study it in detail."}
Q[175126]={d="你在这儿！\n\n<Deirdre 咧嘴一笑，满口发黑的牙齿。>\n\n这活儿花的力气可不小，别以为轻松。但最后我还是办到了，哦，没错。Scadeald 没有哪个女巫能做出我这样的成绩：\n\n我找出了破解 Morgwena 布在暗骨深渊周围守护法阵的反咒。\n\n你必须去那里，而且要尽快。赶在她完成仪式之前。赶在 Scadeald 生下那东西之前……\n\n了结 Morgwena，就像你了结 Serenya 那样。别怕：我会守在附近……万一事情出了岔子。",dEN="There you are!\n\n<Deirdre smiles with a mouth full of blackened teeth.>\n\nIt took no small effort, don't think it didn't. But in the end I did it, oh yes. No other witch in Scadeald could have achieved what I have:\n\nUncovered the counterspell to the wards Morgwena wove around the Shadowbone Depths.\n\nThat is where you must go, and with all haste. Before she completes the ritual. Before Scadeald gives birth to that thing...\n\nEnd Morgwena, as you ended Serenya. Fear not: I will remain close at hand... should matters turn sour.",o="进入暗骨深渊，在 Morgwena 完成仪式之前击败她。",oEN="Enter the Shadowbone Depths and defeat Morgwena before she completes the ritual.",p="你听见那些声音了吗？所有被献祭者的灵魂……我永远忘不了他们是怎样绝望地攀住这个世界，试图逃脱根植之影的巨口。",pEN="Do you hear the voices? The spirits of all those who were sacrificed... I will never forget how desperately they clung to this world, trying to escape the jaws of the Rooted Shadow.",c="大母死了。\n\n<<Deirdre> 在宣告 Morgwena 之死时，声音变得古怪起来。也许她在为此庆祝。又或者她在掩饰悔意。>\n\n而且死得还不够早。\n\nMorgwena 留下了一份苦涩的遗产，但没有了她的阴影笼罩，我们 Ealdir 将体会到一种我们甚至不知道曾被剥夺的自由。\n\n而在随之而来的权力真空中……",cEN="The Great Mother is dead.\n\n<Deirdre's voice takes on a strange cast as she declares Morgwena's death. Perhaps she celebrates it. Or perhaps she is hiding regret.>\n\nAnd not soon enough.\n\nMorgwena leaves a bitter legacy, but without her shadow looming over us, we Ealdir will discover a kind of freedom we did not even know had been denied to us.\n\nAnd in the power vacuum that follows..."}
Q[175127]={d="并非所有从 Ealdir 手中逃脱的人都躲进了这座矿场。在那场追捕的混乱中，我好像看到我们的一些人朝海滩方向逃去。\n\n如果到现在他们还没能自己回来，我怕他们可能处境极其危险。",dEN="Not all of us who escaped the Ealdir took shelter in this mine. In the chaos of the pursuit, I thought I saw some of our folk fleeing toward the beach.\n\nIf they haven't made it back on their own by now, I fear they may be in dire trouble.",o="查明逃往消退海岸的 Rockrend 难民的下落。",oEN="Discover the fate of the Rockrend refugees who fled to the Fading Shore.",c="<一具不动的尸体，摊在海岸上。海鸥啄去了他的眼睛，只留下两个空荡荡的、血淋淋的眼窝>\n\n<零星的破烂衣物下露出咬痕、抓痕，还有更奇怪的东西；像是被刺出来的伤>",cEN="<An unmoving corpse, sprawled along the shoreline. Gulls have pecked at his eyes, leaving behind two empty, bloodied sockets.>\n\n<Here and there, the shredded clothing reveals bites, scratches, and something stranger still; wounds that resemble stabs.>"}
Q[175128]={d="<这个人在与鱼人的搏斗中死去，鱼人在礁石的另一侧建起了他们的村庄。他们有可能掳走了俘虏，若真如此，也许还有幸存者可以营救。>\n\n<深入鱼人聚居地，救出 Rockrend 的囚徒。>",dEN="<This man died defending himself from the murlocs, who have raised their village on the far side of the rocks. It is possible they have taken captives, in which case there may still be survivors left to rescue.>\n\n<Venture into the murloc settlement and save the prisoners of Rockrend.>",o="深入消退海岸的鱼人村庄，救出 Rockrend 的囚徒，然后向 Thandel 报告。",oEN="Venture into the murloc village, in the Fading Shore, rescue the Rockrend prisoners, and then report to Thandel.",p="你带来什么消息？",pEN="What news do you bring?",c="还有更多幸存者？我这就安排一支由我最精锐的部下组成的队伍前往海滩，立刻把他们带到安全的地方！",cEN="More survivors? I shall see to it that a company of my finest men is sent to the beach to bring them to safety at once!"}
Q[175129]={d="<重创这个人的鱼人，和你在别处见过的鱼人不一样。>\n\n<杀掉他们能减少 Scadeald 要面对的问题。>",dEN="<The murlocs who mortally wounded this man are not like the murlocs you have encountered elsewhere.>\n\n<Killing them would thin the list of troubles facing Scadeald.>",o="在消退海岸消灭羽鳞鱼人的威胁。",oEN="Eliminate the Quillscale Murlocs threat on the Fading Shore.",p="对，出什么事了？",pEN="Yes, what’s going on?",c="我看你回来时浑身是血。\n\n<那股气味飘来时，矮人皱起了鼻子。>\n\n鱼人？不过……闻起来不太一样。算了。我猜你把他们狠狠揍了一顿。很好。让他们哀嚎着爬回海里去。他们离我们的海岸越远越好。我们眼下的麻烦已经够多了。",cEN="I see you've returned covered in blood.\n\n<The dwarf wrinkles his nose as the smell reaches him.>\n\nMurlocs? Though... it smells different. Ah, well. I suppose you gave them a proper thrashing. Good. Let them crawl back to the ocean whining. The farther they are from our shores, the better. We've enough troubles to bear as it is."}
Q[175130]={d="<一根来自前所未见的鱼人种族的棘刺。尖端似乎涂着毒液，比刚磨好的长矛还要锋利。>\n\n<把它交给有能力研究其来历的人，会是明智之举。>",dEN="<A quill from a species of murloc never before seen. The tip appears to be coated in poison and cuts deeper than a freshly whetted spear.>\n\n<It would be wise to deliver this to someone capable of studying its origin.>",o="把未知的鱼人棘刺交给 Graysky 的 Alcarian。",oEN="Deliver the unknown murloc quill to Alcarian in Graysky.",c="瞧瞧这是什么？！\n\n小心！<Alcarian 后退一步，险些被那尖端刺伤。>\n\n你说这是你从鱼人身上拔下来的？嗯……那它们看起来像海胆？一种极其古怪的变异。\n\n以奥术艺术与科学学院的名义，我向你致谢。",cEN="What have we here?\n\nCareful! <Alcarian takes a step back. He narrowly avoids injuring himself on the tip.>\n\nAnd you say you plucked this from a murloc? Hm... They looked like sea urchins, then? A most peculiar mutation.\n\nOn behalf of the Academy of Arcane Arts and Sciences, you have my thanks."}
Q[175131]={d="<Kildar 做了个简短而不耐烦的手势，叫你过去。他的目光阴沉而忧虑。>\n\n你说你叫<name>，对吧？嗯。好。你正合适。\n\n我有项任务交给你。我本想派我的山民去，但他们都被 Frostmane、雪怪、野猪、雪豹、熊、狼，还有……绊住了。\n\n<Kildar 深吸一口气。>\n\n仔细听好：一支外交车队不久前从铁炉堡出发，前往城邦 Dun Kazad。出了岔子。他们在蜿蜒公路上遭到了伏击，虽然大使活了下来并得以继续行程，但他们已经请求增援。\n\n你就是那支援军。",dEN="<Kildar motions for you to approach with a sharp, impatient gesture. His gaze is grim and troubled.>\n\nYou said your name was <name>, right? Aye. Good. You'll do.\n\nI have a mission for you. I'd send my mountaineers, but I've got them tied up with the Frostmanes, and the wendigos, and the boars, and the leopards, and the bears, and the wolves, and...\n\n<Kildar takes a deep breath.>\n\nListen closely: a diplomatic convoy recently departed Ironforge for the city-state of Dun Kazad. Something went wrong. They were ambushed right on the Winding Road, and while the ambassador survived and was able to continue the journey, they've requested reinforcements.\n\nYou are those reinforcements.",o="侦察蜿蜒公路上的伏击现场，调查发生了什么，并找到大使 Thargas Anvilmar。",oEN="Scout the ambush site on the Winding Road, investigate what happened, and track down Ambassador Thargas Anvilmar.",p="<一张被撕破的纸片，潮湿，半埋在雪里。>",pEN="<A torn piece of paper, damp and half-buried in the snow.>",c="<一份加密的文件；文字看起来是字母与空格的随机组合，不属于你所知的任何语言或方言。>\n\n<从周围的情况看，这里显然曾是伏击者的营地；一个他们不得不匆匆拆除的营地。>",cEN="<An encrypted document; the text appears to be a random combination of letters and spaces, and does not correspond to any language or dialect you know.>\n\n<Judging by the surroundings, it is clear that this was the ambushers' camp; a camp they had to dismantle in great haste.>"}
Q[175132]={d="<这封密信的内容或许能揭示伏击者的身份以及他们执行的命令。>\n\n<沿着蜿蜒公路前行会抵达 Nivelarn；村里也许有人能破译文件的内容。>\n\n<酒馆老板通常对邻里间的一切流言了如指掌，认识的人也最多。先去问问 Nivelarn 的酒馆老板，也许是个好主意。>",dEN="<The contents of this missive could shed light on the identity of the ambushers and the orders they were following.>\n\n<Following the Winding Road leads to Nivelarn; there might be someone in the village capable of deciphering the document's contents.>\n\n<Innkeepers are usually privy to every rumor in their neighborhood and know more people than anyone else. It might be a good idea to start by consulting the innkeeper of Nivelarn.>",o="与 Nivelarn 的酒馆老板 Dalignir 谈谈，请他帮忙找个能破译密信中加密内容的人。",oEN="Speak with Dalignir, the innkeeper of Nivelarn, and ask for his help in finding someone capable of deciphering the encrypted content of the missive.",p="嗯？我能……帮你什么忙吗？",pEN="Yes? . Can I... help you with somethin'?",c="你……你不是酒馆老板派来的吧？\n\n<Gorlin 认真地听你讲述；或者说，一个醉汉所能做到的认真。>\n\n所以他确实派你来了，但不是为了他的钱。好。好。让我看看那份文件；总不会那么……那么……难破解吧。",cEN="You... you weren't sent by the innkeeper, were ye?\n\n<Gorlin listens to your story intently; or as intently as a drunkard can manage.>\n\nSo he did send ye, then, but not for his coin. Good. Good. Let me see that document; it can't be that... that... hard to crack."}
Q[175133]={d="<矮人努力把目光集中在加密的密信上。过了好一会儿，他咕哝了一声。>\n\n\"破解这玩意儿比我预想的费事得多。太多了！不过…… ，不过我愿意做个交易。\n\n你看，我跟你说过我欠酒馆老板钱；那并不完全是实话。他和我是做了个交易：他免了我的债，我就帮他干些杂活。其中最主要的，就是喂他农场里的牦牛，还有清扫牛棚。\n\n我可不是要在这儿干坐着什么都不干！你照料牦牛的时候，我就试着破译这该死的信息。",dEN="<The dwarf struggles to focus his gaze on the encrypted missive. After a long while, he lets out a grunt.>\n\n\"Crackin' this is gonna take more work than I reckoned. Way too much! But... , but I'm willin' to strike a deal.\n\nYe see, I told you I owe the innkeeper coin; that ain't entirely true. Him and me made a bargain: in exchange for clearin' my debt, I'd help 'im with a few chores. Chief among 'em, feedin' and cleanin' the yaks at his farm.\n\nIt ain't that I'm just gonna sit here idly! While you tend to the yaks, I'll try to decipher this damned message.",o="喂养 Nivelarn 农场的牦牛，并清理它们畜栏里脏污的垫草。",oEN="Feed the yaks at the Nivelarn farms and clean the dirty straw from their stables.",p="牦牛那边怎么样？",pEN="How'd it go with the yaks?",c="你们可真快！太快了！早知道我就多要你们帮几个忙了。\n\n总之，我快弄完了。稍等一下；我想再核对一遍这份译文……",cEN="Ye were fast! Too fast! . If I'd known, I'd have asked you for a few more favors.\n\nAnyway, I'm almost through. Give me just a moment; I want to double-check this translation..."}
Q[175134]={d="除了牦牛之外，还有一件事。作为我和 Dalignir 所做交易的一部分，我答应帮他在酒馆里给客人上啤酒。\n\n可我是个学者！这种事有失我的身份，再说，我还得帮你处理这个，对吧？\n\n<Gorlin 带着恶作剧般的笑容晃了晃那封加密的密信。>\n\n你去办。跟他谈谈，就说你是我派来的；说我和你已经达成了交易。",dEN="There's one more thing, aside from the yaks. As part of the bargain I struck with Dalignir, I agreed to help 'im serve beer to the patrons of the inn.\n\nBut I'm a scholar! . Such a thing would be beneath me, and besides, I've got to help you with this, right?\n\n<Gorlin shakes the encrypted missive with a mischievous grin.>\n\nYe handle it. Talk to 'im and tell 'im ye're here on my behalf; that you and me have made a deal.",o="去酒馆找 Dalignir，代 Gorlin 帮他把啤酒端给口渴的客人们。",oEN="Talk to Dalignir at the inn and help him serve beer to the thirsty patrons on Gorlin's behalf.",p="办完了？ 。好。好，嗯。",pEN="Is it done? . Good. Good, aye.",c="<Gorlin 的双颊先是一阵通红，随后他爆发出大笑。>\n\n我…… ，我快弄完了。对……",cEN="<Gorlin's cheeks flush bright red for a moment before he bursts into laughter.>\n\nI... , I'm almost through. Yes..."}
Q[175135]={d="对，我弄完了。而且…… <Gorlin 的目光最后一次扫过他誊写出的文件>。以我母亲的胡子起誓……\n\n<他几乎像是瞬间清醒了。>\n\n信里说的不多，但有一点很清楚：伏击外交车队的人，是听命于 Dun Kazad 内部的某个人。那个人把参议员 Anvilmar 视为威胁……也视为机会。\n\n他们接到的命令不是杀他，而是吓唬他。\n\n我想你该走了。你必须警告 Thargas Anvilmar 他身处险境。有个有权势的人正在密谋对付他，而那人就在近旁。",dEN="Yes, I'm finished. And... <Gorlin's eyes scan the document he has transcribed one last time>. By my mother's beard...\n\n<He almost seems to sober up instantly.>\n\nThe letter says little, but it makes one thing clear: those who ambushed the diplomatic convoy were takin' orders from someone inside Dun Kazad. Someone who saw Senator Anvilmar as a threat... and an opportunity.\n\nThey weren't ordered to kill 'im, but to scare 'im.\n\nYe must be off, I reckon. you have to warn Thargas Anvilmar of the danger he's in. Someone powerful is conspirin' against 'im, and they're close by.",o="在 Dun Kazad 找到铁炉堡外交车队的首领参议员 Thargas Anvilmar，把你查到的一切告诉他。",oEN="Search Dun Kazad for Senator Thargas Anvilmar, head of the Ironforge diplomatic convoy, and update him on what you have discovered.",p="所以你说，是山民队长 Kildar 派你来的？",pEN="So you say Captain Mountaineer Kildar sent ye?",c="你为铁炉堡立下了无可估量的功劳，朋友。\n\n伏击者是从 Dun Kazad 接到命令的，这不过证实了我们未来几天的外交工作有多么关键。\n\n我的表亲和我会一起主持铁炉堡与这座城市之间的会谈；一场矮人人民迫切需要的会谈。\n\n以我的名誉起誓，我们一定会成功，哪怕有那只阴谋的黑手在暗中作祟。",cEN="Ye have rendered an invaluable service to Ironforge, friend.\n\nThat the ambushers took their orders from Dun Kazad is naught but confirmation of how vital our diplomatic work will be in the comin' days.\n\nTogether, my cousin and I can lead the reunion between Ironforge and this city; a reunion the dwarven people so desperately need.\n\nAnd we shall succeed, on my honor, despite the schemin' hand that conspires against us."}
Q[175136]={d="我有一项任务交给你，还有一个头衔；就当是晋升吧。\n\n我要你以铁炉堡特使的身份，去见这座城市的 Thane，Azaghal Stonesong。去为他效力，并代表 Magni 国王协助 Dun Kazad 的政务，以示善意。\n\n与此同时，我的表亲和我会继续调查这个阴谋，直到找出下令发动袭击的人。运气好的话，到时候你已经赢得了 Thane 的友谊……\n\n以及他的信任。",dEN="I have a mission for ye, and a title; consider it a promotion.\n\nI want you to speak with the Thane of this city, Azaghal Stonesong, in your capacity as a Special Envoy of Ironforge. Place yourself at his service and assist the government of Dun Kazad as a gesture of goodwill from King Magni Bronzebeard.\n\nMeanwhile, my cousin and I will investigate the plot until we find the person who ordered the attack. With any luck, by then ye'll have earned the Thane's friendship...\n\nAnd his trust.",o="前往 Dun Kazad 城的觐见广场，向 Thane Azaghal Stonesong 报到。",oEN="Present yourself to Thane Azaghal Stonesong at the Audience Plaza in the city of Dun Kazad.",c="我猜你是随使团来的。\n\n<Dun Kazad 的 Thane 从他浓密凌乱的眉毛下投来的目光透着冷酷的权威，对世俗的烦恼漠不关心。>\n\n省下你那些含沙射影的指控吧。Thargas 参议员遭遇的伏击是一场不幸的巧合；在这座城市里，在所有可能的地方里，没有一个有荣誉感的矮人会密谋杀害一位矮人同胞。",cEN="You come with the delegation, I assume.\n\n<The look the Thane of Dun Kazad gives you from beneath his thick, sprawling eyebrows reeks of cold authority, detached from worldly troubles.>\n\nSpare me your veiled accusations. The ambush Senator Thargas suffered was a tragic coincidence; no dwarf of honor in this city, of all places, would have conspired to kill a fellow dwarf."}
Q[175137]={d="你说要为我效力？\n\n<Thane 的声音里带着猜疑。>\n\n你能为这座城市的矮人提供什么样的服务？你擅长战斗吗？精通治疗之术吗？或许是建筑？\n\n<他那对巨大的眉毛微微一动，伴随着这些问题。>\n\n无论如何，我接受你的效力。我会让我的将军 Baugwolf 决定如何最好地发挥你的才能。",dEN="Place yourself at my service, you say?\n\n<The Thane's voice is tinged with suspicion.>\n\nAnd what manner of service could you offer the dwarves of this city? Are you skilled in combat? Are you versed in the healin' arts? In construction, perhaps?\n\n<A subtle movement of his titanic eyebrows accompanies the questions.>\n\nOne way or another, I accept your service. I shall let Baugwolf, my general, decide how best to put your talents to use.",o="在 Dun Kazad 与将军 Baugwolf 交谈，看看你能如何协助城防。",oEN="Speak with General Baugwolf in Dun Kazad to see how you can assist with the city's defense.",c="<Baugwolf 听完你要说的话，带着军事化的务实急迫感不耐烦地点了点头>。\n\n我明白了，嗯。不必多说。Dun Kazad 一向是个安静的地方；一处避难所。但近来，这座城市接二连三地遭遇危机：\n\n冰鬃巨魔和他们入侵王之路；黑铁矮人的侵扰与破坏……还有你们所属的这支车队，以及由此引发的政治地震。\n\n活儿跟麻烦一样多。问题是：你担得起吗？",cEN="<Baugwolf listens to what you have to say and nods with impatience, a military and pragmatic haste.>\n\nI see, aye. Say no more. Dun Kazad has always been a quiet place; a refuge. But in recent times, the city has faced one crisis after another:\n\nThe Frostmane trolls and their invasion of the Kingsway; the Dark Iron incursions and their sabotages... and this convoy ye're part of, with the resultin' political earthquake.\n\nWork is as plenty as the troubles. The question is: will you measure up?"}
Q[175138]={d="如果你已经到了 Dun Kazad，那你一定见过 Kheled-Zaram 的湖水。很久以前，这座城市的矮人允许在湖岸边修建 Metantenna 前哨站；那是矿道地铁的一处瞭望哨与维护枢纽，那条地铁连接着暴风城与铁炉堡。\n\n最近我们收到了前哨站发出的求救信号。虽然严格来说那不归我们管，但以如今世道的状况，我怀疑若我们不出手，不会有别人去救他们。\n\n我们，当然包括你，既然你已经向 Thane 宣誓效力。\n\n命令清楚了吗？",dEN="If you've made it to Dun Kazad, then you've surely laid eyes upon the waters of Kheled-Zaram. Long ago, the dwarves of this city permitted the construction of Metantenna Outpost upon the lakeshore; a watchpost and maintenance hub for the Deeprun Tram connecting Stormwind and Ironforge.\n\nWe recently received a distress signal from the outpost. While they aren't strictly our concern, given the state of the world, I doubt anyone else is coming to their aid if we don't step in.\n\n'We,' of course, includes you, ever since you pledged your services to the Thane.\n\nAre your orders clear?",o="前往 Metantenna 前哨站，与机械工程师 Naudin Screwdriver 交谈。",oEN="Travel to Metantenna Outpost and speak with Mekengineer Naudin Screwdriver.",c="终于！终于派人来了！\n\n我快疯了！如果还没疯的话！",cEN="At last! At last, they send someone!\n\nI was about to lose my mind! If I haven't lost it already, that is!"}
Q[175139]={d="警报，又是警报！地铁的水下玻璃处于危急状态！\n\n连接铁炉堡和暴风城的那条线路就从我们脚下穿过。那些城里人以为它从海底穿过……哈！才不是！它从一座冻湖下面穿过；对，就是这座冻湖！这里是寒霜蟹的家，而它们就是玻璃上那些缺口和划痕的罪魁祸首！\n\n警报响个不停，我不能让 Metantenna 前哨站无人看守；这地方整个都可能炸上天！你来负责！穿上潜水服，拿上高强度胶带，把玻璃外侧补好。\n\n既然你在那儿……顺便帮我个忙，减少一下寒霜蟹的数量。",dEN="Alerts and more alerts! The Tram's underwater glass is in critical condition!\n\nThe line connecting Ironforge and Stormwind passes right beneath our feet. Those city-slickers think it crosses under the sea... hah! No! It runs beneath a frozen lake; yes, this very frozen lake! It's home to the Frosty Crabs, and they are the ones responsible for all the nicks and scratches on the glass!\n\nI can't leave Metantenna Outpost unattended with all these alarms blaring; the whole place could blow sky-high! You take charge! Put on the diving suit, grab the heavy-duty adhesive tape, and patch up the exterior of the glass.\n\nAnd while you're at it... do me a favor and thin out the Frosty Crab population.",o="穿上潜水服，修补矿道地铁玻璃的外侧，并杀死寒霜蟹",oEN="Don the diving suit, repair the exterior of the Deeprun Tram's glass, and slay Frosty Crabs",p="警报，警报，还是警报！外面到底出什么事了？",pEN="Alerts, alerts, and more alerts! What is happening out there?",c="警报安静下来了！哈！\n\n让我算一算……\n\n<他低声咕哝着，每说一个词就在他的机械控制台上敲一下>。\n\n胶带的耐久度是 3 上的 7……种群数量减少了 15 个单位……温度在 6 到 7 度之间波动……地铁的流量增长了2E……\n\n<他猛地敲下一个键，结果立刻出来了。他兴奋地喊道>：\n\n百分之一百三十七！",cEN="The alarms have gone silent! Ha!\n\nLet me calculate...\n\n<He murmurs, punctuating every word with a clack on his mechanical console.>\n\nThe tape has a durability of 7 over 3... the population has been reduced by a value of 15... the temperature is fluctuating by 6 to 7 degrees... and the Tram's flow has increased by '2E'...\n\n<He slams a key and the result is immediate. He shouts enthusiastically:>\n\nOne hundred and thirty-seven percent!"}
Q[175140]={d="我觉得这玻璃还能撑上几个月。可是……危急状态的通知停不下来。我不明白。这是个玩笑吗？一定是个玩笑！\n\n除非……嗯。\n\n<Naudin 的眼睛像跳蚤一样在控制屏上乱窜，同时胡乱按着按钮。>\n\n警报不是从这个前哨站发出的，而是从车站。Metantenna 车站，在主设施那边！\n\n去那儿找我的上级，高级机械工程师 Dolrix。如果他需要人手，他会告诉你要做什么。",dEN="The glass should hold for a few more months, I think. But... the critical status notifications won't stop. I don't understand. Is this a joke? It has to be a joke!\n\nUnless... hm.\n\n<Naudin's eyes dart across the control screen like fleas while he mashes buttons at random.>\n\nThe alarm isn't originating from this outpost, but from the station. Metantenna Station, in the primary facilities!\n\nHead over there and find my superior, High Mekgineer Dolrix. If they need assistance, he'll tell you what needs doing.",o="前往 Metantenna 车站，查明正在发生什么。",oEN="Travel to Metantenna Station and discover what is happening.",p="警告！警告！",pEN="WARNING! WARNING!",c="<警报机器人迈着像鸭子一样摇摇摆摆的步子走过来。虽然它每次闪烁的红光都刺得你睁不开眼，你还是从它的螺栓间感到一种明显的机械式痛苦>。\n\n警告！需要行动！警告！警告！",cEN="<The Alarm-o-Bot approaches with a waddling, duck-like gait. Though its red light blinds you every time it flashes, you sense a distinct mechanical distress in its bolts.>\n\nWARNING! ACTION REQUIRED! WARNING! WARNING!"}
Q[175141]={d="警告！危险！\n\n穴居人！\n\n<机器人的声音破裂开来，听起来像一支悲伤而走调的小号。灯光暗了几秒钟。>\n\n穴居人——杀——了——我——的——创——造——者！\n\n<警报重新活了过来，疯狂地闪烁。>\n\n警告！危险！复仇！",dEN="WARNING! DANGER!\n\nTROGGS!\n\n<The bot's voice cracks, sounding like a sad, out-of-tune trumpet. The light dims for a few seconds.>\n\nTROGGS — KILL — MY — CREATOR!\n\n<The alarm snaps back to life, flashing frantically.>\n\nWARNING! DANGER! REVENGE!",o="在 Metantenna 车站击败裂天线穴居人。",oEN="Defeat the Antennasplitter Troggs at Metantenna Station.",p="警告！危险！",pEN="WARNING! DANGER!",c="<它那些像杠杆一样的腿杂乱无章地摆动，让你想起……一支欢快的舞蹈。你决定就这么理解。>",cEN="<The chaotic flailing of its lever-like legs reminds you of... a happy dance. You decide to roll with that interpretation.>"}
Q[175142]={d="警告！紧急！价值！\n\n<警报机器人匆忙朝营地里散落的一块废料走了几步。>\n\n零件——机器——价值！\n\n收集！收集！零件！",dEN="WARNING! URGENT! VALUE!\n\n<The Alarm-o-Bot takes a few hurried steps toward one of the scrap pieces scattered across the camp.>\n\nPART — MACHINE — VALUE!\n\nCOLLECT! COLLECT! PART!",o="在 Metantenna 车站收集 Metantenna 零件。",oEN="Gather Metantenna Parts at Metantenna Station.",p="警告！收集！",pEN="WARNING! COLLECT!",c="<它一说完，底盘上就打开一个小舱门，用来存放组件。你把零件放了进去。>\n\n我——携带！零件！价值！",cEN="<Once it finishes, a small hatch opens in its chassis to store the components. You deposit the parts inside.>\n\nI CARRY! PART! VALUE!"}
Q[175143]={d="<两声微弱的哔声之后，警报机器人进入休眠模式，开始播放一段录音：高级机械工程师 Dolrix 最后的时刻。>\n\nMetantenna 车站已经失守！那些穴居人……他们从内部蜂拥而出。他们在听从一个黑铁矮人的命令。他一定是用暗影魔法奴役了他们脆弱的心智。我们的工程师试图守住设施，但我们没能……“\"\n\n<录音戛然而止。>\n\n<警报机器人闪了闪，重新启动。>\n\n矮人！杀！警告！",dEN="<After two faint beeps, the Alarm-o-Bot enters sleep mode and begins playing a recording: the final moments of High Mekgineer Dolrix.>\n\n“Metantenna Station has fallen! The troggs... they swarmed us from within. They are following the orders of a Dark Iron dwarf. He must have enslaved their feeble minds with Shadow magic. Our engineers tried to secure the facility, but we couldn't...\"\n\n<The recording cuts off abruptly.>\n\n<The Alarm-o-Bot flickers back to life.>\n\nDWARF! KILL! WARNING!",o="击败在 Metantenna 车站率领穴居人的黑铁矮人。",oEN="Defeat the Dark Iron dwarf leading the troggs at Metantenna Station.",p="警告！杀！",pEN="WARNING! KILL!",c="<也许是那不停闪烁、令人压抑的红光，也许是它扬声器持续的尖啸，但你敢发誓，黑铁矮人的死讯让警报机器人很高兴。>",cEN="<Perhaps it's the oppressive red light that won't stop flashing, or the constant screeching of its speakers, but you would swear the news of the Dark Iron's death has made the Alarm-o-Bot happy.>"}
Q[175144]={d="警告！携带！运送！数据！信息！零件！记录！METANTENNA！\n\n<警报机器人转到位，开始朝 Metantenna 前哨站驶去，机械工程师 Naudin Screwdriver 正在那里等候。突然，它猛地停下，转向你，发出一声金属般的尖啸。>\n\n携带单元！目的地：METANTENNA 前哨站！",dEN="WARNING! CARRY! TRANSPORT! DATA! INFORMATION! PARTS! RECORDS! METANTENNA!\n\n<The Alarm-o-Bot wheels into position and begins to trundle toward Metantenna Outpost, where Mekgineer Naudin Screwdriver awaits. Suddenly, it grinds to a halt, spins toward you, and emits a metallic screech.>\n\nCARRY UNIT! DESTINATION: METANTENNA OUTPOST!",o="把警报机器人带到 Metantenna 前哨站。",oEN="Carry the Alarm-o-Bot to Metantenna Outpost.",p="Metantenna 车站那边出什么事了？",pEN="What happened back there at Metantenna Station?",c="<Naudin 一边摇头，一边把一束线缆接到警报机器人身上，几秒钟内就把它拆成了零件。当他取出组件、把电路接进中央主机时，警报机器人发出痛苦的尖啸和杂乱无章的闪光。>\n\n一场由黑铁巫师策划的袭击？还带着一整支听他号令的穴居人军队！\n\n我不知道该怎么看待这件事。这种规模的袭击需要准备。组织。意图。\n\n黑铁矮人究竟想从这一切中得到什么？",cEN="<Naudin shakes his head as he connects a bundle of cables to the Alarm-o-Bot, stripping it for parts in a matter of seconds. As he pries out components and jacks circuits into the central mainframe, the Alarm-o-Bot lets out agonizing screeches and erratic flashes.>\n\nAn attack orchestrated by a Dark Iron sorcerer? With a trogg army at his beck and call!\n\nI don't know what to make of this. An assault of this nature requires preparation. Organization. Intent.\n\nWhat exactly did the Dark Irons hope to gain from all this?"}
Q[175145]={d="<name>，我会留下看守 Metantenna 的设施，但我需要你把这次破坏行动的第一手情况报告给 Baugwolf。\n\n叫他派些卫兵来守住这一带，再派一队机械工程师来恢复车站的运营安全。\n\n与此同时，我会研究警报机器人里储存的数据。也许我能从中提取出一些情报，弄清那个黑铁矮人为什么要让暴风城与铁炉堡之间的矿道地铁停摆。\n\n行动！没时间可浪费了！",dEN="<name>, I'll stay behind to watch over the Metantenna facilities, but I need you to give Baugwolf a first-hand account of this sabotage.\n\nTell him to send some guards to secure the area and a team of mekgineers to restore the station's operational security.\n\nIn the meantime, I'll study the data stored within the Alarm-a-bot. I might be able to extract some intel on why that Dark Iron wanted to disable the Deeprun Tram between Stormwind and Ironforge.\n\nMove it! There's no time to lose!",o="前往 Dun Kazad，把 Metantenna 车站发生的事告诉 Baugwolf。",oEN="Travel to Dun Kazad and inform Baugwolf of the events at the Metantenna Station.",p="黑铁矮人从来不是好邻居，但他们的争端是和铁炉堡。他们才不在乎这座城市。\n\n<一个凶狠的鬼脸在矮人脸上蔓延开来>。\n\nNaudin Screwdriver 要是以为我会派兵去帮他，那他就是疯了。Metantenna 车站和矿道地铁都不归我们管。他把慷慨当成了义务。让他去求联盟帮忙吧！\n\n我们不想卷入这场与黑铁矮人的战争。 <Una feroz mueca se extiende por el rostro del enano>",pEN="The Dark Irons have never been good neighbors, but their quarrel is with Ironforge. They care little for this city.\n\n<A fierce grimace spreads across the dwarf's face.>\n\nNaudin Screwdriver has gone mad if he thinks I'll send soldiers to aid him. Neither the Metantenna Station nor the Tram are our responsibility. He mistakes generosity for duty. Let him beg the Alliance for help!\n\nWe want no part in this war with the Dark Irons.",c="<Baugwolf 的目光中映出要解决这一带所有祸患的决心。>",cEN="<Determination to settle all the region's woes is reflected in Baugwolf's gaze.>"}
Q[175146]={d="你来到这座城市所走的那条路，在 Dun Kazad 城门前不远处就岔开了，继续往山上爬。\n\n在我们自己的语言里，那条古老的小径叫做Scyldrand，寒冬之路。\n\n我需要有人沿着它一直走到 Boreos 要塞。我已经好几天没有他们的消息了。\n\n我们驻扎在那里的战士当时正面对冰鬃巨魔。他们很可能陷入了极大的麻烦。\n\n<Baugwolf 用急迫、紧迫的目光看着你。>\n\n去吧。",dEN="The road you took to reach this city veers off a bit before the gates of Dun Kazad, climbing further up the mountain.\n\nIn our own tongue, that ancient trail is known as 'Scyldrand', the Winter's Path.\n\nI need someone to travel it as far as Fort Boreos. It has been several days since I last had any word from them.\n\nOur warriors stationed there were facing the Frostmane trolls. It is possible they are in grave trouble.\n\n<Baugwolf gives you a pressing, urgent look.>\n\nGo.",o="沿寒冬之路前往 Boreos 要塞，向卫兵队长 Erdruin 报到。",oEN="Travel the Winter's Path to Fort Boreos and report to Guard Captain Erdruin.",p="终于来了！",pEN="Finally!",c="Dun Kazad 的援军？\n\n<看到你只身前来，Erdruin 的希望消退了。>\n\n总比没有强，我想。\n\n<他朝建筑内部指了指。>\n\n你看到的就是仅剩的一切：我们四个，还有我们的狮鹫 Hedgwin。顺便说一句，他受伤了。\n\n那些巨魔……屠杀了其他所有人。",cEN="Reinforcements from Dun Kazad?\n\n<Erdruin's hope fades as he sees you have arrived alone.>\n\nBetter than nothing, I suppose.\n\n<He gestures toward the interior of the building.>\n\nWhat you see is all that is left: the four of us and Hedgwin, our gryphon. He is wounded, by the way.\n\nThe trolls... they slaughtered everyone else."}
Q[175147]={d="如果是 Baugwolf 派你来的，我猜你在外面能照顾好自己。\n\n<Erdruin 粗重的呼吸暴露了他的疲惫。他身边的战士看上去也好不到哪去。>\n\n我们筋疲力尽了……打了这么久，骨头都散了。\n\n你能把还在这座要塞附近游荡的巨魔都解决掉吗？",dEN="If Baugwolf sent you, I take it you're capable of fending for yourself out there.\n\n<Erdruin's heavy breathing betrays his exhaustion. The warriors by his side look no better.>\n\nWe're spent... bone-weary after so much fighting.\n\nCan you finish off the trolls still lurking about this fort?",o="击败在 Boreos 要塞附近游荡的冰鬃巨魔。",oEN="Defeat the Frostmane trolls prowling around Fort Boreos.",p="那他们死了吗？",pEN="Are they dead, then?",c="肮脏的生物……连杀他们都让我反胃。他们的血弄脏了雪地。他们的足迹玷污了我们的道路。还有那双脚趾的丑恶双脚！\n\n至少在死后，他们不再呼吸我们的空气了。我们的山间清风。\n\n要是我还有半点力气，真想好好抱你一下！",cEN="Foul creatures... Even killing them turns my stomach. Their blood stains the snow. Their tracks defile our paths. Those abominable, two-toed feet!\n\nAt least, in death, they cease to breathe our air. Our mountain breeze.\n\nI'd give you a proper embrace if I had any strength left in me!"}
Q[175148]={d="这地方不只是一座堡垒。\n\n它曾是巢穴，我们在这里饲养狮鹫。\n\n巨魔来袭时，有些逃走了。另一些倒下了，为守卫巢穴战到最后。虽然冰鬃巨魔是无情的敌人，我却很难相信他们有条理到能毁掉最后一枚蛋。\n\n也许还来得及救下几枚。你愿意把在外面找到的蛋都带给我吗？",dEN="This place is more than just a fortress.\n\nIt was a roost, where we bred our gryphons.\n\nWhen the trolls struck, some fled. Others fell, fighting to the last to defend their nests. And while the Frostmanes are ruthless foes, I find it hard to believe they were methodical enough to destroy every last egg.\n\nThere may still be time to save a few. Will you bring me any eggs you find out there?",o="从寒冬之路上 Boreos 要塞周围的巢穴中取回狮鹫蛋。",oEN="Recover Gryphon Eggs from the nests around Fort Boreos on the Winter's Path.",p="你找到了吗？那些巨魔有没有留下一枚完好的蛋？",pEN="Did you find any? Did those trolls leave even a single egg intact?",c="太少了，不过这本来就是痴心妄想。\n\n运气好的话，等我们收复寒冬之路后，Daumor Peak 的 Bromli 也许能匀出几头他自己的狮鹫给我们。",cEN="They are few, but then, my hope was a fool's hope.\n\nWith luck, Bromli of Daumor Peak will be able to spare a few of his own gryphons once we've reclaimed the Winter's Path."}
Q[175149]={d="袭击我们的那些巨魔不过是冰鬃大军的先锋。而他们听命于一个工头。\n\n人类那句话怎么说来着？船长与他的船一同沉没，我记得是这样。\n\n<一道邪恶的闪光点亮了矮人乌黑的眼睛。>\n\n在你就地屠杀他手下的时候，让他毫发无伤地走掉，那真是太可惜了。\n\n去找他。他一定就在附近徘徊。解决他之后，把他的头带给 Dargran。你会在寒冬之路更前方找到他——假如巨魔还没把他解决掉的话。\n\n他是我们的……斥候。",dEN="The trolls who fell upon us were but the vanguard of the Frostmane host. And they were following the orders of a taskmaster.\n\nHow do the humans put it? 'The captain goes down with his ship,' I believe.\n\n<A wicked glint lights up the dwarf's dark eyes.>\n\nIt would be a crying shame to let him walk away scot-free while you're slaughtering his men.\n\nSeek him out. He must be lingering nearby. And once you've dealt with him, take his head to Dargran. You'll find him further along the Winter's Path, assuming the trolls haven't done for him yet.\n\nHe's our... scout.",o="击败冰鬃劫掠者的首领，并把他的头交给 Dargran。",oEN="Defeat the leader of the Frostmane raiders and deliver his head to Dargran.",p="站住。",pEN="Hold it right there.",c="那是……\n\n<Dargran 慢慢放下了他的步枪。>\n\n我敢说那颗头上处处都带着 Erdruin 的手笔。所以那个老顽固还活着，是吧？话说回来，我为什么想要一颗砍下来的巨魔头？\n\n这一切都太病态了。\n\n不过，既然你在这儿，我倒是可以多要一双帮手。",cEN="That...\n\n<Dargran slowly lowers his rifle.>\n\nThat head has Erdruin's handiwork written all over it, I wager. So, that old curmudgeon is still kicking, is he? Now, why in the world would I want a severed troll head?\n\nRight macabre, the lot of it.\n\nStill, seeing as you're here, I could use an extra pair of hands."}
Q[175150]={d="我们来谈谈补给。\n\n要不是部落，那些野人还会拿着木棍和石头来找我们麻烦。\n\n他们在下面凑合搭起来的那个小村落，底下压着成山的箱子。他们已经用了几周来支撑他们与山谷人类的战争。\n\n把你找到的每个箱子都砸碎。在下面制造些混乱。",dEN="Let's talk supplies.\n\nIf it weren't for the Horde, those savages would still be coming at us with nothing but sticks and stones.\n\nThat hamlet they've cobbled together down there sits on mountains of crates. They've been using them for weeks to fuel their war against the humans down in the valley.\n\nSmash every crate you can find. Sow some chaos down there.",o="摧毁寒冬之路沿线 Frostmane 营地里部落的补给。",oEN="Destroy the Horde supplies at the Frostmane camp along the Winter's Path.",p="事情办成了吗？",pEN="Is the deed done?",c="很好。\n\n没有了部落的支持，这就等于把他们打回石器时代。",cEN="Good.\n\nWithout the Horde's backing, it'll be like sending them back to the Stone Age."}
Q[175151]={d="至于这些 Frostmane 是如何运作的……我们知道的少得可怜，而就连这点也超出我们想知道的。但有一点是肯定的：没有部落那只手的指引，他们的整个战略都会崩解。他们绝不可能协调起这种规模的袭击。\n\n我知道你走到这里已经流了不少血，但我必须请你再拼最后一把。\n\n斩杀下面村庄里混在 Frostmane 中间的部落士兵。\n\n他们的沉默，是我们只能用他们的性命买来的奖励。",dEN="As for how these Frostmanes operate... we know precious little, and even that is more than we'd care to. But one thing is certain: without the Horde's hand guiding them, their entire strategy would crumble. They'd never have been capable of coordinating a strike on this scale.\n\nI know you've already spilled much blood to make it this far, but I must ask for one final effort.\n\nCut down the Horde soldiers walking among the Frostmanes in the village below.\n\nTheir silence is a prize we can only buy with their lives.",o="杀死寒冬之路沿线 Frostmane 营地里的部落奸细。",oEN="Slay the Horde agents at the Frostmane camp along the Winter's Path.",p="很抱歉让你做这种事。",pEN="I'm sorry to have tasked you with such a thing.",c="我从这上面看到了一切，嗯。\n\n做正确的事从来都不容易。",cEN="I saw it all from up here, aye.\n\nDoing what's right is rarely easy."}
Q[175152]={d="这条小径，寒冬之路，从东到西蜿蜒穿过 Ealdfrost 的群峰。\n\n在危难之时，这个王国的矮人会翻过这同一座山谷，前往 Moroduin 山寻求指点。这并非巧合；因为在远古时代，泰坦们在它积雪的山顶修建了一座观星台。\n\n数千年来，它唯一也是最后的居民是一位名叫 Thrymus 的霜巨人。他同类中最睿智的一个。\n\n我怕他正因为那些 Frostmane 巨魔而陷入极大的危险。而且，就你我说句实话，若有人能走完那条路并全身而返，那一定是你。",dEN="This trail, the Winter's Path, winds through the peaks of Ealdfrost from East to West.\n\nIn times of peril, the dwarves of this realm turn to Mount Moroduin, across this very valley, for counsel. It is no coincidence; for in ages past, the Titans built an observatory upon its snowy summit.\n\nIts sole and final inhabitant for millennia has been a frost giant named Thrymus. The wisest of his kind.\n\nI fear he is in grave danger from those Frostmane trolls. And between the two of us, if anyone can walk that path to its end and return in one piece, it is surely you.",o="沿寒冬之路走到 Moroduin 山顶，保护 Thrymus 免受巨魔侵害。",oEN="Travel the Winter's Path to the summit of Moroduin and protect Thrymus from the trolls.",p="这些……虫子！",pEN="These... insects!",c="啊，我的朋友！\n\n我猜想，若不是你赶到，这个故事会有截然不同的结局。\n\n我叫 Thrymus the Astray。我是此地的看守者。\n\n我承认，它经历过更好的日子……\n\n但客套话就到此为止。这里发生的事，一万年来都未曾有过先例。",cEN="Ah, my friend!\n\nThis tale would have ended quite differently, I suspect, had you not arrived.\n\nMy name is Thrymus the Astray. I am the Custodian of this place.\n\nI admit, it has seen better days...\n\nBut enough with the pleasantries. What has transpired here is without precedent in ten thousand years."}
Q[175153]={d="我了解 Frostmane。啊，我甚至知道他们来自哪个帝国！在远方，世界的北端。Northrend……我的故乡。\n\n但围攻这座神殿的生物不是普通的巨魔。我甚至不相信他们是 Frostmane 的盟友！\n\n我们本可以亲自问他们，但恐怕对话已经不再是选项了。\n\n嗯……\n\n巨魔什么都不会告诉我们，但他们的 Loa 或许愿意开口。\n\n下到他们的村庄，收集他们的灵熏香，然后沿着蜿蜒的小路登上 Cripple Peak。在那里，你会找到一座古老的祭坛，以及一个也许愿意赏脸接见你的灵魂。",dEN="I know the Frostmanes. Ah, I even know the empire from whence they hail! Far away, on the northern reaches of the world. Northrend... my home.\n\nBut the creatures that have besieged this temple are no ordinary trolls. I do not even believe them to be allies of the Frostmanes!\n\nWe could ask them ourselves, but I fear dialogue is no longer an option.\n\nHm...\n\nThe trolls will tell us nothing, but their Loa might be inclined to speak.\n\nDescend to their village, gather their spiritual incense, and follow the path that winds up to Cripple Peak. There, you shall find an ancient altar, and a spirit that may deign to grant you an audience.",o="从寒冬之路 Frostmane 营地的巨魔手中取得灵熏香，并前往 Crippled Peak 的山顶。",oEN="Obtain Spiritual Incense from the trolls at the Frostmane camp on the Winter's Path, and travel to the summit of Crippled Peak.",p="熏香？对于你所求恩惠的对象来说，这点供品微不足道。",pEN="Incense? A pittance of an offering for one whose favor you seek.",c="在屠杀了这么多我的信徒之后还敢站到我面前，你很有胆量。\n\n 不过，我觉得你很有趣。而且你或许还有用处。\n\n你来这里是为了寻求答案，不是吗？\n\n我会给你。",cEN="You have courage, standing before me after slaughtering so many of my followers.\n\nStill, I find you amusing. And you may prove useful yet.\n\nYou are here because you seek answers, are you not?\n\nI shall give them to you."}
Q[175154]={d="跟我来。\n\n我们换个更适合伟大的雪豹之灵的地方谈。一个更僻静……也更危险的地方。\n\n<Loa 的眼中骤然闪过一道警示的光芒。>\n\n小心……",dEN="Follow me.\n\nLet us speak in a place more befitting the Great Leopard Spirit. A place more secluded... and more perilous.\n\n<The Loa's eyes flash with a sudden glint of warning.>\n\nTake care...",o="与 Anzuldin 交谈以前往雪豹神殿。击败病态的软泥怪，找到 Loa 的祭坛。",oEN="Speak with Anzuldin to travel to the Temple of the Snow Leopard. Defeat the Sickly Slimes and find the Loa's altar.",p="（占位）",pEN="PH",c="这是我的神殿。或者说，它曾经是。\n\n那些畸变体屠杀了我的祭司，驱散了信众。",cEN="This is my temple. Or so it was, once.\n\nThose aberrations slaughtered my priests and drove away the faithful."}
Q[175155]={d="现在，就在这里，在我神殿的深处，在过去已是一片墓地、未来已成废墟之处，我会给你答案。\n\n靠近些。",dEN="Now, here, in the depths of my temple, where the past is a graveyard and the future lies in ruin, I shall give you your answer.\n\nDraw near.",o="向 Zuraniz 询问那些袭击 Thrymus 神殿的怪异而有毒的巨魔。",oEN="Ask Zuraniz about the strange, toxic trolls that were attacking Thrymus's temple.",p="满意了吗？",pEN="Satisfied?",c="更糟的是：病光之子从未冒险离开他们那片受辐射的土地这么远。\n\n我相信他们看到了部落的战役所带来的机会，于是抓住时机从背后袭击了 Frostmane 的大军。",cEN="What is worse: the Sicklight Children have never before ventured so far from their irradiated lands.\n\nI believe they saw the opportunity presented by the Horde's campaign, and they have seized the moment to strike at the Frostmane host from the rear."}
Q[175156]={d="冰鬃巨魔再也抵挡不住病光之子多久了。\n\n尤其是在他们把力气浪费在一场本不该卷入的战争之后。\n\n但仅凭他们无法填饱 Matlacan 的饥渴。The-Thing-That-Glows 的野心超越了 Druk'thar 的边界。它的影响已经触及你自己的土地。\n\nRadiance Town 的狂信徒只是冰山一角。\n\n回到你的人民那里去。把这片土地面临的危险告知 Dun Kazad 的矮人，并向……我，或者任何你想求的神祈祷，愿他们在一切都太迟之前采取行动。",dEN="The Frostmane trolls will not be able to hold out against the Sicklight Children much longer.\n\nNot after squandering their strength on a war they should never have entered.\n\nBut Matlacan's hunger will not be sated by them alone. The ambitions of The-Thing-That-Glows transcend the borders of Druk'thar. Its influence is already felt within your own lands.\n\nThe fanatics of Radiance Town are but the tip of the iceberg.\n\nReturn to your people. Inform the dwarves of Dun Kazad of the peril facing these lands, and pray, to me, or to whomever you wish, that they act before it is too late.",o="返回 Dun Kazad，把病光之子带来的威胁告知 Baugwolf。",oEN="Return to Dun Kazad and inform Baugwolf of the threat posed by the Sicklight Children.",p="嗯……",pEN="Hm...",c="<你每说一个词，Baugwolf 的眉头就皱得更深。>\n\n一个从 Gnomeregan 的辐射中诞生的邪教？一个发了疯的巨魔神？\n\n我会派密探北上核实这些说法。毕竟，正如你承认的那样，你的情报来自一个巨魔的灵魂。而谁都知道那些恶鬼是什么德性：\n\n满口谎言、扭曲乖戾、满怀恶意。",cEN="<Baugwolf's brow furrows deeper with every word that leaves your lips.>\n\nA cult born of Gnomeregan's radiation? A maddened troll god?\n\nI shall send agents north to verify these claims. After all, as you have admitted, your information comes from a troll spirit. And everyone knows what those devils are like:\n\nLying, twisted, and full of mischief."}
Q[175157]={d="过来，孩子。我想你很清楚困扰我们 Graysky 邻居的那场冲突。\n\n别以为冰鬃巨魔只满足于夺取 Kharadol 另一侧的土地。他们中的一小撮已经越过桥来到我们这一侧，并在 Anzurak 洞穴里扎下了营。\n\n那地方很可怕；一座古老的巨魔墓地。\n\n作为 Dun Kazad 的主教，我必须请你把这些亵渎者送上刀剑，终结他们邪恶的巫术。",dEN="Approach, child. I imagine you are well aware of the conflict plaguing our neighbors in Graysky.\n\nDo not think for a moment that the Frostmane trolls were content with merely seizing the lands on the far side of the Kharadol. A small number of them have crossed the bridge to our side and entrenched themselves within the Anzurak Caverns.\n\nA terrible place, that; an ancient troll necropolis.\n\nAs Bishop of Dun Kazad, I must ask you to put those blasphemers to the sword and bring an end to their sinister sorcery.",o="击败盘踞在 Anzurak 洞穴中的 Frostmane 巨魔。",oEN="Defeat the Frostmane trolls entrenched within the Anzurak Caverns.",p="事情办好了吗？你有没有受伤？",pEN="Is the deed done? Have you sustained any injuries?",c="我一直把你放在心上祈祷，小家伙。赞美圣光，让你平安归来。\n\n你处决那些亵渎者了吗？\n\n好。很好。你曾是圣光报应的化身。现在，让我把你变成它恩泽的容器。",cEN="I have kept you in my prayers, child. Praise the Light for bringing you back hale and hearty.\n\nHave you put those blasphemers to death?\n\nGood. Very good. You have been the avatar of the Light's retribution. Now, allow me to make you a vessel of its generosity."}
Q[175158]={d="自远古以来，我们矮人便与冰鬃巨魔交战。一个不幸却又不可避免的巧合：我们都把这片山脉称作\"家\"。\n\n虽然他们最近的恶行主要集中于人类省份 Scadeald，但仍有一小撮巨魔跨过 Kharadol 桥，进入了 Dun Kazad 的边界。\n\n他们躲进了 Anzurak 墓地。\n\n那些野人必须死。作为万神殿信条的 Patriarch，我有能力为你的服务提供丰厚的报酬。",dEN="Since time immemorial, we dwarves and the Frostmane trolls have been at war. An unfortunate coincidence, but an inevitable one: we both call these mountains 'home.'\n\nThough their latest transgressions have focused on the human province of Scadeald, a handful of trolls have crossed Kharadol Bridge into the borders of Dun Kazad.\n\nThey have gone to ground in the Anzurak necropolis.\n\nThose savages must die. And as Patriarch of the Creed of the Pantheon, I am in a position to offer a generous reward for your services.",o="击败盘踞在 Anzurak 洞穴中的 Frostmane 巨魔。",oEN="Defeat the Frostmane trolls entrenched within the Anzurak Caverns.",p="倒下了多少？他们有名字吗？",pEN="How many have fallen? Did they answer to a name?",c="我们亲族之间那本血账上又添了一章。\n\n少了一桩要清算的仇怨。\n\n那些野蛮人死了更好。他们的存在本身——呼吸着我们的空气、用他们丑恶的双脚踏脏我们的雪——就是对造物主遗产之美的侮辱。",cEN="Another chapter in the bloody ledger between our kin.\n\nOne less grudge to settle.\n\nThose barbarians are better off dead. Their very existence, breathing our air, marking our snow with their abominable feet, is an insult to the beauty of the Makers' legacy."}
Q[175159]={d="还有一件事。\n\n那些盘踞在 Anzurak 洞穴里的巨魔听从一个女巫的黑暗命令。而圣光知道，她所图谋的只有恶意。\n\n我在幻象中看见了她。我看见她把灵魂从坟墓中拽出。我看见她以他们为食。\n\n你必须终结这一切。她所亵渎的那些灵魂……我知道他们是巨魔，我也很清楚他们是亵渎者。但他们拥有灵魂，而在圣光眼中，那是神圣的。\n\n作为 Dun Kazad 的主教，我不能视而不见。",dEN="There is something more.\n\nThose trolls entrenched within the Anzurak Caverns follow the dark commands of a witch. And the Light knows she plots nothing but ill intent.\n\nI saw her in a vision. I saw her wrenching spirits from their graves. I saw her feasting upon them.\n\nYou must bring this to an end. Those spirits she is desecrating... they are trolls, I know, and I am well aware they are blasphemers. But they possess souls, and that is sacred in the eyes of the Light.\n\nAs Bishop of Dun Kazad, I cannot look the other way.",o="在 Anzurak 洞穴中击败率领噬骨巨魔的女巫。",oEN="Defeat the witch leading the Bonesurper trolls within the Anzurak Caverns.",p="赞美圣光。",pEN="Praise the Light.",c="她死了；我知道。圣光向我低语了此事。\n\n你拥有教会的感激，而且，虽然我无法代表他们发言，我猜想你也拥有那些被你从女巫的饥渴中救下的巨魔灵魂的感激。",cEN="She is dead; I know it. The Light whispered it to me.\n\nYou have the gratitude of the Church, and though I cannot speak for them, I suspect you also have the gratitude of the troll spirits you saved from the witch's hunger."}
Q[175160]={d="要不是那个率领他们的女巫，Anzurak 洞穴里的巨魔根本不会成为现在这样的大麻烦。\n\n他们选择这个地方绝非偶然。Anzurak 是一座古老的墓地，而那个女巫一直在搅扰她祖先的安眠，以他们的灵魂为食；假如他们真有这种东西的话。\n\n你看到了吗？那些野人什么都不敬畏，连自己的祖先都不敬畏。\n\n杀了他们是一种仁慈。就从她开始。",dEN="The trolls within the Anzurak Caverns wouldn't be half the problem they are, were it not for the witch leading them.\n\nTheir choice of location is no coincidence. Anzurak is an ancient necropolis, and that witch has been disturbing the rest of her forebears to feast upon their souls; if they even possess such things.\n\nYou see? Those savages respect nothing, not even their own ancestors.\n\nKilling them would be a mercy. Starting with her.",o="在 Anzurak 洞穴中击败率领噬骨巨魔的女巫。",oEN="Defeat the witch leading the Bonesurper trolls within the Anzurak Caverns.",p="你回来了。",pEN="You have returned.",c="所以女巫死了。\n\n<Patriarch 的声音毫无情绪。他灰色眼睛里的目光更像一位公证人，而不像一位灵性导师。>\n\n如果方便的话，告诉我她的名字。我想记录下来。我们对万神殿的虔诚并不只通过祈祷来表达；对我们这些信徒而言，没有比收集、整理并分享知识更神圣的工作了。",cEN="So, the witch is dead.\n\n<The Patriarch's voice is devoid of emotion. The gaze from his gray eyes is more akin to that of a notary than a spiritual guide.>\n\nTell me her name, if you please. I wish to record it. Our devotion to the Pantheon is expressed through more than mere prayer; there is no labor more sacred to us, his faithful, than to gather, organize, and share knowledge."}
Q[175161]={d="山羊肉是我们的招牌菜！\n\n你没听说过？我不意外；我们几乎一块都不外销。每一块从那些门里进来的肉，都在这里、就在这家酒馆里被吃光！\n\n<矮人发出一阵自豪的大笑，但笑到一半，他开始咳出一团浓稠的痰。>\n\n想尝一口，顺便赚点金币吗？那就拿上这把大口径短枪，去 Kheled-Zaram 的冻湖周围猎些山羊回来。\n\n在你弄到足够喂饱整座城的肉之前，别回来！",dEN="Goat meat is our specialty!\n\nHaven't heard of it before? I'm not surprised; we hardly export a single scrap. Every bit of meat that comes through those doors is devoured right here in this very inn!\n\n<The dwarf lets out a proud laugh, but mid-chuckle, he starts hacking up a thick glob of phlegm.>\n\nWant to have a taste and earn yourself some gold? Then grab this blunderbuss and head out to hunt goats around the frozen lake of Kheled-Zaram.\n\nDon't come back until you've got enough meat to feed the whole city!",o="在 Kheled-Zaram 冻湖附近猎杀山羊并收集它们的肉。",oEN="Hunt goats in the vicinity of the frozen lake of Kheled-Zaram and collect their meat.",p="炭火已经备好了！肉呢？",pEN="The coals are ready! Do you have the meat?",c="<矮人用力拍了一下你带来的那些肉块。>\n\n这才叫好东西！干得漂亮。离一座山还差了点，但够我们撑过今天了。\n\n拿你那份吧，小子！",cEN="<The dwarf gives the cuts of meat you've brought a resounding slap.>\n\nNow this is the good stuff! Well done. You fell a bit short of a mountain, but it's more than enough to get us through the day.\n\nTake your share, kid!"}
Q[175162]={d="你觉得我这台智能蒸汽坦克怎么样？相信我，这是工程学的杰作：坚固、稳定、可靠。真正的大工匠之作。\n\n它只需要几处代码与系统上的微调，来稳定齿轮、辅助瞄准功能，并调节内部温度。侏儒式人工智能。\n\nMetantenna 前哨站的机械工程师 Naudin Screwdriver 会在我们把坦克交付给客户之前完成升级。\n\n我从你脸上看出来了：你迫不及待想试驾，对吧？很好……但前提是你保证把它完好无损地送到 Naudin 那儿。",dEN="What do you say to my Smart Steam Tank? A masterpiece of engineering, believe me: robust, stable, and reliable. A true tinkerer's craft.\n\nIt just needs a few code and system tweaks to stabilize the gears, assist with the aiming functions, and regulate the interior temperature. Artificial Gnomish Intelligence.\n\nMekgineer Naudin Screwdriver, over at the Metantenna Outpost, will handle the updates before we deliver the tank to the client.\n\nI can see it in your face: you're dying for a test drive, aren't you? Very well... but only if you promise to get it to Naudin in one piece.",o="登上智能蒸汽坦克，把它送到 Metantenna 前哨站的机械工程师 Naudin Screwdriver 那里。",oEN="Mount the Smart Steam Tank and deliver it to Mekgineer Naudin Screwdriver at the Metantenna Outpost.",p="好像我的麻烦还不够多似的！",pEN="As if I didn't have enough problems already!",c="Norhi 造的机器没有一台不是最后变成碎片的。全都要怪他那套该死的系统代码！\n\n如果运行它的程序智商跟一个拿着两片铜钹的穴居人差不多，那坚固的底盘又有什么用？",cEN="There isn't a machine Norhi builds that doesn't end up in smithereens. It's all thanks to his god-awful system code!\n\nWhat good is a solid chassis if the program running it has the intelligence of a trogg with two cymbals?"}
Q[175163]={d="Norhi 造这台蒸汽坦克不是一时兴起；那是联盟军方为 Andraste 要塞下的订单。我们必须把它修好！\n\nDun Kazad 附近被摧毁的矮人坦克或许还能提供一些有价值的模块，用来重建 Norhi 的坦克。\n\n我听说一个侏儒式旋转陀螺零件很久以前掉进了湖底……也把它捞回来，我们会用得上！\n\n你把所有东西带来之后，我会亲自负责收拾这堆烂摊子。",dEN="Norhi didn't work on this steam tank on a whim; it was a commission from the Alliance military for Fortress Andrastre. We must repair it!\n\nThe destroyed dwarven tanks near Dun Kazad might still yield some valuable modules to reconstruct Norhi's tank.\n\nI have word that a rotary gyro-gnomic part fell into the depths of the lake some time ago... retrieve that as well, we'll be needing it!\n\nAs soon as you bring me everything, I'll personally take charge of fixing this disaster.",o="收集旧坦克模块，并从冻湖湖底取回旋转陀螺零件。",oEN="Gather Old Tank Modules and recover the Rotary Gyro-gnomic Part from the bottom of the frozen lake.",p="别以貌取零件，不管它多旧多锈：只要能装进它的位置……那就是完美的零件！",pEN="Don't underestimate a part's appearance, no matter how old or rusted it may be: if it fits into place... it's the perfect part!",c="零件都拿到了吗？拿到了？好。我刚装完程序。有了它和你带来的东西，我转眼就能把坦克准备好。\n\n很讽刺，对吧？拆解过去的冲突，只为让战争的机器继续碾压。\n\n一再重复的冲突，转啊转……就像这个旋转陀螺零件！\n\n<机械工程师把那个零件卡进坦克上的一个槽位，在那里它在物理上永远不可能再旋转或转动。>",cEN="Do you have the parts? Yes? Good. I've just finished installing the program. With that and what you've brought, I'll have the tank ready in a heartbeat.\n\nIronical, isn't it? Scrapping the conflicts of the past just to keep the machinery of war grinding on.\n\nConflicts that repeat, spinning round and round... just like this rotary gyro-gnomic part!\n\n<The Mekgineer snaps the part into a slot in the tank where it is physically impossible for it to ever spin or rotate again.>"}
Q[175164]={d="嗒哒！没有机械工程师 Naudin 修不好的东西。\n\n那么，想不想登上一台真正的智能蒸汽涡轮坦克？\n\n把修好的坦克开到 Andraste 要塞。还有，拿着这个！\n\n<Naudin 递给你一叠厚厚的文件，里面满是图纸、注解和操作说明。最后几页用极小的字写着条款与条件。>\n\n你到 Andraste 之后，把这些交给 Moore 指挥官。",dEN="Ta-da! There's nothing Mekgineer Naudin cannot fix.\n\nNow, do you want to climb aboard a real Smart Steam Turbo-Tank?\n\nDrive the repaired tank to Fortress Andraste. And take this!\n\n<Naudin hands you a thick bundle of documents filled with diagrams, annotations, and operating instructions. The final pages, in very fine print, detail the terms and conditions.>\n\nOnce you reach Andraste, deliver these to Commander Moore.",o="把智能蒸汽涡轮坦克开到 Andraste 要塞",oEN="Drive the Smart Steam Turbo-Tank to Fortress Andraste",p="<Moore 指挥官向你尊敬地点了点头，等着你开口。>",pEN="<Commander Moore gives you a respectful nod, awaiting your words.>",c="这是……？\n\n<指挥官的眼睛冰冷而幽暗。浓密的眉毛框住了他猜疑的目光。>\n\n那么，是坦克。而他们让你当了传话的<boy/girl>。\n\n我只希望这台坦克比上一台撑得久一些。",cEN="Is this...?\n\n<The Commander's eyes are cold and dark. Bushy eyebrows frame his suspicious gaze.>\n\nThe tank, then. And they've had you play the part of the messenger <boy/girl>.\n\nI only hope this tank lasts longer than the last one."}
Q[175165]={d="Kazadmere 湖一年中大部分时间都结着冰。所以我们这些在这一带打鱼的人只好……动点脑筋。\n\n湖面上的每个冰洞里都插着一面旗，每面旗都连着一个鱼钩。鱼咬钩一拉，旗子就会弹起来提醒我们。\n\n看那边：现在有好几面旗子立起来了。去那儿收你的战利品吧，不过小心！当你把那些鱼拉出水面时……嗯，有些会彻底发疯！",dEN="Lake Kazadmere stays frozen for most of the year. That is why we fishermen in these parts have had to get... creative.\n\nEvery hole in the lake's surface has its own flag, and every flag is connected to a hook. When a fish bites and pulls, the flag pops up to warn us.\n\nLook there: several flags are up right now. Head over and claim the prize, but watch yourself! When you pull those fish out of the water... well, some of them go absolutely berserk!",o="启动捕鱼装置，收取 Kazadmere 的鱼。",oEN="Activate the fishing devices and collect Kazadmere fish.",p="Kazadmere 的鱼很滑溜；你要是抓得不够快，它们会直接回到水里去。你都抓到了吗？",pEN="The fish of Kazadmere are slippery; if you don't grab them fast, they'll head right back into the water. Did you get them all?",c="它们给你添了点麻烦，是吧？\n\n我感谢你的出力。你几乎不费吹灰之力做到的事，我得花上好几个小时；湖面太滑了，像我这样的老家伙要是不留心脚下，早就一头栽进去了。",cEN="They gave you a bit of a struggle, eh?\n\nI appreciate the effort. What took you next to no time would have taken me hours; the lake's surface is so slick that an old-timer like me, if I didn't watch my step, would've taken a dunk a long time ago."}
Q[175166]={d="这座城市是勇敢斗士们的家园，两百年来他们用生命守卫着我们的边界。\n\n最近，我们最受爱戴的战士之一倒下了。又一个死于巨魔嗜战之饥的牺牲者。\n\n他的名字是 Holdor Stonefist。\n\n我要你去雪幕公墓参加他的葬礼。表达你的敬意；了解我们的习俗。并确保他得到他的功绩所应得的荣誉。",dEN="This city is home to brave champions who have defended our borders with their lives for the last two hundred years.\n\nRecently, one of our most beloved warriors has fallen. Another victim of the trolls' hunger for war.\n\nHis name was Holdor Stonefist.\n\nI want you to visit the Snowveil Cemetery and attend his funeral. Pay your respects; learn our ways. And see to it that he is given the honors his deeds have earned him.",o="在雪幕公墓参加斗士 Holdor Stonefist 的葬礼，并与他的遗孀交谈。",oEN="Attend the funeral of the champion Holdor Stonefist at the Snowveil Cemetery and speak with his widow.",c="<那位矮人女子的脸是一副不可动摇的面具。尽管悲恸使她的双眼蒙上阴云，她仍保持着如石般的镇定。>\n\n你不是 Dun Kazad 人。\n\n我想，我亡夫赢得了如此敬仰，以至于四面八方的人都来悼念他。\n\n这里欢迎你。",cEN="<The dwarf woman's face is an unshakeable mask. Despite the grief clouding her eyes, she maintains a stony composure.>\n\nYou are not from Dun Kazad.\n\nI suppose my late husband inspired such admiration that folk from all corners come to honor him.\n\nYou are welcome here."}
Q[175167]={d="这可能让你觉得奇怪，但我必须请你帮个忙。我正需要一种全新的视角，而谁能比一个陌生人更适合提供它呢？\n\n参加这场仪式的还有圣光教会的主教 Beorn，以及万神殿信条的 Patriarch Khazemil。他们都盼着我把亡夫的灵魂献给他们各自的信仰；一个他生前没来得及自己做出的选择。\n\n去同他们谈谈。了解他们的信仰与信条，再把你的想法告诉我。",dEN="It may seem strange to you, but I must ask a favor. I find myself in need of a fresh perspective, and who better to offer it than a stranger?\n\nWe are joined in this ceremony by Bishop Beorn, of the Church of the Holy Light, and Patriarch Khazemil, of the Creed of the Pantheon. Both expect me to consecrate my late husband's soul to their respective faiths; a choice he had no time to make for himself in life.\n\nSpeak with them. Familiarize yourself with their beliefs, their tenets, and share your insights with me.",o="与主教 Beorn 和 Patriarch Khazemil 交谈，了解他们的信仰与信条。",oEN="Speak with Bishop Beorn and Patriarch Khazemil to learn about their beliefs and tenets.",p="你有什么想法要告诉我吗？",pEN="Do you have any insights for me?",c="那么，你跟他们谈过了？\n\n<Bilna 凝视着地平线，陷入沉思。过了很久，她回过神来；她那双大眼睛里满是悲伤。>\n\n让你的直觉指引你，选择偏袒他们中的哪一位。\n\n与此同时，我会试着与这个决定和解。",cEN="You have spoken with them, then?\n\n<Bilna gazes into the horizon, lost in her thoughts. After a long moment, she comes to; her large eyes filled with sorrow.>\n\nLet your instincts guide you, and choose which of the two to favor.\n\nIn the meantime, I shall try to make my own peace with the decision."}
Q[175168]={d="又是你。\n\n说吧，我能帮你什么？",dEN="You again.\n\nTell me, how might I be of service?",o="告知主教 Beorn，你愿意协助这场仪式。",oEN="Inform Bishop Beorn of your willingness to assist with the ceremony.",p="很好。",pEN="Very well.",c="以教会的名义，我接受你的帮助。\n\n这里有很多事要做。运气好的话，我们的努力或许能打动可怜的 Holdor 的遗孀，让她把丈夫的灵魂献给圣光。",cEN="And in the name of the Church, I accept your aid.\n\nThere is much work to be done here. With any luck, our labors may yet inspire poor Holdor's widow to consecrate her husband's spirit to the Light."}
Q[175169]={d="啊，你的好奇心是一种美德。\n\n你又带着更多问题回来了吗？",dEN="Ah, your curiosity is a virtue.\n\nDo you return with more questions?",o="告知 Patriarch Khazemil，你愿意协助这场仪式。",oEN="Inform Patriarch Khazemil of your willingness to assist with the ceremony.",p="好。",pEN="Good.",c="你的这份心意让我们所有人感到荣幸。\n\n让我们齐心协力，你和我，为斗士 Holdor 的声名重添光彩，也为他的遗孀带来慰藉。",cEN="Your readiness honors us all.\n\nLet us strive together, you and I, to bring luster to the memory of the champion Holdor, and comfort to his widow."}
Q[175170]={d="这座公墓是 Dun Kazad 矮人最神圣的地方之一。\n\n但看看你四周：\n\n不是积起来的雪，就是到处疯长的杂草。逝者值得尊重；至少，他们的名字应该清晰可辨。\n\n我自己已经整理了几座坟墓。你愿意帮我清理剩下的吗？",dEN="This cemetery is among the most sacred places for the dwarves of Dun Kazad.\n\nBut take a look around you:\n\nWhen it isn't the piling snow, it is the weeds that have overgrown everywhere. The departed deserve respect; their names should be legible, at the very least.\n\nI have tidied a few graves myself. How would you like to help me clear the rest?",o="帮忙清理雪幕公墓。",oEN="Help tidy up Snowveil Cemetery.",p="你弄完了吗？",pEN="Are you finished?",c="很好。这是个开始。",cEN="Good. It is a start."}
Q[175171]={d="矮人，和我们的造物主一样，是秩序的造物。秩序存在于我们所做的一切之中。\n\n但我们也是凡人，因此也会犯错。这就是为什么时间对我们的作品如此残酷。\n\n证据就在你眼前。\n\n我几乎认不出这座公墓已经变成了怎样的荒草丛。\n\n帮我清理它。逝者应该得到比他们的掘墓人给予他们的更多尊重。",dEN="Dwarves, like our Makers, are beings of Order. And Order is present in everything we do.\n\nBut we are also mortal and, therefore, fallible. This is why time is so cruel to our works.\n\nThe proof lies here before you.\n\nI hardly recognize the thicket this cemetery has become.\n\nHelp me clear it. The departed deserve more respect than their gravediggers have shown them.",o="帮忙清理雪幕公墓",oEN="Help tidy up Snowveil Cemetery",p="准备好了？",pEN="Ready?",c="你让秩序重回这座公墓。\n\n只是一时。\n\n迟早，正如世间万物一样，混乱终将再一次将它收回。",cEN="You have restored Order to the cemetery.\n\nFor a time.\n\nSooner or later, as with all things, chaos will eventually reclaim it once more."}
Q[175172]={d="有件事让我不安。\n\n当我质问掘墓人坟墓的状况时，他说了一句话，让我怎么也无法不去想。\n\n他说他不敢独自来公墓。他从没看见过什么，但他听到了声音。低吼。还有雪地里的脚步声。\n\n他确信有什么害兽在附近安了家，谁也改变不了他的想法。\n\n你能去看看吗？",dEN="There is a matter that troubles me.\n\nWhen I confronted the gravedigger regarding the state of the graves, he said something I cannot stop dwelling upon.\n\nHe said he is afraid to come to the cemetery alone. He never saw anything, but he heard sounds. Growls. And footsteps in the snow.\n\nHe is convinced some kind of vermin has settled nearby, and nothing will change his mind.\n\nCould you go and take a look?",o="调查公墓周边，找出威胁的来源。然后清除它。",oEN="Investigate the outskirts of the cemetery to find the source of the threat. Then, neutralize it.",p="暴戾之气写在你的脸上。你发现了什么，我的孩子？",pEN="Violence is written across your face. What have you discovered, my child?",c="雪怪？这么近？\n\n赞美圣光，指引你的手对抗那些野兽。现在我明白掘墓人了，我几乎庆幸他疏忽了自己的职责！\n\n谁知道那些雪怪要是抓住他会对他做什么……",cEN="Yetis? So close?\n\nPraise the Light for guiding your hand against those beasts. I understand the gravedigger now, and I am almost glad he neglected his duties!\n\nWho knows what the yetis would have done to him had they caught him..."}
Q[175173]={d="雪地里的脚印。巨大，五趾。\n\n是新的。\n\n我很惊讶竟没人注意到。没人拉响警报。在公墓周围短短走上一圈，就足以发现好几处。\n\n你知道这意味着什么吗？\n\n这附近有雪怪。而雪怪永远是威胁。\n\n找到他们的巢穴，终结他们。",dEN="Footprints in the snow. Enormous, five-toed.\n\nRecent.\n\nI am surprised no one has noticed. That no one has sounded the alarms. A short walk around the cemetery was enough to discover several.\n\nDo you know what they mean?\n\nThat there are yetis nearby. And yetis are always a threat.\n\nFind their lair and put an end to them.",o="调查公墓周边，找出威胁的来源。然后清除它。",oEN="Investigate the outskirts of the cemetery to find the source of the threat. Then, neutralize it.",p="暴力是件奇妙的东西：追根溯源，它是混乱的一种表现；然而，秩序也可以借它来强加于人。",pEN="Violence is a curious thing: at its root, it is an expression of chaos; and yet, Order can be imposed through it.",c="你解决了那些雪怪，这是天大的好消息。但我必须问你：你对它们了解到什么了吗？有什么奇闻异事吗？有什么让它们区别于其他部族的地方吗？\n\n这些知识对万神殿信条有极大的价值。\n\n一切学识都是神圣的。",cEN="It is great news that you have dealt with the yetis. But I must ask: did you learn anything about them? Any curiosities? Anything that set them apart from other tribes?\n\nSuch knowledge is of extreme value to the Creed of the Pantheon.\n\nAll Lore is sacred."}
Q[175174]={d="这座城市有一种丧葬传统：用山顶燃烧的火焰点燃一支蜡烛，再以它照亮逝者的坟墓。\n\n拿着这个。\n\n<矮人递给你一支朴素的蜡烛，白得像雪一样纯净。>\n\n登上山顶的路漫长而艰难；严寒与疲惫会侵蚀你的身体。但你的灵魂将从未如此轻盈。\n\n到了山顶，去找守焰者 Enril，带着被他圣火点燃的蜡烛回来。",dEN="There is a funeral tradition in this city: to light a candle from the flame that burns atop the mountain, and with it, illuminate the grave of the departed.\n\nTake this.\n\n<The dwarf offers you a simple candle, of a white so pure it matches the snow.>\n\nThe ascent to the summit is long and arduous; the cold and exhaustion will take their toll on your body. But never will your spirit feel so light.\n\nOnce at the top, seek out Flamekeeper Enril and return with the candle lit by his sacred fire.",o="沿着通往 Helgen Peak 的山路向上，向守焰者 Enril 报到。",oEN="Follow the path that ascends to Helgen Peak and present yourself to Flamekeeper Enril.",c="手拿蜡烛，紫色皮肤，牙齿打颤……你是为团结之炬而来的，对吧？\n\n<Enril 缓缓摇头，像是在自言自语。>\n\n恐怕我帮不了你。",cEN="Candle in hand, purple skin, chattering teeth... You're here for the Brazier of Unity, aren't you?\n\n<Enril shakes his head slowly, as if to himself.>\n\nI cannot help you, I'm afraid."}
Q[175175]={d="在 Dun Kazad 的矮人中间，有一个为土灵而设的传统：用山顶团结之炬中燃烧的火焰点燃一支蜡烛。\n\n<Khazemil 极其庄重地把一支白蜡烛放进你摊开的掌心。>\n\n你愿意走上通往 Helgen 峰顶的那条路吗？如果你愿意踏上这次攀登，就到顶峰去找守焰者，请他替斗士 Holdor Stonefist 点燃这支蜡烛。",dEN="Among the dwarves of Dun Kazad, there is a tradition for the Earthen: to light a candle from the flame that burns within the Brazier of Unity, atop the mountain.\n\n<With great solemnity, Khazemil places a white candle into your open palms.>\n\nWill you walk the path to the summit of Helgen? If you are willing to undertake the climb, seek out the Flamekeeper at the peak and ask him to light this candle for the champion Holdor Stonefist.",o="沿着通往 Helgen Peak 的山路向上，向守焰者 Enril 报到。",oEN="Follow the path that ascends to Helgen Peak and present yourself to Flamekeeper Enril.",c="手拿蜡烛，紫色皮肤，牙齿打颤……你是为团结之炬而来的，对吧？\n\n<Enril 缓缓摇头，像是在自言自语。>\n\n恐怕我帮不了你。",cEN="Candle in hand, purple skin, chattering teeth... You're here for the Brazier of Unity, aren't you?\n\n<Enril shakes his head slowly, as if to himself.>\n\nI cannot help you, I'm afraid."}
Q[175176]={d="这上面的元素反复无常；最近扫过山峦的那场暴风雪过后，留下了一群冰霜元素。\n\n它们每一个都充满敌意。\n\n从这里开始，通往山顶的路变得凶险。说实话，我正要前往 Dun Kazad 请求 Thane 的援助。\n\n但你来了。而且你看起来相当能干。也许……也许你愿意亲自去对付那些元素？",dEN="The elements are fickle up here; the last snowstorm to sweep across the mountain left a cohort of frost elementals in its wake.\n\nHostile, every last one of them.\n\nThe path to the summit is treacherous from this point on. To be honest, I was just about to head for Dun Kazad to request the Thane's assistance.\n\nBut here you are. And you look capable enough. Perhaps... perhaps you would consider facing the elementals yourself?",o="击败在 Helgen Peak 游荡的冰霜元素。",oEN="Defeat the Frost Elementals roaming Helgen Peak.",p="你的身体几乎散不出热量了。小心；冻死是件很阴险的事。",pEN="Your body is barely radiating any heat. Be careful; death by cold is a treacherous thing.",c="你把它们解决了。\n\n我知道，因为外面的寒意似乎没那么刺骨了，你不觉得吗？\n\n这座山峰从没让积雪下的土地露出来过，将来也不会；我早就习惯了。但那些该死的元素……它们居然真的让我发抖了！",cEN="You've finished them off.\n\nI can tell because it feels a bit less bitter out here, don't you think?\n\nThis peak has never bared its earth from beneath the snow, and it never will; I am used to that. But those damned elementals... they actually managed to make me shiver!"}
Q[175177]={d="作为守焰者，我的责任是确保团结之炬永不熄灭。\n\n我们 Dun Kazad 的矮人在三锤之战黎明离开铁炉堡之后，第一次点燃了它。我们并不打算让它在三氏族放下分歧、和平重归矮人人民之前熄灭。\n\n从我的营地里取几根木桩来，把它们投进山顶圣炬的火焰里。",dEN="As Flamekeeper, my responsibility is to ensure that the Brazier of Unity never ceases to burn.\n\nWe, the dwarves of Dun Kazad, first lit it after leaving Ironforge at the dawn of the War of the Three Hammers. And we do not intend to let it die until the Three Clans have set aside their differences, and peace returns to the dwarven people.\n\nSalvage a few wooden stumps from my camp and cast them into the brazier's flames at the summit.",o="从 Enril 的营地收集木桩，把它们投进团结之炬以添旺火焰。",oEN="Gather wooden stumps from Enril's camp and throw them into the Brazier of Unity to feed the flames.",p="<一个噼啪作响的身影，裹在火舌与黑烟之中。>",pEN="<A crackling silhouette, wreathed in tongues of fire and curtains of black smoke.>",c="一份木头的祭品。\n\n我的饥饿正变得不耐烦。不过，我不认得你的脸。\n\n告诉我……那些冰霜恶魔没有伤害我的守焰者吧？",cEN="An offering of wood.\n\nMy hunger was growing impatient. Yet, I do not recognize your face.\n\nTell me... those frost demons haven't harmed my Keeper, have they?"}
Q[175178]={d="我明白了。\n\n你不仅走完了通往这座顶峰的路——那是会让许多人双膝发软的壮举——还直面了那些冰霜恶魔，把它们赶回元素位面。\n\n而这一切只为了一支蜡烛。\n\n<一声轰响迸发开来，像是一阵大笑，又或许是火焰的噼啪声。>\n\n那位逝者生前一定是个了不起的斗士，才值得你付出到这种地步。\n\n你拥有我的祝福。带上蜡烛，回公墓去吧。",dEN="I see.\n\nNot only have you walked the path to this summit, a feat that would have buckled the knees of many, but you have also faced the frost demons and cast them back to their elemental plane.\n\nAnd all for a candle.\n\n<A sound erupts, like a great laugh or perhaps the crackling of the fire.>\n\nThe departed must have been quite the champion in life for you to go to such lengths.\n\nYou have my blessing. Take the candle and return to the cemetery.",o="等团结之灵点燃蜡烛，再把它带回公墓。",oEN="Wait for the Spirit of Unity to light the candle, and carry it back to the cemetery.",p="你回来了。我们一直在等你。",pEN="You have returned. We were waiting for you.",c="<Bilna 那双蒙着雾气的眼睛亮了起来，映出蜡烛摇曳的火光。>\n\n团结之烛。我们最根深蒂固的传统之一。一种少有人能得的荣誉。这真正地荣耀了我的丈夫。\n\n至于信仰的问题……",cEN="<Bilna's glassy eyes light up, reflecting the flickering flame of the candle.>\n\nThe Candle of Unity. One of our most deep-rooted traditions. An honor like few others. This truly honors my husband.\n\nAnd as for the matter of faith..."}
Q[175179]={d="我已经决定把丈夫的灵魂献给圣光。\n\n他生前对战争了解得够多了；死亡与暴力数不胜数。如果圣光能给 Holdor 哪怕一丝安宁，并给我带来一丝慰藉……\n\n你愿意留下来听主教 Beorn 的布道吗？\n\n等你准备好让仪式开始时，就去告诉他。",dEN="I have decided to consecrate my husband’s soul to the Light.\n\nHe knew enough of war in life; death and violence in abundance. If the Light can offer Holdor even a small measure of peace, and bring me a shred of comfort...\n\nWill you stay to hear Bishop Beorn's sermon?\n\nSpeak with him when you are ready for the ceremony to begin.",o="告知主教 Beorn，仪式可以开始了。",oEN="Inform Bishop Beorn that the ceremony may commence.",p="嗯？",pEN="Yes?",c="完成了。\n\n愿圣光将他留在它的荣耀之中，也愿它赐予他的亲人慰藉。\n\n死亡对活着的人总是更难承受。",cEN="It is done.\n\nMay the Light hold him in its glory, and may it grant solace to his kin.\n\nDeath is always harder on the living."}
Q[175180]={d="Holdor 常常谈到遗产。他的希望是留给我们一座更安全、更强盛的城市。\n\n更加自主。\n\n他从未对灵性表现出多大兴趣，但我相信他会欣赏万神殿信条的务实。\n\n知晓，铭记，荣耀。这就是我们现在必须为亡夫做的事。\n\n等你准备好让仪式开始时，就去告诉 Patriarch。",dEN="Holdor often spoke of legacy. It was his hope to leave us a city that was safer, stronger.\n\nMore sovereign.\n\nHe never took much interest in spirituality, but I believe he would have appreciated the pragmatism of the Creed of the Pantheon.\n\nTo know, to remember, to honor. This is what we must do now for my late husband.\n\nSpeak with the Patriarch when you are ready for the ceremony to begin.",o="告知 Patriarch Khazemil，仪式可以开始了。",oEN="Inform Patriarch Khazemil that the ceremony may commence.",p="嗯？",pEN="Yes?",c="言辞朴素，却真挚。\n\n现在，真正的工作开始了：因为铭记就是背负一副重担，它虽带来慰藉，却也可能导致疲惫。\n\n当他们感到记忆的重压即将把自己碾碎时，万神殿信条会在这里指引他们。",cEN="Austere words, yet sincere.\n\nNow the true work begins: for to remember is to carry a burden, and while it provides comfort, it can also lead to exhaustion.\n\nThe Creed of the Pantheon will be here to guide them when they feel the weight of memory is about to crush them."}
Q[175181]={d="你拥有我的感激。没有你的帮助，我相信 Stonefist 一家最终会选择万神殿信条。\n\n那当然是一种高尚的宗教，却缺乏慰藉。而当人面对死亡时，最需要的首先是怜悯。\n\n不过，我还有最后一个忙要请你帮。你经过 Dun Kazad 时，去拜见我的上级主教 Degarn。告诉他 Stonefist 一家已皈依圣光。",dEN="You have my gratitude. Without your help, I believe the Stonefists would have ended up choosing the Creed of the Pantheon.\n\nA noble religion, of course, but one lacking in solace. And when one faces death, what they need above all else is compassion.\n\nI have one final favor to ask of you, however. When you pass through Dun Kazad, present yourself to Bishop Degarn, my superior. Tell him that the Stonefists have converted to the Holy Light.",o="前往 Dun Kazad，告知主教 Degarn，Stonefist 一家已皈依圣光。",oEN="Travel to Dun Kazad and inform Bishop Degarn of the Stonefist family's conversion to the Holy Light.",p="（占位）",pEN="PH",c="尽管我们有种种分歧，在圣光之中我们都是一体的：农夫、矿工，或是像 Holdor 这样的斗士。连国王和 Thane 也一样。\n\n愿圣光指引你的脚步，我的孩子。",cEN="Despite our differences, we are all one in the Light: farmers, miners, or champions like Holdor. Even kings and Thanes.\n\nMay the Light guide your steps, my child."}
Q[175182]={d="我在这里的工作已经结束，但我还有最后一项任务要托付给你。\n\nPatriarch Arbilun 是我这一派系在 Dun Kazad 的教长。我要你回到城里去，把这座公墓里发生的一切都告诉他。\n\n告诉他，斗士 Holdor Stonefist 和他的家人已经皈依了万神殿信条。",dEN="My work here is concluded, but I have one last task to entrust to you.\n\nPatriarch Arbilun is the dean of my order in Dun Kazad. I want you to return to the city and inform him of everything that has transpired in this cemetery.\n\nTell him that the champion Holdor Stonefist and his family have converted to the Creed of the Pantheon.",o="前往 Dun Kazad，告知 Patriarch Arbilun，Stonefist 一家已皈依万神殿信条。",oEN="Travel to Dun Kazad and inform Patriarch Arbilun of the Stonefist family's conversion to the Creed of the Pantheon.",p="（占位）",pEN="PH",c="我们来自尘土，也终将归于尘土。我们从它那里借来的一切，最终都要还回去。\n\n从最卑微的矮人到最强大的领主；这是我们所有人的共同之处。无论你多么富有、多么高贵，到头来，我们不过是化作血肉的石头。",cEN="From the earth we come, and to the earth we return. Everything we have borrowed from it, we eventually give back.\n\nFrom the humblest dwarf to the most powerful lord; it is what we all have in common. No matter how rich or noble, in the end, we are naught but stone softened into flesh."}
Q[175183]={d="仔细听好：我的表亲 Thorazin 和我一直在顺着这桩阴谋的线索往下追。\n\n起初，我们以为这是黑铁矮人的阴谋。但不是，远非如此。\n\n一切线索都指向 Thane 本人：Azaghal Stonesong。\n\n我们担心他正在密谋对铁炉堡发动战争。\n\nThorazin 和我都被人监视，但你仍然可以自由行动。所以，记住我的话：前往 Ada-Gumbad 要塞。它属于铜须氏族，离这里不远。\n\n你必须发出警报！",dEN="Listen closely: my cousin Thorazin and I have continued pulling at the threads of this plot.\n\nAt first, we believed it to be a Dark Iron conspiracy. But no, far from it.\n\nEverything points to the Thane himself: Azaghal Stonesong.\n\nWe fear he is plotting a war against Ironforge.\n\nThorazin and I are being watched, but you are still permitted to travel freely. So, mark my words: head to the fortress of Ada-Gumbad. It belongs to the Bronzebeard Clan and lies not far from here.\n\nYou must sound the alarm!",o="前往 Ada-Gumbad 要塞向山民队长报到，就 Thane 的阴谋发出警报。",oEN="Report to the Mountaineer Captain at Ada-Gumbad Fortress and sound the alarm regarding the Thane's plans.",p="这简直荒谬。我凭什么知道真是 Thargas 派你来的？",pEN="That is simply preposterous. How am I to know that Thargas truly sent you?",c="<Farignar 仔细查看 Thargas 给你的印章，认出那是铁炉堡参议员之印。>\n\n这就打消了一切疑虑，嗯。确实。\n\n<他显然很不情愿地承认了。在一段漫长而沉重的沉默之后，他补充道：>\n\n说实话，我早就怀疑城里在酝酿着什么。我们与之小规模冲突了一段时间的 Shadowburn 公会，被人看到运送带有 Dun Kazad 标记的补给与军械。\n\n偷窃、破坏……我原本是这么猜的。现在我知道我错了。",cEN="<Farignar inspects the seal Thargas gave you, identifying him as a Senator of Ironforge.>\n\nThis clears any doubt, aye. It does.\n\n<He admits with visible difficulty. After a long, heavy silence, he adds:>\n\nTruth be told, I've suspected something was brewing in the city for a while now. The Shadowburn Guild, whom we've been skirmishing with for some time, has been spotted carrying supplies and armaments bearing the mark of Dun Kazad.\n\nTheft, sabotage... that's what I assumed. I see now that I was mistaken."}
Q[175184]={d="如果 Dun Kazad 的 Thane 真的渴求战争，这座要塞将是第一个感受到他锤击的地方。\n\n这意味着我不能再把力气浪费在对付公会上。\n\n你出现在这里，足以证明 Anvilmar 参议员信任你。因此，我也信任你。\n\n到前线去。帮我的部下击退 Shadowburn 公会的黑铁矮人，好让他们能够有序撤退。",dEN="If the Thane of Dun Kazad truly hungers for war, this fortress will be the first to feel the strike of his hammer.\n\nThat means I cannot afford to keep wasting my strength fighting the Guild.\n\nYour presence here is proof enough that Senator Anvilmar trusts you. Therefore, I shall as well.\n\nHead to the front. Help my men push back the Dark Irons of the Shadowburn Guild so they can make an orderly withdrawal.",o="在 Ada-Gumbad 要塞附近协助击败 Shadowburn 公会的斥候与游骑。",oEN="Help defeat the Shadowburn Guild Scouts and Outriders in the vicinity of Ada-Gumbad Fortress.",p="你在数自己在前线砍倒了多少黑铁矮人吗？",pEN="Are you keeping count of the Dark Irons you've cut down at the front?",c="目前这样就够了。\n\n我讨厌把地盘让给那些疯子，但我宁愿谨慎行事，把 Ada-Gumbad 的力量留给前方真正的战争。",cEN="This will suffice for now.\n\nI loathe ceding ground to those lunatics, but I would rather err on the side of caution and reserve the strength of Ada-Gumbad for the real war ahead."}
Q[175185]={d="公会使役的火焰元素死亡时会释放出一种精华：一种余烬。\n\n我认识一些炼金师，他们会为有机会研究它们而付出大笔钱财；而我们恐怕得把它们用在更实际的用途上。\n\n收集一些那样的余烬，用它们为在前线受伤的山民烙合伤口。",dEN="The fire elementals enslaved by the Guild release an essence upon death: a sort of ember.\n\nI know alchemists who would pay a handsome sum for the chance to study them; we, I'm afraid, must put them to a more practical use.\n\nGather a few of those embers and use them to cauterize the wounds of the mountaineers who were injured at the front.",o="从公会使役的元素身上收集余烬，用它们为 Ada-Gumbad 山民烙合伤口。",oEN="Collect embers from the Guild's enslaved elementals and use them to cauterize the wounds of the Ada-Gumbad Mountaineers.",p="如果战争真的迫在眉睫，我们必须极其谨慎地管理要塞的医疗补给。",pEN="If war is truly on the horizon, we must manage the fortress's medical supplies with the utmost care.",c="这才叫一石二鸟。真是一笔绝佳的资源投入！\n\n那些余烬止血的效果，比我们的绷带所能做到的都要好得多。",cEN="Now that's what I call killing two birds with one stone. A fine investment of resources, indeed!\n\nThose embers did a better job stopping the bleeding than our bandages ever could have."}
Q[175186]={d="我在这里组织要塞的防御时，有一项新任务交给你。\n\n这次的事情稍微更微妙、更危险一些。\n\n我要你找到 Engrym。他是公会里的一个矮人。一名卧底。他为我们充当线人，但我已经有一阵子没收到他的消息了，我怕是最坏的情况。\n\n如果他还活着，你会在 Flamehowl 洞穴附近找到他。运气好的话，他能帮我们弄清公会与 Dun Kazad 之间的联系，以及 Thane 的战争计划。",dEN="While I organize the defense of this fortress, I have a new task for you.\n\nSomething a bit more sensitive and dangerous this time.\n\nI want you to find Engrym. He is a dwarf within the Guild. An infiltrated one. He acts as an informant for us, but I haven't heard from him in a while, and I fear the worst.\n\nIf he still lives, you'll find him near Flamehowl Cave. With any luck, he'll be able to help us clear up the link between the Guild and Dun Kazad, and the Thane's plans for war.",o="在 Flamehowl 洞穴附近寻找公会的线人 Engrym。",oEN="Search for Engrym, the Guild informant, in the vicinity of Flamehowl Cave.",p="<那个矮人像余烬般的双眼朝你的方向投来惊恐的一瞥。>",pEN="<The dwarf's ember-like eyes cast a frightened glance in your direction.>",c="你不是…… <Engrym 那双余烬般的眼睛带着狂热而偏执的目光盯着你。>\n\n你不是公会的人。\n\n那么，是山民队长 Farignar 派你来的。\n\n这儿的形势变得复杂了。",cEN="You aren't... <Engrym's ember-like eyes fix you with a feverish, paranoid gaze.>\n\nYou aren't one of the Guild.\n\nMountaineer Captain Farignar sent you, then.\n\nThings have gotten complicated around here."}
Q[175187]={d="作为他们效力的回报，大术士 Thaurgrim 用暗影烈焰浸泡那些雪怪作为奖赏。\n\n活下来的被锻造成了火焰与余烬的造物；公会的精锐，他自己的荣誉护卫。\n\n无论 Thaurgrim 的谋划是什么，雪怪都是其中的核心。我们越早把他们从这场博弈中清除掉，对我们所有人就越好。\n\n在里面见到多少就杀多少。",dEN="In exchange for their service, Arch-Warlock Thaurgrim rewarded the yetis by bathing them in Shadowflame.\n\nThose who survived were forged into creatures of fire and ember; the Guild's elite, his very own honor guard.\n\nWhatever Thaurgrim's designs may be, the yetis are central to them. The sooner we remove them from the equation, the better for us all.\n\nSlay as many of them as you can find in there.",o="消灭 Flamehowl 洞穴内 Shadowburn 部族的雪怪。",oEN="Eliminate the yetis of the Shadowburn tribe within Flamehowl Cave.",p="他们死了吗？",pEN="Are they dead?",c="单打独斗时，灰影雪怪是可怕的敌人。但当它们成群作战时，几乎无可匹敌。\n\n你敢于闯入它们的巢穴并活着出来，其中的价值比你想象的更大。",cEN="Individually, the Ashenshade yetis are formidable foes. But when they fight as a pack, they are nigh unbeatable.\n\nThere is more merit than you realize in having ventured into their den and made it out with your life."}
Q[175188]={d="在 Flamehowl 洞穴最深处的中心，是术士 Ketheric，Thaurgrim 的左右手。\n\n<从他的语气听来，Engrym 对他的鄙夷似乎甚至超过了大术士本人。>\n\n我要你杀了他，把他的誓约之戒带给我。\n\n接下来的计划需要它。",dEN="Deep within the heart of Flamehowl Cave lies Warlock Ketheric, Thaurgrim's right hand.\n\n<From his tone, it almost seems as if Engrym despises him even more than the Arch-Warlock himself.>\n\nI need you to kill him and bring me his oath ring.\n\nWe're going to need it for the next part of the plan.",o="在 Flamehowl 洞穴深处击败术士 Ketheric，取得他的誓约之戒。",oEN="Defeat Warlock Ketheric in the depths of Flamehowl Cave and obtain his Oath Ring.",p="戒指拿到了吗？",pEN="Do you have the ring?",c="所以你杀了他。\n\n<Engrym 的目光像被拨动的篝火余烬一样炽烈起来。>\n\n而且你拿到了他的戒指。很好！",cEN="So, you killed him.\n\n<Engrym's gaze flares up like embers being stirred in a bonfire.>\n\nAnd you have his ring. Good!"}
Q[175189]={d="我跟你说的关于灰影雪怪和 Thaurgrim 黑暗巫术的那些话，不过是个故事；是公会拿流言缝缝补补拼出来的宣传。\n\n我恐怕真相要阴险得多。也更难捉摸。\n\n但我早就怀疑答案就在里面。\n\n<Engrym 猛地朝洞穴方向一指。>\n\n把你找到的任何器物和遗物都带给我；任何可能揭示公会的起源和 Thaurgrim 的暗影烈焰的东西。",dEN="What I've told you regarding the Ashenshade yetis and Thaurgrim's dark sorcery is nothing more than a tale; Guild propaganda stitched and patched together with rumors.\n\nThe truth, I fear, is far more insidious. And elusive.\n\nBut I've suspected for some time that the answers lie within.\n\n<Engrym points toward the cave with a sharp gesture.>\n\nBring me any artifacts and relics you find; anything that might shed light on the origins of the Guild and Thaurgrim's Shadowflame.",o="从 Flamehowl 洞穴中取回黑暗巫术器物。",oEN="Recover Dark Sorcery Artifacts from within Flamehowl Cave.",p="你找到什么有用的东西了吗？",pEN="Have you found anything of use?",c="你收集到的清单相当可观。\n\n<Engrym 的眼睛像跳蚤一样在器物与遗物之间乱窜。>\n\nThaurgrim 一定在雪怪中间待了很久，才终于揭开了暗影烈焰的秘密。\n\n但这一切有件奇怪的事。\n\n雪怪总是充满敌意，领地意识极强。他们为什么会容忍大术士的存在？为什么看起来他们甚至还……欢迎他？",cEN="You've gathered quite the inventory.\n\n<Engrym's eyes dart from artifact to relic like fleas.>\n\nThaurgrim must have spent a great deal of time among the yetis before he finally unlocked the secret of the Shadowflame.\n\nBut there is something strange about all this.\n\nYetis are invariably hostile and fiercely territorial. Why did they tolerate the Arch-Warlock's presence? Why does it seem as though they even... welcomed him?"}
Q[175190]={d="把手给我。\n\n<Engrym 把 Ketheric 的戒指滑到你的手指上。接着他开始低声念诵咒语>。\n\n一道幻象附魔。它会让你拥有 Ketheric 的外貌；要探索 Thaurgrim 之伤，你肯定需要它。\n\n如果 Dun Kazad 的 Thane 与 Shadowburn 公会真的勾结在一起，你会在那里找到揭露他们阴谋所需的证据。",dEN="Give me your hand.\n\n<Engrym slides Ketheric's ring onto your finger. He then begins to murmur the words of an incantation.>\n\nAn illusionary enchantment. It will grant you Ketheric's likeness; one you'll certainly need to explore Thaurgrim's Wound.\n\nIf the Thane of Dun Kazad and the Shadowburn Guild are truly in league, you will find the evidence you need to expose their plot there.",o="探索 Thaurgrim 之伤，收集能把 Shadowburn 公会与 Dun Kazad 的 Thane 联系起来的阴谋证据。",oEN="Explore Thaurgrim's Wound and gather evidence of the plot linking the Shadowburn Guild to the Thane of Dun Kazad.",p="<一份脏兮兮的文件，看上去与你的调查毫不相关。>",pEN="<A filthy document, seemingly irrelevant to your investigation.>",c="<一份被许多人经手过的文件，沾着煤烟，有些褶皱。>\n\n<虽然很容易被忽略，但其中有些东西吸引了你的注意，迫使你停下来读一读。>",cEN="<A document handled by many, smudged with soot and somewhat crumpled.>\n\n<Though it would be easy to overlook, something about it catches your eye and compels you to stop and read.>"}
Q[175191]={d="<文件内容如下：>\n\n\"随着大术士的计划逐步实现，公会的职责也将扩大。\"\n\n\"Thaurgrim 之伤内的所有工人在此被召集前往 Blackfathom 堡，接受新的命令。\"\n\n\"缺席并非可选。\"",dEN="<The document reads as follows:>\n\n\"As the Arch-Warlock's plans come to fruition, the Guild's responsibilities expand.\"\n\n\"All workers within Thaurgrim's Wound are hereby summoned to Blackfathom Hold to receive new orders.\"\n\n\"Attendance is not optional.\"",o="前往 Blackfathom 堡，听取公会的新命令。",oEN="Report to Blackfathom Hold to hear the Guild's new orders.",p="Ketheric！我的大人，您……",pEN="Ketheric! My lord, you...",c="Ketheric 大人。\n\n<Nagrim 深深低头，行了一个大幅度的鞠躬礼。>\n\n我料想您已经知晓这些命令了。尽管如此，我还是要问：灰影雪怪准备好了吗？\n\n如您所知，Thaurgrim 打算把他们当作攻打 Ada-Gumbad 的矛尖。",cEN="My lord Ketheric.\n\n<Nagrim bows his head in a deep, sweeping reverence.>\n\nI take for granted that you were already privy to these orders. Even so, I must ask: are the Ashenshade yetis prepared?\n\nAs you know, Thaurgrim intends to use them as the tip of the spear for the assault on Ada-Gumbad."}
Q[175192]={d="那些新兵。\n\n他们知道你是谁，因为他们听过你的名号。而且，他们自然已经学会畏惧它。\n\n我本打算走到他们中间，给几个人上一堂纪律课，但我相信你能远比我把他们镇服得更有效。",dEN="The recruits.\n\nThey know who you are because they have heard your name. And, naturally, they have learned to fear it.\n\nI had intended to walk among them and teach a lesson in discipline to a few, but I believe you would be far more effective at cowing them into submission.",o="向公会新兵发起挑战并击败他们。",oEN="Challenge the Guild recruits to combat and defeat them.",p="我的大人。",pEN="My lord.",c="你……你把他们杀了。\n\n<话一出口，Nagrim 就后悔了，赶忙补充道：>\n\n我是说，您做得很好！轮不到我质疑您。而那些懒骨头死了更好。正好杀一儆百。",cEN="You... you've killed them.\n\n<Immediately after uttering these words, Nagrim thinks better of it and hurries to add:>\n\nI mean, you've done well! It is not my place to question you. And those slackers are better off dead. To serve as an example."}
Q[175193]={d="还有另一件事。\n\n我本来绝不会想到拿这种事来烦您，但既然您坚持，我相信您会比我的手下成功得多。\n\n黑石奴隶已经闹了一段时间的麻烦。他们态度桀骜，干活也远没有尽力。\n\n您觉得能给其中几个人上一课吗？",dEN="There is another matter.\n\nIt never would have occurred to me to trouble you with such a thing, but since you insist, I am certain you will have far more success than my men.\n\nThe Blackrock slaves have been causing trouble for some time now. Their attitude is defiant, and they aren't working nearly as fast as they could.\n\nDo you think you could teach a few of them a lesson?",o="惩戒 Thaurgrim 之伤里的黑石奴隶。",oEN="Discipline the Blackrock slaves of Thaurgrim's Wound.",p="我的大人。",pEN="My lord.",c="希望我的手下都看到了。那手法；你乐在其中的样子。还有他们尖叫的样子……",cEN="I hope my men saw it all. The technique; the way you relished in it. The way they screamed..."}
Q[175194]={d="你不在的时候出了个意料之外的麻烦：\n\n暗影灼烧之灵又挣脱了一次。\n\n女巫团试着安抚它，但你知道那些想当术士的家伙……他们根本不配与你相比！\n\n我想这一次需要你的本领来制伏它。",dEN="An unforeseen complication has arisen in your absence:\n\nThe Shadowburn Spirit has broken loose once again.\n\nThe coven has tried to appease it, but you know those aspiring warlocks... they aren't fit to hold a candle to you!\n\nI believe they will require your expertise to subdue it this time.",o="在 Thaurgrim 之伤击败暗影灼烧之灵。",oEN="Defeat the Shadowburn Spirit in Thaurgrim's Wound.",p="你把那个闹腾的灵体重新按回原位了吗？",pEN="Have you put that rowdy spirit back in its place?",c="女巫团的耻辱。你不得不亲自去对付暗影灼烧之灵，这充分说明了他们多么缺乏才能……\n\n别担心；我会确保他们为此受到亲自惩处。",cEN="A disgrace to the coven. That you had to go in person to deal with the Shadowburn Spirit speaks volumes about their lack of talent...\n\nDon't you worry; I'll see to it they are punished personally for this."}
Q[175195]={d="您的风范，我的大人，激励着我们所有人。我的部下不会很快忘记这堂谦卑之课。我也不会。\n\n一个领袖，也终究得亲自动手。\n\n既然一切都已准备妥当，我们该通知我们在 Dun Kazad 的联络人了。这才是配得上您巫术的任务！城里那些蠢货就算把手穿过您的幻象，也认不出那是假的。\n\n替我向 Thorazin 问好。那个矮人已被证明是一枚有用的棋子；我想您也会同意。他那一腔野心……",dEN="Your disposition, my lord, inspires us all. My men will not soon forget this lesson in humility. Nor shall I.\n\nA leader, too, must get his hands dirty.\n\nNow that everything is prepared, we should inform our contact in Dun Kazad. Now this is a task worthy of your sorcery! Those fools in the city wouldn't recognize your illusions even if they passed their hands right through them.\n\nGive my regards to Thorazin. A useful pawn, that dwarf has proven to be; you'll agree, I'm sure. All that ambition of his...",o="离开 Thaurgrim 之伤，把你查到的关于公会阴谋与 Thorazin Anvilmar 涉入其中的一切告知 Engrym。",oEN="Leave Thaurgrim's Wound and inform Engrym of everything you have discovered regarding the Guild's plot and Thorazin Anvilmar's involvement.",p="（占位）",pEN="PH",c="<Engrym 那双余烬般的眼睛暗了下去，几乎熄灭。>\n\n<他的心神飘向某个遥远的地方。你给了他太多需要思索的信息。>",cEN="<Engrym's ember-like eyes darken until they are nearly extinguished.>\n\n<His mind wanders to a distant place. You have given him much information to ponder.>"}
Q[175196]={d="<Engrym 抚着下巴。>\n\n不，这其实说得通。如果 Thorazin 的野心是夺回铁炉堡的王座、复兴 Anvilmar 王朝，他需要一支军队。\n\n第一步是挑起外交危机，把铁炉堡和 Dun Kazad 推入公开战争。他的表亲、参议员 Thargas，从一开始就是他不知情的棋子。\n\n我猜计划是等国王与 Thane 的军队互相消耗殆尽之后，让公会再加入战局。可究竟是什么疯狂让 Thorazin 以为他能控制这些狂信徒？\n\n你必须立刻在 Dun Kazad 拉响警报。直接告知 Thane Azaghal Stonesong。",dEN="<Engrym strokes his chin.>\n\nNo, it actually makes sense. If Thorazin's ambition is to reclaim the throne of Ironforge and restore the Anvilmar dynasty, he needs an army.\n\nThe first step is to provoke a diplomatic crisis to push Ironforge and Dun Kazad into open war. His cousin, Senator Thargas, has been his unwitting pawn from the very beginning.\n\nI suspect the plan is for the Guild to join the fray once the King's and the Thane's armies have ground each other down. But what madness led Thorazin to believe he could ever control these fanatics?\n\nYou must raise the alarm in Dun Kazad at once. Inform Thane Azaghal Stonesong directly.",o="前往 Dun Kazad，直接告知 Thane Azaghal Stonesong。",oEN="Travel to Dun Kazad and inform Thane Azaghal Stonesong directly.",c="<当你把关于公会阴谋和 Thorazin Anvilmar 计划的发现一一说出时，Thane 的眉头沉重地皱了起来。>\n\n那只老鼠 Thorazin。我从来就不喜欢他。要不是他已经和他的表亲逃了，我早就把他处决了！\n\n我猜他们和你谈过之后不久就离开了城市。前往铁炉堡。\n\n那个该死的矮人。棋盘上的棋子正摆在他想要的位置。他的表亲、那位参议员，会一字不差地把 Thorazin 想让他听到的话告诉 Magni。而没有人会怀疑他的说辞。\n\n铜须氏族会向我们宣战。",cEN="<The Thane's brow furrows with a heavy gravity as you share your findings regarding the Guild's plot and Thorazin Anvilmar's designs.>\n\nThat rat Thorazin. I never liked him. I'd have him executed if he hadn't already fled with his cousin!\n\nThey left the city shortly after speaking with you, I suspect. Bound for Ironforge.\n\nCurse that dwarf. He has the pieces on the board exactly where he wants them. His cousin, the Senator, will tell Magni exactly what Thorazin wants him to hear. And no one will doubt his word.\n\nThe Bronzebeards will declare war upon us."}
Q[175198]={d="我看见你和 Darengar 大人说话了。不是那帮贱民派你来的吧？ <Sermon Spada 带着高傲而审视的目光看了你一眼。>\n\n但听我说。他们当然没有。我猜你更像个雇佣兵。\n\n事情是这样的，暴风城北门聚了一群愤怒的民众，要求就 Scadeald 的局势给出答复。我们迄今尝试的办法都没能让他们平静下来，但我想到，某个跟他们\"身份\"相近的人说的话，也许比一纸官方文书更管用。\n\n去和他们谈谈。必要的话，威吓他们。等你办完，去找我的侄子 Thair Spada，他正在城门口站岗。",dEN="I saw you speaking with Lord Darengar. The rabble did not send you, I trust? <Sermon Spada gives you a haughty, appraising look.>\n\nBut listen to me. Of course they did not. You are something closer to a mercenary, I suppose.\n\nAs it happens, we have an angry mob at Stormwind's north gate, demanding answers about the situation in Scadeald. Nothing we have tried so far has managed to calm them, but it occurs to me that the words of someone of their “station” may serve better than an official document.\n\nSpeak with them. Intimidate them, if necessary. And when you are finished, find my nephew, Thair Spada, who stands guard at the gate.",o="告知暴风城矮人区忧心忡忡的市民，贵族院已经听到了他们的请愿。",oEN="Inform the concerned citizens in Stormwind's Dwarven District that the House of Nobles has heard their pleas.",p="我不建议此时进入 Scadeald。",pEN="I do not recommend entering Scadeald at this time.",c="我叔叔……？本来没必要派人来的。我只是在按部就班地履行我的职责。\n\n城门的局势在控制之中……只是\"控制\"这个词开始显得有点夸张了。\n\n无论如何，谢谢你费心在这件事上伸了把手。\n\n我希望我叔叔和贵族院能早日屈尊采取行动。",cEN="My uncle...? There was no need to send anyone. I am performing my duty as expected.\n\nThe situation at the gate is under control... though the word “control” is starting to feel generous.\n\nIn any case, thank you for taking the trouble to lend a hand in all this.\n\nI hope my uncle and the House of Nobles deign to act soon."}
Q[175199]={d="<更仔细地检查这块矿石时，你注意到一处奇怪的反常：一道既不属于石头、也不属于照在它上面的光的\"影子\">\n\n<在去找能解读这种异常、并判定它是否与矿工们的遭遇有关的人之前，多收集一些样本会是明智之举。>",dEN="<Upon examining the ore more closely, you notice a strange irregularity: a “shadow” that belongs neither to the stone nor to the light falling upon it.>\n\n<It would be wise to collect more samples before seeking someone capable of interpreting this anomaly, and determining whether it is connected to what happened to the miners.>",o="在 Ironbough 矿场收集暗影矿石，并找个能分析它的人。",oEN="Collect shadowed ore in Ironbough Mine and find someone who can analyze it.",p="你给我带了什么来？",pEN="What have you brought me?",c="嗯……这是什么？\n\n<Beldred 在她那长得离谱的鼻子的阴影下打量那块矿石。>\n\n这些石头上散发的魔法让我觉得熟悉。\n\n把你找到的全部给我，从今往后，离这种矿石远一点。\n\n前提是你还想保住你来找我帮忙时所表现出的那点理智……\n\n<她发出一声尖利的笑。>",cEN="Hm... What do we have here?\n\n<Beldred inspects the ore beneath the shadow of her very long nose.>\n\nThe magic emanating from these stones feels familiar.\n\nGive me everything you found, and from now on, keep away from this ore.\n\nAssuming you wish to preserve what little sanity you display by asking me for help...\n\n<A shrill laugh escapes her.>"}
Q[175200]={d="到头来，我们都会得到圣光的宽恕。只是对某些人而言，赦免的代价是他们的性命。\n\n你愿意成为它神圣审判的器具吗？\n\n通常，告解的封印是不可侵犯的原则。但圣光已允许向你揭示三个名字：\n\nAldren 修士、圣骑士 Abigail，以及 Samuel Crowe。圣光认为这三人没有一个值得怜悯。\n\n记住：我们的职责不是解读它的意志，而是执行它。如有必要，就字面意义上地执行。",dEN="In the end, we all find the Light's forgiveness. Though for some, absolution comes at the cost of their lives.\n\nWill you be the instrument of its holy judgment?\n\nOrdinarily, the seal of confession is an inviolable principle. But the Light has allowed three names to be revealed to you:\n\nBrother Aldren, Paladin Abigail, and Samuel Crowe. The Light has found none of the three worthy of mercy.\n\nRemember: it is not our place to interpret its will, but to execute it out. Literally, if necessary.",o="在 Hallow Wind 修道院及其周围杀死 Aldren 修士、圣骑士 Abigail 和 Samuel Crowe。",oEN="Kill Brother Aldren, Paladin Abigail, and Samuel Crowe in and around Hallow Wind Abbey.",p="有什么要忏悔的吗？",pEN="Anything to confess?",c="圣光的意志已经实现。\n\n悔恨，若是真诚的，并不带来安慰……它带来创伤。而带来创伤的，方能救赎。\n\n告诉我：你可曾为任何事悔恨？",cEN="The will of the Light has been fulfilled.\n\nRepentance, when sincere, does not comfort... it wounds. And what wounds, redeems.\n\nTell me: do you repent of anything?"}
Q[175201]={d="从 Graysky 派来的那些镀锡铁皮莽夫，没一个能解决豺狼人的问题——除非他们说的\"解决\"是指\"杀掉他们\"。要是那样的话，你也不会听见我抱怨。\n\n无论如何，我帮不了你更多了。这是请你离开我小屋的客气说法。\n\n<Beldred 用一根长得离谱的手指指向门口。>\n\n那就再见啦！去干你最擅长的事吧，我也不知道是什么；杀东西、采花……或者跟人聊天。对，就这个！把你在那儿的发现告诉 Amros 队长。那个人啊，Amros，唉？那么忧心忡忡……我敢肯定他就没离开过酒馆。",dEN="None of those tin-plated brutes they send from Graysky are going to solve the gnoll problem, unless by “solve” they mean “kill them.” Not that you will hear me complain, if that is the case.\n\nOne way or another, I can do nothing more for you. Which is the polite way of inviting you out of my hut.\n\n<Beldred points to the door with one of her very long fingers.>\n\nGoodbye, then! Go and do whatever it is you do best, I do not know; kill things, pick flowers… Or talk to people. Yes, that! Tell Captain Amros what you have discovered. What a man, that Amros, eh? So concerned… and I am sure he has not moved from the tavern.",o="把 Ironbough 矿场发生的事告知 Amros Dhagor 队长。",oEN="Inform Captain Amros Dhagor of what happened in Ironbough Mine.",p="<队长看上去忧心忡忡。>",pEN="<The captain appears concerned.>",c="不管有没有诅咒，Graysky 那边都会想听你的报告。总比没有强，我想。\n\n我会留在这儿；你知道的，以防事情有变。",cEN="Curse or no curse, they will want to hear your report in Graysky. Better than nothing, I suppose.\n\nI will stay here; you know, in case things take a turn."}
Q[175202]={d="回 Graysky 去，把你了解到的一切报告给 Draewyn 爵士。全部：无论是荒诞的还是平淡的。不要遗漏任何细节。\n\n卫队的领主指挥官是个判断力可靠的人。如果这桩诅咒之事里有什么真相，他会知道该怎么做。\n\n直到我们再见，<name>。这是我的荣幸。",dEN="Return to Graysky and report what you have learned to Sir Draewyn. Everything: the fantastical and the ordinary. Omit no detail.\n\nThe lord commander of the guard is a man of sound judgment. If there is any truth to this matter of a curse, he will know what to do.\n\nUntil we meet again, <name>. It has been an honor.",o="前往 Graysky，向 Draewyn 爵士报告。",oEN="Travel to Graysky and report to Sir Draewyn.",c="<Draewyn 爵士以无限的耐心听完了你的叙述。>\n\n矿场塌方。矿工被困。矿工们在绝望中诉诸食人。而不久之后，他们遭到诅咒，被变成豺狼人作为惩罚。\n\n<有那么一瞬间，你担心 Draewyn 爵士会放声大笑。>\n\n嗯，在 Scadeald 见过更离奇的事。我会让人进一步调查这件事。\n\n在那之前，你拥有 Graysky 的感激。",cEN="<Sir Draewyn listens to your account with infinite patience.>\n\nA mine collapse. Trapped miners. Miners who, in their desperation, resort to cannibalism. And some time later, they suffer a curse that turns them into gnolls, as punishment.\n\n<For a moment, your fear Sir Draewyn might burst into laughter.>\n\nWell, stranger things have been seen in Scadeald. I will have this matter investigated further.\n\nUntil then, you have Graysky's gratitude."}
Q[175203]={d="三姐妹居住在 Swiftwater 瀑布之间一处隐蔽的洞穴中。从 Graysky 到她们那里最快的路，是穿过“祖母的良药”的地下室。\n\n你得从我们左边的后院溜进去。两位姐妹经营着那家店：Hilda 和 Zelda，草药师。在地面上。\n\n要是被她们抓住，她们做的事会比朝你扔一捆草药更糟。",dEN="The Three Sisters dwell in a hidden cave within the waterfalls of the Swiftwater. The quickest way to reach them from Graysky is through the cellar of “Grandmother's Remedy.”\n\nYou'll have to slip in through the back courtyard, to our left. Two sisters run the shop: Hilda and Zelda, herbalists. On the surface.\n\nIf they catch you, they'll do worse than throw a bundle of herbs at you.",o="潜入祖母的良药的地下室，使用暗门。然后找到三姐妹。",oEN="Sneak into the cellar of Grandmother's Remedy and use the secret trapdoor. Then find the Three Sisters.",c="Alanna，可怜的孩子。\n\n<三个女人——少女、主妇与老妪——同时开口，完全同步。>\n\n我们知道事情会变成这样，却还是没有插手。我们从不插手。但 Scadeald 与我们不同；不。而那个可怜、可怜的男人太容易被诱惑了。\n\n你是为了他强加于他爱人的那个受诅咒的存在而来的，不是吗？",cEN="Alanna, poor child.\n\n<The three women, maiden, matron, and crone, speak at once, in perfect synchrony.>\n\nWe knew it would come to this, and yet we did not intervene. We never do. But Scadeald is not as we are; no. And that poor, poor man was seduced far too easily.\n\nYou are here about the cursed existence he forced upon his beloved, are you not?"}
Q[175204]={d="一个比你来得更早的男人，就在几周之前。Carden。他寻求一种被禁的药剂，某种不可能之物：\n\n能治愈死亡本身的魔法。\n\n我们警告过他篡改神圣循环的后果，但他不肯听。而终于，一个声音在他心智的边缘低语，向他提供了我们曾拒绝给予他的知识。\n\n你想破除这诅咒吗？那就去它诞生的地方：Hallow Wind 修道院下方的地穴。正是在那里，Carden 犯下了 Cardinal 之罪，以一种亵渎的躯体的形式。\n\n<三姐妹最后长长地、沉默地看了你一眼。>",dEN="A man came before you, some weeks past. Carden. He sought a forbidden medicine, something impossible:\n\nMagic that could cure death itself.\n\nWe warned him of the consequences of tampering with the Sacred Cycle, but he would not listen. And in time, a voice whispered at the edges of his mind, offering him the knowledge we had denied him.\n\nDo you wish to break the curse? Then go to the place of its birth: the crypts beneath the Hanging Abbey. It was there that Carden committed the Cardinal Sin, in the form of a blasphemed body.\n\n<The Three Sisters fix you with one last long, silent look.>",o="深入 Hallow Wind 修道院的地穴，击败红衣主教 Royce。",oEN="Venture into the crypts of Hallow Wind Abbey, and defeat Cardinal Royce.",p="阴险的 Scadeald……仅仅一句低语，就足以把一个悲恸男人的爱扭曲成某种可怕而危险的东西。",pEN="Treacherous Scadeald... A single whisper was enough to twist a grieving man's love into something terrible and dangerous.",c="诅咒正在解除。雨不会永远下个不停。\n\n<三姐妹完全同步地开口。她们的眼中闪着认出你的光。>\n\nCarden 的罪已得赎偿，大循环的平衡已经恢复。\n\nAlanna 很幸运，找到她的是你，而不是别人。",cEN="The curse is lifting. No rain falls forever.\n\n<The Three Sisters speak in perfect synchrony. Their eyes gleam with recognition.>\n\nCarden's sin has been atoned for, and the balance of the Great Cycle restored.\n\nAlanna was fortunate that you found her, and no other."}
Q[175205]={d="被 Carden 从死亡中复活的那些人很快就会化为灰烬。到那时，Alanna 就能得到她爱人从她那里偷走的安息。\n\n记住这个教训：暗影没有能对付你的武器，除了你亲手放进它手中的那一件。情人的执念、疯子的暴怒、圣徒的僵直……\n\n一切都能被扭曲变形。\n\n<三姐妹在离去前三次祝福你的名字。>\n\n现在走吧。离开这个地方。你在这个故事里的角色已近尾声。Graysky 那些铁皮士兵会想知道你已经处理掉了 Cresthairn 的威胁。",dEN="Those whom Carden raised from death will soon be ash. And with that, Alanna will have the rest her beloved stole from her.\n\nRemember this lesson: the Shadow has no weapon against you save the one you place in its hand. The lover's obsession, the madman's wrath, the saint's rigidity...\n\nAll can be twisted out of shape.\n\n<The Three Sisters bless your name three times before taking their leave.>\n\nNow go. Leave this place. Your part in this tale draws to its end. The tin soldiers in Graysky will want to know you have dealt with the threat in Cresthairn.",o="返回 Graysky，把 Cresthairn 发生的事报告给 Draewyn 爵士。",oEN="Return to Graysky and report what happened in Cresthairn to Sir Draewyn.",c="我收到了一封 Elroth 神父的来信。他无法解释原因，但看来地穴中的威胁已经解决了。\n\n我想，是时候把那地方好好扫一遍了。\n\n<Draewyn 爵士从摊在桌上的文件中抬起目光，赞许地朝你点了点头。>\n\n我不知道你做了什么，但它奏效了。\n\n你拥有 Graysky 的感激。",cEN="I received a missive from Father Elroth. He cannot explain how, but it seems the threat in the crypts has been resolved.\n\nTime to pass a broom through the place, I suppose.\n\n<Sir Draewyn lifts his gaze from the documents spread across the table and gives you an approving nod.>\n\nI don't know what you did, but it worked.\n\nYou have Graysky's gratitude."}
Q[175206]={d="抱歉打扰你，但我现在实在忙不过来。我母亲不能丢下店铺不管，我父亲脑子里的事又太多；一边是 Windswept 奶酪正在赢得的声誉，一边是暴风城的局势……\n\n你能帮我一件小事吗？我有一批货送晚了。\n\n我只需要把这批什锦奶酪送到暴风城公园的那位精灵 Zaradiel 手里。花不了你多少时间，而你会帮了我一个大忙。",dEN="Sorry to trouble you, but I am rather overwhelmed at the moment. My mother cannot leave the shop unattended, and my father has too much on his mind; between the reputation Windswept cheese is gaining and the situation in Stormwind...\n\nCould you help me with a small matter? I am late with a delivery.\n\nI only need this assortment of cheeses delivered to Zaradiel, the elf in Stormwind Park. It will take no time at all, and you would be doing me an enormous favor.",o="把什锦奶酪送到暴风城公园的 Zaradiel 手中。",oEN="Deliver the cheese assortment to Zaradiel in Stormwind Park.",p="你带着什锦奶酪吗？",pEN="Do you have the cheese assortment?",c="<那位女精灵小心地接过什锦奶酪，端详了片刻，然后微微点了点头。\n\n这一定是那位奶酪匠学徒订的货……终于来了。在暴风城，连最简单的差事都在考验一个活了几个世纪的人的耐心。\n\n<她优雅地取下一小块奶酪，默默品尝，从容地品味着。>\n\n不错。但一旦你尝过 Windswept 奶酪，一切就都不一样了。Trias 一家有大麻烦了……",cEN="<The elf takes the cheese assortment carefully, studying it for a moment before giving you a slight nod.>\n\nThis must be the cheesemaker's apprentice's order... At last. In Stormwind, even simple errands test the patience of someone who has lived for centuries.\n\n<She delicately takes a small piece of cheese and tastes it in silence, considering it calmly.>\n\nNot bad. But once you have tasted Windswept cheese, nothing else is quite the same. The Trias family is in serious trouble..."}
Q[175207]={d="<关于 Scadeald 省以及如今笼罩它的危机，黑暗的消息与不祥的流言正传遍暴风城王国乃至更远的地方。>\n\n<对于王国和联盟而言，这无疑是坏消息。但它们也为像你这样的冒险者提供了机会：献出你的本事，填满你的钱袋，闯出你的名声。>\n\n<多打听一些消息会是明智之举。>",dEN="<Dark news and sinister rumors circulate through the Kingdom of Stormwind and beyond concerning the province of Scadeald and the crisis now gripping it.>\n\n<They are, without doubt, ill tidings for the kingdom and for the Alliance. But they also present an opportunity for adventurers like you to offer your services, fatten your purse, and carve out a reputation.>\n\n<It would be wise to search for more information.>",o="进一步了解 Scadeald 的危机。",oEN="Learn more about the crisis in Scadeald.",c="<那人的衣着表明他是个外来者。深暗的色调，以及他马匹的架势，都表明他是 Scadeald 省的子民。>\n\n<他浓密的眉毛给他的目光添了几分严厉。>\n\n嗯？",cEN="<The man's attire marks him as a foreigner. The dark, muted colors, as well as the bearing of his horse, identify him as a citizen of the province of Scadeald.>\n\n<His thick brows lend his gaze a certain severity.>\n\nYes?"}
Q[175208]={d="这不是我第一次看见你和领主指挥官交谈，我还擅自向他打听了你的事。\n\n他是个寡言的人，听他开口称赞别人就更罕见了。但他称赞了你。而如果你赢得了他的信任，那你也赢得了我的。\n\n<矮人的目光变得哀伤。>\n\n不久前，我收到了 Kharanos 的山民队长 Kildar 的一封密信；一件万分紧急的事，关乎这片土地与城邦 Dun Kazad。\n\n去向他报到。告诉他，是 Graysky 的 Gramgir 派你来的。",dEN="It's not the first time I've seen you speak with the Lord Commander, and I took the liberty of asking him about you.\n\nHe's a man of few words, and rarer still is it to hear him offer praise. But he praised you. And if you've earned his trust, then you've earned mine as well.\n\n<The dwarf's gaze grows sorrowful.>\n\nNot long ago, I received a missive from Mountaineer Captain Kildar in Kharanos; a matter of the utmost urgency, concerning these lands and the city-state of Dun Kazad.\n\nPresent yourself before him. Tell him Gramgir sends you, from Graysky.",o="前往 Kharanos，向山民队长 Kildar 报到。",oEN="Travel to Kharanos and present yourself before Mountaineer Captain Kildar.",c="<Kharanos 的山民队长以一份精确拿捏的耐心听着你说。>\n\n那么是 Gramgir 派你来的。从 Graysky 到这儿，一定是段不短的路程。",cEN="<The mountaineer captain of Kharanos listens to you with a sharply measured dose of patience.>\n\nGramgir sends you, then. Must’ve been quite the trek from Graysky to here."}
Q[175209]={o="相关",oEN="Related"}
Q[175210]={o="前往 Druk'thar 岛 Zandor 的酋长小屋，向巫医 Zalarjin 报到。",oEN="Report to Witch Doctor Zalarjin in the headman's hut in Zandor, on the island of Druk'thar."}
Q[175211]={d="我们最不需要的就是更多你这样的人。\n\n<Alotzon 昂着头，往旁边啐了一口。\n\n这一切袭击都是你的错。你的承诺。你的交易……但我猜 Zalarjin 说得对：十字军是个威胁，而你能帮我们对抗他们。\n\n你想做点有用的事吗？\n\n我的长矛手 Tarjani 出去在海滩上抵挡他们了。她还没回来。如果她还活着，一定是躲起来了，受了伤，或者被围住了。\n\n找到她。",dEN="Last thing we needed was more of your kind.\n\n<Alotzon spits to the side, his head held high.>\n\nDis whole attack be your fault. Your promises. Your bargains… But I suppose Zalarjin be right: da crusaders are a threat ya can help us fight.\n\nYa want ta do somethin’ useful?\n\nMy spear, Tarjani, went out ta hold ’em back on da beach. She ain’t returned yet. If she still breathes, she be hidden, wounded, or surrounded.\n\nFind her.",o="Tarjani，Zandor 之矛，在十字军袭击海岸后失踪了。",oEN="Tarjani, the Spear of Zandor, who went missing after the crusader attack on the shore.",p="嗯？",pEN="Yes?",c="<Tarjani 仍躲在染血的岩石之间，呼吸急促，一只手紧紧按在肋侧。>\n\n<她花了一会儿才认出你是盟友。直到那时她才放下武器。>\n\n部落……\n\n当然。\n\n<她试图起身，但剧痛迫使她单膝跪倒在地。>",cEN="<Tarjani remains hidden among bloodstained rocks, her breath ragged, one hand pressed tight against her side.>\n\n<It takes her a moment to recognize you as an ally. Only then does she lower her weapon.>\n\nHorde...\n\nOf course.\n\n<She tries to rise, but the pain forces her down onto one knee.>"}
Q[175212]={d="Zandor 的人们认为海岸上的十字军是某种报复。你知道的：我们在南边 Scadeald 挑起的那场战争。\n\n他们是否正确并不重要。重要的是我们能把这个局面转变成对我们有利的东西：\n\n我们可以让他们看到部落的价值。\n\n拿着这些命令。把它们交给驻扎在村子各处的我们的士兵。现在比以往任何时候都更需要我们做出表率。",dEN="Da people of Zandor believe da crusaders on their shores be some kind of reprisal. Ya know: da war we started in Scadeald, ta da south.\n\nWhether dey be right or not is irrelevant. What matters is dat we can turn da situation ta our advantage:\n\nWe can show ’em da Horde’s worth.\n\nTake dese orders. Deliver ’em ta our soldiers posted around da village. Now more than ever, we need ta set an example.",o="把 Zalarjin 的新命令交给驻扎在 Zandor 的部落士兵。",oEN="Deliver Zalarjin’s new orders to the Horde soldiers stationed in Zandor.",p="现在是时候证明，部落的纪律之中自有力量。",pEN="Now be da time ta show dere is strength in Horde discipline.",c="很好。\n\n十字军之所以能走到这一步，不过是因为这岛上没人料到来袭，也没人成功组织起一次像样的反击。\n\n<巫医斜眼看了 Alotzon 一眼。>\n\n他不在乎战争的那套规矩。但我们的纪律之中自有力量。\n\n运气好的话，接下来几天会让他看清这个道理。",cEN="Good.\n\nDa crusaders have only gotten dis far because nobody on dis island expected an attack, and nobody has managed ta organize a proper counterattack.\n\n<The witch doctor casts a sidelong glance at Alotzon.>\n\nHe does not care for da bureaucracy of war. But dere is strength in our discipline.\n\nWith luck, da coming days will open his eyes ta dat truth."}
Q[175213]={d="我杀了几个，但人太多了。\n\n<Tarjani 痛得咬紧牙关。>\n\n他们带着一种病态的信念行动。他们相信他们的圣光会把他们从任何危险中拯救出来。\n\n让他们看看自己错得有多离谱。能杀多少就杀多少。 <Tarjani rechina los dientes por el dolor>",dEN="I killed a few of dem, but dere be too many.\n\n<Tarjani grits her teeth against the pain.>\n\nDey act with a sick conviction. And dey believe their Light will save dem from any danger.\n\nShow dem how wrong dey are. Kill as many as ya can.",o="在 Druk'thar 岛上杀死 Hallow Wind 十字军的新兵。",oEN="Slay Hallow Wind Crusaders Aspirant on the island of Druk’thar.",p="你把他们都杀了吗？",pEN="Have ya killed dem?",c="<Tarjani 虚弱而心不在焉地点了点头>。\n\n少了一些……很好。\n\n要是你部落派来的所有士兵都像你这样战斗，我们早就把这群瘟疫清除了。",cEN="<Tarjani gives a weak, distracted nod.>\n\nA few less... Good.\n\nIf all da soldiers your Horde sent fought like you, we would have wiped out dis plague already."}
Q[175214]={d="<Tarjani 握着一块漆黑的石头，它随着一声几乎听不见的低语而颤动，像是被困在冰下的声音>。\n\n<犹豫片刻之后，她把那块幽魂石交给你。它触手冰冷，冷得发痛>。\n\n拿着这个。用它对付他们的船。困在里面的灵魂知道该怎么做。它们会钻进他们的身体，把恐惧灌满他们的肺，再把它们拖入水底。",dEN="<Tarjani holds a dark stone that trembles with a barely audible murmur, like voices trapped beneath the ice.>\n\n<After a moment of hesitation, she hands you the spectral stone. It is so cold to the touch that it hurts.>\n\nTake dis. Use it against their ships. Da spirits trapped within will know what ta do. Dey will enter their bodies, fill their lungs with fear, and drag dem down into da water.",o="用 Tarjani 的幽魂石对付 Hallow Wind 的船舰，将它们击沉。",oEN="Use Tarjani’s spectral stone against the Hallow Wind vessels to sink them.",p="不要惧怕那些灵魂。它们知道你是谁。也知道你为什么而来。它们不会为难你。",pEN="Do not fear da spirits. Dey know who ya are. And dey know what ya came ta do. Dey will leave ya be.",c="对……\n\n我感觉到了。\n\n<Tarjani 露出一抹短暂而凶悍的笑容>。\n\n十字军的惨叫将永远在这些水域中回荡。而他们的灵魂将沉入他们的圣光也无法触及的深处。\n\n干得好，部落。 <Tarjani muestra una breve y feroz sonrisa>",cEN="Yes...\n\nI felt it.\n\n<Tarjani bares a brief, ferocious smile.>\n\nDa screams of da crusaders will echo forever in dese waters. And their spirits will sink ta depths their Light cannot reach.\n\nGood work, Horde."}
Q[175215]={d="Samael 神父……谁……？啊，对……\n\n<Tarjani 只用近乎耳语的声音说话。她那发热的目光表明她可能没剩多少时间了>。\n\n灵魂们愤怒了。它们害怕。这些十字军的首领进了 Alta'tharon，正在复活我们祖先的木乃伊。\n\n<Tarjani 虚弱地指向附近的废墟>。\n\n你不能容许这种亵渎……让死者重归安宁……",dEN="Father Samael... Who...? Ah, yes...\n\n<Tarjani speaks in little more than a whisper. Her feverish stare suggests she may not have much time left.>\n\nDa spirits are furious. Frightened. Da leader of dese crusaders has gone into Alta'tharon, and he be raising da mummies of our ancestors.\n\n<Tarjani points weakly toward the nearby ruins.>\n\nYa cannot allow dis desecration... Bring peace back ta da dead...",o="进入 Alta'tharon，击败 Samael 神父召唤的砾光木乃伊。",oEN="Enter Alta'tharon and defeat the Gravelight mummies raised by Father Samael.",p="Alta'tharon 的死者已经受够了。",pEN="Da dead of Alta'tharon have suffered enough already.",c="你为死者带来了安息。\n\n<那幽灵低下头。她空洞的眼睛似乎从很远的地方望着你；也许是另一个世界>。\n\n我叫 Osairas；曾经是一位 Drakkari 女祭司。我死在把我们带到这些海岸的船上，是最早被埋葬在这里的人之一。\n\n那个圣光之人亵渎了我的坟墓。",cEN="Ya have brought rest ta da dead.\n\n<The apparition bows her head. Her empty eyes seem to look at you from very far away; another world, perhaps.>\n\nMy name be Osairas; a Drakkari priestess, once. I died on da ship dat brought us ta dese shores, and I was among da first ta be buried here.\n\nDa man of da Light has desecrated my tomb."}
Q[175216]={d="那个圣光之人……他对我们做的一切……他给自己挣来了比死亡更糟的命运。\n\n<Osairas 从脖子上取下一枚古老的幽魂护身符。它一碰到你的手，就变得坚实>。\n\n我是带着它下葬的。等 Samael 倒下时用它。把他的灵魂从躯体里拽出来，锁进我们的一只陪葬瓮里。\n\n让他在那里布道吧，孤独地、在黑暗之中，直到他忘记自己那些话的含义。",dEN="Dat man of da Light... what he has done ta us... He has earned a fate worse than death.\n\n<Osairas removes an ancient spectral amulet from around her neck. As it touches your hands, it becomes solid.>\n\nI was buried with dis. Use it when Samael falls. Tear his spirit from his body, and lock it inside one of our funerary jars.\n\nLet him preach in dere, alone and in darkness, until he forgets da meaning of his own words.",o="击败 Samael 神父，用 Osairas 的护身符捕获他的灵魂，并把它封进一只巨魔陪葬瓮中。",oEN="Defeat Father Samael, capture his spirit with Osairas's amulet, and imprison it inside a troll funerary jar.",p="你带来 Tarjani 和十字军的消息了吗？",pEN="Do ya bring news of Tarjani and da crusaders?",c="<Alotzon 默默地听着你讲述 Alta'tharon 的地穴以及十字军首领 Samael 神父所受的惩罚>。\n\n你说有一种能让死者复生的圣光？我们从没听说过这种东西。\n\n<他看向 Zalarjin，想听听他的意见。巫医摇了摇头>。\n\n你为 Zandor 做的事，比我预想的更为重大，<race>。\n\n这并不意味着我信任你的部落。但这已经是第一步。",cEN="<Alotzon listens in silence as you tell him of the crypts of Alta'tharon and the punishment dealt to the crusaders' leader, Father Samael.>\n\nA kind of Light dat can give life ta da dead, ya say? We have never heard of such a thing.\n\n<He looks to Zalarjin for his opinion. The witch doctor shakes his head.>\n\nYa have done Zandor a greater service than I imagined, <race>.\n\nIt does not mean I trust your Horde. But it be a first step."}
Q[175217]={d="这座岛会安全。暂时。\n\n<Alotzon 说这话时的语气，仿佛这些字尝起来像灰烬。>\n\n但 Druk'thar 并不止于 Zandor，我的担忧也一样。袭击之前，我派 Jakunda 带一小队人去了 Sown 海岸。他们要去查看北面的隘口，寻找其他登陆的迹象。\n\n他们没有回来。\n\n循着他们的踪迹走。找营火、脚印、被压平的草；任何能说明他们遭遇的痕迹。",dEN="Da island be safe. For now.\n\n<Alotzon says those words as if they taste like ash.>\n\nBut Druk'thar does not end at Zandor, and neither do my concerns. Before da attack, I sent Jakunda ta da Sown Coast with a small group. Dey were ta check da northern passes and look for signs of other landings.\n\nDey have not returned.\n\nFollow their trail. Look for campfires, tracks, flattened grass; any sign of what became of dem.",o="沿着 Sown 海岸追踪 Jakunda 的踪迹，查明他的队伍遭遇了什么。",oEN="Follow Jakunda's trail along the Sown Coast and discover what happened to his group.",p="<Jakunda 抬起一只手，像是要你压低声音。>",pEN="<Jakunda raises a hand, as if asking you to lower your voice.>",c="<Jakunda 抬起一只手，仿佛在请你放低声音。>\n\n保持冷静。这些雪人很不安，而且理由充分。他们最不需要的就是更多喊叫声。\n我猜是 Alotzon 派你来的。\n\n<听完你的回答，传来一声长长而疲惫的叹息。>\n\n我想十字军仍然是他的头等大事，但这儿的情况也没好到哪去。",cEN="<Jakunda raises a hand, as if asking you to lower your voice.>\n\nStay calm. Dese yeti be unsettled, and with good reason. Da last thing dey need is more shouting.\nAlotzon sent ya, I suppose.\n\n<A long, weary sigh follows your answer.>\n\nI suppose da crusaders are still his priority, but things are no better here."}
Q[175218]={d="你让 Alotzon 印象深刻，但 Zandor 不过是个村庄。重要的决定都在 Thundrakar 做出。\n\n<Zalarjin 在你面前展开一张该地区的地图。他的手指先指向岛屿，随后沿着海岸线滑向内陆。>\n\nThundrakar 是 Frostmane 的首都，也是 Mexitla 统治的所在地。她忙于处理比这座岛上的十字军严重得多的问题。\n\n那些问题或许你能帮上忙。\n\n去向她报到。投身她的麾下。少说话，多倾听，不要许下你日后无法变成优势的承诺。",dEN="Ya have impressed Alotzon, but Zandor be little more than a village. Da important decisions are made in Thundrakar.\n\n<Zalarjin spreads a map of the region before you. His fingers point to the island first, then slide along the coast and inland.>\n\nThundrakar be da capital of da Frostmane, and da seat of Mexitla's rule. She keeps herself busy with problems on a far greater scale than da crusaders on dis island.\n\nProblems ya may be able ta help with.\n\nPresent yourself before her. Enter her service. Speak little, listen well, and promise nothing ya cannot later turn ta advantage.",o="前往 Thundrakar，以部落的名义向 Mexitla 公主报到，投身她的麾下。",oEN="Present yourself before Princess Mexitla in Thundrakar and enter her service in the name of the Horde.",p="<公主的双眼如同两杆长矛，将你刺穿。>",pEN="<The princess's eyes are two spears, piercing you through.>",c="所以，这就是你那坚定不移的忠诚……\n\n<她说话时几乎没有提高声音，却迫使在场所有人安静下来、凝神倾听。>\n\n在我的人民受了这么多苦之后，你的效劳尝起来相当单薄。毕竟，若不是部落和它的野心，我们也不会落到这个境地。\n\n但说到底，我想责任只在我自己。\n\n<一道坚定的光芒点亮了公主的双眼。>\n\n很好。那就这样。我接受你的效劳。",cEN="So, your unwavering loyalty...\n\n<She barely raises her voice when she speaks, forcing everyone present into silence and attention.>\n\nAfter all my people have suffered, your service tastes rather thin. After all, we would not find ourselves in this position were it not for the Horde and its ambition.\n\nBut at the end of the day, I suppose the blame is mine alone.\n\n<A flash of determination lights the princess's eyes.>\n\nVery well. So be it. I accept your service."}
Q[175219]={d="他们说 Wangard 的新领主 Gharma 是个残暴的暴君。他的打手已经切断了上山的路。接下来就是公开的战争了。\n\n那是一场屠杀。那些没有立刻向他宣誓效忠的雪人被杀死了。只有少数几个得以逃脱并向我们报信。\n\n以 Druk'thar 目前的状况，我怀疑 Alotzon 不会派人来帮忙。但你……你的气息对他们来说是陌生的，而且显然你懂得怎么打一场架。\n\n听起来像是找死，但你愿意潜入 Wangard，杀掉那个暴君吗？",dEN="They say da new lord of Wangard, Gharma, be a violent despot. His thugs have already cut off da road up da mountain. Next comes open war.\n\nIt was a slaughter. Da yeti who did not swear loyalty ta him at once were killed. Only a few managed ta flee and warn us.\n\nWith things as dey are in Druk'thar, I doubt Alotzon will send anyone ta help. But you... Your scent will be unknown ta dem, and it be clear ya know your way around a fight.\n\nSounds like an invitation ta suicide, but would ya be willing ta sneak into Wangard and kill da tyrant?",o="进入 Wangard，击败暴君雪崩Gharma。",oEN="Enter Wangarda and defeat Despot Gharma, the Avalanche.",p="<那个雪人不过是一堆血淋淋的残躯，被随意地摊在地上。>",pEN="<The yeti is little more than a bloodied heap, sprawled carelessly on the ground.>",c="<Ruhl 的皮毛上沾满暗色的血。虽然脉搏微弱，他仍在呼吸。无论如何，那些伤口很难看；他只剩几分钟可活了。>\n\nGharma……雪崩。Gharma……流放者……\n\n打手……凶手……\n\n<一阵深咳震动着他的胸膛。>",cEN="<Ruhl's fur is stained with dark blood. Though his pulse is weak, he is still breathing. One way or another, the wounds are ugly; he has only minutes left to live.>\n\nGharma... the Avalanche. Gharma... the Exile...\n\nThugs... murderers...\n\n<A deep cough shakes his chest.>"}
Q[175220]={d="Wangard 的旧领主 Ohlos 是一位睿智的领袖，深受族人的爱戴。也许，尽管心怀恐惧，仍有一些雪人愿意为正义而起身对抗这位新暴君。\n\n尤其是当他们看见你在收拾他的打手时。\n\n务必尽可能多杀一些。",dEN="Da old lord of Wangard, Ohlos, was a wise leader, beloved by his people. It be possible dat, despite their fear, some yeti still be willing ta rise up for what is right against da new despot.\n\nEspecially if dey see ya putting down his thugs.\n\nMake sure ya kill as many as ya can.",o="在 Wangard 击败 Gharma 的打手，用他们的死激励忠于旧领主 Ohlos 的雪人。",oEN="Defeat Gharma's thugs in Wangarda and inspire the yeti loyal to Ohlos, their former lord, with their deaths.",p="<那个雪人不过是一堆血淋淋的残躯，被随意地摊在地上。>",pEN="<The yeti is little more than a bloodied heap, sprawled carelessly on the ground.>",c="<你有一种感觉，Ruhl 正在吐出他最后几口痛苦的呼吸。>\n\n全都……白费了……",cEN="<You get the sense that Ruhl is drawing his final, agonized breaths.>\n\nAll... for nothing..."}
Q[175221]={d="<雪人用最后一口气，喃喃说出几个沾满血的字。>\n\nGharma……并非一直……是巨人。\n\n有什么……改变了他。<一阵咳嗽把血喷得到处都是。> 让他长大……让他变得……怪物一般。\n\n我去查……\n\n洞穴……\n\nSoulfrost……\n\nSoulfrost……\n\n<这是这个雪人此生说出的最后的话。>",dEN="<With his final breath, the yeti mutters a few bloodstained words.>\n\nGharma... not always... giant.\n\nSomething... changed him. <A fit of coughing sprays blood in every direction.> Made him grow... Made him... monstrous.\n\nI investigate...\n\nCave...\n\nSoulfrost...\n\nSoulfrost...\n\n<It is the last word this yeti will ever speak.>",o="找到 Soulfrost 洞穴，查明 Gharma 怪物般成长的缘由。",oEN="Find Soulfrost Cave and uncover the reason behind Gharma's monstrous growth.",p="嗯？",pEN="Yes?",c="小心！这洞穴……你没看见吗？从后壁渗出来的水带有辐射。\n\n你认识这个词吗？你知道它是什么意思吗？\n\n带——有——辐——射。被污染。被玷污。被腐化……\n\n\"屎\"，<他带着一丝嘲弄补充道，仿佛那是你唯一能听懂的词。>",cEN="Careful! This cave... Can't you see it? The water seeping through the back wall is irradiated.\n\nDo you know the word? Do you know what it means?\n\nI-rra-di-a-ted. Contaminated. Polluted. Tainted...\n\n“Poop,” <he adds with a touch of mockery, as if it were the only word you could understand.>"}
Q[175222]={d="<药剂师正要挥手让你走，但最后一刻似乎改变了主意。>\n\n其实，既然你来了……\n\n<他递给你一只玻璃小瓶。空的。>\n\n去那个水潭一趟，好吗？把小瓶浸到液体里。我要你亲自把采集到的样本带给 Mexitla 公主。她会想知道病河的辐射扩散到了多远。",dEN="<The apothecary is about to wave you off, but appears to think better of it at the last moment.>\n\nActually, since you're here...\n\n<He offers you a glass vial. Empty.>\n\nGo over to the pool, would you? Dip the vial into the liquid. I want you to take the sample you collect to Princess Mexitla in person. She will want to know just how far the Sickened River's radiation has spread.",o="把玻璃小瓶浸入 Soulfrost 洞穴内受污染的水潭，然后把样本带给 Thundrakar 的 Mexitla 公主。",oEN="Dip the glass vial into the contaminated pool inside Soulfrost Cave, then bring the sample to Princess Mexitla in Thundrakar.",p="那么……？",pEN="Well...?",c="<公主仔细地听着。>\n\n所以，是 Soulfrost 洞穴。这不是好兆头；尽管我们已经尽力，辐射仍在扩散。\n\n而 Wangard 的这位新暴君喝了那个受污染水潭里的水？\n\n<有那么一瞬间，王冠的重量似乎沉重得难以承受。随后她很快恢复了镇定。>\n\n你拥有我的感激。",cEN="<The princess listens carefully.>\n\nSo. Soulfrost Cave. That is not a good omen; the radiation is spreading, despite our efforts.\n\nAnd this new despot of Wangard drank from that tainted pool?\n\n<For a moment, the weight of the crown seems too heavy to bear. Then she quickly regains her composure.>\n\nYou have my gratitude."}
Q[175224]={d="Druk'thar 的灵魂们变得不安。你感觉不到吗？你意识边缘的低语。\n\n它们索要供品。\n\n<Olira 指向 Zandor 的篝火，火焰低沉而苍白地噼啪作响。>\n\n你想帮忙吗？我需要你去采集我们称作\"圣礼嫩芽\"的植物，然后抓一大把投进篝火里。\n\n这是 Zandor 的一项神圣仪式；它会教导这座岛上的灵魂容忍你的部落的存在。",dEN="Da spirits of Druk'thar grow restless. Can ya not feel it? Whispers at da edges of your mind.\n\nDey demand offerings.\n\n<Olira points to the bonfire of Zandor, its flames crackling low and pale.>\n\nYa want ta help? I need ya ta gather da plant we call Sacramental Sprout, and throw a good handful of it into da bonfire.\n\nIt be a sacred ritual here in Zandor; it will teach da spirits of dis island ta tolerate da presence of your “Horde.”",o="在 Druk'thar 岛上采集圣礼嫩芽，把它们投进 Zandor 的篝火，以鼓舞巨魔并安抚灵魂。",oEN="Gather sacramental sprouts on the island of Druk'thar and throw them into Zandor's bonfire to inspire the trolls and appease the spirits.",p="灵魂们在等待他们的供品。",pEN="Da spirits await their offering.",c="那些声音已经平息。灵魂们满意了。\n\n<Olira 吸了一口篝火的芳香烟雾，微微一笑。>\n\n要他们接受与部落共享这座岛的想法，还需要时间，但以我的经验，他们会比许多活人更早接受我们两族之间的同盟。",cEN="Da voices have grown calm. Da spirits be pleased.\n\n<Olira breathes in the aromatic smoke from the bonfire and smiles.>\n\nIt will still take dem time ta accept da idea of sharing dis island with da Horde, but in my experience, dey will accept da alliance between our peoples before many of da living do."}
Q[175225]={d="战争有许多种杀死人的方式；有些比另一些更快。\n\n<Haraze 双臂交叉，神情阴沉。>\n\n饥饿也许是其中最糟的。而 Thundrakar 要靠我们才能吃上饭。\n\n幸运的是，灵魂们给了我答案：我们要一石二鸟。\n\n你要去海岸，对吧？拿上我的刀。用它把你杀死的十字军切分。然后把能用的肉带到 Thundrakar 交给 Nozdaru。",dEN="War has many ways ta kill; some quicker than others.\n\n<Haraze folds his arms, his expression grim.>\n\nHunger be perhaps da worst of all. And Thundrakar depends on us for food.\n\nFortunately, da spirits have given me da answer: we kill two birds with one stone.\n\nYa are headed ta da coast, yes? Take my knife. Use it ta carve up da crusaders ya kill. Then bring da usable meat ta Nozdaru in Thundrakar.",o="从 Hallow Wind 十字军身上取得人肉条，送到 Thundrakar 的 Nozdaru 那里。",oEN="Obtain strips of human meat from the Hallow Wind crusaders and deliver them to Nozdaru in Thundrakar.",p="我能帮你什么？",pEN="How can I help ya?",c="那是……人肉？\n\n<一阵厌恶掠过巨魔的脸。>\n\n别误会我；我们的储备已经开始见底，而这批货来得正是时候。\n\n只是……人肉又干又柴。这里有些人宁愿挨饿。",cEN="Dat be... human meat?\n\n<A look of disgust crosses the troll's face.>\n\nDo not misunderstand me; our stores were beginning ta run low, and this shipment comes at da best possible time.\n\nIt is just... human meat be dry and stringy. Some here would rather fast."}
Q[175226]={d="啊，你已经加入部落了，是吗？靠近点，再靠近点！看看我这简陋祭坛里的水。\n\n我叫 Alzana。女巫。女祭司。\n\n如果你愿意，我可以给你讲讲我们的 Loa。曾经，他们倾听我们。他们是我们的守护神、我们的保护者、我们的指引者。\n\n但唉！时间并非白白流逝，我们 Frostmane 已经失去了他们曾赐予我们的恩宠。\n\n所以告诉我：你想让我讲讲他们吗？",dEN="Ah, ya come wit’ da Horde, yes? Come closer, come closer! Take a look at da waters of my humble altar.\n\nMy name be Alzana. Witch. Priestess.\n\nI can tell ya of our Loa, if ya wish. Once, dey listened to us. Dey were our tutelary gods, our protectors, our guides.\n\nBut ah! Time has not passed for nothin’, and we Frostmane have lost da favor dey once gave us.\n\nSo tell me: ya want me to speak of dem?",o="听 Alzana 讲述 Frostmane 的 Loa 的故事。",oEN="Listen to Alzana’s tale about the Loa of the Frostmane.",p="对 Loa 的传说感兴趣吗？",pEN="Interested in the Loa's lore?",c="现在你已经知道我们 Loa 的名字了。\n\n到外面的世界去，走我们走过的路，与我们的族人交谈，了解他们的习俗……也许有一天，我们的 Loa 会知道你的名字。",cEN="Now ya know da names of our Loa.\n\nGo out into da world, walk our roads, speak wit’ our people, learn their customs… and perhaps one day our Loa will know your name."}
Q[175227]={d="随着王国的覆灭，那座古老的墓地和死亡 Loa 的神殿先成了一处避难所，随后变成了一座城市：流亡中的首都。\n\n然而，这并不合 Tzotec 的心意。\n\n<Mexitla 毫不掩饰她的怨恨。>\n\n死亡 Loa 觉得受了侮辱。自那以后，他越来越少听我们说话。但他的恩宠反复无常。而我对你有一种预感。\n\n去向他的大祭司 Jabul 报到。告诉他是我派你去的。",dEN="With the fall of the kingdom, the old necropolis and temple of the Loa of Death became a refuge first, and a city after: the capital in exile.\n\nThis did not please Tzotec, however.\n\n<Mexitla makes no effort to hide her resentment.>\n\nThe Loa of Death felt insulted. Since then, he has listened to us less and less. But his favor is fickle. And I have a feeling about you.\n\nPresent yourself before Jabul, his High Priest. Tell him I sent you.",o="在 Thundrakar 向 Tzotec 的大祭司 Jabul 报到。",oEN="Present yourself before Jabul, High Priest of Tzotec, in Thundrakar.",c="<死亡 Loa 的大祭司带着高傲的神情看着你。>\n\n公主给我送来一个陌生人。\n\n有意思。但也不算完全出乎意料；我已经习惯了她的怪癖。\n\n如果 Mexitla 相信你能帮我们修复与 Tzotec 的纽带，那就这样吧。",cEN="<The High Priest of the Loa of Death regards you with a haughty expression.>\n\nThe Princess sends me a stranger.\n\nCurious. But not entirely unexpected; I am accustomed to her eccentricities by now.\n\nIf Mexitla believes you can help mend our bond with Tzotec, then so be it."}
Q[175228]={d="Tzotec 大祭司的职责之一，就是安抚死者。\n\n而近来，他们有理由感到不安。\n\n拿着这个。<Jabul 把一种奇特的熏香放进你手中。> 你曾向 Mexitla 宣誓效忠，不是吗？而她又把你派到我这里，所以，照办吧：\n\n进入地穴，在墓前点燃灵熏香。一份简单的供品，足以安抚大多数。\n\n其他的……嗯，你会发现的。",dEN="Among the duties of Tzotec's High Priest is the appeasement of the dead.\n\nAnd lately, they have reason to be restless.\n\nTake this. <Jabul places a strange incense in your hands.> You swore your unwavering loyalty to Mexitla, did you not? And she sent you to me, so obey:\n\nEnter the crypts and light the spiritual incense at the tombs. A simple offering, enough to calm most of them.\n\nOthers... Well, you will find out.",o="在 Thundrakar 的地穴中点燃灵熏香，安抚亡者的灵魂。",oEN="Light spiritual incense in the crypts of Thundrakar to calm the spirits of the dead.",p="别让死者久等。",pEN="Do not keep da dead waiting.",c="所以熏香奏效了。\n\n<Jabul 心不在焉地对自己点了点头。他甚至没等你确认结果。>\n\n希望 Tzotec 当时在听。",cEN="So the incense worked.\n\n<Jabul nods to himself, distracted. He does not even wait for you to confirm your success.>\n\nI hope Tzotec was paying attention."}
Q[175229]={d="我想你听说过病光之子。他们的腐化，他们所崇拜的辐射，蔓延到各处。甚至在我们脚下。\n\n缓慢地，非常缓慢地，它从他们的山谷渗出来，一直渗到 Thundrakar 最深处的地穴。\n\n<Jabul 抿紧了嘴唇。>\n\n结果，畸形的生物开始出现：辐射软泥，以及更糟的畸变体。\n\n杀了它们。",dEN="I imagine you have heard of the Sicklght Children. Their corruption, the radiation they worship, spreads everywhere. Even beneath our feet.\n\nSlowly, very slowly, it has seeped from their valley until it reached the deepest crypts of Thundrakar.\n\n<Jabul presses his lips together.>\n\nAnd as a result, malformed creatures have begun to appear: radiation slimes, and aberrations worse still.\n\nKill them.",o="消灭在 Thundrakar 深处显现的污染畸变体。",oEN="Eliminate the contaminating aberrations that have manifested in the depths of Thundrakar.",p="看着点脚下……",pEN="Watch where ya step...",c="好。\n\n这解决不了问题，但人不能总是解决问题。往往只能满足于治标。\n\n<Jabul 的目光飘向你头顶上方某个无限遥远的地方。>\n\n你已经证明了自己有用。",cEN="Good.\n\nIt does not solve the problem, but one cannot always do so. Often, one must settle for treating the symptoms.\n\n<Jabul's gaze drifts for a moment toward some infinitely distant point above your head.>\n\nYou have proven useful."}
Q[175230]={d="你和你的人是在 Druk'thar 上岸的，对吧？\n\n那么你一定见过 Zandor 村上方的吊桥，以及高悬在崖壁上雕出的祭坛。\n\n那是 Morakki 的陵墓，我们的第一位国王。\n\n我原想，也许他的恩泽能帮我们引起 Tzotec 的注意。但为此，我们需要一份配得上一国之君的供品。\n\n<Jabul 压低了声音>\n\n墓地的陪葬瓮里藏着贡品珠宝。把它们取来。然后在 Morakki 的祭坛上献上它们。 <Jabul baja la voz>",dEN="You and yours landed on Druk'thar, did you not?\n\nThen ya will have seen da hanging bridges above da village of Zandor, and da altar carved high into da cliffside.\n\nIt is da tomb of Morakki, our first king.\n\nI thought perhaps his favor might help us gain Tzotec's attention. But for dat, we will need an offering worthy of a king.\n\n<Jabul lowers his voice.>\n\nDa funerary urns of da necropolis hold tribute jewels. Take dem. Then offer dem at Morakki's altar.",o="从 Thundrakar 的陪葬瓮中取得贡品珠宝，并在 Morakki 的祭坛上献上。",oEN="Obtain tribute jewels from the funerary urns of Thundrakar and offer them at Morakki's altar.",p="<祭坛上方升起的那道阴影，像一支即将燃尽的蜡烛的火苗般摇曳。>",pEN="<The shadow rising over the altar flickers like the flame of a candle about to burn out.>",c="<祭坛周围的空气沉重。一个低沉的声音从古老的石头中升起。>\n\n从死者那里偷来的珠宝。\n\n<一个幽魂般的身影在你面前升起，庄严而可怖。>\n\nJabul，Jabul！你还在纳闷，为什么死亡 Loa 对你的祈祷充耳不闻……",cEN="<The air around the altar is heavy. A deep voice rises from the ancient stone.>\n\nJewels stolen from da dead.\n\n<A spectral figure rises before you, solemn and terrible.>\n\nJabul, Jabul! And still ya wonder why da Loa of Death turns a deaf ear ta your prayers..."}
Q[175231]={d="我生前是 Tzotec 虔诚的信徒。我可以替你们说情，是的……但看看四周。我的祭坛已经变成了一个粪坑。\n\n<Morakki 的阴影指向那块被海鸥粪便涂成白色的石头>\n\n你们不仅把墓地变成城市而亵渎了它：你们还任由神殿沦为废墟。\n\n想要我的帮助？那就把祭坛清理干净。铲除那些肮脏的鸟，恢复生者从我这里剥夺的尊严。",dEN="I was a devoted follower of Tzotec in life. I could intercede on your behalf, yes... But look around. My altar has become a cesspit.\n\n<Morakki's shadow points to the stone, painted white by seagull droppings.>\n\nYa have not only desecrated da necropolis by turning it into a city: ya have allowed da temple ta fall into ruin.\n\nYa want my help? Then clean da altar. Eradicate those filthy birds and restore da dignity da living have denied me.",o="铲除玷污 Thundrakar 群峰的海鸥，清理 Morakki 的祭坛。",oEN="Eradicate the seagulls profaning the peaks of Thundrakar and clean Morakki's altar.",p="死去的国王依然是国王。",pEN="A dead king is still a king.",c="<Morakki 默默地注视着祭坛。>\n\n这样也就够了。\n\n这并不能抹去那冒犯，但这是个开始。再说，在这样的时代，尊重似乎是比金子更稀有的货币。",cEN="<Morakki contemplates the altar in silence.>\n\nThat will suffice.\n\nIt does not erase the offense, but it is a beginning. And in any case, in these times, respect seems a rarer coin than gold."}
Q[175232]={d="我的躯体并不长眠于此。\n\n这座陵墓只是刻在石头上的象征，仅此而已；一座供生者铭记并献上贡品的纪念碑。\n\n我的骨骸，实际上安放在下方，在金字塔神殿的殡葬室里。\n\n去那里。跪在 Tzotec 面前，以我的名义吟诵那段古老的祈祷。\n\n如果这位 Loa 还记得我的声音，他会透过你们的嘴唇听到它。",dEN="My body does not lie here.\n\nDis tomb be a symbol carved in stone, nothing more; a monument for da living ta remember, and ta offer their tributes.\n\nMy bones, in truth, rest below, in da mortuary chamber of da ziggurat.\n\nGo dere. Kneel before Tzotec and intone da ancient prayer in my name.\n\nIf da Loa still remembers my voice, he will hear it through your lips.",o="进入王室殡葬室，以 Morakki 之名向 Tzotec 吟诵祈祷。",oEN="Enter the royal mortuary chamber and intone a prayer to Tzotec in Morakki's name.",p="古老的字句比石头更沉重。",pEN="Ancient words weigh more than stone.",c="<你还没来得及开口，Jabul 就抬起了一只手，仿佛他已经知道发生了什么。>\n\n我感觉到了。我们都感觉到了。连蜡烛都把火焰弯下，向死亡 Loa 致意。\n\n<Jabul 花了一点时间找回自己的骄傲。>\n\nMorakki 已经代为求情。而 Tzotec……Tzotec 在听。",cEN="<Jabul raises a hand before you can say anything, as if he already knows what happened.>\n\nI felt it. We all did. Even da candles bent their flames in reverence before da Loa of Death.\n\n<Jabul takes a moment to restore his pride.>\n\nMorakki has interceded. And Tzotec... Tzotec listens."}
Q[175233]={d="<从他看你的眼神看来，你的胜利对 Tzotec 的大祭司而言滋味苦涩>\n\n我花了数年时间献上祈祷。举行献祭。忍受他沉默带来的羞辱。\n\n在我们承受了这一切之后……他直到现在才肯开口。对你开口。\n\n<那个\"你\"从他嘴里射出，像一支离弦的箭>\n\n那就这样吧。跨过 Great Beacon 的门槛，攀上它的顶端。死亡 Loa 会在那里等你。",dEN="<By the look he gives you, your triumph tastes bitter to Tzotec's High Priest.>\n\nI have spent years raisin' prayers. Performin' sacrifices. Endurin' da humiliation of his silence.\n\nAfter all we have endured... only now does he deign ta speak. With you.\n\n<That “you” leaves his mouth like an arrow loosed from a bow.>\n\nSo be it. Cross da threshold of da Great Beacon and climb ta its summit. Da Loa of Death will be waitin' for ya there.",o="跨过 Great Beacon 的门槛，在它的顶端与 Tzotec 交谈。",oEN="Cross the threshold of the Great Lighthouse and speak with Tzotec at its summit.",p="如果死亡召唤你，就应声而去。",pEN="If Death calls for you, answer.",c="自从我上次在这上面接见来客，已经过去了数不清的冬天。\n\n不用说，那是一位 Frostmane。\n\n但你，<race>，引起了我的兴趣。\n\n别浪费口舌讲述是什么把你带到我面前：我完全清楚是 Mexitla 公主派你来的，也清楚你是奉 Zalarjin 之命去到她面前的。\n\n这几个世纪以来我一直沉默。\n\n但我并非一无所见。",cEN="Countless winters have passed since I last granted an audience up here.\n\nNeedless to say, it was to a Frostmane.\n\nBut you, <race>, have captured my interest.\n\nDo not waste your breath recounting what brings you before me: I know full well that Princess Mexitla sent you, and that you came before her on Zalarjin's orders.\n\nI have remained silent through all these centuries.\n\nBut I have not been blind."}
Q[175234]={d="你需要我的恩泽。但我和 Frostmane 之间还有债要清：我神殿的亵渎、我仪式的荒废……\n\n这一切削弱了我在彼岸的存在。而死亡的国度是一个争夺激烈的地方。\n\n如果我要崛起，如果我要帮你，我需要养料。而事实上，我觊觎一份绝妙的奖品已经有一段时间了：一棵古老世界之树的活着的火花。\n\n去 Frostbark 森林找 Tizare。她会给你需要的细节。",dEN="You need my favor. But I still have debts to settle with the Frostmane: the profanation of my temple, the neglect of my rituals...\n\nAll of this weakened my presence in the Other Side. And the realm of death is a fiercely contested place.\n\nIf I am to rise, if I am to aid you, I need sustenance. And as it happens, for some time now I have had my eye on an exquisite prize: the living spark of an ancient World Tree.\n\nSeek out Tizare in Frostbark Woods. She will give you the details you need.",o="在 Frostbark 森林向 Tizare 报到。",oEN="Present yourself before Tizare in Frostbark Forest.",c="<Tizare 看着你到来，一点也不意外，仿佛她已经等了一段时间>。\n\n你就是 Tzotec 与之交谈的那个人，是吧？\n那么我把我的底牌交给你。多亏了你，我也听到了他的声音。\n\n他叫我来到这个地方，把你到来所需的一切都准备好。\n\n我们有活儿要干。",cEN="<Tizare watches you arrive without surprise, as though she has been waiting for some time.>\n\nYou be da one Tzotec spoke to, yah?\nDen I give ya my tanks. T'anks to you, I heard his voice too.\n\nHe told me to come to dis place, an' make everytin' ready for ya comin'.\n\nWe got work to do."}
Q[175235]={d="曾经，这一带生长着一棵世界之树。它的生命短暂，如今除了几根树根，几乎什么都没剩下。\n\n但它仍是一处力量之地。它石化的残骸依然攀附着翡翠梦境。\n\nTzotec 打算以那种连结为食。\n\n所以仔细听好，<race>。",dEN="Once, this region held a World Tree. Its life was brief, and hardly anythin' remains of it now but a few roots.\n\nBut it still be a place of power. And its petrified corpse still clings to da Emerald Dream.\n\nTzotec means to feed on dat connection.\n\nSo listen close, <race>.",o="在 Frostbark 森林听 Tizare 说明计划。",oEN="Listen to Tizare's plan in Frostbark Woods.",p="仔细听好。",pEN="Listen close.",c="现在你明白了。至少，明白得够多了。\n\n<Tizare 朝森林侧了侧头。>\n\n把花和果实带回来；谁挡在路上都不重要。",cEN="Now ya understand. Enough, at least.\n\n<Tizare inclines her head toward the forest.>\n\nBring da flower and da fruit; don't matter who stands in your way."}
Q[175236]={d="Coldhorn 雪人把雪花守护在呜咽洞穴，也就是他们的家里。\n\n正如你能想象的，那朵花是他们最珍视的宝物。他们的传说里说，他们失去它的那一天，山上的雪将会死去，世界将变成一团火球。\n\n<Tizare 叹了口气>\n\n时间会证明他们错了。拿走那朵花，不必为他们的迷信操心。 <Tizare suspira>",dEN="Da Coldhorn yeti keep da Snowblossom in Whimpering Cave, their home.\n\nAs ya can imagine, da flower be their most precious possession. Their legends say dat on da day they lose it, da snow on da mountains will die, and da world will become a ball of fire.\n\n<Tizare sighs.>\n\nTime will prove dem wrong. Take da flower, and don't trouble yourself over their superstitions.",o="取得 Coldhorn 雪人在呜咽洞穴中守护的雪花。",oEN="Obtain the Snowblossom guarded by the Coldhorn yeti in Whimpering Cave.",p="花被摘下时不会尖叫。",pEN="A flower does not scream when it is plucked.",c="<Tizare 以出乎意料的轻柔接过那朵花。>\n\n美丽。脆弱。短暂。三件总是一同出现的事。\n\n对。这个能用。 <Tizare toma la flor con una delicadeza inesperada>",cEN="<Tizare takes the flower with unexpected delicacy.>\n\nBeautiful. Fragile. Fleeting. Three tings dat go hand in hand.\n\nYes. Dis will do."}
Q[175237]={d="霜果存放在根植圣所中。\n\nFrostbark 的熊怪最初是通过大树与翡翠梦境的连结来到这片土地的，他们把这种果实变成了崇拜之物。\n\n别跟他们争论。别想和平解决这件事。不值得，我们也没时间。\n\n拿走果实，然后回来。",dEN="Da Frostfruit rests in da Rooted Sanctuary.\n\nDa Frostbark furbolgs first came to dese lands through da Great Tree's bond with da Emerald Dream, and made da fruit into an object of worship.\n\nDo not argue with dem. Do not try to do dis peacefully. It ain't worth it, and we got no time.\n\nTake da fruit and return.",o="取得 Frostbark 熊怪在根植圣所中守护的霜果。",oEN="Obtain the Frostfruit guarded by the Frostbark furbolgs in the Rooted Sanctuary.",p="森林给予。我们只是收取。",pEN="Da forest gives. We simply collect.",c="<Tizare 用手指转动着果实，端详它被霜冻硬化的表皮>。\n\n迷人。它在跳动，像一颗心脏。\n\n这样一来，它就与每一颗心脏终将遭遇的命运相同。\n\n死亡。",cEN="<Tizare turns the fruit between her fingers, studying its skin, hardened by frost.>\n\nFascinatin'. It beats, like a heart.\n\nIn dat way, it shares da fate every heart will suffer one day.\n\nDeath."}
Q[175238]={d="作为大树的遗存，花与果实都在 Tzotec 的触及范围之外。它们是生命的遗物，而他是死亡 Loa。水火不容。\n\n要让他吞食其中蕴含的能量，我们必须先用死亡魔法为它们调味。\n\n<Tizare 递给你一枚黑色护身符，冷得像放在尸体眼睛上的硬币。>\n\n把它用在你杀死的 Coldhorn 雪人和 Frostbark 熊怪的尸体上。他们的灵魂将被不可解开地系于死亡 Loa 的胃口之下。",dEN="As vestiges of da Great Tree, da flower and da fruit be beyond Tzotec's reach. Dey be relics of Life, and he be da Loa of Death. Water and oil.\n\nFor him to devour da energy dey hold, we must season dem first with death magic.\n\n<Tizare hands you a black amulet, cold as a coin laid over a corpse's eyes.>\n\nUse it on da bodies of da Coldhorn yeti and Frostbark furbolgs ya kill. Their souls will be bound beyond untanglin' to da Loa of Death's apetites.",o="用 Tizare 的护身符施于 Coldhorn 雪人与 Frostbark 熊怪的尸体，夺取他们的灵魂。",oEN="Use Tizare's amulet on the corpses of Coldhorn yeti and Frostbark furbolgs to claim their souls.",p="新鲜的灵魂更轻。",pEN="Fresh souls weigh less.",c="<Tizare 把护身符举到耳边，仿佛在听里面的什么东西>。\n\n对。这就够了。\n\n他们当然不高兴。但他们的痛苦会很短暂，在那之后他们会得到安宁。真正的安宁。",cEN="<Tizare raises the amulet to her ear, as if listening to something inside.>\n\nYes. Dis will be enough.\n\nDey not happy, of course. But their agony will be brief, and after dat dey will know peace. True peace."}
Q[175239]={d="雪花。霜果。还有你偷来的那些灵魂。死亡 Loa 很满意。对你满意。\n\n只剩下仪式了。\n\n<一阵狂热的笑容在 Tizare 脸上铺开一张皱纹的网。>\n\n萌芽祭坛是一座古老的 Frostmane 神殿，建在大树中空树干的遗骸之中。\n\n把所有东西带到祭坛，把遗物浸入幼树的树液。树的魔法当然会抵抗。守护者会来。但没关系。\n\n我们的胜利是注定的。",dEN="Da Snowblossom. Da Frostfruit. And da souls ya stole. Da Loa of Death be pleased. With you.\n\nOnly da ritual remains.\n\n<A manic smile spreads a web of wrinkles across Tizare's face.>\n\nDa Altar of da Bud be an ancient Frostmane temple built in da remains of da Great Tree's hollow trunk.\n\nBring everytin' to da altar and sink da relics into da sapling's sap. Da tree's magic will resist, of course. Guardians will come. But it won't matter.\n\nOur triumph be predestined.",o="把花与果实带到萌芽祭坛，获得神圣萌芽的祝福。",oEN="Bring the flower and the fruit to the Altar of the Sapling and obtain the Sacred Bud's Blessing.",p="并非一切神圣之物都仁慈。",pEN="Not everytin' sacred be kind.",c="<一阵颤抖出卖了 Tizare 平静的面具。她的宗教狂热如此强烈，看上去几乎要落泪>。\n\n你做到了。死亡之种是你的了。我感觉到它的搏动。我的双腿发软……\n\n太庄严了。",cEN="<A tremor betrays Tizare's mask of serenity. Her religious fervor is so intense she seems on the verge of tears.>\n\nYa did it. Da Seed of Death be yours. I feel its pulse. My legs go weak...\n\nIt be sublime."}
Q[175240]={d="Tzotec 失去耐心了。我感觉到他的饥饿。他的声音命令我：\n\n你必须尽快到他面前去。他那残酷的喙对死亡之种的渴望，胜过这世上任何宝藏。\n\n哦，我的主人！要是您没有为我安排另一种命运，我也乐于把我的灵魂献给您！\n\n<在长久的沉默之后，Tizare 用更平静的眼神看着你。>\n\n等你准备好了就告诉我。死亡 Loa 在等你。",dEN="Tzotec grows impatient. I feel his hunger. His voice commands me:\n\nYou must present yourself before him as soon as ya can. His cruel beak craves da Seed of Death more than any treasure in dis world.\n\nOh, my lord! I would gladly give ya my soul as well, had ya not set another fate before me!\n\n<After a long silence, Tizare looks at you with calmer eyes.>\n\nTell me when ya be ready. Da Loa of Death awaits ya.",o="等你准备好前往 Great Beacon 顶端拜访 Tzotec，并把死亡之种交给他时，与 Tizare 交谈。",oEN="Speak with Tizare when you are ready to visit Tzotec atop the Great Beacon, and deliver the Seed of Death to him.",p="我没有看错你，凡人。",pEN="I was not wrong about you, mortal.",c="我一直跟着你的脚步。\n\n我看见了你洒下的每一滴血，看到雪地被染红时我欢欣不已。\n\n我听见了你敌人的惨叫，品尝了他们的绝望。\n\n当然，我也尝过了你作为贡品献给我的那些灵魂。\n\n<Tzotec 的双眼闪着贪婪的光>。\n\n只剩下吞食死亡之种了。",cEN="I have followed your steps.\n\nI have seen every drop of blood you spilled, and rejoiced to see the snow stained red.\n\nI have heard the screams of your enemies, and savored their despair.\n\nAnd of course, I have tasted the souls you offered me in tribute.\n\n<Tzotec's eyes flash, ravenous.>\n\nOnly the Seed of Death remains to be consumed."}
Q[175241]={d="好。\n\n很好。\n\n<死亡 Loa 的声音断断续续。他的全部注意力似乎都用在消化那颗种子上了。>\n\n至于我的祝福……别说 Tzotec 言而无信。与 Frostmane 不同，我仍然记得荣誉的含义。\n\n你拥有我的祝福。时机到来时，我的力量会助你一臂之力。要确保那头名叫 Matlacan 的野兽死去，还有谁比我更合适？",dEN="Good.\n\nVery good.\n\n<The Loa of Death speaks with a halting voice. It seems all his focus is on digesting the seed.>\n\nAs for my blessing... Let it not be said that Tzotec breaks his word. Unlike the Frostmane, I still remember the meaning of honor.\n\nYou have my blessing. When the time comes, my power will aid you. Who better than I to ensure the death of that beast once called Matlacan?",o="告知 Mexitla 死亡 Loa Tzotec 的祝福。",oEN="Inform Mexitla of the blessing of the Loa of Death, Tzotec.",p="又是你。过了一阵子了。说吧。",pEN="Tú de nuevo. Ha pasao un tiempo. Habla.",c="让一位公主说不出话来，是件稀罕事。\n\n当我请你去和 Jabul 谈谈时，我只有一点微弱的希望，觉得你也许能帮上我们。\n\n但这个…… <Mexitla 深吸一口气，仿佛死亡 Loa 的祝福能在空气中被感觉到>。\n\n这不是帮助。这是救赎。",cEN="It be a rare thing to leave a princess wit'out words.\n\nWhen I asked ya to speak wit' Jabul, I had a faint hope you might help us.\n\nBut dis... <Mexitla takes a deep breath, as if the Loa of Death's blessing could be felt in the air itself.>\n\nDis was not help. Dis was salvation."}
Q[175242]={d="Zarkon 不承认 Mexitla 的权威。\n\n他说，一个与外来者做交易的公主不配统治 Frostmane。正如你所见，这是危险的话。\n\n<Kekazar 往地上啐了一口。>\n现在他和他的战士正擅自攻打 Dun Argan 的矮人。如果他们还没死，也一定快了。\n去找 Zeken。他会知道那个白痴把自己弄到哪儿去了。",dEN="Zarkon does not recognize Mexitla's authority.\n\nHe says a princess who bargains with outsiders does not deserve ta rule da Frostmane. Dangerous words, as ya can see.\n\n<Kekazar spits on the ground.>\n\nNow he and his warriors are attackin' da dwarves of Dun Argan on their own. If dey are not dead yet, dey must be close ta it.\n\nFind Zeken. He will know where dat idiot has gotten himself.",o="在 Dun Argan 附近寻找 Zarkon 的战士。",oEN="Find Zarkon's warriors near Dun Argan.",c="<Zeken 带着混合着不信任与玩味的神情把你上下打量了一番>。\n\n是 Kekazar 派你来的？\n\n哈。\n\n公主的追随者和她一模一样：谁给帮助他们都接受……",cEN="<Zeken looks you up and down with a mix of distrust and amusement.>\n\nKekazar sent ya?\n\nHa.\n\nDa princess's followers are just like her: dey will take help from anyone..."}
Q[175243]={d="Zarkon 带着另外几个人先走了一步。他还没回来。\n\n这可能意味着两件事：要么矮人杀了他，要么他正忙于杀矮人。\n\n<Zeken 咧嘴一笑，露出满口牙齿。>\n\n我宁愿相信是后者。\n\n杀掉 Dun Argan 的山民。把他们的胡子带给我。唯一的好胡子就是死胡子。\n\n要是他们中有谁死得太慢，就问问他们的胡子朋友在哪儿。",dEN="Zarkon went on ahead with a few others. He has not come back.\n\nThat can mean two things: either da dwarves killed him, or he be too busy killin' dwarves.\n\n<Zeken smiles with all his teeth.>\n\nI prefer ta think it be da second.\n\nKill Dun Argan mountaineers. Bring me their beards. Da only good beardling be a dead beardling.\n\nAnd if any of dem take too long ta die, ask where their bearded friends are.",o="杀死 Dun Argan 的山民，收集他们的胡子作为凭证",oEN="Kill Dun Argan mountaineers and collect their beards as proof",p="你是……？",pEN="And you are...?",c="<Zarkon 从你手中夺过一把血淋淋的胡子，赞许地端详着>。\n\n好。\n\n矮人懂得的事不多。血是其中之一。",cEN="<Zarkon tears a bloodied beard from your hands and studies it with approval.>\n\nGood.\n\nDwarves understand few things. Blood be one of dem."}
Q[175244]={d="矮人爱他们的箱子。\n\n装食物的箱子。装火药的箱子。装工具的箱子。大概还有装着更多箱子的箱子。\n\n<Zeken 递给你一支熏黑的火把。>\n\n烧掉他们的补给。要是它们爆炸，那就更好。要是顺便带走几个大胡子，那就更好不过。",dEN="Dwarves love their crates.\n\nCrates with food. Crates with powder. Crates with tools. Crates with more crates inside, probably.\n\n<Zeken hands you a blackened torch.>\n\nBurn their supplies. If they explode, even better. If they take a few bearded ones with them, better still.",o="用 Zeken 的火把摧毁 Dun Argan 的补给。",oEN="Use Zeken's torch to destroy Dun Argan's supplies.",p="那是什么味道？你把一切都烧成灰了，还是那只是你身上的味儿？",pEN="What dat smell? Ya burn everytin’ to da ground, or dat just you?",c="我从这儿都能听到爆炸声。\n\n那是你干的？\n\n<Zarkon 爆发出一阵响亮的大笑。>",cEN="I could hear da explosions from here.\n\nDat was your doin'?\n\n<Zarkon bursts into loud laughter.>"}
Q[175245]={d="Mexitla 叫我叛徒。卖国贼。\n\n<Zarkon 耸了耸肩，尽管他下颌的紧绷出卖了他。>\n\n但她在和部落虚耗时间的时候，我在做 Frostmane 本该做的事：杀矮人。\n\nDun Argan 里面有 Bengral，那个领着这个地洞的矮小鼹鼠。\n\n砍下他的头，带给 Mexitla。\n\n让公主看到，尽管我们有分歧，我依然在为我的人民效力。",dEN="Mexitla calls me rebel. Traitor.\n\n<Zarkon shrugs, though the tension in his jaw betrays him.>\n\nBut while she wastes time with da Horde, I do what da Frostmane should be doin': killin' dwarves.\n\nInside Dun Argan is Bengral, da pint-sized mole who leads dis burrow.\n\nCut off his head and bring it ta Mexitla.\n\nLet da princess see dat, despite our differences, I still serve my people.",o="在 Dun Argan 杀死 Bengral，把他的头带给 Mexitla。",oEN="Kill Bengral in Dun Argan and bring his head to Mexitla.",p="这是……啊，当然是 Zarkon。这颗头比他的道歉更有分量。",pEN="That is... Ah, Zarkon, of course. That head weighs more than his apology.",c="<那颗被砍下的矮人头颅凝固在一个比公主的脸更有表情的苦相里>。\n\n这不是道歉。\n\n<Mexitla 沉默了几秒钟>。\n\n但要是不承认它的用处，我就是个傻瓜。他对王室的亏欠并未偿清。\n\n只是被推迟了。 <Mexitla permanece en silencio unos segundos>",cEN="<The dwarf's severed head is frozen in a grimace more expressive than the princess's face.>\n\nThis is not an apology.\n\n<Mexitla remains silent for a few seconds.>\n\nBut I would be a fool not to recognize its usefulness. His debt to the crown is not settled.\n\nOnly postponed."}
Q[175246]={d="大河流在冰下挣扎。\n\n病光之子在河岸上徘徊，寻找霜层中的裂缝，向他们可怕的变异之神祈祷。一切都是为了把辐射向下游传播。\n\n<一阵厌恶的苦相绷紧了 Shivara 脸上的肌肉。>\n\n到目前为止，我们的萨满还能遏制辐射。但敌人在这段时间里从未停止向我们施压。\n\n公主一直偏爱着你，不是吗？如果你是来帮忙的，就去河边向 Telkin 报到。他会知道如何利用你的潜能。",dEN="The Great River agonizes beneath da ice.\n\nDa Sicklight Children prowl its banks, searchin' for cracks in da frost, raisin' prayers ta their terrible mutant god. All ta spread da radiation downstream.\n\n<A grimace of disgust tightens the muscles in Shivara's face.>\n\nSo far, our shamans have managed ta contain da radiation. But da enemy has not stopped pressin' us all dis time.\n\nDa princess has favored ya, has she not? If ya are here ta help, present yourself ta Telkin, by da riverbank. He will know how ta make use of your potential.",o="沿大河的封冻河段向 Telkin 报到。",oEN="Present yourself before Telkin along the frozen stretch of the Great River.",p="冰还撑得住，暂时……这场胜利不会持久。",pEN="Da ice holds, for now... This victory will not last.",c="<Telkin 双手按在冰面上。他说话时并不看你。>\n\n是 Shivara 派你来的。\n\n好。",cEN="<Telkin keeps both hands upon the ice. He does not look at you when he speaks.>\n\nShivara sent ya.\n\nGood."}
Q[175247]={d="病光之子并不特别敏捷，也不强壮。但他们的武器淬了毒，而这是一种缓慢灼烧的毒：\n\n它让皮肉翻开、血液发热、精神虚弱。\n\n<Telkin 递给你一瓶淡绿色的药水。>\n\n已有数名萌芽之仆在保护这条河的冰面时倒下了。把这药水用在那些还在呼吸的人身上。神圣萌芽的树液；一份治疗的馈赠。就连最顽固的毒也无法与我们的树相匹敌。",dEN="Da Sicklight Children are not especially agile, nor strong. But their weapons be poisoned, and it be a poison dat burns slowly:\n\nIt leaves da flesh open, da blood hot, and da spirit weak.\n\n<Telkin hands you a greenish potion.>\n\nSeveral Servants of da Bud have fallen protectin' da ice of dis river. Use dis potion on those who still breathe. Sap of da Sacred Bud; a gift of healin'. Not even da most stubborn poison can match da power of our tree.",o="用 Telkin 的复原药水治疗受伤的萌芽之仆。",oEN="Use Telkin's revitalizing potion to heal the wounded Servants of the Bud.",p="小心地把树液滴进药水里。一滴就足以治愈最难看的伤口。",pEN="Dose da sap in da potion carefully. A single drop should be enough ta heal even da ugliest of wounds.",c="<Telkin 的表情难以解读。他也许正全神贯注地听你说话，也许已陷入深深的恍惚。>\n\n五个。好。每条命都算数。",cEN="<Telkin's expression is impossible to read. He might be listening to you with all the attention in the world, or sunk deep in trance.>\n\nFive. Good. Every life counts."}
Q[175248]={d="尽管我们尽了力，辐射仍在扩散。缓慢地，非常缓慢地。但它在推进。\n\n<Telkin 指向冻河河床里几块被困住的淡绿色冰块。>\n\n唯一阻止它的办法就是击败它。为此，唤醒冰元素。迫使辐射成形。\n\n然后摧毁它。",dEN="Despite our efforts, da radiation keeps spreadin'. Slowly, very slowly. But it advances.\n\n<Telkin points to several greenish blocks of ice trapped in the frozen riverbed.>\n\nDa only way ta stop it is ta defeat it. To do dat, awaken da elemental ice. Force da radiation ta take form.\n\nAnd destroy it.",o="唤醒受污染的冰块，摧毁从中出现的冰霜元素。",oEN="Awaken the contaminated ice blocks and destroy the elemental frost that emerges from them.",p="对辐射永远要小心。",pEN="Always be careful with radiation.",c="你们已经遏制住了辐射。暂时。\n\n这是一场短暂的胜利。只要病神仍在引领他的孩子，辐射就会继续蔓延。",cEN="Ya have contained da radiation. For now.\n\nA fleeting victory, dis was. Da radiation will keep spreadin' as long as da Sick God leads his Children."}
Q[175249]={d="上游有东西。我一直没提，因为我不想把你送去送死。\n\n但在我所见之后，也许你能面对它并摧毁它。\n\n<Telkin 短暂地把双手从冰面上移开，专注地看着你。>\n\n一个生于滞涩河流的灵体；它腐化的元素显化。你净化掉的那些受污染霜冻只是它众多形态之一。\n\n如果你能摧毁它，就去向 Shivara 报告。",dEN="There be something upstream. I did not speak of it until now because I did not want ta send ya ta your death.\n\nBut after what I have seen, perhaps ya can face it and destroy it.\n\n<Telkin briefly pulls his hands from da ice, and looks at ya intensely.>\n\nA spirit born of da stagnant river; an elemental manifestation of its corruption. Da contaminated frost ya purged was only one of its many forms.\n\nIf ya manage ta destroy it, report ta Shivara.",o="在上游的水坝处击败滞涩之灵 Kegare。",oEN="Defeat Kegare, the Stagnant Spirit, at the dam upstream.",p="死水滋生毒物。",pEN="Stagnant water breeds poison.",c="<Shivara 的眼中闪着领悟的光。>\n\nKegare 死了？我原以为这种事不可能。\n\n愿幼树的祝福与你同在。我们欠你一份人情，<class>。",cEN="<Shivara's eyes shine with understanding.>\n\nKegare is dead? I did not think such a thing was possible.\n\nMay da Sapling's blessing be with ya. We are in your debt, <class>."}
Q[175251]={d="Tzotec 是第一个撤回恩宠的 Loa。但不是最后一个。最后那个是风之 Loa。Hekana。\n\n<公主念出这个名字时，语气中夹杂着敬畏与挫败。>\n\n她的祭司们献上的祈祷无人应答。她的祭坛一片沉寂。连曾守护峰顶的风也转而与我们为敌。\n\n而我们不知道原因。\n\n去找大祭司 Kezajin。不久前我派他去恢复那位 Loa 的恩宠，但从那以后就没听到他的消息。他可能需要帮助。",dEN="Tzotec was da first Loa to withdraw his favor from us. But he was not da last. Dat was da Loa of da Winds. Hekana.\n\n<The princess speaks the name with a mixture of reverence and frustration.>\n\nHer priests raise prayers dat go unanswered. Her altars stand silent. Even da winds dat once protected da summit have turned against us.\n\nAnd we do not know why.\n\nFind High Priest Kezajin. I tasked him with restoring da Loa's favor some time ago, but I have heard nothin' from him since. He may need help.",o="找到风之大祭司，查明 Hekana 为何背弃她的教团。",oEN="Find the High Priest of the Winds and discover why Hekana has turned her back on her cult.",p="风在怒吼。",pEN="Da winds be furious.",c="<Tanzuro 转向你，显然很担忧。>\n\n你是以 Mexitla 的名义来的？\n\n那你来晚了。我的导师、大祭司 Kezajin，几天前动身前往 Faz'Faron。\n\n而他本该已经回来了……",cEN="<Tanzuro turns to you, plainly troubled.>\n\nYou come on Mexitla's behalf?\n\nDen you come too late. High Priest Kezajin, my master, left for Faz'Faron some days ago.\n\nAnd he should have returned by now..."}
Q[175252]={d="我的导师出发去寻找 Hezari，风之 Loa 的女儿。他希望她知道她母亲为何背弃我们；也希望能得到她的帮助，赢回她母亲的恩宠。\n\n<Tanzuro 忧虑地望向森林。>\n\n但一定出了什么岔子。否则导师早该回来了。\n\n你说过是公主派你来的，对吗？那就在风抹去他的足迹之前找到 Kezajin。\n\n从 Faz'Faron 村开始。",dEN="My master set out in search of Hezari, daughter of da Loa of da Winds. He hoped she would know why her mother had turned away from us; and dat she might help us win back her favor.\n\n<Tanzuro looks toward the forest with apprehension.>\n\nBut sometin' must have gone wrong. Else my master would have come back by now.\n\nYou said the princess sent you, didn't ya? Den find Kezajin before da wind wipes away his tracks.\n\nStart wit' da village of Faz'Faron.",o="在 Faz'Faron 村寻找 Kezajin",oEN="Find Kezajin in the village of Faz'Faron",p="跟着风走，但不要相信它。",pEN="Follow da wind, but don't trust it.",c="<Kezajin 看上去伤痕累累；负了伤，一条腿瘸着，下颌紧绷，牙齿因疼痛而龇露。>\n\n别……别靠太近。\n\n<Kezajin 艰难地呼吸着。>\n\nHekana 的女儿们，那些鹰身女妖……她们病了。\n\n我开始明白她们的母亲为什么憎恨我们了。",cEN="<Kezajin looks battered; wounded and lame in one leg, his jaw clenched, his teeth bared in a grimace of pain.>\n\nNo... don't come too close.\n\n<Kezajin struggles for breath.>\n\nHekana's daughters, da harpies... Dey be sick.\n\nI begin to understand why their mother hates us."}
Q[175253]={d="在病光之子袭击这里之前，Faz'Faron 是个治疗者之村。他们的药用植物能缓解最严重的发热，他们的药膏能愈合最难看的伤口。\n\n废墟里一定还留着能帮我的东西。否则……\n\n<Kezajin 咳嗽时痛得弯下腰。他用一只颤抖的手按住肋侧的伤口。>\n\n替我办这件事，但要小心仍在村里游荡的那些狂信徒。他们一看见你就会攻击……就像对我那样。",dEN="Before da Sicklight Children attacked dis place, Faz'Faron was a village of healers. Its medicinal plants could soothe da worst fevers, and its salves could close da ugliest wounds.\n\nDere must be sometin' left among da ruins dat can help me. Otherwise...\n\n<Kezajin doubles over in pain as he coughs. He presses a trembling hand against the wound in his side.>\n\nDo dis for me, but be careful wit' da fanatics still prowlin' da village. Dey will attack ya on sight... just as dey did me.",o="收集 Faz'Faron 的药膏，并击败仍在村中游荡的病光狂信徒。",oEN="Gather Faz'Faron salves and defeat the Sickly Light fanatics still prowling the village.",p="我的思绪在燃烧。我的时辰已屈指可数。有药能治这个吗？",pEN="My thoughts burn. My hours be numbered. Dere be medicine for dat?",c="<Kezajin 忍着疼痛涂上药膏。>\n\n啊……\n\n这……这应该能给我多争取几个小时……足够帮你完成把我带到这里的那个目的。\n\n<Kezajin 抬起目光望向森林。>\n\n找到 Hezari。",cEN="<Kezajin applies the salve with restrained pain.>\n\nAh...\n\nDis... dis should buy me a few more hours... enough to help ya fulfill da purpose dat brought me here.\n\n<Kezajin raises his gaze toward the forest.>\n\nFindin' Hezari."}
Q[175254]={d="这片森林里的鹰身女妖都是风之 Loa Hekana 的后裔。\n\n曾经，她们是 Faz'Faron 之人的朋友。但当病光之子来袭时，他们的辐射把她们逼疯了。\n\n<Kezajin 把他的仪式权杖交给你。>\n\n用我的权杖把我祝福的力量引导到她们身上。只要她们中任何一个还残留哪怕一丝理智，你应该就能把它引出来。",dEN="Da harpies of dis forest all descend from Hekana, da Loa of da Winds.\n\nOnce, dey were friends to da people of Faz'Faron. But when da Sicklight Children attacked, dey drove dem mad wit' their radiation.\n\n<Kezajin hands you his ceremonial scepter.>\n\nUse my scepter to channel my blessing upon dem. If even a spark of sanity remains in any of dem, ya should be able to draw it out.",o="用 Kezajin 的权杖祝福 Faz'Faron 森林中受辐射的鹰身女妖。",oEN="Use Kezajin's scepter to bless the irradiated harpies of the Faz'Faron forest.",p="奏效了吗？",pEN="Did it work?",c="<Kezajin 用颤抖的手取回权杖。>\n\n奏效了吗？\n\n<听着你的回答，他闭上双眼，一脸挫败。>\n\n我明白了。那些狂信徒的辐射没有寻常的解药。医药不行，魔法也不行。\n\n那么，我们还剩什么希望？",cEN="<Kezajin takes back the scepter with a trembling hand.>\n\nDid it work?\n\n<As he listens to you, he closes his eyes, defeated.>\n\nI see. Da radiation of dose fanatics has no ordinary cure. Not medicine, not magic.\n\nWhat hope be left to us, den?"}
Q[175255]={d="Hezari 和这片森林里其他鹰身女妖不同。\n\n没有一份配得上她的供品就去接近她，是不明智的。\n\n<Kezajin 朝树林指了指。>\n\n我需要干净的骨头，这应该不成问题，森林里到处都是野兽。尽量先杀掉那些受辐射折磨的，就当作一种仁慈。\n\n给我带几根骨头来，我会做一份配得上 Hezari 的贡品。在那之前不要靠近她。",dEN="Hezari is not like da other harpies of dis forest.\n\nIt would not be wise to approach her wit'out a worthy offering.\n\n<Kezajin points toward the trees.>\n\nI need clean bones, which should not be a problem, wit' all da beasts prowlin' da forest. Try to kill da ones sufferin' from da radiation first, as a mercy.\n\nBring me a few bones, and I will make a tribute worthy of Hezari. Do not go near her until den.",o="在 Faz'Faron 附近从野生动物身上收集骨头，好让 Kezajin 制作献给 Hezari 的供品。",oEN="Gather bones from the wildlife near Faz'Faron so Kezajin can craft an offering to Hezari.",p="骨头记得生命的样子。",pEN="Bone remembers the shape of life.",c="<Kezajin 把骨头放在雪地上，开始用绳子和皮革组装一个小小的神像，一边干活一边喃喃祈祷。>\n\n我想这样就行了。\n\n如果 Hezari 还听得进道理，她会同意听我们说的。",cEN="<Kezajin lays the bones upon the snow and begins assembling a small idol with cord and leather, murmuring a prayer as he works.>\n\nI tink dis will do.\n\nIf Hezari still listens to reason, she will agree to hear us."}
Q[175256]={d="Hezari 躲在附近的一个洞穴里。我相信她受了伤，就像我一样。\n\n<Kezajin 把那座骨制神像交给你。>\n\n把这份贡品献给她。不要威胁她，也不要怜悯她；那几乎更糟。低下头倾听，等她说完了，再告诉她是什么把你带到了她面前。\n\n问问她，我们怎样才能赢回她母亲的恩宠。",dEN="Hezari hides in a nearby cave. I believe she be wounded, like me.\n\n<Kezajin hands you the bone idol.>\n\nOffer her dis tribute. Do not threaten her, nor pity her; dat would be near worse. Bow your head and listen, and when she has finished speakin', tell her what brings ya before her.\n\nAsk her how we may win back her mother's favor.",o="向 Hezari 报到，献上 Kezajin 准备的贡品。",oEN="Present yourself before Hezari and offer her the tribute prepared by Kezajin.",p="<Hezari 痛得蜷缩起来。她的羽毛暗淡，呼吸听起来疲惫不堪。>",pEN="<Hezari curls in on herself in pain. Her feathers are dull, and her breathing sounds exhausted.>",c="我的母亲……她鄙视我们……她厌恶我们的软弱……厌恶她的女儿。她的追随者……她的信徒……\n\n她看见了虔诚把病光之子变成了什么，于是决定不再要任何巨魔的崇拜。\n\n改变主意是她的天性。她是风；我是微风。我本会去劝她，可我快死了，凡人。而这病没人能治……\n\n没人能治愈辐射……\n\n除了……也许……三女巫。",cEN="My mother... she despises us... She is repulsed by our weakness... Repulsed by her daughter. Her followers... Her faithful...\n\nShe has seen what devotion has made of the Sicklight Children, and has decided she wants no troll worship at all.\n\nIt is in her nature to change her mind. She is wind; I am breeze. I would try to persuade her, but I am dying, mortal. And no one can cure this sickness...\n\nNo one can cure radiation...\n\nExcept... perhaps... the Three Witches."}
Q[175257]={d="三女巫古老而强大……比我母亲更强大。也更危险……\n\n<Hezari 说得十分吃力；每一个字都是一阵刺痛。>\n\n去 Hieratic 宫殿……向死者献上一枚眼之珠宝，并向古代祭司的灵魂寻求指点。\n\n他们……会知道如何召唤……三女巫。",dEN="The Three Witches are ancient and powerful... More powerful than my mother. More dangerous, too...\n\n<Hezari speaks with effort; every word a stab of pain.>\n\nGo to the Hieratic Palace... Offer an Eye Jewel to the dead, and seek counsel from the spirits of the priests of old.\n\nThey... will know how to call... the Three Witches.",o="从 Hieratic 宫殿的雕刻头颅中取得一枚完好的眼之珠宝，并在其祭坛上献上它。",oEN="Obtain an Intact Eye Jewel from the carved heads of the Hieratic Palace and offer it at its altar.",p="<祭坛旁不过一缕阴影；它可能是任何东西。>",pEN="<Barely a rag of shadow by the altar; it could be anything.>",c="<空气在祭坛上方折叠起来。那个灵魂用毫无表情的目光盯着你。>\n\n一枚完好的眼之珠宝。一道被剜去的目光。这是渴望看见彼岸之人的贡品。\n\n<Patlazar 侧了侧头。>\n\n说吧，陌生人。你的影子给这座宫殿带来了什么债？",cEN="<The air folds over the altar. The spirit fixes you with an expressionless stare.>\n\nAn intact Eye Jewel. A mutilated gaze. Da tribute of one who wishes to see da Other Side.\n\n<Patlazar inclines his head.>\n\nSpeak, stranger. What debt brings your shadow to dis palace?"}
Q[175258]={d="我们 Frostmane 最初来到这些海岸时，是三女巫指引了我们。\n\n她们教给我们这片土地的秘密，以及曾居住于此的众灵的伟大。\n\n自那以后，她们很少插手。\n\n要召唤她们，你必须吟诵三重连祷。三块石板。三个名字。三道咒语。",dEN="Da Three Witches guided da Frostmane when we first came to dese shores.\n\nDey taught us da secrets of dese lands, and da greatness of da spirits who dwelled here.\n\nSince den, dey have rarely interfered.\n\nTo summon dem, ya must intone da Triple Litany. Three tablets. Three names. Three spells.",o="在 Hieratic 宫殿的废墟中吟诵三块古老石板的连祷。",oEN="Intone the litanies of the three ancient tablets in the ruins of the Hieratic Palace.",p="呼唤三次。偿付三次。",pEN="Three times it be called. Three times it be paid.",c="她们听见了连祷，并以撼动生者世界与死者世界的声音作出了回应。\n\n三女巫在三重回音洞穴中等你。\n\n别让她们久等。",cEN="Dey heard da litany, and answered wit' voices dat shook da world of da livin' and da world of da dead.\n\nDa Three Witches be waitin' for ya in da Cave of Three Echoes.\n\nDo not keep dem waitin'."}
Q[175259]={d="三位女巫会在三重回音洞穴中等你。\n\n见习者、主母与智者。\n\n别让她们久等。",dEN="Da Three Witches be waitin' for ya in da Cave of Three Echoes.\n\nDa Novice, da Mistress, and da Sage.\n\nDo not keep dem waitin'.",o="在 Hieratic 宫殿附近的三重回音洞穴中寻找三女巫的巢穴。",oEN="Find the Three Witches' lair in the Cave of Three Echoes, near the Hieratic Palace.",c="<三女巫用六只完全同步地眨动、转动的眼睛看着你。>\n\n自从上次被召唤以来，已经过去很久了。\n\n<她们的声音如同一体般说话，仿佛她们是同一个生物。>\n\n进来，进来。我们知道你想要什么，而我们有一个交易要提。",cEN="<The Three Witches look at you with six eyes that blink and move in perfect synchrony.>\n\nIt been a long time since last we been called.\n\n<Their voices speak as one, as though they were a single creature.>\n\nCome in, come in. We know what ya want, and we have a bargain to offer."}
Q[175260]={d="所以你想治愈无法治愈之物，嗯？Gnomeregan 的毒，在触及河流 Loa 之后变得神圣。\n\n<三道声音交织在一起，无法分辨。>\n\n我们可以救 Hezari 的命。但在此生，甚至在来世，一切都有代价。\n\n你来选择要献出什么：\n\n你的命。\n\n一个你憎恨、但对方并不憎恨你的人的命。\n\n或者一个憎恨你、而你并不憎恨对方的人的命。",dEN="So ya wish to cure what cannot be cured, eh? Da poison of Gnomeregan, made sacred when it touched da Loa of da Rivers.\n\n<The three voices weave together, impossible to tell apart.>\n\nWe can save Hezari's life. But in dis life, and even in da next, everytin' demands a price.\n\nYou choose what ya will give:\n\nYour life.\n\nDa life of someone ya hate, but who does not hate ya in return.\n\nOr da life of someone who hates ya, but whom ya do not hate.",o="选择要以什么作为交换，换取三女巫的相助。",oEN="Choose what to sacrifice in exchange for the Three Witches' aid.",p="没有伤口，就没有治愈。",pEN="There can be no healing without a wound.",c="<三位发出古老而残忍的大笑。>\n\n别怕；不管你选什么，我们早就决定帮你了。\n\n我们打个响指，赫扎莉身上的毒就会被清除。\n\n一……二……然后……\n\n<三个女巫整齐划一地打了个响指。>\n\n成了。就这么简单。",cEN="<The three release an ancient, cruel laugh.>\n\nDo not fear; whatever ya chose, we had already decided to help ya.\n\nOne snap of our fingers, and Hezari will be cured of da poison dat afflicts her.\n\nOne... Two... And...\n\n<The three witches snap their fingers in perfect unison.>\n\nDone. As easy as dat."}
Q[175261]={d="赫扎莉呼吸着纯净的空气。她脑中的声音沉寂了。\n\n换句话说：我们救了她。\n\n<三根手指指向洞穴的顶部。>\n\n我们头顶上方有一座小祭坛。在顶上敲响那面鼓，赫扎莉就会回应召唤。\n\n我们在这段故事里的部分到此结束。说服风之罗阿现在是你的事了。",dEN="Hezari breathes clean air. Da voices in her head have gone silent.\n\nIn other words: we saved her.\n\n<Three fingers point toward the roof of the cave.>\n\nA small altar stands above our heads. Sound da drum at da summit, and Hezari will answer da call.\n\nOur part in dis story ends here. Convincin' da Loa of da Winds be your task now.",o="敲响受祝福的鼓，让赫扎莉带你去见坦祖罗。",oEN="Sound the blessed drum and let Hezari carry you to Tanzuro.",p="告诉我！",pEN="Tell me!",c="<赫扎莉完好而庄严地降落下来，坦祖罗抬头望去。有那么一瞬，他说不出话。>\n\n赫扎莉！\n\n<坦祖罗跪倒在地。>\n\n我的师父呢？凯扎金呢？",cEN="<Tanzuro looks up as Hezari descends, whole and majestic. For a moment, he cannot speak.>\n\nHezari!\n\n<Tanzuro falls to his knees.>\n\nWhat of my master? What of Kezajin?"}
Q[175262]={d="通往山顶的路已经清了。这是个征兆：赫卡娜准你觐见。\n\n但你不能空手而去。\n\n<坦祖罗指着在峭壁周围翻卷的气流。>\n\n罗阿的神圣羽毛落在风所决定之处。在你攀登途中收集它们，并把它们带回她的神庙。",dEN="Da path to da summit has cleared. It be a sign: Hekana grants ya an audience.\n\nBut ya cannot go wit' empty hands.\n\n<Tanzuro points toward the currents twisting around the crag.>\n\nDa Loa's sacred feathers fall where da wind decides. Gather dem on your climb, and return dem to her temple.",o="在通往风之神殿的登顶之路上收集赫卡娜的祝福羽毛。",oEN="Collect Hekana's Blessed Feathers along the path ascending to the Temple of the Winds.",p="<风之罗阿的眼睛闪着光，残忍而戏谑。>",pEN="<The Loa of the Winds' eyes gleam, cruel and amused.>",c="你。\n\n<风之罗阿说出那个\"你\"字时，带着无尽的轻蔑。>\n\n你赢得了死亡罗阿佐特克的青睐，这引起了我的注意。从那时起我就一直在观察你。\n\n你真是个奇特的生灵。如此固执……你在下面做的那一切……还把三女巫牵扯进来！\n\n你赢得了我的敬意。",cEN="You.\n\n<The Loa of the Winds speaks that “you” with infinite contempt.>\n\nThat you won the favor of Tzotec, Loa of Death, caught my attention. I have watched you since.\n\nWhat a curious creature you are. So stubborn... Everything you did down below... involving the Three Witches!\n\nYou have earned my respect."}
Q[175263]={d="虽然通往山顶的路是畅通的，走的时候也要当心。无论如何都不要变得太过自信。\n\n风无常，赫卡娜更是狡诈。哪怕她看似愿意听你说话……在上面走错一步，你就死定了。",dEN="Though da path to da summit remains clear, be careful as ya walk it. And under no circumstance should ya grow overconfident.\n\nDa wind be fickle, and Hekana treacherous. Though she seems willin' to hear ya... one false step up dere, and ya can count yourself dead.",o="沿山径前行，活着登上风之神殿。",oEN="Walk the mountain path and survive the ascent to the Temple of the Winds.",p="<风之罗阿的眼睛闪着光，残忍而戏谑。>",pEN="<The Loa of the Winds' eyes gleam, cruel and amused.>",c="<风之罗阿的眼睛闪着光，残忍而戏谑。>\n\n登顶在某种程度上是一场考验。也是对你无礼的一点小小惩罚。\n\n可你就在这儿，活着，还精神十足。\n\n好。我们谈谈吧。",cEN="<The Loa of the Winds' eyes gleam, cruel and amused.>\n\nThe ascent was a test, in part. And a small punishment for your insolence.\n\nBut here you are, alive and kicking.\n\nGood. Let us speak."}
Q[175264]={d="病光之子如今对马特拉坎的虔诚，和诺莫瑞根事故之前没什么两样。\n\n盲信是一种自残。我也不像其他罗阿那样，要求膜拜和无条件服从。自负与骄傲是沉重之物。是负担。可我是风！\n\n轻盈，狂暴，不可驯服。\n\n我不喜欢我的教团。可你……你的执拗让我着迷。就像山前的风，固执地顶着岩石。\n\n你想要我的祝福？",dEN="The Sicklight Children are as devoted to Matlacan now as they were before the Gnomeregan accident.\n\nBlind faith is a form of self-mutilation. And I am not like the other Loa, demanding worship and unconditional obedience. Ego and pride are heavy things. Burdens. But I am wind!\n\nLight, furious, untamable.\n\nMy cult displeases me. But you... your stubbornness fascinates me. Like wind against the mountain, obstinately pressing against the stone.\n\nYou want my blessing?",o="与赫卡娜交谈，听听她要说什么。",oEN="Speak with Hekana and listen to what she has to say.",p="我可以是狂风……也可以是微风。",pEN="I can be a gale... as I can be a breeze.",c="很好。\n\n你的公主想要点看得见摸得着的东西，好安抚霜鬃族。而我所驱动的风，难以度量。\n\n风啊，风啊！难道我的天性就是为众人所知，却无人理解？",cEN="Very well.\n\nYour princess wants something tangible, something to comfort the Frostmane. The winds I move are difficult to measure.\n\nWinds, winds! Is it my nature to be known by all, and understood by none?"}
Q[175265]={d="拿着这个。\n\n<风之罗阿伸出一只带爪的脚，托着一枚你从未见过的宝石>\n\n墨希特拉的父亲，国王麦克顿，当年把它赠给了我。\n\n把它交给公主，作为你与我说过话、而我已同意赐予你祝福的凭证。\n\n当你准备离开风之神殿时，去跟东风欧罗说话。他的气流会把你送往雷霆卡尔。",dEN="Take this.\n\n<The Loa of the Winds extends a taloned foot, holding a jewel unlike any you have ever seen.>\n\nMexitla's father, King Mecton, gifted it to me in his day.\n\nGive it to the Princess as proof that you have spoken with me, and that I have agreed to grant you my blessing.\n\nWhen you are ready to leave the Temple of the Winds, speak with Euro, the East Wind. His current will carry you to Thundrakar.",o="与欧罗交谈，让风把你送往雷霆卡尔，然后向墨希特拉禀报风之罗阿的恩准。",oEN="Speak with Euro so the wind may carry you to Thundrakar, then inform Mexitla of the Loa of the Winds' favor.",p="你带来了风之罗阿的消息吗？",pEN="Ya bring news of da Loa of da Winds?",c="风之罗阿的恩准把战争的天平压向了我们这边。\n\n我们的处境，以及我们麾下的兵力，依旧岌岌可危。但有赫卡娜站在我们这边……风向我们吹来了。\n\n你又一次超出了我的期望，<race>。让所有人都知道，你是苍角公主的左右手。",cEN="Da favor of da Loa of da Winds tips da scales of war in our favor.\n\nOur situation, and da forces at our command, remain precarious. But wit' Hekana on our side... favorable winds be blowin'.\n\nYa have exceeded my expectations once again, <race>. Let all know dat ya be da right hand of da Princess of Palehorn."}
Q[175266]={d="你要去法兹法隆？\n\n村子里除了尸体和病光之子，你找不到任何人。我们只有少数几个人逃了出来。\n\n结果又被穴居人抓了去。\n\n这个洞穴里的穴居人不一样。他们吸进了诺莫瑞根的辐射。他们更聪明。更有组织。而且野心危险。\n\n想帮忙吗？进他们的巢穴深沼洞穴去，杀几个。让他们为自己对我族人做的事付出代价。",dEN="Ya headin’ to Faz’Faron?\n\nYa won’t find anyone in da village but corpses and Sicklight Children. Only a few of us managed to flee.\n\nOnly to be captured by da troggs.\n\nDa troggs in dis cave be different. Dey have breathed da radiation of Gnomeregan. Dey be smarter. Better organized. And dey got dangerous ambitions.\n\nYa wanna help? Go into their warren, Deepmire Cavern, and kill a few of dem. Make dem pay for what dey did to my people.",o="在深沼穴居人受辐射影响的存在蔓延苍角之前，击败他们。",oEN="Defeat the Deepmire troggs before their irradiated presence spreads through Palehorn.",p="你把他们杀了吗？",pEN="Ya killed dem?",c="少了十三个。\n\n这不足以遏制他们，但会让他们明白，低估我们是错的。\n\n谢谢你，<race>。",cEN="Thirteen fewer.\n\nIt won’t be enough to contain dem, but it will teach dem dey were wrong to underestimate us.\n\nT’anks, <race>."}
Q[175267]={d="穴居人在他们的巢穴里叫喊、咆哮、互相斗殴。但从他们洞穴传出的所有声响里，也能听到哀号……和哀求。\n\n那是法兹法隆巨魔的喊声；是被穴居人掳走的那些人。若他们还活着，绝不是出于仁慈。但也许，无论穴居人对他们做了什么，我们还来得及救他们。\n\n进入深沼，找到笼子的钥匙。释放你找到的每一个被囚巨魔。",dEN="Da troggs in dere scream, grunt, and fight among themselves. But among all da noises comin’ out of their cave, ya can also hear wails… and pleas.\n\nDey be da cries of da trolls of Faz’Faron; da ones da troggs kidnapped. If dey still live, it ain’t out of mercy. But perhaps, whatever da troggs have done to dem, we still be in time to save dem.\n\nGo into Deepmire and find da cage key. Free every captive troll ya find.",o="深入深沼洞穴，取得穴居人的万能钥匙，解救法兹法隆的俘虏。",oEN="Venture into Deepmire Cavern, obtain the troggs’ master key, and free the captives of Faz’Faron.",p="我不知道穴居人对他们做了什么，也不知道他们为什么想留他们活口……\n\n但我想他们不会愿意谈起。",pEN="I don’t know what da troggs have done to dem, or why dey wanted to keep dem alive…\n\nBut I don’t tink dey will want to speak of it.",c="<内卡莉闭了会儿眼。睁开时，她的神情依旧冷硬，但其中有什么松动了。>\n\n好。\n\n法兹法隆流的血已经够多了。\n\n我不知道那些难民能否在这里找到安宁。我也不知道我们之中有没有人能找到。但至少，他们不会在笼子里惨叫着死去。\n\n<内卡莉微微低下头。>\n\n我们欠你一条命，<race>。",cEN="<Nekali closes her eyes for a moment. When she opens them, her expression remains hard, but something in it has loosened.>\n\nGood.\n\nFaz’Faron has bled enough.\n\nI don’t know if dose refugees will find peace here. I don’t know if any of us will. But at least dey won’t die screamin’ in a cage.\n\n<Nekali bows her head, barely.>\n\nWe owe ya our lives, <race>."}
Q[175268]={d="<那具古老的魔像静立在废墟之间，像是祭司庭院里又一尊雕像。直到它体内有什么东西动了。>\n\n<一连串破碎的画面涌入你的思绪。一座神庙，完好无损。霜鬃祭司在吟诵。一场献祭……>\n\n<接着那种感觉变了。疲惫。服从。数个世纪漫无目的的行走。被剥夺了职责的守卫，守护着空荡的厅堂和破碎的祭坛。>\n\n<魔像缓缓抬起一只手，指向在废墟中巡逻的其他构造体。>\n\n<它想让你赐予它们安息。>",dEN="<The ancient golem stands motionless among the ruins, like one more statue in the priestly grounds. Until something stirs within it.>\n\n<A succession of broken images invades your thoughts. A temple, whole and unspoiled. Frostmane priests intoning chants. A sacrifice...>\n\n<Then the feeling changes. Exhaustion. Obedience. Centuries of aimless steps. Guardians stripped of purpose, protecting empty halls and shattered altars.>\n\n<The golem slowly raises one hand toward the other constructs patrolling the ruins.>\n\n<It wants you to grant them rest.>",o="摧毁祭司宫殿中的达卡莱构造体，释放被困其中的灵魂残片。",oEN="Destroy the Drakkari constructs in the Priestly Palace to release the spiritual remnants trapped within them.",p="<魔像静静地等待着。一阵微弱的震动传遍它石质的身躯。>",pEN="<The golem waits in silence. A faint vibration runs through the stone of its body.>",c="<你回来时，那具古老的魔像以近乎鞠躬的姿态向你致意。>\n\n<在构造体倒下的地方，仍飘浮着淡蓝色的灵魂丝缕，在雪与石之间渐渐消散。没有声音，但你感到某种近似解脱的东西。>\n\n<魔像向你伸出一只布满裂纹的手。短短一瞬，你脑中充满最后一个印象：古老的感激，沉重如山。",cEN="<Upon your return, the ancient golem greets you with something like a bow.>\n\n<Where the constructs fell, pale-blue strands of spirit still drift, fading between snow and stone. There are no voices, but you feel something like relief.>\n\n<The golem extends a cracked hand toward you. For one brief instant, your mind fills with one final impression: ancient gratitude, heavy as a mountain.>"}
Q[175269]={d="他们是难民……<诺扎玛用一根瘦长的手指指着躲在废墟间的巨魔。>\n\n他们来自法兹法隆。病光之子来袭时，许多人死了；而逃出来的那些人，很多又落进了穴居人的爪子里。\n\n你想帮忙的话，就从白牙崖上生长的树上给我们摘些果子来。那填不饱任何人的肚子，但能缓解等待……等援军到来的这段等待。\n\n因为他们会来的。\n\n迟早的事。\n\n对吧？",dEN="Dey be refugees… <Notzama points a long, famished finger at the trolls sheltering among the ruins.>\n\nDey come from Faz’Faron. Many died when da Sicklight Children attacked, and of dose who fled, many ended up in da troggs’ claws.\n\nIf ya want to help, bring us fruit from da trees growin’ on Whitefang Cliff. It won’t fill anyone’s belly, but it will ease da wait… while reinforcements come.\n\nBecause dey will come.\n\nSooner or later.\n\nRight?",o="在白牙崖采集水果，分给诺扎玛收留的难民。",oEN="Gather fruit from Whitefang Cliff and offer it to the refugees Notzama has taken in.",p="你给所有人都分过食物了吗？",pEN="Ya fed everyone?",c="好。看来我什么也没剩下了。\n\n那没关系。\n\n他们比我更需要。再说……嗯，我的胃口比较难满足。",cEN="Good. Nothin’ left for me, I suppose.\n\nDat be all right.\n\nDey need it more than I do. And anyway… well, my appetite be harder to satisfy."}
Q[175270]={d="与其他罗阿不同，阿祖尔丁没有组织化的教团。他的祭司在雪地里追踪足迹，远离我们的视线，只在觉得必要时才下山。\n\n<墨希特拉皱起眉，若有所思。>\n\n我们需要他的祝福，但无法强求。在找到他的大祭司坦扎妮娅之前，我们甚至无从开口请求。\n\n她的下落不明，不过我听说她的几名祭司曾在索拉松村附近出现过。去那儿。打听她的消息。",dEN="Unlike other Loa, Azuldin has no ordered cult. His priests follow tracks in da snow, far from our eyes, and only come down from da mountains when dey feel dey must.\n\n<Mexitla frowns, thoughtful.>\n\nWe need his blessing, but we cannot demand it. We cannot even ask for it until we first find his High Priestess, Tzania.\n\nHer whereabouts be unknown, though I have heard some of her priests were seen near da village of Zorazon. Go dere. Ask for her.",o="前往索拉松村，打听雪之罗阿的大祭司坦扎妮娅的下落。",oEN="Go to the village of Zorazon to learn the whereabouts of Tzania, High Priestess of the Loa of the Snows.",c="<沃尔赞带着显而易见的倦意上下打量你。>\n\n所以公主终于想起我们了。可真是时候。\n\n<那巨魔发出一声干涩而无喜意的笑。>\n\n说吧，<race>。不过你要是来求援的，去排队吧。",cEN="<Volzan looks you up and down with obvious weariness.>\n\nSo da princess finally remembers us. How timely.\n\n<The troll lets out a dry, joyless laugh.>\n\nSpeak, <race>. But if ya come askin’ for help, get in line."}
Q[175271]={d="大祭司坦扎妮娅？没有。我没见过她。就算她路过这儿，有这么多难民，也根本认不出谁是谁。\n\n索拉松已经成了法兹法隆、阿拉金，以及其他不复存在的村庄幸存者的避难所。\n\n全因为有人捅了马蜂窝。\n\n<沃尔赞迎着你的目光。>\n\n但几天前，一群阿祖尔丁的祭司在碎裂洞穴聚集。他们要进行一场仪式。要是他们还在那儿，也许能帮你找到坦扎妮娅。",dEN="The High Priestess Tzania? No. I haven’t seen her. Even if she has passed through here, with all these refugees, it be hard to tell anyone apart.\n\nZorazon has become a refuge for survivors from Faz’Faron, Ar’akin, and other villages dat no longer exist.\n\nAll because someone kicked da hornet’s nest.\n\n<Volzan holds your gaze.>\n\nBut a few days ago, a group of Azuldin’s priests gathered in Splintered Cave. Dey were goin’ to perform a ritual. If dey still be dere, perhaps dey can help ya find Tzania.",o="前往碎裂洞穴，寻找阿祖尔丁的祭司。",oEN="Go to Splintered Cave and find Azuldin’s priests.",p="你找到那些祭司了吗？",pEN="Did ya find da priests?",c="<听着你的讲述，沃尔赞脸上严厉的神情褪去了。>\n\n他们……全都死了？\n\n<他沉默了片刻。眼里满是恐惧。>\n\n坦扎妮娅的遗体不在他们当中？好。好。那她还有活着的希望。",cEN="<Volzan’s hard expression drains from his face as he listens to your account.>\n\nAll of dem… dead?\n\n<For a moment, he says nothing. His eyes fill with fear.>\n\nAnd Tzania’s body was not among dem? Good. Good. Den dere be hope she still lives."}
Q[175272]={d="<沃尔赞用手抹了把脸，像是在理清思绪。>\n\n我认识一个人，也许能帮我们查清那些祭司的死因。\n\n沿海边，离这儿不远，有一座废弃的人类村庄。叫暗湾。虽然已成废墟，但暗湾住着一位总愿意帮忙的女人；当然，是要付报酬的……\n\n她叫瑟拉娜。是个女巫。\n\n找到她，请她帮忙查明碎裂洞穴里发生了什么。",dEN="<Volzan drags a hand down his face, as though trying to order his thoughts.>\n\nI know someone who might help us shed light on da priests’ deaths.\n\nOn da coast, not far from here, dere be an abandoned human village. Darkcove, it be called. Though it lies in ruins, Darkcove be home to a woman always willin’ to help; for a price, of course…\n\nHer name be Serana. And she be a witch.\n\nFind her, and ask for her help in uncoverin’ what happened in Splintered Cave.",o="在废弃的暗湾村寻找瑟拉娜。",oEN="Find Serana in the abandoned village of Darkcove.",c="<老妇人见到你并不惊讶。倒像是早就在等你。>\n\n是索拉松的巨魔派你来的，对吧？他们想要答案。\n\n这次死的是谁？来吧，全都告诉我。",cEN="<The old woman does not startle at the sight of you. Rather, she seems to have been expecting you.>\n\nThe trolls of Zorazon sent you, didn’t they? They want answers.\n\nWho has died this time? Come now, tell me everything."}
Q[175273]={d="原来如此。整个教团被灭。当然，你想知道「为什么」、「怎么」和「何时」。没错，我能帮你……但斯凯德尔的女巫不施恩惠。我们谈交易。\n\n<瑟拉娜露出一个焦黄、缺牙的笑容。>\n\n部落袭击这个村子时，有些人留下来战斗。他们死得很快，算是走运的。其余的人逃进了矿坑。等他们终于出来时，已不再是人，而是某种更低劣的东西。被浸透这片土地的诅咒扭曲之物。\n\n这就是我的价码：我要你去杀了他们，收起他们的骨骸。我会给他们一场应得的葬礼。",dEN="So. An entire cult murdered. And of course, you want to know “why,” “how,” and “when.” Yes, I can help you… but the witches of Scadeald do not grant favors. We strike bargains.\n\n<Serana flashes a yellow, gap-toothed smile.>\n\nWhen the Horde attacked this village, some stayed behind to fight. They died quickly, the lucky ones. The rest fled into the mine. When they finally came out, they were no longer men, but something less. Something twisted by the curse that soaks these lands.\n\nThis is my price: I want you to kill them and gather their bones. I will give them the burial they deserve.",o="击败暗湾的豺狼人，收集他们的骨骸，好让瑟拉娜让他们永久安息。",oEN="Defeat the Darkcove gnolls and gather their bones so Serana can lay them to rest.",p="你让他们安息了吗？",pEN="Have you granted them rest?",c="<瑟拉娜一根一根接过那些骨骸，那份轻柔放在她骨节嶙峋的手上显得格格不入。>\n\n这是哈兰。这个是玛拉。而这小小的一个……他没能活过第十个冬天。\n\n<老妇人沉默了很久。然后，她眼含泪水说道：>\n\n我会把他们一个个带回家，葬在那里。",cEN="<Serana receives the bones one by one, with a delicacy that seems out of place in her knotted hands.>\n\nThis was Harlan. This one, Mara. And this little one… he never reached his tenth winter.\n\n<The old woman falls silent for a long while. Then, with watery eyes, she says:>\n\nI will carry each of them home, and bury them there."}
Q[175274]={d="这片土地上有笑声。\n\n<瑟拉娜侧过头，仿佛此刻仍能听见。>\n\n大笑鬣狗。一个古老而残忍的灵魂。它的嘲弄随着暗湾的人们混进了矿坑，在那里教会了他们互相吞噬。\n\n杀掉他们并不足以让它的笑声沉寂。\n\n拿着这枚护符。用在你沿途留下的尸体上。若他们身上还残留着人性，它就能保住他们的本质。",dEN="There is laughter in this land.\n\n<Serana tilts her head, as if she can hear it even now.>\n\nThe Great Hyena. An old and cruel spirit. Its mockery slipped into the mine with the people of Darkcove, and there taught them to devour one another.\n\nKilling them will not be enough to silence its laughter.\n\nTake this amulet. Use it on the corpses you leave in your wake. If anything human remains in them, it will save their essence.",o="用瑟拉娜的护符净化暗湾豺狼人的尸体。",oEN="Use Serana’s amulet to purify the corpses of the Darkcove gnolls.",p="你听见那笑声了吗？",pEN="Do you hear the laughter?",c="<瑟拉娜接过护符。其中的魔法似乎已经耗尽。>\n\n寂静。随之而来的，是安宁。\n\n<老妇人收拢手指，握紧护符。>\n\n大笑鬣狗的上下颚一旦咬合，就不会轻易吐出它咬住的腐肉。但今天，你扯下了一大块。",cEN="<Serana takes the amulet. The magic within it seems spent.>\n\nSilence. And with it, peace.\n\n<The old woman closes her fingers around the amulet.>\n\nOnce the Great Hyena’s jaws close, he does not surrender the carrion he has bitten so easily. But today, you tore away a good piece."}
Q[175275]={d="现在我们准备好了。\n\n<瑟拉娜对着护符低声念了咒语，然后把它还给你。它很冷。比以往任何时候都冷。>\n\n当死亡来得暴烈时，灵魂的一部分和它的记忆会留下，渗入生者的世界。\n\n把护符用在那些祭司的尸体上。你能召唤他们的灵魂，但只有一瞬。\n\n一个问题。一个回答。仅此而已。",dEN="Now we are ready.\n\n<Serana murmurs a spell over the amulet before returning it to you. It is cold. Colder than ever.>\n\nWhen death is violent, part of the spirit and its memory remain behind, soaking into the world of the living.\n\nUse the amulet on the priests’ bodies. You will be able to call their spirits, but only for a moment.\n\nOne question. One answer. Nothing more.",o="用瑟拉娜的附魔护符审问碎裂洞穴中被杀害的祭司的灵魂。",oEN="Use Serana’s haunted amulet to question the spirits of the murdered priests in Splintered Cave.",p="你查出什么了吗？",pEN="Did ya discover anytin’?",c="<沃尔赞攥紧拳头。>\n\n是坦扎妮娅杀了他们。她自己的祭司。可她为什么要这么做？为什么……？\n\n<沃尔赞向群山投去哀求的目光。>\n\n那个活着逃出来的泽拉基。你必须赶在她之前找到他。",cEN="<Volzan clenches his fists.>\n\nTzania killed dem. Her own priests. But why would she do such a thing? Why…?\n\n<Volzan lifts an imploring gaze toward the mountains.>\n\nDat Zeraki who escaped alive. Ya must find him before she does."}
Q[175276]={d="那些灵魂提到了一个叫泽拉基的巨魔？\n\n是的，我认识他。他属于安祖尔丁的祭司阶层。要是他从碎裂洞穴逃了出来，要是他在追查大祭司背叛的答案……他一定是去阿拉金了。\n\n<沃尔赞指向群山。>\n\n阿拉金是坦扎妮娅的故乡。\n\n去那儿，<race>。找到阿拉金。找到泽拉基。并祈祷他还有舌头能说话。",dEN="Da spirits mentioned a troll named Zeraki?\n\nYes, I know him. He belongs to the priest caste of Anzuldin. If he escaped Splintered Cave, if he be lookin’ for answers about da High Priestess’ betrayal… he will have gone to Ar’akin.\n\n<Volzan points toward the mountains.>\n\nAr’akin be Tzania’s home village.\n\nGo dere, <race>. Find Ar’akin. Find Zeraki. And pray he still has a tongue wit’ which to speak.",o="找到坦扎妮娅的出生地——阿拉金村。",oEN="Find the village of Ar’akin, Tzania’s birthplace.",p="<雪豹一眨不眨地盯着你。它眼中有某种过于聪慧的东西。>",pEN="<The snow leopard watches you without looking away. There is something far too intelligent in its eyes.>",c="<雪豹低下头。随后，一个疲惫的声音挤进你的脑海。>\n\n别出声。\n\n阿拉金已经不是从前的样子了。\n\n<那野兽望向村子。>\n\n它属于病光。",cEN="<The leopard lowers its head. Then a tired voice pushes its way into your mind.>\n\nMake no noise.\n\nAr’akin be not what it was.\n\n<The beast looks toward the village.>\n\nIt belongs to da Sickllight."}
Q[175277]={d="<泽拉基的声音在你脑中震颤，低沉而苦涩。>\n\n就像篮底一颗烂掉的苹果，阿拉金已经病了有些时日了。\n\n但我仍不知道坦扎妮娅是起因……还是结果。\n\n<雪豹的眼睛闪着光。>\n\n进阿拉金去。杀掉向你举兵的狂信徒。但若有人投降，就让他活。\n\n我怀疑这个村子为了活下去，别无选择，只能加入病光之子。",dEN="<Zeraki’s voice vibrates inside your head, low and bitter.>\n\nLike a rotten apple at da bottom of a basket, Ar’akin has been sick for some time.\n\nBut I still do not know if Tzania be da cause… or da consequence.\n\n<The leopard’s eyes flash.>\n\nEnter Ar’akin. Kill da fanatics who raise weapons against ya. But if anyone surrenders, let dem live.\n\nI suspect dis village had no choice but to join da Sicklight Children to survive.",o="进入阿拉金，击败病光武装分子。饶恕投降者。",oEN="Enter Ar’akin and defeat the Sickly Light militants. Spare those who surrender.",p="别把正义和嗜血混为一谈。",pEN="Do not mistake justice for hunger.",c="<泽拉基嗅了嗅空气。他的胡须颤动着。>\n\n没有投降的不是最勇敢的，而是最狂热的。他们的死或许能左右其余人的想法。\n\n尤其是因为你对其余所有人都手下留情。\n\n<雪豹向你低下头。",cEN="<Zeraki sniffs the air. His whiskers tremble.>\n\nDose who did not surrender were not da bravest, but da most fanatical. Their deaths may help sway da minds of da rest.\n\nEspecially because ya showed mercy to everyone else.\n\n<The leopard inclines his head to you.>"}
Q[175278]={d="我上次造访阿拉金时，是拉贾津智者领导着村子。\n\n一个谨慎的巨魔。老得拿不动武器，却受所有人敬重。\n\n要是他还听得进道理，拉贾津就能告诉你村子为何投靠病光，以及坦扎妮娅为何背叛雪之罗阿安祖尔丁。\n\n去找他，问问他。",dEN="Sage Rajazin led the village last time I visited Ar’akin.\n\nA cautious troll. Too old to wield a weapon, but respected by all.\n\nIf he still listens to reason, Rajazin can tell ya why da village joined da Sicklight, and why Tzania betrayed Anzuldin, Loa of da Snows.\n\nFind him and ask him.",o="与阿拉金村的拉贾津智者交谈，查明村子为何向病光之子屈服。",oEN="Speak with Sage Rajazin in the village of Ar’akin to discover why the village surrendered to the Children of the Sickly Light.",p="那老家伙说了什么？",pEN="What did da old one say?",c="坦扎妮娅……蠢货！\n\n<泽拉基后退一步，仿佛那些话打在他身上。>\n\n她是我们中最强的，是安祖尔丁最宠爱的。这还不够吗？\n\n现在我明白了，那场背叛不是断裂，而是终结。她一直都有病。\n\n至少，她的心智如此。",cEN="Tzania… Fool!\n\n<Zeraki takes a step back, as if the words had struck him.>\n\nShe was da strongest of us, Anzuldin’s favorite. Was dat not enough?\n\nNow I understand da betrayal was not a break, but a culmination. She was always sick.\n\nHer mind, at least."}
Q[175279]={d="还有别的事。\n\n<泽拉基的声音沉闷。>\n\n我觉得阿拉金的人在洞穴里藏着什么。我听说他们谈起一只新生的生物，被辐射\"祝福\"过。\n\n他们当中最虔诚的人把它当作神圣的偶像。他们相信光辉之神通过它痛苦的尖叫向他们说话。\n\n杀掉那生物。终结它的痛苦。也让那些狂信徒明白，他们的神是假的。",dEN="There be somethin’ more.\n\n<Zeraki’s voice sounds subdued.>\n\nI believe da people of Ar’akin be hidin’ somethin’ in da cave. I have heard dem speak of a newborn creature, “blessed” by radiation.\n\nDa most devoted among dem treat it like a sacred idol. Dey believe da Radiant God speaks to dem through its screams of agony.\n\nKill da creature. End its sufferin’. And show dose fanatics dat their god be false.",o="深入阿拉金的洞穴，杀死那只新生的憎恶。",oEN="Venture into Ar’akin’s cave and slay the newborn abomination.",p="那只憎恶你处理掉了吗？",pEN="Have ya dealt wit’ da abomination?",c="<泽拉基低下头。>\n\n已经成了。你做到了。\n\n<他沉默了很久。>\n\n病光为它的追随者预备的命运，比它赐予敌人的死亡更糟。它使人畸形、扭曲、腐化、染病。\n\n而它把这叫作\"祝福\"。\n\n坦扎妮娅本该看见这一点。本该明白这一点。\n\n可她还是选择了它。",cEN="<Zeraki lowers his head.>\n\nDen it be done. Ya did it.\n\n<He remains silent for a long while.>\n\nDa Sicklight reserves for its followers a fate worse than da death it grants its enemies. It deforms, twists, corrupts, and sickens.\n\nAnd calls it “blessing.”\n\nTzania had to see it. Had to know it.\n\nAnd still she chose it."}
Q[175280]={d="阿拉金没人知道坦扎妮娅去了哪儿，对吧？那我只能去追踪她。与此同时……\n\n<雪豹把目光投向布满废墟的山坡。>\n\n阿兰达克废墟里藏着一条通往霜生洞穴的密道。在旧日，我们安祖尔丁的祭司用它往返于河谷与这一带之间。\n\n要是坦扎妮娅把它的存在透露给了病光之子，事情就会变得非常棘手。\n\n我需要你去查一查。",dEN="No one in Ar’akin knows where Tzania went, do dey? Den I will have to track her. Meanwhile…\n\n<The leopard turns his gaze toward the ruin-strewn slope.>\n\nDa ruins of Arandrak hide a secret passage leadin’ to da Frostbirth Caverns. In old times, we priests of Anzuldin used it to cross between da river valley and dis region.\n\nIf Tzania has revealed its existence to da Sicklight Children, dey can make tings very difficult.\n\nI need ya to investigate.",o="穿过阿兰达克通道，找到霜生洞穴。",oEN="Traverse the Arandrak passage and find the Frostbirth Caverns.",p="<霜巨人似乎拿不准该把你当盟友还是敌人。>",pEN="<The frost giant seems uncertain whether to treat you as ally or enemy.>",c="小小的<race>。\n\n<奥尔格林的声音像冰层开裂般隆隆作响。>\n\n你来晚了。病光正穿过这些洞穴推进。里面，你只会找到死亡与悲伤。",cEN="Little <race>.\n\n<Olgrim’s voice rumbles like cracking ice.>\n\nYou are too late. The Sicklight pushes through these caverns. Inside, you will find only death and sorrow."}
Q[175281]={d="霜生洞穴不只是一条通道；它是无数白豹——雪之子的家园。\n\n<奥尔格林攥紧一只巨拳。霜花在他指节上噼啪作响。>\n\n后来那些染病的人带着他们的「祝福」来了。如今豹子从体内发光。它们灼烧。它们咬自己的幼崽。幼崽互相撕咬……\n\n恐怕唯一的解药就是死亡。杀掉那些被感染的豹子。连它们的幼崽也杀。尤其是那些可怜的幼崽……别让它们再受苦。\n\n还要确保罪魁祸首受到惩罚。",dEN="The Frostbirth Caverns are more than a passage; they are home to countless white leopards, children of the snow.\n\n<Olgrim clenches an enormous fist. Frost crackles over his knuckles.>\n\nThen those sick ones came with their blessings. Now the leopards glow from within. They burn. They bite their cubs. The cubs bite one another…\n\nI fear the only cure is death. Kill the afflicted leopards. Even their cubs. Especially their poor cubs… Spare them the suffering.\n\nAnd make certain the guilty are punished.",o="杀死霜生洞穴中被污染的豹子，并击败腐化它们的光辉先知。",oEN="Slay the contaminated leopards of the Frostbirth Caverns and defeat the Radiant Prophets who corrupted them.",p="洞穴安静下来了吗？",pEN="Did the caves fall silent?",c="<泽拉基静静地听着。>\n\n那些豹子是安祖尔丁本人的后裔。我一直担心会发生这样的事。\n\n杀掉它们是对的，<race>。当病光占据一个人的心智，你已经看到接下来是什么：\n\n痛苦。疯狂。羞辱。",cEN="<Zeraki listens in silence.>\n\nDose leopards descended from Anzuldin himself. I feared sometin’ like dis might have happened.\n\nKillin’ dem was da right choice, <race>. When da Sicklight takes hold of a mind, ya have seen what follows:\n\nPain. Madness. Shame."}
Q[175282]={d="我们得封住通道。封闭这些洞穴。\n\n<奥尔格林抬头望向凹凸不平的石头穹顶。>\n\n这座山老了。它累了。只要我们客气地请求，它会愿意崩塌。\n\n有几根冰柱支撑着这处隘口。打断几根，剩下的事交给山的重量。\n\n霜生洞穴将成为那些可悲巨魔的坟墓。",dEN="We must close the passage. Seal the caverns.\n\n<Olgrim raises his eyes to the uneven stone ceiling.>\n\nThe mountain is old. Tired. It will agree to collapse, if we ask it politely.\n\nThere are pillars of ice holding up the gorge. Break a few, and the mountain’s weight will do the rest.\n\nThe Frostbirth Caverns shall be the tomb of those wretched trolls.",o="使霜生洞穴的数处塌方，封死病光之子使用的通道。",oEN="Collapse several sections of the Frostbirth Caverns to block the passage used by the Sicklight Children.",p="山在等待。",pEN="Da mountain waits.",c="<一声遥远的轰鸣在洞穴中回荡。雪、碎石与尘土像白灰一样从穹顶落下。>\n\n好。\n\n<奥尔格林把一只手按在冰封的岩壁上。>\n\n路封上了。这样一来，你救下了几只豹子的性命。",cEN="<A distant roar rolls through the cavern. Snow, stone, and dust fall from the ceiling like white ash.>\n\nGood.\n\n<Olgrim rests one hand against the frozen wall.>\n\nThe way is closed. With that, you have saved the lives of a few leopards."}
Q[175283]={d="我查到了坦扎妮娅的下落。\n\n<泽拉基的声音里没有半点得意。要说有什么，他听起来比以往任何时候都更害怕。>\n\n那个疯女人去了安祖尔丁本人的神庙。她想让雪之罗阿染病，好让他遭受和马特拉坎同样的命运。\n\n她熟悉我的气味。可你的……你们两个素未谋面。要是我们当中有谁能让她措手不及，那就是你。\n\n而事到如今，你已经证明了自己是最强的。",dEN="I have found out where Tzania is.\n\n<There is no trace of triumph in Zeraki’s voice. If anything, he sounds more frightened than ever.>\n\nDa madwoman went to da very temple of Anzuldin himself. She means to make da Loa of da Snows sick, so he suffers da same fate as Matlacan.\n\nShe knows my scent. Yours, however… you two have never met. If one of us can surprise her, it be you.\n\nAnd by now, ya have already proven yourself the stronger.",o="进入安祖尔丁的神庙，净化光辉腐化，并击败坦扎妮娅。",oEN="Enter the temple of Anzuldin, cleanse the Radiant Corruption, and defeat Tzania.",p="<冰冷的空气在罗阿周围震颤。>",pEN="<The icy air vibrates around the Loa.>",c="你在苍角的雪地上走过的每一步，我都感受到了。你跋涉了很远才来到这里。\n\n<安祖尔丁的声音在你脑海中回响。>\n\n你目睹了一切：我的大祭司的罪。我的祭司们的死。我的后裔的疾病……我的神庙所遭的亵渎。\n\n可什么也没能让你退缩。\n\n<罗阿每说一个字，空气都在颤抖。>\n\n事实上，你已赢得了我的祝福。",cEN="I have felt each of your steps in the snows of Palehorn. You have traveled far to reach this place.\n\n<Anzuldin’s voice echoes in your thoughts.>\n\nYou have witnessed it all: the sin of my High Priestess. The deaths of my priests. The sickness of my progeny… the profanation of my temple.\n\nBut nothing cowed you.\n\n<The air trembles with each word the Loa speaks.>\n\nYou have earned my blessing, indeed."}
