Q[175348]={d="我还有件事要交给你。最后一趟差事，配得上一位已证明自己是杜恩卡扎德之友的人。\n\n你去过灰空，对吧？<鲍格沃夫并不等你回答。>好，好。\n\n我要你去见守备队长德雷温爵士，禀报冬日小径的情况。告诉他，我们正竭尽全力把霜鬃族挡在桥的这一侧。\n\n还有，把深铁矿道车的破坏事件也告诉他。\n\n去吧。他会想尽快听到我们的消息。",dEN="I have another task for you. One last errand worthy of someone who has proven to be a friend of Dun Kazad.\n\nYou have been to Graysky, have you not? <Baugwolf does not wait for you to answer.> Good, good.\n\nI need you to report to Sir Draewyn, commander of the guard, and inform him of the situation on the Winter Path. Tell him we are doing everything we can to contain the Frostmane on this side of the bridge.\n\nAnd tell him about the trouble with the Deeprun Tram sabotage.\n\nGo. He will want news from us as soon as possible.",o="向灰空的德雷温爵士禀报杜恩卡扎德的处境和他们面临的麻烦。",oEN="Report to Sir Draewyn at Graysky, and inform him of Dun Kazad's situation and the troubles they are facing.",c="<德雷温爵士仔细听完你关于杜恩卡扎德处境及其所面临麻烦的禀报。>\n\n<然后，他笑了。>\n\n你和我们的邻居矮人打交道，办得不错。\n\n只要一有余力，我就设法从灰空派出援军。",cEN="<Sir Draewyn listens carefully to your report on Dun Kazad's situation and the troubles they face.>\n\n<Then, he smiles.>\n\nYou have done good work with our neighbors, the dwarves.\n\nAs soon as we are able, I will see about sending reinforcements from Graysky."}
Q[175349]={d="你有没有兴趣获得祖母妙药所有商品的一生折扣？\n\n那就听好了，我这儿有件差事，除了会走路之外什么本事都不需要。\n\n<希尔达递给你一只水晶小瓶，里面盛着明亮闪烁的液体。>\n\n我要你把这个送去邓郡的乌莉拉·灰谷。路上是这副光景，几乎没商队肯出灰空。而那可怜的女人几周前就订了这瓶药膏。\n\n我连想都不愿想，她的皮疹到现在恶化成什么样子了。",dEN="Would you be interested in earning a lifetime discount on every product we sell at Grandmother's Remedy?\n\nThen pay attention, because I have a task for which you need no talent beyond the ability to walk.\n\n<Hilda hands you a glass vial containing a bright, shimmering liquid.>\n\nI need you to take this to Ulira Greyvale, in Dunshire. With things as they are on the road, hardly any caravans are leaving Graysky. And the poor woman requested this ointment several weeks ago already.\n\nI do not even want to imagine how much worse her rash must have grown by now.",o="把希尔达的药膏交给邓郡的乌莉拉·灰谷。",oEN="Deliver Hilda's Ointment to Ulira Greyvale in Dunshire.",p="有什么我能帮你的吗？\n\n<一片难看的皮疹覆在女人的部分脸、脖子和手背上。她抓得太狠，皮都破了。>",pEN="Can I help you with something?\n\n<An ugly rash covers part of the woman's face, her neck, and the backs of her hands. She has scratched so much that her skin is raw.>",c="那是……？\n\n<乌莉拉接过小瓶的郑重，就像祭司在弥撒前接过圣物一般。>\n\n我都快疯了。我几乎坐不住！一整天从屋里走到屋外，又从屋外走回屋里。\n\n虽然当时我已经预付过钱，还是请你收下这个。算是赔你的辛苦。",cEN="Is that...?\n\n<Ulira takes the vial with the same ceremony with which a priest might receive a sacred relic before mass.>\n\nI was going mad. I could barely sit still! All day pacing from the house to outside, and back inside again.\n\nThough I paid for it in advance at the time, please accept this. For your trouble."}
Q[175350]={d="你。\n\n<泽尔达顽皮地招手让你靠近。要不是她脸上的皱纹那么多，你也许会以为她在跟你调情。>\n\n我要请你帮个忙。就叫它\"差事\"吧。你会发现这事非常简单：\n\n我需要你把这枚护符送到暗影井村。更确切地说，送到塞德温的马厩。\n\n他要说什么，别理他，直接把护符交给他的一头牛。哪一头？\n\n你见到她就知道了。本能会告诉你。",dEN="You.\n\n<Zelda beckons you closer with a playful gesture. If the wrinkles on her face were less generous, you might think she was flirting with you.>\n\nI need to ask you a favor. A “task,” let us call it. You will see it is a very simple matter:\n\nI need you to take this amulet to the village of Shadewell. More specifically, to Cedwyn's stable.\n\nIgnore him, if he says anything, and give the amulet directly to one of his cows. Which one?\n\nWhen you see her, you will know. Instinct will tell you.",o="把泽尔达的护符交给暗影井塞德温马厩里的那头牛。",oEN="Take Zelda's amulet to the cow in Cedwyn's stable, in Shadewell.",p="哞——？",pEN="Moooo?",c="<那头牛的眼睛像木桩一样钉住你。那对黑色瞳孔后面有什么在游动，激起你一股原始的逃跑冲动。>\n\n<一个声音挤进你的思绪。那头牛的眼睛是两潭深不见底的黑暗。>\n\n\"你做得很好。现在走吧。别向任何人提起我。\"",cEN="<The cow's eyes fix upon you like stakes. Something swims behind those black pupils, awakening in you a primal urge to flee.>\n\n<A voice forces its way into your thoughts. The cow's eyes are two wells of deep blackness.>\n\n“You have done well. Now go. And speak to no one of me.”"}
Q[177877]={d="许多年来，安其拉的古老废墟一直荒废而沉寂。塞纳里奥议会始终密切关注着那片废墟，但除了偶尔出现的巨型虫子之外，那其实是相当安静的差事。\n\n直到最近，我们才收到塞纳里奥议会关于墙内活动频繁的消息。他们目前正在筹备一次远征进行调查。\n\n加入塞纳里奥部队，调查那片废墟。杀死你在那里发现的任何虫子和敌对生物。",dEN="For many years the old ruins of Ahn'Qiraj laid deserted and dormant. The Cenarion Circle always kept a close eye on those ruins but outside of a few oversized bugs here and there it was quite a silent duty.\n\nOnly very recently have we received messages from the Cenarion Circle about high activity within the Walls. They are currently preparing an expedition to investigate.\n\nJoin the Cenarion forces and investigate the ruins. Slay any bugs and other hostile creatures that you find there.",o="阻止安其拉的入侵。",oEN="Stop the Ahn'Qiraji invasion.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177878]={d="历史记载，数千年前强大的古拉巴什帝国被一场大规模内战撕成碎片。一群颇具影响力的巨魔祭司召唤出一位古老而可怕的血神——夺灵者哈卡的化身。最终，祭司们被击败并遭到流放。\n\n如今，我们收到报告称，一群自称哈卡莱的新祭司正试图重现仪式，将哈卡召唤到我们的世界。\n\n前往祖尔格拉布，阻止那些仪式者将哈卡释放到艾泽拉斯！",dEN="History says that thousands of years ago the powerful Gurubashi Empire was torn apart by a massive civil war. An influential group of troll priests called forth the avatar of an ancient and terrible blood-god - Hakkar the Soulflayer. Ultimately, the priests were defeated and exiled.\n\nNow in the current day we have received reports that a new group of priests that call themselves the Hakkari are trying to recreate the rituals to summon Hakkar to our world.\n\nTravel to Zul'Gurub and stop the ritualists from unleashing Hakkar onto Azeroth!",o="让夺灵者永远沉默！",oEN="Silence the Soulflayer!",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177879]={d="黑龙奈法利安，死亡之翼之子，目前正在黑石山上层尖塔中调动他的军队，其中包括黑石氏族的兽人、尖石食人魔和燃棘巨魔。但这些甚至都不是这条黑龙藏在那块岩石中的最强力量。彩色巨龙、黑龙、黑色龙人、雏龙以及所有已知巨龙军团的蛋等等。他创造终极巨龙军团的实验已经严重失控，危险至极。\n\n我们必须终结他的疯狂，以及他那支由龙类憎恶组成的炽热大军。\n\n集结起来，前往黑翼之巢，杀死奈法利安。",dEN="The dragon Nefarian, son of Deathwing, is currently mobilizing his armies consisting of orcs from the Blackrock clan, Spirestone Ogres and Smolderthorne Trolls in the upper spires of the Blackrock Mountain. But those aren't even the most powerful forces the black dragon is hiding within that rock. Chromatic dragons, black dragons, black wyrmkin, whelps and eggs of all known dragon flights and many more. His experiments in creating the ultimate dragon flight have gotten far out of control and way too dangerous.\n\nWe need to put an end to his madness and his fiery army of dragonic abominations.\n\nGather up and travel to the Blackwing Lair and slay Nefarian.",o="杀死奈法利安！",oEN="Slay Nefarian!",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177880]={d="在黑石山下的洞穴深处，有一个被黑铁矮人称为\"熔火之心\"的地方。那是一个布满熔岩魔像、火元素和其他炽热生物的深渊。它们全都效忠于被称为火焰之王拉格纳罗斯的存在，他是居住在艾泽拉斯深处元素位面的元素领主之一。\n\n我们的间谍报告称，他们正在准备最后的仪式，要将拉格纳罗斯召唤到我们的世界。召唤一位元素领主可能会给整个艾泽拉斯带来巨大的灾难与毁灭。\n\n必须不惜一切代价阻止这一切！集结一支军队，前往熔火之心，杀死任何挡路的人。",dEN="Deep down in the caverns below the Blackrock Mountain lies a place the Dark Iron Dwarves call the \"Molten Core\". A chasm filled with golems made of lava, fire elementals and other fiery creatures. They all serve the being known as Ragnaros the Firelord, one of the elemental lords residing in the elemental planes deep inside Azeroth.\n\nOur spy reports tell us that they are preparing the final rituals to summon Ragnaros to our world. The summoning of an elemental Lord could cause great disasters and destruction all around Azeroth.\n\nThat must be prevented at any cost! Gather an army, travel to the Molten Core and slay anyone that stands in your way.",o="熄灭火焰之王！",oEN="Extinguish the Firelord!",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177881]={d="我们的斥候报告，死亡之翼的女儿奥妮克希亚目前正藏身在尘泥沼泽深处的巢穴中。在被人发现她就是卡特拉娜·普瑞斯托女士，并且是暴风城国王瓦里安·乌瑞恩失踪的罪魁祸首之后，她逃到了那里。\n\n我们必须趁她最虚弱的时候发动攻击！\n\n召集所有有能力的冒险者，前往奥妮克希亚的巢穴，干掉她！",dEN="Our scouts report that Onyxia, the daughter of Deathwing, is currently hiding inside her lair deep in the swamps of the Dustwallow Marsh. She fled there after she was discovered to be Lady Katrana Prestor and was responsible for the disappearance of Varian Wrynn, King of Stormwind.\n\nWe need to strike now when she's at her weakest!\n\nGather any able-bodied adventurers, travel to Onyxias lair and take her out!",o="杀死奥妮克希亚！",oEN="Slay Onyxia!",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177882]={d="虽然血色十字军的主要目标是抗击天灾，但他们对所有生者种族同样极其危险。在盲目的狂热中，他们真的相信任何非人类种族要么是天灾的一员，要么与之结盟。",dEN="Although the Scarlet Crusades main focus is to fight the Scourge they are ever so dangerous to all the living races too. In their blind fanaticism they actually believe that any non-human race is either part of the scourge or allied with them.",o="在斯坦索姆阻止血色十字军。",oEN="Stop the Scarlet Crusade in Stratholme.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177883]={d="瑞文戴尔男爵曾是一位富有的地主，克尔苏加德的支持者，也是瘟疫谷物在北方人类王国蔓延的主要罪魁祸首之一。\n\n如今他指挥着目前盘踞在斯坦索姆东部的天灾部队，不断与血色十字军争夺斯坦索姆的完全控制权。\n\n潜入叛徒的巢穴，将他绳之以法！",dEN="Baron Rivendare, once a rich landowner, supporter of Kel'thuzad and one of the main delinquents responsible for the spread of the plagued grain across the northern human kingdoms.\n\nHe is now commanding the scourge forces that are currently infesting the eastern parts of Stratholme. Continously fighting against the Scarlet Crusade over full control of Stratholme.\n\nVenture into the traitors lair and bring him to justice!",o="杀死瑞文戴尔男爵。",oEN="Kill Baron Rivendare.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177884]={d="通缉！\n\n因犯下对抗生命本身的罪行，并制造了无穷无尽的天灾憎恶！\n\n黑暗院长加丁及其同伙目前居住在西瘟疫之地的通灵学院。\n\n死活不论。",dEN="Wanted!\n\nFor crimes against life itself and the creation of endless scourge abominations!\n\nDarkmaster Gandling and his Cohorts that are currently residing in Scholomance in the Western Plaguelands.\n\nDead.",o="杀死黑暗院长加丁。",oEN="Kill Darkmaster Gandling.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177885]={d="有传言说，黑铁氏族的矮人效忠于一个名为拉格纳罗斯的强大邪恶存在。他被称为\"火焰之王\"，是目前居住在艾泽拉斯深处元素位面的元素领主之一。如果他们将其\"神明\"召唤到我们位面的努力成功，可能会给艾泽拉斯带来绝对的灾难。\n\n这一情况必须被调查并处理！\n\n前往黑石深渊，终结他们的召唤企图！",dEN="Rumors have it that the dwarves of the Dark Iron clan are serving a great evil being known as Ragnaros. Also titled \"The Firelord\", he is one of the elemental lords currently residing in the elemental planes deep inside Azeroth. If their efforts to summon their \"deity\" to our planes are succesful, it could spell absolute disaster for Azeroth.\n\nThis situation needs to be investigated and taken care of!\n\nGo to the Blackrock Depths and put an end to their summoning efforts!",o="摧毁黑铁氏族。",oEN="Destroy the Dark Iron Clan.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177886]={d="致所有寻求财富与荣耀的冒险者！名为维克图斯的龙人、奈法利安的造物，目前居住在下黑石塔，因他对所有种族犯下的骇人罪行而被通缉。他的实验和他本身的存在都与生命为敌。",dEN="To all adventurers looking for riches and glory! The Wyrmkin and creation of Nefarian called Overlord Wyrmthalak currently residing in the Lower Blackrock Spire is wanted for his hideous crimes against all races. His experiments and his very existence go against life itself.",o="杀死维克图斯霸主。",oEN="Kill Overlord Wyrmthalak",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177887]={d="我们收到报告称，上黑石塔内的活动突然增加。看起来黑龙奈法利安正在调动他的兽人部队，准备对火焰之王的巢穴发动全面进攻，企图夺取黑石山的完全控制权。\n我们绝不能让他得逞！如果奈法利安成功招募黑铁矮人为其效力，对我们所有人都可能是灾难性的！\n\n目前达基萨斯将军负责军备工作。\n\n前往上黑石塔，杀死达基萨斯将军和他的爪牙！",dEN="We have received reports of a sudden rise of activity within the Upper Blackrock Spire. It seems that the black dragon Nefarian is mobilizing his orcish forces to prepare an all-out assault on the lair of the Firelord in an attempt to seize full control over the Blackrock Mountain.\nWe can't let this happen! If Nefarian manages to recruit the Dark Iron Dwarves for his efforts it could be disastrous for all of us!\n\nCurrently General Drakkisath is in charge of the arming effort.\n\nTravel to the Upper Blackrock Spire to kill General Drakkisath and his minons!",o="终结达基萨斯的暴政。",oEN="Put an end to Drakkisath's tyranny.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177888]={d="东厄运之槌废墟的居民崇拜一种非常强大的物品，名为\"神秘宝珠\"。许多旅行者曾试图与当地居民谈判获取这些宝珠。有时成功，有时……\n这一切必须结束。\n\n为了让神秘宝珠的丰富来源对所有人开放，我们必须杀死东厄运之槌废墟的现任居民。",dEN="The population of the eastern Dire Maul Ruins worship very powerful objects called \"Mystic Orbs\". Many travelers have tried to negotiate with its inhabitants to obtain the orbs from them. Sometimes with success and sometimes..\nThis has to end.\n\nTo make the plentiful source of Mystic orbs availablefor everyone we have to slay the current inhabitants of the eastern Dire Maul ruins.",o="杀死扭曲者奥兹恩。",oEN="Kill Alzzin the Wildshaper.",p="地下城的居民仍在呼吸。等你穿越时间线完成任务后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再度归于沉寂。你穿越时间线的英勇已成传奇，英雄。去领取你的奖赏吧。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177889]={d="通缉！\n\n一位第三方委托人悬赏任何能击败现任戈多克食人魔之王的人。这位国王对外来者不太\"开放\"。这位匿名委托人希望扶植一位对与戈多克食人魔达成各种贸易协定稍微\"开放\"一些的国王。\n\n前往北厄运之槌，干掉现任戈多克之王。",dEN="Wanted!\n\nA third party contractor has set a reward out for anyone that can take down the current king of the Gordok Ogres. The king is not very \"open\" to outsiders. The anonymous contractor wants to instate a king that is a bit more \"open\" for various trade agreements with the Gordok Ogres.\n\nTravel to Diremaul North and take out the current king of the Gordoks.",o="杀死戈多克大王。",oEN="Slay King Gordok.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177890]={d="托塞德林王子曾是艾萨拉女王的忠实仆从，一位辛德拉，也是暗夜精灵古城埃雷萨拉斯——即今日的厄运之槌——的领袖。永恒之井毁灭后，托塞德林王子将一只恶魔囚禁在埃雷萨拉斯的废墟中，并让他的臣民汲取它的力量，从而维持对幸存辛德拉的统治。\n\n长期接触恶魔力量扭曲了托塞德林的心智，使他成为艾泽拉斯的巨大威胁。\n\n杀死王子的唯一方法是摧毁环绕能量柱的守卫，以降低力场。完成之后，摧毁伊莫塔尔。王子的力量大幅削弱后，你便可以攻击并终结他。",dEN="Prince Tortheldrin was a loyal servant to Queen Azshara, a Shen'dralar and the leader of the ancient night elven city Eldre'Thalas known today as Dire Maul. After the Well of Eternity's destruction, Prince Tortheldrin maintained control over the surviving Shen'dralar by imprisoning a demon in the ruins of Eldre'Thalas and letting his subjects siphon its strength.\n\nThe exposure to demonic power twisted Tortheldrin's mind and made him a great danger to Azeroth.\n\nThe only way of killing the prince is to destroy the guardians surrounding the pylons to lower the force field. When this is done, destroy Immol'thar. With the Prince's power greatly reduced, you may attack and end him.",o="杀死托塞德林王子。",oEN="Kill Prince Tortheldrin.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177891]={d="我不愿在没有更多训练的情况下派你去执行如此危险的任务，但威胁已经出现。在应对这一威胁之前，先召集一支由熟练冒险者组成的小队。\n\n深入哀嚎洞穴，在穆坦努斯的噩梦进入我们的世界之前阻止他。",dEN="I'm loath to send you on such a dangerous task without more training, but the threat has presented itself now. Gather a party of skilled adventureres before you take on this threat.\n\nTravel deep into the Wailing Caverns and stop Mutanus before his nightmare enters our world.",o="进入哀嚎洞穴并杀死吞噬者穆坦努斯。",oEN="Enter The Wailing Caverns and slay Mutanus the Devourer.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177892]={d="我不愿在没有更多训练的情况下派你去执行如此危险的任务，但威胁已经出现。在应对这一威胁之前，先召集一支由熟练冒险者组成的小队。\n\n找到进入影牙城堡内院的方法。一路杀穿幽灵与狼人的军队，在阿鲁高法师的阴影蔓延到银松森林之外前杀死他。",dEN="I'm loath to send you on such a dangerous task without more training, but the threat has presented itself now. Gather a party of skilled adventureres before you take on this threat.\n\nFind a way to enter the inner courtyard of Shadowfang Keep. Fight your way through the army of ghosts and worgen and kill Archmage Argugal before his shadow extends past Silverpine Forest.",o="进入影牙城堡并杀死阿鲁高法师。",oEN="Enter Shadowfang Keep and slay Archmage Arugal.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177893]={d="许多年来，安其拉的古老废墟一直荒废而沉寂。塞纳里奥议会始终密切关注着那片废墟，但除了偶尔出现的巨型虫子之外，那其实是相当安静的差事。\n\n直到最近，我们才收到塞纳里奥议会关于墙内活动频繁的消息。他们目前正在筹备一次远征进行调查。\n\n加入塞纳里奥部队，调查那片废墟。杀死你在那里发现的任何虫子和敌对生物。",dEN="For many years the old ruins of Ahn'Qiraj laid deserted and dormant. The Cenarion Circle always kept a close eye on those ruins but outside of a few oversized bugs here and there it was quite a silent duty.\n\nOnly very recently have we received messages from the Cenarion Circle about high activity within the Walls. They are currently preparing an expedition to investigate.\n\nJoin the Cenarion forces and investigate the ruins. Slay any bugs and other hostile creatures that you find there.",o="阻止其拉虫人的入侵。",oEN="Stop the Qiraji invasion.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177895]={d="我不愿在没有更多训练的情况下派你去执行如此危险的任务，但威胁已经出现。在应对这一威胁之前，先召集一支由熟练冒险者组成的小队。\n\n肃清盘踞在死亡矿井中的强盗。终结首领艾德温·范克里夫，以确保威胁被真正清除。",dEN="I'm loath to send you on such a dangerous task without more training, but the threat has presented itself now. Gather a party of skilled adventureres before you take on this threat.\n\nRout the bandits that have taken up residence in the Deadmines. Put an end to leader Edwin Vancleef to ensure the threat is truly dealt with.",o="进入死亡矿井并杀死艾德温·范克里夫。",oEN="Enter The Deadmines and slay Edwin Vancleef.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177896]={d="英雄，我还有另一项危险的任务交给你。希望你身边有些值得信赖的同伴。\n\n侏儒们做得太过分了。他们在诺莫瑞根摆弄的科技太危险了……这要到什么时候才是个头？如果不加以阻止，冒险者们会整天玩弄科技而不是摧毁它……你明白我的意思。去摧毁机械师瑟玛普拉格。",dEN="I have another dangerous task for you hero. I hope you have some trusted companions at your side.\n\nThe gnomes have gone too far. The technology they play with in Gnomergan is too dangerous... where does it end? Adventurers will be playing on technology all day instead of destroying it if we don't... you get the idea. Go destroy Mekgineer Thermaplugg.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177897]={d="英雄，我还有另一项危险的任务交给你。希望你身边有些值得信赖的同伴。\n\n我们的间谍告诉我们，刺鬃酋长夏尔嘉一直在与天灾谈判。进入剃刀沼泽，在天灾与野猪人结成同盟之前干掉夏尔嘉！",dEN="I have another dangerous task for you hero. I hope you have some trusted companions at your side.\n\nOur spies tell us that Charlga Razorflank has been negotiating with the Scourge. Enter Razorfen Kraul and bring Charlga down before an alliance between the scourge and quilboars can be made!",o="进入剃刀沼泽并杀死刺鬃酋长夏尔嘉。",oEN="Enter Razorfen Kraul and slay Charlga Razorflank.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177898]={d="英雄，我还有另一项危险的任务交给你。希望你身边有些值得信赖的同伴。\n\n黑澗深渊中有一个本不该被打扰的生物正在苏醒。别让阿库麦尔浮出水面。",dEN="I have another dangerous task for you hero. I hope you have some trusted companions at your side.\n\nA creature is stirring that should have never been disturbed in Blackfathom Depths. Do not allow Aku'mai to reach the surface.",o="进入黑澗深渊并杀死阿库麦尔。",oEN="Enter Blackfathom Deeps and slay Aku'mai.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177899]={d="英雄，你的力量已经成长。我几乎觉得这次不是派你去执行自杀任务了……几乎。\n\n奥法师杜安至今还欠着图书馆的逾期罚款。这完全不可接受。前往血色修道院，给予他公正且完全正当的惩罚。死亡。",dEN="You've grown in strength hero. I almost feel like I'm not sending you on a suicide mission this time... almost.\n\nArcanist Doan still has unpaid library late fees. It's totally unacceptable. Visit the Scarlet Monastary and deliver his fair and totally justified punishment. Death.",o="进入血色修道院并杀死奥法师杜安。",oEN="Enter The Scarlet Monastery and slay Arcanist Doan.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177900]={d="英雄，你的力量已经成长。我几乎觉得这次不是派你去执行自杀任务了……几乎。\n\n我们本来乐意让血色十字军自生自灭……可你能相信吗，那些狂信徒中的一个竟然想竞选总统？！别误会……我反对他们阻止亡灵，但当你开始谈论人类是优等种族，并靠仇恨与恐惧展开竞选时，你就开始看起来像是该被一斧子劈在脸上的候选人了。去把他们全部杀光。",dEN="You've grown in strength hero. I almost feel like I'm not sending you on a suicide mission this time... almost.\n\nWe were content to leave the Scarlet Crusade to their own devices... but can you believe one of those fanatics wants to run for President?! Don't get me wrong... I'm opposed to them stopping the undead, but when you start talking about how humans are the master race and run on a campaign of hate and fear you start to look like a good candidate for an axe to the face. Go kill the lot of them.",o="进入血色修道院并杀死赫洛德和血色指挥官莫格莱尼。",oEN="Enter The Scarlet Monastery and slay Herod and Scarlet Commander Mograine.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177901]={d="英雄，你的力量已经成长。我几乎觉得这次不是派你去执行自杀任务了……几乎。\n\n看来我们没能及时阻止野猪人与天灾的谈判。一位强大的巫妖正在剃刀高地组建亡灵大军。这次彻底杀死寒冰使者阿门纳尔。",dEN="You've grown in strength hero. I almost feel like I'm not sending you on a suicide mission this time... almost.\n\nIt looks like we wern't quick enough to prevent the quilboar negotiations with the Scourge. A powerful lich is raising an undead army in Razorfen Downs. Kill Amnennar the Coldbringer for good this time.",o="进入剃刀高地并杀死寒冰使者阿门纳尔。",oEN="Enter Razorfen Downs and slay Amnennar the Coldbringer.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177902]={d="我开始觉得你可能真有潜力。想证明我看得没错吗？\n\n看来我是唯一一个在历史课上认真听讲的人？你听说过沙怒氏族吗？他们要对塔纳利斯历史上最血腥的篇章负责，这可不是小事！在乌克兹·沙顶酋长的氏族强大到足以挑战地精之前杀死他。",dEN="I'm beginning to think you might have potential. Care to prove me right?\n\nIt seems I'm the only one who paid attention in history class? Every heard of the Sandfury clan? They were responsible for the most bloody chapter in the history of Tanaris, and that's saying something! Kill Chief Ukorz Sandscalp before his clan is strong enough to challenge the goblins.",o="进入祖尔法拉克并杀死乌克兹·沙顶酋长。",oEN="Enter Zul'Farrak and slay Chief Ukorz Sandscalp.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177903]={d="我开始觉得你可能真有潜力。想证明我看得没错吗？\n\n这个不是上头派给我的，不过……你肯定不信！有个半人马说我妈胖！我知道一个完美的复仇办法。前往玛拉顿……然后杀了他的妈！胖的那个就是她。这就让他长记性了。",dEN="I'm beginning to think you might have potential. Care to prove me right?\n\nThis one didn't come from my superiors but... You won't believe this! Some centaur called my mom fat! I know the perfect way to get revenge. Travel to Mauradon... and kill his mom! She's the fat one. That'll teach him.",o="进入玛拉顿并杀死瑟莱德丝公主。",oEN="Enter Maraudon and slay Princess Theradras.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[177904]={d="我开始觉得你可能真有潜力。想证明我看得没错吗？\n\n黑铁矮人在荒芜之地挖出了一座古老的泰坦城市。前往那座古城，摧毁矮人们想为他们的主人取回的一切。",dEN="I'm beginning to think you might have potential. Care to prove me right?\n\nThe Dark Iron Dwarves have unearthed an ancient Titan city in the Badlands. Travel to the ancient city and destroy whatever it is the dwarves hope to retrieve for their master.",p="地牢中的居民仍在喘息。当你穿越时光线完成使命后再回来。",pEN="The dungeon's denizens still draw breath. Return when you have completed your mission across the timeways.",c="往昔的回响再次归于沉寂。你穿越时光线的英勇已成为传说，英雄。领取你的奖励。",cEN="The echoes of the past grow silent once more. Your bravery across the timeways is legendary, Hero. Claim your reward."}
Q[180133]={d="与新玩家组队并帮他们完成内容，即可获得导师印记！与新玩家组队期间，你还能获得飞升印记、神秘宝珠和神秘符文。\n\n当队伍中的新玩家杀死地下城或团队副本首领，或获得成就时，你将获得导师印记、飞升印记、神秘宝珠和符文。\n\n当队伍中的新玩家完成战场、竞技场，或交付任务时，你将获得导师印记和飞升印记。\n\n本周与新玩家组队并帮助他们，即可获得新的导师印记。",dEN="You can earn Marks of Mentorship by grouping up with new players and helping them complete content! You will also earn Marks of Ascension, Mystic Orbs and Mystic Runes while grouped with New Players.\n\nWhen a new player in your group kills a Dungeon or Raid Boss or Earns an Achievement you will earn Marks of Mentorship, Marks of Ascension, Mystic Orbs and Runes.\n\nWhen a new player in your group completes a Battleground, Arena or Turns in a Quest you will earn Marks of Mentorship and Marks of Ascension.\n\nGroup with and help new players and earn new Marks of Mentorship this week.",o="与新玩家组队并完成可获得导师印记的内容，来帮助他们！只有新获得的导师印记才计入进度。",oEN="Help new players by grouping with them and completing content that awards Marks of Mentorship! Credit is only awarded for newly earned Marks of Mentorship.",p="你的任务尚未完成。完成契约后回到告示板来。",pEN="Your task is not yet complete. Return to the board when you have fulfilled the contract."}
Q[189190]={d="在神秘祭坛上打开附魔收藏标签页，从你的附魔收藏中选取一个附魔，将其应用到生效附魔槽位，然后选择保存更改以激活你的神秘附魔。\n\n激活收藏中的附魔需要神秘宝珠，可通过告示板的日常任务、地下城与团队副本、战场，或击败世界中的敌人获得！\n\n1 个传说附魔可应用于祭坛中央的大槽位。\n\n3 个史诗附魔可应用于内环的中型槽位。\n\n其余槽位中，你可以随意应用任意数量的稀有和优秀附魔。其中许多附魔可叠加至多 3 层。将鼠标悬停在收藏中的附魔上，即可查看其最大叠加层数。",dEN="Open the Enchant Collection tab from a Mystic Altar, select an Enchant from your Enchant Collections and apply it to an Active Enchant slot, then select Save Changes to activate your Mystic Enchant.\n\nActivating Enchants from your collection requires Mystic Orbs, which can be earned from Daily Quests on the Call Board, Dungeons and Raids, Battlegrounds or defeating enemies in the world!\n\n1 Legendary Enchant can be applied to the large center slot in the Altar.\n\n3 Epic Enchants can be applied in the medium slots in the inner ring.\n\nYou can apply as many Rare and Uncommon Enchants in the remaining slots as you'd like. Many of these Enchants can stack up to 3 times. Mousing over the Enchant in the collection reveals its max stack size.",o="前往祭坛，从你的附魔收藏中选用一个神秘附魔，应用到生效附魔槽位。",oEN="Visit an Altar and apply a Mystic Enchant from your Enchant Collection to an Active Enchant slot.",p="你在飞升之路上还有事要做。完成当前任务后再回来。",pEN="You still have work to do on the path of Ascension. Return when you have completed the task at hand.",c="干得好，英雄！你在飞升之路上进展顺利。继续前进吧。\n相关",cEN="Well done, Hero! You are progressing nicely on the path of Ascension. Keep pushing forward.\nRelated"}
Q[199999]={d="当一名游侠，不只是拿起弓，或躲在树荫里作战，<name>。\n\n当一名游侠，本质上意味着你与荒野有着深厚的联结。你是它的守护者。\n\n我派我的猎鹰乔去周边侦察，可它一直没回来。\n\n请你找到它，让它回到我身边。",dEN="Being a Ranger is more than just picking up a bow, or fighting from the cover of the trees, <name>.\n\nBeing a Ranger, at its core, means that you have a profound connection to the wilds. You are its protector.\n\nI sent my falcon, Jo, to scout the surrounding areas, but he has not returned.\n\nPlease, find him and direct him to return back to me.",o="在北郡谷一带寻找欧文的猎鹰。",oEN="Find Owen's falcon in the Northshire Valley area.",c="这只猎鹰受了伤，腿上仔细绑着一张字条。",cEN="This falcon is injured and there is a note carefully tied around its leg."}
Q[200000]={d="附近的灌木丛里有什么在动。\n\n你正遭到攻击！",dEN="Something is rustling in the nearby bushes.\n\nYou're under attack!",o="杀死那只可疑的生物。",oEN="Slay the suspicious creature.",c="那生物一定就是袭击乔的元凶。\n\n我得处理乔的伤口。",cEN="That creature must have been what attacked Jo.\n\nI should tend to Jo's wounds."}
Q[200001]={d="你发现猎鹰身上附着一张字条，上面写着：\n\n<如果你正在读这段话，说明你找到了我的朋友。这张字条旁还有一小瓶红色药水。若它受了伤就喂给它，它自会知道接下来该怎么做。>",dEN="You find a note attached to the falcon that reads:\n\n<If you are reading this, you have found my friend. Attached to this note is a small red vial. Give it to him if he is injured, and he will know what to do next.>",o="对猎鹰使用红色药水。",oEN="Use the Red Vial on the falcon.",p="你回来了……还把我的药水瓶带回来了。好。",pEN="You've returned...and you've brought me back my vial. Good.",c="谢谢你找到乔。它已经回到我身边了，跟往常一样健康。\n\n我又派它去执行另一次侦察任务了。\n\n……你是说，有人在乔附近看到一只奇怪的生物，还袭击了你？那一定就是伤了我家孩子的东西。\n\n我得好好查一查这件事。照你的描述，不管这东西是什么，它都不是艾尔文森林的原生物种。",cEN="Thank you for finding Jo. He has already returned to me, healthy as ever.\n\nI've already sent him on yet another scouting mission.\n\n... you're saying a strange creature was seen near Jo and that it attacked you? That must have been the creature that injured my boy.\n\nI'll have to look into this more. Based on your description, whatever this is, it's not native to Elwynn Forest."}
Q[200002]={d="当一名游侠，不只是抄起一把弓，或躲在树荫里作战，<name>。\n\n当一名游侠，本质上意味着你与荒野有着深厚的联结。你是它的守护者。\n\n我派我的猎鹰塔洛斯去周边侦察，可它一直没回来。\n\n请你找到它，让它回到我身边。",dEN="Being a Ranger is more than just picking up a bow, or fighting from the cover of the trees, <name>.\n\nBeing a Ranger, at its core, means that you have a profound connection to the wilds. You are its protector.\n\nI sent my falcon, Talos, to scout the surrounding areas, but he has not returned.\n\nPlease, find him and direct him to return back to me.",o="在冷脊谷寻找巴鲁尔的猎鹰。",oEN="Find Baruhr's falcon in Coldridge Valley.",p="你还把我的药水瓶带回来了。我知道这意味着什么。谢了，小子。",pEN="An' you've brought my vial back. I know what this means. Thank you lad.",c="看来这就是那只猎鹰，而且它似乎受了伤。",cEN="This seems to be the falcon in question, and it seems injured."}
Q[200003]={d="附近的灌木丛里有什么在动。\n\n你正遭到攻击！",dEN="Something is rustling in the nearby bushes.\n\nYou're under attack!",o="杀死那只可疑的生物。",oEN="Slay the suspicious creature.",c="猎鹰看起来很不安。一定是那只可疑的生物袭击了它！",cEN="The falcon seems distraught. It must have been the suspicious creature who attacked it!"}
Q[200004]={d="你发现猎鹰身上附着一张字条，上面写着：\n\n<如果你正在读这段话，说明你找到了我的朋友。这张字条旁还有一小瓶红色药水。若它受了伤就喂给它，它自会知道接下来该怎么做。>",dEN="You find a note attached to the falcon that reads:\n\n<If you are reading this, you have found my friend. Attached to this note is a small red vial. Give it to him if he is injured, and he will know what to do next.>",o="对猎鹰使用红色药水。",oEN="Use the Red Vial on the falcon.",p="是啊，小子，塔洛斯已经回来了。谢谢你。",pEN="Aye lad, Talos has already returned. Thank you.",c="谢谢你找到塔洛斯。它已经回到我身边了，跟往常一样健康。\n\n我又派它去执行另一次侦察任务了。\n\n……你是说，有人在塔洛斯附近看到一只奇怪的生物，还袭击了你？那一定就是伤了我家孩子的东西。\n\n我得好好查一查这件事。照你的描述，不管这东西是什么，它都不是丹莫罗的原生物种。",cEN="Thank you for finding Talos. He has already returned to me, healthy as ever.\n\nI've already sent him on yet another scouting mission.\n\n... you're saying a strange creature was seen near Talos and that it attacked you? That must have been the creature that injured my boy.\n\nI'll have to look into this more. Based on your description, whatever this is, it's not native to Dun Morogh."}
Q[200005]={d="当一名游侠，不只是抄起一把弓，或躲在树荫里作战，<name>。\n\n当一名游侠，本质上意味着你与荒野有着深厚的联结。你是它的守护者。\n\n我派我的猎鹰布莉姆去周边侦察，可它一直没回来。\n\n请你找到它，让它回到我身边。",dEN="Being a Ranger is more than just picking up a bow, or fighting from the cover of the trees, <name>.\n\nBeing a Ranger, at its core, means that you have a profound connection to the wilds. You are its protector.\n\nI sent my falcon, Brim, to scout the surrounding areas, but he has not returned.\n\nPlease, find him and direct him to return back to me.",o="在影谷寻找海德里尔的猎鹰。",oEN="Find Hydriel's falcon in Shadowglen.",c="看来这就是那只猎鹰，而且它似乎受了伤。",cEN="This seems to be the falcon in question, and it seems injured."}
Q[200006]={d="附近的灌木丛里有什么在动。\n\n你正遭到攻击！",dEN="Something is rustling in the nearby bushes.\n\nYou're under attack!",o="杀死那只可疑的生物。",oEN="Slay the suspicious creature.",c="猎鹰看起来很不安。一定是那只可疑的生物袭击了它！",cEN="The falcon seems distraught. It must have been the suspicious creature who attacked it!"}
Q[200007]={d="你发现猎鹰身上附着一张字条，上面写着：\n\n<如果你正在读这段话，说明你找到了我的朋友。这张字条旁还有一小瓶红色药水。若它受了伤就喂给它，它自会知道接下来该怎么做。>",dEN="You find a note attached to the falcon that reads:\n\n<If you are reading this, you have found my friend. Attached to this note is a small red vial. Give it to him if he is injured, and he will know what to do next.>",o="对猎鹰使用红色药水。",oEN="Use the Red Vial on the falcon.",p="太棒了。布莉姆回来了！",pEN="Absolutely wonderful. Brim has returned!",c="谢谢你找到布莉姆。她已经回到我身边了，跟往常一样健康。\n\n我又派她去执行另一次侦察任务了。\n\n……你是说，有人在布莉姆附近看到一只奇怪的生物，还袭击了你？那一定就是伤了我家孩子的东西。\n\n我得好好查一查这件事。照你的描述，不管这东西是什么，它都不是泰达希尔的原生物种。",cEN="Thank you for finding Brim. She has already returned to me, healthy as ever.\n\nI've already sent him on yet another scouting mission.\n\n... you're saying a strange creature was seen near Brim and that it attacked you? That must have been the creature that injured my boy.\n\nI'll have to look into this more. Based on your description, whatever this is, it's not native to Teldrassil."}
Q[200008]={d="当一名游侠，不只是抄起一把弓，或躲在树荫里作战，<name>。\n\n当一名游侠，归根结底意味着你与荒野有着深厚的联结。你是它的守护者。\n\n我派我的猎鹰比奇去周边侦察，可它一直没回来。\n\n请你找到它，让它回到我身边。",dEN="Bein' a Ranger is more than just pickin' up a bow, or fightin' from the cover of the trees, <name>.\n\nBein' a Ranger, ultimately, means that you have a deep connection to the wilds. You are its guardian.\n\nI sent my falcon, Beaky, to scout the surrounding areas, but he has not returned.\n\nPlease, find him and direct him to return back to me.",o="在试炼谷寻找你的塔尔敦的猎鹰。",oEN="Find your Tar'dun's falcon in Valley of Trials.",c="看来这就是那只猎鹰，而且它似乎受了伤。",cEN="This seems to be the falcon in question, and it seems injured."}
Q[200009]={d="附近的灌木丛里有什么在动。\n\n你正遭到攻击！",dEN="Something is rustling in the nearby bushes.\n\nYou're under attack!",o="杀死那只可疑的生物。",oEN="Slay the suspicious creature.",c="猎鹰看起来很不安。一定是那只可疑的生物袭击了它！",cEN="The falcon seems distraught. It must have been the suspicious creature who attacked it!"}
Q[200010]={d="你发现猎鹰身上附着一张字条，上面写着：\n\n<如果你正在读这段话，说明你找到了我的朋友。这张字条旁还有一小瓶红色药水。若它受了伤就喂给它，它自会知道接下来该怎么做。>",dEN="You find a note attached to the falcon that reads:\n\n<If you are reading this, you have found my friend. Attached to this note is a small red vial. Give it to him if he is injured, and he will know what to do next.>",o="对猎鹰使用红色药水。",oEN="Use the Red Vial on the falcon.",p="Lok'tar，<name>。你干得很好。",pEN="Lok'tar, <name>. You have done well.",c="谢谢你找到比奇。它已经回到我身边了，跟往常一样健康。\n\n我又派它去执行另一次侦察任务了。\n\n……你是说，有人在比奇附近看到一只奇怪的生物，还袭击了你？那一定就是伤了我家孩子的东西。\n\n我得好好查一查这件事。照你的描述，不管这东西是什么，它都不是杜隆塔尔的原生物种。",cEN="Thank you for finding Beaky. He has already returned to me, healthy as ever.\n\nI've already sent him on yet another scouting mission.\n\n... you're saying a strange creature was seen near Beaky and that it attacked you? That must have been the creature that injured my boy.\n\nI'll have to look into this more. Based on your description, whatever this is, it's not native to Durotar."}
Q[200011]={d="当一名游侠，不只是抄起一把弓，或躲在树荫里作战，<name>。\n\n当一名游侠，本质上意味着你与荒野有着深厚的联结。你是它的守护者。\n\n我派我的猎鹰费洛去周边侦察，可它一直没回来。\n\n请你找到它，让它回到我身边。",dEN="Being a Ranger is more than just picking up a bow, or fighting from the cover of the trees, <name>.\n\nBeing a Ranger, at its core, means that you have a profound connection to the wilds. You are its protector.\n\nI sent my falcon, Felo, to scout the surrounding areas, but he has not returned.\n\nPlease, find him and direct him to return back to me.",o="在附近一带寻找克拉丽丝的猎鹰。",oEN="Find Clarisse's falcon in the surrounding area.",c="看来这就是那只猎鹰，而且它似乎受了伤。",cEN="This seems to be the falcon in question, and it seems injured."}
Q[200012]={d="附近的灌木丛里有什么在动。\n\n你正遭到攻击！",dEN="Something is rustling in the nearby bushes.\n\nYou're under attack!",o="杀死那只可疑的生物。",oEN="Slay the suspicious creature.",c="猎鹰看起来很不安。一定是那只可疑的生物袭击了它！",cEN="The falcon seems distraught. It must have been the suspicious creature who attacked it!"}
Q[200013]={d="你发现猎鹰身上附着一张字条，上面写着：\n\n<如果你正在读这段话，说明你找到了我的朋友。这张字条旁还有一小瓶红色药水。若它受了伤就喂给它，它自会知道接下来该怎么做。>",dEN="You find a note attached to the falcon that reads:\n\n<If you are reading this, you have found my friend. Attached to this note is a small red vial. Give it to him if he is injured, and he will know what to do next.>",o="对猎鹰使用红色药水。",oEN="Use the Red Vial on the falcon.",p="你今天找到费洛，可是立了大功。谢谢你。",pEN="You have done a great deed today by finding Felo. Thank you.",c="谢谢你找到费洛。它已经回到我身边了，跟往常一样健康。\n\n我又派它去执行另一次侦察任务了。\n\n……你是说，有人在费洛附近看到一只奇怪的生物，还袭击了你？那一定就是伤了我家孩子的东西。\n\n我得好好查一查这件事。照你的描述，不管这东西是什么，它都不是提瑞斯法林地的原生物种。",cEN="Thank you for finding Felo. He has already returned to me, healthy as ever.\n\nI've already sent him on yet another scouting mission.\n\n... you're saying a strange creature was seen near Felo and that it attacked you? That must have been the creature that injured my boy.\n\nI'll have to look into this more. Based on your description, whatever this is, it's not native to Tirisfal Glades."}
Q[200014]={d="当一名游侠，不只是抄起一把弓，或躲在树荫里作战，<name>。\n\n当一名游侠，本质上意味着你与荒野有着深厚的联结。你是它的守护者。\n\n我派我的猎鹰基德去周边侦察，可它一直没回来。\n\n请你找到它，让它回到我身边。",dEN="Being a Ranger is more than just picking up a bow, or fighting from the cover of the trees, <name>.\n\nBeing a Ranger, at its core, means that you have a profound connection to the wilds. You are its protector.\n\nI sent my falcon, Keed, to scout the surrounding areas, but he has not returned.\n\nPlease, find him and direct him to return back to me.",o="在红云台地寻找纳瓦特的猎鹰。",oEN="Find Nawat's falcon in Red Cloud Mesa.",c="看来这就是那只猎鹰，而且它似乎受了伤。",cEN="This seems to be the falcon in question, and it seems injured."}
Q[200015]={d="附近的灌木丛里有什么在动。\n\n你正遭到攻击！",dEN="Something is rustling in the nearby bushes.\n\nYou're under attack!",o="杀死那只可疑的生物。",oEN="Slay the suspicious creature.",c="猎鹰看起来很不安。一定是那只可疑的生物袭击了它！",cEN="The falcon seems distraught. It must have been the suspicious creature who attacked it!"}
Q[200016]={d="你发现猎鹰身上附着一张字条，上面写着：\n\n<如果你正在读这段话，说明你找到了我的朋友。这张字条旁还有一小瓶红色药水。若它受了伤就喂给它，它自会知道接下来该怎么做。>",dEN="You find a note attached to the falcon that reads:\n\n<If you are reading this, you have found my friend. Attached to this note is a small red vial. Give it to him if he is injured, and he will know what to do next.>",o="对猎鹰使用红色药水。",oEN="Use the Red Vial on the falcon.",p="你没有辜负我，也没有辜负基德。谢谢你，<name>。",pEN="You have not failed me, nor have you failed Keed. Thank you, <name>.",c="谢谢你找到基德。它已经回到我身边了，跟往常一样健康。\n\n我又派它去执行另一次侦察任务了。\n\n……你是说，有人在基德附近看到一只奇怪的生物，还袭击了你？那一定就是伤了我家孩子的东西。\n\n我得好好查一查这件事。照你的描述，不管这东西是什么，它都不是莫高雷的原生物种。",cEN="Thank you for finding Keed. He has already returned to me, healthy as ever.\n\nI've already sent him on yet another scouting mission.\n\n... you're saying a strange creature was seen near Keed and that it attacked you? That must have been the creature that injured my boy.\n\nI'll have to look into this more. Based on your description, whatever this is, it's not native to Mulgore."}
Q[200017]={d="啊，<class>。你的日子终于到了。\n\n血。到了这个地步，你总该以某种方式对它相当熟悉了。血即生命。但血，你很快就会明白，也是力量。\n\n我要你想象一下，在一个你能操控他人身体生命精髓的世界里，你能做到什么。只需手腕一抖，就碾碎他们的五脏六腑……\n\n令人陶醉。\n\n时机到了，你会学到更多。眼下，我需要你帮我继续自己的研究，而借此我也能帮你学习。\n\n这附近有一部巨著，当地的匪徒已经得知了它的下落，而我正需要它来做研究。他们中的一个人拿着我的书：一个血法师。替我取回来，我敢肯定他们中有人随身带着。",dEN="Ahh, <class>. Your day has finally come.\n\nBlood. Something you should be well acquainted with at this point, in some way or another. Blood is life. But blood, as you will soon learn, is also power.\n\nI want you to imagine what you can be capable of in a world in which you can control the very life essence of another beings body. To simply crush their insides with the flick of a wrist...\n\nIntoxicating.\n\nIn due time, you will learn more. For now, I require your assistance in pursuing my own studies and through this I will also be able to help you learn.\n\nNearby is a tome, that of which the local bandits have become privy too, and one of which I require for my studies. One of them has my tome - a Blood Wizard. Collect it for me, I'm sure one of them has it on them.",o="从迪菲亚血法师手中取回血之书。",oEN="Collect the Tome of Blood from the Defias Blood Wizard.",p="了不起。你刚才说这书在谁手里？",pEN="Impressive. Who did you say had this tome again?",c="一个迪菲亚血法师？\n\n有意思……\n\n不过，仔细检查之后，这本书一文不值。你留着吧。\n\n等你更强了，日后再回来找我。也许我们还能再合作。",cEN="A Defias Blood Wizard?\n\nInteresting...\n\nWell, upon further inspection, this tome is worthless. You can have it.\n\nReturn to me in the future when you are stronger. Maybe we can work together again."}
Q[200018]={d="啊，<class>。你的日子终于到了。\n\n血。到了这个地步，你总该以某种方式对它相当熟悉了。血即生命。但血，你很快就会明白，也是力量。\n\n我要你想象一下，在一个你能操控他人身体生命精髓的世界里，你能做到什么。只需手腕一抖，就碾碎他们的五脏六腑……\n\n令人陶醉。\n\n时机到了，你会学到更多。眼下，我需要你帮我开展自己的研究，而借此我也能帮你学习。\n\n这附近有一部巨著，在格雷尔营地一个可疑的暗夜精灵手里，我正需要它来做研究。替我取回来。",dEN="Ahh, <class>. Your day has finally come.\n\nBlood. Something you should be well acquainted with at this point, in some way or another. Blood is life. But blood, as you will soon learn, is also power.\n\nI want you to imagine what you can be capable of in a world in which you can control the very life essence of another beings body. To simply crush their insides with the flick of a wrist...\n\nIntoxicating.\n\nIn due time, you will learn more. For now, I require your assistance in pursuing my own studies and through this I will also be able to help you learn.\n\nNearby is a tome held by a suspicious Night Elf in the Grell camps, and one of which I require for my studies. Collect it for me.",o="从可疑的暗夜精灵手中取回血之书。",oEN="Collect the Tome of Blood from the suspicious Night Elf.",p="了不起。你刚才说这书在谁手里？",pEN="Impressive. Who did you say had this tome again?",c="一个血法师？\n\n有意思……\n\n不过，仔细检查之后，这本书一文不值。你留着吧。\n\n等你更强了，日后再回来找我。也许我们还能再合作。",cEN="A Blood Wizard?\n\nInteresting...\n\nWell, upon further inspection, this tome is worthless. You can have it.\n\nReturn to me in the future when you are stronger. Maybe we can work together again."}
Q[200019]={d="啊，<class>。你的日子终于到了。\n\n血。到了这个地步，你总该以某种方式对它相当熟悉了。血即生命。但血，你很快就会明白，也是力量。\n\n我要你想象一下，在一个你能操控他人身体生命精髓的世界里，你能做到什么。只需手腕一抖，就碾碎他们的五脏六腑……\n\n令人陶醉。\n\n时机到了，你会学到更多。眼下，我需要你帮我开展自己的研究，而借此我也能帮你学习。\n\n这附近有一部巨著，在一个翻找附近废弃房屋的可疑血精灵手里，我正需要它来做研究。替我取回来。",dEN="Ahh, <class>. Your day has finally come.\n\nBlood. Something you should be well acquainted with at this point, in some way or another. Blood is life. But blood, as you will soon learn, is also power.\n\nI want you to imagine what you can be capable of in a world in which you can control the very life essence of another beings body. To simply crush their insides with the flick of a wrist...\n\nIntoxicating.\n\nIn due time, you will learn more. For now, I require your assistance in pursuing my own studies and through this I will also be able to help you learn.\n\nNearby is a tome, that of which is possessed by a suspicious Blood Elf rummaging in the abandoned houses nearby, and one of which I require for my studies. Collect it for me.",o="从可疑的血精灵手中取回血之书。",oEN="Collect the Tome of Blood from the suspicious Blood Elf.",p="了不起。你刚才说这书在谁手里？",pEN="Impressive. Who did you say had this tome again?",c="一个血法师？\n\n有意思……\n\n不过，仔细检查之后，这本书一文不值。你留着吧。\n\n等你更强了，日后再回来找我。也许我们还能再合作。",cEN="A Blood Wizard?\n\nInteresting...\n\nWell, upon further inspection, this tome is worthless. You can have it.\n\nReturn to me in the future when you are stronger. Maybe we can work together again."}
Q[200020]={d="啊，<class>。你的日子终于到了。\n\n血。到了这个地步，你总该以某种方式对它相当熟悉了。血即生命。但血，你很快就会明白，也是力量。\n\n我要你想象一下，在一个你能操控他人身体生命精髓的世界里，你能做到什么。只需手腕一抖，就碾碎他们的五脏六腑……\n\n令人陶醉。\n\n时机到了，你会学到更多。眼下，我需要你帮我开展自己的研究，而借此我也能帮你学习。\n\n这附近有一部巨著，就在小恶魔游荡的那个洞穴里，在一个古怪的巨魔手里，我正需要它来做研究。替我取回来，我敢肯定他们中有人随身带着。",dEN="Ahh, <class>. Your day has finally come.\n\nBlood. Something you should be well acquainted with at this point, in some way or another. Blood is life. But blood, as you will soon learn, is also power.\n\nI want you to imagine what you can be capable of in a world in which you can control the very life essence of another beings body. To simply crush their insides with the flick of a wrist...\n\nIntoxicating.\n\nIn due time, you will learn more. For now, I require your assistance in pursuing my own studies and through this I will also be able to help you learn.\n\nNearby is a tome, in da cave where the imps roam, held by an odd Troll, and one of which I require for my studies. Collect it for me, I'm sure one of them has it on them.",o="从神秘的巨魔手中取回血之书。",oEN="Collect the Tome of Blood from the mysterious Troll.",p="你干得不错，伙计。你刚才说这书在谁手里？",pEN="You be doin' good, mon. Who did you say had this tome again?",c="一个血法师？\n\n有意思……\n\n不过，仔细检查之后，这本书一文不值。你留着吧。\n\n等你更强了，日后再回来找我。也许我们还能再合作。",cEN="A Blood Wizard?\n\nInteresting...\n\nWell, upon further inspection, this tome is worthless. You can have it.\n\nReturn to me in the future when you are stronger. Maybe we can work together again."}
Q[200021]={d="一切就这样开始了。\n\n你好，<name>。我已经能感觉到，你开始感受到那股在你血脉中燃烧的残余邪能力量。我羡慕你，曾几何时，我也没像现在这样习惯它。\n\n你是恶魔猎手，因此你处在凡人与恶魔之类存在的边界上。不过，与其他人不同，你和我不会落入邪能魔法所提供的力量陷阱——许多其他修行者常常在不知不觉中陷入其中。也许有一天你甚至会强大到能化身为恶魔形态，但眼下，你的邪能强化会让你大放异彩，激发出真正的潜能。\n\n让我把话说清楚：部落和联盟对我们毫无用处，但他们必须相信我们是他们的盟友，我们宏大的目标才可能实现。别忘了这一点。当一切到达紧要关头时，别忘了你真正的效忠对象在哪里。\n\n现在，来个考验。附近放置了一个强大恶魔的头骨，名叫洛'克。去把它找出来给我。",dEN="And so it begins.\n\nGreetings, <name>. I can already tell that you have begun to feel the residual fel power that burns within your veins. I envy you, there was once a time where I was not so used to it as I am now.\n\nYou are Felsworn, and as such, you are at the border of mortality and the likes of demons. However, unlike some, you and I will not fall to the traps of power that fel magic provides, and that so many other practitioners fall too, often unbeknownstly. Perhaps you will even become powerful enough to take on a demonic form someday, but for now, your Fel Empowerment will do you wonders at bringing out your true potential.\n\nLet me make myself clear, the Horde and Alliance are of no use to us, but they must believe we are their allies in order for our greater goals to become achievable. Do not forget this. When it all comes to a head, do not forget where your true allegiance lays.\n\nAnd now, a test. A skull of a powerful demon known as Lo'k has been placed in the surrounding area. Find it for me.",o="取回洛'克的头骨。",oEN="Retrieve the skull of Lo'k.",p="你干得很好，<name>。",pEN="You have done well, <name>.",c="也许你会问，我为什么要你去取回这个头骨。\n\n恶魔头骨往往承载着巨大的邪能力量。今天，我把它交给你。\n\n不过，如果你更愿意，我可以把这个头骨的力量注入一柄强大的剑中。\n\n选择权在你；无论你选什么，它都会为你所用。",cEN="You may be wondering why I had you retrieve this skull.\n\nDemon skulls are often vessels of immense fel power. Today, I give this to you.\n\nHowever, if you prefer, I can infuse the power of this skull into a powerful sword.\n\nThe choice is yours, whatever it may be, it will serve you well."}
Q[200022]={d="一切就这样开始了。\n\n你好，<name>。我已经能感觉到，你开始感受到那股在你血脉中燃烧的残余邪能力量。我羡慕你，曾几何时，我也没像现在这样习惯它。\n\n你是一名恶魔猎手，因此你处在凡人与恶魔之类存在的边界上。不过，与其他人不同，你和我不会落入邪能魔法所提供的力量陷阱——许多其他修行者常常在不知不觉中陷入其中。也许有一天你甚至会强大到能化身为恶魔形态，但眼下，你的邪能强化会让你大放异彩，激发出真正的潜能。\n\n让我把话说清楚：部落和联盟对我们毫无用处，但他们必须相信我们是他们的盟友，我们宏大的目标才可能实现。别忘了这一点。当一切到达紧要关头时，别忘了你真正的效忠对象在哪里。\n\n现在，来个考验。附近放置了一个强大恶魔的头骨，名叫卡兹。去把它找出来给我。",dEN="And so it begins.\n\nGreetings, <name>. I can already tell that you have begun to feel the residual fel power that burns within your veins. I envy you, there was once a time where I was not so used to it as I am now.\n\nYou are Felsworn, and as such, you are at the border of mortality and the likes of demons. However, unlike some, you and I will not fall to the traps of power that fel magic provides, and that so many other practitioners fall too, often unbeknownstly. Perhaps you will even become powerful enough to take on a demonic form someday, but for now, your Fel Empowerment will do you wonders at bringing out your true potential.\n\nLet me make myself clear, the Horde and Alliance are of no use to us, but they must believe we are their allies in order for our greater goals to become achievable. Do not forget this. When it all comes to a head, do not forget where your true allegiance lays.\n\nAnd now, a test. A skull of a powerful demon known as Kaz has been placed in the surrounding area. Find it for me.",o="取回卡兹的头骨。",oEN="Retrieve the skull of Kaz.",p="你干得很好，<name>。",pEN="You have done well, <name>.",c="也许你会问，我为什么要你去取回这个头骨。\n\n恶魔头骨往往承载着巨大的邪能力量。今天，我把它交给你。\n\n不过，如果你更愿意，我可以把这个头骨的力量注入一柄强大的剑中。\n\n选择权在你；无论你选什么，它都会为你所用。",cEN="You may be wondering why I had you retrieve this skull.\n\nDemon skulls are often vessels of immense fel power. Today, I give this to you.\n\nHowever, if you prefer, I can infuse the power of this skull into a powerful sword.\n\nThe choice is yours, whatever it may be, it will serve you well."}
Q[200023]={d="一切就这样开始了。\n\n你好，<name>。我已经能感觉到，你开始感受到那股在你血脉中燃烧的残余邪能力量。我羡慕你，曾几何时，我也没像现在这样习惯它。\n\n你是一名恶魔猎手，因此你处在凡人与恶魔之类存在的边界上。不过，与其他人不同，你和我不会落入邪能魔法所提供的力量陷阱——许多其他修行者常常在不知不觉中陷入其中。也许有一天你甚至会强大到能化身为恶魔形态，但眼下，你的邪能强化会让你大放异彩，激发出真正的潜能。\n\n让我把话说清楚：部落和联盟对我们毫无用处，但他们必须相信我们是他们的盟友，我们宏大的目标才可能实现。别忘了这一点。当一切到达紧要关头时，别忘了你真正的效忠对象在哪里。\n\n现在，来个考验。附近放置了一个强大恶魔的头骨，名叫帕克斯。去把它找出来给我。",dEN="And so it begins.\n\nGreetings, <name>. I can already tell that you have begun to feel the residual fel power that burns within your veins. I envy you, there was once a time where I was not so used to it as I am now.\n\nYou are Felsworn, and as such, you are at the border of mortality and the likes of demons. However, unlike some, you and I will not fall to the traps of power that fel magic provides, and that so many other practitioners fall too, often unbeknownstly. Perhaps you will even become powerful enough to take on a demonic form someday, but for now, your Fel Empowerment will do you wonders at bringing out your true potential.\n\nLet me make myself clear, the Horde and Alliance are of no use to us, but they must believe we are their allies in order for our greater goals to become achievable. Do not forget this. When it all comes to a head, do not forget where your true allegiance lays.\n\nAnd now, a test. A skull of a powerful demon known as Pax has been placed in the surrounding area. Find it for me.",o="取回帕克斯的头骨。",oEN="Retrieve the skull of Pax.",p="找得好。",pEN="Good find.",c="也许你会问，我为什么要你去取回这个头骨。\n\n恶魔头骨往往承载着巨大的邪能力量。今天，我把它交给你。\n\n不过，如果你更愿意，我可以把这个头骨的力量注入一柄强大的剑中。\n\n选择权在你；无论你选什么，它都会为你所用。",cEN="You may be wondering why I had you retrieve this skull.\n\nDemon skulls are often vessels of immense fel power. Today, I give this to you.\n\nHowever, if you prefer, I can infuse the power of this skull into a powerful sword.\n\nThe choice is yours, whatever it may be, it will serve you well."}
Q[200024]={d="欢迎，<class>。你是来下毒的，可以这么说吧？\n\n我一直乐于教导新晋和有志的用毒大师，但作为回报，我有时需要你帮个忙。这没问题吧？\n\n看看你四周。这里有形形色色的市民。但他们是纯净的，这很好，未受污染。我这儿有一瓶我调制的药剂。它的作用不该由你来操心。\n\n我需要你把它泼洒在特定的三个人身上：第一，阳语者塔蕾西亚；第二，贝利·恐恨；第三，多纳尔·瘟织者。\n\n办完这些就回来找我，我会让你的时间花得值。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. Have you come to poison the well, so to speak?\n\nI am always willing to teach new and aspiring masters of the venomous arts, but in return, I sometimes require a favor. This is fine, yes?\n\nLook around you. There are citizens of every shade. But they are pure, which is good, they are untainted. Here I have a concoction that I have made. What it does, should not be of concern to you.\n\nWhat I need is for you to splash it on three people in particular; first, Sunspeaker Talethia, second, Bailey Horrorhate, and third, Dornall Plagueweaver.\n\nReturn to me when you have done this and I will make it worth your time.",o="把神秘药剂泼洒在附近的市民身上。",oEN="Splash the mysterious concoction on nearby citizens.",p="欢迎回来。我交代的事你办了吗？",pEN="Welcome back. Have you done what I asked?",c="我知道你在纳闷我为什么让你做这件事。\n\n时机到了，你自然会知道。\n\n现在没什么可担心的了。我也为你调制了一瓶类似的药剂，带上它，明智地使用。\n\n再会，<name>。",cEN="I know you're wondering why I had you do this.\n\nIn due time, you will learn.\n\nThere is nothing else to worry about now. I've made you a similar concoction, take it with you, and use it wisely.\n\nFarewell, <name>."}
Q[200025]={d="欢迎，<class>。你是来下毒的，可以这么说吧？\n\n我一直乐于教导新晋和有志的用毒大师，但作为回报，我有时需要你帮个忙。这没问题吧？\n\n看看你四周。这里有形形色色的市民。但他们是纯净的，这很好，未受污染。我这儿有一瓶我调制的药剂。它的作用不该由你来操心。\n\n我需要你把它泼洒在特定的三个人身上：第一，流亡者泰露萨拉；第二，黑暗屠戮者哈伦多尔；第三，奥金尼的巴雷拉姆。\n\n办完这些就回来找我，我会让你的时间花得值。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. Have you come to poison the well, so to speak?\n\nI am always willing to teach new and aspiring masters of the venomous arts, but in return, I sometimes require a favor. This is fine, yes?\n\nLook around you. There are citizens of every shade. But they are pure, which is good, they are untainted. Here I have a concoction that I have made. What it does, should not be of concern to you.\n\nWhat I need is for you to splash it on three people in particular; first, Exodite Telusaara, second, Darkslayer Harrendor, and third, Baarelam of the Auchenai.\n\nReturn to me when you have done this and I will make it worth your time.",o="把神秘药剂泼洒在附近的市民身上。",oEN="Splash the mysterious concoction on nearby citizens.",p="欢迎回来。我交代的事你办了吗？",pEN="Welcome back. Have you done what I asked?",c="我知道你在纳闷我为什么让你做这件事。\n\n时机到了，你自然会知道。\n\n现在没什么可担心的了。我也为你调制了一瓶类似的药剂，带上它，明智地使用。\n\n再会，<name>。",cEN="I know you're wondering why I had you do this.\n\nIn due time, you will learn.\n\nThere is nothing else to worry about now. I've made you a similar concoction, take it with you, and use it wisely.\n\nFarewell, <name>."}
Q[200026]={d="欢迎，<class>。你是来下毒的，可以这么说吧？\n\n我一直乐于教导新晋和有志的用毒大师，但作为回报，我有时需要你帮个忙。这样没问题吧？\n\n看看你四周。这里有形形色色的市民。但他们是纯净的，这很好，未受污染。我这儿有一瓶我调制的药剂。它的作用不该由你来操心。\n\n我需要你把它泼洒在特定的三个人身上；第一，潘加乔·窥日者；第二，奥莫古尔格·真言者；第三，涅凯·复生者。\n\n办完这些就回来找我，我会让你的时间花得值。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. Have you come to poison da well, so to speak?\n\nI am always willing to teach new and aspiring masters of the venomous arts, but in return, I sometimes require a favor. Dis fine, yes?\n\nLook around you. There are citizens of every shade. But they are pure, which is good, they are untainted. Here I have a concoction that I have made. What it does, should not be of concern to you.\n\nWhat I need is for you to splash it on three people in particular; first, Pangajo Sunseer, second, Omogulg the Truthbearerr, and third, Nekai the Reanimator.\n\nReturn to me when you have done this and I will make it worth your time.",o="把神秘药剂泼洒在附近的市民身上。",oEN="Splash the mysterious concoction on nearby citizens.",p="欢迎回来。我交代的事你办了吗？",pEN="Welcome back. Have you done what I asked?",c="我知道你在纳闷我为什么让你做这件事。\n\n时机到了，你自然会知道。\n\n现在没什么可担心的了。我也为你调制了一瓶类似的药剂，带上它，明智地使用。\n\n再会，<name>。",cEN="I know you're wondering why I had you do this.\n\nIn due time, you will learn.\n\nThere is nothing else to worry about now. I've made you a similar concoction, take it with you, and use it wisely.\n\nFarewell, <name>."}
Q[200027]={d="欢迎，<class>。看来你已经很熟悉瑟拉图斯的力量了。\n\n让我来指引你，朋友。我有个任务，而且是紧要的任务。据我们的斥候说，我有个朋友在矿坑里受了伤。我刚收到消息，本已打算动身，但我觉得这任务正适合你这样的人去做。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. I can see you've already become well acquainted with the powers of Sseratus.\n\nLet me guide you, friend. I have a task, a critical one at that. I have a friend down in the mines who is injured, according to our scouts. I only just got word of it and would have been on my way, but I believe this is a task that would be perfect for one such as yourself.\n\nFind my friend, heal him with the power of your Loa's Brew, and then return to me.",o="用 1 级罗阿药剂治疗你导师受伤的朋友。",oEN="Heal the injured friend of your trainer with rank 1 Loa's Brew.",c="哦，谢谢，谢谢你！我现在感觉好多了。",cEN="Oh, thank you, thank you! I feel better now."}
Q[200028]={d="太感谢你了，朋友！有些狗头人不好，他们因为小瓦祖就是他自己而伤害他。\n\n让我说清楚：狗头人只想挖洞。我们敲石头，做蜡烛，探索世界。我和我的同胞都不明白为什么有人恨我们。我们不想惹人厌。对不起。\n\n我感谢那些没有伤害我的好朋友……替我谢谢你的朋友照顾我，也谢谢你帮忙！\n\n哦……不，等等。看你身后！他回来了！！！",dEN="Thank you so much friend! Some Kobold not nice, they hurt Lil Wa'zoo for bein' himself.\n\nLet me make clear: Kobold just want dig. We hit rock, make candle, explore world. My brethren, we no get why some hate us. We no mean to be nuisance. Am sorry.\n\nI thank my good friends who no hurt me... Thank your friend for me for looking out for me, and thank you for help too!\n\nOh...no, wait. Look behind you! He back!!!",o="杀死欺负小瓦祖的那个狗头人！",oEN="Kill the Kobold who bullied Lil Wa'zoo!",c="什么？你没想到我会是狗头人的朋友？\n\n小瓦祖已经向我汇报了，还讲了你的事迹。现在他回到矿坑里，替我们打探消息。哈哈哈！\n\n他让我把这个给你。",cEN="What? You didn't expect me to be friends with a Kobold?\n\nLil Wa'zoo has already reported back to me and told me of your deeds. He is now back in the mines, spying for us. Hahaha!\n\nHe told me to give you this."}
Q[200029]={d="Zug zug，<class>。看来你已经很熟悉瑟拉图斯的力量了。\n\n让我来指引你，伙计。我有个任务，而且是紧要的任务。据我们的斥候说，我有个朋友在沙漠里被蝎子所伤。我刚收到消息，本已打算动身，但我觉得这任务正适合你这样的人去做。\n\n他是个强壮的巨魔。巨魔中的巨魔。老实说，不少人都被那些该死的蝎子弄伤了。但不管怎样，保持勤勉。\n\n找到我的朋友，用你的罗阿药剂治好他，然后回来找我。",dEN="Zug zug, <class>. I can see you've already become well acquainted with the powers of Sseratus.\n\nLet me guide you, mon. I have a task, a critical one at that. I have a friend out in da desert who, according to our scouts, has been injured by the scorpids. I only just got word of it and would have been on my way, but I believe this is a task that would be perfect for one such as yourself.\n\nHe's a strong troll. A troll's troll. And in all honesty, many be gettin' injured by those damn scorpids. But regardless, stay diligent.\n\nFind my friend, heal him with the power of your Loa's Brew, and then return to me.",o="用 1 级罗阿药剂治疗你导师受伤的朋友。",oEN="Heal the injured friend of your trainer with rank 1 Loa's Brew.",c="谢谢！我现在感觉好多了。我能感应到罗阿。",cEN="Thank you! I feel better now. I can feel da Loa."}
Q[200030]={d="我的同胞们正在这儿设法应付蝎子的麻烦。这比看上去更危险。\n\n我不是第一个受伤的。我只能向罗阿祈祷自己没中毒。但我确实受了伤。谢谢你治好我，伙计。\n\n哦，不！看你身后，伙计！有一只蝎子正回来想补上最后一击！",dEN="My brethren be out here tryin' to deal wit da scorpid situation. It be more dangerous than it look.\n\nI am not da first one to be injured. I can only pray to da Loa that I was not poisoned. But I did get hurt. Thank you for healing me, mon.\n\nOh, no! Look behind you, mon! One of da scorpids be comin' back to finish da job!",o="消灭蝎子潜伏者。",oEN="Slay the Scorpid Stalker.",c="希比已经告诉我你做了什么。\n\n我为你骄傲，伙计。\n\n拿着这个。",cEN="Hi'bi told me what you did.\n\nI'm proud of you, mon.\n\nTake this."}
Q[200031]={d="Ishnu-alah，<name>。我看得出艾露恩没有忘记你，很好，我正需要一位如此蒙福之人。\n\n身为唤星者，我们是艾露恩的勇士，因此必须践行她的意志——无论它把我们带往何方，无论那是什么。\n\n但当大地沐浴在和平之中时，人必须学会依然向艾露恩致敬，这样当大地再度充满战争与绝望时，她才会在那里指引我们。\n\n前往附近的月井朝圣，步入它那神奇的水中，冥想并向女神致敬，然后回来找我。",dEN="Ishnu-alah, <name>. I see Elune has not forgotten you, good, I could use one so blessed.\n\nAs Starcallers, we are champions of Elune, and as such, we must carry out her will - wherever it takes us, and whatever it must be.\n\nBut, when the land is embroiled with peace, one must learn to still pay respects to Elune, so that she will be there to guide us when the land is yet again filled with war and despair.\n\nMake a pilgrimage to the nearby Moonwell, step inside its magical waters, meditate, and pay respects to the goddess, then return to me.",o="前往附近的月井赞美艾露恩。",oEN="Head to the nearby Moonwell to praise Elune.",c="艾露恩的恩泽自你身上散发，<name>。女神很满意。\n\n我有两件受艾露恩祝福的武器供你选择。\n\n以艾露恩选民的身份出发吧。我们后会有期。",cEN="Elune's grace radiates from you, <name>. The goddess is pleased.\n\nI have two weapons for you to choose from, blessed by Elune.\n\nGo forth as Elune's Chosen. We will meet again."}
Q[200032]={d="Kodo'ish，<name>。我看得出姆莎没有忘记你，很好，我正需要一位如此蒙福之人。\n\n身为唤星者，我们是姆莎的勇士，因此必须践行她的意志——无论它把我们带往何方，无论那是什么。\n\n但当大地沐浴在和平之中时，人必须学会依然向姆莎致敬，这样当大地再度充满战争与绝望时，她才会在那里指引我们。\n\n前往山中的姆莎神龛朝圣，冥想并向女神致敬，然后回来找我。",dEN="Kodo'ish, <name>. I see Mu'sha has not forgotten you, good, I could use one so blessed.\n\nAs Starcallers, we are champions of Mu'sha, and as such, we must carry out her will - wherever it takes us, and whatever it must be.\n\nBut, when the land is embroiled with peace, one must learn to still pay respects to Mu'sha, so that she will be there to guide us when the land is yet again filled with war and despair.\n\nMake a pilgrimage to the shrine to Mu'sha in the mountains, meditate, and pay respects to the goddess, then return to me.",o="前往古老的姆莎神龛赞美姆莎。",oEN="Head to the ancient shrine to Mu'sha to praise Mu'sha.",c="姆莎的恩泽自你身上散发，<name>。月神很满意。\n\n我有两件受姆莎祝福的武器供你选择。\n\n以姆莎选民的身份出发吧。我们后会有期。",cEN="Mu'sha's grace radiates from you, <name>. The moon is pleased.\n\nI have two weapons for you to choose from, blessed by Mu'sha.\n\nGo forth as Mu'sha's Chosen. We will meet again."}
Q[200033]={d="Bal'a dash，malanore，<name>。我看得出艾露恩没有忘记你，很好，我正需要一位如此蒙福之人。\n\n身为唤星者，我们是艾露恩的勇士，因此必须践行她的意志——无论它把我们带往何方，无论那是什么。\n\n但当大地沐浴在和平之中时，人必须学会依然向艾露恩致敬，这样当大地再度充满战争与绝望时，她才会在那里指引我们。\n\n北面的山中有一座古老的雕像，纪念当年泰兰德亲自率军登陆东部王国——那是对天灾本身的一次直接进攻，也帮助了我的族人。\n\n自雕像立起之日起，它便倒塌了，也被人遗忘。然而，它仍是艾露恩追随者的朝圣之地。去那里，冥想并向女神致敬，然后回来找我。",dEN="Bal'a dash, malanore, <name>. I see Elune has not forgotten you, good, I could use one so blessed.\n\nAs Starcallers, we are champions of Elune, and as such, we must carry out her will - wherever it takes us, and whatever it must be.\n\nBut, when the land is embroiled with peace, one must learn to still pay respects to Elune, so that she will be there to guide us when the land is yet again filled with war and despair.\n\nIn the mountains to the north is a old statue dedicated to the time when Tyrande herself landed her forces upon the Eastern Kingdoms - a direct assault against the scourge itself, and aided my people.\n\nSince the time that the statue was erected, it has fallen, and been forgotten. Yet it remains as a pilgrimage site for followers of Elune. Go there, meditate, and pay respects to the goddess, then return to me.",o="找到倒塌的雕像，赞美艾露恩。",oEN="Find the toppled statue and praise Elune.",c="艾露恩的恩泽自你身上散发，<name>。女神很满意。\n\n我有两件受艾露恩祝福的武器供你选择。\n\n以艾露恩选民的身份出发吧。我们后会有期。",cEN="Elune's grace radiates from you, <name>. The goddess is pleased.\n\nI have two weapons for you to choose from, blessed by Elune.\n\nGo forth as Elune's Chosen. We will meet again."}
Q[200034]={d="啊哈，<name>，欢迎，你喜欢你这副凡人的模样吗？时候到了，我们要一步步把地狱释放到艾泽拉斯之上。\n\n你很清楚，我们人不多，但我们的数量会随时间增长。我想不必提醒你，部落的处境不是你首要关心的。他们不过是工具，是一面盾牌，好让我们推进自己的目标。\n\n每一步、每一刻，我们都必须在这个世界上制造混乱，但我们绝不能泄露自己的秘密：我们是恶魔；因此，我有件小任务交给你。\n\n有个苦工，懒到难以想象，无论你怎么使劲都别想让他干活。\n\n我的上级派我来处理他。我们可以给他加薪，可以用棍子打到他听话，甚至可以直接劝他干活。但是……\n\n杀了他，我们会给他的死编个借口。大概就说遭了蝎子袭击。",dEN="Aha, <name>, welcome, do you like your mortal visage? The time has come for us to unleash hell upon Azeroth, one step at a time.\n\nAs you well know, there are only so many of us, but our numbers will grow with time. I need not remind you, I assume, that the plight of the Horde is not your primary concern. They are but a tool, a shield, so that we may further our own goals.\n\nAt every step, at every moment, we must wreck havoc on this world, yet we must not give up our secret - that we are demons - and as such, I have a little task for you.\n\nThere is a peon, one of which is so unfathomably lazy that he could not be made to do work no matter how hard you tried.\n\nI have been tasked by my superiors here to deal with him. We could give him a pay raise, we could beat him with a stick until he listens, we could even try to simply convince him to work. But...\n\nKill him, we'll make up an excuse for how he died. Scorpid attack, probably.",o="杀死那个懒得难以想象的苦工。",oEN="Kill the unfathomably lazy peon.",c="好，好。你也许注意到，有些人会试着劝说苦工去干活。有些人甚至可能动用武力，但从不下死手。\n\n这些都不是我们的选项，<class>。他该死，还有更多人同样该死。\n\n作为你血腥成功的凭证，我赠你一件强大的装备，以地狱之火锻造。Lok'tar ogar，差不多是这意思。啊哈！",cEN="Good, good. You may be noticing that some would attempt to convince a peon to simply work. Some may even use force, but never lethal.\n\nThese are not options for us, <class>. He deserved death, and there will be many more who do as well.\n\nAs a token of your bloody success, I present to you a powerful piece of equipment, forged in helfire. Lok'tar ogar, or something. Aha!"}
Q[200035]={d="啊哈，<name>，欢迎，你喜欢你这副凡人的模样吗？时候到了，我们要一步步把地狱释放到艾泽拉斯之上。\n\n你很清楚，我们人不多，但我们的数量会随时间增长。我想不必提醒你，部落的处境不是你首要关心的。他们不过是工具，是一面盾牌，好让我们推进自己的目标。\n\n每一步、每一刻，我们都必须在这个世界上制造混乱，但我们绝不能泄露自己的秘密：我们是恶魔；因此，我有件小任务交给你。\n\n有个人一直在丧钟镇惹是生非。他醒来之后就疯了似的四处制造混乱。\n\n我的上级派我来处理他。通常我会跟这种人交朋友，但我们必须做出一副站在他们那边的样子。\n\n杀了他，我们会给他的死编个借口。",dEN="Aha, <name>, welcome, do you like your mortal visage? The time has come for us to unleash hell upon Azeroth, one step at a time.\n\nAs you well know, there are only so many of us, but our numbers will grow with time. I need not remind you, I assume, that the plight of the Horde is not your primary concern. They are but a tool, a shield, so that we may further our own goals.\n\nAt every step, at every moment, we must wreck havoc on this world, yet we must not give up our secret - that we are demons - and as such, I have a little task for you.\n\nThere is an individual who has been causing trouble in Deathknell. When he awoke, he simply ran amok causing havoc.\n\nI have been tasked by my superiors here to deal with him. Normally, I'd be friends with someone like this, but we must give the illusion that we are on their side.\n\nKill him, we'll make up an excuse for how he died.",o="杀死发狂的亡灵。",oEN="Kill the crazed Undead.",c="好，好。他已经被处理掉了。\n\n他该死，还有更多人同样该死。\n\n作为你血腥成功的凭证，我赠你一件强大的装备，以地狱之火锻造。Lok'tar ogar，差不多是这意思。啊哈！",cEN="Good, good. He is dealt with.\n\nHe deserved death, and there will be many more who do as well.\n\nAs a token of your bloody success, I present to you a powerful piece of equipment, forged in helfire. Lok'tar ogar, or something. Aha!"}
Q[200036]={d="啊哈，<name>，欢迎，你喜欢你这副凡人的模样吗？时候到了，我们要一步步把地狱释放到艾泽拉斯之上。\n\n你很清楚，我们人不多，但我们的数量会随时间增长。我想不必提醒你，联盟的处境不是你首要关心的。他们不过是工具，是一面盾牌，好让我们推进自己的目标。\n\n每一步、每一刻，我们都必须在这个世界上制造混乱，但我们绝不能泄露自己的秘密：我们是恶魔；因此，我有件小任务交给你。\n\n有个萨特本不该出现在这里。他正在给影谷当地的居民惹麻烦。\n\n我的上级派我来处理他。\n\n杀了他，萨特在这儿可不受待见。",dEN="Aha, <name>, welcome, do you like your mortal visage? The time has come for us to unleash hell upon Azeroth, one step at a time.\n\nAs you well know, there are only so many of us, but our numbers will grow with time. I need not remind you, I assume, that the plight of the Alliance is not your primary concern. They are but a tool, a shield, so that we may further our own goals.\n\nAt every step, at every moment, we must wreck havoc on this world, yet we must not give up our secret - that we are demons - and as such, I have a little task for you.\n\nThere is a satyr who should not be here. He is causing trouble for the local residents of Shadowglen.\n\nI have been tasked by my superiors here to deal with him.\n\nKill him, Satyrs are not seen kindly here.",o="杀死影谷的欺诈者萨特。",oEN="Kill the Satyr Trickster in Shadowglen.",c="好，好。那萨特死了。\n\n他该死，还有更多人同样该死。\n\n作为你血腥成功的凭证，我赠你一件强大的装备，以地狱之火锻造。Dioniss aca，差不多是这意思。啊哈！",cEN="Good, good. The Satyr is dead.\n\nHe deserved death, and there will be many more who do as well.\n\nAs a token of your bloody success, I present to you a powerful piece of equipment, forged in hellfire. Dioniss aca, or something. Aha!"}
Q[200037]={d="再对着我的头盔笑一次，我就把这些刀刃插进你胸口，<name>。\n\n……你很有胆量。我能感觉到，你是来向我求教的。今天确实有件简单的任务交给你，年轻的<class>。\n\n山谷里有个人正走向生命的尽头。巅峰之时，他是战场上的巨兽，夺走过许多性命。可如今，他在山谷自己的家中过着平静的生活。\n\n他会死去，暗影界会收走他的灵魂。但今天还不是他的日子。不过，我能感到他渴望离开这一界，却不清楚自己离去之后将面对什么。\n\n你也许没料到会是这样的任务，但我恳请你去看望他，与他聊聊。",dEN="Smirk one more time when looking at my helmet, and I'll put these blades in your chest, <name>.\n\n...you are bold. I can sense you have come to me to learn. I do have a simple task for you today, young <class>.\n\nIn the valley is a man who is nearing his end. In his prime, he was a behemoth on the battlefield and took many lives. But now, he lives a quaint life in his own home in the valley.\n\nHe will die and the Shadowlands will claim him. But today is not his day. Yet, I can feel his yearning to leave this plane, but he is unaware of what lays before him once he is gone.\n\nYou may not have expected such a task, but I would humbly ask you to pay him a visit and have a chat.",o="去北郡谷拜访老詹金斯。",oEN="Visit Old Man Jenkins in Northshire Valley.",c="你也许没料到会是这样的任务，<name>。但要明白，暗影界会召唤那些已经准备好的人，而知道何时收取灵魂，与收取灵魂本身同样重要。\n\n为了酬谢你帮助我们的朋友，我会奖励你这双靴子。愿它为你所用，它附有魔法，能让你在水面上行走。",cEN="You may not have expected such a task, <name>. But it is important to understand that the Shadowlands call for those who are ready, and knowing when to claim a soul can be just as important as the reclamation of the soul itself.\n\nFor helping our friend out here, I will reward you with these boots. May they serve you well, as they are enchanted to allow you to walk on the surface of water itself."}
Q[200038]={d="欢迎，<class>。关于你来到影谷的事，我听到了很多。我有很多东西要教你。\n\n但你来得正是时候，因为我有件特别的任务交给你。\n\n阿尔德拉斯这里有一位老精灵，正走向生命的尽头。巅峰之时，他是战场上的巨兽，夺走过许多性命。可如今，他在阿尔德拉斯过着平静的生活。\n\n他会死去，暗影界会收走他的灵魂。但今天还不是他的日子。不过，我能感到他渴望离开这一界，却不清楚自己离去之后将面对什么。\n\n你也许没料到会是这样的任务，但我恳请你去看望他，与他聊聊。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. I have heard much about your arrival here in Shadowglen. I have much to teach you.\n\nBut you have come to me at the perfect moment, for I have a special task for you.\n\nHere in Aldrassil is an old elf who is nearing his end. In his prime, he was a behemoth on the battlefield and took many lives. But now, he lives a quaint life in Aldrassil.\n\nHe will die and the Shadowlands will claim him. But today is not his day. Yet, I can feel his yearning to leave this plane, but he is unaware of what lays before him once he is gone.\n\nYou may not have expected such a task, but I would humbly ask you to pay him a visit and have a chat.",o="去阿尔德拉斯拜访萨拉多尔。",oEN="Visit Thalador in Aldrassil.",c="你也许没料到会是这样的任务，<name>。但要明白，暗影界会召唤那些已经准备好的人，而知道何时收取灵魂，与收取灵魂本身同样重要。\n\n为了酬谢你帮助我们的朋友，我会奖励你这双靴子。愿它为你所用，它附有魔法，能让你在水面上行走。",cEN="You may not have expected such a task, <name>. But it is important to understand that the Shadowlands call for those who are ready, and knowing when to claim a soul can be just as important as the reclamation of the soul itself.\n\nFor helping our friend out here, I will reward you with these boots. May they serve you well, as they are enchanted to allow you to walk on the surface of water itself."}
Q[200039]={d="再对着我的头盔笑一次，我就把这把刀刃插进你胸口，<name>。\n\n……你很有胆量。我能感觉到，你是来向我求教的。今天确实有件简单的任务交给你，年轻的<class>。\n\n丧钟镇有个人，可以这么说，本已临近生命的尽头，却被天灾杀死，又再度复活。\n\n这一次，他会死去，暗影界会收走他的灵魂。但今天还不是他的日子。不过，我能感到他渴望离开这一界，却不清楚自己离去之后将面对什么。\n\n你也许没料到会是这样的任务，但我恳请你去看望他，与他聊聊。",dEN="Smirk one more time when looking at my helmet, and I'll put this blade in your chest, <name>.\n\n...you are bold. I can sense you have come to me to learn. I do have a simple task for you today, young <class>.\n\nIn Deathknell is a man, you could say, who was near his end, only to then be killed by the Scourge and risen yet again.\n\nHe will die and the Shadowlands will claim him, this time. But today is not his day. Yet, I can feel his yearning to leave this plane, but he is unaware of what lays before him once he is gone.\n\nYou may not have expected such a task, but I would humbly ask you to pay him a visit and have a chat.",o="去丧钟镇拜访达林·索夫特。",oEN="Visit Dalin Soft in Deathknell.",c="你也许没料到会是这样的任务，<name>。但要明白，暗影界会召唤那些已经准备好的人，而知道何时收取灵魂，与收取灵魂本身同样重要。\n\n为了酬谢你帮助我们的朋友，我会奖励你这双靴子。愿它为你所用，它附有魔法，能让你在水面上行走。",cEN="You may not have expected such a task, <name>. But it is important to understand that the Shadowlands call for those who are ready, and knowing when to claim a soul can be just as important as the reclamation of the soul itself.\n\nFor helping our friend out here, I will reward you with these boots. May they serve you well, as they are enchanted to allow you to walk on the surface of water itself."}
Q[200040]={d="你好，<class>。很高兴你今天能陪我来墓地。\n\n天气真好，是吧？\n\n看来你已经熟悉了不死之身，你复活死者的本事令我印象深刻。\n\n也许你能为我所用，我相信你不会介意。我想召唤一个特别强大的亡灵，但我不敢亲自尝试；我太重要了。\n\n而你不一样，你若在这里成功，能学到不少。要是失败了呢？那我就干脆把你复活成我的仆从。\n\n别想太多。让我把举行仪式的具体位置标在你的地图上。你必须收集特定的物品才能完成仪式。\n\n现在，去吧。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. Glad you could join me in the graveyard today.\n\nBeautiful day, isn't it?\n\nIt seems you've already been acquainted with undeath, I am impressed by your ability to raise the dead.\n\nPerhaps you could be used to my benefit, which I'm sure you would not mind. I have a particularly powerful Undead that I wish to summon, but I dare not attempt it myself - I am far too important.\n\nYou, however, could learn quite a lot by succeeding here. And if you are to fail? I will simply raise you as my own.\n\nDo not overthink it. Let me mark your map to the location of where my ritual must be had. You must collect specific items in order to complete the ritual.\n\nNow, be gone.",o="找到仪式法阵并与其互动。",oEN="Find and interact with the ritual circle.",c="<仪式法阵随着死灵能量搏动>",cEN="<The ritual circle pulsates with necromantic energy>"}
Q[200041]={d="仪式法阵旁的地上有一张字条。要召唤那亡灵怪物，我必须把以下材料带到仪式法阵。\n\n- 骨头\n- 新鲜血肉\n- 头骨\n\n附近的迪菲亚匪徒正好有需要的东西。",dEN="There is a note on the floor by the ritual circle. In order to summon the Undead monstrosity, I must bring the following ingredients to the ritual circle.\n\n- Bones\n- Fresh Flesh\n- Skull\n\nThe nearby Defias bandits have just what is needed.",o="杀死迪菲亚兄弟会匪徒，搜取他们的骨头、血肉和头骨。",oEN="Kill Defias Bandits and loot their bones, flesh, and skull.",p="<你把材料放入仪式法阵>",pEN="<You place the ingredients on the ritual circle>",c="<仪式法阵开始喷涌。怪物正被召唤出来>",cEN="<The ritual circle begins to erupt. The monster is being summoned>"}
Q[200042]={d="<材料在一团烟雾中消散于仪式法阵>\n\n……好像有点不对劲。\n\n召唤失败了，再检查一下仪式法阵。但要小心，它很不稳定。",dEN="<The materials dissipate into the ritual circle into a puff of smoke>\n\n...something seems off.\n\nThe summon has failed, inspect the ritual circle again. But be careful, it is unstable.",o="杀死那只亡灵怪物。",oEN="Kill the Undead Monstrocity.",p="你为什么回来了？",pEN="Why have you returned?",c="嗯，我早就料到会这样。\n\n不过，嘿，你没死。你已经是个更出色的死灵法师了！\n\n拿着，我派其他学徒去收拾了你那场战斗的残骸，他们做了这个。\n\n拿着它，从我眼前消失。",cEN="Well, that's exactly what I thought would happen.\n\nBut, hey, you didn't die. You're a better Necromancer already!\n\nHere, I sent my other apprentices to gather the scraps from your battle, they made this.\n\nTake it and get out of my sight."}
Q[200043]={d="你好，<class>。很高兴你今天能陪我来墓地。\n\n天气真好，是吧？\n\n看来你已经熟悉了不死之身，你复活死者的本事令我印象深刻。\n\n也许你能为我所用，我相信你不会介意。我想召唤一个特别强大的亡灵，但我不敢亲自尝试；我太重要了。\n\n而你不一样，你若在这里成功，能学到不少。要是失败了呢？那我就干脆把你复活成我的仆从。\n\n别想太多。让我把举行仪式的具体位置标在你的地图上。你必须收集特定的物品才能完成仪式。\n\n现在，去吧。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. Glad you could join me in the graveyard today.\n\nBeautiful day, isn't it?\n\nIt seems you've already been acquainted with undeath, I am impressed by your ability to raise the dead.\n\nPerhaps you could be used to my benefit, which I'm sure you would not mind. I have a particularly powerful Undead that I wish to summon, but I dare not attempt it myself - I am far too important.\n\nYou, however, could learn quite a lot by succeeding here. And if you are to fail? I will simply raise you as my own.\n\nDo not overthink it. Let me mark your map to the location of where my ritual must be had. You must collect specific items in order to complete the ritual.\n\nNow, be gone.",o="找到仪式法阵并与其互动。",oEN="Find and interact with the ritual circle.",c="<仪式法阵随着死灵能量搏动>",cEN="<The ritual circle pulsates with necromantic energy>"}
Q[200044]={d="要召唤那亡灵怪物，我必须把以下材料带到仪式法阵。\n\n- 骨头\n- 新鲜血肉\n- 头骨\n\n附近的穴居人正好有需要的东西。",dEN="In order to summon the Undead monstrosity, I must bring the following ingredients to the ritual circle.\n\n- Bones\n- Fresh Flesh\n- Skull\n\nThe nearby Troggs have just what is needed.",o="杀死穴居人，搜取他们的骨头、血肉和头骨。",oEN="Kill Troggs and loot their bones, flesh, and skull.",p="<你把材料放入仪式法阵>",pEN="<You place the ingredients on the ritual circle>",c="<仪式法阵开始喷涌。怪物正被召唤出来>",cEN="<The ritual circle begins to erupt. The monster is being summoned>"}
Q[200045]={d="<材料在一团烟雾中消散于仪式法阵>\n\n……好像有点不对劲。\n\n召唤失败了，再检查一下仪式法阵。但要小心，它很不稳定。",dEN="<The materials dissipate into the ritual circle into a puff of smoke>\n\n...something seems off.\n\nThe summon has failed, inspect the ritual circle again. But be careful, it is unstable.",o="杀死那只亡灵怪物。",oEN="Kill the Undead Monstrocity.",c="嗯，我早就料到会这样。\n\n不过，嘿，你没死。你已经是个更出色的死灵法师了！\n\n拿着，我派其他学徒去收拾了你那场战斗的残骸，他们做了这个。\n\n拿着它，从我眼前消失。",cEN="Well, that's exactly what I thought would happen.\n\nBut, hey, you didn't die. You're a better Necromancer already!\n\nHere, I sent my other apprentices to gather the scraps from your battle, they made this.\n\nTake it and get out of my sight."}
Q[200046]={d="你好，<class>。很高兴你今天能陪我来墓地。\n\n天气真好，是吧？\n\n看来你已经熟悉了不死之身，你复活死者的本事令我印象深刻。\n\n也许你能为我所用，我相信你不会介意。我想召唤一个特别强大的亡灵，但我不敢亲自尝试；我太重要了。\n\n而你不一样，你若在这里成功，能学到不少。要是失败了呢？那我就干脆把你复活成我的仆从。\n\n别想太多。让我把举行仪式的具体位置标在你的地图上。你必须收集特定的物品才能完成仪式。\n\n现在，去吧。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. Glad you could join me in the graveyard today.\n\nBeautiful day, isn't it?\n\nIt seems you've already been acquainted with undeath, I am impressed by your ability to raise the dead.\n\nPerhaps you could be used to my benefit, which I'm sure you would not mind. I have a particularly powerful Undead that I wish to summon, but I dare not attempt it myself - I am far too important.\n\nYou, however, could learn quite a lot by succeeding here. And if you are to fail? I will simply raise you as my own.\n\nDo not overthink it. Let me mark your map to the location of where my ritual must be had. You must collect specific items in order to complete the ritual.\n\nNow, be gone.",o="找到仪式法阵并与其互动。",oEN="Find and interact with the ritual circle.",c="<仪式法阵随着死灵能量搏动>",cEN="<The ritual circle pulsates with necromantic energy>"}
Q[200047]={d="要召唤那亡灵怪物，我必须把以下材料带到仪式法阵。\n\n- 骨头\n- 新鲜血肉\n- 头骨\n\n附近的格雷尔正好有需要的东西。",dEN="In order to summon the Undead monstrosity, I must bring the following ingredients to the ritual circle.\n\n- Bones\n- Fresh Flesh\n- Skull\n\nThe nearby Grells have just what is needed.",o="杀死格雷尔，搜取他们的骨头、血肉和头骨。",oEN="Kill Grells and loot their bones, flesh, and skull.",p="<你把材料放入仪式法阵>",pEN="<You place the ingredients on the ritual circle>",c="<仪式法阵开始喷涌。怪物正被召唤出来>",cEN="<The ritual circle begins to erupt. The monster is being summoned>"}
Q[200048]={d="<材料在一团烟雾中消散于仪式法阵>\n\n……好像有点不对劲。\n\n召唤失败了，再检查一下仪式法阵。但要小心，它很不稳定。",dEN="<The materials dissipate into the ritual circle into a puff of smoke>\n\n...something seems off.\n\nThe summon has failed, inspect the ritual circle again. But be careful, it is unstable.",o="杀死那只亡灵怪物。",oEN="Kill the Undead Monstrocity.",c="嗯，我早就料到会这样。\n\n不过，嘿，你没死。你已经是个更出色的死灵法师了！\n\n拿着，我派其他学徒去收拾了你那场战斗的残骸，他们做了这个。\n\n拿着它，从我眼前消失。",cEN="Well, that's exactly what I thought would happen.\n\nBut, hey, you didn't die. You're a better Necromancer already!\n\nHere, I sent my other apprentices to gather the scraps from your battle, they made this.\n\nTake it and get out of my sight."}
Q[200049]={d="Zug zug，<class>。很高兴你今天能陪我来墓地。\n\n今天天气不错，是吧？\n\n看来你已经熟悉了不死之身，你复活死者的本事令我印象深刻。\n\n也许你能为我所用，我相信你不会介意。我想召唤一个特别强大的亡灵，但我不敢亲自尝试；我太重要了。\n\n而你不一样，你若在这里成功，能学到不少。要是失败了呢？那我就干脆把你复活成我的仆从。\n\n别想太多。让我把举行仪式的具体位置标在你的地图上。你必须收集特定的物品才能完成仪式。\n\n现在，去吧。",dEN="Zug zug, <class>. Glad you could join me in the graveyard today.\n\nWeather is good today, isn't it?\n\nIt seems you've already been acquainted with undeath, I am impressed by your ability to raise the dead.\n\nPerhaps you could be used to my benefit, which I'm sure you would not mind. I have a particularly powerful Undead that I wish to summon, but I dare not attempt it myself - I am far too important.\n\nYou, however, could learn quite a lot by succeeding here. And if you are to fail? I will simply raise you as my own.\n\nDo not overthink it. Let me mark your map to the location of where my ritual must be had. You must collect specific items in order to complete the ritual.\n\nNow, be gone.",o="找到仪式法阵并与其互动。",oEN="Find and interact with the ritual circle.",c="<仪式法阵随着死灵能量搏动>",cEN="<The ritual circle pulsates with necromantic energy>"}
Q[200050]={d="要召唤那亡灵怪物，我必须把以下材料带到仪式法阵。\n\n- 骨头\n- 新鲜血肉\n- 头骨\n\n附近的邪恶魔仆正好有需要的东西。",dEN="In order to summon the Undead monstrosity, I must bring the following ingredients to the ritual circle.\n\n- Bones\n- Fresh Flesh\n- Skull\n\nThe nearby Vile Familiars have just what is needed.",o="杀死邪恶魔仆，搜取他们的骨头、血肉和头骨。",oEN="Kill Vile Familiars and loot their bones, flesh, and skull.",p="<你把材料放入仪式法阵>",pEN="<You place the ingredients on the ritual circle>",c="<仪式法阵开始喷涌。怪物正被召唤出来>",cEN="<The ritual circle begins to erupt. The monster is being summoned>"}
Q[200051]={d="<材料在一团烟雾中消散于仪式法阵>\n\n……好像有点不对劲。\n\n召唤失败了，再检查一下仪式法阵。但要小心，它很不稳定。",dEN="<The materials dissipate into the ritual circle into a puff of smoke>\n\n...something seems off.\n\nThe summon has failed, inspect the ritual circle again. But be careful, it is unstable.",o="杀死那只亡灵怪物。",oEN="Kill the Undead Monstrocity.",c="嗯，我早就料到会这样。\n\n不过，嘿，你没死。你已经是个更出色的死灵法师了！\n\n拿着，我派其他学徒去收拾了你那场战斗的残骸，他们做了这个。\n\n拿着它，从我眼前消失。",cEN="Well, that's exactly what I thought would happen.\n\nBut, hey, you didn't die. You're a better Necromancer already!\n\nHere, I sent my other apprentices to gather the scraps from your battle, they made this.\n\nTake it and get out of my sight."}
Q[200052]={d="你好，<class>。很高兴你今天能陪我来墓地。\n\n天气真好，是吧？\n\n看来你已经熟悉了不死之身，你复活死者的本事令我印象深刻。\n\n也许你能为我所用，我相信你不会介意。我想召唤一个特别强大的亡灵，但我不敢亲自尝试；我太重要了。\n\n而你不一样，你若在这里成功，能学到不少。要是失败了呢？那我就干脆把你复活成我的仆从。\n\n别想太多。让我把举行仪式的具体位置标在你的地图上。你必须收集特定的物品才能完成仪式。\n\n现在，去吧。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. Glad you could join me in the graveyard today.\n\nBeautiful day, isn't it?\n\nIt seems you've already been acquainted with undeath, I am impressed by your ability to raise the dead.\n\nPerhaps you could be used to my benefit, which I'm sure you would not mind. I have a particularly powerful Undead that I wish to summon, but I dare not attempt it myself - I am far too important.\n\nYou, however, could learn quite a lot by succeeding here. And if you are to fail? I will simply raise you as my own.\n\nDo not overthink it. Let me mark your map to the location of where my ritual must be had. You must collect specific items in order to complete the ritual.\n\nNow, be gone.",o="找到仪式法阵并与其互动。",oEN="Find and interact with the ritual circle.",c="<仪式法阵随着死灵能量搏动>",cEN="<The ritual circle pulsates with necromantic energy>"}
Q[200053]={d="要召唤那亡灵怪物，我必须把以下材料带到仪式法阵。\n\n- 骨头\n- 新鲜血肉\n- 头骨\n\n附近的食尸鬼正好有需要的东西。",dEN="In order to summon the Undead monstrosity, I must bring the following ingredients to the ritual circle.\n\n- Bones\n- Fresh Flesh\n- Skull\n\nThe nearby Ghouls have just what is needed.",o="杀死食尸鬼，搜取他们的骨头、血肉和头骨。",oEN="Kill Ghouls and loot their bones, flesh, and skull.",p="<你把材料放入仪式法阵>",pEN="<You place the ingredients on the ritual circle>",c="<仪式法阵开始喷涌。怪物正被召唤出来>",cEN="<The ritual circle begins to erupt. The monster is being summoned>"}
Q[200054]={d="<材料在一团烟雾中消散于仪式法阵>\n\n……好像有点不对劲。\n\n召唤失败了，再检查一下仪式法阵。但要小心，它很不稳定。",dEN="<The materials dissipate into the ritual circle into a puff of smoke>\n\n...something seems off.\n\nThe summon has failed, inspect the ritual circle again. But be careful, it is unstable.",o="杀死那只亡灵怪物。",oEN="Kill the Undead Monstrocity.",c="嗯，我早就料到会这样。\n\n不过，嘿，你没死。你已经是个更出色的死灵法师了！\n\n拿着，我派其他学徒去收拾了你那场战斗的残骸，他们做了这个。\n\n拿着它，从我眼前消失。",cEN="Well, that's exactly what I thought would happen.\n\nBut, hey, you didn't die. You're a better Necromancer already!\n\nHere, I sent my other apprentices to gather the scraps from your battle, they made this.\n\nTake it and get out of my sight."}
Q[200055]={d="我能感觉到一股邪恶的存在。\n\n你也能感觉到，对吧？所以你才在最恰当的时刻来找我。\n\n这儿就有一个。一个女巫。满身邪恶与歹意。\n\n愿圣光祝福我们接下来要做的事。\n\n拿着，接过这支火把。她就在这儿，我已经把她的位置标在你的地图上。对她使用火把，揭露她的真身。杀了她。毫不留情。\n\n她被杀掉之后就回来找我。\n\n该死的女巫。",dEN="I can feel an evil presence.\n\nYou can feel it too, can't you? That is why you have come to me at the most opportune of times.\n\nThere is one here. A witch. Brooding with evil and malintent.\n\nMay the Light bless us for what we're about to do.\n\nHere, take this torch. She's here and I've marked her location on your map. Use the torch on her to reveal her true self. Kill it. No mercy.\n\nReturn to me when it's been slain.\n\nDamned witches.",o="揭露女巫并杀死她。",oEN="Reveal the witch and kill her.",p="你回来了。",pEN="You have returned.",c="又一个邪恶生物被逐出了我们的世界。\n\n……然而。\n\n还有那么多等着被消灭。保持警觉。\n\n拿着，收下这些，让它们在你们对抗邪恶的战斗中指引你。",cEN="Yet another evil creature banished from our world.\n\n... and yet.\n\nStill so many others to destroy. Be vigilant.\n\nHere, take these, let them guide you in your battles with evil."}
Q[200056]={d="我能感觉到一股邪恶的存在。\n\n你也能感觉到，对吧？所以你才在最恰当的时刻来找我。\n\n这儿就有一个。一个女巫。满身邪恶与歹意。\n\n愿圣光祝福我们接下来要做的事。\n\n拿着，接过这支火把。她就在这儿，我已经把她的位置标在你的地图上。对她使用火把，揭露她的真身。杀了她。毫不留情。\n\n她被杀掉之后就回来找我。\n\n该死的女巫。",dEN="I can feel an evil presence.\n\nYou can feel it too, can't you? That is why you have come to me at the most opportune of times.\n\nThere is one here. A witch. Brooding with evil and malintent.\n\nMay the Light bless us for what we're about to do.\n\nHere, take this torch. She's here and I've marked her location on your map. Use the torch on her to reveal her true self. Kill it. No mercy.\n\nReturn to me when it's been slain.\n\nDamned witches.",o="揭露女巫并杀死她。",oEN="Reveal the witch and kill her.",p="你回来了。",pEN="You have returned.",c="又一个邪恶生物被逐出了我们的世界。\n\n……然而。\n\n还有那么多等着被消灭。保持警觉。\n\n拿着，收下这些，让它们在你们对抗邪恶的战斗中指引你。",cEN="Yet another evil creature banished from our world.\n\n... and yet.\n\nStill so many others to destroy. Be vigilant.\n\nHere, take these, let them guide you in your battles with evil."}
Q[200057]={d="我能感觉到一股邪恶的存在。\n\n你也能感觉到，对吧？所以你才在最恰当的时刻来找我。\n\n这儿就有一个。一个女巫。满身邪恶与歹意。\n\n愿圣光祝福我们接下来要做的事。\n\n拿着，接过这支火把。她就在这儿，我已经把她的位置标在你的地图上。对她使用火把，揭露她的真身。杀了她。毫不留情。\n\n她被杀掉之后就回来找我。\n\n该死的女巫。",dEN="I can feel an evil presence.\n\nYou can feel it too, can't you? That is why you have come to me at the most opportune of times.\n\nThere is one here. A witch. Brooding with evil and malintent.\n\nMay the Light bless us for what we're about to do.\n\nHere, take this torch. She's here and I've marked her location on your map. Use the torch on her to reveal her true self. Kill it. No mercy.\n\nReturn to me when it's been slain.\n\nDamned witches.",o="揭露女巫并杀死她。",oEN="Reveal the witch and kill her.",p="你回来了。",pEN="You have returned.",c="又一个邪恶生物被逐出了我们的世界。\n\n……然而。\n\n还有那么多等着被消灭。保持警觉。\n\n拿着，收下这些，让它们在你们对抗邪恶的战斗中指引你。",cEN="Yet another evil creature banished from our world.\n\n... and yet.\n\nStill so many others to destroy. Be vigilant.\n\nHere, take these, let them guide you in your battles with evil."}
Q[200058]={d="你好，<class>。你来得正是时候。\n\n我丢了一枚吊坠，它相当强大。所谓“丢”也许不是恰当的说法，不过算了，我们最好别在字眼上纠缠。\n\n好吧，既然你要帮我，我至少该向你解释发生了什么。那就说吧。\n\n我当时正试图让当地的迪菲亚改信安舍之阳，向他们讲解它与神圣圣光的联系……可他们并不乐意接受，把我赶走了。\n\n慌乱之中，我把吊坠掉了。请你帮我找回来。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. You have arrived at the perfect time.\n\nI have lost a pendant of mine that is quite powerful. Lost may be the wrong word, but alas, we best not get lost in the semantics.\n\nWell, I guess I owe it to you to at least explain what happened if you're going to help me. So here goes.\n\nI was attempting to convert the local Defias to follow the Sun of An'she and explaining the connection to the Holy Light... but they did not take kindly to this and ran me off.\n\nIn my haste, I dropped my pendant. Please, find it for me.",o="找到丢失的吊坠。",oEN="Find the lost pendant.",p="你回来了。",pEN="You have returned.",c="<吊坠闪闪发光。散发出强烈的神圣气息>\n\n你做得很好，<name>。这枚吊坠我就送给你了。\n\n把它收好，因为有一天你可能还会需要它，而我也许能教你如何解锁它更多的力量。",cEN="<The pendant glimmers. It gives off a strong holy presence>\n\nYou have done well, <name>. This pendant, I will give to you.\n\nKeep it close, for someday, you may need it again and I may teach you how to unlock far more of its powers."}
Q[200059]={d="我能感觉到一股邪恶的存在。\n\n你也能感觉到，对吧？所以你才在最恰当的时刻来找我。\n\n这儿就有一个。一个女巫。阴沉沉的，满身邪恶与歹意。\n\n愿圣光祝福我们接下来要做的事。\n\n拿着，接过这支火把。她就在这儿。对她使用火把，揭露她的真身。杀了她。毫不留情。\n\n她被杀掉之后就回来找我。\n\n该死的女巫。",dEN="I can feel an evil presence.\n\nYou can feel it too, can't you? That is why you have come to me at the most opportune of times.\n\nThere is one here. A witch. Brooding with evil and malintent.\n\nMay the Light bless us for what we're about to do.\n\nHere, take this torch. She's here. Use the torch on her to reveal her true self. Kill it. No mercy.\n\nReturn to me when it's been slain.\n\nDamned witches.",o="揭露女巫并杀死她。",oEN="Reveal the witch and kill her."}
Q[200060]={d="你好，<class>。你来得正是时候。\n\n我丢了一枚吊坠，它相当强大。所谓“丢”也许不是恰当的说法，不过算了，我们最好别在字眼上纠缠。\n\n好吧，既然你要帮我，我至少该向你解释发生了什么。那就说吧。\n\n我当时在安威玛尔南边扎营，想监视当地的穴居人。不幸的是，一天夜里我睡着时，他们一伙人伏击了我，把我赶走，还洗劫了我的营地。\n\n慌乱之中，我把吊坠掉了。请你帮我找回来。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. You have arrived at the perfect time.\n\nI have lost a pendant of mine that is quite powerful. Lost may be the wrong word, but alas, we best not get lost in the semantics.\n\nWell, I guess I owe it to you to at least explain what happened if you're going to help me. So here goes.\n\nI was camping out to the south of Anvilmar in an attempt to spy on the local Trogg population. Unfortunately, one night while I was asleep I was ambushed by a group of them and they drove me out and pillaged my camp.\n\nIn my haste, I dropped my pendant. Please, find it for me.",o="找到丢失的吊坠。",oEN="Find the lost pendant.",p="是啊，小子。你办到了。",pEN="Aye, lad. You've done it.",c="<吊坠闪闪发光。散发出强烈的神圣气息>\n\n你做得很好，<name>。这枚吊坠我就送给你了。\n\n把它收好，因为有一天你可能还会需要它，而我也许能教你如何解锁它更多的力量。",cEN="<The pendant glimmers. It gives off a strong holy presence>\n\nYou have done well, <name>. This pendant, I will give to you.\n\nKeep it close, for someday, you may need it again and I may teach you how to unlock far more of its powers."}
Q[200061]={d="你好，<class>。你来得正是时候。\n\n我丢了一枚吊坠，它相当强大。所谓“丢”也许不是恰当的说法，不过算了，我们最好别在字眼上纠缠。\n\n好吧，既然你要帮我，我至少该向你解释发生了什么。那就说吧。\n\n我当时想向格雷尔证明，他们也能追随圣光……可这兆头不妙。他们把我赶出了营地，我勉强保住性命逃了出来。\n\n慌乱之中，我把吊坠掉了。请你帮我找回来。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. You have arrived at the perfect time.\n\nI have lost a pendant of mine that is quite powerful. Lost may be the wrong word, but alas, we best not get lost in the semantics.\n\nWell, I guess I owe it to you to at least explain what happened if you're going to help me. So here goes.\n\nI was attempting to show the Grell that they too can turn the Light... but it did not bode well. They chased me out of their camp and I barely made it out alive.\n\nIn my haste, I dropped my pendant. Please, find it for me.",o="找到丢失的吊坠。",oEN="Find the lost pendant.",p="耶，你办到了！！",pEN="Yay, you've done it!!",c="<吊坠闪闪发光。散发出强烈的神圣气息>\n\n你做得很好，<name>。这枚吊坠我就送给你了。\n\n把它收好，因为有一天你可能还会需要它，而我也许能教你如何解锁它更多的力量。",cEN="<The pendant glimmers. It gives off a strong holy presence>\n\nYou have done well, <name>. This pendant, I will give to you.\n\nKeep it close, for someday, you may need it again and I may teach you how to unlock far more of its powers."}
Q[200062]={d="你好，<class>。你来得正是时候。\n\n我丢了一枚吊坠，它相当强大。所谓“丢”也许不是恰当的说法，不过算了，我们最好别在字眼上纠缠。\n\n好吧，既然你要帮我，我至少该向你解释发生了什么。那就说吧。\n\n我当时想向当地营地里的血色十字军证明，我们可以合作，因为我们同样追随圣光。\n\n他们并不乐意接受，把我赶出了营地……\n\n慌乱之中，我把吊坠掉了。请你帮我找回来。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. You have arrived at the perfect time.\n\nI have lost a pendant of mine that is quite powerful. Lost may be the wrong word, but alas, we best not get lost in the semantics.\n\nWell, I guess I owe it to you to at least explain what happened if you're going to help me. So here goes.\n\nI was attempting to show the Scarlet Crusaders at the local camps that we can work together, as we both follow the light.\n\nThey did not take kindly to this and they ran me out of their camp...\n\nIn my haste, I dropped my pendant. Please, find it for me.",o="找到丢失的吊坠。",oEN="Find the lost pendant.",p="你找到吊坠了吗，<name>？",pEN="Have you found the pendant yet, <name>?",c="善有善报，<name>。",cEN="One good deed deserves another, <name>."}
Q[200063]={d="你好，<class>。你来得正是时候。\n\n我丢了一枚吊坠，它相当强大。所谓“丢”也许不是恰当的说法，不过算了，我们最好别在字眼上纠缠。\n\n好吧，既然你要帮我，我至少该向你解释发生了什么。那就说吧。\n\n我当时想向当地营地里的血色十字军证明，我们可以合作，因为我们同样追随圣光。\n\n他们并不乐意接受，把我赶出了营地……\n\n慌乱之中，我把吊坠掉了。请你帮我找回来。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. You have arrived at the perfect time.\n\nI have lost a pendant of mine that is quite powerful. Lost may be the wrong word, but alas, we best not get lost in the semantics.\n\nWell, I guess I owe it to you to at least explain what happened if you're going to help me. So here goes.\n\nI was attempting to show the Scarlet Crusaders at the local camps that we can work together, as we both follow the light.\n\nThey did not take kindly to this and they ran me out of their camp...\n\nIn my haste, I dropped my pendant. Please, find it for me.",o="找到丢失的吊坠。",oEN="Find the lost pendant.",p="你找到吊坠了吗，<name>？",pEN="Have you found the pendant, <name>?",c="善有善报，<name>！",cEN="One good deed deserves another, <name>!"}
Q[200064]={d="你好，<class>。你来得正是时候。\n\n我丢了一枚吊坠，它相当强大。所谓“丢”也许不是恰当的说法，不过算了，我们最好别在字眼上纠缠。\n\n好吧，既然你要帮我，我至少该向你解释发生了什么。那就说吧。\n\n我当时想向那些野猪人展示圣光……没成功。\n\n他们并不领情，把我赶出了营地……\n\n慌乱之中，我把吊坠掉了。请你帮我找回来。",dEN="Greetings, <class>. You have arrived at the perfect time.\n\nI have lost a pendant of mine that is quite powerful. Lost may be the wrong word, but alas, we best not get lost in the semantics.\n\nWell, I guess I owe it to you to at least explain what happened if you're going to help me. So here goes.\n\nI was attempting to show those pigmen the light... it did not work.\n\nThey did not take kindly to this and they ran me out of their camp...\n\nIn my haste, I dropped my pendant. Please, find it for me.",o="找到丢失的吊坠。",oEN="Find the lost pendant.",p="你找到吊坠了吗，运气如何，<name>？",pEN="Have you had any luck finding the pendant, <name>?",c="善有善报，<name>。",cEN="One good deed deserves another, <name>."}
Q[200065]={d="哎呀！你好啊，邻居！\n\n我看你是那种爱鼓捣发明的人，老实说，我一直在找像你这样的人。我想造一种特别的枪，可以说是自制的枪，但我还需要些金属。\n\n那边狗头人营地附近有些金属，可以用来给你和我各造一把枪。给我弄点回来，我就动手开工！",dEN="Why I'll be! Howdy there neighbor!\n\nI see you be the tinkerin' type and I was honestly on the look out for one like you. I'm tryin' to make a special type of gun, a homemade gun some might say, but I need some more metal.\n\nThere is some metal out there near the kobold camps that could be used to create a gun for you and me. Collect me some and I'll go tinkerin' away!",o="收集 3 块废金属。",oEN="Collect 3 Scrap Metal.",p="你真是个好手！",pEN="You're a true scrapper!",c="嗯，这太完美了！\n\n我用这些金属给自己造好了一把新枪，你猜怎么着？我也给你造了一把！\n\n拿去吧，祝你今天过得愉快！",cEN="Well, this is perfect!\n\nI was able to use this metal to finish a new gun for me and, guess what, I made you one too!\n\nTake it and have a great day!"}
Q[200066]={d="哎呀！你好！你是<name>，对吧？？\n\n我看你是那种爱鼓捣发明的人，老实说，我一直在找像你这样的人。我想造一种特别的枪，可以说是自制的枪，但我还需要些金属。\n\n那边有座被穴居人占据的废弃营地附近有些金属，可以用来给你和我各造一把枪。给我弄点回来，我就动手开工！",dEN="Why I'll be! Howdy there! <name>, was it??\n\nI see you be the tinkerin' type and I was honestly on the look out for one like you. I'm tryin' to make a special type of gun, a homemade gun some might say, but I need some more metal.\n\nThere is some metal out there near one of those abandoned camps that are infested with troggs that could be used to create a gun for you and me. Collect me some and I'll go tinkerin' away!",o="收集 3 块废金属。",oEN="Collect 3 Scrap Metal.",p="你找到废金属了吗？",pEN="Have you found the scrap yet?",c="嗯，这太完美了！\n\n我用这些金属给自己造好了一把新枪，你猜怎么着？我也给你造了一把！\n\n拿去吧，祝你今天过得愉快！",cEN="Well, this is perfect!\n\nI was able to use this metal to finish a new gun for me and, guess what, I made you one too!\n\nTake it and have a great day!"}
Q[200067]={d="你好。你是<name>，对吧？欢迎来到阿尔德拉斯。\n\n你看起来像是那种爱鼓捣发明的人，老实说，我一直在找像你这样的人。我想造一种特别的枪，可以说是自制的枪，但我还需要些金属。\n\n那边格雷尔营地附近有些金属，可以用来给你和我各造一把枪。给我弄点回来，我就动手开工！",dEN="Greetings. <name>, was it? Welcome to Aldrassil.\n\nYou seem to be the tinkering type and I was honestly on the look out for one like you. I'm trying to make a special type of gun, a homemade gun some might say, but I need some more metal.\n\nThere is some metal out there near the grell camps that could be used to create a gun for you and me. Collect me some and I'll go tinkering away!",o="收集 3 块废金属。",oEN="Collect 3 Scrap Metal.",p="你找到废金属了吗？",pEN="Have you found the scrap yet?",c="嗯，这太完美了！\n\n我用这些金属给自己造好了一把新枪，你猜怎么着？我也给你造了一把！\n\n拿去吧，祝你今天过得愉快！",cEN="Well, this is perfect!\n\nI was able to use this metal to finish a new gun for me and, guess what, I made you one too!\n\nTake it and have a great day!"}
Q[200068]={d="Zug，zug，<name>。\n\n今天我要证明兽人的巧思。Lok'tar ogar！我要给自己造一把枪，如果你帮我，也给你造一把！\n\n小恶魔的洞穴里有些金属，可以用来给你和我各造一把枪。给我捡点回来，我就动手造枪。",dEN="Zug, zug, <name>.\n\nToday, I will prove the ingenuity of the Orcs. Lok'tar ogar! I will create a gun for me, and if you help me, for you!\n\nThere is some metal out there in the imp cave that could be used to create a gun for you and me. Collect me some and I build gun.",o="收集 3 块废金属。",oEN="Collect 3 Scrap Metal.",p="你找到废金属了吗？",pEN="Have you found the scrap yet?",c="嗯，这太完美了！\n\n我用这些金属给自己造好了一把新枪，你猜怎么着？我也给你造了一把！\n\n拿去吧，祝你今天过得愉快！",cEN="Well, this is perfect!\n\nI was able to use this metal to finish a new gun for me and, guess what, I made you one too!\n\nTake it and have a great day!"}
Q[200160]={d="欢迎，<class>。我一直在冷脊谷等候你的到来。\n\n你来向我求取智慧，那么我就把智慧传授给你。\n\n成为<class>大师的第一步，是掌握熊之道。每一次精通之后都会有新的挑战，但眼下，我们先专注于释放你内心野性本能的意义。\n\n熊是庞大而凶猛的生物。它们只知道自己生存所需，那就是杀戮。想要从一个决心取你性命的熊爪下逃脱，几乎无能为力。\n\n借由熊，我们获得凶猛、残暴与力量，毫不留情。\n\n用取走此地西边霜鬃巨魔的性命来向我证明你明白了这一点，我会奖赏你。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. I have awaited your arrival here in Coldridge Valley.\n\nYou come to me for wisdom, and as such, I will deliver.\n\nThe first step to becoming a master <class> is mastering the way of the bear. With each successive mastery will come yet another challenge, but for now, let's focus on what it means to unlock your inner savage instincts.\n\nBears are large, ferocious creatures. They know only what they must to survive, and that is to kill. There is little one can do to escape from a bear who wishes to end their life.\n\nThrough the bear we gain savagery, viciousness, and strength, without mercy.\n\nShow me that you understand this by ending the lives of the Ice Trolls to the west of here and I will reward you.",o="杀死 8 只霜鬃巨魔幼崽。",oEN="Kill 8 Frostmane Troll Whelps.",c="啊哈！你向我证明了你确实强大。为此，我以熊本身的象征作为奖赏。愿它在你旅途中指引你，赐你力量战胜敌人。",cEN="Aha! You have shown me that you are truly powerful. For this, I reward you with a symbol of the Bear itself. May it guide you on your journeys and give you strength over your foes."}
Q[200161]={d="欢迎，<class>。我一直在阿尔德拉斯等候你的到来。\n\n你来向我求取智慧，那么我就把智慧传授给你。\n\n成为<class>大师的第一步，是掌握熊之道。每一次精通之后都会有新的挑战，但眼下，我们先专注于释放你内心野性本能的意义。\n\n熊是庞大而凶猛的生物。它们只知道自己生存所需，那就是杀戮。想要从一个决心取你性命的熊爪下逃脱，几乎无能为力。\n\n借由熊，我们获得凶猛、残暴与力量，毫不留情。\n\n用取走附近洞穴里网木蜘蛛的性命来向我证明你明白了这一点，我会奖赏你。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. I have awaited your arrival here in Aldrassil.\n\nYou come to me for wisdom, and as such, I will deliver.\n\nThe first step to becoming a master <class> is mastering the way of the bear. With each successive mastery will come yet another challenge, but for now, let's focus on what it means to unlock your inner savage instincts.\n\nBears are large, ferocious creatures. They know only what they must to survive, and that is to kill. There is little one can do to escape from a bear who wishes to end their life.\n\nThrough the bear we gain savagery, viciousness, and strength, without mercy.\n\nShow me that you understand this by ending the lives of the Webwood Spiders in the cave near here and I will reward you.",o="杀死 8 只网木蜘蛛。",oEN="Kill 8 Webwood Spider.",p="你完成任务了吗，<name>？",pEN="Have you completed the task, <name>?",c="啊哈！你向我证明了你确实强大。为此，我以熊本身的象征作为奖赏。愿它在你旅途中指引你，赐你力量战胜敌人。",cEN="Aha! You have shown me that you are truly powerful. For this, I reward you with a symbol of the Bear itself. May it guide you on your journeys and give you strength over your foes."}
Q[200162]={d="Zug zug，<class>。我一直在试炼谷等候你的到来。\n\n你来向我求取智慧，那么我就把智慧传授给你。\n\n成为<class>大师的第一步，是掌握熊之道。每一次精通之后都会有新的挑战，但眼下，我们先专注于释放你内心野性本能的意义。\n\n熊是庞大而凶猛的生物。它们只知道自己生存所需，那就是杀戮。想要从一个决心取你性命的熊爪下逃脱，几乎无能为力。\n\n借由熊，我们获得凶猛、残暴与力量，毫不留情。\n\n用取走此地北边邪能潜伏者的性命来向我证明你明白了这一点，我会奖赏你。",dEN="Zug zug, <class>. I have awaited your arrival here in the Valley of Trials.\n\nYou come to me for wisdom, and as such, I will deliver.\n\nThe first step to becoming a master <class> is mastering the way of the bear. With each successive mastery will come yet another challenge, but for now, let's focus on what it means to unlock your inner savage instincts.\n\nBears are large, ferocious creatures. They know only what they must to survive, and that is to kill. There is little one can do to escape from a bear who wishes to end their life.\n\nThrough the bear we gain savagery, viciousness, and strength, without mercy.\n\nShow me that you understand this by ending the lives of the Felstalkers north of here and I will reward you.",o="杀死 4 只邪能潜伏者。",oEN="Kill 4 Felstalkers.",c="啊哈！你向我证明了你确实强大。为此，我以熊本身的象征作为奖赏。愿它在你旅途中指引你，赐你力量战胜敌人。",cEN="Aha! You have shown me that you are truly powerful. For this, I reward you with a symbol of the Bear itself. May it guide you on your journeys and give you strength over your foes."}
Q[200163]={d="欢迎，<class>。我一直在红云台地等候你的到来。\n\n你来向我求取智慧，那么我就把智慧传授给你。\n\n成为<class>大师的第一步，是掌握熊之道。每一次精通之后都会有新的挑战，但眼下，我们先专注于释放你内心野性本能的意义。\n\n熊是庞大而凶猛的生物。它们只知道自己生存所需，那就是杀戮。想要从一个决心取你性命的熊爪下逃脱，几乎无能为力。\n\n借由熊，我们获得凶猛、残暴与力量，毫不留情。\n\n用取走近处峡谷里野猪人的性命来向我证明你明白了这一点，我会奖赏你。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. I have awaited your arrival here in Red Cloud Mesa.\n\nYou come to me for wisdom, and as such, I will deliver.\n\nThe first step to becoming a master <class> is mastering the way of the bear. With each successive mastery will come yet another challenge, but for now, let's focus on what it means to unlock your inner savage instincts.\n\nBears are large, ferocious creatures. They know only what they must to survive, and that is to kill. There is little one can do to escape from a bear who wishes to end their life.\n\nThrough the bear we gain savagery, viciousness, and strength, without mercy.\n\nShow me that you understand this by ending the lives of the quilboars at the ravine near here and I will reward you.",o="杀死 8 只钢鬃野猪人。",oEN="Kill 8 Bristleback Quilboar.",p="你把那些野猪人清干净了吗，<name>？",pEN="Have you laid waste to the quilboars, <name>?",c="啊哈！你向我证明了你确实强大。为此，我以熊本身的象征作为奖赏。愿它在你旅途中指引你，赐你力量战胜敌人。",cEN="Aha! You have shown me that you are truly powerful. For this, I reward you with a symbol of the Bear itself. May it guide you on your journeys and give you strength over your foes."}
Q[200164]={d="欢迎，<class>。我一直在冷脊谷等候你的到来。\n\n你来向我求取智慧，那么我就把智慧传授给你。\n\n成为<class>大师的第一步，是掌握熊之道。每一次精通之后都会有新的挑战，但眼下，我们先专注于释放你内心野性本能的意义。\n\n熊是庞大而凶猛的生物。它们只知道自己生存所需，那就是杀戮。想要从一个决心取你性命的熊爪下逃脱，几乎无能为力。\n\n借由熊，我们获得凶猛、残暴与力量，毫不留情。\n\n用取走此地西边霜鬃巨魔的性命来向我证明你明白了这一点，我会奖赏你。",dEN="Welcome, <class>. I have awaited your arrival here in Coldridge Valley.\n\nYou come to me for wisdom, and as such, I will deliver.\n\nThe first step to becoming a master <class> is mastering the way of the bear. With each successive mastery will come yet another challenge, but for now, let's focus on what it means to unlock your inner savage instincts.\n\nBears are large, ferocious creatures. They know only what they must to survive, and that is to kill. There is little one can do to escape from a bear who wishes to end their life.\n\nThrough the bear we gain savagery, viciousness, and strength, without mercy.\n\nShow me that you understand this by ending the lives of the Ice Trolls to the west of here and I will reward you.",o="杀死 8 只霜鬃巨魔幼崽。",oEN="Kill 8 Frostmane Troll Whelps.",c="啊哈！你向我证明了你确实强大。为此，我以熊本身的象征作为奖赏。愿它在你旅途中指引你，赐你力量战胜敌人。",cEN="Aha! You have shown me that you are truly powerful. For this, I reward you with a symbol of the Bear itself. May it guide you on your journeys and give you strength over your foes."}
Q[200165]={d="啊，<name>，我很久以前就预见了你的到来。现在，是时候教你成为一名时光术士意味着什么了。编织空间与时间最本源的织理。等同于神明……\n\n别让我把话说得太满。因为<name>，你在时光魔法上还是个新手，在我允许你带着如此潜在的力量存在于这个世界之前……你必须学会控制自己。\n\n身为时光术士，你是时间魔法的大师。这意味着你必须在最根本的层面上尊重时间。正好，我把法杖落在了修道院的某个地方。\n\n你有 2 分钟。去帮我找回来。",dEN="Ahhh, <name>, I saw your arrival long ago. Now it is time to teach you what it means to be a Chronomancer. To weave the very fabric of space and time. To be equivalent to a god...\n\nLet me not get ahead of myself. For you, <name>, are new to the world of chronomancy, and before I can allow you to inhabit this world with such latent power... you must learn how to control yourself.\n\nAs a Chronomancer, you are a master of time magic. This means you must respect time on the most foundational of levels. It just so happens that I left my wand somewhere in the abbey.\n\nYou have 2 minutes. Find it for me.",o="在北郡修道院寻找索利多米的法杖。",oEN="Find Soridormi's wand in Northshire Abbey.",p="啊，你回来了？",pEN="Ahh, you've returned.",c="欢迎回来，<name>。我就知道你会及时找到我的法杖。字面意义上的及时。\n\n这根法杖给你。希望它对你有所帮助。事实上，我知道它一定会的。",cEN="Welcome back, <name>. I knew you would find my wand in time. Literally.\n\nThis wand is for you. I hope it serves you well. In fact, I know it will."}
Q[200166]={d="啊，<name>，我很久以前就预见了你的到来。现在，是时候教你成为一名时光术士意味着什么了。编织空间与时间最本源的织理。等同于神明……\n\n别让我把话说得太满。因为<name>，你在时光魔法上还是个新手，在我允许你带着如此潜在的力量存在于这个世界之前……你必须学会控制自己。\n\n身为时光术士，你是时间魔法的大师。这意味着你必须在最根本的层面上尊重时间。正好，我把法杖落在了这座建筑的某个地方。\n\n你有 2 分钟。去帮我找回来。",dEN="Ahhh, <name>, I saw your arrival long ago. Now it is time to teach you what it means to be a Chronomancer. To weave the very fabric of space and time. To be equivalent to a god...\n\nLet me not get ahead of myself. For you, <name>, are new to the world of chronomancy, and before I can allow you to inhabit this world with such latent power... you must learn how to control yourself.\n\nAs a Chronomancer, you are a master of time magic. This means you must respect time on the most foundational of levels. It just so happens that I left my wand somewhere in this building.\n\nYou have 2 minutes. Find it for me.",o="在安威玛尔寻找哈罗多姆的法杖。",oEN="Find Harodormu's wand in Anvilmar.",p="啊，你回来了？",pEN="Ahh, you've returned.",c="欢迎回来，<name>。我就知道你会及时找到我的法杖。字面意义上的及时。\n\n这根法杖给你。希望它对你有所帮助。事实上，我知道它一定会的。",cEN="Welcome back, <name>. I knew you would find my wand in time. Literally.\n\nThis wand is for you. I hope it serves you well. In fact, I know it will."}
Q[200167]={d="啊，<name>，我很久以前就预见了你的到来。现在，是时候教你成为一名时光术士意味着什么了。编织空间与时间最本源的织理。等同于神明……\n\n别让我把话说得太满。因为<name>，你在时光魔法上还是个新手，在我允许你带着如此潜在的力量存在于这个世界之前……你必须学会控制自己。\n\n身为时光术士，你是时间魔法的大师。这意味着你必须在最根本的层面上尊重时间。正好，我把法杖落在了这儿这座建筑的某个地方。\n\n你有 2 分钟。去帮我找回来。",dEN="Ahhh, <name>, I saw your arrival long ago. Now it is time to teach you what it means to be a Chronomancer. To weave the very fabric of space and time. To be equivalent to a god...\n\nLet me not get ahead of myself. For you, <name>, are new to the world of chronomancy, and before I can allow you to inhabit this world with such latent power... you must learn how to control yourself.\n\nAs a Chronomancer, you are a master of time magic. This means you must respect time on the most foundational of levels. It just so happens that I left my wand somewhere in the in this building here.\n\nYou have 2 minutes. Find it for me.",o="在阿尔德拉斯寻找卡莱多姆的法杖。",oEN="Find Kaleidormu's wand in Aldrassil.",p="啊，你回来了？",pEN="Ahh, you've returned.",c="欢迎回来，<name>。我就知道你会及时找到我的法杖。字面意义上的及时。\n\n这根法杖给你。希望它对你有所帮助。事实上，我知道它一定会的。",cEN="Welcome back, <name>. I knew you would find my wand in time. Literally.\n\nThis wand is for you. I hope it serves you well. In fact, I know it will."}
Q[200168]={d="啊，<name>，我很久以前就预见了你的到来。现在，是时候教你成为一名时光术士意味着什么了。编织空间与时间最本源的织理。等同于神明……\n\n别把话说得太满。因为<name>，你在时光魔法上还是个新手，在我允许你带着如此潜在的力量存在于这个世界之前……你必须学会控制自己。\n\n身为时光术士，你是时间魔法的大师。这意味着你必须在最根本的层面上尊重时间。正好，我把法杖落在了隔壁房子的某个地方。\n\n你有 2 分钟。去帮我找出来。",dEN="Ahhh, <name>, I saw your arrival long ago. Now it is time to teach you what it means to be a Chronomancer. To weave the very fabric of space and time. To be equivalent to a god...\n\nLet me not get ahead of myself. For you, <name>, are new to the world of chronomancy, and before I can allow you to inhabit this world with such latent power... you must learn how to control yourself.\n\nAs a Chronomancer, you are a master of time magic. This means you must respect time on the most foundational of levels. It just so happens that I left my wand somewhere next door.\n\nYou have 2 minutes. Find it for me.",o="在丧钟镇寻找夸尔多米的法杖。",oEN="Find Quardormi's wand in Deathknell.",p="啊，你回来了？",pEN="Ahh, you've returned.",c="欢迎回来，<name>。我就知道你会及时找到我的法杖。字面意义上的及时。\n\n这根法杖给你。希望它对你有所帮助。事实上，我知道它一定会的。",cEN="Welcome back, <name>. I knew you would find my wand in time. Literally.\n\nThis wand is for you. I hope it serves you well. In fact, I know it will."}
Q[200169]={d="阿拉希山脉有个邪恶的雪人，把城里冬幕节的礼物全偷走了！\n\n拜托，你必须把它们找回来。你要是不去……嗯，想想孩子们吧！那可太惨了！\n\n你打倒他，我会奖赏你。他叫霜爪。去阿拉希山脉找到他，杀了他！",dEN="There's an evil Yeti in the Alterac Mountains who has stolen ALL of the Winter's Veil presents in the city!\n\nPlease, you must return them. If you do not... well, just think of the children! It will be horrible!\n\nI will reward you for taking him down. His name is Frostclaw. Find him in the Alterac Mountains and slay him!",o="在阿拉希山脉杀死霜爪。",oEN="Slay Frostclaw in the Alterac Mountains.",c="你办到了！因为你拯救了冬幕节，我有份礼物给你。谢谢你！\n\n要是那雪人不知怎么从坟墓里爬回来……你就等着吧。而我会在这儿，准备好再给你更多礼物，只为你再杀他一次！",cEN="You've done it! Because you saved Winter's Veil - I have a gift for you. Thank you!\n\nIf that Yeti somehow comes back from the grave... you'll be waiting. And I'll be here, ready to give you more presents for killing him!"}
Q[200170]={d="你好，<name>。很高兴你终于能来见我了，我一直在等你的到来。\n\n今天，给像你这样有志成为符文大师的人上一堂简单的解题课。也许你能成功，也许不能。\n\n这儿，我有一块符文。符文上刻着一个谜语。解开这个谜语，然后回来找我。\n\n要提示？我能告诉你的最好提示就是：这个谜语的答案在旅店里面。不是外面。\n\n你回来时我就知道你有没有解开，别担心。成功了，我就奖赏你。",dEN="Greetings, <name>. I'm glad you could finally join me, I have awaited your arrival.\n\nToday, a simple lesson in problem solving for an aspiring Runemaster such as yourself. Perhaps you will succeed, perhaps you will not.\n\nHere, I have a rune. Etched on the rune is a riddle. Figure the riddle out and return to me.\n\nA hint? The best I can do is tell you that the answer to this riddle lays within the Inn. Not without.\n\nI will know when you return if you have figured it out or not, do not worry. Succeed, and I will reward you.",o="解开刻在符文石上的谜语。",oEN="Figure out the riddle etched on the runestone.",p="我能感觉到符文就在你身上。了不起。",pEN="I can feel the runestone is in your presence. Impressive.",c="你在别人可能失败的地方成功了，但最艰难的课程不会最先到来。\n\n无论如何，你的决心令我印象深刻。把你刚带来的符文石拿去吧，在你的旅途中使用它，愿它指引你。\n\n等你更强了再回来找我，我们继续上课。",cEN="You have succeeded where some may have failed, but the hardest lessons do not come first.\n\nRegardless, I am impressed by your determination. Take the runestone that you just brought me and use it in your travels, may it guide you.\n\nReturn to me when you are stronger and we will continue your lessons."}
Q[200171]={d="你已踏上探索者之路的第一步，但前方的路漫长，而且满是隐藏的功课。\n\n我们得到消息，一位经验丰富的老手出现在某座主城附近。据说这位游侠对野外生存之术有着深厚的造诣，通晓大地、野兽，以及在人迹罕至之处求生的法门。\n\n你目前的技艺已为你此番远行做好了准备。前往最近的主城，寻找这位大师。在那里，你将继续受训，并开始以你从未想象过的方式理解荒野。\n\n找到他时，要有底气地开口。荒野听见一切，它偏爱那些带着荣誉前行的人。",dEN="You've taken your first steps on the path of the ranger, but the road ahead is long and full of hidden lessons.\n\nWord has reached us of a seasoned practitioner who has appeared near one of the capital cities. This ranger is said to possess deep knowledge in the art of bushcraft, an understanding of the land, the beasts, and the ways to survive where few dare tread.\n\nYour current skills have prepared you for this journey. Travel to the nearest capital and seek out this master. There, you will continue your training and begin to understand the wilds in ways you never imagined.\n\nWhen you find them, speak with purpose. The wild hears all, and it favors those who walk with honor.",o="与卫兵交谈，在附近的主城找到你的职业训练师。",oEN="Speak to a guard to find your class trainer in a nearby capital city.",c="哼，你看着挺有前途。我有件再合适不过的任务给你。",cEN="Hmph, you look promising. I've got just the task for you."}
Q[200172]={d="我的猎鹰带回了令人不安的消息。它侦察时发现了一处偏僻的洞穴，隐藏在灰谷森林深处，似乎就是那只袭击你的野兽之主所在的位置。\n\n更令人不安的是，据猎鹰所见，我认出那只野兽与你初次试炼时袭击你的那只极为相似。它们相似而独特。毫无疑问。\n\n在我把位置告诉你之前，我需要你做一件东西。制作一张皮革地图。这是我们的传统之一。它必须手工制作，并灌注你的专注。只有这样，我才会标出通往营地的路。\n\n等你带着地图回来，我就把你所求之物给你。之后，就看你能否追踪到他们，并面对等待你的一切。",dEN="My falcon has returned with troubling news. While scouting it spotted a secluded cave hidden deep within the wilds of Ashenvale that seems to house the location of the owner of the beast that attacked you.\n\nMore disturbingly, by the falcon’s eye, I recognized a beast not unlike the one that attacked you during your first trial. It is a similar and unique creature. There is no doubt.\n\nBefore I can share the location with you, I need you to create something for me. Craft a leather map. This is one of our traditions. It must be made by hand and imbued with your focus. Only then will I mark the path to the camp.\n\nOnce you return with the map, I will give you what you seek. Then, it is up to you to track them down and face whatever awaits.",o="制作一张地图，并把它交给你的训练师。",oEN="Craft a Map and return it to your trainer.",p="任务完成之后再回来找我。",pEN="Return to me only when your task is complete.",c="你做得很好。这张地图上带着一位准备好开拓自己道路的游侠的印记。",cEN="You've done well. This map bears the marks of a ranger ready to claim their path."}
Q[200173]={d="你制作的地图已经派上了用场。我会标出我的猎鹰侦察到的位置。它就在灰谷森林深处，远离任何有人行走的道路。\n\n在那里，你希望能找到我们一直在找的人，以及与他同在的一只生物——与你初次试炼时袭击你的那只并无太大不同。它们同时出现绝非巧合。有什么东西把它们联系在一起。\n\n你必须前往那里，直面荒野中等待的一切真相。这场试炼需要的可能远不止你的战斗技巧。准备好动用你武器库里的每一件工具。",dEN="The map you crafted has served its purpose. I will mark the location that my falcon scouted. It lies deep within the wilds of Ashenvale, far from any traveled road.\n\nThere, you will hopefully find the one we have been searching for and with them, a creature not unlike the one that attacked you during your first trial. Their presence is no coincidence. Something connects them.\n\nYou must go to this place and confront whatever truths wait in the wild. This trial may require far more than just your combat skillset. Be prepared to use every tool in your arsenal.",o="找到猎人最后一次现身的洞穴。",oEN="Find the cave where the Hunter was last seen.",p="等你解决了那个猎人，就回来找我。",pEN="When you have dealt with the Hunter, return to me.",c="你回来了。这意义比你想象的更重大。\n\n你站稳了脚跟，直面了潜藏的猎手，带回了荒野长久隐藏的答案。\n\n如今道路属于你自己，而它把你引向更深处。\n\n但那个问题仍然悬在空中。为什么？",cEN="You made it back. That means more than you know.\n\nYou stood your ground, faced what hunted you, and returned with answers the wild had long kept hidden.\n\nYour path is yours now, and it leads deeper still.\n\nBut the question remains. Why?"}
Q[200174]={d="这么说……扎'博尔走了。\n\n他本可以是我们中的一员。但他选择了野兽，而非弓。他以为与荒野的友谊重于敬畏。猎人们正是错在这里。他们模糊了界限。他们紧抱野兽，视之如至亲。\n\n游侠不会。我们精准地走在那条界线上。\n\n猎人索取。游侠知道何时索取，何时静观。我们确实养猎鹰，但不是因为它们可爱。它们有用。它们侦察。它们生存。算它们走运，它们身上没有值得剥取的毛皮。\n\n<name>，你展现出了力量，但如果你想成为的不只是又一个枪法不错的追踪者，你就得证明更多。\n\n我们游侠机敏。我们聪明。我们如雾般消散，如燧石般出击。我们中有些人守护森林的安宁。另一些人……则夺取这世界拒绝给予我们的东西。两条路都以同样的方式开始。\n\n在荆棘谷，莫什奥格食人魔坟冢里藏着一只箱子，握在莫格奥格领主手中。大多数人永远找不到它。更少有人能打开它。这需要机巧。\n\n如果你能找出它，里面有一封信，以及你成为探索者公会新兵的下一个步骤。\n\n找到它。打开它。读一读。证明你是谁。",dEN="So… Za’Bor is gone.\n\nCould’ve been one of us, once. But he chose the beasts over the bow. Thought friendship with the wild meant more than respect. That’s where Hunters go wrong. They blur the line. They cling to beasts like they’re kin.\n\nRangers don’t. We walk that edge with precision.\n\nHunters take. Rangers know when to take, and when to watch. We keep falcons, yes, but not because they’re cute. They serve. They scout. They survive. Lucky for them they don’t have hides worth skinning.\n\n<name>, you’ve shown strength, but if you want to be more than just another tracker with good aim, you’ll need to prove something else.\n\nRangers are slick. We’re clever. We vanish like mist and strike like flint. Some of us keep the peace in the woods. Some... take what the world denies us. Either path begins the same.\n\nIn Stranglethorn Vale, there’s a chest hidden in the Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mounds in the hands of the Mogg'Ogg Lords. Most will never acquire it. Fewer still open it. It takes guile.\n\nIf you can figure it out, inside you’ll find a letter and your next step towards becoming an Initiate of the Ranger’s Guild.\n\nFind it. Open it. Read. Prove yourself.",o="找到并打开藏在荆棘谷的上锁箱子。",oEN="Find and open the locked chest hidden in Stranglethorn Vale.",p="入会仪式开始了。",pEN="Initiation begins."}
Q[200175]={d="你打开了很多人打不开的东西。\n\n这说明了一些事。也许足够了。也许还不够。\n\n这封信不只是一张字条，它是一扇门。一扇我们不会为任何人打开的门。\n\n如果你正在读这段话，说明你的名字正在公会里某人的嘴边。也许是被低声提起。也许是被咒骂。但终究是被提到了。这意味着你正被注视着……被考验着。\n\n游侠不是被挑选出来的。他们靠自己证明。\n\n迷雾谷里有一只野兽……一只大猩猩，庞大、暴烈，倔强得像树皮。当地人叫他迷雾谷头领。我们则称他为你的第一个真正猎物。\n\n猎杀他。杀死他。剥下他的皮。\n\n然后把那张皮带给探索者公会的任何一名成员。\n\n要是他们没把你笑走，那就说明这张皮是真的。你也是。\n\n这不是荣耀。也不是正义。这是你道路上划下的第一刀。\n\n这张纸上会附有一张地图，标明你目标的位置。动作要快，免得丛林反过来吞了你。",dEN="You’ve opened what many could not.\n\nThat says something. Maybe enough. Maybe not.\n\nThis letter isn’t just a note, it’s a door. One we don’t open for just anyone.\n\nIf you’re reading this, your name’s on someone’s lips back at the Guild. Maybe whispered. Maybe cursed. But mentioned all the same. That means you're being watched... and tested.\n\nRangers aren’t picked. They prove themselves.\n\nThere’s a beast in Mistvale Valley... a gorilla, large, violent, stubborn as tree bark. Locals call him the Mistvale Alpha. We call him your first real mark.\n\nHunt him. Kill him. Skin his hide.\n\nThen bring that hide to any Ranger’s Guild associate.\n\nIf they don’t laugh you off, it means the hide’s real. And so are you.\n\nThis ain’t glory. It’s not justice. It’s the first cut on your path.\n\nOn this paper will contain a map to the location of your target. Move swiftly, before the jungle eats you instead.",o="杀死迷雾谷头领并取走它的皮。",oEN="Kill the Mistvale Alpha and collect its hide.",p="我希望你是带着好消息来的？",pEN="You have arrived with good news, I hope?",c="哎哟，哎哟……这张皮可不是迷雾谷随便哪只野兽的。\n\n厚实。布满伤疤。还带着山谷的腥臭。你找到他了。你把他放倒了。\n\n大多数人连头领的面都见不到。能活着撑过这一遭的更少。而能有头脑把他剥得干干净净、把证据一路带回来的，更是少之又少。但你做到了。\n\n这说明了一些事。\n\n我们不会轻易授予头衔，<name>。但这个？这足以把你的名字刻进名册。\n\n从今天起，你就是探索者公会的新兵了。\n\n等你体验过艾泽拉斯更多的风貌之后，尽快回来找我，<name>，我们再继续往下走。\n\n眼下，从这两件武器里挑一件吧。它们每一件都是你今日成就的纪念。",cEN="Well now… That hide didn’t come from just any Mistvale beast.\n\nThick. Scarred. Still carries the stink of the valley. You found him. You brought him down.\n\nMost never even see the Alpha. Fewer live through the attempt. And fewer still have the sense to skin him clean and carry proof all the way back. But you did.\n\nThat says something.\n\nWe don’t hand out titles lightly, <name>. But this? This gets your name etched into the ledger.\n\nFrom this day forward, you’re an Initiate of the Ranger’s Guild.\n\nReturn to me soon when you have experienced more of what Azeroth has to offer, <name>, and we will continue from there.\n\nFor now, choose one of these two weapons. Each of these serves as a momento of your accomplishments today."}
Q[200199]={d="啊，终于！我一直在等一位像我这样的<race>来继承这门令人艳羡的行当！\n\n……你很有胆量。我能感觉到，你是来向我求教的。今天确实有件简单的任务交给你，年轻的<class>。\n\n就在这间屋子里，有个侏儒正走向生命的尽头，吉罗索·疾闪。尽管一生充满冒险与成就，他却为自己即将到来的终结而愤懑。\n\n他会死去，暗影界会收走他的灵魂。但今天还不是他的日子。不过，我能感到他渴望离开这一界，却不清楚自己离去之后将面对什么。\n\n你也许没料到会是这样的任务，但我恳请你去看望他，与他聊聊。",dEN="Ahh, finally, I have awaited another <race> such as myself to pursue such an envious craft!\n\n...you are bold. I can sense you have come to me to learn. I do have a simple task for you today, young <class>.\n\nIn this very room is a gnome who is near his end, Gyrothor Turbospark. Despite a life full of adventure and fulfillment, he is bitter of his encroaching end.\n\nHe will die and the Shadowlands will claim him. But today is not his day. Yet, I can feel his yearning to leave this plane, but he is unaware of what lays before him once he is gone.\n\nYou may not have expected such a task, but I would humbly ask you to pay him a visit and have a chat.",c="你也许没料到会是这样的任务，<name>。但要明白，暗影界会召唤那些已经准备好的人，而知道何时收取灵魂，与收取灵魂本身同样重要。\n\n为了酬谢你帮助我们的朋友，我会奖励你这双靴子。愿它为你所用，它附有魔法，能让你在水面上行走。",cEN="You may not have expected such a task, <name>. But it is important to understand that the Shadowlands call for those who are ready, and knowing when to claim a soul can be just as important as the reclamation of the soul itself.\n\nFor helping our friend out here, I will reward you with these boots. May they serve you well, as they are enchanted to allow you to walk on the surface of water itself."}
Q[200255]={d="我能感觉到一股邪恶的存在。\n\n你也能感觉到，对吧？所以你才在最恰当的时刻来找我。\n\n这儿就有一个。一个女巫。阴翳，满怀邪恶与歹意。\n\n愿圣光祝福我们接下来要做的事。\n\n拿着，接过这支火把。她就在安威玛尔这儿，我已经把她的位置标在你的地图上。对她使用火把，揭露她的真身。杀了她。毫不留情。\n\n她被杀掉之后就回来找我。\n\n该死的女巫。",dEN="I can feel an evil presence.\n\nYou can feel it too, can't you? That is why you have come to me at the most opportune of times.\n\nThere is one here. A witch. Brooding with evil and malintent.\n\nMay the Light bless us for what we're about to do.\n\nHere, take this torch. She's here in Anvilmar and I've marked her location on your map. Use the torch on her to reveal her true self. Kill it. No mercy.\n\nReturn to me when it's been slain.\n\nDamned witches.",o="揭露女巫并杀死她。",oEN="Reveal the witch and kill her.",p="你回来了，哇！",pEN="You have returned, wow!",c="又一个邪恶生物被逐出了我们的世界。\n\n……然而。\n\n还有那么多等着被消灭。保持警觉。\n\n拿着，收下这些，让它们在你们对抗邪恶的战斗中指引你。",cEN="Yet another evil creature banished from our world.\n\n... and yet.\n\nStill so many others to destroy. Be vigilant.\n\nHere, take these, let them guide you in your battles with evil."}
Q[202566]={d="听好了，冒险者。每个佣兵和农夫都以为自己能挥剑，可守住一个阵地呢？那需要真正的骨气。湖畔镇能顶住兽人的侵袭好几个月，就是因为我们的卫兵懂得在关键时刻守住阵线。你想学我们这一套？那就证明你有这份胆识。无论如何都别擅离岗位。你一旦脱离队列，就算失败。我们的人民所依靠的，正是敌人冲锋时毫不迟疑的卫兵和斥候。",dEN="Listen here, adventurer. Every sellsword and farmhand thinks they can swing a sword, but defending a position? That takes real backbone. Lakeshire has stood against orc raids for months because our guards know how to hold the line when it matters. You want to learn what we know? Then prove you've got the spine for it. Don't you dare step away from that post, no matter what comes at you. The moment you break ranks, you've failed. Our people depend on guards and scouts who won't flinch when the enemy charges.",o="帮助斥候彼得守住他的岗位。",oEN="Help Scout Peter defend his post.",p="还撑得住？好。但先别松懈，下一波攻势会更猛。",pEN="Still holding? Good. But don’t relax yet, the next wave hits harder.",c="看来你守住了阵地。你没有退缩。这正是我爱看到的。也许你终究不只是一个普通佣兵。\n\n多亏了你，镇上的居民今晚能睡得更安稳些。你已在那些坚守阵线的人当中赢得了一席之地。\n\n拿着这个，就当是湖畔镇的一点敬意。但别让它冲昏了头。下一场战斗永远就在山脊那边。",cEN="So, you held your ground. Didn't flinch. That’s what I like to see. Maybe you’re not just another sellsword after all.\n\nThe townsfolk can sleep a little easier tonight, thanks to you. You’ve earned your place among those who stand the line.\n\nTake this, consider it a token of Lakeshire’s respect. But don’t let it go to your head. The next fight’s always just over the ridge."}
Q[202567]={d="听好了，新兵。挥刀是一回事。当死神的吐息贴着你脖子时还能守住阵地呢？那需要胆量。联盟的狗又推进到我们的土地上了。但他们会明白，面对绝不后退的战士是什么滋味。我们的哨站依然屹立，因为我们不计代价地守住阵线。你想在部落中赢得一席之地吗？那就证明你在战斗见血时不会崩溃。\n\n守住你的岗位。不要犹豫。不要失败。部落不需要懦夫。",dEN="Listen up, grunt. Swingin’ a blade is one thing. Holdin’ your ground when death’s breath is on your neck? That takes guts. The Alliance dogs have pushed into our lands again. But they’ll learn what it means to face warriors who don't back down. Our outpost still stands because we hold the line — no matter the cost. You want to earn your place among the Horde? Prove you won’t break when the fight turns bloody.\n\nStand your post. Don’t flinch. Don’t fail. The Horde has no use for cowards.",o="帮助卫兵洛拉克守住他的岗位。",oEN="Help Guard Lorak defend his post.",c="不错。在关键时刻你守住了阵地。在这地方，这可不是小事。\n\n你不只是泥地里又一把刀。你与部落并肩而立，没有退缩。",cEN="Not bad. You held your ground when it counted. That means something out here.\n\nYou are not just another blade in the dirt. You stood with the Horde and you did not falter."}
Q[207491]={d="霸主伦萨克在力量谷等你。\n\n<萨尔向你致意。>\n\n别让你的观众久等，英雄。",dEN="Overlord Runthak awaits your arrival in the Valley of Strength.\n\n<Thrall salutes you.>\n\nDo not keep your public waiting, hero.",o="去力量谷寻找霸主伦萨克。",oEN="Seek out Overlord Runthak in the Valley of Strength.",p="让我看看这个。",pEN="Let me see this.",c="选择你的奖赏，让你辉煌胜利的庆典开始吧。",cEN="Choose your reward and let the celebration of your glorious victory begin."}
Q[207496]={d="去英雄谷找马廷利少校，<name>。他正等着你……",dEN="Seek out Major Mattingly in the Valley of Heroes, <name>. He will be expecting you...",o="去英雄谷寻找马廷利少校。",oEN="Seek out Major Mattingly in the Valley of Heroes.",p="让我看看这个。",pEN="Let me see this.",c="<name>，能享有这般仪式的人寥寥无几。请选择你的奖赏，好让我们开始庆典。",cEN="Few are graced with such ceremony, <name>. Please, choose your reward so that we may begin the celebration."}
Q[207632]={d="叶片的表皮泛着浓烈的绿光。表面极其粗糙，露出许多叶脉与褶皱。\n\n要是让你猜，你会说这片叶子来自某种古老而强大的存在。\n\n也许你该去找这片叶子原本的主人？",dEN="The epidermis of the leaf glows a bright green. The surface is extremely rugose, exposing several veins and wrinkles.\n\nIf you had to take a guess, you would say this leaf came from something ancient and powerful.\n\nMaybe you should find the original owner of this leaf?",o="找到古老石化之叶的主人。祝你好运，<name>；这世界可大得很。",oEN="Find the owner of the Ancient Petrified Leaf. Good luck, <name>; It's a big world.",c="我当然认得自己的叶子。你看看！它保存得完好无损。\n\n你把它送回来，真是太客气了，<class>。\n\n也许你能为我们效力，我们也能为你效劳。",cEN="Of course I recognize my own leaves. Look at that! It's in perfect condition.\n\nHow good of you to return it, <class>.\n\nPerhaps you could be of service to us and we to you."}
Q[207782]={d="前往英雄谷，与元帅阿弗拉西亚比交谈。",dEN="Go to the Valley of Heroes and speak with Field Marshal Afrasiabi.",o="前往暴风城的英雄谷，与元帅阿弗拉西亚比交谈。",oEN="Venture to the Valley of Heroes in Stormwind City and speak with Field Marshal Afrasiabi.",p="你那儿拿着什么？让我看看。",pEN="What do you have there? Let me see.",c="<元帅阿弗拉西亚比鞠了一躬。>\n\n选择你的奖赏，让庆典开始吧！",cEN="<Field Marshal Afrasiabi bows.>\n\nChoose your reward, let the celebration begin!"}
Q[207784]={d="去力量谷寻找霸主伦萨克。",dEN="Seek out Overlord Runthak in the Valley of Strength.",o="在奥格瑞玛与霸主伦萨克交谈。他在力量谷等着你。",oEN="Speak with Overlord Runthak in Orgrimmar. He stands waiting for you in the Valley of Strength.",p="你那儿拿着什么？让我看看。",pEN="What do you have there? Let me see.",c="选择你的奖赏吧，好让我把这头野兽的脑袋挂起来，让所有人都看见。",cEN="Choose your reward so that I may mount the head of the beast for all to see."}
Q[207786]={d="你手捧容器时，能听到一声微弱的低语。\n\n\"把我……从这座……牢笼里……释放出来。\"\n\n\"两件将我们联结之物……\n\n以四者铸成的钢铁……\n精华……火焰之王。\"\n\n\"德米特里安……希利苏斯……\"",dEN="As you hold the vessel in your hand you can hear a faint whisper.\n\n\" Release me ... from this ... prison.\"\n\n\"Two that binds us ...\n\nsteel made of four ...\n\nessence ... firelord.\"\n\n\"Demitrian ... Silithus ...\"",o="要将逐风者桑德兰从他的牢笼中释放，你必须把重生容器、10 块元素之力和火焰之王精华交给希利苏斯的高级领主德米特里安。",oEN="To free Thunderaan the Windseeker from his prison, you must present the Vessel of Rebirth, 10 bars of Elementium, and the Essence of the Firelord to Highlord Demitrian in Silithus.",p="如有必要，就让整个世界屈服！",pEN="Bring the world to its knees if you must!",c="我连做梦都不敢预见这一天。\n\n看吧，凡人。\n\n看看那比存在本身更古老的存在！\n\n看看那曾与泰坦和神明都交过手的存在！\n\n站起来，我的主人！挣脱你的枷锁！",cEN="Even in dreams I did not dare foresee this day.\n\nBehold, mortal.\n\nBEHOLD HE WHO IS OLDER THAN EXISTENCE!\n\nBEHOLD HE WHO HAS FACED TITAN AND GOD ALIKE!\n\nRISE MY MASTER! BREAK FROM YOUR BONDS!"}
Q[207787]={d="你打败了逐风者。拿起那柄沉睡的剑刃，逼那卑鄙的骗子德米特里安用你为他的背叛所提供的材料，唤醒雷霆之怒。",dEN="You have defeated the Wind Seeker. Take the dormant blade and force the lying wretch, Demitrian, to use the materials you provided for his betrayal to wake Thunderfury.",o="把沉睡的御风之刃交给高级领主德米特里安。",oEN="Present the Dormant Wind Kissed Blade to Highlord Demitrian.",p="<德米特里安在你面前缩成一团。>",pEN="<Demitrian cowers in your presence.>",c="求你别伤害我！拿去吧！把剑刃拿去！让德米特里安重建他那可悲的人生吧！",cEN="Please do not harm me! Take it! Take the blade! Leave Demitrian to reshape his pathetic life!"}
Q[208184]={p="尽可能了解我们的敌人至关重要。如果你给我带来一些他们的器物，也许我能破译封印在符文中的古老力量，为我们所用。",pEN="It is of great importance to know as much as we can about our enemies. If you bring me some of their artefacts, I might be able to decrypt the ancient powers sealed within the runes to use to our advantage.",c="现在让我们看看……太棒了！我们的努力有了回报！我把这些符文抄录进了这份铭文。把它用在肩部装备上，以驾驭其中蕴含的古老力量。",cEN="Now let us see... splendid! Our efforts have paid off! I have copied these runes into this inscription. Use it on a piece of shoulder gear to harness the ancient powers embedded within."}
Q[208185]={p="尽可能了解我们的敌人至关重要。如果你给我带来一些他们的器物，也许我能破译封印在符文中的古老力量，为我们所用。",pEN="It is of great importance to know as much as we can about our enemies. If you bring me some of their artefacts, I might be able to decrypt the ancient powers sealed within the runes to use to our advantage.",c="现在让我们看看……太棒了！我们的努力有了回报！我把这些符文抄录进了这份铭文。把它用在肩部装备上，以驾驭其中蕴含的古老力量。",cEN="Now let us see... splendid! Our efforts have paid off! I have copied these runes into this inscription. Use it on a piece of shoulder gear to harness the ancient powers embedded within."}
