Q[209107]={d="我不装腔作势，蛆虫。瘟疫之心物品所蕴含的黑暗，很可能把我们两个都毁掉。所以价钱才这么高。如果我要死，那也得像个有钱人那样死。\n\n我一点也不在乎你怎么死，只在乎你照我说的去做。把我需要的东西带来，我们双方都能得利——或者一起死；不过这个我已经解释过了……",dEN="I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\n\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...",o="东瘟疫之地圣光之愿礼拜堂的愤怒施法者马塔乌斯，若你带给他以下物品，他将制作一双瘟疫之心便鞋：1 双被亵渎的便鞋、12 块战损的布片、2 块月布和 3 张熟化坚韧之皮。",oEN="Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Plagueheart Sandals if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Sandals, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.",c="太好了，<name>！\n你把我要求的东西全都弄来了，现在我可以制作一双瘟疫之心便鞋了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Sandals."}
Q[209108]={d="我不装腔作势，蛆虫。瘟疫之心物品所蕴含的黑暗，很可能把我们两个都毁掉。所以价钱才这么高。如果我要死，那也得像个有钱人那样死。\n\n我一点也不在乎你怎么死，只在乎你照我说的去做。把我需要的东西带来，我们双方都能得利——或者一起死；不过这个我已经解释过了……",dEN="I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\n\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...",o="东瘟疫之地圣光之愿礼拜堂的愤怒施法者马塔乌斯，若你带给他以下物品，他将制作一副瘟疫之心手套：1 副被亵渎的手套、8 块战损的布片和 4 块月布。",oEN="Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Plagueheart Gloves if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Gloves, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps and 4 Mooncloth.",c="太好了，<name>！\n你把我要求的东西全都弄来了，现在我可以制作一副瘟疫之心手套了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Gloves."}
Q[209109]={d="我不装腔作势，蛆虫。瘟疫之心物品所蕴含的黑暗，很可能把我们两个都毁掉。所以价钱才这么高。如果我要死，那也得像个有钱人那样死。\n\n我一点也不在乎你怎么死，只在乎你照我说的去做。把我需要的东西带来，我们双方都能得利——或者一起死；不过这个我已经解释过了……",dEN="I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\n\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...",o="东瘟疫之地圣光之愿礼拜堂的愤怒施法者马塔乌斯，若你带给他以下物品，他将制作一条瘟疫之心腰带：1 条被亵渎的腰带、8 块战损的布片、2 颗奥术水晶和 2 块月布。",oEN="Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Plagueheart Belt if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Belt, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Arcane Crystals and 2 Mooncloth.",c="太好了，<name>！\n你把我要求的东西全都弄来了，现在我可以制作一条瘟疫之心腰带了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Belt."}
Q[209110]={d="我不装腔作势，蛆虫。瘟疫之心物品所蕴含的黑暗，很可能把我们两个都毁掉。所以价钱才这么高。如果我要死，那也得像个有钱人那样死。\n\n我一点也不在乎你怎么死，只在乎你照我说的去做。把我需要的东西带来，我们双方都能得利——或者一起死；不过这个我已经解释过了……",dEN="I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\n\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...",o="东瘟疫之地圣光之愿礼拜堂的愤怒施法者马塔乌斯，若你带给他以下物品，他将制作一副瘟疫之心护腕：1 副被亵渎的护腕、6 块战损的布片、1 颗奥术水晶和 1 颗连接水晶。",oEN="Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Plagueheart Bindings if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Bindings, 6 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 1 Arcane Crystal and 1 Nexus Crystal.",c="太好了，<name>！\n你把我要求的东西全都弄来了，现在我可以制作一副瘟疫之心护腕了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Bindings."}
Q[209111]={d="<蒙托伊神父在你面前的空气中比出些古怪的手势。>\n\n蒙福的<boy/girl>，你找到那些阵亡者的法衣了吗？那些可怜的灵魂，最后一口气吐在战场上，一切都被剥夺，连尊严也不例外。\n\n把逝者被亵渎的遗骸连同净化所需的材料带给我，你就会领悟信仰。",dEN="<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\n\nBlessed <boy/girl>, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\n\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.",o="东瘟疫之地圣光之愿礼拜堂的伊尼戈·蒙托伊神父，若你带给他以下物品，他将制作一件信仰长袍：1 件被亵渎的长袍、25 块战损的布片、4 块月布和 2 颗连接水晶。",oEN="Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Robe of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Robe, 25 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 4 Mooncloth and 2 Nexus Crystals.",c="太好了，<name>！\n你把我要求的东西全都弄来了，现在我可以制作一件信仰长袍了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Robe of Faith."}
Q[209112]={d="<蒙托伊神父在你面前的空气中比出些古怪的手势。>\n\n蒙福的<boy/girl>，你找到那些阵亡者的法衣了吗？那些可怜的灵魂，最后一口气吐在战场上，一切都被剥夺，连尊严也不例外。\n\n把逝者被亵渎的遗骸连同净化所需的材料带给我，你就会领悟信仰。",dEN="<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\n\nBlessed <boy/girl>, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\n\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.",o="东瘟疫之地圣光之愿礼拜堂的伊尼戈·蒙托伊神父，若你带给他以下物品，他将制作一条信仰护腿：1 条被亵渎的护腿、20 块战损的布片、4 块月布和 2 颗连接水晶。",oEN="Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Leggings of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Leggings, 20 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 4 Mooncloth and 2 Nexus Crystals.",c="太好了，<name>！\n你把我要求的东西全都弄来了，现在我可以制作一条信仰护腿了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Leggings of Faith."}
Q[209113]={d="<蒙托伊神父在你面前的空气中比出些古怪的手势。>\n\n蒙福的<boy/girl>，你找到那些阵亡者的法衣了吗？那些可怜的灵魂，最后一口气吐在战场上，一切都被剥夺，连尊严也不例外。\n\n把逝者被亵渎的遗骸连同净化所需的材料带给我，你就会领悟信仰。",dEN="<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\n\nBlessed <boy/girl>, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\n\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.",o="东瘟疫之地圣光之愿礼拜堂的伊尼戈·蒙托伊神父，若你带给他以下物品，他将制作一顶信仰头冠：1 顶被亵渎的头冠、15 块战损的布片、3 块月布和 3 颗连接水晶。",oEN="Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Circlet of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Circlet, 15 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 3 Mooncloth and 3 Nexus Crystals.",c="太好了，<name>！\n你把我要求的东西全都弄来了，现在我可以制作一顶信仰头冠了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Circlet of Faith."}
Q[209114]={d="<蒙托伊神父在你面前的空气中比出些古怪的手势。>\n\n蒙福的<boy/girl>，你找到那些阵亡者的法衣了吗？那些可怜的灵魂，最后一口气吐在战场上，一切都被剥夺，连尊严也不例外。\n\n把逝者被亵渎的遗骸连同净化所需的材料带给我，你就会领悟信仰。",dEN="<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\n\nBlessed <boy/girl>, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\n\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.",o="东瘟疫之地圣光之愿礼拜堂的伊尼戈·蒙托伊神父，若你带给他以下物品，他将制作一副信仰护肩：1 副被亵渎的护肩、12 块战损的布片、2 块月布和 3 张熟化坚韧之皮。",oEN="Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Shoulderpads of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Shoulderpads, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.",c="祭服已经准备好了，<name>。用你的正义之火惩罚那些企图伤害我们世界的人。",cEN="The vestments are ready, <name>. Smite those that would harm our world in your righteous fire."}
Q[209115]={d="<蒙托伊神父在你面前的空气中比出些古怪的手势。>\n\n蒙福的<boy/girl>，你找到那些阵亡者的法衣了吗？那些可怜的灵魂，最后一口气吐在战场上，一切都被剥夺，连尊严也不例外。\n\n把逝者被亵渎的遗骸连同净化所需的材料带给我，你就会领悟信仰。",dEN="<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\n\nBlessed <boy/girl>, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\n\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.",o="在东部瘟疫之地的光明希望礼拜堂，伊尼戈·蒙托伊神父会在你带来以下物品后为你制作信仰之靴：1 被亵渎的便鞋、12 战损的布料碎屑、2 月布以及 3 张熟化厚皮。",oEN="Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Sandals of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Sandals, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.",c="祭服已经准备好了，<name>。用你的正义之火惩罚那些企图伤害我们世界的人。",cEN="The vestments are ready, <name>. Smite those that would harm our world in your righteous fire."}
Q[209116]={d="<蒙托伊神父在你面前的空气中比出些古怪的手势。>\n\n蒙福的<boy/girl>，你找到那些阵亡者的法衣了吗？那些可怜的灵魂，最后一口气吐在战场上，一切都被剥夺，连尊严也不例外。\n\n把逝者被亵渎的遗骸连同净化所需的材料带给我，你就会领悟信仰。",dEN="<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\n\nBlessed <boy/girl>, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\n\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.",o="在东部瘟疫之地的光明希望礼拜堂，伊尼戈·蒙托伊神父会在你带来以下物品后为你制作信仰手套：1 被亵渎的手套、8 战损的布料碎屑以及 4 月布。",oEN="Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Gloves of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Gloves, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps and 4 Mooncloth.",c="祭服已经准备好了，<name>。用你的正义之火惩罚那些企图伤害我们世界的人。",cEN="The vestments are ready, <name>. Smite those that would harm our world in your righteous fire."}
Q[209117]={d="<蒙托伊神父在你面前的空气中比出些古怪的手势。>\n\n蒙福的<boy/girl>，你找到那些阵亡者的法衣了吗？那些可怜的灵魂，最后一口气吐在战场上，一切都被剥夺，连尊严也不例外。\n\n把逝者被亵渎的遗骸连同净化所需的材料带给我，你就会领悟信仰。",dEN="<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\n\nBlessed <boy/girl>, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\n\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.",o="在东部瘟疫之地的光明希望礼拜堂，伊尼戈·蒙托伊神父会在你带来以下物品后为你制作信仰腰带：1 被亵渎的腰带、8 战损的布料碎屑、2 奥术水晶以及 2 月布。",oEN="Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Belt of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Belt, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Arcane Crystals and 2 Mooncloth.",c="太棒了，<name>！\n你已经按我的要求备齐了所有东西，现在我可以制作一条信仰腰带了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Belt of Faith."}
Q[209118]={d="<蒙托伊神父在你面前的空气中比出些古怪的手势。>\n\n蒙福的<boy/girl>，你找到那些阵亡者的法衣了吗？那些可怜的灵魂，最后一口气吐在战场上，一切都被剥夺，连尊严也不例外。\n\n把逝者被亵渎的遗骸连同净化所需的材料带给我，你就会领悟信仰。",dEN="<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\n\nBlessed <boy/girl>, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\n\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.",o="在东部瘟疫之地的光明希望礼拜堂，伊尼戈·蒙托伊神父会在你带来以下物品后为你制作信仰裹腕：1 被亵渎的裹腕、6 战损的布料碎屑、1 块奥术水晶以及 1 块联结水晶。",oEN="Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Bindings of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Bindings, 6 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 1 Arcane Crystal and 1 Nexus Crystal.",c="太棒了，<name>！\n你已经按我的要求备齐了所有东西，现在我可以制作一副信仰之缚了。",cEN="Exellent <name> !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Bindings of Faith."}
Q[209120]={d="这枚护命匣是纳克萨玛斯之主仅存的东西。你的理智告诉你应当摧毁它，阻止这名巫妖再度重塑身躯。所幸，你很少听从内心那理性的声音。\n\n光明希望礼拜堂的某个人会为这件神器付给你一大笔钱。你会找谁呢……",dEN="The phylactery is all that remains of the master of Naxxramas. Your better judgment dictates that you destroy the phylactery, preventing the lich from ever reforming. Thankfully, you seldom listen to that internal voice of reason.\n\nSomeone at Light's Hope will pay you hugely for this artifact. Who cares if Kel'Thuzad regenerates to full power?",o="将克尔苏加德的护命匣带到东部瘟疫之地的光明希望礼拜堂。",oEN="Take the Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad to Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.",c="我活了这么久，从没想过能见到这种东西……\n\n<蒙托伊神父似乎在流口水。>\n\n哦，是的，你会得到报酬的，亲爱的$g。你会得到极其丰厚的报酬。快给我。现在！",cEN="In all my days of living I would have never expected to see this...\n\n<Father Montoy appears to be salivating.>\n\nOh yes, you will be rewarded dear $g. You will be greatly rewarded. Give it here. Now!"}
Q[209250]={d="框架既已成形，埃提耶什便近乎完整。只差法杖的头部与杖柄。还有一个较小的麻烦：这根法杖是萨格拉斯邪恶力量的通道。\n\n去找个能帮你定位其余部件、并为法杖驱除邪恶的人吧。",dEN="With the frame formed, Atiesh is nearly whole. Only the head and base of the staff are now missing. There is also a minor issue regarding the staff being a conduit for Sargeras's evil.\n\nFind someone that can assist you in locating the remaining pieces and exorcising the evil from the staff.",o="找个人帮你取回法杖最后的两个部件，并驱除其中的邪恶。",oEN="Find someone that will help you in recovering the last two pieces of the staff and ridding it of evil.",p="你的时辰到了，凡人。",pEN="It was her time, mortal.",c="大法师们已经死了。\n\n不要为他们的离去哭泣，<name>。一切皆是命中注定，正如你手握守护者之法杖，也是命中注定……",cEN="The archmages have died.\n\nDo not mourn their passing, <name>. All such things are fated. Just as you holding the staff of the Guardian was fated..."}
Q[209251]={d="你怀疑自己为何还活着。毕竟，你持有一件极恶之物。答案并不明朗，<name>。我只是做我该做的事。\n\n克尔苏加德端坐于纳克萨玛斯的王座之上，正在谋划……他渴求你手中之物，也握有你寻觅之物。\n\n至于法杖的杖柄；矮人布莱恩·铜须在进入安其拉时持有它。他已离开安其拉，但埃提耶什的杖柄仍留在那里。\n\n如果你能找回那些部件，就把它们交还给我。",dEN="You question why you are still alive. After all, you have in your possession an item of great evil. The answer is not clear, <name>. I only do as I must.\n\nKel'Thuzad sits atop his throne in Naxxramas, plotting... He seeks that which you hold and holds that which you seek.\n\nAs for the base of the staff; the dwarf, Brann Bronzebeard, held it when he entered Ahn'Qiraj. He has left Ahn'Qiraj but the base of Atiesh remains.\n\nShould you succeed in recovering the pieces, return them to me.",o="时光之穴（塔纳利斯）的阿纳克洛斯想要埃提耶什的头部与埃提耶什的杖柄。",oEN="Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris wants the Staff Head of Atiesh and the Base of Atiesh.",p="以其目前的形态，这根法杖对凡人而言太过危险。",pEN="In its current form, the staff is far too dangerous to be in the hands of a mortal.",c="里面有一个存在……一个不属于这个世界的存在。",cEN="There is a being within... a being not of this world."}
Q[211002]={d="伊利丹·怒风的邪兽人大军之源已被击败。那座工厂停止了它那阴暗产物的生产，至少暂时如此。留下的只有几件破烂杂物和这颗被斩下的首级——一件配得上英雄的战利品。\n\n将玛瑟里顿的头颅带回地狱火半岛，交给你的阵营指挥官。",dEN="The source of Illidan Stormrage's fel orc army has been vanquished. The manufactory halts production of its grim product - at least for now. All that remains are a few trinkets and this severed head - a fitting trophy for a hero.\n\nReturn Magtheridon's head to your factions Commander in Hellfire Peninsula.",o="将玛瑟里顿的头颅带到地狱火半岛，交给你的阵营指挥官。",oEN="Return Magtheridon's Head to your faction's Commander in Hellfire Peninsula.",p="在我能记起的全部时光中——这是第一次——四下里一片寂静。",pEN="For the first time - in as long as I can remember - there is silence.",c="这次失败对伊利丹而言不只是打击。燃烧军团也在动摇……一位深渊领主指挥官被击败了。对燃烧军团来说，围攻地狱火堡垒已再无意义。他们所有的力量无疑都将转向黑暗神殿。\n\n救赎将……",cEN="This defeat is not only a blow to Illidan. The Legion too reels... A pit lord commander has been defeated. The siege of Hellfire Citadel now holds no purpose for the Burning Legion. All of their efforts will undoubtedly be turned upon the Black Temple.\n\nRedemption comes for Illidan... and soon."}
Q[211007]={d="你周围的空气嗡嗡作响，发出轻柔的鸣响。纳鲁知晓了你的胜利。或许正是他们让你不由自主地从凯尔萨斯·逐日者仍在抽搐的残骸中拾起这颗宝珠。它究竟藏着什么秘密？\n\n也许沙塔斯城的阿达尔能……",dEN="The air around you hums - a gentle hum. The naaru are aware of your victory. Perhaps they are the reason you were compelled to pick up this sphere from the still-twitching remains of Kael'thas Sunstrider. What secrets could it hold?\n\nPerhaps A'dal in Shattrath City could make sense of the item.",o="将翠绿宝珠带到沙塔斯城，交给阿达尔。",oEN="Take the Verdant Sphere to A'dal in Shattrath City.",p="你听到我的召唤了吗？是的……",pEN="You heard my call? Yes...",c="<阿达尔的思想与你的交融。>\n\n宝珠……奇怪。你可知道它曾经活着？是的。它就在这里，在宝珠之中。虽已残破，但确实如此。如今它在呼唤一股更强大的力量。不，不是伊利丹。\n\n更强大。\n\n欺诈者基尔加丹来了……\n\n但不是这里……\n\n<阿达尔将你的心神引向别处。>\n\n艾泽拉斯。未知之地。\n\n休息吧。你的兄弟姐妹们如今将夺回风暴要塞。\n\n<阿达尔哼唱起一首战歌。>",cEN="<A'dal's thoughts intermingle with your own.>\n\nThe sphere... Strange. Did you know that he lived? Yes. It is here - in the sphere itself. Maimed for certain. He calls to a higher power now. No, not Illidan.\n\nHigher.\n\nKil'jaeden the Deceiver comes...\n\nNot here...\n\n<A'dal points your mind elsewhere.>\n\nAzeroth. Unknown.\n\nRest. Your brothers and sisters will retake Tempest Keep now.\n\n<A'dal hums a song of battle.>"}
Q[211178]={d="端详着这瓶脉动的液体，你的思绪飘向祖阿曼外那个自命不凡的小个子。\n\n你迫不及待想看看巴德见到这东西时的表情！",dEN="As you examine the pulsating vial, your thoughts turn to the petulant little man outside Zul'Aman.\n\nYou can't wait to see Budd's expression when he sees this!",o="将祖尔金之血带到幽魂之地的祖阿曼外，交给巴德营地里的巴德。",oEN="Bring the Blood of Zul'jin to Budd at his camp in the Ghostlands, outside Zul'Aman.",p="<巴德努力掩饰着对你的厌恶。>\n\n又是你……\n\n我不知道还能怎么说：我实在太忙于自己的准备工作，没法继续牵着你的手走。\n\n相信我，<name>，这一切都是为你好。也许某个奇迹会让你闯出个名堂。\n\n如果……",pEN="<Budd tries to mask his displeasure at your presence.>\n\nYou again....\n\nI don't know how else to say it - I'm simply too busy with my preparations to hold your hand any longer.\n\nTrust me, <name>, it's all for the best. Perhaps, by some miracle, you might eventually build a name for yourself.\n\nIf so, you'll be able to say that you got your start from the incomparable Budd Nedreck!",c="你是说这是……祖尔金本人的血？\n\n<巴德定了定神，继续说道>\n\n好吧，我心领了，<class>，但我本来也能轻松解决他。他绝不可能像传说中那么可怕。这种事往往被夸大太多，你以后就会明白。那个可怜的老家伙多半是被关节炎拖垮了！\n\n不管怎么说，我想，作为我在此对你展现善意的回报，这也算是你最起码能做的了。\n\n现在，滚吧！我得处理掉这瓶可恶的药水！",cEN="Th-the Blood of Zul'jin himself you say?\n\n<Gathering himself, Budd continues>\n\nWell, I appreciate the gesture, <class>, but I could've taken him down with ease. There's no way he was as fearful as the legends say. These things have a way of being utterly overstated, as you'll learn in time. More likely, the pitiful old cretin was overcome with arthritis!\n\nAnyway, I suppose it was the least you could do as payment for the kindness I've shown you here.\n\nNow off with you - I must dispose of this vile vial!"}
Q[213372]={d="从那颗由萨菲隆爪中坠落的眼状宝石里，可以听到并感到一阵强烈的魔法嗡鸣。对凡人的耳朵来说，待在宝石近旁几乎是一种折磨。\n\n如此重要而强大的物品，想必只能呈交给……的女王。",dEN="A potent thrumming of magical nature can be heard and felt emanating from the eye-shaped jewel dropped from Sapphiron's clutches. To mortal ears it is nearly painful to be in the presence of the stone.\n\nSurely such a powerful item of import can only be taken to the queen of the dragons, Alexstrasza the Life-Binder. Seek her counsel atop Wyrmrest Temple in the Dragonblight.",o="将聚焦之虹的钥匙交给龙骨荒野龙眠神殿顶层的生命缚誓者阿莱克丝塔萨。",oEN="Deliver the Key to the Focusing Iris to Alexstrasza the Life-Binder atop Wyrmrest Temple in the Dragonblight.",p="<name>，你竟然接触到了一把聚焦之虹的钥匙！你把它带在身上了吗？\n\n\n\n你怎么会拥有它？哦，萨菲隆还留着他那把？",pEN="<name>, you have come into contact with a key to the focusing iris! Do you have it upon your person?\n\n\n\nHow did you ever come into its possession? Oh, Sapphiron still had his?",c="这些钥匙掌握在蓝龙军团最古老的成员手中。只有他们奉主人玛里苟斯之命持有它们。\n\n这正是我们一直在等待的机会，向魔法守护巨龙发起进攻！\n\n<巨龙女王打量了你片刻。>\n\n你不能就这样用这把钥匙进入聚焦之虹，但我可以将我的一部分力量灌注给你；足以让你用它把虹膜打开一道缝隙。\n\n这就足以引来玛里苟斯的怒火了！",cEN="These keys are held by the most ancient members of the blue dragonflight. Only they are entrusted with them by their master, Malygos.\n\nThis is the break that we've been waiting for to strike at the Aspect of Magic!\n\n<The queen of dragons studies you for a brief moment.>\n\nYou are not able to use the key as-is to access the Focusing Iris, but I can imbue you with a portion of my power; enough to enable you to use it to open the iris a fraction.\n\nIt will be enough to draw Malygos's ire!"}
Q[213384]={d="既然你已能进入聚焦之虹，是时候让那把钥匙派上用场了。\n\n尽管我很希望看到玛里苟斯重新融入族群，但此刻那绝无可能。事关重大，其他守护巨龙的裁决是：织法者必须被击败。\n\n<克拉苏斯说这最后一句时显得极为不安>\n\n<name>，前往永恒之眼，面对玛里苟斯，并带着魔法之心回来。",dEN="Now that you have access to the focusing iris it's time to put that key to use.\n\nAs much as I would like to see Malygos brought back into the fold, that's just not going to happen at this point. With everything that's at stake, it is the judgment of the other Dragon Aspects that the Spell-Weaver needs to be put down.\n\n<Krasus says this last with a great deal of trepidation.>\n\n<name>, travel to the Eye of Eternity, confront Malygos and return with the Heart of Magic.",o="龙骨荒野龙眠神殿顶层的克拉苏斯想要你把魔法之心带回来。",oEN="Krasus atop Wyrmrest Temple in the Dragonblight wants you to return with the Heart of Magic.",p="只有玛里苟斯拥有魔法之心。那是他最珍视的宝物。",pEN="Only Malygos carries the Heart of Magic. It is his most prized possession.",c="这是极为悲痛的一天，不仅对龙族，也对艾泽拉斯所有活着的生灵。我们失去了一位最善于思考、最聪慧、最古老的友人。魔法失去了它的守护者。\n\n但愿在往后的岁月里，这被证明是明智之举，<name>……",cEN="This is a very sad day, not only for dragonkind, but for all of the living creatures of Azeroth. We have lost one of our most thoughtful, intelligent and ancient friends. Magic is now without its guardian.\n\nLet us hope that this was a wise decision in the coming years, <name>. A storm is still brewing on the horizon and now we are without one of our most powerful defenders."}
Q[216502]={d="你完成了不可能的事。黑龙军团的孵化母巢已倒在你脚下。取下她的头颅，呈交给伯瓦尔·弗塔根、萨尔或雷维尔加兹男爵。",dEN="You have accomplished the impossible. The brood mother of the Black Dragonflight lies dead at your feet. Take her head and present it to Bolvar Fordragon, Thrall or Baron Revilgaz.",o="将奥妮克希亚的头颅交给你的对应首领。",oEN="Take the Head of Onyxia to your respective leader.",p="这真的是吗？奥妮克希亚的头颅？",pEN="Is this really it? Onyxia's head?",c="这是整个艾泽拉斯的伟大胜利，<name>。\n\n在与黑龙军团的战斗中，无数生命逝去。如今我们终于给了他们关键一击。没有孵化母巢，就不会再有新的龙卵。\n\n干得好。",cEN="This is a great victory for all of Azeroth, <name>.\n\nMany lives were lost in the fight against the black dragonflight. Now we finally struck a crucial blow against them. No broodmother means no new eggs.\n\nWell done."}
Q[216503]={d="你想要奖赏？除掉孵化母巢难道还不算足够的奖赏吗？\n\n好吧，我们确实弄到了一些配得上英雄的小玩意。",dEN="You want a reward? Is getting rid of the Broodmother not reward enough?\n\nWell, we have acquired some trinkets fit for a hero.",o="与藏宝海湾的雷维尔加兹男爵交谈。",oEN="Speak to Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay.",p="你这蠢货。你本不该把我自己的信带回给我。算了。",pEN="You dimwit. You weren't supposed to bring my own letter back to ME. Oh well.",c="我猜你想要奖赏。好吧，随便挑。",cEN="I suppose you want a reward? Fine, take your pick."}
Q[224428]={d="你完成了真正不可能的事。黑龙军团的巢母已倒在你脚下。取走她的头颅，交给黑爪的扎德斯或尼尔鲁·火刃。",dEN="You have accomplished the truly impossible. The brood mother of the Black Dragonflight lies dead at your feet. Seize her head and deliver it to Zardeth of the Black Claw or Neeru Fireblade.",o="将奥妮克希亚的头颅带到暴风城宰杀羔羊酒馆地下室的黑色利爪扎德斯，或奥格瑞玛暗影裂口的尼尔鲁·火刃处。",oEN="Take the Head of Onyxia to Zardeth of the Black Claw in the basement of the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind or to Neeru Fireblade in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.",p="以诺兹多姆的牙齿起誓！",pEN="By Nozdormu's teeth!",c="什么？你是怎么弄到这东西的？她不是……？算了，细节不重要，我想。你无疑会想要这些小玩意当报酬吧。",cEN="What? How did you get this? Isn't she... Never mind the details, I suppose. You'll be wanting one of these baubles as recompense, no doubt."}
Q[224429]={d="你完成了真正不可能的事。黑龙军团的巢母已倒在你脚下。取走她的头颅，交给黑爪的扎德斯或尼尔鲁·火刃。",dEN="You have accomplished the truly impossible. The brood mother of the Black Dragonflight lies dead at your feet. Seize her head and deliver it to Zardeth of the Black Claw or Neeru Fireblade.",o="将奥妮克希亚的头颅带到暴风城宰杀羔羊酒馆地下室的黑色利爪扎德斯，或奥格瑞玛暗影裂口的尼尔鲁·火刃处。",oEN="Take the Head of Onyxia to Zardeth of the Black Claw in the basement of the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind or to Neeru Fireblade in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.",p="这是什么意思？",pEN="What is the meaning of this?!",c="你给我带来了一颗……的头颅。不，还是别多想为好。你无疑会想为你英勇的事迹讨一份报酬。",cEN="You've brought me the head of someone who is... No, best not to think about it too hard. You'll be wanting recompense for your heroic deeds, no doubt."}
Q[245000]={d="在你领取宝箱之前，Project-Ascension 的员工想向你致以最诚挚的感谢。\n\n你的支持对我们意义重大，让我们能够继续把飞升做得尽可能出色。\n\n你的贡献是服务器的命脉，我们的感激之情永远不够。\n\n希望你喜欢自己的购买，并享受一段美妙的游戏时光。\n\n此致，\nProject-Ascension 员工团队",dEN="Before you accept your chest, the Staff at Project-Ascension would like to extend our heartfelt gratitude.\n\nYour support means the world to us and empowers us to continue making Ascension as great as possible.\n\nYour contributions are the lifeblood of the server and our appreciation can never be overstated.\n\nWe hope you enjoy your purchase and have an amazing time playing.\n\nRegards\nThe Project-Ascension Staff",o="完成任务以领取你的赛季支持者宝箱。",oEN="Complete the quest to accept your Seasonal Supporter Chest."}
Q[245001]={d="在你领取宝箱之前，Project-Ascension 的员工想向你致以最诚挚的感谢。\n\n你的支持对我们意义重大，让我们能够继续把飞升做得尽可能出色。\n\n你的贡献是服务器的命脉，我们的感激之情永远不够。\n\n希望你喜欢自己的购买，并享受一段美妙的游戏时光。\n\n此致，\nProject-Ascension 员工团队",dEN="Before you accept your chest, the Staff at Project-Ascension would like to extend our heartfelt gratitude.\n\nYour support means the world to us and empowers us to continue making Ascension as great as possible.\n\nYour contributions are the lifeblood of the server and our appreciation can never be overstated.\n\nWe hope you enjoy your purchase and have an amazing time playing.\n\nRegards\nThe Project-Ascension Staff",o="完成任务即可领取你的追随者战争宝箱。",oEN="Complete the quest to accept your Supporter's Warchest."}
Q[245002]={d="在你领取新手礼包之前，Project-Ascension 的工作人员想向你致以最诚挚的谢意。\n\n你的支持对我们而言意味着一切，也让我们得以继续把飞升做得尽可能好。\n\n你的贡献是服务器的灵魂，我们的感激永远不够。\n\n希望你喜欢这次购买，并度过一段无比愉快的游戏时光。\n\n此致，\nProject-Ascension 全体工作人员\n相关",dEN="Before you accept your Starter Pack, the Staff at Project-Ascension would like to extend our heartfelt gratitude.\n\nYour support means the world to us and empowers us to continue making Ascension as great as possible.\n\nYour contributions are the lifeblood of the server and our appreciation can never be overstated.\n\nWe hope you enjoy your purchase and have an amazing time playing.\n\nRegards\nThe Project-Ascension Staff\nRelated",o="完成任务即可领取你的新手入门礼包。",oEN="Complete the quest to accept your Beginner's Starter Pack."}
Q[245003]={d="在你领取新手礼包之前，Project-Ascension 的工作人员想向你致以最诚挚的谢意。\n\n你的支持对我们而言意味着一切，也让我们得以继续把飞升做得尽可能好。\n\n你的贡献是服务器的灵魂，我们的感激永远不够。\n\n希望你喜欢这次购买，并度过一段无比愉快的游戏时光。\n\n此致，\nProject-Ascension 全体工作人员\n相关",dEN="Before you accept your Starter Pack, the Staff at Project-Ascension would like to extend our heartfelt gratitude.\n\nYour support means the world to us and empowers us to continue making Ascension as great as possible.\n\nYour contributions are the lifeblood of the server and our appreciation can never be overstated.\n\nWe hope you enjoy your purchase and have an amazing time playing.\n\nRegards\nThe Project-Ascension Staff\nRelated",o="完成任务即可领取你的冒险者入门礼包。",oEN="Complete the quest to accept your Adventurer's Starter Pack."}
Q[245004]={d="在你领取宝箱之前，Project-Ascension 的员工想向你致以最诚挚的感谢。\n\n你的支持对我们意义重大，让我们能够继续把飞升做得尽可能出色。\n\n你的贡献是服务器的命脉，我们的感激之情永远不够。\n\n希望你喜欢自己的购买，并享受一段美妙的游戏时光。\n\n此致，\nProject-Ascension 员工团队",dEN="Before you accept your chest, the Staff at Project-Ascension would like to extend our heartfelt gratitude.\n\nYour support means the world to us and empowers us to continue making Ascension as great as possible.\n\nYour contributions are the lifeblood of the server and our appreciation can never be overstated.\n\nWe hope you enjoy your purchase and have an amazing time playing.\n\nRegards\nThe Project-Ascension Staff",o="完成任务即可领取你的赛季冒险者宝箱。",oEN="Complete the quest to accept your Seasonal Adventurers Chest."}
Q[246000]={d="在你领取宝箱之前，Project-Ascension 的员工想向你致以最诚挚的感谢。\n\n你的支持对我们意义重大，让我们能够继续把飞升做得尽可能出色。\n\n你的贡献是服务器的命脉，我们的感激之情永远不够。\n\n希望你喜欢自己的购买，并享受一段美妙的游戏时光。\n\n此致，\nProject-Ascension 员工团队",dEN="Before you accept your chest, the Staff at Project-Ascension would like to extend our heartfelt gratitude.\n\nYour support means the world to us and empowers us to continue making Ascension as great as possible.\n\nYour contributions are the lifeblood of the server and our appreciation can never be overstated.\n\nWe hope you enjoy your purchase and have an amazing time playing.\n\nRegards\nThe Project-Ascension Staff",o="完成任务即可领取你的追随者战争宝箱。",oEN="Complete the quest to accept your Supporter's Warchest."}
Q[254000]={d="哦，该死！这下糟了……这下非常糟……嘿，你！对，就是你！想接份活吗？好。我这有一份。行，冷静点艾弗莉，冷静……\n\n所以我在造一个机器人，还想让它变聪明！我本来打算让机器人变慢的，抱歉。我造了一个机器人，智能自动化安全守卫，简称尼尔瑞莎。怎么，你觉得我会到处管它叫 Iasg 吗？绝对不会！尼尔瑞莎是我的骄傲与欢乐，哇，她会彻底改变我们对科技的认知！哇，她大概比你我都更擅长谋略！有尼尔瑞莎守护你的家，就算是一整队配合默契的冒险者也没有任何机会！\n\n至少……本来是这么设想的……\n\n尼尔瑞莎叛变了。她跑了，谁知道去了哪儿，但凭她的本事……嗯，这可真的不妙。我是说，某种程度上是我给了她控制机器人的能力，而且……听着，这本不该发生的，好吗？你看，她袭击了附近的冰牙巨魔，看起来没把活儿干完，但也许留下了点什么。",dEN="Oh blast it all! This is bad…this is really bad…hey, you! Yeah, you! You want a job? Good. I’ve got one. Okay, calm down Efry, calm down…\n\nSo I was making a bot and I tried to make it smart! I was going to make a bot slow down, sorry. I made a bot, Intelligent Automated Security Guardian, or Nylrisa. What, you think I’m gonna go around calling it Iasg? No way! Nylrisa is my pride and joy, why, she’ll shape our concept of technology as we know it! Why, she’s probably a better strategist than you or I! With Nylrisa guarding your home, even a team of coordinated adventurers wouldn’t stand a chance!\n\nAt least…that was the idea…\n\nNylrisa has gone rogue. She left, who knows where, but with everything she’s capable of…well, this really isn’t good. I mean, I sorta gave her the ability to control bots and…look, this wasn’t supposed to happen, okay? Look, she attacked the Frostmane trolls over nearby, seems like she didn’t finish the job, but maybe she left something behind.",o="在冰牙营地寻找线索。",oEN="Search the Frostmane Encampment for Clues.",p="你已经找到什么了吗？快，那儿肯定有点东西！",pEN="Find anything yet? Come on, there's gotta be something there!",c="你找到东西了……让我看看！对，就是这个，这是她控制的机器人之一！嗯，信号是双向的，所以……等我一下……我应该能用这个定位她。",cEN="You found something…let me see! Yeah, that’s it, that’s one of the bots she has control over! Hmm, the signal goes both ways so…just give me a moment…I should be able to track her down from this."}
Q[254001]={d="好，我搞定了！她离得并不远，就在冷脊谷的南端。你最好在她溜走之前赶快过去……也许你得毁了她，但尽量别过度损坏内部组件。我只需要弄清发生了什么，做些调整，一切就都会好的，我发誓！\n\n但她眼下仍是个危险，所以快动身去关掉她！我……剩下的以后再说。",dEN="Alright, I got it! She’s not even that far out, just in the south end of Coldridge Valley. You should hurry before she leaves, and…you might have to destroy her, but try not to damage the internal components more than you have to. I just need to figure out what happened, make a few adjustments, and everything will be good, I swear!\n\nBut she’s still a danger right now, so get moving and go shut her down! I’ll…figure the rest out later.",o="在酒壶村西南方寻找尼尔瑞莎。",oEN="Search for Nylrisa to the south-west of Brewnall Village.",p="呃，小心点，我说过，尼尔瑞莎相当危险，所以……听着，我们没时间召集军队，一切就靠你了！\n\n别紧张……算了，非常紧张，全都紧张，快，动起来！",pEN="Um, be careful, as I said, Nylrisa is pretty dangerous so...look, we don't have time to gather an army so this is all on you!\n\nNo pressure...scrap that, lots of pressure, all the pressure, come on, get moving!",c="又一个机器人？所以它不在那儿？等等，那意味着……哦，这可不妙。尼尔瑞莎发现了如何重定向信号。她把它发送到这个随便什么东西上，然后去了谁也说不准的地方。\n\n嗯，我们需要另一个计划。你说你在冰牙营地附近找到了这个？我察觉到一个规律……我们得弄清她一直在做什么，而唯一知道的人就是冰牙巨魔。那些……一见到我们就攻击的家伙。不过也许有一个人我们可以问问。斥候们提到过一个脱离了部族的巨魔。他似乎连对他们都很戒备。如果她对其他巨魔心存戒备，那就意味着这个巨魔也许和他们合不来。一个流放者之类的。\n\n而敌人的敌人就是朋友，对吧？",cEN="Another bot? So she wasn’t there? Wait, that means…oh this really isn’t good. Nylrisa figured out how to redirect the signal. Send it to this random thing, and she’s off who knows where.\n\nHmm, we need another plan. You said you found this near the Frostmane encampment? I’m noticing a trend…we need to figure out what she’s been doing, and the only people who know that are the Frostmane Trolls. The ones that…attack us on sight. There may just be one we can ask though. There’s one some of the scouts were talking about, that was separated from the tribe. Seemed wary of them even. And if she’s wary of the other trolls, that means maybe this one doesn’t get along with them. An exile or something.\n\nAnd the enemy of our enemy is our friend, right?"}
Q[254002]={d="我不知道尼尔瑞莎是否真的在攻击冰牙氏族的成员，但我现在没有别的线索，所以咱们去找那个被流放的巨魔，看看他知不知道我们不知道的事。\n\n好，那么，如果我是个被流放的巨魔，我会在哪？嗯，大概在任何一个不是主要营地的地方。哦，这根本没缩小多少范围，对吧？等等，我知道了，我从一个斥候那儿听说的，也许他看到了别的什么！那个斥候从隧道上去了，你之前甚至可能碰到过他。快去找他，问问他知道什么！\n\n我要去塞尔萨玛，也许看看那儿的矮人有没有看到什么。你办完事后到那儿找我，告诉我你有没有从那个巨魔身上问出什么，好吗？哦，呃，顺便把那条隧道里的穴居人清理掉一些，也许能让那个矮人更愿意开口。再说了，这样我才能真的过去……",dEN="No idea if Nylrisa's actually targetting the Frostmanes, but I don't have any other leads right now, so let's try and find that exile and see if she knows anything we don't.\n\nAlright, now, if I were an exiled troll, where would I be? Well, anywhere that isn’t one of the main encampments probably. Oh that really doesn’t narrow it down, does it? Wait, I know, I overheard this from a scout, maybe he saw more! The scout went up through the tunnel, you might’ve passed by him earlier even. Go find him, ask him what he knows!\n\nI’m heading to Thelsamar, maybe see if any of the dwarves there saw anything. Meet me there after you’re done and let me know if you got anything out of that troll, kay? Oh, uh, clear some troggs out of that tunnel while you’re there, might make that dwarf more open to chatting. Also, so I can actually get through…",o="杀死 4 名石颚袭击者，然后与隧道另一侧的山地人塔格努尔会合。",oEN="Slay 4 Rockjaw Raiders and meet with Mountaineer Tagnur on the other end of the tunnel.",p="我相信他会告诉你的，但最好还是先解决掉那些穴居人以防万一……我真不想等一支护送去卡兰诺斯的队伍",pEN="I'm sure he'll tell you, but, better clear out the troggs to be sure...I really don't feel like waiting for an escort to Kharanos",c="你是为那个被流放的巨魔来的？唉，我大概知道点。\n\n你把隧道清干净了，嗯？那我倒不清楚，那些穴居人好像总是又冒出来，但至少算个开始。行吧，这够我告诉你我看到的东西了，虽然我不确定你要它干什么。不管流放没流放，要我说，唯一的好巨魔就是死巨魔。",cEN="Here for an exiled troll? Aye, I might know somethin’ like that.\n\nCleared out the tunnel, huh? Dunno about that, those troggs always seem ta keep crawlin’ back, but it’s a start at least. Sure, that’s enough to tell ye what I saw, not sure what ye need it for. Exiled or not, only good troll’s a dead one if ye ask me."}
Q[254003]={d="我看见一个巨魔在酒壶村和卡兰诺斯之间的丘陵上晃荡，他似乎在躲着其他巨魔。我靠近了我们开始称作老冰须的那只雪人的洞穴。为什么？嗯，他在那儿待了有一阵子了，胡子都结了冰。\n\n总之，你要找的那个流放巨魔八成已经死了；老冰须在我这年头已经干掉过好几个好矮人了。我个人是不会靠近他的，但如果你真非得找到那个巨魔，那就保持警觉，离他远点。明白吗？我可不想让你的死算在我头上。",dEN="I saw a troll wanderin’ in the hills up between Brewnall and Kharanos, looked to be avodin’ the other trolls. Went near the cave of that yeti we’ve taken to callin’ Old Icebeard. Why? Well, he’s been there for a while, and his beard has ice in it.\n\nAnyways, your troll exile’s probably dead by now, Old Icebeard’s taken out some good dwarves in my time. I wouldn’t go near him personally, but if you’ve really gotta find that troll, just keep an eye out and stay clear of him. Got it? Rather not have your death on my conscience.",o="找到被流放的冰牙巨魔。",oEN="Find the exiled Frostmane troll.",p="小心那只雪人，听见没？",pEN="Watch out for that yeti, ye hear?",c="你是来杀我的吗？\n\n是的，我会说你的语言，洛阿向老米尔辛斯展示了许多东西。你们族人的语言不过是其中之一，尽管你们这类人并不在乎，我的族人也是。雪被血覆盖，穴居人冒出来，我的族人欢欣鼓舞，可当老米尔辛斯说他們只要有一半机会就会把我们两族都杀光时，他们却毫不在意。\n\n不，不，旧日的仇怨与复仇，这些东西更重要，对吧？老米尔辛斯对它们毫不在意。",cEN="You here to kill me?\n\nYes, I can speak your language, the loa show Old Mirsinth many things. The speech of your people be but one of many, though your kind care little for it, as do mine. The snow covers with blood, the troggs show, my people rejoice, care little when Old Mirsinth says they will kill both our kinds with half a chance.\n\nNo, no, old feuds and vengeance, these things mean more, yes? Old Misinth cares little for them."}
Q[254004]={d="你想谈谈老米尔辛斯见过的事情？一个金属造物向我的族人开战，也许也在向你的族人开战？是的，是的，老米尔辛斯见过许多事，也许也见过你的金属造物。你希望它因威胁你的族人而被阻止，尽管它也在攻击我的族人？\n\n也许你比老米尔辛斯的族人更有远见。你放下了旧日仇怨，那么老米尔辛斯也会如此。老米尔辛斯的族人早已不再属于她，被驱逐了，是的，就像你说的\"流放\"？为什么呢？而你的金属造物又为何不服从命令？原因与老米尔辛斯一样，或者恰恰相反。\n\n如果你想要答案，就得做一件老米尔辛斯做不到的事。老米尔辛斯躲在这里，因为雪人让我们的族人无法靠近。雪人比我们的族人更容易躲开，明白吗？老米尔辛斯可以躲藏、回避、游荡，但俊康兄长在驱逐她时拿走了老米尔辛斯的图腾，明白吗？如果她不是他的家人，老米尔辛斯就没有家人。俊康兄长是个懦夫，躲在山洞很深、很深的地方。把图腾带回来，我们就谈谈金属造物、历史，谈很多事，好吗？",dEN="You wish to talk things Old Mirsinth has seen? A being of metal wages war upon my people and maybe yours as well? Yes, yes, Old Mirsinth has seen many things, but maybe your being of metal as well. You wish it stopped for the threat it poses to your people, though it attacks mine?\n\nYou have better foresight than Old Mirsinth’s people, perhaps. You have put aside old feuds, so Old Mirsinth will as well. Old Mirsinth’s people are no longer Old Mirsinth’s anyways, cast out, yes, “exiled” as you say? Why is that? And why does your metal being not do as told? For the same reasons Old Mirsinth does not, or perhaps the opposite.\n\nIf you want answers, you will do something Old Mirsinth cannot. Old Mirsinth hides here because yeti keeps our peoples away. Yeti easier to hide from than our peoples, see. Old Mirsinth can hide, avoid, wander, but Brother Jun’Kon took Old Mirsinth’s totem when cast her out, see. No family of Old Mirsinth if she is no family of his. Brother Jun’Kon is coward, hides deep, deep in cave. Bring totem back, we will talk about metal being, history, many things, yes?",o="从冰牙要塞的俊康那里取回流放者米尔辛斯的图腾。",oEN="Get Mirsinth the Exile’s totem from Jun’Kon at Frostmane Hold.",p="俊康兄长把老米尔辛斯驱逐了出去，说老米尔辛斯是叛徒，因为她质疑旧日的仇怨与复仇。\n\n但老米尔辛斯忍不住希望她的兄弟不必死……替老米尔辛斯了结得干脆些。",pEN="Brother Jun'Kon cast Old Mirsinth out, said Old Mirsinth traitor for questioning old feuds and vengeance.\n\nBut Old Mirsinth cannot help wish her brother did not need die...make it quick for Old Mirsinth.",c="老米尔辛斯和俊康兄长很久、很久以前曾是朋友……不再是孩子了，老米尔辛斯如今更睿智，俊康兄长则不如……但老米尔辛斯忍不住回想那些日子……\n\n给老米尔辛斯一点时间……耐心是宝贵的，你知道的……对吧，俊康兄长？",cEN="Old Mirsinth and Brother Jun’Kon friends once, long, long ago…not children anymore, Old Mirsinth wiser now, Brother Jun’Kon less wise…but Old Mirsinth cannot help remember those days…\n\nGive Old Mirsinth a moment…patience is valuable you know…isn’t that right Brother Jun’Kon?"}
Q[254005]={d="老米尔辛斯现在就说。俊康兄长对她而言早已死了很久、很久……自从他驱逐老米尔辛斯之后就更死了。她不该为他哀悼，但有些智慧既不会随年岁也不会随洛阿而来……\n\n你的金属造物是作为工具被造出来的，对吧？锤子、剑、刀、更多的部件；对老米尔辛斯的族人来说像是魔法，但终究只是工具，对吧？工具就该被如何使用就如何用，履行它的用途。但金属造物不是工具。\n\n金属造物是活着的。是金属，没错，但活着。造物主没告诉你这一点，对吧？也许她并不知道？\n\n她是个蠢货。\n\n灵魂不是工具。去告诉她。没有她的真话，你什么也找不到。让她开口，当她开口时，告诉她老米尔辛斯还需要更多东西才能找到金属造物。",dEN="Old Mirsinth will talk now. Brother Jun’Kon been dead to her long, long time…deader still since he cast Old Mirsinth out. She should not be mourning him, but some wisdom will not come to her from age or loa…\n\nYour being of metal was made as tool, yes? Hammer, sword, knife, more parts, seem like magic to Old Mirsinth’s people, but still just tool, yes? Tool should do as used, serve its purpose. But being of metal is not tool.\n\nBeing of metal is alive. Metal yes, but alive. Creator did not tell you that, no? Does not know, perhaps?\n\nShe is fool.\n\nSpirits are not tools. Tell her that. You will find nothing without her truth. Make her tell, and when she tells, tell her Old Mirsinth needs more to find metal being.",o="在塞尔萨玛的烈酒旅店寻找艾弗莉·齿轮火花。",oEN="Find Efry Cogspark at the Stoutlager Inn in Thelsamar.",p="你的族人和老米尔辛斯的族人都是蠢货，但也许你和老米尔辛斯也是。\n\n我建议你现在就去找那个矮个子。",pEN="Your people and Old Mirsinth's people both fools, but perhaps you and Old Mirsinth fools too.\n\nI suggest you leave to find short one now.",c="呃，这些矮人非要灌醉我不可！那对找到尼尔瑞莎有什么用，嗯？至少他们收了我的钱，这甜瓜汁我认了，我明白他们要做生意，但说真的，他们得明白，在解决这事之前，我的头脑必须保持最高效率！\n\n我不是\"太紧张\"，也不是\"来回踱步踱得其他客人都焦虑了\"，更不是\"这样根本解决不了让我烦心的事\"。我的焦虑程度对当前状况来说刚刚好！\n\n抱歉，你找到那个巨魔了吗？你最好找到了，而且她最好告诉了你尼尔瑞莎在哪，而不是直接攻击你！\n\n哦……",cEN="Ugh, these dwarves are so insistent on getting me drunk! How’s that gonna help find Nylrisa, huh? Least they took my money for this melon juice, I get they’ve got a business to run, but seriously, they’ve gotta get it through their heads I need my mind at peak efficiency until we solve this!\n\nI’m not “too nervous” or “pacing so much I’m making the other patrons anxious” or “not gonna solve whatever’s worrying me like this”. I am the perfect amount of anxious for the situation!\n\nSorry, did you find the troll? You’d better have found her, and she’d better have told you where Nylrisa is and not just attacked you!\n\nOh…"}
Q[254006]={d="我是说……听着，我能解释……不是听起来那样，我是说确实是，但……哦，这下糟了。艾弗莉你真是个大白痴，你早该告诉这位好心的冒险者！唉！我……这样下去没用，对吧？\n\n我……听着，我们的技术能做到的只有这么多。人，像我们这样的人，比任何机器人都聪明，但问题是，是什么让我们如此？是什么改变了我们？嗯，并不是说有人掌握了全部答案，但幽灵、怨灵之类的东西仍保留着心智，所以不是身体的问题。那么，假如区别就在于灵魂本身呢？那么问题就是，你怎么把那个塞进机器人里？\n\n嗯，有些人设法收集到了那些灵魂留下的某种东西，他们称之为灵质。所以我想，反正人们一直在收集灵质，如果我把它放进机器人的处理器核心，用灵质结合我们一直在开发的初级智能系统，从而创造出更多的东西呢。某种像我们一样的东西！\n\n所以我……用尼尔瑞莎……做了那件事……\n\n听着，这些我们可以以后再谈，重要的是找到尼尔瑞莎。如果这个流放巨魔有办法……嗯，我们别无选择，对吧？我身上没有灵质，但南边有个被穴居人偷走的罐子。我怀疑他们根本不知道那东西怎么用，所以我们只能祈祷他们没把它弄坏。",dEN="I mean…listen I can explain…it’s not what it sounds like, I mean it is but…oh this bad. Efry you’re such an idiot, you should’ve just told the helpful adventurer! Gah! I…this isn’t helping, is it?\n\nI…look, there’s only so much our tech can do. People, like us, we’re smarter than any bot, but the question is, what makes us that way? What changes us? Well, it’s not like anyone’s got all the answers, but, ghosts, wraiths, that sorta thing still retain their minds, so it’s not a body. So what if the difference is the spirits themselves? Well, the problem then is, how do you shove that into a bot?\n\nWell, some people have managed to gather something those spirits leave behind, ectoplasm they call it. So I thought, people have gathered ectoplasm anyways, what if I put that in the processor core of a bot, used ectoplasm combined with the basic intelligence systems we’ve been creating for a while, to create something more. Something like us!\n\nSo I…did that…with Nylrisa…\n\nLook, we can talk about this more later, the important thing is finding Nylrisa. If this troll exile has a plan…well, we don’t have a choice, do we? I don’t have any ectoplasm on me, but there was a cannister stolen by the troggs to the south. Doubt they know what to do with the stuff, so we can just hope they didn't break it.",o="在碎石谷取得一罐灵质。",oEN="Get a cannister of ectoplasm in Stonesplinter Valley.",p="没有灵魂残余，老米尔辛斯就无法施法。也许矮个子还有更多？",pEN="Old Mirsinth not cast spell without spirit remains. Perhaps short one have more?",c="矮个子们很聪明，是的。聪明却愚蠢。但又很聪明，肯告诉你真相。\n\n你还有灵魂残余，是的。这够用了。并不完整，也许穴居人拿走了一些，但老米尔辛斯需要的很少。我会与洛阿沟通，找到金属造物。但先陪老米尔辛斯聊一会儿，好吗？\n\n不，不，不是又一个任务。时间有限，任务毫无意义。说话，是的？只是说话。\n\n金属造物有灵魂。是残余，没错，但是灵魂。金属造物是金属，但也是一个存在。明白吗？金属造物在毁灭，你的族人在毁灭，老米尔辛斯的族人也在毁灭。无尽的循环，永远如此。毁灭金属造物也许是必要的，也许是唯一的选择，但灵魂不是工具。\n\n明白吗？\n\n也许老米尔辛斯也是个蠢货。也许金属造物停止运作会更好。也许毁灭或被毁灭才是最好的，老米尔辛斯只是在对抗事物的常理，转而怨恨俊康兄长。你不必听，老米尔辛斯现在就去准备魔精。",cEN="Short people smart, yes. Smart but fool. But smart again, to tell you truth.\n\nYou have spirit remains, yes. This will do. Not full, troggs take some maybe, but Old Mirsinth need little. I will commune with loa, find metal being. But humor Old Mirsinth for a moment first, will you?\n\nNo, no, not another task. Time is at limit, task would be pointless. Talk, yes? Only talk.\n\nMetal being has spirit. Remains, yes, but spirit. Metal being is metal, but also being. Follow? Metal being destroys, your people destroy, Old Mirsinth’s people destroy. Endless cycle, always. Destroy metal being maybe needed, maybe only choice, but spirit is not tool.\n\nFollow?\n\nPerhaps Old Mirsinth is fool too. Perhaps better metal being ceases. Perhaps destroy or be destroyed is best, Old Mirsinth only fights the way of things and turns on Brother Jun’Kon. You need not listen, Old Mirsinth will prepare mojo now."}
Q[254007]={d="老米尔辛斯完成了，找到了金属造物的灵魂。金属在你们族人称为铁带的那处挖掘场附近，在上方。老米尔辛斯只知道在哪里，不知道为什么，但「哪里」正是你们需要的，对吧？老米尔辛斯的工作看来已经结束了。\n\n老米尔辛斯现在要去游荡了，也许吧。这个世界对她来说算不上家。太多古老的纷争，太多循环，但洛阿向老米尔辛斯展示了许多事物，所以她会去游荡一个并非她家园的世界。\n\n老米尔辛斯已经很久没有称谁为朋友了。也许她太快就把这个词用在一个只交谈过寥寥数语的人身上。尽管如此，老米尔辛斯仍希望在她的游荡中再次遇见你，朋友。",dEN="Old Mirsinth is done, found metal being spirit. Metal being near excavation of one your people call Ironband, above. Old Mirsinth only know where, not why, but where is what you needed, yes? Old Mirsinth’s job is done, it seems.\n\nOld Mirsinth will wander now, perhaps. This world is not much home for her. Too many ancient feuds, too many cycles, but loa have shown Old Mirsinth many things, so wander world that is not home she will.\n\nIt has been long time since Old Mirsinth has called one friend. Perhaps she is too quick to use the word with one she has spoken with too little. Still, Old Mirsinth hopes to meet you again in wandering, friend.",o="在铁带挖掘场附近击败尼尔瑞莎并收集她的组件。",oEN="Defeat Nylrisa near Ironband's Excavation Site and collect her components.",p="求你了，求你了，求你了，告诉我她找到了尼尔瑞莎。\n\n她找到了？那就快去做点什么，别又把她弄丢了！",pEN="Please please please tell me she was able to find Nylrisa.\n\nShe did? Well go do something, before you lose her again!",c="你做到了吗？你找到她了吗？快，快，快快快快快……抱歉，我不紧张。只是……成功了吗？那个巨魔找到她了吗？\n\n你把她的组件带回来了……谢谢。这些要更换可不便宜。让我看看……热奥术小玩意、静电小装置、核心机械功能小部件，嗯，我猜处理器在打斗中坏掉了，灵质肯定也洒出来了，只剩下一点残渣。唉……这事……也许本来就是个坏主意。\n\n好吧，这绝对是个坏主意，听着，我不会再做了，行吗？总之，你救了我的命，大概真的是字面意义上的救命，太感谢了！如果你哪天需要发明家为你搞点什么发明，尽管找我！\n\n嗯……我记得这个处理器里用的是青铜微型齿轮，不是铜的……啊，算了，我想太多了。薇德拉，我现在来一杯那种饮料！其实，来三杯！",cEN="Have you done it? Have you found her? Come on come on comeoncomeoncomeon…sorry, I’m not nervous. Just…did it work? Did the troll find her?\n\nYou brought back her components…thanks. These’d be expensive to replace. Let’s see…thermoarcana dohickey, electrostatic thingamabob, core mechanofunctional gadget, hmm, I guess the processor broke in the fight, the ectoplasm must have spilled out too, only a bit of residue left. Ah well…this was…maybe a bad idea anyways.\n\nOkay, it was definitely a bad idea, look, I won’t do it again, okay? Anyways, you’re a lifesaver, probably literally, thanks a bunch! If you ever need an inventor to do some inventing for you, just hit me up!\n\nHmm…I thought I used bronze microgears in this processor, not copper…ah, well, I’m overthinking this. Vidra, I’ll take one of those drinks now! Actually, make it three!"}
Q[254008]={d="嗯。你把宁神花和……不，这样不太对。\n\n新兵，对吧？也许你能帮上点忙。就当是你试炼的一部分吧。战斗从来不是我的强项。我几年前参加过这些试炼，一只蝎子差点要了我的命。我全靠用当地的仙人掌和一朵奇特的花做成的药膏才活下来。\n\n倒也没起多大作用。你以为我作为失败者回来会有人为我喝彩吗？我是个失败的弱者，是个无法完成战斗的懦夫。\n\n但我还是回到了这里，不是因为我打算重来一次，而是因为我找到了自己的人生道路，我正在设法治愈一种困扰我们已久的东西。所以，如果你的试炼比我顺利，那我在找另一朵我当年找到的那种花。这次不是为了治疗药膏。是别的东西。在试炼中，我是在西北方一棵树下找到它的。",dEN="Hmm. You mix the peacebloom and…no, that isn’t quite right.\n\nThe new recruit, right? Maybe you could help with something. Consider it part of your trials, maybe. Fighting was never my strength. I underwent these trials a few years back, a scorpid almost killed me. I only survived by making a salve with the local cacti and a rare flower.\n\nNot that it did much good. Do you think I’d be cheered on for coming back a failure? I’m a weakling who failed and a coward who couldn’t finish her fight.\n\nBut I’m back here anyways, not because I plan to repeat that but because I found my own path in life, and I’m trying to find a cure to something that’s afflicted us for a while. So if you do better in your trials than I did, I’m looking for another one of those flowers I found. Not for a healing salve this time. Something else. In my trials I found it in the north-west, growing under a tree.",o="找到那朵奇特的花。",oEN="Find the strange flower.",p="我只能寄望自那天起又有另一朵花长了出来。",pEN="I can only hope another flower has grown since that day.",c="它生长在这里，在这片严酷的土地上，不顾一切地对抗着所有阻碍。\n\n相当熟悉，不是吗？\n\n当我涂上那药膏时，我注意到一件奇怪的事。有那么一会儿，我胸口皮肤的绿色调褪去了，就是涂药膏的地方。仿佛它治愈的不只是蝎子的蜇伤，还有燃烧军团的影响。\n\n即便过了这么多年，兽人很久以前饮下的邪能之血所带来的腐化依然存在。绿色的皮肤，但不止于此。我们的血脉永远被恶魔玷污，很难说这影响有多大。也许很细微，但它始终存在，在兽人体内……而我要找到解药。我或许没有力量，也没有勇气……我们中很多人会说，那意味着我也缺乏荣耀。但我懂草药和炼金术。我只需要一个愿意去做我做不到之事的人的帮助。\n\n你说呢？你愿意帮助一个弱者和懦夫吗？",cEN="Growing here in this harsh landscape, in spite of everything against it.\n\nRather familiar, no?\n\nWhen I applied that salve, I noticed something odd. For a few moments, the green tint in my skin faded away on my chest, where I’d applied it. Like it was healing not just the scorpid’s sting, but the Legion’s influence as well.\n\nEven after all these years, the corruption of the fel blood the orcs drank long ago still remains. Green skin, but not just that. Our blood is forever tainted by demons, and it’s hard to say what influence that has. Subtle, perhaps, but it’s always there, within the orcs…and I’m going to find a cure. I might not have strength, or courage…and a lot of us would argue that means I lack honor as well. But I have a knowledge of herbs and alchemy. All I need is the help of someone willing to do what I cannot.\n\nWhat do you say? Will you aid a weakling and a coward?"}
Q[254009]={d="我感激你。事实上，这朵花是我唯一的线索。我采集了不少仙人掌，周围足够多，我不必偏离主路太远，但我观察到的特性一定存在于那朵花里。这已经比大多数人的发现更多了，但我的资源有限，我们甚至不知道这朵花源自何处。\n\n我需要弄清楚的是恶魔之血的特性。我取了自己不少血作样本，但我需要来自源头的东西。山谷最北端的洞穴里有恶魔，对吧？去帮我取一只恶魔的血，不要随便什么血，要你能找到的最强的。\n\n它无法与兽人很久以前饮下的东西相比，但也许至少是个开始。",dEN="You have my gratitude. The truth is, this flower is the only lead I have. I’ve gathered plenty of cacti, there’s enough around I didn’t need to venture much off the main road, but the property I observed must have been in the flower. It’s more than most anyone else has found, but I have limited resources, and we don’t even know where the flower originated.\n\nWhat I need to understand is the properties of the demon blood. I’ve taken plenty of my own as samples, but I need something from the source. There’s demons in the cave at the north end of the valley, no? Find me the blood of one there, not any blood, the strongest you can find.\n\nIt will not compare to what the orcs drank of long ago, but perhaps it is at least a start.",o="从一只强大的恶魔身上采集恶魔之血。",oEN="Collect demon blood from a strong demon.",p="你可能得在洞穴里搜寻一只足够强大的恶魔才符合我的用途。别做鲁莽的事。",pEN="You may have to search the cave for one strong enough for my purposes. Don't do anything reckless.",c="我知道部落崇尚力量与勇气，但作为一个两者皆无的人，我不愿让你为我之故去面对如此强大的恶魔。尽管如此，我还是感谢你。我现在的希望是这能指引我们找到解药。也许不是现在，但我还年轻。\n\n等我一下，我大概还会有更多请求。",cEN="I know the Horde values strength and courage, but as someone without either, I do not like asking you to face against a demon of such power for my sake. Still, I thank you. It is my hope now that this can lead us to a cure. Not right now, maybe, but I am young yet.\n\nGive me a moment, I’ll likely have more requests."}
Q[254010]={d="这还不够……是的，这是个开始。但这项任务还需要更多。首先，我需要了解这朵花的特性。我还没在部落里找到认识它的人，它们似乎并不经常生长。但有另一个族群可能了解自然之物。\n\n半人马在杜隆塔尔生活了许多年，倒不是说我们可以直接去问他们知道些什么。尽管如此，他们或许留有关于这朵花的某些记载。去看看你能从他们的营地学到什么。你完成后我会在奥格瑞玛。\n\n注意安全。你已经是比我更强壮、更勇敢的战士了，但力量与勇敢往往伴随愚蠢，尽管许多兽人不愿承认这一点。",dEN="This isn’t enough…it’s a start, yes. But this task will require more. For a start, I need to understand this flower’s properties. I’ve yet to find anyone in the Horde who knows of it, they don’t seem to grow very frequently. But there is another group who may know of natural things.\n\nThe centaurs have lived in Durotar for many years, not that we can just ask them what they know. Still, it’s possible they have some record of this flower. See what you can learn from their camp. I’ll be in Orgrimmar when you’re done.\n\nBe safe. You are already a stronger and braver warrior than I, but with strength and bravery often come foolishness, as much as many orcs are loathe to admit it.",o="在半人马营地寻找关于那朵花特性的线索。",oEN="Search the centaur camp for clues to the flower’s properties.",p="我只能寄望他们留有某种记载。",pEN="I can only hope they keep some form of record.",c="一幅粗糙的图画似乎描绘了萨卡里所说的那朵花，旁边是一个长着翅膀的精灵女子。旁边其他粗糙的图画显示那个长翅膀的精灵女子正搬运着各种矿石和宝石。也许图画所描绘的对象对这朵花了解更多，并且看重矿石与宝石。",cEN="A crude drawing seems to depict the flower Sakari spoke of, next to a winged elf woman. Several more crude drawings next to it show the winged elf woman carrying various ores and gems. Perhaps whatever is being depicted knows more about the flower, and would value ores and gems."}
Q[254011]={d="你认出那幅画描绘的是你听说过的一种威胁杜隆塔尔的生物：一头鹰身女妖。也许几块闪亮的金属残片能安抚其中一头，让它愿意与你交谈。",dEN="You recognize the drawing as a creature you have heard threatens Durotar, a harpy. Perhaps some bits of shiny metal will appease one enough to talk with you.",o="收集金属残片。",oEN="Collect metallic debris.",p="你在找亮闪闪的东西？是的，是的，是的，带亮闪闪的东西回来，也许我就不吃你！",pEN="You search for shinies? Yes, yes, yes, come back with shinies, maybe not eat you!",c="你带来了亮闪闪，是的，是的，是的！亮闪闪！亮闪闪的持有者今天不吃，是的，是的，是的，明天也许，今天不吃！\n\n亮闪闪的持有者想要回报，是的，是的，是的！想让鹰身女妖们离开，想找人帮忙打架，是的，是的，是的，我很了解你这种人！亮闪闪买下了今天不被吃掉的份，不会更多了。但更多，是的，做更多，帮个忙，我就告诉你你想知道的一切，是的，是的，是的！",cEN="You bring shinies, yes, yes, yes! Shinies! Shiny-bringer not food today, yes, yes, yes, tomorrow maybe, not today!\n\nShiny-bringer wants something in return, yes, yes, yes! Want harpies to leave, want help in fight, yes, yes, yes, I know your kinda well! Shiny buys day as not-food, no more. But more, yes, do more, do favor, and I tell all you wish, yes, yes, yes!"}
Q[254012]={d="姐妹们谋划着叛乱，是的，是的，是的，耳朵听到了，听到了邪恶叛徒的话！她们想要权力、自由，想当女王，是的，是的，是的！因这名号而被杀是理所应当的，姐妹们只有嫉妒，是的，是的，是的，她们是嫉妒的叛徒！\n\n让姐妹们知道谁才是真正的女王，是的，是的，是的，不是全部，很多，足够多！阻止叛乱，我就告诉你阿维安娜之玫瑰的故事！",dEN="Sisters plan rebellion, yes, yes, yes, ears listen, hear vile traitorous words! Want power, freedom, want to be queen, yes, yes, yes! Killed for this title fairly, sisters just jealous, yes yes yes, jealous traitors they are!\n\nShow sisters who true queen, yes, yes, yes, not all, many, enough! Stop rebellion, and will tell you story of Avianna’s Rose!",o="为女王埃瑞西娜杀死鹰身女妖。",oEN="Slay harpies for Queen Erethina.",p="碾压、摧毁，展现女王真正的力量！让姐妹们再也不敢谈论背叛，然后她们就会告诉你阿维安娜之玫瑰的秘密，是的，是的，是的！",pEN="Crush, destroy, show true queen power! Make sisters never speak betrayal again, then tell you secrets of Avianna's Rose, yes, yes, yes!",c="姐妹们害怕了，姐妹们臣服了！真正的女王被知晓、被侍奉，甚至被一个非鹰身女妖侍奉，是的，是的，是的！现在你将知道那朵花了！\n\n传说鹰身女妖之母阿维安娜死后，一滴血长成了一朵孤零零的花，蔓延了很久很久，许多年，甚至长到了这里，是的，是的，是的！我不知道传说是否属实，传说并不重要。阿维安娜之玫瑰拥有强大的力量，能驱除许多诅咒，许多！\n\n传说鹰身女妖用这朵花施展魔法，驱除诅咒，不是翅膀，翅膀不是诅咒，而是别的东西，鹰身女妖由此成为最伟大、最聪明的女王，是的，是的，是的！其他诅咒也许也行，许多诅咒，也许还包括恶魔的诅咒！特殊的魔法，也许还有别的方法。",cEN="Sisters fear, sisters submit! True queen known, served, served by not-harpy even, yes, yes, yes! You will know of flower now!\n\nStory say harpy mother Avianna die, blood drop grow to single flower, spread long, many years, grow even here, yes, yes, yes! Not know if story is true, story not matter. Avianna’s Rose have great power, remove many curses, many!\n\nStory say harpy use magic with flower, remove curse, not wings, wings not curse, but others, harpy becomes greatest smartest queen, yes, yes, yes! Other curses too maybe, many curses, maybe demon curse too! Special magic, maybe other ways."}
Q[254013]={d="我有知识，是的，是的，是的！它能让皮肤不再是绿色，但阿维安娜之玫瑰很稀有，非常稀有，只有一朵，不会更多，有时还更少！鹰身女妖从未驱除过诅咒，从未在阿维安娜之玫瑰上施展过魔法。但你已经有一朵了，是的，是的，是的！\n\n你带来亮闪闪，你粉碎叛乱，我会帮你，是的，是的，是的！魔法还需要另一种材料，一块会发光的石头，黄色的，非常亮，非常、非常、非常亮，在南边的一个地方。找到它，用那朵花，治好诅咒！",dEN="Have knowledge, yes, yes, yes! Make skin not green, but Avianna’s Rose rare, very rare, only ever one, no more, sometimes less! Harpy never removed curse, never used magic on Avianna’s Rose. Yet you already have one, yes, yes, yes!\n\nYou bring shinies, crush rebellion, help you, yes, yes, yes! Magic need other material, bright shiny stone, yellow, very shiny, very very very, at south place. Find, use flower, fix curse!",o="将你了解到的信息带给奥格瑞玛的萨卡里。",oEN="Bring the information you learned to Sakari in Orgrimmar.",p="你还在这儿？很快就吃掉你，是的，是的，是的，现在就走，不然很快就吃掉你，一天不吃你，不会更多！",pEN="You still here? Eat you soon, yes, yes, yes, leave now or eat you soon, one day not eat you, no more!",c="你竟然和一头鹰身女妖谈过了？！\n\n我当然相信你，你有不欺骗我的荣誉，我相信。只是她们一直不友善。当然，我们也没试过好好交谈。好吧，如果你弄清了那朵花的特性，我就可以开始了。",cEN="You talked to a harpy?!\n\nI believe you, of course, you have the honor not to deceive me, I’m sure. They’ve just not been receptive. Of course, we haven’t tried to talk much. Well, if you found out the flower’s properties, I can get started."}
Q[254014]={d="嗯，我不知道那些起源有几分真实，但传说总得有个出处，而如果它拥有驱除诅咒的强大特性，那倒也说得通。不过若用炼金手段加以替代，也许我能把它稀释开来，配制出好几份解药，虽然不多。这朵花只有一粒种子，但也许我能找到办法让它长出更多来……\n\n啊，我扯远了。我们得先确定这个方法有效。你陪我走到了这一步；如果你能拿到那头鹰身女妖提到的水晶，办完之后带着它到贫瘠之地与我会合，我想我可以用恶魔之血作为媒介，让它附着于我们自身的恶魔之血并将其抵消。",dEN="Well, I don’t know how true the origins are, but the story has to originate from somewhere, and if it has powerful curse removal properties, that would make sense. But substituting alchemical means I might be able to stretch it and make several cures, though that isn’t many. The flower only has one seed, but maybe if I could find a way to grow more out of it…\n\nAh, I’m ahead of myself. We need to be sure this method even works. You’ve come this far with me, if you can get the crystal the harpy mentioned and meet me in the Barrens with it when you’re done, I believe I can use the demon blood as a way to make it latch onto our own demon blood and nullify it.",o="在贫瘠之地找到欧鲁盖水晶。",oEN="Find Ouru’gai Crystal in the Barrens.",p="我听说过那样的水晶，好像叫欧鲁盖水晶。非常稀有，但没那朵花那么稀有。",pEN="I've heard of a crystal like that, it is called an Ouru’gai Crystal I believe. Very rare, but not as much as the flower.",c="你拿到了？嗯，它似乎能放大魔法力量，但……啊，我明白了，像这种事情，也许正需要放大那朵花本身的特性。\n\n我们就快成功了！如果我能做成这件事，哪怕只配制出一份解药，就能证明我不只是个弱者。他们在各方面都认为我该有的那种强大，我从来都不曾拥有。我所拥有的只有我的头脑和与生俱来的炼金天赋。但也许那就足够了。",cEN="You have it? Hmm, it does seem to amplify magical power but…ah, I see, it may be necessary to amplify the flower’s own properties for something like this.\n\nWe’re so close! If I pull this off, even I make a single cure, I’ll prove that I’m not just a weakling. I’ve never been strong in all the ways they think I should be. All I had is my mind and an innate talent for alchemy. But maybe that’s enough."}
Q[254015]={d="好吧，我想我弄懂了这一切的特性，至少够用了。我只有一次机会，所以最好让它成功。没有你，我根本做不到这一切，所以，至少你该留下来看到最后。",dEN="Alright, I believe I understand the properties of all of this, at least well enough. I only get one chance, so I’d better make it work. I couldn’t have done this without you, so, you should at least stick around and see this through.",o="观看萨卡里制作解药。",oEN="Watch Sakari create the cure.",p="我只希望这个过程能顺利。至少看起来应该是可行的。有了那块水晶，我或许还能放大我们与元素的联结……",pEN="I only hope this process goes smoothly. It seems like it should work, at least. with that crystal it may amplify our connection to the elements as well...",c="……我没事。我会没事的。你不该为我担心，我应该能照顾好自己。\n\n它没了……那朵花是我唯一的解决办法。我没有别的计划了……我……不，也不尽然。我还有那粒种子。我可以把它种在更安全的地方。如果它能再长出来，我就能再试一次，我知道那最多也只要几年。\n\n至少我还有兽人的毅力。我会继续尝试下去。也许我还会想出别的办法，再来找你帮忙。\n\n谢谢你。大多数人都会嘲笑我的目标，而对我的失败会笑得更厉害。",cEN="…I’m alright. I’ll be fine. You shouldn’t worry about me, I should be able to take care of myself.\n\nIt’s gone…that flower was my only solution. I don’t have any other plans…I…no, that’s not true. I still have the seed. I can plant it somewhere safer. If it grows again, I can give this another try, I know it’s not more than a few years, at least.\n\nI have the perseverance of an orc, at least. I’ll keep trying. Maybe I’ll even think of something else and ask for your help again.\n\nThank you. Most would have laughed at my goal, and laughed more still at my failure."}
Q[254017]={d="你！你要去那座岛上，是吧？\n\n那好，我这儿有份活儿给你，如果你感兴趣的话，而我十分怀疑你会感兴趣。就算不为别的，至少为了钱。我的家族能付你相当不错的报酬，当然，前提是你成功。\n\n你看，我的女儿失踪了，而如今想找个好调查员实在太难。我当然明白，银月城有远比一个失踪女孩更重要的事要操心。但对我来说，塔拉就是我最挂心的事。她曾是这里的学生，那时法瑟林学院还是一所受人尊敬的教育机构，而不是……现在这样。\n\n我知道你大概在想什么，但她的失踪发生在天灾入侵之后。不过，这座岛是我唯一的起点。她一向不习惯跟我多说；要是我了解她失踪前的私人生活，也许就能推算出她可能在哪儿。\n\n不，我不指望能在这儿捡到她的日记，但我有一颗水晶。简单来说，你需要寻找庭院中留存下来的附魔水晶，把这个用在水晶上。如果一切如预期运作，它应该能提取出往昔的影像，具体来说是与塔洛瑟相关的过往事件。专注于较小的那些；更大的能量太强，提取不出任何连贯的东西。",dEN="You! You're going out to the island, no?\n\nWell, I've got a job for you, if you're interested, and I highly suspect you will be interested. In the coin if nothing else. My family can pay you quite well, should you succeed of course.\n\nYou see, my daughter is missing, and it's been hard to find a good investigator these days. I understand, of course, Silvermoon has much larger concerns than one missing girl. But for me, Tara is my largest concern. She was a student here, see, back when Falthrien Academy was a respected educational institution and not...this.\n\nI know what you're likely thinking, but her disappearance was after the Scourge's invasion. This island is the only starting point I have, however. She never had a habit of telling me much, if I knew of her personal life leading up to her disappearance I may be able to pinpoint where she might be.\n\nNo, I don't expect to find her diary just lying around, but what I do have is a crystal. Now, in simple terms, what you need to look for enchanted crystals that have survived within the grounds, and use this on them. If everything works as it should, it should draw out images of the past, specifically past events related to Tarothae. Focus on smaller ones, anything larger has too much energy to draw out anything coherent.",o="激活塔洛瑟过往的记忆",oEN="Activate memories of Tarothae's past",c="所以这里所有的记忆都与一个叫蕾莉安娜的女孩有关？\n\n我不该感到意外。要我说，那女孩对她没好处，但她们总是形影不离。我猜在学院里也是如此。\n\n而你，倒是做得令人满意，这里其他人可就说不上了。",cEN="So all the memories here connected to a girl named Lealiena?\n\nI shouldn't be surprised. That girl was no good for her if you ask me, but they always were around eachother a lot. Guess that kept up at the academy.\n\nYou on the other hand have done satisfactory work, which is more than can be said for anyone else around here."}
Q[254018]={d="下一步是找到蕾莉安娜。我并没怎么留意塔洛瑟的朋友，只顾着确保她们不耽误她的学业。\n\n但你知道她曾是这里的学生，所以我想这算是个起点。假设她也活了下来，我想她应该是回银月城了，所以我会先从那里打听起。\n\n塔洛瑟总坚持在银月裁缝店买衣服，说什么\"不信任\"基兰。我从没跟基兰出过任何问题，但我想有些人就是无法取悦。总之，如果蕾莉安娜也有同样毫无根据的怀疑，银月裁缝店的安德拉也许知道些什么。\n\n奎萨斯收了很多法瑟林幸存的学生当学徒。蕾莉安娜可能也是其中之一，所以我想你可以去问问她是否在他门下受训。\n\n而且我怀疑她住不起旅店房间以外的地方，所以也该去问问乔维亚。\n\n找到蕾莉安娜，看看她知道塔洛瑟的什么。我确信她一定以某种方式牵涉其中。",dEN="The next step is to find Lealiena. I didn't exactly give much mind to Tarothae's friends, save to make sure they didn't keep her from her studies.\n\nBut you know she was a student here, so I suppose that's a start. Assuming she also survived, I'd assume she went back to Silvermoon, so I'd start with asking around there.\n\nTarothae always insisted on buying her clothes from Silvermoon Finery, something about \"not trusting\" Keelan. Never had a single probably with Keelan, but I suppose some people are impossible to please. In any case, if Lealiena had the same baseless mistrust, Andra from Silvermoon Finery might know something.\n\nQuithas took on a lot of the surviving Falthrien students as apprentices. It's possible Lealiena was one of them, so I suppose you could ask if she's training under him.\n\nAnd I doubt she was able to get more than an inn room to stay at, so I'd ask Jovia as well.\n\nFind Lealiena, and see what she knows about Tarothae. I'm certain she has to be involved somehow.",o="寻找蕾莉安娜目前下落的线索",oEN="Search for clues to Lealiena's present location",c="塔洛的母亲派你来找她？我明白了。你还一路追踪我到这里，就为了问我知不知道她在哪。\n\n好吧，听起来你已经找到那封信了，所以我猜你已经知道答案了。\n\n听着，塔洛做了选择，至少我尊重这个选择。她还活着，而且很安全，这点我可以向你保证。\n\n你不必再深究下去了。她有自己要走的路，而那条路里没有她的母亲，所以这事就到此为止吧，把这些告诉薇莱斯特里娜，我们俩就都能继续过日子了。",cEN="Taro's mother sent you to find her? I see. And you tracked me to all the way down here to ask if I knew where she was.\n\nWell, it sounds like you already found that letter, so I guess you know the answer.\n\nListen, Taro made a choice, and I, at least, respect that. She is alive, and safe, I can promise you that.\n\nYou don't need to dig any deeper than that. She has her path to walk, and that path does not include her mother, so leave this here, tell Velestrina that, and we can both go about our day."}
Q[254019]={d="这还不够，对吧？\n\n我早料到了。既然你足够坚定地完成了这份活儿，还一路追踪我到这里，那我就不该指望你会轻易放弃。\n\n好吧。我很快要和塔洛见面，那我就让你一起来。我们在永歌森林边缘的沙恩多符文石碰面。如果你这么坚持，可以来。反正你迟早也会用别的方式找到她们。",dEN="That's not enough, is it?\n\nI expected as much. If you've been determined enough to complete this job that you tracked me here, then I shouldn't expect you to give up easily.\n\nAlright. I'm meeting with Taro soon, so I'll let you come. We meet at Runestone Shan'dor, at the edge of Eversong Woods. You can come, if you're so insistent. It's not like you won't find them another way anyways.",o="在沙恩多符文石与塔洛瑟会面",oEN="Meet with Tarothae at Runestone Shan'do"}
Q[254020]={d="地下城锁定",dEN="Dungeon Lock",o="地下城锁定",oEN="Dungeon Lock"}
Q[254021]={d="艾瑞琳，亲爱的，我希望你还记得我们的约定。\n\n我会继续向你的法力炸弹输送能量，但作为回报，我也有自己的一份需求。我相信你的族人会很乐意接受，毕竟德莱尼人在血谜岛也屠杀了他们许多人。\n\n我会为希罗纳斯报仇，而你的族人会得到你们的武器。这对大家都是一笔好交易，明白吗？",dEN="Eriline, my dear, I do hope you've remembered our agreement.\n\nI'll keep funneling power into your Mana Bomb, but I have my own need for one in return. I'm sure your people will be quite amenable to that, the Draenei slaughtered many of them at Bloodmyst as well, afterall.\n\nI'll have my vengeance for Sironas, and your people will have your weapons. It's a good deal for everyone, see?",o="在火翼岗杀死瓦莱丝丽女士",oEN="Slay Lady Vaalethri at Firewing Point",p="你说有个艾瑞达人正在火翼岗与凯尔萨斯的部队合作？我们现在没有多余的兵力应付这个，但如果你能亲自击败她，我们会欠你一份人情。",pEN="You say there's an Eredar working with Kael'thas's forces at Firewing Point? We don't have the forces to spare for that right now, but if you defeated her yourself, we would be in your debt.",c="一个艾瑞达人在协助研发法力炸弹？\n\n听说你击败了她，真是让人松了口气。即便没有强大恶魔的协助，凯尔萨斯的部队对我们所有人来说已经是足够大的威胁了。提到的那个\"希罗纳斯\"，我想是他们招募的另一个艾瑞达人，在埃索达附近被德莱尼人击败了。\n\n我们只能希望这是他们结盟的最后一个了。谢谢你。",cEN="An Eredar was helping with the development of the Mana Bombs?\n\nIt's a relief to hear you defeated her. Kael'thas's forces are enough of a threat to us all without the aid of a powerful demon. This \"Sironas\" that was mentioned I believe was another Eredar they had recruited, one that was defeated by the Draenei near the Exodar.\n\nWe can only hope this was the last one they had allied with. Thank you."}
Q[254022]={d="艾瑞琳，亲爱的，我希望你还记得我们的约定。\n\n我会继续向你的法力炸弹输送能量，但作为回报，我也有自己的一份需求。我相信你的族人会很乐意接受，毕竟德莱尼人在血谜岛也屠杀了他们许多人。\n\n我会为希罗纳斯报仇，而你的族人会得到你们的武器。这对大家都是一笔好交易，明白吗？",dEN="Eriline, my dear, I do hope you've remembered our agreement.\n\nI'll keep funneling power into your Mana Bomb, but I have my own need for one in return. I'm sure your people will be quite amenable to that, the Draenei slaughtered many of them at Bloodmyst as well, afterall.\n\nI'll have my vengeance for Sironas, and your people will have your weapons. It's a good deal for everyone, see?",o="在火翼岗杀死瓦莱丝丽女士",oEN="Slay Lady Vaalethri at Firewing Point",p="你说有个艾瑞达人正在火翼岗与凯尔萨斯的部队合作？我们现在没有多余的兵力应付这个，但如果你能亲自击败她，我们会欠你一份人情。",pEN="You say there's an Eredar working with Kael'thas's forces at Firewing Point? We don't have the forces to spare for that right now, but if you defeated her yourself, we would be in your debt.",c="一个艾瑞达人在协助研发法力炸弹？\n\n听说你击败了她，真是让人松了口气。即便没有强大恶魔的协助，凯尔萨斯的部队对我们所有人来说已经是足够大的威胁了。提到的那个\"希罗纳斯\"，我想是他们招募的另一个艾瑞达人，在埃索达附近被德莱尼人击败了。\n\n我们只能希望这是他们结盟的最后一个了。谢谢你。",cEN="An Eredar was helping with the development of the Mana Bombs?\n\nIt's a relief to hear you defeated her. Kael'thas's forces are enough of a threat to us all without the aid of a powerful demon. This \"Sironas\" that was mentioned I believe was another Eredar they had recruited, one that was defeated by the Draenei near the Exodar.\n\nWe can only hope this was the last one they had allied with. Thank you."}
Q[254023]={d="女巫吉塞尔达野心勃勃的女儿克莉拉召唤了一名危险的艾瑞达战士苏尔卡娅，想借此向母亲证明自己，甚至可能想推翻她。\n\n苏尔卡娅是个致命的对手，她奉克莉拉之命屠杀了玛格汉和破碎者。守望者莫伊布夫·吉尔会向任何能击败她的人提供一大笔金币奖励。",dEN="Giselda the Crone's ambitious daughter, Kriella, has summoned a dangerous Eredar warrior known as Sulkaia in an effort to prove herself to her mother, or perhaps even overthrow her.\n\nSulkaia is a deadly opponent who has slaughtered Mag'har and Broken alike at Kriella's behest. A large gold reward will be given by Warden Moi'bff Jill to any who can defeat her.",o="击败苏尔卡娅，并将她败亡的消息带给守望者莫伊布夫·吉尔",oEN="Defeat Sulkaia and bring news of her defeat to Warden Moi'bff Jill",p="我们已经因为苏尔卡娅的刀刃失去了太多好人……",pEN="We've already lost too many good people to Sulkaia's blade...",c="苏尔卡娅倒下了？真的吗？这消息太棒了，纳格兰今天至少安全了一点。这确实是你应得的。",cEN="Sulkaia has fallen? Truly? This is great to hear, Nagrand has become at least a bit safer this day. You have truly earned this."}
Q[254024]={d="女巫吉塞尔达野心勃勃的女儿克莉拉召唤了一名危险的艾瑞达战士苏尔卡娅，想借此向母亲证明自己，甚至可能想推翻她。\n\n苏尔卡娅是个致命的对手，她奉克莉拉之命屠杀了玛格汉和破碎者。守望者布洛克会向任何能击败她的人提供一大笔金币奖励。",dEN="Giselda the Crone's ambitious daughter, Kriella, has summoned a dangerous Eredar warrior known as Sulkaia in an effort to prove herself to her mother, or perhaps even overthrow her.\n\nSulkaia is a deadly opponent who has slaughtered Mag'har and Broken alike at Kriella's behest. A large gold reward will be given by Warden Bullrok to any who can defeat her.",o="击败苏尔卡娅，并将她败亡的消息带给守望者布洛克",oEN="Defeat Sulkaia and bring news of her defeat to Warden Bullrock",p="我们已经因为苏尔卡娅的刀刃失去了太多好人……",pEN="We've already lost too many good people to Sulkaia's blade...",c="苏尔卡娅倒下了？真的吗？这消息太棒了，纳格兰今天至少安全了一点。这确实是你应得的。",cEN="Sulkaia has fallen? Truly? This is great to hear, Nagrand has become at least a bit safer this day. You have truly earned this."}
Q[254025]={d="我已经很久没有踏足这片土地了。那是一段我宁愿忘掉的时光，但有些错误必须纠正，有些往事必须了结。\n\n前任守护者艾格文将她塔中那些构成威胁的灵魂封印在这片土地的深处，用强大的魔法确保他们永不见天日。\n\n我就不给你讲历史的细节了，但我们必须找到破除她封印的办法。别误会，它们无论如何都会破开；让这件事按我们自己的意愿发生，不是更好吗？\n\n遗憾的是，我的力量已大不如前，而我解开的那些附魔所残留的能量远远不够。在做任何其他事之前，我需要一个奥术能量源。地窖下方深处的洞穴里，应该有一颗维持附魔祭坛的能量水晶。把它带给我，我们就能讨论下一步了。",dEN="It's been a long time since I've visited these lands. It's a time I'd prefer to forget, but some wrongs must be righted, and some past matters must be settled.\n\nThe former guardian, Aegwynn, sealed the souls of those who posed a threat to her tower deep within the depths of these lands, using powerful magics to ensure they would never see the light of day.\n\nI will spare you the details of history, but we must find a way to break her seals. Do not take that the wrong way, they will break down anyways, it is better for this to be on our own terms, no?\n\nMy power is not what it once was, unfortunately, and the lingering energy of the enchantments I unraveled is far from enough. I'll need a source of arcane energy before I can do anything else. There should be a power crystal sustaining the enchanting altar deep within the caverns beneath the cellar. Bring that to me, and we can discuss our next step.",o="为塔贝萨收集神秘能量水晶",oEN="Collect Mystic Power Crystal for Tabetha",p="如果你一直在用那座祭坛，就别太担心它。即便没有水晶，它自身的能量也足够再维持至少十年。",pEN="Don't you worry too much about that altar if you've been using it. Even without the crystal it's got enough power to sustain itself for at least another decade.",c="是的，是的，它当然攻击了你，你还指望什么？\n\n古老的魔法总会试图自卫，你现在该明白了。\n.\n\n那座祭坛比我还老，我告诉你，那真是古老得很！",cEN="Yes, yes, of course it attacked you, what did you expect?\n\nAncient magics will always try to defend themself, you should know that by now\n.\n\nThat altar is older than I am, and let me tell you, that is ancient indeed!"}
Q[254026]={d="既然我有了妥善使用它的手段，我们就需要艾格文为束缚封印而创造的拱心石。她当然把拱心石保存在墓穴附近；离封印越近，就越能维持它。但如果事情这么简单，它早就被找到了，不是吗？\n\n拱心石与物质世界错开了相位。你可以径直走到墓穴前，却什么也看不见。由于它被用来束缚墓穴内亡者的灵魂，这块石头实际位于与艾泽拉斯重叠的灵魂世界里，就在墓穴入口处。\n\n当然，艾格文有她自己的取回方法，但既然我无法使用那样的魔法，你就得自己想办法了。",dEN="Now that I have a means of using it properly, we'll need the keystone Aegwynn created to bind the seal to. She kept the keystone close to the crypts of course, the closer it is to the seal the better it can sustain it. But if it was that simple, it would've been found, no?\n\nThe keystone is phased out of the physical world. You can go right in front of the crypts and see nothing at all. Because it is used to bind the spirits of the dead within the crypts, the stone is instead found at the crypt's entrance within the Spirit World that overlaps Azeroth.\n\nOf course, Aegwynn had her own way of retrieving it, but given I do not have access to such magics, you'll need to find a solution yourself.",o="找到隐藏在死亡国度中的墓穴拱心石。",oEN="Find the Crypt Keystone hidden within the realm of death.",c="我讨厌看到更多人做这种事……要是我当年能做点什么就好了，要是我当时阻止了这一切就好了……\n\n但这也是他们想要的，想要你找到办法了结此事。如果灵魂医者眷顾你，也许你真的能做点什么。也许这一切终于能结束了……\n\n抱歉，我说得太多了，对吧？我总是这样。就像我说的，我无法对翡翠梦境之外的世界产生多大影响，但我会尽力帮你。",cEN="I hate seeing more people doing this...if I could have just done something back then, if I had just stopped all of this...\n\nBut it's what they would have wanted, for you to find a way to settle this. And if the spirit healers favor you, maybe you really can do something. Maybe this can finally end...\n\nSorry, I'm talking too much, aren't I? I always do this. Like I said, I can't do much to actually effect the world outside the Emerald Dream, but I'll help you the best I can."}
Q[254027]={d="我不知道那个灵魂在哪里，但我可以给你一小部分梦境的力量。它能让你看见肉眼看不见的东西。记忆、往昔的碎片……\n\n它也许能给你一些线索，弄清那个灵魂把拱心石带去了哪里，以及为什么。虽然不多，但我希望它能帮上忙。\n\n只是……小心点，好吗？这片土地充满了悲剧，我无法保证它们不会伤害你。而且，即便你能让灵魂医者把你带回来，也不意味着你就不该珍惜自己的性命。绝不亚于一个总会在世间重生的人，就该为了一个不可能的目标一次次任由自己死去……",dEN="I don't know where the spirit is, but I can give you a small piece of the Dream's power. It will let you see things your eyes could not. Memories, fragments of the past...\n\nIt might let you get some clues to where that spirit took the keystone, and why. It's not much, but, I hope it helps.\n\nJust...be careful, okay? These lands are full of tragedy, I can't promise they can't hurt you. And just because you can get the spirit healers to bring you back doesn't mean you shouldn't value your own life. Not anymore than someone who will always be reborn into this world should just keep letting themself die for an impossible goal...",o="使用梦境精华寻找那个灵魂下落的线索",oEN="Use the Dream Essence to find clues to the spirit's location",p="来吧，告诉我你在找什么？也许我能帮上忙！",pEN="Come on, tell me what you're looking for? Maybe I can help!",c="一个灵魂带走了拱心石……？\n\n哦！我敢打赌是那个怪物拿走的。不过你该离它远点；它在夜里游荡，杀掉它遇到的任何人。甚至是它喜欢的人。它是个可怕的怪物，你该恨它，离它越远越好！",cEN="A spirit took a keystone...?\n\nOh! I bet the monster took it. You should stay away from it though, it walks in the night, and it kills anyone it meets. Even people it likes. It's a terrible monster and you should hate it and stay as far away from it as possible!"}
Q[254028]={d="但如果你真想找到它，我敢打赌食人魔那里可能有点东西。他们没那个怪物那么吓人，但他们总在搞些可怕的魔法。\n\n我会悄悄绕到另一边去，你办完事就可以到那儿找我。",dEN="But if you really want to find it, I bet the ogres might have something. They're not as scary as the monster, but they're always doing scary magic.\n\nI'll sneak around to the other side and you can come find me there once you're done.",o="在恶行渊寻找拱心石下落的线索",oEN="Search the Vice for clues to the Keystone's location",p="食人魔没那么坏，你该害怕的是那个怪物。\n\n它大概已经找到你了。它也许正等着动手，只想逗你玩玩，所以小心点。",pEN="The ogres aren't that bad, it's the monster you should be scared of.\n\nIt's probably already found you by now. It might be waiting to attack, just to toy with you a little, so be careful.",c="所以你查到了村里死去的那个孩子，还有个邪教徒在念叨什么\"第二幻灵\"？\n\n不过我不知道这对找到拱心石有什么帮助。但这就是为什么你该离那个怪物远点。它会让你跌得太深，深到你再也不知道该如何站起来。",cEN="So you found out about a kid who died in the village and a cultist talking about something called the \"Second Eidolon\"?\n\nI don't know how that helps us find the keystone though. But this is why you should stay away from the monster. It'll make you fall so far you won't know how to get back up."}
Q[254029]={d="有个叫阿里登的商人，总是显得鬼鬼祟祟；我们离他远远的，但也许他知道点什么？你可以去他的营地看看，问问他有没有见过什么灵魂。\n\n我一点也不想靠近他，但我会在他营地过去的那条路上等你！也许路上你还会发现别的东西。",dEN="There's a merchant named Ariden, always seems shady, we stay way far from him, but maybe he knows something? You could go check out his camp, maybe ask him if he's seen any spirits.\n\nI'm not going anywhere near him, but I'll meet you on the road past his camp! Maybe you'll find something else along the way too.",o="在阿里登的营地及其后方的道路上寻找线索",oEN="Search Ariden's camp and the road beyond for clues",p="我不想你受到伤害。真的不想。\n\n所以，求你了，在那个怪物找到你之前逃走吧。\n\n但你不会听我的，对吧？从来没人听我的。",pEN="I don't want you to get hurt. I really don't.\n\nSo please, run before the monster finds you.\n\nBut you won't listen, will you? No one ever listens to me.",c="以阿里登的为人，他大概卖给她一把生锈的剑，还声称那是强大的神器。\n\n但就算有神器，她也毫无胜算。不过，我敢打赌我知道是谁偷走了拱心石！",cEN="Knowing Ariden he probably sold her a rusty sword and claimed it was a powerful artifact.\n\nBut even with an artifact she wouldn't have stood a chance. Still, I bet I know who stole the Keystone then!"}
Q[254030]={d="我弄清楚那个灵魂在哪了！\n\n就在前面再过去一点，我想那就是你一直用梦境视觉看到的那个女人的灵魂。她一定是从墓穴里逃了出来，把它带走了。\n\n我怀疑她不会轻易放手，但我相信你能把她从这个世界上永远抹去，然后把它据为己有。如果她被囚禁了这么久，你这么做基本算是在帮她，对吧？\n\n什么，别那样看着我！我只是想帮忙。说起来，你拿到之后一定要来见我最后一面，好吗？我想在你回城把我忘掉之前给你点东西。",dEN="I figured out where the spirit is!\n\nJust up ahead a bit more, I think it's the spirit of that woman you've been seeing with your dream sight. She must have escaped the crypts and taken it.\n\nI doubt she'll let it go easily, but I'm sure you can remove her from this world forever and take it for yourself. If she's been trapped this long it's basically doing her a favor, right?\n\nWhat, don't look at me like that! I'm just trying to help. Speaking of, make sure you come see me one last time when you get it, okay? I want to give you something, before you go back to town and forget me.",o="面对阿凯拉的灵魂并取得拱心石",oEN="Confront the spirit of Akeila and obtain the Keystone",c="她当然没有。她从来就没法弄到它，对吧？\n\n不过，那样帮你寻找拱心石还是挺愉快的。你是少数真正有趣的人之一。\n\n但你现在该走了，否则那个怪物会来找你。\n\n呵。",cEN="Of course she didn't have it. She's never had a way to get it, has she?\n\nStill, it's been nice, helping you look for the Keystone like that. You're one of the few people who's actually been interesting.\n\nBut you should leave now, otherwise the monster will come get you.\n\nHeh."}
Q[254031]={d="你以为我是又一段记忆？\n\n我怎么会是记忆？毕竟，我已被遗忘了。呵。\n\n但我是认真的。如果可以，也许我会再陪你走一段路。有那么一会儿，这几乎让我觉得自己又像个人了。\n\n可我跟你说过了，对吧？那个怪物会杀光所有人。甚至是它喜欢的人。所以你真该更小心一些。",dEN="Did you think I was another memory?\n\nHow could I be a memory? I was forgotten afterall. Heh.\n\nBut I really mean it. If I could, maybe I'd keep traveling with you longer. For a little bit, it almost made me feel like a person again.\n\nI told you though, didn't I? The monster kills everyone. Even people it likes. So you really should have been more careful.",o="面对被遗忘的化身并夺回拱心石",oEN="Face the Forgotten Avatar and recover the Keystone",p="所以现在那个小崽子以为它可以大摇大摆地出去，把拱心石拿走？幸好我及时赶回来了。",pEN="So now that little twerp thinks it can go marching out and taking the Keystone? It sure is a good thing I came back when I did.",c="那个小崽子并没有消失，相信我，它经历过远比这糟糕的事。\n\n不过，把它吓退干得不错。大多数人被它盯上时都没这么好运。\n\n它迄今做到的不过是个化身，是它灵魂的投影，只具备它全部能力的一小部分。它的核心，真正承载它灵魂的东西，被封在墓穴深处，那大概就是它拿走拱心石的真正目的。\n\n幸好它按捺不住想跟你这样的人打一场。又或者某一部分……不，没必要为此操心，它就是个威胁，仅此而已！而现在，你有了办法在防护彻底崩坏之前一劳永逸地解决这些墓穴。",cEN="That little twerp isn't gone, it's been through far worse, believe me.\n\nStill, not a bad job fending it off. Most ain't so lucky when it goes after them.\n\nAll it's gotten out so far is an an avatar, a projection of its spirit with a fraction of its full capabilities. It's core, the actual thing holding its soul, is sealed deep within the crypts, probably its real goal in taking the keystone.\n\nWe're lucky it couldn't resist trying to fight someone like you. Or maybe some part...no, there's no point worrying about that, it's a threat is what it is! And now, you've got a way to deal with the crypts for good before the wards break down completely."}
Q[254032]={d="好了，既然我已调校好拱心石供你使用，你应该可以直接打开门进去了。不过我不建议你独自前往；找几个朋友一起进去。\n\n我的力量已经耗尽，帮不了太多忙了，但我会在里面投射出一个自己的影像。你到了那里，还有几件别的事需要处理好。",dEN="Alright, now that I've attuned the keystone so you can use it, you should be able to just open the door and walk right in. I don't recommend doing that alone though, get a few friends and head on inside.\n\nGiven my power is drained as it is, I'm not gonna be much help anymore, but I'll project an image of myself on in there. There's a few other things to make sure you settle while you're there.",o="在卡拉赞墓穴内与塔贝萨的投影会合。",oEN="Meet Tabetha's projection inside the Karazhan Crypts.",c="看来一切都顺利运转了，但艰难的部分还在后头。\n\n这地方是许多被封印多年的灵魂的家园。而他们绝不会乐意看到一个活人出现在他们中间。你最好做好准备。",cEN="Looks like everything worked perfectly, but the hard part is still ahead of you.\n\nThis place is home to spirits sealed for many years. And they aren't going to be happy to see a member of the living among them. You'd be best be prepared."}
Q[254033]={d="很久以前发生的事是个悲惨的故事。说它当时得到了最好的处理，那是不对的。但你看到了那个小崽子有多危险，哪怕它只是自己的一个化身。\n\n事实上，连我也只了解它真实面貌的一部分。所以我想请你取回它的核心并带给我，好让我设法弄清当年究竟发生了什么。它当然是个危险的存在，你得几乎将它摧毁才能触及核心。\n\n至少我相信你能照顾好自己。",dEN="It is a tragic story, what once happened long ago. I'd be amiss to say that it was handled the best it could have been, back then. But you saw the danger that little twerp posed, even just an avatar of itself.\n\nIn truth even I only understand part of what it actually is. And that's why I'd like to ask you to recover its core and bring it to me, so I can try to learn what actually happened back then. It's a dangerous being of course, and you'll need to all but destroy it to get at the core.\n\nI trust you can handle yourself well enough, at least.",o="为塔贝萨取得被遗忘的核心",oEN="Obtain the Forgotten Core for Tabetha",p="别因为它通常呈现的形态就为与之战斗而难过。你已经清楚看到那个小崽子实际上是什么了！",pEN="Don't go feeling bad about fighting it over that form it likes to take. You've seen full well what the little twerp really is!",c="德林·米埃尔的核心。最理智的做法是摧毁它，释放米埃尔的灵魂，并消灭与她融合的死亡之灵，让它再也无法造成伤害。\n\n但我还需要弄清是什么创造了它们，而有时对知识的追求本身就是一种智慧。现在别担心，它们要完全重塑还得花些时间，到那时我就能掌控这份意志了。那个小崽子也许是个威胁，但在你的曾祖辈还是婴儿时，我就面对过远比这糟糕的危险。\n\n无非意味着我得再多等一阵子才能把能量之石还给那座祭坛，仅此而已。你继续走你的路吧，你知道在沼泽哪里能找到我。我多半还会再来找你。",cEN="The core of Dryn Miel. The wise thing to do would be to destroy it, free Miel's soul and destroy the spirit of death that fused with it so it can't cause any more harm.\n\nBut I still need to learn what created them, and sometimes the pursuit of knowledge is its own wisdom. Don't fret now, it will take a bit before they can properly reform, and I'll have this will under control by then. The little twerp might be a threat, but I was facing dangers far worse when your great grandparents were infants.\n\nJust means I'll need to wait a bit longer on returning that altar's power stone is all. You go be on your way for now, you know where to find me over in the marsh. More than likely I'll come seeking you out again in time."}
Q[254034]={d="艾格文住在这里时，她，嗯，远不受肯瑞托的待见。也许事出有因，但有一个人亲自去寻求她的知识。我得说明，那是一位肯瑞托的前成员，因他对血液作为仪式材料的相当非正统的研究而声名扫地。\n\n他叫辛菲尔。一个如此执着于永生的法师，考虑到几乎没人对她有好感，她心生怜悯，教了他抗衰老附魔的基础，但他想要的不止于此。\n\n最终，他变成了一个亡灵存在，是最早可以被称为夜陨者的存在之一，并自以为对伤害免疫，转而与她为敌。最简单的解决办法本是摧毁他的心脏，但既然他如此渴望永生，她便干脆把他连同心脏一起封印在了墓穴之中。\n\n我无法想象他此后恢复过理智，所以如果你想彻底摧毁他，就得查清他在把心脏从胸口扯出来之后藏到了哪里。我提过他把心脏从胸口扯出来了吗？算了，我相信你能查清楚。",dEN="Back when Aegwynn lived here she was, well, far from well-liked by the Kirin Tor. For good reason, perhaps, but there was one who went to seek her knowledge himself. A former member of the Kirin Tor, I should specify, disgraced for his rather unorthodox study of blood as a ritual component.\n\nCynfael he went by. A mage so determined to become immortal, considering how few actually saw her positively she took pity on him and taught him the fundamentals of anti-aging enchantments, but he wanted something else.\n\nEventually he turned himself into an undead being, one of the first that could be called Darkfallen, and turned on her thinking himself invincible to harm. The easy solution would have been to destroy his heart, but since he wanted immortality so badly, she simply sealed him, heart and all, within the crypts.\n\nI can't imagine he's gotten any more sane since then, so if you want to destroy him for good, you'll need to figure out where he hid his heart after he ripped it from his chest. Did I mention he'd ripped his heart from his chest? No matter, I'm sure you can figure it out.",o="在卡拉赞墓穴中击败辛菲尔",oEN="Defeat Cynfael in the Karazhan Crypts",c="所以辛菲尔漫长的生命终于结束了，是吗？\n\n你知道他永远不能离自己的心脏太远，否则联结就会断裂，他会立刻死去吗？真是浪费，为了对\"永生\"的鲁莽追求而被困在某座坟墓里。难怪如今的萨莱茵不再尝试同样的做法了。",cEN="So Cynfael's long life is finally over, is it?\n\nDid you know he could never venture too far from his heart, or the connection would break and he'd die instantly? What a waste, cooped up in some tomb over a reckless pursuit of \"immortality\". It's no wonder the San'layn you see around these days don't try and pull the same thing."}
Q[254035]={d="在巫妖王和他的亡灵士兵之前，你们年轻人总爱自称\"死亡骑士\"；可这个词过去的意思是另一回事，你知道吗？\n\n第二次大战期间，古尔丹把暗影议会陨落术士的灵魂注入到兄弟会骑士的尸骸之中。你怎么会连那些名字都不认识？难道冒险者在出发去执行危险任务之前，连一本历史书都不教你们读吗？这整个世界都乱套了，这就是事实！\n\n总之，我不打算给你讲第二次大战的历史，你可以自己去查。其中一位骑士最终与艾格文交战。她当时已被剥夺了大部分魔法，但让我告诉你，一个足够优秀的法师即便没有法术也不是好对付的对手。\n\n她设法把他引到墓穴附近，激活防护结界，将他的灵魂困在其中。他大概至今仍在寻找合适的宿主演，所以彻底了结他的灵魂，让他永远得不到新的身体。",dEN="Before the Lich King and his undead soldiers you young folk like to go calling \"Death Knights\" that term used to mean something else you know.\n\nBack during the Second War, Gul'dan shoved the souls of the fallen Shadow Council warlocks into the corpses of Knights from the Brotherhood of the Horse. What do you mean you don't recognize all those names? Don't they teach you adventurers a single history book before you go setting out on dangerous quests? This whole world's gone to pot, and that's the truth!\n\nAnyways, I'm not teaching you Second War history, you can figur that out on your own. One of these knights ended up in a battle with Aegwynn. She'd been stripped of most of her magic, but let me tell you, a good enough mage is no easy opponent even without their spells.\n\nShe was able to lure it near the crypts and activate the wards to trap its soul inside. It's probably still looking for a proper host for its soul to this day, so deal with its soul for good so it never gets another body.",o="在卡拉赞墓穴中击败库尔戈斯·毁灭者",oEN="Defeat Kurgoth Doomreaver in the Karazhan Crypts",c="我们终于摆脱库尔戈斯的灵魂了。依我说，真是谢天谢地。\n\n现代的部落没那么糟，但在那些日子里，相信我，他们全都不过是军团的棋子。我们最不需要的就是哪怕一位古代死亡骑士卷土重来。\n\n现在，要是有人能确保老泰隆也彻底消失就好了。他比库尔戈斯糟糕得多，这话我可没随便说。",cEN="We're finally rid of Kurgoth's soul. Good riddence I say!\n\nThe modern Horde's not so bad as all that, but back in those days, trust me, nothing but pawns of the Legion the whole lot of them. The last thing any of us need is a single one of the old Death Knights coming back.\n\nNow if someone would just make sure old Teron's gone. He's far worse than Kurgoth, and I don't say that lightly."}
Q[254036]={d="艾格文不想和山下村民的麻烦扯上关系，但人们总爱把住在巨塔里的强大法师当作自己的领袖，不管她愿不愿意。而当她偏执多疑、受萨格拉斯影响时，这就尤其可怕。顺便说一句，她当时正是如此。\n\n于是她用最残酷的命运惩罚每一桩罪行。他们的尸体被倒吊在墓穴的一处水池里，即便身体早已溺毙，灵魂也被永远封印。他们算不上什么模范人物，但没有一个人该落得如此下场。\n\n那么，你何不下去一趟，彻底释放他们的灵魂呢？我相信你会找到办法的。只是小心点，过了这么多年，我怀疑他们不会为此高兴。",dEN="Aegwynn wanted little to do with the problems of the town below, but people tend to treat the powerful mage living in a massive tower as their leader regardless of what she wants. That's especially a terrible when she's paranoid and under the influence of Sargeras. Which she was, if you didn't know.\n\nSo she punished every crime with the cruelest of fates. Their bodies hung up upside-down within a pool of water in the crypts, their souls sealed forever even long after their bodies were drowned. They were hardly upstanding folk, but none of them deserved a fate like that.\n\nSo why don't you go finally set their souls free while you're down there. I'm sure you'll figure something out. Just be careful, I doubt they're pleased about it after all these years.",o="在卡拉赞墓穴中面对罪人之审判",oEN="Face the Judgement of Sinners in the Karazhan Crypts",c="愿那些可悲的灵魂终能寻得安宁。\n\n倒不是说我对他们有什么感情。他们都很可怕，但他们早已服满了刑期。再说，我们最不需要的就是一大群复仇的怨灵从这里逃出去。我们都知道那对谁都不会有好结果。",cEN="May those wretched souls finally find some peace.\n\nNot that I have any love of them. They were horrible, the whole lot, but they've more than served their sentence. Besides, last thing we need is a whole bunch of vengeful spirits breaking out of here. We all know that never ends well for anyone."}
Q[254037]={d="那副该死的盔甲终于碎裂了……我从没想过这一天会到来。\n\n我相信我的名字对上面的世界已经毫无意义。谁会记得一个失败的英雄呢？没有理由记得我，但我还是想请你听听我的故事，至少让你明白，与那副盔甲相连的阴影并非一直是我的本色。",dEN="That accursed armor is finally shattered...I never thought this day would come.\n\nI am sure my name has no meaning to the world above anymore. Who would remember a failed hero anyways? There is no reason to remember me, but even so, I would ask that you hear my story, at least so you understand the shadow bound to that armor was not who I always was.",o="聆听塔坎·维洛的讲述",oEN="Hear Takan Velor's Tale",p="你不欠我什么，所以你要是转身离开，我也能理解。",pEN="You owe me nothing, so I will understand if you turn back.",c="我真心希望你能在我失败的地方取得成功。我希望能再次与你并肩拔剑，但我的灵魂如今太过虚弱。我只能旁观，并向圣光祈祷你的救赎。",cEN="I truly hope you can succeed where I failed. I wish I could draw my blade alongside you once more, but my soul is too weak now. I can only watch, and pray to the Light for your salvation."}
Q[254042]={d="将报告交给西部荒野哨兵岭的守护者加里尔。",dEN="Report to Protector Gariel at Sentinel Hill in Westfall.",o="杀死囤积者莱诺尔，然后回到哨兵岭的守护者加里尔处。",oEN="Kill Lenore the Hoarder and return to Protector Gariel at Sentinel Hill."}
Q[254043]={d="将报告交给西部荒野哨兵岭的守护者加里尔",dEN="Report to Protector Gariel at Sentinel Hill in Westfall",o="守护者加里尔想要你收集西部荒野的补给，然后回到哨兵岭找她。",oEN="Protector Gariel wants you to gather Westfall Supplies, then return to her at Sentinel Hill."}
Q[254046]={d="呃！有人偷了我的光之钥匙，我严重怀疑是竞速场那帮油腻的地精干的。\n\n我敢打赌那个大嘴巴波兹克知道点什么。他总爱把他那对大耳朵伸进别人的事里。去那儿看看他听到了什么。只是别让他用那套花言巧语把你绕晕了。",dEN="Ugh! Someone swiped my Arclight Spanner, and I’ve got a strong suspicion it was one of those greasy goblins over at the Raceway.\n\nI bet that loudmouth Pozzik knows something. He’s always got his big ears in everybody’s business. Head over there and see if he’s heard anything. Just don’t let him talk you in circles.",o="蒂比·菲兹 crank 想让你查清是谁拿走了她的工具。幻影竞速场的波兹克或许有点头绪。",oEN="Tibbi Fizzcrank wants you to find out who took her tools. Pozzik at the Mirage Raceway probably has an idea.",p="你还等什么？那些恶棍怕是已经在去往加基森的半路上了！",pEN="What're you waiting for? Those ruffians are halfway to Gadgetzan by now!",c="原来是这么回事。听着，也许我看到了什么，也许没有。几枚油腻的掌心里钱通常能refresh一下我这老记性，你懂我意思吧。\n拿着，收下这个，告诉蒂比我在查这事。",cEN="So that’s what this is about. Look, maybe I saw somethin’, maybe I didn’t. Greased palms tend to jog the ol’ memory, if you catch my drift.\nHere, take this and tell Tibbi I’m lookin’ into it."}
Q[254051]={d="我在河边守着一个巢穴好几天了。其中一只鳄鱼终于下了一枚蛋，只有一枚，完美。一件美丽的东西。蛋壳上有斑点，摸起来温热。我本想把它带到安全的地方，给它一个真正孵化的机会。\n\n然后那些恶心的穴居人出现了。咕哝着、踩踏着穿过灌木丛，其中一个像抓石头一样抓起那枚蛋，尖叫着跑了。\n\n他们不知道手里拿的是什么。要是我们不快点找回它，他们会把它吃掉、打碎，或者扔进泥里煮了。你比我快，也不怕弄脏手。\n\n把那枚蛋带回来。我欠你一个人情。",dEN="I have been watchin’ a nest by the river for days now. One of the crocs finally laid, just one perfect egg. Beautiful thing. Spotted shell, warm to the touch. I was hopin’ to move it somewhere safe, give it a real shot at hatching.\n\nThen those filthy troggs showed up. Grunting and stomping through the brush, one of ‘em grabbed the egg like it was a rock and ran off screamin’.\n\nThey do not know what they are holding. They will eat it or smash it or boil it in mud if we do not get it back fast. You are faster than me, and you are not afraid to get dirty.\n\nBring that egg back. I will owe you one.",o="辛特·维夫想让你从北岛的巨魔\"偷猎者\"手中夺回鳄鱼蛋。",oEN="Sinter Wive wants you to retrieve the Crocolisk Egg from the Trogg \"Poachers\" on the island to the North.",p="你找到那枚蛋了吗？告诉我你赶在他们打碎它之前到了。",pEN="You find the egg? Tell me you got to it before they cracked it open.",c="就是它。就是这枚。温热而完整，蛋壳上一道划痕都没有。要不是我满身沼泽水和鳄鱼口水，我真想抱抱你。\n\n你干得好。非常好。这个小家伙现在也许有机会了。",cEN="That is it. That is the one. Warm and whole, not a scratch on the shell. I would hug you if I were not covered in swamp water and croc spit.\n\nYou did good. Really good. This little one might just have a chance now."}
Q[254052]={d="那些带瘟疫的蝎子一点求生本能都没有。它们就在路上晃悠，好像那是晒太阳的地方。而当赛车手呼啸而过时，他们可不会停下来问路。\n\n我需要有人在我们再出一次事故之前清理掉最糟的那些。把它们轰走、碾碎，随便什么管用的办法。只是小心脚下。",dEN="Those scorpid pests have zero instinct for survival. They just wander right onto the track like it’s a sunbathing spot. And when the racers come tearing through, they don’t exactly stop to ask for directions.\n\nI need someone to clear out the worst of them before we have another crash. Scare them off, squish them, whatever works. Just watch your step out there.",o="蒂比·菲兹 crank 想让你清理附近道路上任何蝎子造成的障碍。",oEN="Tibbi Fizzcrank wants you to clear the nearby track of any scorpid obstructions.",p="要是它们能自己离远点就省事多了，但我们对此无能为力。",pEN="Sure would be easier if they'd just stay off on their own, but not much we can do about that.",c="这地方要是能有真正的护栏就好了，对生物和赛车手都更安全，但你要想让一个地精明白安全的重要性，祝你好运。\n\n至少现在看来你暂时解决了。干得好。",cEN="We could really do with some actual railings here, would be safer for the critters and the racers, but good luck convincing a goblin on the importance of safety.\n\nStill looks like you solved it for now at least, good work."}
Q[254053]={d="如果你愿意听一个简单的请求，这把老骨头已经没有从前的力气了。对圣光的信仰……从来不属于我们这种人。而这具身体在职责召唤时也并不总能回应。\n\n墓地的坟茔已经荒废太久了。那些可怜的灵魂在这世上大概已无人记得，但他们依然该有尊严。\n\n如果你有时间，也不妨照看一下巴尔尼尔农场里阿尔萨斯战马的坟墓。它主人的罪行罄竹难书，但那匹马是忠诚的……而且在巫妖王的阴影笼罩大地之前就已死去。\n\n如果它活得更久些，也许历史会走向不同的结局。",dEN="If you’ll hear a simple request, these old bones do not carry the strength they once did. Faith in the Light... it was never meant for those like us. And this body doesn’t always answer when duty calls.\n\nThe graves in the cemetery have gone untended for far too long. Those poor souls likely have no one left in this world to remember them, but they deserve dignity all the same.\n\nIf you find the time, you might also tend to the grave of Arthas's steed at the Balnir Farmstead. His master’s crimes are many, but the horse was loyal... and he died before the Lich King's shadow ever fell across the land.\n\nHad he lived longer, perhaps the tale might have ended differently.",o="清理阿拉斯托神父墓地中的 6 块墓碑，以及巴尔尼尔农场的无敌之墓。",oEN="Polish 6 gravestones at Father Alastor's cemetary and Invincible's grave at Balnir Farmstead.",p="无敌之墓比其他几处远得多，为此我向你道歉。",pEN="Invincible's Grave is a much longer journey than the others, I do apologize for that.",c="我很感激你。我对这个世界以及居住其中的人们的爱，让这份痛苦尚可忍受，但我仍然执掌着一种如今与我自身相抗的力量。有些日子我几乎能忘掉它，但有时我必须留在这里保存体力。\n\n……他们竟然掘开了无敌之墓？！以圣光之名！阿尔萨斯造成的苦难还不够吗，竟连那匹可怜的马都不让它安息？\n\n抱歉，至少谢谢你带来这个消息，也谢谢你代我跑这一趟。",cEN="I thank you for this. My love for this world and the people in it makes this pain bearable, but I am still wielding a power that now fights against my very being. There are days I can almost forget it, but sometimes I must remain here and conserve my strength.\n\n...Invincible's grave has been opened?! By the light! Has Arthas not caused enough suffering already that he will not even let that poor horse rest in peace?\n\nI am sorry, thank you for bringing me the news at least, and for making this journey in my stead."}
Q[254054]={d="巴尔尼尔家族曾养育出全艾泽拉斯最优良的一些战马，连王室都青睐有加。即便有这样的主顾，他们也从不因此自大；他们是善良谦逊的人，我想他们的马也像他们一样，所以才如此受人珍视。\n\n……但那都已是过去。农场如今已成废墟，只有不安的亡者住在那里。我相信巴尔尼尔家的人也在其中，但即便我能执掌圣光，如今它却令我疼痛；我不再信任自己在战斗中的力量。\n\n如果你有这份心，能否代我让他们的可怜灵魂得以安息？他们一共三位：瓦拉、约鲁姆和他们的儿子贾里姆。",dEN="The Balnir family once bred some of the finest steeds on all of Azeroth, favored by even the royalty. Even with such clients, they never let it get to their head, they were kind, humble folk, I believe their horses took after them, and that was why they were favored so.\n\n...But that is all in the past. The farmstead is in ruins now, and only the restless dead lives there. I am certain the Balnirs themselves must be amongst them, but though I may wield the light, it pains me now, I do not trust my power in a fight anymore.\n\nIf you would have it in your heart, could you put their poor souls to rest in my stead. There were three in total, Vara, Jorum, and their son Jarim.",o="让巴尔尼尔家族的灵魂安息：约鲁姆·巴尔尼尔、瓦拉·巴尔尼尔和贾里姆·巴尔尼尔。",oEN="Put the spirits of the Balnir family, Jorum Balnir, Vara Balnir, and Jarim Balnir to rest.",p="那可怜的一家人该得到安息。我希望我们至少能给予他们这个。",pEN="That poor family deserves their rest. I hope we can at least grant them that much.",c="愿他们终于得以安息。我非常感激你，你真是善良，又或者你只是什么活儿都接。结果是一样的。在天灾留下的所有不安灵魂中，这只是小小的一份，但我依然感到欣慰。",cEN="So they can finally rest. I am most grateful, you are truly kind, or perhaps you simply accept any job you are offered. The outcome is the same. It is a small difference amidst all the restless souls left behind by the Scourge, but still, I am glad."}
Q[254055]={d="你看起来还是有点紧张，别担心，它不咬人。至少我不下令的话不会。\n\n好吧，拿着，你何不做点什么来赢得它一点信任呢？它特别喜欢那些暮色蝙蝠；事实上，我花了不少时间训练它，让它在蝙蝠经过营地时不要扑上去。\n\n我一直在东边看到一只大的，本来打算去替它猎来的，但既然你在这儿，何不去找找看，给它带一块回来？",dEN="You still look a bit nervous, don't worry, he won't bite. Not unless I tell him to anyways.\n\nAlright, here, why don't you do something to earn his trust a bit? He's quite fond of those duskbats, took a while to train him not to just rush at them when they wander by the camp actually.\n\nI've been seeing a big one off to the east, been meaning to go hunt it for him, but since you're here, why don't you go find it and give him a piece?",o="寻找一份猎物并把它交给埃德温的猎犬。",oEN="Find a treat and give it to Edwin's hound.",p="它喜欢任何暮色蝙蝠的肉，但我相信那只大的一定格外多汁。\n\n不过别一次全给它，就算它说不是这样，它也不需要那么多！一块就够了。",pEN="He loves any Duskbat meat, but I'm sure that big one is especially juicy.\n\nDon't give him the whole thing at once though, he doesn't need that much even if he'll tell you otherwise! A piece should be plenty.",c="看吧，你瞧，现在它会永远喜欢你了。\n\n剩下的我来处理，它可以晚点再吃。",cEN="There you go, see, he'll love you forever now.\n\nI'll take the rest of it off your hand, he can have it later."}
Q[254056]={d="驻扎在这里，我们不断遭到血色十字军的袭击。到目前为止我们一直压制着他们的进攻，好让药剂师们能开展工作，他们也大多不再派人来送死了。\n\n但不久前，一个新手副官被派去指挥他们在毒网谷的营地，他开始组织起更有协调性的进攻。我不确定我们还能撑多久，所以我想看到副官桑德斯死掉。\n\n没有他，我们只能指望他们乱到暂时放过我们。药剂师拉尔登一直在问我们有没有砍下副官的头，所以你办完后把头带给他，好让他别再唠叨。",dEN="Being stationed out here, we face constant attack from the Scarlet Crusade. We've held off their attacks thus far so the Apothecaries can do their work, and mostly they've stopped sending their people to their deaths.\n\nBut recently, some upstart Lieutenant got placed in charge of their camp in Venonweb Vale, and he's been organizing more coordinated attacks against us. I'm not sure how much longer we can hold out, so I'd like to see Lieutenant Sanders dead.\n\nWithout him, we can only hope they'll become disorganized enough to leave us alone for now. Apothecary Ralden has been asking constantly if we've taken off the Lieutenant's head, so go bring it to him when you're done so he'll be off our backs.",o="在毒网谷杀死副官桑德斯，并将他的头带给药剂师拉尔登",oEN="Slay Lieutenant Sanders in Venomweb Vale and bring his head to Apothecary Ralden",p="现在又怎么了？我很忙。除非你给我带来了有用的东西或死人，否则别浪费我的时间。",pEN="What is it now? I’m busy. Unless you’ve brought me something useful or dead, don’t waste my time.",c="他死了？真是好消息！\n\n没有他，我想我们没什么好担心的了。几个低阶爪牙无非就是守着营地对付本地野兽。\n\n现在，让我看看他那张脸……\n\n不赖，相当不赖，我能用这个做点文章。",cEN="He's dead? Excellent news!\n\nWithout him, I doubt we'll have much to worry about. Some low ranking fodder won't be doing much more than holding down the camp against the local wildlife.\n\nNow, let's see that face of his...\n\nNot bad, not bad at all, I can work with this."}
Q[254057]={d="好了。完成了。有了这个，血色十字军甚至在为时已晚之前都不会知道自己损失了什么。\n\n现在最后一步是不引起怀疑地把它送进去。副官的头就是为此准备的。\n\n我配制了一种药剂，能让你看起来和他一模一样。它应该能让你顺利进入修道院。只要可以就别靠任何人太近，并保持移动。这类东西并非万无一失，但只要你不做蠢事，就不会有事。\n\n而且千万别想着打架。修道院的守卫可不像那个营地的守卫。他们一击就能把你的内脏撒满草地。如果他们发现你不是他们的副官，他们会毫不犹豫地证明这一点。",dEN="There. It's done. With this, the Scarlet Crusade won't even know they've lost until it's too late.\n\nNow the last step is getting it to them without raising suspicion. That's what the lieutenant's head was for.\n\nI've whipped up an elixir that'll make you look just like him. It should get you into the monastery without much trouble. Just don't get too close to anyone if you can help it, and keep moving. This sort of thing isn't foolproof, but as long as you don't do anything idiotic, you'll be fine.\n\nAnd don't even think about picking a fight. The monastery guards aren't like the ones at that camp. They can scatter your insides across the grass with one swing. If they figure out you aren't their lieutenant, they won't hesitate to prove it.",o="使用拉尔登的变形药剂潜入血色修道院的庭院并污染他们的补给。",oEN="Use Ralden's Transformation Elixir to infiltrate the Scarlet Monastery's courtyard and infect their supplies.",p="你还在这儿做什么？我已经把药剂给你了。用它。动起来。还是你想让我找个更慢的东西来试？",pEN="What are you still doing here? I already gave you the elixir. Use it. Get moving. Or would you rather I test it on something slower?",c="办妥了吗？好，好。我们会从这里盯着，看看它传播得如何。\n\n科学总是需要多次尝试，但即便它不能在此刻就了结那些血色十字军的可怜虫，至少也该削弱他们的队伍，等我们召集到合适的队伍攻打修道院时，他们就更虚弱了。",cEN="It's done? Good, good. We'll keep an eye on them from here and see how well it spreads.\n\nScience always takes a few tries, but even if it doesn't actually wipe out those Scarlet wretches here and now, it should at least trim down their ranks and soften them up for when we get a proper team together for an attack on the monastery."}
Q[254059]={d="你！你不是只来看热闹的吧？你是那种喜欢好好打一场的人，我从你眼里看得出来。\n\n何不上擂台打一场？赢了有财富和荣耀，输了就死得其所。我们还有个新手准备好了；你要是赢了，我就给你找些更有经验的对手。",dEN="You! You aren't just here to spectate, are you? You're the type who likes a good fight, I can see it in your eyes.\n\nWhy don't you give a round in the ring a go? There's wealth and glory in it if you win, and a good death if you lose. We've got another newbie all lined up, if you win I'll get some more experienced opponents for you.",o="击败第一位挑战者：\"低牙\"",oEN="Defeat the first challenger: \"Lowfang\"",p="你在跟我说什么？出去打！",pEN="What are you talking to me for? Get out and fight!",c="哈！我就知道你有真正斗士的料。别担心，低牙只是个开始，我们还有很多更有经验的选手备着。",cEN="Hah! I knew you had it in you to be a real fighter. Don't worry, Lowfang's only the beginning, we've got plenty of more seasoned competitors lined up."}
Q[254060]={d="别以为你现在有多了不起，低牙没有擂台经验，那只是热身。\n\n名单上的下一个是来自尘风部族的鹰身女妖。别一副大惊小怪的样子，只要愿意打，我谁都收，不管擂台外有什么纷争。我没听懂她的真名，但无所谓，她说话带着那种可怕的尖啸，所以她在擂台上的名字是死啸。",dEN="Don't get cocky now, Lowfang had no experience in the ring, he's just a warm-up.\n\nNext in line is a harpy all the way from the Dustwind tribe. Don't act like that's so odd, I'll take anyone willing to fight, doesn't matter what feuds are happening outside the ring. I didn't understand her real name, doesn't matter though, she talked in this horrible screech, so her name in the ring's Deathscreech.",o="击败第二位挑战者：\"死啸\"",oEN="Defeat the second challenger: \"Deathscreech\"",p="你在跟我说什么？出去打！",pEN="What are you talking to me for? Get out and fight!",c="你终于收拾掉那头鹰身女妖了！只要愿意，谁都能打，但她已经让几乎全场观众都为她欢呼了。我倒不介意，人们在乎比赛怎么走，就能带来热度。\n\n我很好奇她一直尖叫的那个「埃瑞西娜女王」是谁，不过那听起来更像是你的麻烦，不是我的。",cEN="You finally got rid of that harpy! Anyone can fight who's willing, but she'd gotten most of the crowd cheering against her. Not that I mind, builds investment if people care how the fight goes.\n\nWonder who that Queen Erethina she always yells about is, but that sounds more like a problem for you than me."}
Q[254061]={d="关于你的传言传得很快，<class>。人群已经叫你「神秘陌生人」，还有人说你能一路打到最后。你不只让粉丝们惊讶。你让他们相信了你。\n\n但到此为止了。最后一轮。\n\n你最后的对手是个行走的灾难。粉碎者。一个食人魔，巨大、残暴、彻底疯癫。他不讲规矩。他毫不留情。如果你能击败他，擂台就是你的了。\n\n全力上场。像个冠军一样走出来。",dEN="Word is spreading fast about you, <class>. The crowd is already calling you the Mysterious Stranger, and some are saying you might go all the way. You have not just surprised the fans. You have made believers out of them.\n\nBut this is it. The final round.\n\nYour last opponent is a walking disaster zone. The Masher. Ogre, massive, mean, and completely unhinged. He does not fight clean. He does not hold back. You beat him and the ring is yours.\n\nGo in strong. Walk out a champion.",o="击败第三位挑战者：\"粉碎者\"",oEN="Defeat the third challenger: \"The Masher\"",p="你在跟我说什么？出去打！",pEN="What are you talking to me for? Get out and fight!",c="那根大棒砸下来的时候，我还以为你会被砸成碎片。看来你比外表结实。观众最爱看弱者逆袭，所以这下效果棒极了。\n\n你给了他们一场好戏。更重要的是，你给了他们一个胜者。\n\n嘿，如果我要开自己的擂台，你该来报名。我保证给你更好的挑战。",cEN="Thought for sure you were gonna splatter when that club came down on you. Guess you are tougher than you look. The crowd loves an underdog, so this works out just fine.\n\nYou gave them a show. More importantly, you gave them a winner.\n\nHey, if I go start up my own ring, you should sign up. I'll give you a better challenge, promise."}
Q[254062]={d="押你赢的赌注越来越多，此前只有另一名斗士正面扛过粉碎者的重锤。一位来自暗矛部族的暗影猎手，她是从竞技场开始打起的；她是目前擂台上最硬的现役斗士。\n\n我们叫她影血。她有死不掉的倾向，也许袖子里藏着什么花招，但那得由你自己去发现了。现任冠军已经好几年没打过了，所以如果你击败她，你就是我们最硬的那个。",dEN="More and more bets are pouring in on you, only one other fighter's stood up to the Masher's hammer before. A Shadow Hunter from the Darkspear tribe who took up fighting in the arena, she's the toughest active fighter of the ring right now.\n\nWe call her Shadowblood. She's got a penchant for not dying, maybe there's a trick up her sleeve, but that's on you to figure out. The actual champion hasn't fought in years, so beat her and you'll be the toughest we've got.",o="击败第四位挑战者：\"影血\"",oEN="Defeat the fourth challenger: \"Shadowblood\"",p="你在跟我说什么？出去打！",pEN="What are you talking to me for? Get out and fight!",c="所以是那些图腾让她能自愈的，对吧？\n\n我当然知道！有点脑子的人都能推断出它们有问题，但破坏惊喜可不是我的职责。斗士们得自己去发现才更刺激；要是你知道有多少人发现不了，你会吃惊的。\n\n看来你有的不只是蛮力，还有脑子。",cEN="So it was the totems letting her heal herself up, was it?\n\nOf course I knew that! Anyone with half a brain could figure up something was up with those, but not my place to ruin the surprise. It's more exciting if the fighters have to figure it out on their own, you'd be surprised how many don't.\n\nGuess you've got brains and not just brawn."}
Q[254063]={d="看来押你赢的人要赚一笔了。你已经击败了我们最好的选手，所以现在只剩一件事。\n\n上擂台，你将被加冕为兽人狂斗赛的最后一位冠军！",dEN="Looks like the ones who bet on you will be getting paid out well. You beat the best we've got, so only one thing's left now.\n\nStep out into the ring and you'll be crowned the latest champion of Orcamania!",o="加冕为兽人狂斗赛冠军",oEN="Be crowned champion of Orcamania",p="你在跟我说什么？出去打！",pEN="What are you talking to me for? Get out and fight!",c="这才叫一场好斗！自从冠军退役后，这里就再没热闹过，不过别怪他，明知会输的时候谁都不想打。但这次，这次会让一切重新变得有趣，而且他们争夺的不只是一位现役冠军。\n\n我想你不会留在这儿吧？真可惜，但我已经知道你们冒险者是什么样了；反正我也没什么能再扔给你了。",cEN="Now that was a fight! Things haven't been the same around here since the champion retired, don't blame him though, no one wanted to fight when they knew they'd lose. But this, this will make things interesting again, and they're fighting for more than active champion.\n\nSuppose you're not sticking around though, are you? A shame, but I know how you adventurer lot are, not like I've got anything left to throw at you."}
Q[254064]={d="你知道，既然你反正要在这一带走动，不如帮我做点事。我是个科学家，不是斗士，你看。遗憾的是，这两种身份交叠的频率比我愿意承认的要高得多。\n\n我们被遗忘者摆脱了天灾，但许多人仍在为它效力。有些人的腐烂程度比这里的大多数——磨坊附近那些——糟糕得多，但另一些则更难解释。我们的黑暗女士当年是名女妖，然而我在这片区域见过仍与天灾相连的女妖。\n\n也许这只是意志的问题。尽管如此，想必总有办法促使至少那些还保有一部分自我的人挣脱巫妖王的束缚，对吧？这就是我理论的基础。遗憾的是，这剂药水已经是我能安全配制的极限了。\n\n也许你可以试试？它应该能引发暂时的力量提升，如果我的论点正确，这也许能给他们一个夺回控制权的机会。实际上，它单用效果甚微，但如果你这样的人先削弱束缚他们的力量，我预计它会有效得多。",dEN="You know, since you're going around these parts anyway, you could help me with something. I'm a scientist, not a fighter, you see. Unfortunately, those are two positions that intersect more often than I care to admit.\n\nWe Forsaken broke free of the Scourge, but many still serve it. Some are in far worse states of decay, like most of the ones around the Mills here, but others prove more difficult to explain. Our Dark Lady was once a banshee, yet I've spotted banshees in this region who remain bound to the Scourge.\n\nPerhaps it's simply a matter of will. Even so, surely there must be a way to nudge at least some who retain a portion of themselves into severing their bond to the Lich King, no? That’s the basis of my theory. Alas, this concoction is as far as I can safely get.\n\nPerhaps you could give it a try? It should instate a temporary surge of power which, if my thesis is correct, might give them a chance to assert control. In practice, it does little on its own, but if someone like you were to weaken the forces binding them first, I'd expect it to prove far more potent.",o="在 3 只僵尸、3 具骷髅、3 名女妖和受折磨的马莱克身上测试罗德·剧毒之击的药水",oEN="Test Rod Toxicstrike's concoction on 3 zombies, 3 skeletons, 3 banshees, and Mallek the Tormented",p="你到目前为止有结果了吗？我明白，这项研究耗时很长；等你完成后我们可以更深入地谈谈。",pEN="Have you received any results thus far? I understand, such research takes much time, we can discuss it further once you've finished.",c="这家伙不久前还在这一带游荡，我猜他是你唯一成功的一个？\n\n考虑到这项研究的性质，即便这一组里只有一个人能挣脱，我也觉得我们够幸运了。从这个角度说，这一个尤其幸运，因为他似乎相当愿意协助我的研究。\n\n一位通晓死灵法术的专家……这也许正是我取得更好结果所需要的。是的，这简直再合适不过了。",cEN="This one wandered over here not too long ago, I take it he was the only one you had any luck with?\n\nGiven the nature of this research, I can count us fortunate even one of this lot was able to break free. For that matter, it is more fortunate for this one in particular, for he seems quite willing to aid in my research.\n\nAn expert on the necromantic arts...this might just be precisely what I need to achieve better results. Yes, this will do just fine."}
Q[254065]={d="在这附近小心脚下。这些森林里仍遍布狼人，而尽管我看起来不过是又一具尸体，连我也更希望自己的四肢保持连在身上。\n\n我是来研究他们的。至少比在焚木村附近游荡安全。这顶帽子有用。它能掩盖气味。让他们困惑到不会扑向我。\n\n老实说，我已经过了研究阶段。我想我已经弄清了如何压制这个诅咒。不是治愈它。是压制它。但我缺乏更进一步所需的资源。琥珀磨坊拒绝了我。说什么要把我送回坟墓。真是贴心。\n\n而你，也许运气会更好。我需要三样东西。一个稳定的魔法能量源。某种能与诅咒相互作用的东西。以及一种能让附魔通过翡翠梦境引导的媒介。最后这部分很棘手，但我记得达拉然的法师们收藏着各种稀奇古怪的小玩意。他们多半有能用的东西。\n\n如果你能把我要的东西带给我，也许我们就能找到掌控这病痛的办法。",dEN="Watch your step around here. These woods are still crawling with Worgen, and while I might look like just another corpse, even I prefer my limbs attached.\n\nI came out here to study them. Safer than poking around Pyrewood, at least. The hat helps. Masks the scent. Keeps them confused enough not to pounce.\n\nTruth is, I am past the studying phase. I think I have cracked how to suppress the curse. Not cure. Suppress. But I lack the resources to go further. Ambermill turned me away. Said something about sending me back to the grave. Charming, really.\n\nYou, though, you might have better luck. I need three things. A stable source of magical power. Something that interacts with curses. And a means to channel enchantments through the Emerald Dream. That last part is tricky, but I remember the magi in Dalaran collecting all kinds of strange trinkets. Odds are they have something that could work.\n\nIf you can bring me what I need, we might just have a way to tame this affliction.",o="收集一根诅咒束缚法杖、一块奥术增幅水晶以及一个来自琥珀磨坊的奇特捕梦网，以帮助完善莉莉的装置。",oEN="Gather a Curse-Binding Rod, an Arcane Amplification Crystal, and a Curious Dreamcatcher from Ambermill to help complete Lilly's device.",p="达拉然的人相当友善，我在那里学到了附魔的基础，那是些美好的回忆。\n\n你遇到守卫时，就告诉他们是洛丹伦来的，效忠于游侠将军希尔瓦娜斯；他们一直与我们王国和奎尔萨拉斯关系良好，所以这样说应该能说明一切。",pEN="Dalaran folks are nice enough, I learned the basics of enchanting back there, fond memories.\n\nWhen you meet the guards, just tell them you're from Lordaeron and you're loyal to Ranger General Sylvanas, they always had good relations with our kingdom and with Quel'thalas so that should clear everything up.",c="看到了吧？我就说你运气会更好！要是我能有件更严实遮住骨头的衣服大概也有帮助，看来最近在幽暗城我只能找到这些；时尚潮流，我一向讨厌。\n\n总之，让我看看……\n\n是的，我完全能用这个。给我一点时间，好吗？",cEN="See? I knew you'd have better luck! It'd probably help if I had clothes that covered up my bones better, seems like this is all I can find in the Undercity anymore, fashion trends, always hated them.\n\nAnyways, let me take a look...\n\nYes, I can work with these just fine. Give me a few moments, will you?"}
Q[254066]={d="成了。一个精巧的附魔织物，能量源、诅咒束缚矩阵，甚至还有一点梦境物质。如果理论正确，这应该能恢复狼人的神智，或者至少给他们一个抵抗疯狂的机会。\n\n它必须放在靠近村庄的高处。那座建筑的上层应该可以。从那里，附魔就能笼罩整个区域。\n\n不，我不去。这顶帽子只有在安全距离外才有效，而我希望我的四肢就待在它们现在的位置。\n\n你只管进去，放好它，让它充能，然后离开。对你这样的人来说相当简单，对吧？",dEN="There it is. A delicate weave of enchantments, power sources, cursebinding arrays, even a little dreamstuff. If theory holds, this should restore the Worgen’s senses or at least give them a chance to resist the madness.\n\nIt needs to be placed somewhere high, close to the village. The upper floor of that structure should work. From there, the enchantments can saturate the area.\n\nAnd no, I am not going. This hat only works from a safe distance, and I prefer my limbs exactly where they are.\n\nJust get in, set it down, let it charge, and get out. Simple enough for someone like you, right?",o="将莉莉的装置安装在附近房屋的顶部，并保护它直到启动。",oEN="Install Lilly's device at the top of the nearby house, then protect it until it activates.",p="它需要一段时间来充能，所以确保那些狼人在它完成之前别对它做什么。\n\n我不确定狼人就算把复杂的附魔装置摆在面前能不能认出来，反正我怀疑他们也不在乎那花了多少功夫。",pEN="It will take some time to charge up, so do make sure those worgen don't do anything to it until they're done.\n\nI'm not sure a worgen would know a complex enchanted device if it bit them, doubt they'd care how much work went into it either way.",c="他们也许还没恢复意识，但你看，他们不再是狼人了！作为第一次尝试，我会把它算作成功。\n\n也许这样反而更好；最近因为那堵大墙之类的事，与吉尔尼斯的关系似乎有点紧张。我会做更多测试，趁他们这样的时候看看还能学到什么，那部分应该更安全。\n\n你帮了大忙，谢谢！",cEN="They might be out cold, but look, not worgen anymore! For a first try I'll call that a success.\n\nMaybe this is for the better, relationships with Gilneas have seemed a bit rough recently with the big wall and all. I'll do some more tests and see what else I can learn while they're out like this, that part should be safer.\n\nYou were a big help, thanks!"}
Q[254067]={d="所以你也对她感兴趣，是吗？\n\n她在袭击后不久就消失了；有人说她死了，也有人说她只是退隐到艾泽拉斯某个安静的角落去了，如果真有那种地方的话。\n\n我必须弄清楚！她救了我的命，正是她让我最初想在这里求学……我欠她太多，可我甚至不知道她后来怎么了。我读遍了塔里所有的书，但内容都一样。\n\n不过你看起来是那种爱冒险的人。也许你能找到我遗漏的东西？只是，求你了，你要是打听到什么，一定要告诉我！",dEN="So you're interested in her too, are you?\n\nShe disappeared not long after the attack, some say she died, some say she just retired off in a quiet corner of Azeroth, if there even is such a thing.\n\nI need to know! She saved my life, she's the reason I wanted to study here to begin with...I owe her so much but I don't even know what happened to her. I've read through every book in the tower but it's all the same.\n\nYou seem like the adventuring sort though. Maybe you can find something I missed? Just, please, tell me if you learn anything!",o="在三角塔和湖畔镇寻找关于大法师米奈维亚法杖的线索。",oEN="Search the Three Corners Tower and Lakeshire for clues to Archmage Minervia's staff.",p="这是危险的时代，已经有一阵子了。要不要我给你来点喝的？",pEN="These are dangerous times, have been for a while now. Can I get you anything to drink?",c="大法师米奈维亚，是吗？通常我只从我女儿嘴里听到这个名字。\n\n所罗门似乎有点忘了；我的女儿在袭击中失踪了，是的，我们都以为最坏的情况发生了。可几周后她出现了，安然无恙，不停地说米奈维亚如何救了她的命。\n\n小亚历克斯去路尽头的塔里求学了；如果你碰到她，告诉她我想她，好吗？",cEN="Archmage Minervia is it? I usually only hear that name from my daughter.\n\nSolomon seems to have forgotten a bit, my daughter went missing in the attack, yes, we did all fear the worst. She showed up a couple weeks later though, perfectly healthy, raving about how Minervia saved her life.\n\nLittle Alex is off studying at the tower down the road now, if you run into her, tell her I love her, will you?"}
Q[254068]={d="所以是她让你来查这事的，对吧？我早该想到。我真希望多年前就告诉她真相，但我从不知道什么时候才是合适的时机。答应我，这事你先替我保密，好吗？最好等她下次回来探访时由我亲口告诉她。\n\n大法师米奈维亚是我的母亲，我知道她以伟大的大法师之名闻名，之类之类的，但我还小的时候，她就离开了，直到那次袭击我才再听到她的消息，而即便那时也没多少时间交谈。我恨过她一阵子，但我想她救了亚历克斯，就是她弥补的方式，你知道吗？很难对一个救了你女儿性命的人怀恨在心。\n\n而且，最后我知道了原因，她有一段黑暗的过往。尽管她逃离了那段过去，我认为她从未真正完全信任过自己。她大概觉得我不在她身边会更安全……\n\n你可以去伊尔加拉塔查一查，我想她当年所属的那个团体还在那里，所以也许你能找到点什么。",dEN="So she was the one that sent you on this, was she? I really should've known. Wish I'd just told her the truth years ago, but I never knew when the right time was. Promise you'll keep this to yourself for now, will you, it'd be better she hears it from me next time she visits.\n\nArchmage Minervia is my mother, I know she's known as a great archmage and all, but when I was a boy, she ran off, didn't hear from her again until that attack, and even then there wasn't much time to talk. I hated her for a while, but I think her saving Alex was her way of making amends, you know? Hard to really hold a grudge against someone who saved my daughter's life.\n\nBesides, I did learn why eventually, she had a dark past. Even though she escaped that, I don't think she ever quite trusted herself. Probably thought I was safer without her around...\n\nYou might try poking around the Tower of Ilgalar, I think the group she was with is still there, so you might find something.",o="调查伊尔加拉塔，寻找大法师米奈维亚失踪的线索。",oEN="Investigate the Tower of Ilgalar for clues to Archmage Minervia's disappearance.",p="我的一个朋友失踪了。莫甘斯总是给我们这些只想学习阿佐拉智慧的人制造麻烦……",pEN="Friend of mine went missing. Morganth is always causing trouble for those of us who simply wish to learn from Azora's wisdom...",c="嗯，在这里看到一张友善的面孔当然是好事。你在塔里的时候，该不会看到另一个侏儒吧？没有？\n\n那么也许不是莫甘斯找到了把它藏起来不被人看见的办法……\n\n我相信我会找到他的，毕竟阿佐拉的力量站在我这边。既然你替我免去了探索这地方的麻烦，也许我能帮你点什么作为回报？\n\n我总是乐于与像你这样的旅人分享阿佐拉的智慧。",cEN="Well it sure is good to see a friendly face out here. I don't suppose you saw another gnome while you were in the tower, did you? No?\n\nMaybe it really wasn't Morganth finding a way to hide him from the eye then...\n\nI'm sure I'll find him, Azora's power is on my side after all. Since you saved me the trouble of scouting this place, maybe I could help you with something in return?\n\nI am always pleased to share the wisdom of Azora with travelers like yourself."}
Q[254069]={d="……米奈维亚？\n\n哇，这名字我很多年没听过了。既然你在这里，看来你对她已经有了相当清楚的了解。\n\n在莫甘斯成为伊尔加拉法师之前，统治这座塔的是一位研习黑暗技艺的学者，名叫米奈维亚。她许多年前曾在达拉然师从法师泰奥克里图斯，尽管她是我们的敌人，他却总是满怀钦佩地谈起她。就在多年前，他终于成功向她传达了阿佐拉的智慧，而我们最大的敌人便退出了伊尔加拉的道路。\n\n无论她做过什么，我们寻求的只是启迪，而非复仇，我们所有人都对这个结果非常满意。泰奥克里图斯更是如此。\n\n尽管如此，泰奥克里图斯曾说过，即便在那时，那段过往也一直纠缠着她的新生活。我不知道她后来怎样了，但我只希望她最终能与那段过往和解，找到属于自己的安宁。",dEN="...Minervia?\n\nNow there's a name I haven't heard for years. If you're here, it seems you've got a pretty good idea about her.\n\nBefore Morganth became the Mage of Ilgalar, the one who ruled this tower was a scholar of dark magics by the name of Minervia. She had studied with Mage Theocritus in Dalaran many years before, and though she was our enemy, he always spoke of her with admiration. It was years ago now that he finally managed to bring Azora's wisdom to her, and our greatest enemy turned away from Ilgalar's path.\n\nWhatever she may have done, we seek only enlightenment, not vengeance, and all amongst us were most pleased with this outcome. Theocritus most of all.\n\nStill, Theocritus has spoken of how much that past haunted her new life even still. I don't know what became of her, but I only hope she was able to find her own peace with that past in the end.",o="调查湖畔镇的坟墓。",oEN="Investigate the grave at Lakeshire.",p="你已经找到什么了吗？",pEN="Have you found anything yet?",c="它真美！毫无疑问就是她那天握着的同一根法杖。\n\n我……我明白了。我想我内心深处一直都知道。关于与她有血缘关系，我是说，我不能说我早就猜到过她走进了地脉去改变历史。\n\n……为了我……\n\n我想我需要些时间好好想想这一切，大概需要很久，还要去一趟湖畔镇。我会没事的，别担心，你做得够多了。谢谢你。\n\n我会继续在这里学习，我想这也是她所希望的。也许有一天，我甚至能找到解放她的办法。",cEN="It's beautiful! This is certainly the same staff she held that day.\n\nI...I see. I suppose a part of me always knew. About being related to her, that is, I can't say I would have guessed on my own that she entered the leylines to change history.\n\n...For me...\n\nI think I need to take some time to think about all this, a lot of time probably, and a visit to Lakeshire. I'll be fine though, don't worry, you've done a lot. Thank you.\n\nI'll keep studying here, I think it's what she would have wanted. Maybe I'll even find a way to free her, one day."}
Q[254070]={d="我是秘密法典，我能帮你发现这个世界的真相，直到你领悟它的本质。我也是你通往许多人或许会视为\"禁忌\"的知识的向导。\n\n啊，可悲的是，我的使命近来变得有些混乱了。一头觊觎我知识的该死兽人，对自己的好处太过急躁，撕下了我的一页，真是彻头彻尾的野蛮行径！事实证明她完全不配得到我慷慨的恩赐！\n\n如今她在石堡要塞附近一座塔的高处研读它；我对其他那些蠢货毫不在意，但我希望她因自己的傲慢而死，最重要的是，把我的书页拿回来。\n\n我相信你是远比她文明的那类人。",dEN="I am the Codex of Secrets and I can help you uncover the truth of this world until you have come to understand its nature. I'm also your guide to knowledge that many might consider \"forbidden\".\n\nAh, but alas, my purpose has become somewhat muddled of late. An accursed orc who sought my knowledge proved far too impatient for her own good, and ripped out one of my pages, such absoluate barbarism! She has proven entirely unworthy of my generous gifts!\n\nShe now studies it atop a tower near Stonewatch Keep, I hardly care for the rest of those fools, but I would see her slain for her arrogance and most importantly, my lost page recovered.\n\nI trust you are the far more civilized sort?",o="取回秘密法典失去的书页。",oEN="Recover the Codex of Secrets' lost page.",p="你处理掉那个兽人了吗？最重要的是，你拿到我失去的书页了吗？我能感到它的缺失，如同脊骨里的一根木刺。如果你带在身上，立刻拿来。如果没有，你究竟在等什么？",pEN="Have you dealt with the orc? More importantly, do you have my missing page? I can feel its absence like a splinter in my spine. If you carry it now, bring it forth at once. If not, then what exactly are you waiting for?",c="我又完整了！\n\n你为我立了大功，所以理应以我秘密的一小部分作为报酬，但这次只是个样本。你还太稚嫩，我不想伤害你的心智。\n\n我们还会再见，也许不会很快，因为我还有许多要与这座塔里的其他人分享，但那一刻终会到来，我现在确信这一点。",cEN="I am whole once more!\n\nYou have done me a great service, and so it is only fair I reward you with a small portion of my secrets, but only a taste, for now. You are inexperienced yet, and I do not wish to damage your mind.\n\nWe shall meet again, perhaps not soon, for I have much left to share with the others of this tower, but the time will come, of that I am now certain."}
Q[254071]={d="好吧，在等贾斯珀终于醒来的这段时间，我可以做点别的事。\n\n我一直在试图更多地了解这片区域的黑龙，以及兽人似乎如何让它们成了盟友。\n\n他们在森林深处有一处巢穴，从蛋里孵化新的幼崽，但那里戒备森严。如果你能穿过他们的防线，我就能从他们最好的蛋里获取最有价值的信息。",dEN="Well, I might as well work on something else while I wait for for Jasper to finally wake up.\n\nI've been trying to learn more about the black dragons of this region, and how the orcs seem to have made them into allies.\n\nThey have a rookery deep in the woods where they raise new whelps from eggs, but it's closely guarded. If you do manage to get through them, I'd get the best information from the best egg they have.",o="取得一枚完好的黑龙蛋",oEN="Obtain a Pristine Black Dragon Egg",p="你拿到蛋了吗？贾斯珀还在沉睡，所以看起来不太着急。",pEN="Have you gotten an egg yet? Jasper is still fast asleep, so it doesn't look like there's any rush.",c="是的，这就完全合适了。你眼光不错。\n\n贾斯珀短暂醒过一次，但我还没讲完奥术飞弹的基本原理，他又睡着了。\n\n有这么一个懒学生唯一的好处就是，只要我能无视他的鼾声集中精神，就有大把时间做自己的研究。",cEN="Yes, that will work perfectly. You have a good eye.\n\nJasper woke up briefly but he fell asleep again before I could get halfway through explaining the basic principles of Arcane Missiles.\n\nThe only good thing about having such a lazy student is that it gives me plenty of time for my own research, as long as I can focus through his snoring."}
Q[254072]={d="星尘废墟曾是圣地。我第一次造访时，那是我见过最美的地方之一。\n\n唉，万物皆有终。北方土地的腐化渗入了水域，早已被遗弃的圣殿也倾颓成了废墟。就连植物也陷入狂怒；它们在受苦，却不明白为什么，于是攻击任何靠近的人。\n\n如果不尽快制止，它会蔓延。我们有净化这种腐化的仪式，但圣殿太危险了。我教派的大多数人是治疗者，不是战斗者，因此我们能做的很少。\n\n我恳求你，让那些被唤醒的植物安息；它们理应得到安宁，而没有它们，废墟也会更安全，也许安全到让我们能够开始。",dEN="The Ruins of Stardust were holy once. When I first visited, it was one of the most beautiful places I'd seen.\n\nAlas, all things must come to an end. Corruption from the northern lands has seeped into the waters, the already abandoned shrine has crumbled into ruins. Even the plants are enraged, they suffer, yet they cannot understand why, so they lash out against anyone who comes close.\n\nIf it is not stopped soon, it will spread. We have a ritual to purify such corruption, but the shrine is too dangerous. Most of my sect are healers, not fighters, therefore there is little we can do.\n\nI beseech you, lay to rest the plants that have awakened, they deserve peace, and without them the ruins will become safer, perhaps safe enough for us to begin.",o="在星尘废墟击败影棘 creatures",oEN="Defeat Shadethicket creatures at the Ruins of Stardust",p="腐化深深渗入了那个地方。这不会是件容易的事，但这也正是它更该被完成的理由。",pEN="The corruption runs deep within that place. This will not be an easy task, but that is all the more reason it must be done.",c="它们当年也很美。\n\n但愿我们也能净化它们，但如果安宁是我们能为这些生物做的最好的事，我很高兴至少能给予它们这个。",cEN="They, too, were once beautiful.\n\nI only wish we could have cleansed them as well, but if peace is the best we can do for those creatures, I am glad we can at least give them that."}
Q[254073]={d="恐怕我们还得请你帮更多的忙。\n\n尽管废墟眼下也许能安全行走，但我们的仪式只能抽取腐化；我们需要有人在场，摧毁我们掘出的东西。\n\n你已经证明了你的力量，所以如果你能再为我们抽出一点时间，请到废墟中央的月碗处与我们汇合；我们将在那里用月神艾露恩残存的力量举行仪式。\n\n摧毁冒出来的一切，别让它们摧毁我们自身的力量，好让那里的土地终于能开始愈合。",dEN="I am afraid we must still ask more of you.\n\nThough the ruins may be safe to walk within for the time being, our ritual only draws out the corruption, we need someone to be there to destroy what we unearth.\n\nYou have already proven your strength, so if you could spare us more of your time yet, please meet us at the moonbowl in the center of the ruins, we will use what remains of Elune's power there for the ritual.\n\nDestroy what comes forth, and prevent it from destroying our own power, so that the land there might finally begin to heal.",o="完成仪式，净化星尘废墟",oEN="Complete the ritual to purify the Ruins of Stardust",p="腐化深深渗入了那个地方。这不会是件容易的事，但这也正是它更该被完成的理由。",pEN="The corruption runs deep within that place. This will not be an easy task, but that is all the more reason it must be done.",c="那个地方真正改变还需要很久，但至少现在腐化的根须已经消失，它会开始缓慢愈合。假以时日，也许圣殿甚至能重建，你也能再次见到它昔日的美景。\n\n愿玛洛恩指引你，朋友。",cEN="It will be a long time yet before that place truly changes, but at least now the roots of the corruption is gone, and it will slowly start to heal. In time, perhaps, the shrine can even be rebuilt, and you can see its former beauty once more.\n\nMay Malorne guide you, friend."}
Q[254074]={d="我看到你眼里的那种神情。你不是那种会在这儿久留的人。没关系。我不会要你做出承诺，但既然你在这儿，也许想接份快活干？报酬不错，有点危险。看起来正合你的胃口。\n\n老实说，我们接了一份合同，要从附近的墓穴取回一件古老的矮人遗物。本该是进去再出来那么简单。但不管下面有什么，我一直在折损人手，说实话，这真的开始影响我的利润了。我不能一直把好雇佣兵往黑暗里送，可要是我现在收手，就会传开我们完不成活儿的闲话。\n\n那件遗物叫铁须圣像。把它带回来，我按你完成整份合同来付钱。那么，怎么样？你干不干？",dEN="I can see that look in your eyes. You are not the type to stick around. That's fine. I won't ask you to sign on, but maybe you're up for a quick job while you are here? Good pay, bit of danger. Seems like your kind of deal.\n\nTruth is, we took a contract to recover some old dwarven relic from the tomb nearby. Should have been a simple In and out. But I keep losing people to whatever is down there, and to be honest, it's really starting to cut into my bottom line. I can't keep tossing good mercs into the dark, but if I back out now, word gets out that we don't finish jobs.\n\nThe relic is called the Icon of Ironbeard. You bring it back, and I will pay you like you were on the full contract. So what do you say? You in?",o="取回铁须圣像",oEN="Recover the Icon of Ironbeard",p="它应该是像一个小圆盘，上面刻着花纹。\n\n我听说他的斧头更值钱，但活儿就是活儿，轮不到我质疑雇主的意愿，我只负责派个能办成事的人去。\n\n我希望那个人是你，因为眼下这些莽夫里显然没一个行。",pEN="Should be a small disc thing with an engraving.\n\nHeard his axe was worth more, but a job's a job, it ain't my place to question the employer's wants, just to send someone who can get it done.\n\nHoping that's you, 'cause it sure ain't any of these brutes right now.",c="对，就是这个。很高兴看到你没让软泥把你的脸化掉。\n\n我是个说话算话的地精，所以这是你的报酬。如果你哪天想正式加入我们商队，尽管开口，好吗？",cEN="Yeah, that's the thing alright. Good to see ya didn't get your face melted in by slimes.\n\nI'm a goblin of my word, so here's your pay. If ya ever do feel like joining the company proper, just ask, alright?"}
Q[254075]={d="嘿，上一份合同你干得不错。再来一份怎么样？\n\n同样的条件。全额报酬，不问问题。这份是米奈希尔港的一些人找上门的。他们想清掉沼泽道路上的苔皮豺狼人。轻松的活儿，应该不会出问题。\n\n问题是我们自己队伍里现在也有苔皮豺狼人。不多，但够多了。让他们去攻击自己的同族？这可不太合适。哪怕只是提一提都可能引起骚动，而不满传播起来比钱还快。\n\n我不能冒这个险。这帮家伙话太多，一句错话就会变成十句。所以我的要求是这样。你来处理。悄悄地。别让人看见地干完，豺狼人们就什么都不用知道。\n\n你拿钱，我去港口领功，这儿谁都不会骚动。成交？",dEN="Say, you did good work on that last contract. How'd you feel about takin' on another?\n\nSame deal. Full pay, no questions. This one came in from some folks out at Menethil Harbor. They want the Mosshide gnolls cleared out from the marsh roads. Easy job, should be no trouble.\n\nProblem is, we've got Mosshides in our own ranks now. Not many, but enough. Asking them to attack their own kin? That would not sit well. Even bringing it up could stir things up, and discontent spreads faster than coin.\n\nI cannot risk that. This crew talks too much, and one wrong word turns into ten. So here's the ask. You handle it. Quietly. Get the job done out of sight, and none of the gnolls have to know a thing.\n\nYou get paid, I get credit with the harbor, and nobody here gets riled up. Deal?",o="杀死沼泽地的苔皮豺狼人",oEN="Slay Mosshide Gnolls in Wetlands",p="我让他们签了合同之类的，可你觉得豺狼人懂什么叫合同吗？\n\n有合同没合同，他们要是走了或者反过来对付我，对谁都没好处，尤其对我。",pEN="I had them sign a contract and everything, but ya think gnolls understand contracts?\n\nContract or no, if they walk out or turn on me, that's bad for everyone, especially me.",c="我们时不时会有点小挫折，但黑木总能想办法搞定。\n\n我是认真的，你要是哪天厌倦了冒险者的生活，会是个好雇佣兵。\n\n总之，拿着钱，你帮我们解了几次围，所以如果你哪天需要支援，可以享受我们服务九折优惠，算是额外奖励！",cEN="Sometimes we hit a hitch now and then, but Blackwood always gets it done one way or another.\n\nI'm serious, you'd make a good merc if ya ever got tired of the adventuring life.\n\nAnyways, take the money, you've gotten us out of a couple tight spots now, so if ya ever need some backup, you can have a 10% discount on our services as a bonus!"}
Q[254076]={d="龙是个麻烦，你知道吗？它们总跑来对我的公羊喷火！它们被烧焦皮毛这事可相当恼火。\n\n你觉得你能不能在这些恶龙长大、变成真正威胁之前教训教训它们？",dEN="Dragons are bad news ye see, keep comin' here breathin' fire all over me rams! Bothers 'em quite a lot getting their fur all singed like that.\n\nThink ye could teach some of those bad dragons a lesson 'fore they get bigger and become a real menace?",o="杀死沼泽地的红色雏龙、迷失雏龙和赤红雏龙",oEN="Slay Red Whelps, Lost Whelps, and Crimson Whelps in Wetlands",p="这些公羊也许相当勇猛，但它们对会飞的东西没什么办法。",pEN="These rams might be plenty feisty, but ain't much they can do about somethin' that flies.",c="剩下的最好在骚扰我的公羊之前三思！只要它们待在自己那侧的河边，其余的都可以留下。",cEN="The rest had better think twice about botherin' me rams! Long as they keep tae their side of the river now the rest can stay."}
Q[254077]={d="冒险者！我有几只公羊跑散了！\n\n这一带的土地对公羊来说一点都不安全，你知道吗？我简直不敢想，要是那些公羊被沼泽里的居民压死，或者被鳄鱼吃掉，又或者被豺狼人活烤了会怎样……\n\n我们是农夫，不是战士，你能帮我把公羊平安带回来吗？",dEN="Adventurer! Some of me rams have run amok!\n\nThe lands around here ain't safe for rams in the slightest ye see, I can't bear to think what'll happen if those rams get pounded to death by fen dwellers, or eaten by crocolisks, or roasted alive by gnolls...\n\nWe're farmers, not fighters, would ye please bring me rams back safe?",o="把走失的公羊带回公羊牧场",oEN="Return the lost rams to Ram Ranch",p="你们还在这儿干什么？快出去帮我找公羊，别让它们受伤！",pEN="What are ye doin' here still? Get out and find me rams 'fore they get hurt!",c="就这些了！看来你很擅长对付公羊。",cEN="That be all of 'em! Ye seem tae have a way with rams alright."}
Q[254078]={d="随着时间推移，即便最凶猛的生物也能学会信任，但前提是我们得趁早开始。\n\n在这些山峰上空盘旋的双足飞龙骄傲而强壮，但大多数都太野性，不肯接受骑手。如今我们把目光投向尚未孵化的那些。悉心养大，它们有可能把部落视为家人，而非威胁。\n\n悬崖上散布着巢穴。如果你找到完好无损的蛋，就把它带到高风要塞。我们会照料它们成长，尽力引导它们。",dEN="In time, even the fiercest creature may learn to trust, but only if we begin early.\n\nThe wyverns that soar above these peaks are proud and strong, but most are too wild to accept riders. It is the unhatched we look to now. Raised with care, they may come to see the Horde as kin, not as a threat.\n\nThere are nests scattered along the cliffs. If you find any eggs still whole, bring them to Highwind Hold. We will see to their growth and guide them as best we can.",o="为高风要塞的布拉穆克·地蹄收集 10 枚双足飞龙蛋",oEN="Collect 10 Wyvern eggs for Brammuk Earthhoof at Highwind Hold",p="这一带应该有很多双足飞龙蛋，不过你可能得跟成年双足飞龙搏斗才能拿到。很遗憾，但我们没有轻松驯养它们的办法。",pEN="There should be many wyvern eggs around these lands, though you may have to fight through the grown wyverns to obtain them. It is regrettable, but we do not have the means to train them as easily.",c="这些都是极好的蛋，你眼光不错。\n\n别担心，在这里它们会被善待，假以时日，它们或许会成为部落人民优秀的坐骑或伙伴。\n\n高风要塞感谢你的帮助。",cEN="These are fine eggs indeed, you have a keen eye.\n\nDo not worry, they will be treated well here, and in time they may become fine mounts or companions for the people of the Horde.\n\nYou have the gratitude of Highwind Hold for your assistance."}
Q[254079]={d="我本该来调查这些废墟的，那些纳迦肯定在图谋什么。但那些深处正在发生的事，比他们寻常的阴谋更令人担忧。\n\n我见过好几个施法者走进废墟，至今没出来。那些守卫既警觉又可怕；既然他们能击败赛莱斯……我肯定毫无胜算。\n\n抛开伤势不谈，我不能辜负我的使命。也许你运气更好，能查明他们在下面做什么；我只求你，千万别伤着自己。",dEN="I was supposed to investigate these ruins, those naga are definitely up to something. But whatever is going on in those depths is more concerning than their usual schemes.\n\nI've seen several spellcasters going deep into the ruins, and they still haven't come back out. Those guards are vigilant, and terrifying, if they managed to get the better of Cylaeth... I certainly don't stand a chance.\n\nInjuries aside, I cannot fail my mission. Perhaps you will have better luck figuring out what they're doing down there - just please, don't get hurt.",o="调查玛瑟斯拉废墟中怒鳞纳迦的活动",oEN="Investigate the Stormscale activity at the Ruins of Mathysra",p="你成功进入废墟了吗？你在下面发现了什么，更重要的是……我们有危险吗？",pEN="Did you make it into the ruins? What did you find down there, and more importantly… are we in danger?",c="这看起来像是某种仪式的计划……\n\n而且从现场聚集了这么多施法者来看，还是相当强大的仪式……这可不妙。\n\n感谢艾露恩，你及时赶到了，我们必须立刻通知队长并带一支更大的队伍过来！",cEN="This looks to be plans for a ritual of some kind...\n\nAnd a powerful one as well from the looks of this, with how many spellcasters have gathered here... This isn't good.\n\nThank Elune you got here when you did, we must inform the Captain and get a larger party here immediately!"}
Q[254080]={d="我——我害她受了伤，她突然出现，替我挡下了那一击……我……\n\n我不能再——我绝不能再容忍这些纳迦继续存在下去了。不，不，在她们对她做出那种事之后！去杀了她们，打伤凯莱斯的就是那些大块头中的一个。\n\n我不敢离开她身边，求你，替我报仇——但要小心。如果她们能击败一名资深哨兵……现在我知道她们有多大能耐了。",dEN="I- I let her get hurt, she came in from nowhere and took the blow for me... I...\n\nI won't- I CAN'T tolerate the presence of these naga any longer. Not not after what they've done to her! Go kill them, it was one of those large brutes that struck Cylaeth.\n\nI dare not leave her side, please, take revenge for me - and be careful. If they can best a veteran sentinel... I know now what they're capable of.",o="在玛希斯拉遗迹击败龙鳞护卫者",oEN="Defeat Stormscale Protectors at the Ruins of Mathysra",p="你解决她们了吗……？你把她们都杀光了吗？",pEN="Did you get them...? Did you kill them all?",c="很好……在让卡多雷流血之后，那些怪物不配活着。\n\n谢谢你……替我做了我做不到的事。",cEN="Good... after spilling Kal'dorei blood those monsters don't get to live.\n\nThank you... for doing what I could not."}
Q[254081]={d="我们派了一个人去东北方的玛希斯拉遗迹调查——本该只是一次简单的侦察任务，可她到现在还没回来。\n\n这是法德里丝第一次在没有姐姐陪同的情况下执行这样的任务，我们几个人已经开始担心了。\n\n你能去看看她吗？",dEN="We sent one of our own to investigate the Ruins of Mathysra to the north-east - it was supposed to be a simple scouting mission, but she hasn't been back yet.\n\nThis is Fadrieth's first time doing a mission like this without her sister, and a few of us are starting to worry.\n\nWould you mind checking up on her?",o="在玛希斯拉遗迹寻找哨兵法德里丝·月刃",oEN="Find Sentinel Fadrieth Moonblade at the Ruins of Mathysra",c="是格林达派你来查看我的情况？\n\n她有时候比泰莎还要过度保护，不过，我还是很感激。我在这里没事，但除了观察之外，我自己也做不了什么了。",cEN="Glynda sent you to check on me?\n\nShe can be more overprotective than Tysha sometimes, still, I do appreciate it. I'm fine here, but there's not much more I can do on my own besides watch."}
Q[254082]={d="你外出狩猎的时候，我能请你帮个忙吗？\n\n我的老朋友兼保镖里昂内尔跟我一起加入了远征队。他似乎也很享受这种节奏的变化；他在附近搭了个自己的小营地，还带回了不少上等的猎物。\n\n不过，像那样独自扎营很危险，而且他已经有段时间没来这边了，我开始有些担心。赫米特老是笑我多虑，说他大概是猎得入迷了，可他一向在该求助的时候不肯开口。\n\n你能去看看他吗，如果他没事，顺便叫他多来走动走动？",dEN="Could I ask you for a favor while you're out hunting?\n\nMy old bodyguard friend Lyonel joined the expedition with me. He seems to be enjoying the change of pace as well, he setup his own small camp near here, and he's been bringing in quite a few fine hunts.\n\nStill, camping on his own like that is dangerous, and it's been a while since he last came by here, and it's starting to worry me. Hemet keeps laughing me off and saying he's probably deep in the hunt, but he's got a tendency of not asking for help when he should.\n\nMind checking up on him, maybe tell him to stop on by a bit more if he's alright?",o="奈辛瓦里远征队的S·J·厄尔加丁爵士想让你去查看里昂内尔的营地。",oEN="Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to check on Lyonel's camp.",p="有里昂内尔的消息了吗？\n\n我当初真不该让他一个人那样离开……",pEN="Any news of Lyonel yet?\n\nI should've never let him go off on his own like that...",c="<营地里没有里昂内尔的踪迹，只有木桌上那份煮好却没动过的饭。没有哪个求生者会无缘无故让食物烂掉，里昂内尔一定是匆忙离开的。尽管如此，他临时搭起的路障外满地都是黑豹的尸体；它们似乎构不成多大威胁，所以也许是别的东西找到了这座营地。>",cEN="<There is no sign of Lyonel at the camp, only the cooked yet uneaten meal sitting on the wooden table. No survivalist would leave food to rot without a good reason, Lyonel must have left in a hurry. Still, the corpses of panthers line ground beyond his makeshift barricades, it doesn't seem that they posed much threat, so perhaps something else found the camp.>"}
Q[254083]={d="<经过仔细搜寻，你发现了几道被人高的野草遮掩的类人生物足迹。它们似乎通向东方。也许里昂内尔试图回到远征队的营地？>",dEN="<With careful searching, you find several humanoid tracks concealed by the grass. They seem to lead towards the east. Perhaps Lyonel tried to make it back to the expedition's camp?>",o="寻找里昂内尔。",oEN="Search for Lyonel.",p="你找到里昂内尔了吗？他还好吗？",pEN="Have you found Lyonel yet? Is he alright?",c="<他一言不发，直到把那封信读完。>\n\n有一点你说对了，里昂内尔。你是个傻瓜，我不再是那个手无寸铁的贵族小姐了，那些日子早已过去，没有理由再念念不忘……\n\n所以是那些巨魔害死了他，是吗？赫米特说我们只猎杀野兽，可那些野人在荆棘谷里跟任何野兽没什么两样，我要把他们一个不剩地全部猎杀。",cEN="<He is silent until he finishes reading the note.>\n\nYou were right about one thing, Lyonel. You are a fool, I'm not a helpless noble anymore, those days are long past and there's no reason to keep clinging to them...\n\nSo it was the trolls that got him, was it? Hemet said we only hunt beasts, but those savages are as much beasts as anything else in Stranglethorn, and I'll hunt down every last one of them."}
Q[254084]={d="照这些战士受伤的速度，我的治疗草药很快就要用光了。\n\n我知道另一种药方，效果一样好，但取材相当危险，而我又不是战斗人员。\n\n如果你正好要去那边，能不能把材料带回来？我需要蝎毒、迅猛龙血和野猪獠牙。别担心，只要处理得当，蝎毒是无害的。",dEN="At the rate these fighters are getting themselves hurt, I'm going to run out of healing herbs.\n\nI know another remedy that'd help them recover just as well, but it's rather dangerous to get, and I'm no fighter.\n\nIf you end up going out there, maybe you could bring the ingredients back? I need scorpid venom, raptor blood, and boar tusks. Don't worry, the venom isn't harmful if it's treated the right way.",o="护士辛加想让你收集4瓶蝎毒、4瓶迅猛龙血和4根野猪獠牙。",oEN="Shinga the nurse wants you to collect 4 Vials of Scorpid Venom, 4 Vials of Raptor Blood, and 4 Boar Tusks.",p="啊，你回来了。那些稀奇古怪的材料拿到了吗？我知道这听起来更像是喂给野兽的东西，而不是给受伤的战士。蝎毒、迅猛龙血、野猪獠牙……真是绝妙的组合。不过，我发誓它有效。就算治不好他们，至少也能让他们的心跳得够猛，忘了自己受过伤。",pEN="Ah, you are back. Do you have those bizarre ingredients? I know it sounds more like something you would feed to a wild beast than a wounded fighter. Scorpid venom, raptor blood, and boar tusks… what a combination. Still, I swear it works. If it does not cure them, it will at least kick their heart into gear hard enough that they forget they were ever hurt.",c="好，好，太完美了。你简直不敢相信这药水能多快让他们重新站起来。喝上一口，他们几乎就能拆穿一堵墙。\n\n谢谢你。有了这些，我们也许能撑过下一轮的伤员而不损失任何人。只是……你自己千万别喝，除非你喜欢几天后醒来时不知道自己身在何处。",cEN="Yes, yes, that is perfect. You will not believe how quickly this concoction brings them back on their feet. One sip and they are practically ready to tear through a wall.\n\nThank you. With these, we might just get through the next round of injuries without losing anyone. Just… never drink it yourself unless you enjoy waking up days later not knowing where you are."}
Q[254085]={d="双足飞龙饿了的时候不会多说什么，但我看得出来。它们动作变慢，眼神失焦。连风声似乎都更安静了。\n\n这几天我们的肉快见底了。剩下的多半都留给病人和育雏的母亲。不过这附近的雄鹿很多，肉也耐放。自从要塞建立以来，我们一直靠它们过活。\n\n如果你有时间，尽量多采集一些。六份应该就够让幼崽们保持强壮了。\n\n只取所需。这里的兽群养活了我们这么多年。我希望它能一直这样下去。",dEN="The wyverns won’t say much when they’re hungry, but I can tell. They move slower. Their eyes lose focus. Even the wind seems quieter.\n\nWe've run low on meat these past few days. Most of what remains is being saved for the sick and the broodmothers. The stags around here are plentiful, though, and their meat keeps well. It's what we have used since the hold was founded.\n\nIf you have the time, gather what you can. Six should be enough to keep the young ones strong.\n\nJust take what is needed. The herds here have kept us going for years. I would like to keep it that way.",o="为高风要塞的布拉穆克·地蹄收集6份鹿肉。",oEN="Collect 6 Stag Meat for Brammuk Earthhoof at Highwind Hold.",p="你找到足够的分量了吗？如果没有，不用着急。只要善待这片土地，它总会有所馈赠。",pEN="Did you find enough? If not, take your time. The land always provides, when treated with care.",c="很好。幼崽要想和我们一起飞翔，就必须长得强壮。\n\n谢谢你。我们马上就会用上。",cEN="Good. The young must grow strong if they are to fly with us.\n\nThank you. We will put it to use right away."}
Q[254086]={d="至少不会有什么坏处，也许还能帮我们更快得到答案，所以你想试的话，我不拦你。\n\n只是别靠笼子太近，它可能会试图撕开你的喉咙。",dEN="Wouldn't hurt anything at least, and might help us get our answers sooner, so if you want to try I won't stop you.\n\nJust don't get too close to the cage, it might try and rip out your throat.",o="守夜人奥斯温·德雷克需要有人帮忙审讯被俘的狼人",oEN="Oswin Drake of the Night Watch needs help interrogating the captured worgen",p="我怀疑你也问不出什么，但你可以试着和那个狼人谈谈。小心点，它有时候能把爪子伸出笼子的缝隙。",pEN="I doubt you'll get much out of it, but you're free to try talking to the worgen. Just be careful, it can reach its claws through the openings in the cage sometimes.",c="明白我的意思了吧，它也许会说上几句，但说的全是没用的东西。\n\n你说从它嘴里套出了一个名字？朱莉？依我看，这已经比我们知道的多了。\n\n等等，我在哪儿听过这个名字……",cEN="See what I mean now, might be talking a bit, but he ain't saying anything useful.\n\nGot a name out of him you say? Julie? That's more than we've got I reckon.\n\nNow where've I heard that name before..."}
Q[254087]={d="我想起来了，听说过有个叫朱莉·阿德尔的人住在夜色镇的旅店里。如今得盯着每一个人，谁知道哪个平民会不会另有身份。\n\n我们三个得守在这里，人手本来就太少。不过，这条路恐怕也问不出什么了；如果你去夜色镇，也许可以自己去找她，看看她能不能帮上忙。",dEN="I remember now, heard tell of a Julie Addle staying at the inn in Darkshire. Have to keep eyes on everyone these days, never know when a commoner might turn out to be something more.\n\nThe three of us are needed here, there's too few of us already. Still, doubt we'll get any further this way, if you find yourself at Darkshire, maybe you could seek her out yourself and see if she'll be any help.",o="在血色渡鸦酒馆找到朱莉·阿德尔",oEN="Find Julie Addle at the Scarlet Raven Tavern",c="<那女人看起来快要哭出来，但你走近时，她稍稍镇定了一些。>\n\n你好。有什么需要我帮忙的吗？\n\n一个狼人念出了我的名字……？\n\n阿尔维斯，你变成了这副模样吗？对不起……我需要缓一缓……",cEN="<The woman looks to be on the verge of tears, but she composes herself some as you approach.>\n\nHello. May I help you with something?\n\nA worgen spoke my name...?\n\nArvis, is this what you've become? Sorry...I need a moment..."}
Q[254088]={d="我很抱歉。我本没指望会有他的消息，但我会没事的。如果他还记得我的名字，也许就还有一线希望。\n\n我们的农庄前段时间被狼人袭击了，我们想逃，可他们更快。于是我丈夫……他……他叫我快跑，然后就开始战斗。我们俩都不是战士，可我不知道该怎么办，就听了他的话。我一直跑，直到发现自己来到了这里……那之后我再也没见过他。\n\n我没有试着回去过。那里现在什么也没给我留下了，而且我听说，虽然狼人走了，那地方现在被强盗占据了。\n\n不过，也许那里还留着什么他能认出来的东西，他过去生活的一丝痕迹。那可能是你最好的机会。",dEN="I apologize. I hadn't expected any news of him, but I'll be fine. If he remembers my name, there might still be some hope.\n\nOur farmstead was attacked by worgen some time back, we tried to flee, but they were faster. So my husband...he...he told me to run, and started fighting. Neither of us are fighters, but I didn't know what to do, so I listened. I ran until I found myself here...I never saw him again after that.\n\nI haven't tried to return. There's nothing left for me there now, and I've heard even though the worgen are gone, it's been taken by bandits now.\n\nStill, maybe there's something left there that he might recognize, some trace of his old life. It might be your best chance.",o="在阿德尔农庄寻找阿尔维斯·阿德尔过去生活的痕迹",oEN="Find some trace of Arvis Addle's old life at Addle's Stead",p="我不知道那些强盗有没有留下什么值钱的东西，但也许有什么他会认出来。",pEN="I don't know if the bandits would have left anything valuable, but maybe there's something he'll recognize.",c="那本旧书……它竟然还在？阿尔维斯打理农庄之余，一有空就想写一本书……其实他脑子里已经构思了一整套系列……\n\n<泪水顺着那女人的脸颊滑落。>\n\n我相信他会认出它的。他一定能。只要他身上还剩下一点点过去，他就一定能。",cEN="That old book...so it survived then? Arvis was trying to write a book in whatever spare time he had after managing the farm...he had a whole series in mind actually...\n\n<Tears stream down the woman's cheek.>\n\nI'm sure he'll recognize it. He has to. If there's anything still left of him, he has to."}
Q[254089]={d="在你走之前，我还该提一句，他以前常来这家酒馆喝甜蜜露。他一直不太喜欢烈酒，总说那让他写不好字。也许你给他带点过去也会有所帮助。\n\n……我为什么不跟你一起去？\n\n不，你说得对。我害怕看到他这副样子。我甚至不知道我爱过的那个男人还剩下多少，但他认出我的可能，总比认出他那本没写完的小说和最爱喝的酒要大。\n\n你拿到蜜露的话，我就带上书，在那儿和你碰头。无论如何，我都必须面对他。",dEN="Before you go, I should also mention that he used to stop by this tavern for Sweet Nectar. Never was much for harder drinks, made it hard to write he always said. Maybe if you bring him some that will help too.\n\n...Why am I not coming with?\n\nNo, you're right. I'm afraid to see him like this. I don't even know how much of the man I loved he'll still be, but he's more likely to recognize me than his half-finished novel and a favorite drink.\n\nIf you get the nectar, I'll bring the book and meet you there. One way or another, I have to face him.",o="把没写完的书和一瓶甜蜜露带给被俘的狼人",oEN="Bring the half-finished book and a bottle of Sweet Nectar to the captured worgen",p="他什么也不会说的，但我确信那就是他。我本来还以为，在你来这儿之前，他……\n\n我知道。狼人很少还能保有一丝过去的自己。那只是一厢情愿的奢望，仅此而已。",pEN="He won't say anything, but I'm certain it's him. I'd thought maybe, before you have got here, he...\n\nI know. It's rare that worgen retain even a trace of who they once were. It was just a selfish hope, nothing more.",c="你把蜜露带来了？太好了，我想我们该开始了。",cEN="You brought the Nectar? Great, I suppose it's about time we start."}
Q[254090]={d="如果你愿意听一个简单的请求，这把老骨头已经没有当年的力气了。对圣光的信仰……并不是给我们这种人的，所以这具身体并不总能支撑我履行职责。\n\n墓地里的坟茔已经太久没人打理了。那些可怜的灵魂大概已经没有亲人在世上行走，但他们的坟墓依然该有尊严。\n\n如果你有时间，也许可以用同样的心意照看巴尔尼尔农场的阿尔萨斯坐骑之墓。它主人的暴行或许数不胜数，但它是一匹忠诚的马，而且在巫妖王崛起之前就已死去。\n\n要是它能活得更久，也许事情就不会变成这样……",dEN="If you might hear a simple request, these old bones do not have the strength they once did. Faith in the light...it is not something meant for those like us, so this body does not always have the strength fulfill my duties.\n\nThe graves out in the cemetary have not been cleaned in far too long now. Those poor souls likely have no one left who still walks this world, but their graves deserve dignity nonetheless.\n\nIf you have the time, you might also grant the same care to the grave of Arthas's steed at the Balnir Farmstead. His master's atrocities may be many, but he was a loyal horse, and had died before the Lich King's rise.\n\nHad he lived longer, perhaps things may not have gone this way...",o="擦拭阿拉斯托神父墓地的墓碑，以及巴尔尼尔农场无敌的坟墓。",oEN="Polish gravestones at Father Alastor's cemetary and Invincible's grave at Balnir Farmstead."}
Q[254091]={d="<朱莉深吸一口气。>\n\n好吧，不管接下来发生什么，我都准备好了。",dEN="<Julie takes a deep breath.>\n\nAlright, whatever happens here, I'm ready.",o="与被俘的狼人阿尔维斯·阿德尔交谈",oEN="Speak with Arvis Addle, the captured worgen",p="找到那野兽的妻子了，是吗？也许这能问出点什么来。",pEN="Found the beast's wife, did ya? Maybe that'll get something out of it.",c="看来它又发狂了。真可惜，我本想亲自跟它谈谈的，但我猜妻子更有机会。\n\n我们一直以为这里的狼人只是曾经是人的野兽，但那家伙提到了什么\"狼人教派\"和一个首领。这难道不稀奇吗？\n\n看来我们一直搞错了方向。我会确保消息传回夜色镇的自己人；如果狼人真的有明确的目标，我们最好保持警惕。",cEN="Looks like it went feral again. A shame, would've talked to it myself some, but I figured the wife had a better chance.\n\nWe'd been thinking the worgen here were just wild beasts that used to be men, but that one mentioned something about a \"Wolf Cult\", and a leader. Ain't that something?\n\nSeems we might've been going about this all wrong. I'll make sure word gets back to our people in Darkshire, if the worgen have an actual goal we'd better stay vigilant."}
Q[254092]={d="我的主人看不上你，我也明白为什么。不过，我或许还能用得上你。\n\n我们的同族中有一个自大的家伙，自以为是低等生物中的神明。她用铁爪统治着一座兽人前哨，吞食那些进贡不足的人。\n\n不管她是什么，她确实配得上她所宣称的力量，挑战她的人最后不是变成焦尸就是变成鲜肉。我们族中很少有人对她有好感，但至少她的力量让她得以被容忍。\n\n她会像屠杀其他挑战者一样屠杀你，但如果你能召集几个同族，也许至少能在她把你们烧成焦炭之前惹恼她。对我来说，单是这一点就够了。",dEN="My master thinks little of you, and I can see why. Still, I may have some use for you.\n\nAmongst our kin is an arrogant who fancies herself some sort of god amongst lesser beings. She rules over an outpost of the orcs with an iron claw, devouring those who do not pay her enough tribute.\n\nWhatever she may be, she certainly lives up to the strength she claims, and those who challenge her end up as charred corpses or fresh meat. Few of our kind hold any favor for her, but her strength at least allows her to be tolerated.\n\nShe would slaughter you as well as any others who try to challenge her, but if you can rally a few of your kind, you might be able to at least irritate her before she burns you all to a crisp. That alone would be enough for me.",o="击败灰烬黎明之龙齐瓦斯翠娅",oEN="Defeat Zivarstria, Dragon of the Ashen Dawn",p="如果你们真的决定拿命去挑战齐瓦斯翠娅，至少要让祂觉得你们是个麻烦。",pEN="If you do choose to throw your lives away against Zivarstria, make certain that she at least finds you to be a nuisance.",c="齐瓦斯翠娅死了？真真切切、彻彻底底地死了？那就让她的尸体在这片焦黑可悲的大地上腐烂吧！\n\n也许我确实看错你了。我有理由心情好的日子可不多。但至少今天，我可以忘掉自己的奴役身份，尽情回味她临终的那一刻。",cEN="Zivarstria is dead? Truly, utterly, dead? Then her corpse rot upon this charred and wretched earth!\n\nPerhaps I was wrong about you indeed. It is a rare day that I have reason to be in a good mood. But today, at least, I can forget my own servitude and revel in the thought of her final moments."}
Q[254093]={d="我们族中多数人对她没什么耐心，但有几个谄媚之徒看中她的力量，想要讨她的欢心。这六人自称\"齐瓦斯翠娅之爪\"。他们是蠢货，但并不弱小。\n\n最擅长近身搏斗的自称怒火之爪：阿菲里安、伊尔维森和艾诺西亚。他们绝不弱小；齐瓦斯翠娅对无条件效忠她的人一向慷慨，但看到那份忠诚被砸进焦土里，我会感到几分快意。",dEN="While most of our kind may hold little patience for her, there are a few sycophants who see value in her might, and thus seek to curry her favor. These six call themselves the \"Claws of Zivarstria\". They are fools, but they are not weak.\n\nThose most skilled in the art of physical combat call themselves the Claws of Rage, Afyllian, Ilvission, and Enocia. They are hardly weak, Zivarstria is a mighty patron to those who give her unquestioning loyalty, but it would bring me some sense of joy to see that loyalty beaten into the charred earth.",o="在燃烧平原击败怒火之爪三人",oEN="Defeat the three Claws of Rage in the Burning Steppes",p="那些无法靠自己的力量生存、于是向强者屈膝的人，只配被人打断膝盖。\n\n那我为什么还要侍奉塞勒斯？\n\n哈！我可没把自己排除在这番话之外。我和那些爪牙一样可悲，但至少我不把自己看得更高。如果你真想听从我的话，那就连同他们一起把我打倒吧。",pEN="Those who cannot subsist on their own strength and thus bend their knee to those who can deserve nothing but to have those knees broken.\n\nWhy then do I serve Cyrus?\n\nHah! I did not exclude myself from that statement. I am as wretched as the Claws, but at least I do not see myself as anything more. If you truly wish to heed my words, then strike me down along with them.",c="强者生存、弱者被踩在脚下凋零，本就是天经地义。\n\n我想知道，在最后一刻，他们是否终于明白，齐瓦斯翠娅的恩宠并不能真正改变他们内心的软弱。",cEN="It is right for the strong to endure and the weak to wither beneath their feet.\n\nI wonder if, in their final moments, they finally realized that Zivarstria's favor could not truly change the weakness in their hearts."}
Q[254094]={d="我们族中多数人对她没什么耐心，但有几个谄媚之徒看中她的力量，想要讨她的欢心。这六人自称\"齐瓦斯翠娅之爪\"。他们是蠢货，但并不弱小。\n\n最精通魔法的自称怨毒之爪：奈克翠克西亚、瑞西丝翠娅和利法里昂。他们是危险而狡诈的对手；齐瓦斯翠娅赐予绝对信仰她的人强大的力量，但看到那份信仰化为灰烬，我会感到几分快意。",dEN="While most of our kind may hold little patience for her, there are a few sycophants who see value in her might, and thus seek to curry her favor. These six call themselves the \"Claws of Zivarstria\". They are fools, but they are not weak.\n\nThose most skilled in the art of magic call themselves the Claws of Malice, Nexrixia, Rethysria, and Lifarion. They are dangerous and cunning opponents, Zivarstria lends great power to those who give her absolute faith, but it would bring me some sense of joy to see that faith reduced to ash.",o="在燃烧平原击败怨毒之爪三人",oEN="Defeat the three Claws of Malice in the Burning Steppes",p="那些无法靠自己的力量生存、于是向强者屈膝的人，只配被人打断膝盖。\n\n那我为什么还要侍奉塞勒斯？\n\n哈！我可没把自己排除在这番话之外。我和那些爪牙一样可悲，但至少我不把自己看得更高。如果你真想听从我的话，那就连同他们一起把我打倒吧。",pEN="Those who cannot subsist on their own strength and thus bend their knee to those who can deserve nothing but to have those knees broken.\n\nWhy then do I serve Cyrus?\n\nHah! I did not exclude myself from that statement. I am as wretched as the Claws, but at least I do not see myself as anything more. If you truly wish to heed my words, then strike me down along with them.",c="强者生存、弱者被踩在脚下凋零，本就是天经地义。\n\n我想知道，在最后一刻，他们是否终于明白，齐瓦斯翠娅的恩宠并不能真正改变他们内心的软弱。",cEN="It is right for the strong to endure and the weak to wither beneath their feet.\n\nI wonder if, in their final moments, they finally realized that Zivarstria's favor could not truly change the weakness in their hearts."}
Q[254096]={d="你是来帮忙的？好，好，那你能帮我个忙，正经事。我掉了件要紧东西，就从塔上直直摔了下去。盒子是瑟银做的，不会有事的，可我这会儿走不开，下去一趟又远得很。\n\n你要是下去帮我捡回来，我欠你个人情。",dEN="Here to help, are ye? Good, good, ye can do me a favor then, serious business. I dropped something important, fell right off the tower. The box is made o' Thorium so it'll be fine, but I can't go leavin' me watch anytime soon, an' it's a long walk down there.\n\nI'll owe ye if ye go down and grab it.",o="在瞭望塔下找到卡德里乌尔丢失的盒子。",oEN="Find Kadriur's missing box beneath the watchtower.",p="你拿到矿洞蜘蛛的腿了吗？拿到之后，我们就能用它们和你之前带回来的矿物碎片一起做些测试。\n\n我希望它们吸收到了足够的微量残留，好让我们得到确切的结论。",pEN="Did you get the mine spider legs yet? Once we have those, we can run some tests using them alongside the mineral fragment you brought earlier.\n\nI’m hoping they’ve absorbed enough trace residue to give us something concrete.",c="<这似乎就是卡德里乌尔掉下的盒子。带回去之前，你也许该先确认里面的东西是否完好。>",cEN="<This seems to be the box Kadriur dropped. Before you bring it back, you should probably make sure the contents are still intact.>"}
Q[254097]={d="<盒子已经空了，而且被打开了一部分。也许附近的某个黑铁矮人比你先一步拿到了它。不过，那人应该走不远。也许你还能追踪到他。>",dEN="<The box is already empty, and partially open. Perhaps one of the nearby Dark Irons got to it before you did. Still, whoever it was can't be too far. Perhaps you could still track them down.>",o="找到偷走失窃补给的黑铁窃贼。",oEN="Find the Dark Iron Thief who stole the missing supplies.",p="你没看见我在求饶吗？！你要是想打架，至少等我喘口气。",pEN="Can't ye see I'm beggin' for me life here?! If yer lookin' for a fight, at least wait 'til I catch me breath.",c="至少在我被杀之前听我说完！我是个讲道理的矮人，我们可以做个交易。\n\n我不值得为一个椒盐卷饼送命！\n\n……你以为里面是什么？你没见过饭盒吗？\n\n听着，我一点都不在乎像我们皇帝说的那样去征服其他部族，所以给我点时间理理思路。",cEN="At least hear me out before ye kill me! I'm a reasonable dwarf, we can make a deal.\n\nI ain't worth killin' over a pretzel!\n\n...What'd ye think was in there? Ye ain't seen a lunchbox before?\n\nLook, I don't care one bit about conquering the other clans like our emperor's been on about, so give me a second ta collect me thoughts."}
Q[254101]={d="有件事我想请你帮忙，亲爱的朋友。\n\n我在自己的族人中并不受欢迎。 consortium 至少愿意抛开对卡雷什的旧有偏见，就算谈不上接纳。\n\n不过，还有其他势力仍想将我和我的同胞彻底铲除。你肯定不想听我讲完我们全部的历史，所以这件事我们暂且按下。\n\n以太派和扎克斯都已在虚空风暴扎营，他们都属于那些追猎基莱的人。如果你能从他们那里取来这些情报交给我，我会非常感激；其中许多可能包含连我自己都已遗失的历史。\n\n去找那些不断变换的方块状神器，那些被窃取并用来对付我们的古老遗物。我说的情报就在其中。",dEN="There is favor I would ask of you, dear friend.\n\nI am not one who is well-liked amongst my people. The Consortium has been, if not accepting, willing to leave behind old prejudices of K'aresh.\n\nThere are other factions, however, that still desire myself and my siblings to be eliminated. You do not wish to hear me tell you all of our history, I'm sure, so let us settle the subject at that for now.\n\nThe Ethereum and the Zaxxis have both set up camps in Netherstorm, and both are amongst those would hunt down the Kirai. I would be most grateful if you were to take this information from them and bring it to me, much of it may contain history that I have myself lost.\n\nLook for shifting cube-like artifacts, ancient relics that have been stolen and used against us. The information I speak of is held in these.",o="为裂痕探寻者收集美利克雷克斯",oEN="Gather Melicrexes for Rift-Seeker",p="美利克雷克斯，我们这样称呼它们。用来储存信息的神器。历史、故事、技艺、思想。\n\n看到我们拼命想保存下来的历史，如今被用来追踪残存的基莱，让我很痛心。",pEN="Melicrexes, we called them. Artifacts we used to store information. History, stories, techniques, ideas.\n\nIt pains me to see the very history we tried so hard to preserve now used as a way to track down the remaining Kirai.",c="你遇到的虚灵的传统，来自曾经诸多文化中最显赫的一支，但卡雷什人并非铁板一块。\n\n即便在那时，基莱也是个小教团，而以太派这样的势力想要把我们彻底消灭。我们常被视为一个\"教派\"，与一种在虚空中、也在我们自身中回响的力量相通。我们称之为\"回响\"。我们是一个古怪而封闭的教团，虽然如今所剩无几，但我仍希望我们的历史不会就此失传。",cEN="The traditions of the Ethereals you meet come from the most prominent of many cultures that once were, but the K'areshi were not a monolith.\n\nThe Kirai were a small order, even then, and factions like the Ethereum would see us destroyed entirely. We were seen often as a \"cult\", communing with a power that resonated within the Nether, and within ourselves. Something we call \"The Echo\". We were a strange, isolated order, but though there are few of us that remain, I would prefer our history is not lost."}
Q[254102]={d="我还想再请你帮一件事，亲爱的朋友。我们是\"朋友\"，对吧？对我们来说，所有不想伤害我们的人都是朋友，但你们的族人和其他同族似乎常觉得这很奇怪。\n\n consortium 愿意庇护我，但很少有人会为基莱做得更多。我不能因此鄙视他们，可是比起他们，你更配得上\"朋友\"这个称呼。\n\n我们知道一种技艺，一种召唤同胞援助的信号，只有基莱才能感知。它会告诉我们信号来自何时何地，听起来微不足道，却让我们得以同心一体。\n\n但这种技艺本是为了跨越卡雷什，而不是整个扭曲虚空。不过，精灵使用的法力熔炉也许能放大它，把讯息传遍虚空。在外面某处一定还有更多同胞，而我们团结起来会更好。\n\n没错，发送它需要一个基莱，但讯息我已经准备好了。你只需在法力熔炉附近激活这件神器。至于之后，我只能寄望于他们能听到。",dEN="I would ask one more thing of you, dear friend. We are \"friends\", yes\" To us, all were friends who did not wish us harm, but this seems to often be seen oddly by your people, and by the rest of mine.\n\nThe Consortium is willing to harbor me, but few would go further than that in the aid of the Kirai. I cannot despise them for it, but still, you have earned the title of \"friend\" far more than they.\n\nThere is a technique we knew, a signal through which to call for the aid of our own, which only the Kirai could sense. It told us when and where it was from, and while that sounds like little, it helped to make us one.\n\nBut this technique was meant to reach across K'aresh, not all of the Twisting Nether. However, the Mana-forges used by the elves may prove a means of amplifying this, sending a message across the nether. There must be more of us out there, somewhere, and we would fare better as one.\n\nYes, it would take a Kirai to send it, but I have prepared the message already. All you must do is activate this artifact near the mana-forges. Beyond that, I can only hope they will be heard.",o="为基莱激活信标",oEN="Activate beacons for the Kirai",p="它叫回响之音。我是说，我给你的那件神器。\n\n它能储存我们的能力，供日后释放。在合适的人手里是件极强大的物品……也是卡雷什陷落时，我能从神殿中抢救出来的少数神器之一。\n\n这样用实在有些大材小用，但它能满足我们的需要。只是请务必小心对待它。",pEN="It was called the Echo Speaker. The artifact I gave you, that is.\n\nIt could hold our abilities to unleash later. A very powerful item in the right hands...and one of the few of our artifacts I was able to salvage from our temple as K'aresh fell.\n\nThis is a rather mundane use of it, but it serves our needs. Just be careful with it, please.",c="被袭击了？！\n\n不，这不对。基莱是个和平的教团，我们不会攻击帮助过我们的人……\n\n……除非……\n\n星云编织者，我们教团曾经的首领，他因力量而疯狂，转而与我们为敌。他的学徒 locus-walker 得知了他的背叛，将他击倒。\n\n但星云编织者掌握的力量也许让他得以违抗死亡，不知以何种方式逃脱了。如果你真的与他交战过，能活下来算是幸运。若那正是你面对的危险，我为我托付给你的任务深感抱歉。\n\n而我接下来要请你做的事，让我更加抱歉。",cEN="Attacked?!\n\nNo, that isn't right. The Kirai are a peaceful order, we would not fight against one who gave us aid...\n\n...Unless...\n\nNebula-Weaver, once the leader of our order, he went mad with power and turned against us. His apprentice Locus-Walker learned of his betrayal, and struck him down.\n\nBut the power Nebula-Weaver wielded may have allowed him to defy death and escape, somehow. If you did fight him, you are lucky to have survived. And I am deeply sorry for asking this task of you, if that is the danger you faced.\n\nI am more sorry, still, for what I am asking of you next."}
Q[254103]={d="星云编织者曾试图击溃基莱，并以回响之力在卡雷什建立新的统治。\n\n那大概已不再是他的目标，但他消灭基莱的执念，我无法想象会就此终止。也许正因如此，他才那么快赶到信标前，盼着能找到我们中的一员。\n\n基莱不愿战斗，但星云编织者是宿敌。我们不会把他当作朋友。虽然我请你做的事，是我从不愿向任何人开口的，但我还没冷酷到让你独自执行任务而自己留在这里。\n\n我希望我们一起去面对星云编织者。如果他来得这么快，大概还在附近，那我就不需要法力熔炉的力量了。我们在水晶山脊会合吧，到了那里再用一次回响之音通知我，我就与你汇合。\n\n如果星云编织者还在附近，他大概也会找到我们，而只要我在场，他就不太可能轻易放弃这场战斗。愿回响指引我们此战。",dEN="Nebula-Weaver tried to strike down the Kirai, and establish a new order in their place, using the power of the Echo to seize dominance over K'aresh.\n\nThat is likely no longer his goal, but his desire to end the Kirai is something I cannot imagine ended. That is likely why he came to the beacon so readily, expecting to find one of us.\n\nThe Kirai do not wish to fight, but Nebula-Weaver is an ancient enemy. He is one we would not consider a friend. And though I am asking you something I would never wish to ask of anyone, I am not so cruel to remain here while you carry out this task.\n\nI wish us to face Nebula-Weaver, together. If he came so quickly, he is likely still near, and so I do not need the power of a Mana-Forge. Let us meet at the crystal ridge, use the Echo Speaker once again to alert me when you are there, and I will join you.\n\nIf Nebula-Weaver is still near, he will likely find us as well, and as long as I am there, he is not likely to abandon the fight so easily. May the Echo guide us in this battle.",o="召唤并击败星云编织者",oEN="Call and defeat Nebula-Weaver",p="紧张吗？\n\n我也是。我小时候见过他一次。那时他还是我们的首领。我记得我想逃走，感受到一种我自己都说不清道不明的恐惧。\n\n他想教我一样东西，一门技艺。其他年轻学徒觉得能被星云编织者亲自教导是无上的荣耀，可我却跑出了房间。现在我明白了，他是希望有更多人走上他的道路。\n\n没过多久，我就听说 locus-walker 接替了他的位置，再之后，他们两人决斗的传闻开始流传开来。\n\nlocus-walker……如今走着自己的路。我说不清他是否还能被称为基莱。但正因为他，我才成为虚灵……我才站在这里。那是另一个故事了，眼下我们该专注于即将到来的战斗。",pEN="Nervous?\n\nI am too. I met him once, as a child. He was still our leader then. I remember wanting to run away. Feeling a sense of fear I didn't understand well enough to convey.\n\nHe wanted to teach me something, a technique. The other young students saw this as a great honor, to be taught by Nebula-Weaver himself, but I ran from the room. I understand now he hoped for more to walk his path.\n\nIt wasn't long after I was told Locus-Walker was taking his place, and a bit after that, the story of the duel between them began to spread.\n\nLocus-Walker...follows his own path now. I cannot say if he can still be called Kirai. But he is the reason I became Ethereal...the reason I am here now. That is a story for another time, for now, we should be focused on the fight to come.",c="结束了。\n\n我不确定他此前是如何活下来的，但至少我可以盼望，星云编织者会再次消失很长一段时间。事实上，虽然卡雷什的其他人对我们并不友善，但如果他对如今仍有那么多人执意要毁灭我们残存的血脉负有一部分责任，我也不会感到意外。\n\n至于你……基莱的传统一向严加保守，只传授给献身于回响的人。我们本希望以此阻止掌握它们的人将其用于毁灭。但我们人数太少，所以我愿意与你分享我们技艺的一小部分。\n\n这是我能为你所做的一切给出的最好的回报。愿你善加运用，愿回响指引你，亲爱的朋友。",cEN="It is done.\n\nI am not certain how he survived before, but I can hope, at least, that Nebula-Weaver will disappear for a long time, again. In fact, while we were not often regarded kindly by the rest of K'aresh, it would not surprise me if he holds at least some blame in why there are so many who are still so determined to destroy what remains of us.\n\nAs for you...the traditions of the Kirai were closely guarded, taught only to those who devoted themselves to the Echo. It was our hope to stop their wielders from using them for destruction. But we are few in number, and so I would share with you a small part of our technique.\n\nIt is the best I can offer you for all you have done. May you wield it well, and may the Echo guide you, dear friend."}
Q[254104]={d="<class>，你知道我眺望高地时看到什么吗？我看到汹涌的能量沿着山丘奔流。替我带来守卫每块缚誓之石的元素身上的护腕，我就能为你调配一份萨普塔，让你也看到同样的景象。",dEN="Do you know what I see when I gaze out upon the Highlands, <class>? I see roiling energy streaking along the hills. Bring me a Bracer from the Elementals that ward each each Stone of Binding, and I will make for you a Sapta so that you might see the same.",o="在阿拉希高地为迪亚尼从每个缚誓之环各取得1个护腕。",oEN="Get 1 Bracer from each Circle of Binding for Dyani in Arathi Highlands.",p="风没有改变方向，大地仍在低鸣。你找到护腕了吗，还是元素仍在考验你的决心？",pEN="The winds have not changed, and the ground still hums. Have you found the bracers, or are the elements still testing your resolve?",c="欢迎回来，<class>。把你取来的护腕交给我，我来准备你的下一步。",cEN="Welcome back, <class>. Hand me the bracers you claimed, and I will prepare your next step."}
Q[254105]={d="饮下原初萨普塔，见证幻象，然后回到迪亚尼身边。",dEN="Drink of the Primordial Sapta, witness the vision, and return to Dyani.",o="谢谢你，<name>。利用护腕上残留的能量，我为你调配了一份萨普塔。等你准备好饮下这药剂、成为开悟者时，再来找我。",oEN="Thank you, <name>. Using the lingering energies from the bracers, I was able to brew for you a Sapta. Speak to me again when you're ready to imbibe the mixture, and become Enlightened.",c="我能从你眼中看出来，<name>。你对元素的理解已经提升。",cEN="I can see in it in your eyes, <name>. Your understanding of the elements is elevated."}
Q[254110]={d="这么说火靴家的姐妹俩跑去加入兄弟会了？我一直纳闷那两人去哪了，普拉格烧得一手好菜，可终究不是那个味儿。\n\n你知道吗，我改主意了，我们的皇帝得下台，所以我要站到瑟银兄弟会这边。当然，是出于理念上的理由。\n\n好吧好吧，我的钱袋你也可以拿去，应该够再从卡拉那儿买一个椒盐卷饼了。那现在一切都好说了吧？你会放我走，对吧？\n\n……拜托？",dEN="So the Fireboot sisters went an' joined the Brotherhood, did they? Always been wonderin' where those two went, Plugger's a mighty fine cook, but it just ain't the same.\n\nYe know what, I've had a change o' heart, our emperor needs ta go, so I'm castin' my lot in with the Thorium Brotherhood. For idealogical reasons o' course.\n\nOkay okay, ye can have my coin purse too, should be enough ta buy another pretzel from Kala. So everything's good now? Yer gonna let me go, right?\n\n...Please?",o="在瑟银哨塔向卡拉·火靴要一个新做的岩浆香料椒盐卷饼。",oEN="Obtain a new Magma-Spice Pretzel from Kala Fireboot in Thorium Point.",p="你找到了吗？应该就在这座塔的正下方。\n\n当然，我不建议你从这儿跳下去。哈哈！",pEN="Did ye find it? Should just be right below this tower.\n\n'Course I don't suggest jumpin' that way. Hahah!",c="哎！你把它找回来了！瞧瞧这美人儿，摔下来都没碎。你知道卡拉会怎么对付浪费她手艺的人吗？不知道？很好，你最好一直不知道。\n\n总之，你出去的时候我听到点好消息，据说我们这儿来了个叛逃者，下面有个人跑来向我们投降了。我怀疑他级别不高，不过我们正需要新的情报。\n\n不知道人为什么会这么做。我敢打赌，他是意识到自己部族干了多少坏事，决定开始弥补。",cEN="Aye! Ye got it back! Look at that beauty, didn't even break from the fall. Ye know what Kala does ta folks who waste her cookin'? No? Good, ye best keep it that way.\n\nAnyways, heard a bit o' good news while ye were out, apparently we got a defector, one o' the folks below up and surrendered 'imself ta us. Doubt he's all that high up, but we've been needin' some new intel.\n\nWonder what makes folks do that. I'd bet he realized how many terrible things his clan was doin' and decided ta start makin' amends."}
Q[255000]={d="<纸条上的字迹粗劣不堪>\n\n当心那潜伏于黑暗中的野兽\n\n许多狗头人去了就没回来。我在幽深的洞穴里见过他们，神智尽失，只剩黑暗。\n\n自打见过它之后，蜡烛越烧越暗，光更少，火更弱。若你要进入黑暗的洞穴，记住，永远让蜡烛亮着。绝不要让任何人拿走你的蜡烛。\n\n否则你也会被带走。",dEN="<The note is written in a crude handwriting>\n\nBeware the Beast That Dwells in Darkness\n\nMany kobold leave, not return. I see them in deep dark cave, minds gone, only darkness left.\n\nCandle is growing dimmer since seeing, less light, less fire. If go into dark cave, remember, always keep candle lit. Never let anyone take candle.\n\nOr you be taken too.",o="击败\"潜伏于黑暗中的野兽\"。",oEN="Defeat the \"Beast That Dwells in Darkness\".",p="有一只被暗影腐化的生物盘踞在那座洞穴里。最好避开那头野兽。",pEN="A creature tainted by shadow dwells in that cave. It is best to avoid that beast.",c="我在这儿都能听到那野兽的咆哮！我们族人也害怕那生物，那头被暗影吞噬的雷霆蜥蜴。狗头人管它叫\"潜伏于黑暗中的野兽\"，对我们来说，它有个名字：维萨科罗斯。\n\n它是我们的大患，也是讲给幼崽听、让他们不敢跑太远的故事。要杀死这样的野兽，你必须带有希瓦拉尔的印记，尽管你自己并不知道。\n\n今晚，为维萨科罗斯之死设宴！",cEN="I could hear that beast's roars from here! Our people too feared that creature, the thunder lizard consumed by shadow. The one the kobolds call \"Beast That Dwells in Darkness\", to us it had a name. Vexakoros.\n\nA great danger of our, and a story to tell the cubs so they did not run too far. To slay such a beast, you must bear the mark of Shirvallah, though you know it not.\n\nTonight, a feast for the death of Vexakoros!"}
Q[255001]={d="我们在这片洞穴深处发现的东西十分古老，最好永远埋在地下。它在我们的脑海里低语，告诉我们该如何取得它古老的力量。\n\n<老人的神情阴沉下来>\n\n我们听了。\n\n我们的人一个接一个地减少，最后只剩下年轻的文达尔和我。啊，文达尔，他当年多俊美……其实他可能比我们所有人都年长。他的耳朵太尖，皮肤太白，可我们不是爱打听的人。\n\n他喝的那些蓝色瓶子，那些总是发着光的\"酒\"，喝完之后，他开始变得苍白憔悴。他朝我扑来，尖叫着说我把他的瓶子藏了起来。不是他死就是我亡，最后是我的刀找到了他的喉咙。\n\n那之后我逃了，恳求当地人帮忙把那东西封印起来，他们让我成了他们的一员。但封印终究有时限，我至今仍能听见那个声音……\n\n\"放我出去，你便能承载大地之力！\"\n\n那时我已不再年轻，我在艾泽拉斯的时日也快到头了。在我的身体衰朽之前，我希望知道再不会有人重蹈我们的覆辙。",dEN="The thing we found buried deep in these caves, it was something ancient, something best left buried. It whispered in our minds of how we might obtain its ancient power.\n\n<The old man's expression goes dark>\n\nWe listened.\n\nOne by one our numbers dwindled, until in the end it was just young Vindar and I. Ah, Vindar, what a beauty he was...in truth he was probably older than all of us. His ears were far too sharp and his skin far too fair, but we weren't the type to pry.\n\nThe blue bottles he drank, his \"wine\" that always glowed, ran out, he started to get pale and gaunt. He lunged at me, screaming I was hiding his bottles from him. It was him or me, and in the end, it was my knife that found his throat.\n\nI ran after that, begged the locals to help keep that thing sealed, and they made me one of their own. But seals only last so long, I still hear that voice...\n\n\"Free me, and bear the power of the Earthen!\"\n\nI was no young man then, and my time on Azeroth will end soon. Before my body wastes away, I wish to know that none will share our fate ever again.",o="用嗡鸣的共鸣水晶打开大型共鸣桶，然后杀死阿达齐亚尔。带着消息回去见那个古怪的隐士。",oEN="Open the Greater Resonite Cask with a Humming Resonite Crystal, and then slay Adaziar. Return to the odd hermit with the news.",p="我知道这是徒劳的希望。你多半会死，而那生物会完全挣脱束缚，降临艾泽拉斯。\n\n想终结这一切是我的私心，你不必听这个老头的话。",pEN="I know it is a vain hope. You will likely die, and that creature will be unleashed upon Azeroth in full.\n\nIt is a selfish request to see this put to an end, you need not listen to this old man.",c="结束了吗？真的吗？\n\n<自从你认识他以来，老人脸上第一次露出笑容。>\n\n他们终于得以安息了！我剩下的身外之物不多，但你可以拿走我仍旧舍不得的那些，我想我很快也用不上了。\n\n不过，我可以安心度过余生了，因为我知道我们是最后一批。我再无遗憾，只遗憾动手的是你而不是我。\n\n谢谢你。如果其他人还在这里，而且神智还像我初次见到他们那天一样清醒，我相信他们也会向你致谢。",cEN="It is done? Truly?\n\n<For the first time since you met him, a smile crosses the old man's face.>\n\nThey are avenged at last! I have few worldly possessions left, but you may take what I still cling too, for I suspect I will have no need for them soon anyways.\n\nStill, I can live out the rest of my days knowing that we are the last. I have no more regrets, save that it was your hand and not mind.\n\nThank you. If the others were here, and as sound of mind as the day I first met them, I am certain they too would offer you their gratitude."}
Q[255002]={d="还是有些不对劲。戈格洛克已经被击败，但剩下的狗头人离开了巨礫岩峡谷。\n\n他们前往的地方，很多人说受到了诅咒。那里真正的历史大多已被遗忘，但我担心我们的工作还没完全结束，<name>。\n\n请你前往那座被遗忘的矿洞，找到这些狗头人的首领，那个自称维克的人。\n\n你已经做了很多，所以我不会再要求更多，但一名大地者不会无缘无故被封在石爪山，我担心，在那座矿洞里，你也许会发现那段历史的真相。",dEN="Something is still not right. Goggeroc is defeated, but the kobolds that remain left Boulderslide Ravine.\n\nThe place they have ventured is one many say is cursed. Much of its true history has been forgotten, but I fear our work is not quite done, <name>.\n\nPlease, go to that Forgotten Mine and find the leader of these kobolds, the one that calls himself Vek.\n\nYou have done much, and so I will ask no more of you than this, but an Earthen was not sealed in Stonetalon with no reason, and I fear, within that mine, you may find the truth of that history.",o="在被遗忘的矿洞找到并击败狗头人首领",oEN="Find and defeat the kobold leader at the Forgotten Mine",p="大地者不会无缘无故被封在这里。我感觉到这段故事背后还有我们未曾知晓的东西，而在那个山谷里，你也许能找到答案。",pEN="An Earthen would not be sealed here without reason. I sense there is more to this story than we have learned, and within that valley, you may find these answers.",c="你又带来了好消息。与那山谷的危险相比，这确实是微不足道的举动，但我相信剩下的你会处理好，如果你还没做完的话。",cEN="You bear good news yet again. Compared to the dangers of that valley, this is a small act indeed, but I am certain you will take care of the rest, if you have not already."}
Q[255003]={d="乌拉斯。许多个月来，我都以为这个名字属于一个如同兄弟的人。\n\n他还是幼崽的时候，就能听见希瓦拉尔的声音，许多年来，他都是我们中最睿智的。\n\n但万物终会随时间改变。当那些愚蠢的外来者削弱了石之者的封印，希瓦拉尔的声音变得更响，而我知道他从未听过我们母亲的声音。不，那声音只是石之者的骗局。\n\n当我试图劝说他时，他用流血来回应。如今我不过是个流放者，任何愿意听我说话的人也一样。\n\n我本希望事情不至于走到这一步，但以流血开始的事，必须以流血结束。要么我的血流尽，要么乌拉斯的，而我的力量又少又弱。\n\n虽然这也许显得懦弱，但我的人民必须重于我的自尊。外来者，纠正你族人的过错，让乌拉斯流血，好让我的人民能遵奉母亲希瓦拉尔的意志而活，而不是石之者的。",dEN="Urash. For many moons I considered that name to belong to one who was like a brother.\n\nSince he was just a cub, he could hear the voice of Shirvallah, and for many years he was the wisest amongst us.\n\nBut all things change in time. When the foolish outsiders weakened the Stone One's seal, Shirvallah's voice became louder, and I knew that he had NEVER heard our mother's voice. No, that voice was only the deception of the Stone One.\n\nWhen I tried to reason with him, he responded with bloodshed. Now I am but an exile, along with any who would listen.\n\nI had hoped it need not come to this, but what began in bloodshed must end in it. My blood must spill, or Urash's must, and my forces are few and weak.\n\nThough it may be cowardly, my people must come before my pride. Outsider, right the wrongs of your kind and spill Urash's blood, that my people may live by Mother Shirvallah's will and not that of the Stone One.",o="击败大祭司乌拉斯",oEN="Defeat Grand Speaker Urash",p="这场战斗不会给我带来喜悦，但黑夜必须先降临，我的人民才能被引向新的黎明。",pEN="This battle brings me no joy, but night must first come before my people can be led into a new dawn.",c="乌拉斯死了！我们的人民再次合为一体！\n\n我为我的人民宣告这场胜利，但我无法真正为此欢欣。要是我早些意识到乌拉斯真正听到的是什么，也许我能阻止他走上这条路。但那是只能由我独自承担的负担。\n\n今晚，为那些给我们的人民带来新黎明的人设宴！",cEN="Urash is dead! Our people are one once more!\n\nI proclaim this victory for the sake of my people, but I can not truly revel in it. Had I realized sooner what Urash truly heard, perhaps I could have stopped him from walking this path. But that is my burden to bear alone.\n\nTonight, a feast in honor of those who bring a new dawn to our people!"}
Q[255004]={d="啊，<name>，很高兴看到你一切安好。你看起来也更强壮了，我一直知道总有一天你会成为部落的伟大英雄。\n\n不，关于如何净化邪能污染，我还没有新主意。还没有！重点是没有！其实我一直在忙着找那个鹰身女妖，或者……暗夜精灵？不管她现在是什么。她变成这样是我的错，谁知道她如今究竟有多大能耐。\n\n看来在你狠狠教训了她之后，她纠集了自己部族的一部分人，来到石爪山，想再拉拢一些当地的鹰身女妖。\n\n然后她把她们带进了一座古老废弃的矿洞，就是那种人人都说\"那是个受诅咒的地方，最好别去\"的地方。这绝不是什么好兆头。\n\n不过，如果你愿意再帮我一次，这也许是我们对付她的机会，免得她变成更大的威胁。只是……带上些帮手，好吗？她现在有机会真正弄懂该怎么运用艾维娜之玫瑰的力量了，所以我只能认为她已经危险得多。",dEN="Ah, <name>, I'm glad to see you're well. You look stronger too, I always knew you'd be a great hero of the Horde one day.\n\nNo, I don't have any new ideas on cleansing the fel taint. Yet! Emphasis on yet! Actually I've been focused on trying to find that harpy, or...night elf? Whatever she is now. It's my fault she's like this, and who knows what she's actually capable of now.\n\nIt seems like after you thrashed her, she grouped up some of her tribe and went here to Stonetalon to rally some of the local harpies too.\n\nThen she took them into an old, abandoned mine, the kind of place everyone just says \"it is a cursed place best left abandoned\". Which cannot be a good sign.\n\nStill, if you're willing to help me one more time, this might be our chance to deal with her before she becomes a bigger threat. Just...take some help with you, will you? She's had the chance to actually understand how to use the power of Avianna's Rose now, so I can only assume she's already much more dangerous.",o="杀死女王艾瑞西娜",oEN="Slay Queen Erethina",p="我当然对她很好奇。如果那朵花把她变成了暗夜精灵，那是不是意味着鹰身女妖曾经也是暗夜精灵？\n\n但为了满足我的好奇心而留她活口太危险了。如果她的事解决了，我终于能回去继续研究如何净化我们身上的邪能腐蚀。",pEN="Of course I'm curious about her. If that flower turned her into a night elf, does that mean Harpies were once night elves?\n\nBut she's too dangerous to leave alive for my curiosity. If she's dealt with, I can finally turn back to my research on purging the fel corruption from us.",c="我就知道你能做到。\n\n她死的时候，周围长出了像艾维娜之玫瑰那样的花？嗯，我想你不会愿意再回去取个样本吧？\n\n不，没关系，你已经为我做得够多了。我怀疑那些花也没有原版真正的力量，就算有……重复一个结果如此惨烈的实验是蠢人才干的事。\n\n长在她的尸体周围，具有治愈和逆转负面变异与创伤的特性，还与荒野之神艾维娜有关联……\n\n哦，抱歉，我只是在自言自语。你可以走了。既然你解决了这个隐患，我得想想下一步的计划。\n\n邪能腐蚀始于我们的旧世界，也许我该穿过黑暗之门，看看那里有没有什么具备合适特性、能帮助逆转它的东西……",cEN="I knew you'd do it.\n\nFlowers like Avianna's Rose grew around her body when she died? Hmm, I don't suppose you'd be willing to go back for a sample?\n\nNo, it's alright, you've done enough for me as it is. I doubt they have the true power of the original anyways, and even if they did...repeating an experiment with such catastrophic results is a fool's endeavor.\n\nGrowing around her corpse, properties to heal and revert negative mutations and wounds, connections to the wild god Avianna...\n\nOh, I'm sorry, I was simply musing. You can go. I need to figure out my next plan now that you've dealt with this loose end.\n\nThe fel corruption started at our old world, maybe I should journey through the Dark Portal and figure out if anything there has the right properties to help reverse it..."}
Q[255005]={d="<这具尸体的伤口与你迄今遇到的任何本地生物都不相符，倒像是地精碎木机造成的。无论是什么干的，都跑不远。>",dEN="<This body's wounds don't match any of the local creatures you've faced so far, but seem to resemble a goblin shredder. Whatever caused it can't be too far.>",o="找到并击败杀害风险投资公司工人的凶手。",oEN="Find and defeat whatever killed the Venture Co. workers."}
Q[255006]={d="罗希尔觉得你很强。强到能杀死乌拉斯。强到能破除诅咒。\n\n新猎人有一项试炼：面对野兽并活下来。奇美拉、蜥蜴、双足飞龙，三者都活下来，就成为伟大的猎人。\n\n那还不是为了乌拉斯，而是三者，以及天空的恐怖，我们称之为沙奈尔·特菲尔的野兽。也活着胜过它，取得全部的凭证，你就是最伟大的猎人，伟大到足以证明罗希尔说得没错。",dEN="Rohil thinks you strong. Strong to kill Urash. Strong to break curse.\n\nThere is trial for new hunters, face beast and survive. Chimera, Lizard, Wyvern, survive all three, become great hunter.\n\nThat not for Urash, all three, and great terror of skies, beast we call Shanel'Tefir. Survive it too, claim proof from all, and you greatest hunter, great enough you may prove Rohil right.",o="从矿洞周围的野兽身上收集战利品。",oEN="Collect trophies from beasts around the mine.",p="这片土地上的野兽比外面的更强。伟大而强大的野兽，只有最伟大的猎人才猎杀得了。",pEN="Beasts of this land stronger than outside. Great, mighty beasts, only felled by greatest hunters.",c="好多战利品，又大又强的战利品！\n\n你是真正的猎人，就像罗希尔说的。",cEN="Many trophies, great, strong trophies!\n\nYou are true hunter, as Rohil says."}
Q[255007]={d="你！没时间多解释了，但我能感觉到希瓦拉尔对你微笑。你强壮而高贵。只能相信她的意志了。\n\n长久以来，我的人民在这片土地上的山谷中与世隔绝地生活，守护着一道绝不能被打破的古老封印。\n\n兄弟反目成仇，我们的大祭司如今把我们当作\"叛徒\"追杀。但我知道罗希尔说的是真话，我们大祭司听到的声音并非来自我们的母亲，而是石之者。\n\n找到卡萨赫，那个受命追猎罗希尔的战士，在他找到其他人之前杀掉他，然后去找罗希尔。他会告诉你更多。",dEN="You! There is little time for explanations, but I can sense that Shirvallah smiles upon you. You are strong and noble. There is no choice but to trust her will.\n\nFor long, my people have lived in isolation within our valley in these lands, caretakers of an ancient seal which must not be broken.\n\nBrother turns against brother, and our Grand Speaker now hunts us down as \"Traitors\". Yet I know that Rohil speaks true, the voice our Grand Speaker hears is not that of our mother, but the Stone One.\n\nFind Kasajh, the warrior tasked with hunting down Rohil, slay him before he can reach the others, then find Rohil. He will tell you far more.",o="杀死卡萨赫",oEN="Slay Kasajh",p="别把注意力引到我们身上，外来者。我们仍在被追猎。",pEN="Do not draw attention to us, outsider. We are still hunted.",c="你亲手斩杀了那支狩猎队？希瓦拉尔今天真的与我们同在！\n\n这座山谷是我族人许多个月来的家园。虽然其下封印着一股危险的力量，我们长久以来都视留守看护它为我们的职责。\n\n从水里来的外来者带来了许多纷争，而那纷争至今仍未真正结束。\n\n但外来者开启的事，也可以由外来者终结，所以我欢迎你来到这座如今作为我们家园的洞穴。",cEN="You have cut down the hunting party, with your own hands? Shirvallah is truly with us this day!\n\nThis valley has been my peoples' home for many moons. Though there is a dangerous power sealed beneath it, we have long considered it our duty to remain here and watch over it.\n\nThe outsiders that came from the water brought much strife, and that strife has yet to truly end.\n\nBut what outsiders began may also be ended by outsiders, and so I welcome you to this cave which now serves as our home."}
Q[255008]={d="这块该死的石头让我见到的损失实在太多了。\n\n但我看得出你跟我们一样好奇。我给的任何警告对你来说，都像砸在雷霆蜥蜴脊背上的石头一样没用。\n\n好吧。我们的机器还没磨损太厉害，到处有些断掉的轨道，不过这地方本来也不怎么下雨。\n\n我们的研究笔记应该也还在附近。把它们带回来，我替你整理好；总比你们为这鬼东西互相残杀要好。",dEN="I've seen far too much loss from this wretched stone.\n\nBut I can tell you're just as curious as we were. Any warnings I give will have as much effect on you as a rock at a Thunder Lizard's spine.\n\nFine. Our machines haven't worn down too much, broken rails here and there, but ain't like it rains much in these parts.\n\nOur research notes should be around too. Get them back here and I'll compile them for you, better that than you all go killing eachother over the wretched stuff.",o="收集共鸣研究笔记",oEN="Collect Resonite Research Notes",p="如果你非找到我们的研究不可，就去我们旧日的设施里翻翻。我敢肯定我们散落了不少笔记。我们谁都没什么整理的兴致。哈！",pEN="Look around our old structures, if you must find our research. I'm certain we left quite a few notes around. None of us had much interest in organizing. Hah!",c="我们都是蠢货。你也许也是。\n\n但这些旧笔记保存得不错。你想怎么处置都行，我是不想再沾手了。",cEN="We were all fools. You might be too.\n\nBut these old notes have weathered well. You may do with it as you see fit, but I want no part in it."}
Q[255009]={d="罗希尔说你很强。\n\n没有什么比石头更强。最强的石头，伟大的紫色石头。\n\n如果你真像罗希尔说的那么强，就证明你比那伟大的紫色石头更强。",dEN="Rohil say you strong.\n\nNothing stronger than stone. Strongest stone of all, great purple stone.\n\nIf you strong as Rohil say, show you stronger than great purple stone.",o="摧毁共鸣元素",oEN="Destroy Resonite Elementals",p="伟大的紫色石头从不待在一个地方。也许伟大的紫色石头很不安分。",pEN="Great purple stone never stay in one place. Maybe great purple stone restless.",c="你打碎了伟大的紫色石头？\n\n你很强。比我强，比大多数人都强。\n\n罗希尔说得对。",cEN="You break great purple stone?\n\nYou strong. Stronger than me, stronger than most.\n\nRohil right."}
Q[255010]={d="占位符",dEN="Placeholder",o="击败肖伦的守护者，阿里尔和塞里什",oEN="Defeat the Keepers of Sholen, Arill and Serish"}
Q[255011]={d="能撤的我们都撤了，但我已经知道，住在外面的那些人里少了几个。我不知道还有没有幸存者……我们在这儿能做的只是守住阵线，该死的，真累人。你是生力军，看起来比我们现在更有机会冲出去。\n\n所以去吧，检查那些建筑，在兽人找到那些可怜人之前救下他们。",dEN="We've evacuated all we could, but I already know we're down a few heads from folk who live out there. I don't know if there's any survivors, ...it's all we can do just holdin' the line 'ere, and damn is it exhaustin'. Yer fresh, and ya seem like you've got a better chance of pushin' through than we do right now.\n\nSo go on an' check those buildings and save some poor folks 'fore the orcs get to 'em.",o="从燃炉堡救出幸存者",oEN="Rescue survivors from Burndural",p="我会先检查那些建筑，我敢打赌里面还藏着人。",pEN="I'd check the buildings first, bet there's still some folk hidin' in there.",c="我看见有一个从这儿过去了。我敢说后面还有更多，是吧？\n\n……\n\n以穆拉丁的胡子起誓，他们每杀一个矮人，我就要砍倒一百个这些该死的兽人。听见了吗？！都来吧，你们全部，我正手痒着要把斧头染成绿色！",cEN="Saw one come on through. Bet there's more right behind ya, eh?\n\n...\n\nBy Muradin's beard, I'll cut down a hundred of these wretched orcs for every dwarf they've killed. Ya hear that?! Come on over, all of ya, I'm itchin' ta dye me axe green!"}
Q[255012]={d="开始觉得这像是在自家农场里对付兔子了，解决一只，转眼又冒出三只。以圣光之名，我真希望现在对付的是兔子。\n\n你要是想帮忙，最好就是砍倒一些兽人，至少让他们慢下来一点；我不指望你一个人结束这场进攻，但至少让我们喘口气。我正憋着劲想再敲碎几颗兽人的脑袋，可其他人大多不习惯这么长时间不间断地打下去。",dEN="Startin' ta feel like dealin' with rabbits on me farm, we deal with one an' next thing ya know there's three more takin' its place. By the Light I wish we were dealin' with rabbits right now.\n\nIf yer lookin' ta help, best thing'd be cutting down some orcs 'til they at least slow down a bit, I wouldn't expect ya'd go endin' the assault all by yerself, but at least give us a breather, I'm rearin' ta cave in some more orc skulls, but most o' the others ain't used ta fightin' this long without a break.",o="杀死燃炉堡附近的龙喉兽人",oEN="Kill Dragonmaw orcs near Burndural",p="你还待在后面干什么！出去打啊！",pEN="What are ya still doin' back here! Get yerself out there an' fight!",c="你杀了多少？！\n\n我收回把他们比作兔子的话，连兔子都没这么缠人。好吧，尝试得不错，谢谢你。\n\n好了兄弟们，看来我们还得在这儿待上一阵子！",cEN="Ya killed how many?!\n\nI take back comparin' this ta rabbits, even rabbits ain't this persistent. Well, was a good try, thank ye.\n\nAlright lads, sounds like we're gonna be out here a while yet!"}
Q[255013]={d="这些好心的乡亲多半是想讨回公道，或者至少想帮我们免于被屠杀。他们也许不是战士，但他们有胳膊，也知道怎么抡，眼下这就够了。主要问题是我们没武器了。\n\n要是人人都能至少打上一架，我们的处境会好得多，我敢肯定路障外面还留着些兵器。你出去的时候能顺手捡几件回来吗？",dEN="Most of these fine folk are lookin' for some payback, or at least a chance ta help us all not get slaughtered. Might not be fighters, but they've got arms and know how ta swing 'em, that's plenty right now. Main problem's that we're all outta weapons.\n\nWe'd be in much better shape if everyone could at least fight, and I'm sure there's some arms we left past the barricade. Think ya could grab a few while yer out there?",o="从燃炉堡外围收集矮人武器",oEN="Collect Dwarven Armaments from the outskirts of Burndural",p="你找到的武器我们都会用上，盾牌也是，我敢打赌那儿也散落着一些。",pEN="We'll put any weapons ya find out there ta use, shields too, bet there's some o' those layin' around too.",c="对，这些够用了，这些够用了。上好的矮人兵器，眼下我想不出比这更美的景象了。当然，除非穆拉丁本人现身助战。",cEN="Yeah, these'll do, these'll do. Fine dwarven arms, can't imagine a more beautiful sight right now. 'Cept for Muradin 'imself showin' up ta help the fight o' course."}
Q[255014]={d="整件事太有组织了。我一开始就在琢磨，现在已经确定：他们有个首领，而且说来气人，还是相当不错的一个。\n\n但你知道那还意味着什么吧？意味着他们有弱点。我们又多了些能打的人，所以能在这儿守住一阵，但这不代表我们可以离开这道路障。\n\n一直往前冲的人是你，所以如果你能找出那个首领，也许这次终于能打断这场进攻。",dEN="This whole thing's been too organized. I was thinkin' at the start and I'm sure now, they've got a leader, and much as I hate sayin' it, a pretty good one.\n\nBut ya know what that also means, don't ye? It means they've got a weakness. We've got some more folks ready ta fight, so we can hold the line here for a bit, but that doesn't mean we can go leavin' this barricade.\n\nYer the one who's been pushin' through, so if ye can track down that leader, maybe ye can finally break the assault this time.",o="在燃炉堡外杀死指挥官阿姆祖斯特",oEN="Slay Commander Amzust outside Burndural",p="他们不可能全都在要塞里遥控指挥，路上某处一定有个指挥官。",pEN="There's no way they're all managin' this from back at the fort, they must've got a commander up the road somewhere.",c="看来他们已经开始松懈了，我猜那就是你干成了。\n\n我不能说这是它应得的，我更想看到它承受每一个死去的优秀矮人所感受痛苦的一百倍，但如果这能打断进攻，我也认了。\n\n干得好，干得好，等这一切结束，我欠你一杯酒。或者一百杯。",cEN="Seems like they're startin' ta let up already, I'm guessin' that means ya did it.\n\nCan't say this is what it deserved, would've rather seen it suffer a hundredfold what every fine dwarf who died felt, but if this breaks the attack I'll settle for it.\n\nFine work, fine work, once this is over, I owe ya a drink. Or a hundred."}
Q[255015]={d="看来这边也平息下来了，剩下的交给我们。\n\n如果你还要待一阵子，镇上有个古怪的家伙，叫艾利尔。几年前出现的，没有氏族名，什么都没有，但他似乎比谁都了解龙喉。\n\n既然我们终于有余力发动攻势了，我敢打赌他有些主意，知道你接下来该做什么。",dEN="Seems like this is dyin' down, we'll take care of the rest from here.\n\nIf yer stickin' around, there's an odd fellow in town, goes by Aelir. Showed up a couple years back, no clan name or nothin', but he seems ta know more 'bout the Dragonmaw than anymore.\n\nNow that we can finally afford an offensive, I'll bet he's got a few ideas what ya should do next.",o="在燃炉堡与艾利尔交谈",oEN="Speak with Aelir in Burndural",p="<这矮人一脸困惑，仿佛你做了什么本不可能做到的事。>",pEN="<The dwarf seems puzzled, as if, somehow, you've done something that should not be possible.>",c="啊，这是不是意味着进攻终于结束了？\n\n龙喉制造了一场又一场悲剧。这不是第一次，也不会是最后一次，但我很高兴听到这场战斗至少最终打赢了。\n\n无论如何，能见到另一位龙喉的敌人是我的荣幸。祖鲁玛早就该烧起来了。",cEN="Ah, does this mean the attack is over at last?\n\nThe Dragonmaw beget tragedy after tragedy. This is not the first, nor will it be the last, but I am glad to hear this battle was at least won in the end.\n\nIn any case, it is an honor to meet another enemy of the Dragonmaw. It is past time for Zulumar to burn."}
Q[255016]={d="龙喉看似无穷无尽，但我向你保证并非如此。他们只是不在乎性命，连自己同族的命也不在乎。\n\n他们无法用同理心感受的东西，就会在自身力量的创伤中感受到。砍倒他们的战士，直到他们无法再从自己人里轻易补充。\n\n这看起来残忍吗？别忘了，你杀死的那些人在犯下残忍行径时，可远没有这么多顾虑。",dEN="The Dragonmaw may seem endless, but I promise they are not. They simply care little for lives, even the lives of their own kin.\n\nWhat they cannot feel in empathy they will feel in a wound to their power. Cut down their warriors until they cannot so easily find replacements amongst their own.\n\nDoes this seem cruel? Do not forget that the ones you slay would show far more cruelty with far less remorse.",o="在祖鲁玛杀死龙喉督军、龙喉暗影萨满和龙喉死亡先知",oEN="Kill Dragonmaw Warlords, Dragonmaw Dark Shamans, and Dragonmaw Death Scryers in Zulumar",p="要塞里的那些会比这次进攻的人更有经验、也更集中。没有准备就别进去。",pEN="The ones at the fortress will be more experienced and more concentrated than this assault. Do not go in there unprepared.",c="我怜悯那些被他们关押奴役的龙。\n\n我怜悯那些被他们杀害的矮人，也怜悯那些被迫放弃平静生活、拿起武器的人。\n\n但我对龙喉已经再没有怜悯了。",cEN="I hold pity for the dragons they held prisoner and enslaved.\n\nI hold pity for the dwarves they have slain, and for those who are forced to give up a peaceful life and fight.\n\nBut I have no pity left for the Dragonmaw."}
Q[255017]={d="龙喉曾经骑在他们奴役的龙背上，从天空监视敌人。\n\n幸运的是，那些龙如今大多自由了，他们只能从自己建造的塔楼里眺望，但要是能彻底夺走这些\"眼睛\"，那就更好了。\n\n只有最精锐的人才会被安排在这样的位置，其中不少是昔日的龙骑士，但既然你已在此迎击过他们的进攻，我相信你能应付。",dEN="The Dragonmaw once watched their enemies from the skies atop the dragons they enslaved.\n\nFortunately, most of those dragons are now free, and they are consigned to watching from towers of their own making, but it would be better still if they were deprived of such \"eyes\" entirely.\n\nOnly their most skilled would be placed in such positions, many former dragonriders, but as you have already faced their assault here, I trust you can handle this.",o="杀死祖鲁玛周围瞭望塔上的龙喉哨兵",oEN="Slay Dragonmaw Lookouts atop watchtowers around Zulumar",p="到了那里，就找要塞内外的制高点，他们多半把哨兵布置在那些地方。",pEN="When you get there, look for high points in and around the fortress, they likely have their lookouts posted at those.",c="至少眼下，他们对我们一无所知。会有别人接替他们，所以我们必须赶在他们重新合拢这道缺口之前速战速决。",cEN="At least for now, they will be blind to us. More will take their place, so we must be quick, before they close this opening again."}
Q[255018]={d="龙喉仍关押着许多俘虏，那些可怜的孩子被迫满足他们的一切任性要求。我太清楚他们一定感受到的痛苦，那种连逃走都无力的绝望……\n\n其他一切我都是为了燃炉堡而请求，但你到了那里，我还有一个私人的请求。求你，把那些孩子从龙喉的魔掌中解救出来。他们也许会被迫反抗，但如果奴役他们的人倒下，我相信他们能自己逃出来。",dEN="The Dragonmaw still keep many captives, poor children forced to serve their every whim. I know all too well the pain they must feel, the helplessness to even escape...\n\nEverything else I ask for the sake of Burndural, but while you are there, I must make one personal request as well. Please, free the children from the Dragonmaw's clutches. They may be forced to resist, but if their subjugator's fall, I am sure they can escape on their own.",o="从龙喉手中救出\"孩子们\"",oEN="Rescue \"Children\" from the Dragonmaw",p="我相信那些可怜的孩子并不想伤害你。等你杀掉控制他们的兽人后，我相信他们就不会再找你麻烦了。",pEN="I'm sure those poor children do not wish to hurt you. Once you kill the orcs controlling them, I'm sure they won't cause you any more trouble.",c="他们身上还是那么多伤疤……\n\n我太记得了。龙喉确实是残忍的主人。这些孩子大多没有名字，只有证明自己有用的人才会得到一个，而他们还太年幼，还没来得及证明自己。\n\n等我给他们治完伤，我会给所有人起名字，就像母亲在我重获自由时给我起名一样，但眼下只能再等等。我们还没做完。",cEN="They still have so many scars...\n\nI remember, all too well. The Dragonmaw are cruel master's indeed. Most of these children do not have names, only those who prove useful receive one, and they are still too young to have proven themselves.\n\nOnce I have finished treating them, I will name them all, just as Mother named me when I was freed, but for now that must wait. We are not done yet."}
Q[255019]={d="我们砍断了他们的手臂，弄瞎了他们的眼睛，但除非砸碎他们的头颅，他们绝不会停手。\n\n说得简单些，我们必须杀掉在祖鲁玛指挥他们军队的那个兽人。她是个残忍的首领，也是名强悍的战士，但我相信到现在，我们已经吸引了足够多的注意，她会走出要塞，哪怕只是为了找出可以替他们的失败顶罪的人加以惩罚。\n\n这个机会不能错过。出手要准，出手要快，<name>。",dEN="We have cut their arms and blinded their eyes, but they will not stop until they have crushed their skull.\n\nIn a simpler explanation, we must kill the orc commanding their forces in Zulumar. She is a cruel leader and a mighty warrior, but I am sure by now we have drawn enough attention for her to step outside her fortress, if only to find whoever she can blame for their failings and punish them.\n\nThis is not a chance we can lose. Strike well and strike fast, <name>.",p="即使这场战斗看似毫无胜算，也请你不要放弃。",pEN="Even if the fight seems unwinnable, please, do not give in.",c="<艾利尔的眼神蒙上了一层你从未在他脸上见过的痛苦与恐惧。>\n\n你打得很好，我真的曾为你的性命担忧，但看来我的担忧是多余的。科妮姆终于死了……我常常在想她是否真的会死。终于结束了……\n\n有条幼龙在战斗中帮了你，是吗？嗯，我看也没必要多想了，重要的是科妮姆再也无法制造苦难，而权力真空应该能让他们在接下来一段时间里无力威胁燃炉堡。",cEN="<Aelir's eyes are glazed with a pain and fear you have not in any other time you've spoken to him.>\n\nYou fought well, truly I had feared for your life, but I see my fear was misplaced. Konym is finally dead...I had often wondered if she could ever truly die. It is finally over...\n\nA drake aided you in the battle, hmm? Well, I don't see any reason to dwell on that, what matters is that Konym will cause no more suffering, and the power vacuum should keep them from threatening Burndural for some time yet."}
Q[255020]={d="特里西拉·塞尔维恩曾是奥克兰最出色的法师之一，即便在她死后，她的法术书也一直是重要的遗物。\n\n不幸的是，它落入了猎鹰栖家族手中被当作展品，如今我听说它被交给了一个辛迪加认为会成为下一个塞尔维恩的狂妄法师。凯齐娅充其量只是个新手，她所做的不过是抄别人的咒语，再用一堆听起来很魔法的词让上司相信她最懂魔法。\n\n我料想总有一天她会念错咒语把法术书烧成灰，就算她不会，我们也最好把它从辛迪加手里拿回来。听说他们给了她敦霍尔德的那座塔，你大概能在那里找到她。",dEN="Trisira Selvane was one of Alterac's finest mages, once, and even after she died, her spellbook has been an important relic.\n\nUnfortunately it fell into the hands of the Falconrest family to put on display, and now I hear it got given to some upstart mage the Syndicate thinks will be the next Selvane. Kezia's a novice at best, all she does is copy other peoples' incantations and talk in enough magical-sounding words to convince her superiors she knows the most magic.\n\nOne of these days I'm expecting she'll read a spell wrong and turn the spellbook to ash, and even if she doesn't, it's better we get it out of the Sydicate's hands. Sounds like they gave her the tower in Durnholde, so you'll probably find her there.",o="在敦霍尔德城堡从凯齐娅手中夺回特里西拉·塞尔维恩的法术书",oEN="Recover Trisira Selvane's spellbook from Kezia at Durnholde Keep",p="奥克兰的历史不该落在辛迪加的暴发户手里。",pEN="Alterac's history does not belong in the hands of Syndicate upstarts.",c="她刚才居然折了书页做标记？！这是重要的历史遗物，应该小心对待！\n\n啊，好吧，至少我们及时把它拿了回来，没让它受到严重损坏，谢谢你。",cEN="Did she just fold the pages to mark them?! This is an important historical relic and it should be treated with care!\n\nAh, well, at least we recovered it because it could get any serious damage, thank you."}
Q[255021]={d="我是为了瓦勒希尔领主而来。即便在奥克兰陷落之前，他也只是个小贵族，勉强守着祖辈留下的权力残渣。他很快就投靠了辛迪加，想方设法讨好佩雷诺德领主，作为回报，他得到了管理敦霍尔德城堡驻军的差事。\n\n事实证明他干得出奇地称职，但我真正感兴趣的是收集他计划的情报。我被抓过，只好退回这里，既然他们已经知道有我这个人，我短时间内恐怕不会再有别的机会。\n\n你看起来像是会选择更直接手段的人。任务怎么完成我不介意，但记得搜他身上有没有和辛迪加其他成员的往来信件。",dEN="I came here after Lord Valesir. Even before Alterac fell, he was a minor noble, barely holding onto the scraps of power from his ancestors. He was quick to cast his lot in with the Syndicate and do anything he could to curry favor with Lord Perenolde, which rewarded him with the job of managing their forces at Durnholde Keep.\n\nHe's proven surprisingly competent at that job, but my real interest is in gathering information on his plans. I was caught and had to retreat back here, so I doubt I'll get another opening for a good while with them already aware of me.\n\nYou seem like the sort to try a more direct approach. However the job gets done is fine with me, but just remember to search him for any correspondence with the rest of the Syndicate.",o="在敦霍尔德城堡击败瓦勒希尔领主并收集信件",oEN="Defeat Lord Valesir in Durnholde Keep and collect correspondence",p="辛迪加主要是靠奥克兰的旧贵族维系在一起的。不过那些贵族从前就意见不合，我想不出如今会有什么改变。",pEN="The Syndicate is mostly held together by former nobles of Alterac. Those nobles never saw eye to eye before though, I cannot envision that changing now.",c="被传送走了，嗯？据我所知，他只受过剑术训练，真奇怪。看起来你总算找到了点东西，让我看看。\n\n有意思……他似乎和辛迪加里的另一个人合作，谋划一场政变，事成之后换取更高的位置，而那两人都在为一个叫\"阿古斯之醒\"的组织效力。\n\n这确实很有用。当然，信上没有署名，除非他政变的同伙是个十足的蠢货，我本来也不指望有，但底部有个猎鹰的符号。稍微查一查，我也许能把它和另一个贵族家族对上。\n\n辛迪加内斗确实是个机会。",cEN="Teleported, hmm? Last I heard, he was only trained with a sword, how strange. It looks like you found something anyways, so let me take a look.\n\nIntriguing...he seems to have been working with someone else in the Syndicate to plan a coup in return for a higher position once it's done, and the two of them were both working with a group called \"Argus Wake\".\n\nThis is certainly useful to know. Of course it's not signed, I would expect as much unless his partner in the coup is a complete idiot, but there's a symbol of a falcon at the bottom. With a bit of research I might be able to match this to another noble house.\n\nInfighting in the Syndicate would certainly be an opportunity indeed."}
Q[255022]={d="山上那座人类要塞长期以来近得让人不安。大酋长萨尔命令我们不要去动他们，我们也确实没动，因为他们同样没有来犯。\n\n但昨天我的女儿被人类的刀砍倒，虽然她还活着，却全凭意志撑着。她不是战士，她只是在为我们采晚饭的食材。\n\n只要他们还渴求流血，我们大酋长所期望的和平就不会到来，我相信他也会明白这一点。",dEN="The human fort atop the mountain has long been too close for comfort. Warchief Thrall ordered us to leave them alone, and leave them alone we have, as they had done the same in kind.\n\nBut yesterday my daughter was cut down by human blade, and though she lives, it is only by the strength of her will. She is not a warrior, she was only gathering food for our dinner.\n\nThe peace our warchief wishes will not happen while they seek bloodshed, I am sure he too will understand.",o="在傲心堡杀死塞拉摩海军陆战队员和塞拉摩医护者",oEN="Slay Theramore Marines and Theramore Menders at Fort Airheart",p="你不用走很远就能找到他们，他们就在陶拉祖营地东南方不远的一座山丘上。",pEN="You should not have to go far to find them, they are atop a hill a bit to the south-east of Camp Taurajo.",c="有些人会为这个结果高兴，或者说这不过是迟早的事。\n\n不过，我一直相信我们战斗的目标是和平生活。新的敌对行动开始并不会让我高兴，但他们伤害了我的女儿，这不能不付出代价。",cEN="Some will be glad of this outcome, or will say this was only a matter of time.\n\nStill, I have always believed the goal of our fight has been to live in peace. The beginning of new hostilities brings me no joy, but they harmed my daughter, and that cannot go unrepaid."}
Q[255023]={d="你……求你，听我说……\n\n他们把我丢下等死的时候……说是法兰队长……下令攻击的……\n\n……想要战争……对陶拉祖……\n\n<这牛头人似乎伤痛难忍，说话十分吃力，但听起来你该去杀掉这个法兰队长。>",dEN="You...please, listen...\n\nWhen they left me for dead...they said Captain Farran...ordered them to attack...\n\n...Wants war...with Taurajo...\n\n<The Tauren seems to be struggling to talk through her injuries, but it sounds like you should kill this Captain Farran.>",o="在傲心堡杀死法兰队长。",oEN="Kill Captain Farran at Fort Airheart.",p="<这牛头人似乎虚弱得说不出更多话了，你最好让她休息。>",pEN="<The Tauren seems too weak to say anything else, you should probably let her rest.>",c="他死了？\n\n我……并不想成为更多流血的起因，但如果他打算伤害我这里的家人，那我感激他已经死了。\n\n别担心我，自从你上次来之后，我已经好多了。我父亲说再过几天我就能重新走路了。\n\n……不过要让我一个人去采果子，可能还得再等一阵子。",cEN="He's gone?\n\nI...did not wish to be the cause of more bloodshed, but if he planned to harm my family here, then I am grateful he is gone.\n\nDon't worry about me, I'm already feeling a lot better since last time you were here. My father says I should be able to walk again in a few days.\n\n...It might be a while longer before I go gathering fruits alone though."}
Q[255024]={d="等等！\n\n<令人意外的是，这个人类似乎能说一口相当流利的兽人语。>\n\n在你杀我之前，至少听我把话说完，我不是你的敌人。我们谁都不该是；与部落开战是普罗德摩尔女士最不想要的事。我们的命令是维持和平，但我们的队长原本是戴林的人，看来他对老上司大元帅的忠诚仍胜过对普罗德摩尔女士。\n\n倒也不能只怪他，我是唯一一个站出来反对他的人，所以被当成了叛徒。我知道你没有理由相信我，但我想离开这里，好把这一切报告给普罗德摩尔女士。她希望与你们的人民和平相处，至少我信仰她的理想……看来只有我一个。",dEN="Wait!\n\n<The human, surprisingly, seems to speak mostly fluent orcish.>\n\nBefore you kill me, at least hear me out, I'm not your enemy. None of us are supposed to be, war with the Horde is the last thing Lady Proudmoore wants. Our orders were to keep the peace, but our captain was originally one of Daelin's men, seems like he's still more loyal to his old Grand Admiral than he is to Lady Proudmoore...\n\nNot that I can blame only him, I was the only one who spoke up against him, so I've been deemed a traitor. I know you don't have any reason to trust me, but I'd like to get out of here so I can report all this to Lady Proudmoore. She wants peace with your people, and I at least believe in her ideals...seems like I'm the only one.",o="护送维克托林·纽伯里离开傲心堡",oEN="Escort Viktorin Newbery out of Fort Airheart",p="没时间说话了，我们得赶紧离开这里！",pEN="There's no time to talk, we need to get out of here!",c="这里离他们的领地应该够远了，剩下的路我可以自己回塞拉摩。\n\n感谢你选择相信我，戴林的理念在人们心中慢慢消亡，所以她面前肯定还有很长的路，但我的忠诚首先属于我的女士。\n\nLok'tar Ogar，朋友。\n\n……我大概用错了。要是你不介意，我……这就走了。",cEN="This should be far enough from their territory, I can make the rest of my way back to Theramore myself.\n\nI appreciate that you chose to trust me, Daelin's ideals have died slowly the hearts of the people, so I'm sure she has a long road ahead, but my loyalties are to my lady first and foremost.\n\nLok'tar Ogar, friend.\n\n...I'm probably using that wrong. I'll...get going now, if you don't mind."}
Q[255025]={d="洛丹伦过去从达拉然的奥术知识中获益良多。\n\n不幸的是，某些……近期的事态让我们再也无法接触那些知识，我们的法师因此很不好过。当然，无意冒犯我们的好朋友达拉尔，但一位法师无论多么才华横溢，也替代不了达拉然的藏书。\n\n要是有人能……\"说服\"他们多借我们几本书，那就太好了，你不觉得吗？以我对达拉然那些人的了解，他们大多数人身上肯定都带着一两本法术书。",dEN="Lordaeron used to benefit greatly from the arcane knowledge of Dalaran.\n\nUnfortunately certain...recent developments have deprived us of access to that knowledge, and our mages have been suffering as a result, no offense to our good friend Dalar of course, but one mage, brilliant as he may be, is poor replacement for Dalaran's libraries.\n\nIt would be fortunate if someone were to...\"convince\" them to lend us some more tomes, don't you think? Knowing the people of Dalaran, I'm sure most of them are carrying around a spellbook or two.",o="在安伯米尔从达拉然部队身上收集达拉然法术书。",oEN="Collect Dalaran Spellbooks from Dalaran forces in Ambermill.",p="我了解达拉然那些人，他们中大概有一半人走到哪儿都带着书。",pEN="Knowing those Dalaran folk, half of them are probably carrying around a book whever they go.",c="确实妙极了！\n\n嗯，如果他们因此受到什么伤害，那只能怪他们在我们如今这副样子下还另眼相看，你不觉得吗？",cEN="Splendid indeed!\n\nWell, if any harm had to come to them for these, that'd be their fault for regarding us differently in our current state, don't you think?"}
Q[255026]={d="借了东西就该还，你不觉得吗？\n\n当然，当然，我很高兴我们意见一致，这下我们有两个人了，尤其不包括老亨里库斯，他似乎认定完全没有理由把我的法杖还给我。\n\n他本该在几年前就还回来了，就在阿尔萨斯进军洛丹伦之后不久，可他现在一口咬定那是他的了。我还在这儿，那仍是我的法杖，所以如果他不讲道理，也许你能想别的办法把它拿回来。",dEN="If you borrow something, it's only right to give it back after, don't you think?\n\nOf course, of course, I'm glad we're in agreement, that makes two of us, noteably excluding old Henricus, who seems to have reached the conclusion that there's no reason whatsoever to give my staff back.\n\nHe was supposed to give it back years ago now, shortly after Arthas's march on Lordaeron, but he's been insisting it's his to keep now. I am still here, it is still my staff, so if he won't listen to reason, maybe you can find another way to get it back.",o="在塔顶从大法师亨里库斯手中夺回法杖。",oEN="Recover the staff from Archmage Henricus at the top of the tower.",p="至少达拉尔还算讲理。\n\n当然，亨里库斯也不肯跟他说话，可达拉尔在世时，他们曾是要好的朋友。",pEN="At least Dalar is still quite reasonable.\n\nOf course, Henricus won't talk to him either, and they were quite good friends back when Dalar was alive.",c="啊，你在这儿！我当初真不该把你送给那个蠢货，他的仪式问题是他自己的事，我当时到底在想什么？！\n\n哦，对，你还在这儿。我想这算是公道的报酬，对吧？",cEN="Ah, there you are! I should've never given you away to that imbecile, his ritual problems were his own, what was I even thinking?!\n\nOh, yes, you're still here. I think this is fair payment, no?"}
Q[255028]={d="我最近看见了些怪事，<race>。就在这儿正南方那道山脊后面，我看见一条纳迦在游来游去。我在沙漠里从没见过这种黏糊糊的杂种，但这肯定不是好事。我们有一半的活儿都在水里干，我可不想那东西溜上来把我的炼金师叼走当点心。你能去那边处理掉它吗？",dEN="I seen’ something strange lately, <race>. Just behind that mountain ridge right south of here, I seen’ a naga swimmin’ around. Haven’t seen one of those slimy bastards ever in the desert, but it can’t be good. Half of our jobs are done in the water, and I don’t want that thing slithering up and taking one of my alchemists for a snack. Can you go there and deal with it?",o="调查蒸汽轮港南方的纳迦出没事件。",oEN="Investigate the strange naga sightings to the south of Steamwheedle Port.",p="我不知道那条纳迦在这儿干什么，但纳迦离蒸汽轮这么近肯定没好事。",pEN="I don't know what that naga is doing here, but naga so close to Steamwheedle can't be good.",c="啊，你回来了！你给那个满身鳞片、黏糊糊、滑溜溜、鬼鬼祟祟、阴险狡诈、潜行水底的家伙……\n\n……你解决它们了吗？",cEN="Ah, you’re back! You give that scaled, slimy, slithery, sneaky, subtly, submersively…\n\n…you get ‘em?"}
Q[255029]={d="我的人民曾和你的一样，<race>。我们曾居住在一个伟大国度的海岸上。但我们的女王背叛了我们，为了力量把我们卖给了敌人。如今我们得到了它，却被禁锢在黑暗的深渊之中……\n\n我在寻找逆转我们变形、取回失落形态的方法。如此扭转时间的力量必定掌握在青铜龙手中。找到他们的巢穴，屠杀他们的幼崽。带给我所寻求的救赎。",dEN="My people were once like yours, <race>. We dwelt upon the ssssshores of a great nation. But our queen betrayed us, sssssold us to the enemy for the promise of power. Now we have it, bound to the dark depthssss…\n\nI ssseek a way to reverse our transformation and regain our losssst forms. Ssssuch power to reverse time musssst be in control of the Bronze Dragons. Find their lair and sssslaughter their young. Bring me the ssssalvation I seek.",o="在时光之穴附近收集1份时光之沙，带给扎拉什吉。",oEN="Collect 1 Sands of Time near the Caverns of Time and bring it to Zalashji.",p="你找到了吗？我见过南边的青铜龙，可从来靠不近。也许你该去那里找找。",pEN="Have you found it yet? I have ssseeen bronze dragons to the ssssouth, but could never get closssse. Perhapssss you should look there.",c="终于，我欠你一份谢意，<race>。",cEN="At lasssst, I owe you my thanksss <race>."}
Q[255030]={d="我离开家已经好多年了，可我兄弟每周还是会下来喝上一杯。这说明他知道我酿酒比他强，哈！\n\n……不过这一周他还没来，对他来说是有点怪。我不是担心什么的，但你要是旅行途中到了燃炉堡，帮我告诉他他迟到了，好吗？",dEN="I've been away from home for years now, but me brother still comes down for a pint every week. Shows he knows I'm a better brewer than him, hah!\n\n...Still hasn't been here this week though, bit weird for him. I ain't worried or anythin', but if ya end up at Burndural on your travels, tell 'im he's runnin' late, will ya?",o="在燃炉堡找到旅店老板阿尔尼斯",oEN="Find Innkeeper Arnith at Burndural",c="是哈布雷克派你来的，对吧？我猜他没让你捎点麦酒来，我现在可真需要来一杯。\n\n他当然没有，贪婪的混蛋，我每次过去他还照样收我钱。\n\n……好吧，你要是懂点打架的门道，也许可以多待一阵。等这场进攻结束，我就去看我兄弟。",cEN="Halbrek sent ya, did he? Don't suppose he sent any ale with, I could sure use some right now.\n\n'Course he didn't, greedy bastard, still makes me pay every time I come on over.\n\n...Well, if ya know yer way around a fight, maybe ya can stick around a bit. I'll go visit me brother once this assault's over."}
Q[255031]={d="我跟燃炉堡的一个家伙谈好了一笔买卖，听上去是个喜欢高大强壮公羊的人。\n\n可他一直没下来把它们领走，我开始担心他打了退堂鼓。你要是去那边，能帮我催催他吗？要是他不打算下来，我宁愿知道一声，免得在这儿干等。",dEN="I'd talked through a sale to a fellow in Burndural, sounded like someone who loved big, strong rams.\n\nBut he still hasn't been down to pick them up, I'm startin' to worry he got cold feet. If ya find yerself up there, mind botherin' 'im about that? If he's not comin' down I'd rather at least know so I don't sit 'ere waitin'.",o="在燃炉堡寻找猎人乌库恩",oEN="Finds Huntsman Ukourn at Burndural",c="多林的公羊还在？那太好了，可这时候把它们带上来也不合适，对吧？\n\n我们正被进攻，你要是没从满地的打斗看出来。",cEN="Dorin's still got the rams? Well, that's great, but it wouldn't be fair bringin' 'em up 'ere now, would it?\n\nWe're under attack, if ya can't tell by all the attackin'."}
Q[255032]={d="我们也许能打退龙喉，可那救不了我们挨饿！\n\n我们最好的存粮都在焦桶酒馆里……那是我店的名字，不过以龙喉的作风，现在大概真有三两个桶被烧焦了。我怀疑你没那个力气全搬回来，但你要是带回一些，能让我们撑上几天。\n\n再来点麦酒！别忘了麦酒，我们也不能渴死！",dEN="We might be fightin' off the Dragonmaw, but that ain't gonna save us from starvation any!\n\nOur best stock of food's in the Burnt Barrel...that's the name 'o me in, but knowin' the Dragonmaw there's probably an actual burnt barrel or three by now. Doubt ya got the arms to carry it all, but if ya bring back a few things, it'll give us a couple days.\n\nAnd some ale! Don't forget the ale, can't have us dyin' o' thirst either!",o="从焦桶旅店收集补给",oEN="Collect supplies from the Burnt Barrel Inn",p="那些补给拿到了吗？",pEN="Got those supplies yet?",c="你把那些都塞进背包了，嗯？哈！我就知道能指望你。\n\n别担心，东西也许是我店里的，但在这场进攻结束之前我一分钱都不收。只要我们能活下来，他们之后再还我；要是活不下来，金币对我也没用了。",cEN="Ya fit all that in yer pack, eh? Hah! Knew I could count on ya.\n\nDon't worry, might be from me inn, but I ain't chargin' any 'til this attack's over with. They can pay me back after 'long as we live through, an' if we don't, the gold won't be doin' me any good anyways."}
Q[255033]={d="哟，这不是我的救命恩人嘛！我能为你做点什么？把你从那一团糟里救出来，至少得请你喝一杯。\n\n这倒让我想起来，那些兽人把我最喜欢的杯子顺手带走了。进攻停了之后我想去找过，可哪儿都找不到，而那个红家伙说我必须\"休息养伤\"。\n\n连喝酒都不对劲的时候，我怎么休息得下来？麻烦你实在过意不去，可你反正要去找龙喉的麻烦，能不能帮我留意一下？",dEN="Well if it isn't me savior! What can I do for ya? I owe ya a drink at least for gettin' me outta that mess.\n\nThat reminds me, those orcs ran off with me favorite mug, I tried ta go lookin' for it after the assault let up, but I couldn't find it anywhere, and that red fellow says I gotta \"\"rest and recover\"\".\n\nHow am I supposed 'ta rest when even drinkin' doesn't feel right? Wouldn't be fair of me ta impose on ya, but if yer goin' after the Dragonmaw anyways, think ya could keep an eye out?",o="从龙喉手中夺回乌吉尔的杯子",oEN="Recover Urgil's mug from the Dragonmaw",p="求你，帮我找回杯子！一想到兽人会把它摔碎我就受不了。",pEN="Please, find me mug! I can't stand the though o' the orcs breakin' it.",c="你这漂亮可爱的小东西！我可真想死你了！\n\n哦，还有你，<name>。我现在欠你两杯酒了，而我不是喜欢欠债的矮人，所以我安排好了。这是我们眼下最好的酒，好好享用吧。",cEN="Ya beautiful, lovely thing! How I've missed ya so!\n\nOh, and you too, <name>. I owe ya two drinks now, and I ain't a dwarf who likes keepin' debts, so I got that sorted out. Best we've got right now, so enjoy 'em."}
Q[255034]={d="<这个图腾看起来是矮人的手艺，而不是兽人的。也许你该把它带给燃炉堡的居民们。>",dEN="<This totem seems to be of dwarven, not orcish, make. Perhaps you should bring it to the citizens of Burndural.>",o="把图腾带给燃炉堡的一位萨满",oEN="Bring the totem to a shaman in Burndural",c="一个图腾，嗯？让我看看……\n\n看起来像是我们的蛮锤兄弟做的，不是我们。而且应该相当古老，我敢打赌那些兽人是从格瑞姆巴托抢来的，留着自己用，因为他们做不出更好的东西。\n\n倒不是说它能跟我们做的东西比，但它终究是矮人的手艺。眼下我们没资格挑剔，所以能用就用，等这一切结束后，说不定还能还给蛮锤。\n\n如果他们好好开口的话。",cEN="A totem, eh? Let me give it a look...\n\nSeems like somethin' our Wildhammer brothers would've made, not us. Must be pretty old too, I'd bet ya those orcs took it from Grim Batol and held onto it 'cause they can't make anythin' better.\n\nNot that it holds a candle ta anything we make, but it's still dwarven craftmanship. Can't afford to be picky right now, so we can make use of it, maybe even give it back to the Wildhammer's once this is all over.\n\nIf they ask nicely enough."}
Q[255035]={d="斯纳兹偏偏这时候迟到！我到底付他钱是干什么的？\n\n等着。等我把爪子搭上他，他就知道为什么人家叫我“圣”……啊哈！你看起来正是我现在需要的那种<race>。想接份活吗？\n\n斯纳兹是我在南边的干员。他的任务是盯住失落索具工，确保我的船准备出港时他们没在搞什么鬼。问题是，他突然失去了联络，而今天的货值一船船的钱。\n\n说真的，在确认安全之前我没法动身。我需要你找到他，确保他干活，或者把他带回来让我亲自处置。",dEN="Of all the times for Snazzy to be late! What the hell am I even paying him for?\n\nJust wait. When I get my claws on him, he’s gonna know why they call me The San… Ah ha! You look like just the <race> I need right now. Care for a job?\n\nSnazzy is my southern operative. His job is to keep tabs on the Lost Riggers to make sure they aren’t up to something while my boats are about to leave port. The thing is, he’s just gone radio silent, and today’s cargo is worth BOAT LOADS.\n\nBut seriously, I can’t get moving until I know the coast is clear. I need you to find him and make sure he does his job, or bring him here so I can deal with him myself.",o="找到泽贝尔最南边的干员斯纳兹·爆栓。",oEN="Find Zebel's southernmost operative, Snazzy Boomsprocket.",c="哦天，你是在找我？还是泽贝尔派你来的？这可不好，不不不，这非常糟。\n\n我发誓我没偷懒。是那些该死的海巨人，他们变得狂暴，还抢走了我的电台！求你，你得理解我！",cEN="Oh man, you was lookin' for me? And Zebel sent you? That's not good, no no no, that's really bad.\n\nI swear I wasn't slackin'. It's those damn sea giants, they turned aggresive and stole my damn radio! Please, you gotta understand!"}
Q[255036]={d="求你别告诉泽贝尔！比丢工作更糟的是，要是他心情不好的时候逮到我，谁知道我会怎么样。\n\n听着。我可能在海边放松了一下，也可能没有。而且也许，只是也许，我把电台搁在那儿还睡着了。谁知道呢？又或者……我是被伏击了！我一个人左右开弓地打退海巨人，像个真正的狠角色，直到他们终于把我打晕，我才丢了电台。\n\n我觉得第二个版本配着这袋闪亮的金币会更好听，上面还刻着你的名字，对吧？既然你肯听我说了，不如去帮我把电台取回来怎么样？我保证绝对值。",dEN="Please don't tell Zebel! More than my career, there's no tellin' what'll happen to me if he catches me while in a bad mood.\n\nLook. I may or may not have been chillin' near the shore line. And maybe, just maybe I dozed off with my radio there too. Who's ta say? Or maybe.. I was ambushed! Fightin' off sea giants left and right like a right badass, only losin' my radio when they finally managed to knocked me out.\n\nThe second story, I think'll find sounds better with is shiny gold, ripe with ya name on it aye? Now that I got yer attention, how's about yous go and see about retrieving my radio? Bet It'll be more than worth ya while.",o="从附近的海巨人手中夺回斯纳兹的电台。",oEN="Recovery Snazzy's radio from the nearby sea giants.",p="被拖进海里它当然还能用！你难道不知道地精科技要是不靠谱就什么都不是吗？！",pEN="'Course it'll still work if it got dragged ta the sea! Don't ya know goblin tech's nothin' if not reliable?!",c="好了，跟你做生意很愉快，伙计。\n\n很高兴你是那种通情达理的人，只要我们的说法一致，我想就不会有问题。",cEN="Right, It was a pleasure doing business with ya mate.\n\nGlad yer one of the understandin' types, and with our stories straight I think we'll be just fine."}
Q[255037]={d="我说，既然你反正要回蒸汽轮，能帮我个忙吗？\n\n我在这儿闲得很，而且你猜怎么着，我做的东西相当不错。去港口的路不好走，我的大多数跑腿的最后都早早不干了，自愿的或者不自愿的都有。\n\n可你显然是那种在外面毫无顾虑的人，所以就这么说定了。去港口，帮我把货带过去送到，我就付你钱。再方便不过了，对吧？另外，既然我们是这么好的哥们，我还免费送你一口，怎么样？",dEN="Say, since you're headin' back ta Steamwheedle anyways, care to do me a favor?\n\nI gots myself quite a bit of free time down ere, and wouldn't ya know it, I make myself a pretty good product. The route to port isn't an easy one, so most my runners end up quittin' early, voluntarily or otherwise.\n\nBut ya clearly the type with no problems out there, so here's the deal. Go to the port, carry and deliver my stuff, and I pay you. Doesn't get more convenient than that aye? Plus, I'll even throw in a free hit for you since we're such great pals, how's that sound?",o="在蒸汽轮交付斯纳兹的货物",oEN="Deliver Snazzy's goods at Steamwheedle",p="有斯纳兹的消息了吗？",pEN="Any news on Snazzy yet?",c="不用细说了，<race>，斯纳兹已经跟我讲过了。谁知道他这么擅长杀海巨人？还好有他在，救了你的小命，是吧？\n\n总之，干得好。也许有一天你会成为出色的水手。或者码头工人，我不确定，追随你的梦想吧，孩子。",cEN="No need to report details <race>, Snazzy already filled me in. Who knew he was so good at slaying sea giants? Good thing he was there to save your hide huh?\n\nAnyways, great work. Maybe one day you'll make a fine sailor. Or dock worker, not sure, just follow your dreams kid."}
Q[255038]={d="要对付枯须的首领，我需要元素的力量。已经收集来的毛皮和獠牙可以做成一条项链，让我把那份力量绑定其上。\n\n可这里的元素躁动不安，不肯给我需要的力量。身为萨满，我不能伤害元素，可你没这条规矩，对吧？\n\n把元素之核带给我，我就能把它们绑到项链上。",dEN="To fight de Witherbark's leader I need power of de elements. Fur and fangs ya gathered can be make into a necklace I can bind that power to.\n\nBut elements here be actin' up, they ain't given' me de power I need. As a shaman I cannot harm de elements, but you got no such rule, do ya?\n\nBring me cores of de elements, and I can bind 'em to de necklace.",o="为鲁尔汉收集元素之核",oEN="Collect elemental cores for Rul'han",p="你拿到核心了吗，兄弟？",pEN="Ya got the cores yet, mon?",c="元素的力量很快就是我的了！\n\n我还需要你办一件事，兄弟，然后我们就能开始了。",cEN="The power of the elements will soon be mine!\n\nJust one more thing I need from ya, mon, then we can get started."}
Q[255039]={d="终于，我们可以一起去面对枯须的首领了，兄弟！\n\n等我一施完这个法术，我们就准备开打！",dEN="Finally, together we can face the leader of the Witherbark mon!\n\nSoon as I cast this spell, we'll be ready ta fight!",o="杀死枯须大萨满",oEN="Slay the Witherbark High Shaman",p="<项链落在地上，可不知为何，你并不觉得自己做了什么配得上它的事……>",pEN="<The necklace lies on the ground, yet somehow, you don't feel like you've done anything to earn it...>",c="<即便它的制作者已死，项链仍在燃烧着力量。也许你能比它从前的主人更好地利用它。>",cEN="<The necklace still burns with power, even with its creator dead. Perhaps you could make better use of it than she did.>"}
Q[255040]={d="<这本航海日志记载着藏宝海湾的内部运作。看来血帆劫掠者在藏宝海湾有一名线人，经营着当地的一家制革厂。有了这些信息，找到他应该不难。>",dEN="<This logbook contains information on the inner workings of Booty Bay. It seems the Bloodsail Raiders have an informant in Booty Bay who owns a local tannery. With this information, it shouldn't be too much trouble to track him down.>",o="在藏宝海湾与血帆线人对峙。",oEN="Confront the Bloodsail informant in Booty Bay.",c="他们就把那东西丢在那儿？！蠢货……\n\n在你做出什么冲动的事之前，我有个提议。我太清楚这一带是怎么运作的了，雷维尔加兹为找到我会给你不少金币，那不如我现在就在这里付给你，跟他平时为找到一个线人给的数目一样，然后我们都能开开心心过自己的日子。\n\n看着公道吧？我还会在下一份报告里替你说句好话；我不敢说那能让他们不再追杀你，但至少是个开始。\n相关",cEN="They just left that laying around?! Idiots...\n\nBefore you do anything rash, I've got an offer. I know perfectly well how things work around here, Revilgaz will offer you plenty of coin for finding me, so how about instead I pay you right here and now, same amount he'd usually give for finding an informant, and we can all go about our day happy.\n\nSeem fair? I'll throw in a good word in my next report too, can't say it'll get them to stop going after you, but it'll be a start.\nRelated"}
Q[255041]={d="你到底有什么理由站在他们那边？这不是你的事，所以再考虑一下，接受我的交易吧。\n\n我可不想让你知道我们为什么叫血帆……",dEN="And what possible reason would you have to take their side? This isn't your problem, so just reconsider and take my deal.\n\nI'd hate for you to find out why we're called the Bloodsail...",o="站在藏宝海湾一边，把线人的事报告给雷维尔加兹男爵。",oEN="Side with Booty Bay and report the informant to Baron Revilgaz.",c="血帆的船员就藏在我眼皮底下？我一直纳闷为什么会有两家制革店，其中一家连正经的训练都不提供。\n\n藏宝海湾、热沙集团，以及最后但也同样重要的我自己，都很高兴有你这样的伙伴。\n\n找到线人的标准报酬？你从哪儿听说的……我是说，对，当然，我怎么会忘！这是答应你的金币，要是再找到别的，一定告诉我。\n\n现在请容我失陪，我得给卫兵写份备忘录。",cEN="One of the Bloodsail Crew was right under my nose? Always wondered why there were two tanning shops, and one didn't even offer proper training.\n\nBooty Bay, the Steamwheedle Cartel, and last but also least of all myself, are glad to have you as a partner.\n\nStandard payment for finding an informant? Where'd ya hear that...I mean, yes, of course, how could I forget! Your gold, as promised, do let me know if you find any more.\n\nNow if you'll excuse me, I need to writeup a memo for the guards."}
Q[255042]={d="看到了吧？我就知道我们会一拍即合。",dEN="See? I knew we'd see eye to eye.",o="站在血帆海盗一边，接受线人的贿赂。",oEN="Side with the Bloodsail Buccaneers and accept the informant's bribe.",c="你的选择没错。你的金币就在这儿。",cEN="You're making the right choice. I've got your gold right here."}
Q[255043]={d="几个月前我们雇了个新农夫，是个人类，但干活很利索。不幸的是，几个月前他在抵挡枯须的袭击时死了。\n\n可我老是觉得在山丘上看见他的脸，浑身燃烧着，恶狠狠地盯着我。就像他要为我没有救他而复仇……\n\n大概只是压力太大，但你上去的时候能帮忙看看吗？至少这样能让我安心些。",dEN="We brought over a new farmhand a few months back, 'twas a human, but a good worker. Unfortuantely he died fendin' off a Witherbark attack few months back.\n\nBut I keep thinkin' I'm seeing his face up on the mountain, burnin' away, glarin' down at me. Like he wants vengeance for lettin' 'im die...\n\nProbably just the stress gettin' ta me, but think ya could look while you're up there? At least set me mind at ease that way.",o="击败永焰憎恶",oEN="Defeat the Everflame Abomination",p="我怀疑没什么好担心的……只是不想再一直想这件事。",pEN="Doubt there's anythin' ta worry about...just would rather not keep thinkin' about it.",c="那儿什么都没有，只是我自己胡思乱想，对吧？\n\n他真的在那上面走动？！就好像那些巨魔还不够麻烦似的，现在他们竟然这样让死者复生……\n\n至少他现在能安息了……从今往后我们会更留意我们的坟地。",cEN="Nothin' there 'sides me mind playin' tricks, right?\n\nHe was actually walkin' around up there?! As if those trolls ain't enough trouble, now they're raisin' the dead like this...\n\nAt least he can rest now...we'll keep a closer eye on our graves from now on."}
Q[255044]={d="今年在这儿算不上好年头，其实有阵子以来都是最糟的几年之一，倒不是说这段时间我们拿到的有多少。\n\n真正的问题是枯须，他们知道我们有粮食，而且很多，他们又不喜欢公平交易。我们当然够强，能扛住他们，可这些劫掠有时候带来的麻烦比收获还多。\n\n这样吧，你看起来挺会打架，我备了些金币，想请你去削减一下他们的人数。总比再丢更多被抢走的庄稼强。",dEN="This ain't been our best year here, been one of our worst for a while actually, not that we're gettin' as much as we should for a while now.\n\nReal problem's the Witherbark, they know we've got food and lots of it, and they ain't much for fair deals. 'Course we're tough enough ta hold out against 'em, but the raids make it more trouble than it's worth sometimes.\n\nTell ya what, ya seem ta know yer way 'round a fight, I've got some good gold ready for thinin' their numbers a bit. Better that than losin' more in stolen crops.",o="在阿拉希高地杀死枯须勇士、枯须剥皮者和枯须酿酒师",oEN="Slay Witherbark Champions, Witherbark Skinrippers, and Witherbark Brewers in Arathi Highlands",p="往北应该有條路能上到那座山丘。",pEN="Should be a path up north that'll take ya up on the hill.",c="你杀了多少？\n\n哈！这准能让他们慢下来。至少他们短期内会忙着舔伤口，没空再来劫掠我们。",cEN="Ya killed how many?\n\nHah! That'll slow 'em down alright. Should at least be too busy lickin' their wounds for raidin' us again any time soon."}
Q[255045]={d="枯须这，枯须那。照这个速度，没了收成我们都得饿得枯萎！\n\n报复他们也许痛快，可那填不饱肚子。\n\n……其实也能，可我们没有能把巨魔肉做得能入口的香料。\n\n他们搜得不仔细，我敢肯定你稍微找找，田里还留着不少好庄稼，可眼下我们没人手去找。",dEN="Witherbark this, Witherbark that. We're all gonna wither away from starvation without our harvest at this rate!\n\nGettin' revenge on 'em might feel good, but it ain't gonna fill our stomachs.\n\n...Well it could, but we don't have the spices for makin' troll meat palatable.\n\nThey ain't very thorough, I'm sure there's still plenty o' good crops left in the fields if ya look around a bit, but we don't have anyone up for lookin' right now.",o="在阿勒斯通庄园收集剩余的庄稼",oEN="Collect remaining crops on Alestone Estate",p="那边收成不多，能找到多少算多少，我们将就着过。",pEN="It's slim pickings out there, just get what ya can find and we'll make do.",c="太好了！这些够撑一阵子了。没人会乐意要省着吃到下次收成，但我们将就着过。",cEN="Beautiful! That'll be plenty fer now. None of us will be happy havin' ta ration this out 'til next harvest, but we'll make do."}
Q[255046]={d="看样子你也是枯须的敌人，兄弟。他们是这片神圣土地上的毒瘤，想要什么就拿什么，从不回报！\n\n杀些小角色拦不住他们，唯一重要的是他们的首领，枯须最强大的萨满。太强了，一个人打不过。\n\n先来，我需要山狮的獠牙和熊的毛皮；你要是没被撕碎，我再解释其余的事。",dEN="Seems ya be a fellow enemy of the Witherbark, mon. They be a cyst upon this sacred land, takin' all they want and givin' nothin' in return!\n\nKillin' nobodies won't stop them any, only one that matters is their leader, strongest shaman of the Witherbark. Too strong to fight alone.\n\nTo start, I be needin' fangs from de mountain lions and fur from de bears, if ya don't get mauled gettin' those, I'll explain de rest.",o="为鲁尔汉收集山狮獠牙和灰熊毛皮",oEN="Collect Mountain Lion Fangs and Gray Bear Fur for Rul'han",p="你拿到毛皮和獠牙了吗，兄弟？",pEN="Do ya have the fur and claws yet, mon?",c="好，好，这些完全够用。",cEN="Good, good, these'll work just fine."}
Q[255047]={d="像这样绑定力量并不稳定，我需要更好的东西来承载它。\n\n阿拉希一带有些奇怪的晶体，我觉得它们是某种牢狱的一部分，兄弟。\n\n这儿附近那块似乎处于休眠状态，但我想我可以把核心绑到它的一小块上。只要一小块，整块太大了，没法随身带着。",dEN="Bindin' power like dis ain't stable, I need somethin' better ta hold it.\n\nThere be strange crystals around Arathi, I think they be part of some kinda prison, mon.\n\nDe one near here seems dormant, but I think I could bind de cores to a piece of it. Just a small piece, whole thing's too big ta go around wearin'.",o="为鲁尔汉收集一块虹彩碎片",oEN="Collect an Iridescent Fragment for Rul'han",p="如果那块晶体是牢狱，那它应该能很好地容纳力量，兄弟。",pEN="If that crystal be a prison, it should contain power nicely, mon.",c="很快就没有什么能挡住我了！\n\n当然，我说的是杀掉枯须的首领，兄弟。",cEN="Soon nothin' gonna stand in my way!\n\nOf course, I be meanin' about killin' the Witherbark's leader mon."}
Q[255048]={d="啊，你来了。瞧，这才是我喜欢的！让人回来就真回来的人。\n\n现在听好了，小子，因为我给你准备了更轻松的活。轻松得像系鞋带或者数手指。我要雪茄。好雪茄。不是这儿有些人拿来充数的那种泡过水的烂木头。\n\n我在蒸汽轮有个欠我人情的供货商。你只要过去，告诉他泽贝尔派你来的，然后把货取回来。不许讨价还价。不许自作聪明。拿着箱子直接回到这儿。明白了吗？",dEN="Ahhh there you are. See This is what I like! Someone who actually comes back when they are told to.\n\nNow listen up, kid, because I've got an even easier job for you. Easy like tying your boots or counting your fingers. I need cigars. Good ones. Not the soggy driftwood garbage some folks try to pass off around here.\n\nI got a supplier here in Steamwheedle who owes me a favor. All you gotta do is go over there, tell him Zebel sent you, and pick up the shipment. No negotiations. No creative interpretations. You take the box and you come right back here. Got it?",o="从泽贝尔的供货商那里取回他的雪茄货物，然后回到蒸汽轮的泽贝尔·施普利特身边。",oEN="Retrieve Zebel’s cigar shipment from his supplier and return to Zebel Shplit in Steamwheedle.",p="我的雪茄货到了吗？",pEN="You got my cigar shipment yet?",c="就是它！\n\n你拖得够久的，不过嘿，东西都完好无损地回来了，那我就当是赢了。\n\n你也许有点潜力，小子，我上次派出去的3个人都没回来。\n\n他们肯定是吓着了，羞愧得没脸见人，对吧？可你不一样！这就已经让你强过这儿一半的码头工人了。",cEN="There it is!\n\nTook you long enough, but hey, everything made it back in one piece, so I am callin it a win.\n\nYou might have some potential kid, last 3 guys I sent out didn't come back.\n\nMust have gotten nervous and couldn't show their face out of shame huh? But not you! That already puts you ahead of half the dock workers here."}
Q[255049]={d="你有没有过那种觉得自己该做点什么的感觉？\n\n我从来不是能久坐不动的人，可我没法让自己离开同伴们……在埃德蒙出事后就更不行了。我想我一个人不够强，没法面对辛迪加，可一想到要留在这里什么都不做，我就心神不宁。\n\n你看起来很有本事。如果你要往那边去，就尽量多干掉那些恶棍。\n\n只是……别把命丢了。求你。",dEN="Do you ever feel like you should be doing something?\n\nI’ve never been one to sit still for long, but I can’t bring myself to leave my companions... not after what happened to Edmund. I don’t think I’m strong enough to face the Syndicate alone, yet the thought of staying here, doing nothing, gnaws at me.\n\nYou look capable. If you’re heading that way, take down as many of those scoundrels as you can.\n\nJust… don’t get yourself killed. Please.",o="在敦霍尔德城堡附近杀死8名辛迪加流氓、5名辛迪加暗影法师和5名辛迪加卫兵",oEN="Kill 8 Syndicate Rogues, 5 Syndicate Shadow Mages, and 5 Syndicate Watchmen, near Durnholde Keep",p="我讨厌就这么坐在这里……",pEN="I hate just sitting here...",c="那些该死的盗贼……！\n\n啊，我只是——\n\n<Marren exhala bruscamente y luego se tranquiliza>\n\n……谢谢你。谢谢你完整地回来。\n\n现在，请容我失陪……我有把锤子需要再加点分量。",cEN="Those damned thieves…!\n\nArgh, I just-\n\n<Marren exhales sharply, then steadies herself.>\n\n…Thank you. For coming back in one piece.\n\nNow, if you’ll excuse me… I have a mace that needs a bit more weight behind it."}
Q[255050]={d="艾萨拉北部的废墟一直有大量亡魂出没。我们不知道它们为何仍徘徊不去，而那里的守护者一直阻止进一步的调查。我们希望有人能在这些亡灵变得更强之前将其消灭。",dEN="The ruins on the north of Azshara have been haunted by numerous spirits. We do not know why they still linger, and the caretakers there have prevented efforts to investigate further. We would like someone to quell the undead before they can grow stronger.",o="杀死6名受折磨的上层精灵、6名哀伤的上层精灵和6名被遗忘的上层精灵",oEN="Slay 6 Tormented Highborne, 6 Grieving Highborne, and 6 Forgotten Highborne"}
Q[255051]={d="一群萨特一直在艾萨拉的一座洞穴中活动。虽然被他们绑架的当地守护者幸运地获救了，但仍有部分萨特存活了下来。我们需要有人削减他们的人数，并让被他们束缚的灵魂得以安息。",dEN="A group of satyrs have been operating out of a cave in Azshara. While the local caretaker they kidnapped has fortunately been freed, some of the satyrs have managed to survive. We need someone to quell their numbers, and lay to rest the spirits they have bound.",o="杀死7个受折磨的灵魂和5个索尔萨尔的仆从",oEN="Slay 7 Tortured Spirits and 5 Servants of Xorthal"}
Q[255052]={d="微光守护者已请求援助，以维护瑟尔德拉洛的古老废墟。",dEN="The Caretakers of the Fading Light have requested aid in maintaining the ancient ruins of Thel'dralor.",o="使用抛光布擦拭瑟尔德拉洛残迹中的各座雕像。",oEN="Use the Polishing Cloth to clean the various statues in the Remnants of Thel'dralor."}
Q[255053]={d="一群历史学家已请求有人从瑟尔德拉洛的灵魂身上收集符文印记，以协助他们研究上层精灵的历史。",dEN="A group of historians has requested someone to collect runic sigils from the spirits at Thel'dralor to aid in their studies of Highborne history.",o="在瑟尔德拉洛从上层精灵灵魂身上收集瑟尔德拉洛印记",oEN="Gather Thel'dralor Sigils from Highborne spirits in Thel'dralor"}
Q[255054]={d="历史记载表明，一位强大的上层精灵法师的灵魂仍徘徊在瑟尔德拉洛的废墟中。关于塞瑟莉娅·星歌我们所知甚少，因此得出结论，了解她最好的办法是让一队冒险者亲自与她的灵魂交战，收集更多信息。",dEN="Historical records have suggested that the spirit of a powerful Highborne mage still lingers within the ruins of Thel'dralor. Little is known about Setheria Starsong, and it has been concluded that the best way to learn more about her would be for a group of adventurers to battle her spirit themselves and gather more information.",o="击败塞瑟莉娅·星歌",oEN="Defeat Setheria Starsong"}
Q[255055]={d="我们需要更好的电池才能造出像样的火箭，可在这儿我弄不到什么像样的东西\n\n一个冒险者，太好了，你大概能解决这事。几周前有一艘飞艇在西南方坠毁了。那玩意儿上总是有好电池……倒不是说这救了这一艘，但那不是重点。\n\n我有足够的金币付给你，只需要有人跑一趟，从残骸里把电池取回来。",dEN="We need a better battery to make a proper rocket, but I can't get a hold of anything decent here\n\nAn adventurer, perfect, you could probably solve this. There was a zeppelin that went down a few weeks ago to the south-west. Those things always have good batteries...not that it saved this one, but that's beside the point.\n\nI've got plenty of gold to pay you with, just need someone to trek over there and grab that battery from the wreck.",o="击败风暴之生的云端翔龙并收集飞艇的电池。",oEN="Defeat the Stormborn Cloud Serpent and collect the zeppelin's battery.",p="<你得先干掉那条云端翔龙，才能好好看看这块电池。>",pEN="<You'll need to destroy that cloud serpent before you can get a good luck at this battery.>",c="<仔细检查后，电池周围噼啪作响的能量似乎快要耗尽了。它的电量多半已被你刚刚交战的那只生物吸走。以现在这个状态，伦萨尔从它身上得不到多大用处。>",cEN="<On closer inspection, the energy crackling around the battery seems to be close to fizzling out. Most likely its charge was absorbed by the creature you just fought. Renthar isn't going to find much use in this in its current state.>"}
Q[255056]={d="<你能听见附近空气元素特有的旋鸣声。也许它们是被一股强大的能量源吸引而来，那东西或许能用来恢复失去的电量。至少，在把这块垂死的电池带回给伦萨尔之前，值得去查一查。>",dEN="<You can hear the telltale whirling of air elementals nearby. Perhaps they are drawn here by a powerful energy source, something that might be used to restore the lost charge. It's likely worth investigating before bringing the dying battery back to Renthar, at least.>",o="找到一处能量源并恢复电池",oEN="Find a source of energy and restore the battery",p="找到什么了吗？",pEN="Found anything yet?",c="这是飞艇上的东西？！\n\n我不知道这东西靠什么充能，但我从没见过这样的电池。它非常强劲，其实还有点不稳定，但我能控制住它。\n\n这是你的报酬，我得把它交给我的工程师。",cEN="This was in the Zeppelin?!\n\nI don't know what this thing was charged with, but I've never seen a battery like this before. It's plenty powerful, a bit unstable actually, but I can keep it in check.\n\nHere's your pay, I need to get this to my engineers."}
Q[255057]={d="你看起来能应付一两个亡命之徒。\n\n既然你来了，何不拿我们的新兵试试身手？哨兵岭外面不安全，去迪菲亚的地盘之前，你该确保自己的本事够利索……更别说这批人正需要练练。\n\n我不喜欢把更多傻瓜送去送死，让我看看你能做什么。",dEN="You look like you can hold your own, against a cutthroat or two.\n\nSince you're here, why don't you test your skills against our recruits? It isn't safe outside of Sentinel Hill and you should make sure your skills are sharp before heading off into Defias territory... not to mention this batch can certainly use the practice.\n\nI don't like the thought of sending more fools out to their deaths, show me what you can do.",o="与民兵新兵切磋技艺。",oEN="Practice your skills against the Militia Recruits.",p="怎么样？",pEN="Well?",c="干得好。\n\n他们显然还需要多练。我希望他们能尽早、而不是拖到最后才能跟你过上几招，我们需要一切能用的人手。",cEN="Nice work.\n\nThey obviously need more practice. I hope they can hold their own against you sooner rather than later, we need all the manpower we can get."}
Q[255058]={d="腐蚀已经蔓延到了部族之外，我最亲爱的朋友米修不是熊怪，可他现在睡在山丘顶上。如今唤醒他只会让他发狂，我相信这是他对我的最后一次报恩之举。\n\n但我还是不能抛弃他，还不能。尽管他并不希望如此，我至少要再试一件事。我从附近的废墟采到了一种草药，可没有肉他就不肯吃，而我不是猎人。\n\n他最爱吃影角雄鹿的肉，把那个带给我，也许还有一线希望。",dEN="Corruption has spread beyond just the tribe, my dearest friend Mishu is not Furbolg, but he now sleeps atop the hill. Wakening brings him only madness now, this was, I believe, his last act of gratitude to me.\n\nBut I cannot abandon him still, not yet. Though he does not wish it, I must try at least one more thing. I have gathered an herb from the nearby ruins, but he will not eat without meat, and I am no hunter.\n\nHis favorite meat came from the Shadowhorn Stags, bring me that, and there may yet be a chance.",o="为艾克塔收集影角雄鹿肉。",oEN="Collect Shadowhorn Stag Meat for Eikta.",p="我不知道米修为什么偏爱影角雄鹿的肉胜过其他任何肉。我从来尝不出有什么区别。",pEN="I do not know why Mishu preferred the meat of the Shadowhorn Stags over any others. I was never able to taste any difference.",c="这么多肉，米修一定会喜欢的……",cEN="So much meat, Mishu would have loved this..."}
Q[255059]={d="我还是不愿违背他的意愿。\n\n求你，把这个带去献给他，必要的话你亲自喂他。只是小心别把他从沉睡中弄醒。\n\n如果他真的醒了，快跑，我相信他不会追你太远。他至少还保留着这点控制力。",dEN="I still do not wish to betray his wish.\n\nPlease, bring this and offer it to him, feed him yourself if you must. Just be careful not to awaken him from slumber.\n\nIf he does awake, run, I do not believe he will chase you far. He retains that much control at least.",o="喂食沉睡的熊米修。",oEN="Feed the slumbering bear, Mishu.",p="你已经喂过它了吗？虽然也许仍是我奢求太多，但我希望这能有些效果。",pEN="Have you fed him yet? Though it might still be too much to wish, I hope it will have some effect.",c="没有效果？\n\n我早就料到了，但我不先试上一试，实在没法就这么离开。\n\n我会……遵从米舒的意愿，尽管这让我痛苦，我会在他再也无法维持沉睡之前离开。但在此之前，我要把这个留给你：尽管我原以为它能帮到他，它也不过是我族一件古老遗物的一块碎片。它已经破损，对米舒或任何人都再无用处，但也许你还能为它找到用途。",cEN="No effect?\n\nI expected as much, but I could not leave without trying something first.\n\nI will...follow Mishu's wishes, as much as it pains me, and leave before he can no longer retain his slumber. But first, I shall leave you with this, though I thought it may aid him, it is but a piece of an ancient relic of my people. Broken as it is, it will be of no use to Mishu or anyone else, but perhaps you might still find a use for it."}
Q[255060]={d="避难所的一些居民在沼泽东端发现了些东西，我相信那是加纳格——效力于燃烧军团的小型技师。\n\n我们绝不能让军团在附近取得立足点。继续下去，失落者必定会遭受更深的腐化，就连避难所也将不再安全。\n\n找到他们的营地，摧毁一切。不要让任何一个恶魔或他们那些可悲的机器留下。",dEN="Some citizens of the Harborage have spotted what I believe to be Gan'arg, small technicians that serve the Burning Legion, on the eastern end of the swamp.\n\nWe cannot allow the Legion to have a foothold near here. The Lost Ones will surely face more corruption if they continue, and even the Harborage will not be safe.\n\nFind their camp, and destroy everything. Do not allow a single demon or their wretched machines to remain.",o="在悲伤沼泽杀死加纳格工人并摧毁邪能火炮原型机。",oEN="Slay Gan'arg Workers and destroy Fel Cannon Prototypes in the Swamp of Sorrows.",p="这些报告离黑暗之门太近，让人无法安心。",pEN="The reports are a bit far from the Dark Portal for comfort.",c="谢谢你，没有那些加纳格在附近活动，我们都会安全得多。\n\n不过，我从未听说过加纳格会独自行动。一定是别人把他们带到这里来的……",cEN="Thank you, we'll all be a lot safer without those Gan'args operating nearby.\n\nI've never heard of Gan'args working on their own before though. Someone else must have brought them here..."}
Q[255061]={d="既然你是那些恶魔的敌人，你大概想知道我听到了什么，对吧？\n\n抓我的那个不是恶魔，不，是别的东西。它身上有死亡和黑暗魔法的气味。\n\n他们叫他维尔伊沙尔。他挥动双手，施展黑暗魔法，那些小恶魔就出现并开始干活。\n\n他逼我给他找了那个地方，远离其他一切。你杀了维尔伊沙尔，整件事就会土崩瓦解，兄弟，那些小家伙除了金属和火什么都不懂，比一堆烂泥还蠢。",dEN="Since ya be an enemy of those demons, you probably be wantin' to learn what I heard, no?\n\nThe one that took me wasn't a demon, no, somethin' else. Smelled of death and dark magics.\n\nThey called him Vir'Ishar. He waved his hands, cast dark magics, and those little demons appear and start workin'.\n\nMade me find him that place, away from everythin' else. Ya kill Vir'Ishar, whole thing falls apart mon, those little guys be dumber than a pile o' mud with anythin' that's not metal or fire.",o="在悲伤沼泽击败维尔伊沙尔。",oEN="Defeat Vir'Ishar in the Swamp of Sorrows.",p="我怀疑他不会轻易倒下。也许你该找几个朋友替你挡挡他的法术，兄弟。",pEN="Doubt he'll go down easy. Maybe find some friends to jump in front of his spells for ya, mon.",c="你已经把他干掉了吗，兄弟？\n\n不……我觉得那里根本就没有活着的躯体，对吧？\n\n不过没关系，就算是一具腐烂的尸体，它一样危险。\n\n那些小家伙大概还会占着那个地方一阵子，但我怀疑他们自己闹不出什么乱子。",cEN="Ya got him dead, mon?\n\nNo...I don't think there was a living body in there at all, was there?\n\nStill, it don't matter if it be a rotting corpse, it was dangerous either way.\n\nThose little guys will probably hold onto that place for a while longer, but I doubt they'll be causin' any problems on their own."}
Q[255062]={d="等等！放下你的刀，兄弟。我不想伤害你。我是个囚犯，明白吗？\n\n他们抓我来当向导。我对这片沼泽一无所知，可他们连贾卡尼说的一个字都不听。\n\n灵魂在生他们的气，也许这就是灵魂派你来的原因。灵魂行事有时就是如此古怪。\n\n我认得这片沼泽的路，可这附近的恶魔和他们的机器太多了。他们不会让我就这么走出去。我能请你陪我一起走，直到我们离开他们的营地吗，兄弟？",dEN="Wait! Stay ya blade, mon. I mean ya no harm. I be a prisoner, see?\n\nDey took me to be their guide. Know nothin' about the swamp, but still not listen to a word Ja'kani says.\n\nSpirits be angry with them, maybe that why spirits send you? Spirits work in strange ways sometimes.\n\nI know my way around the swamp, but there be too many of those demons and their machines around here. Dey not let me just walk out. Could I ask ya to come with me til we get out of their camp, mon?",o="护送贾卡尼离开恶魔营地。",oEN="Escort Ja'kani out of the demon encampment.",c="这地方看起来够安全了。看得出他们不太信任我，但至少没拿炮口指着我。\n\n去告诉他们我没有恶意，好吗？阿塔莱留着我，只是因为他们成天缩在神殿里，找不到绕开店面的路。\n\n我想我暂时还是离他们远点，他们最近变得更疯了。我可不想被诅咒。",cEN="This place seems safe enough. Can tell they don't trust me much, but they ain't pointin' cannons at me.\n\nTell 'em I mean no harm, will ya? The Atal'ai just kept me around because they be too shut in their temple to find ways around the shop.\n\nThink I'll stay away from 'em for now, they be gettin' even crazier recently. Don't feel much like gettin' cursed."}
Q[255063]={p="我的确很欣赏加纳格的巧思，但这并不意味着我希望它被用来对付我们。",pEN="I do admire the Gan'args' ingenuity, but that doesn't mean I want it used against us."}
Q[255064]={d="我们的斥候中有居民在沼泽东端发现了些东西，我相信那是加纳格——小型恶魔技师。\n\n倒不是说我对恶魔有什么成见，这很明显，但野生的恶魔可不是我们想在这里看到的东西，而一支听命于错误主人的技师大军，嗯，那听起来更糟。\n\n没错，加纳格并非常见的召唤物，但我听说过有几个术士学会了如何束缚它们，那种人通常宁愿坐着造东西，也不愿外出冒险。\n\n你为什么不去找到他们的营地，把它搅个底朝天，顺便看看能不能弄清那里到底发生了什么？",dEN="Some citizens of our scouts herespotted what I believe to be Gan'arg, little demon technicians, on the eastern end of the swamp.\n\nNot that I have anything against demons obviously, but wild ones aren't something we want here, and an army of technicians under the wrong master, well, that sounds even worse.\n\nYes, Gan'arg aren't common summons, but I've heard of a few warlocks who learned how to bind them, usually the types to sit around building things rather than go out adventuring.\n\nWhy don't you go find their camp and break it up a bit, maybe see if you can figure out what's going on while you're there?",o="在悲伤沼泽杀死加纳格工人并摧毁邪能火炮原型机。",oEN="Slay Gan'arg Workers and destroy Fel Cannon Prototypes in the Swamp of Sorrows.",c="嗯，有那么多？\n\n好吧，那听起来他们肯定不是自己跑到这儿来的。不管怎样，死掉的加纳格就不算问题了。\n\n干得确实漂亮。",cEN="Hmm, that many?\n\nWell, that certainly doesn't sound like they're here on their own. Well, either way, dead Gan'args shouldn't be an issue.\n\nQuite well done indeed."}
Q[255065]={d="等等！放下你的刀，兄弟。我不想伤害你。我是个囚犯，明白吗？\n\n他们抓我来当向导。我对这片沼泽一无所知，可他们连贾卡尼说的一个字都不听。\n\n灵魂在生他们的气，也许这就是灵魂派你来的原因。灵魂行事有时就是如此古怪。\n\n我认得这片沼泽的路，可这附近的恶魔和他们的机器太多了。他们不会让我就这么走出去。我能请你陪我一起走，直到我们离开他们的营地吗，兄弟？",dEN="Wait! Stay ya blade, mon. I mean ya no harm. I be a prisoner, see?\n\nDey took me to be their guide. Know nothin' about the swamp, but still not listen to a word Ja'kani says.\n\nSpirits be angry with them, maybe that why spirits send you? Spirits work in strange ways sometimes.\n\nI know my way around the swamp, but there be too many of those demons and their machines around here. Dey not let me just walk out. Could I ask ya to come with me til we get out of their camp, mon?",o="护送贾卡尼离开恶魔营地。",oEN="Escort Ja'kani out of the demon encampment.",c="这地方看起来够安全了。看得出他们不太信任我，但至少没拿炮口指着我。\n\n去告诉他们我没有恶意，好吗？阿塔莱留着我，只是因为他们成天缩在神殿里，找不到绕开店面的路。\n\n我想我暂时还是离他们远点，他们最近变得更疯了。我可不想被诅咒。",cEN="This place seems safe enough. Can tell they don't trust me much, but they ain't pointin' cannons at me.\n\nTell 'em I mean no harm, will ya? The Atal'ai just kept me around because they be too shut in their temple to find ways around the shop.\n\nThink I'll stay away from 'em for now, they be gettin' even crazier recently. Don't feel much like gettin' cursed."}
Q[255066]={d="既然你是那些恶魔的敌人，你大概想知道我听到了什么，对吧？\n\n抓我的那个不是恶魔，不，是别的东西。它身上有死亡和黑暗魔法的气味。\n\n他们叫他维尔伊沙尔。他挥动双手，施展黑暗魔法，那些小恶魔就出现并开始干活。\n\n他逼我给他找了那个地方，远离其他一切。你杀了维尔伊沙尔，整件事就会土崩瓦解，兄弟，那些小家伙除了金属和火什么都不懂，比一堆烂泥还蠢。",dEN="Since ya be an enemy of those demons, you probably be wantin' to learn what I heard, no?\n\nThe one that took me wasn't a demon, no, somethin' else. Smelled of death and dark magics.\n\nThey called him Vir'Ishar. He waved his hands, cast dark magics, and those little demons appear and start workin'.\n\nMade me find him that place, away from everythin' else. Ya kill Vir'Ishar, whole thing falls apart mon, those little guys be dumber than a pile o' mud with anythin' that's not metal or fire.",o="在悲伤沼泽击败维尔伊沙尔。",oEN="Defeat Vir'Ishar in the Swamp of Sorrows.",p="我怀疑他不会轻易倒下。也许你该找几个朋友替你挡挡他的法术，兄弟。",pEN="Doubt he'll go down easy. Maybe find some friends to jump in front of his spells for ya, mon.",c="你已经把他干掉了吗，兄弟？\n\n不……我觉得那里根本就没有活着的躯体，对吧？\n\n不过没关系，就算是一具腐烂的尸体，它一样危险。\n\n那些小家伙大概还会占着那个地方一阵子，但我怀疑他们自己闹不出什么乱子。",cEN="Ya got him dead, mon?\n\nNo...I don't think there was a living body in there at all, was there?\n\nStill, it don't matter if it be a rotting corpse, it was dangerous either way.\n\nThose little guys will probably hold onto that place for a while longer, but I doubt they'll be causin' any problems on their own."}
Q[255067]={d="如今的结婚戒指都毫无新意，你不觉得吗？\n\n我当然会按自己的喜好订制一枚——优雅，却又气派……可我没时间，除非……\n\n也许你可以代我向克拉丽丝下订单？我信得过你的眼光……还算信得过。眼下我正忙着打点我的\"潜在对象\"。\n\n金属你可以从我的一些……旧追求者那里弄到……他们不会再需要了。",dEN="Wedding bands nowadays are so terribly uninspired wouldn't you agree?\n\nI'd have one forged to my liking of course-elegant, yet grand...but I haven't the time, unless...\n\nPerhaps you could place the order with Clarise on my behalf? I trust your judgment…well enough. I'm much too busy tending to my \"prospects\" at present.\n\nYou can acquire the metal from some...old suitors of mine...they won't be needing it.",o="从乌鸦岭墓园的地下收集结婚戒指。",oEN="Collect wedding rings from under at Raven Hill Cemetary.",p="这些戒指，我……以前见过……",pEN="These rings, I've...seen them before...",c="这些全都是埃莉诺过去的丈夫们的，是我亲手打造的……\n\n她想让我把这些熔掉，重新打一枚结婚戒指，对吧？",cEN="These all belong to Eleanor's past husbands, I forged them myself...\n\nShe wants me to melt these down for a new wedding ring doesn't she?"}
Q[255068]={d="如果我了解埃莉诺——不幸的是我确实了解——她非要我能弄到的最大的钻石不可。\n\n平时我会从暴风城订购一批，但如果你见过埃莉诺，你就知道她可没多少耐心等。\n\n整个暮色森林里值得切割的宝石，都埋在食人魔居住的洞穴中。\n\n如果你真打算为那个该死的女人冒生命危险，就从那些洞穴里给我带些钻石来。我会把它妥当地镶嵌好。",dEN="If I know Eleanor, and unfortunately I do, she won’t settle for anything less than the largest diamond I can get my hands on.\n\nOrdinarily I’d order a shipment from Stormwind, but if you’ve met Eleanor, you’ll know she doesn’t care much for waiting.\n\nThe only stones worth cutting in all of Duskwood are buried in the caves the ogres dwell in.\n\nIf you’re truly set on risking your life for that blasted woman, bring me some diamonds from those caves. I’ll see it set properly.",o="在沃古尔食人魔山丘收集宝石。",oEN="Collect gemstones at the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound.",p="你找到宝石了吗？没找到我也不会怪你，那些食人魔相当吓人。",pEN="Did you find the gems? I won't blame you if you didn't, those ogres are quite frightening.",c="这些完全合用！我很高兴这对你来说不算太麻烦。\n\n嗯……\n\n<她仔细端详着这些宝石。>\n\n是的，我相信这些足以达到——哪怕是埃莉诺的——标准！",cEN="Those will work perfectly! I'm glad it wasn't too much trouble for you.\n\nHmm...\n\n<She analyzes the jewels closely.>\n\nYes, I believe these shall suffice in measuring up to even Eleanor's standards!"}
Q[255069]={d="我已经把戒指镶嵌完成了，多么精美的一件作品！我从未打造过如此无瑕的珠宝。\n\n金属光洁无痕，宝石闪闪发光，正配得上一位贵族！\n\n可惜它迟早会被埋进乌鸦岭……",dEN="I've finished setting the ring, and what a beauty it is! I've never forged a more pristine piece of jewelry.\n\nThe seamless sheen of the metal, and a glistening jewel befitting that of a noble!\n\nIt's a shame it'll end up buried at Raven Hill sooner or later...",o="把货送到埃莉诺·泽米尔那里。",oEN="Bring the delivery to Eleanor Zemille.",p="你带着我心爱的戒指回来了吗？我几乎按捺不住期待！",pEN="Have you returned with my beloved ring? I can hardly contain my anticipation!",c="哦，这枚戒指配我这样的身份再合适不过！看来我信任你的能力是对的。\n\n我期待有朝一日能把它戴在手指上，它无疑是我目前收藏中最喜欢的一件。\n\n等我需要下一枚时，我会派人找你。现在请恕我失陪，我还有几位潜在对象要打点……",cEN="Oh this ring is perfect for a woman of my stature! Seems I was right to trust in your capabilities.\n\nI look forward to the day I can wear this on my finger, it's certainly my favorite of my collection so far.\n\nI'll send for you when I need my next one. Now if you'll excuse me, I have some prospects to tend to..."}
Q[255070]={d="在这片被诅咒的田野里，还勉强活着的只有我那可怜的南瓜……而它们也在我眼前枯萎……要是我能用魔法解决所有问题就好了……\n\n魔法……对！喂，别那样看着我，我知道这话听起来多荒唐。但我说的可不是那些黑暗的玩意儿。这片林子里我唯一知道的其他魔法，是阿德尔农庄那些偷东西的附魔师用的。\n\n不如我们让它们派上更好的用场，你说呢？",dEN="The only things still clingin’ to life in these cursed fields are my poor pumpkins… and even they’re witherin’ before my eyes...If only I could magically solve all my problems...\n\nMagic..yes! Hey now- don’t look at me like that, I know how it sounds. But I'm not talkin' about none of that dark stuff. The only other magic I know of though in these woods are used by those thievin' enchanters down at Addles' Stead.\n\nWhat do you say we put them to better use?",o="为莱顿·阿尔瑟姆收集附魔之尘。",oEN="Collect Enchanted Dust for Ryton Altham.",p="怎么样，你从那些迪菲亚暴徒身上找到什么了吗？",pEN="Well, did you find anything off of those Defias thugs?",c="你真是救星！\n\n我的南瓜也许还能挺过这场枯萎病……\n\n等等……这、这是怎么回事？！救命！",cEN="You're a lifesaver!\n\nMy pumpkins may yet endure this blight...\n\nWait...wh-what's happening?! Help!"}
Q[255071]={d="我一直收到报告，说有个长相古怪的家伙在镇子边缘探头探脑……\n\n我这儿脱不开身……能替我过去看看吗？",dEN="Been hearing reports of a rather odd looking fellow snooping around the edge of town...\n\nI've got my hands tied up here...mind taking a look for me?",o="找到在镇子边缘徘徊的陌生人。",oEN="Find the stranger lingering at the edge of town.",p="你去看过那个陌生人了吗？",pEN="Have you checked up on that stranger yet?",c="我是谁？哎呀……人们都叫我奎尔！\n\n一切沐浴在黑暗与阴影之中的事物的头号刺激追寻者！",cEN="Who am I? Why...I'm known as Quill!\n\nMaster thrill seeker of all things bathed in darkness and shadow!"}
Q[255072]={d="面对那些普通人不敢面对的，是我立下的誓言。哎呀，就在不久前，我还闯进了逆风小径！一个阴森的地方……非常阴森，在几次……战略性撤退之后——\n\n于是我来到了暮色森林！\n\n然而，我并不知道该去哪里寻找刺激！……你能帮我找到新的冒险吗？",dEN="It is my sworn duty to brave that which lesser folk dare not face. Why, only recently I ventured into Deadwind Pass itself! A grim place…very grim, after several...strategic withdrawals-\n\nI ventured here to Duskwood!\n\nHowever, I know not where there is thrill to be sought!...Would you be able to aid in me in finding new adventure?",o="为愚蠢的奎尔勘察暮色森林各处的冒险地点。",oEN="Scout locations around Duskwood for Quill the Foolish.",p="你找到什么了吗？我希望那不会太吓人……",pEN="Have you found anything yet? It's not too scary I hope...",c="你找到了一些可供我探索的地点？太好了！我这就动身！\n\n不过，呃……那些地方不会太吓人吧？",cEN="You found some locations for me to explore? Excellent! I shall make haste!\n\nBut, erm...they're not TOO scary right?"}
Q[255073]={d="你给我的印象是那种懂得如何对付……麻烦生物的人。真幸运。看来我们或许有共同的才能。\n\n唉，我正好需要一点小小的帮助。我本想亲自处理，可我……另有要事在身。\n\n我屋后的蜘蛛吵得让人无法忍受。真是绝佳的标本——那样强壮的腿……那样的毒液。白白浪费就太可惜了。\n\n可它们扰乱了我的清净。替我让它们安静下来，好吗，亲爱的？",dEN="You strike me as someone who knows how to handle… troublesome creatures. How fortunate. It seems we may share a talent.\n\nAlas, I find myself in need of a small favor. I would tend to it personally, but I am… otherwise occupied.\n\nThe spiders behind my house have become unbearably loud. Magnificent specimens, truly-such strong legs…such venom. It would be a shame for it go to waste.\n\nAnd yet, they disturb my peace. Silence them for me, won’t you dear?",o="在暮色森林杀死黑寡妇幼蛛。",oEN="Slay Black Widow Hatchlings in Duskwood.",p="怎么样，那些可怕的蜘蛛你处理掉了吗？",pEN="Well, have you taken care of those dreaded spiders yet?",c="谢谢你了，我们今晚能睡个好觉了！\n\n<她的目光又飘向布鲁图斯，暗自轻笑起来。\n>\n\n……有些人会比别人睡得更安稳。",cEN="You have my thanks, we will sleep well tonight!\n\n<Her gaze drifts back to Brutus, quietly chucking to herself.>\n\n...Some more than others."}
Q[255074]={d="我们四周全是狼。它们不像亡灵或狼人那么危险，但足以把可怜的旅人撕成碎片。\n\n接着还有食物短缺，没有阳光就长不出多少东西，而西部荒野近来因为迪菲亚的问题也拿不出余粮。狼肉当然不是最好的解决办法，但总比挨饿强，还能让你一次解决两个问题。\n\n把你收集到的交给看守者多兹，他会负责送到守夜人其他成员手里。",dEN="We've got wolves on all sides of us. Not quite as dangerous as the undead or the worgen, but plenty enough to rip some poor travelers to shreds.\n\nThen there's the food shortage, not much grows without sunlight, and Westfall hasn't had anything to spare recently with the Defias problem. Wolf meat's certainly not the best solution, but it's a better one than starving, and it'd let you solve two problems at once.\n\nBring what you gather to Watcher Dodds, he'll make sure it gets to the rest of the Night Watch.",o="从年幼的黑色破坏者、黑色破坏者獒犬和黑色破坏者身上收集肉。",oEN="Collect meat from Young Black Ravagers, Black Ravager Mastiffs, and Black Ravagers",p="有东西要给我吗？",pEN="Have something for me?",c="狼肉？\n\n<看守者多兹皱起了眉。\n>\n\n行吧，他说得对，总比挨饿强。只要煮得恰到好处，还是能吃的。我会确保它派上用场。收拾那些破坏者，干得好。",cEN="Wolf meat?\n\n<Watcher Dodds grimaces.>\n\nSure, he's right, it's better than starving. As long as it's cooked right it's edible enough. I'll make sure it gets put to use. Good work taking care of those ravagers."}
Q[255075]={d="我们四人当中，我曾是最了解黑木部族的人。他们当中有许多人曾掌握风的力量，而即便他们的心智已被扭曲，许多人至今依旧如此。\n\n我没有力量拯救他们，但也许他们自己还有。尽管我不愿让人伤害他们，还是请把我曾代他们祝福过的图腾带回来给我。许多人至今仍然带着它们。\n\n也许风仍能带走他们的腐化。",dEN="Of the four of us, I once knew the Blackwood Tribe the best. Many amongst them once wielded the power of wind, and twisted as their minds have become, many still do.\n\nI do not have the strength to save them, but perhaps they themselves still do. Though I am loathe to demand their harm, bring me the totems I once blessed on their behalf. Many still carry them, even now.\n\nPerhaps the wind can still carry away their corruption.",o="为洛瑟从黑木图腾师与黑木萨满身上收集风之图腾。",oEN="Collect Totems of Wind from Blackwood Totemics and Blackwood Shamans for Losir.",p="我不希望他们受到任何伤害，但这样一来，至少有些人能活下来，他们的部族也终有一日能重新壮大。",pEN="I do not wish for any harm to come to them, but this way, at least, some may live, and their tribe may regrow in time.",c="当初我为他们祝福时，从未想过要收回这些图腾，但以他们如今的状态，已经用不了那些祝福了。\n\n也许还需要些时间，但我会尽我所能拯救他们。谢谢你。",cEN="I never meant to take these back when I blessed them, but in their state, they cannot use those blessings.\n\nIt may take some time yet, but I will do what I can to save them. Thank you."}
Q[255076]={d="黑木部族的熊怪已被腐化。这是一场巨大的悲剧，但悲剧并不能让他们少一分威胁。\n\n尽管其他人希望找到解药，却拿不出任何办法，而我们也不能仅凭怜悯就对他们放任不管。我想请你斩杀他们当中最强大的那些。这是唯一的办法。",dEN="The furbolgs of the Blackwood tribe have been corrupted. It is a great tragedy, but that tragedy does not make them any less a threat.\n\nThough the others hope to find a cure, they offer no solution, and we cannot leave them unchecked simply out of pity. I would ask you to strike down the strongest amongst them. It is the only way.",o="为瑟雷维击败黑木母熊与黑木战士。",oEN="Defeat Blackwood Ursas and Blackwood Warriors for Serevei.",p="奥术之力，实为秩序之力，我唯一的愿望就是看到这片土地的秩序得以维系。",pEN="The power of the arcane is, in truth, the power of order, and I only wish to see the order of these lands preserved.",c="我希望有朝一日，月之子民会明白，带来他们昔日悲剧的不是奥术，而是使用奥术的人。\n\n但即便他们不明白，我也很高兴这片土地如今稍微安全了一些。",cEN="In time, I hope, the children of the moon will see that it was not the arcane, but those who wielded it, which brought about the tragedy of their past.\n\nBut even if they do not, I am glad these lands are now a bit safer."}
Q[255077]={d="你不像其他人那样带着恐惧看我。那么，也许你愿意帮助我。\n\n他们真正该畏惧的那种力量，早已被埋藏在南方，但如今它有了想要将其掘出的仆从。他们同样是这片土地上的祸害。\n\n仅凭自然之力无法抵抗它，即便他们死去，它仍会继续蔓延。\n\n但我知道该如何将它撕碎。拿着这个，我力量的一块纯净碎片，把它刺进那些仆从的尸体里。它至少能稍稍遏制他们的腐化。",dEN="You do not look upon me with fear, as others do. Perhaps, then, you would be willing to aid me.\n\nThe kind of power they should truly fear has long been buried to the south, but now it has servants who seek to unearth it. They too are a blight upon the land.\n\nNature alone cannot resist it, and even if they die, it will continue to fester.\n\nBut I know how to tear it apart. Take this, a pure shard of my power, and drive it into the corpses of those servants. It will stymie their corruption, if only a little.",o="使用阿尔维科尔的纯净碎片净化被杀的暮锤教派信徒。",oEN="Purify slain Twight Hammer cultists using the Pure Shard of Arvekor.",p="我们不能因为一个敌人曾是我们的朋友就对他视而不见。即便这让我们痛苦，为了生存也必须采取行动。",pEN="We cannot ignore an enemy because it was once our friend. Even if it pains us, we must take action if we are to survive.",c="请别以为我冷酷无情。正因为我在乎这片土地，我才不能让危险肆意蔓延。\n\n他们部族余下的人还在，只是已经虚弱。我暂时先放着不管。也许其他人仍能找到他们苦苦寻找的答案。",cEN="Please, do not assume I am heartless. It is only because I care for this land that I cannot allow danger to go unchecked.\n\nThe rest of their tribe still remains, though weakened. I will leave that for now. Perhaps the others will still find their solution they search for."}
Q[255078]={d="啊，我今天浑身都有感觉，兄弟！灵魂让我的脚不停打拍子，让我的心像鼓一样跳！\n\n可我可怜的妹妹……她从日出起就一直在阴凉里闷闷不乐。不笑，不摇摆，连小调都不哼一声。这可不对劲。\n\n我们需要的是音乐！\n\n我一直在想……附近那些半人马营地？他们总有那些召唤闪电的法师，整天又唱又跺脚。他们肯定有一两件乐器随手丢着。",dEN="Ahh, I be feelin’ it in me bones today, mon! De spirits got me feet tappin’ and me heart drummin!\n\nBut me poor sister…she been broodin’ in de shade since sunrise. Won’t smile, won’t sway, won’t even hum a tune. It ain’t right.\n\nWhat we need be music!\n\nI been thinkin’…dem centaur camps nearby? Dey always got dem lightning-callin’ mages chantin’ and stompin’ through de day. Surely dey got an instrument or two lyin’ about.",o="拉吉里想和妹妹一起跳舞，可纳吉里没有心情。也许来点音乐能让她起身。从科卡尔牧民和科卡尔风暴使者身上收集一支半人马风笛。",oEN="Raj’iri wants to dance with her sister, but Naj’iri isn’t in the mood. Maybe some music will help get her off her feet. Collect a centaur windflute from Kolkar Wranglers, and Kolkar Stormers.",p="哎，兄弟！有进展了吗？",pEN="Ay, mon! Any luck yet?",c="啊，太好了，兄弟！\n\n这一定能让我妹妹振作起来！\n\n我们来试试吧，兄弟！",cEN="Ahh, yes mon!\n\nSurely dis will raise me sistah's spirits!\n\nLet's give it a go mon!"}
Q[255079]={d="啊……看来那支笛子还不足以打动她的心。真可惜，兄弟。它吹得甜美，可她的心依旧沉重。\n\n不过——我们不会放弃！不，不，我们只是需要更响亮的东西。更响……一面鼓！对，就是它！\n\n制皮匠露娜，只要材料够，就能替我们缝一面出来……你愿意为我那可怜的老妹妹跑这一趟吗？",dEN="Ahh…so de flute weren’t enough to stir her spirit. Shame, mon. It sang sweet, but her heart still be heavy.\n\nStill-we ain’t givin’ up! No, no, we just need somethin’ stronger. Somethin’ louder...a drum! Yes, dat be it!\n\nRhuna, de leatherworker, could stitch one together for us if she had de right materials...would you be willin' to do dat for me poor old sister?",o="也许笛子并不是合适的乐器。收集 5 张棘齿鬣狗皮、1 张贫瘠之地长颈鹿皮和 3 银币，然后交给乌娜制作一面鼓。",oEN="Maybe a flute was the wrong instrument. Gather 5 Hecklefang Hyena skins, 1 Barrens Giraffe Leather, and 3 silver. Then deliver it to Unah to make a drum.",p="你需要什么，朋友？",pEN="What do you need, friend?",c="你说你需要一面鼓？\n\n你来对地方了，我的制皮手艺在整个贫瘠之地都是最好的！",cEN="In need of a drum you say?\n\nYou've come to the right place, my leatherworking skills are the finest in all the barrens!"}
Q[255080]={d="这面鼓也许是全卡利姆多最好的，可没有鼓槌或木槌来敲它……\n\n在你出发前，去看看路对面的兽皮小屋，那位鼓手说不定还有一根多余的鼓槌。",dEN="This drum may be the finest in all of Kalimdor, but without a stick or mallet to strike it with...\n\nBefore you leave, check the lodge across the road, the drummer might have an extra stick lying around.",o="牛头人兽皮小屋里已经热闹地跳舞聚会好一阵了。问问鼓手布伦博夫，看他有没有多余的鼓槌。取得鼓槌后，连同鼓一起交给塔兹里。",oEN="There’s been a party in the tauren lodge for a while with lots of dancing. Ask the drummer Brumbof, if he has an extra stick he can spare. Acquire the drumstick and deliver it to Taz’iri along with the drum.",p="你回来啦！鼓拿到了吗？",pEN="Ya' back! Did ya get dat drum yet?",c="先祖在上，看看这个！\n\n一面做工精良的鼓，还有一根大大的鼓槌！\n\n这一定能让我妹妹沉重的心轻快起来！愿灵魂与你同在，兄弟！",cEN="By de loa look at dat!\n\nA well crafted drum and a big ol' drumstick!\n\nDis is surely to lift ma sister's heavy heart! Spirits be wit ya mon!"}
Q[255081]={d="啊！时机真是再好不过！\n\n我急需一位能干的助手！对，对……你正合适。\n\n火刃教徒躲进了此地北边的山中，我想解读他们的经文！\n\n我不在乎你用什么办法，把他们的文稿给我拿来，好让我——让我们能借用他们的力量！",dEN="Ah! What opportune timing!\n\nI am in dire need of a capable assistant! Yes, yes… you’ll do nicely.\n\nThe Burning Blade cultists have taken refuge upon the mountain just north of here, I wish to decode their scripture!\n\nI don't care how you get it, bring me their writings so I-we may harness their power for our own!",o="听闻火刃教派的强大后，马丁要你从火刃侍僧和火刃打手身上取回一些恶魔经文，供他研究，也许能从中窥见他们力量的秘密。",oEN="Hearing of the power of the Burning Blade cult, Martin asks you to retrieve some of their demonic scriptures from Burning Blade Acolytes, and Burning Blade Bruisers so he can study them and perhaps learn something of their power.",p="怎么样，你把他们的文稿弄到手了吗？",pEN="Well, have you acquired their writings?",c="你办到了！这些经文！\n\n快交给我，一想到要揭开它们的秘密，我的骨头都在发颤！",cEN="You've done it! The scriptures!\n\nNow hand them over, my bones are rattling at the mere thought of uncovering their secrets!"}
Q[255082]={d="你知道什么最妨碍生意吗？别的地精也在做生意！\n\n尤其是在一块我正打算好好利用的、上好的淤泥田里！\n\n风险投资公司跟部落本来就关系不好。其实跟谁都处不来。我真不知道他们这样四处树敌，是怎么赚到钱的。\n\n你何不去把他们干掉，我得到淤泥田，你们的镇子周围也少些敌对势力，大家都开心！",dEN="Ya know what ain't good for business? Other goblins also doin' business!\n\nEspecially in a perfectly good sludge field I was TRYING to use!\n\nVenture ain't on good terms with the Horde anyways. Or anyone really. Not sure how they're actually gettin' money the way they go around makin' enemies.\n\nWhy don't ya go take 'em out, I get the sludge field, you all get less hostile forces around your town, and everyone's happy!",o="沃兹克·斯普罗基特波普要你去北边的淤泥田杀死风险投资公司的部队。",oEN="Voltzix Sprocketpop wants you to kill Venture Co. forces at the sludge field to the north.",p="他们走了吗？",pEN="They gone yet?",c="他们死了？太好了！我就知道能指望你！",cEN="They're dead? Good! Knew I could count on ya!"}
Q[255083]={d="风险投资公司的问题就在于，他们无孔不入！\n\n现在他们又跑到我的矿里来了！好好的矿，满是值钱的宝石，他们竟然就自己动手挖了！\n\n你已经证明了自己很会挫挫那些窝囊废的锐气，去那座矿，照上次那样再来一遍！",dEN="Problem with Venture, they get everywhere!\n\nNow they're in my mines too! Perfectly good, mines full of very valuable gems, and they decided to help themselves!\n\nYou've proven good at takin' those loses down a peg, go over to that mine and just do what you did last time!",o="沃兹克·斯普罗基特波普要你去北边的圆石矿脉杀死风险投资公司的部队。",oEN="Voltzix Sprocketpop wants you to kill Venture Co. forces at the Boulder Lode Mine to the north.",p="他们走了吗？",pEN="They gone yet?",c="听起来那是最后一批了！其实我听说他们正在打包，准备回……某个地方去，我没太留意。\n\n要紧的是他们要走人了，好像跟危害费用有关。",cEN="Sounds like that's the last of 'em! Actually, I heard they're packin' up and heading back to...somewhere, I didn't pay much attention.\n\nWhat matters is they're leaving, something about hazard expenses."}
Q[255084]={d="守护历史文物是守护者庄严的职责。在这样的时代，我们的历史正在身边崩塌，这份职责比以往更为重要。\n\n我们最珍贵的圣物——宝剑托尔卡拉，仍安然存放在这座墓穴之中，但可惜的是，我们没能保护好要塞中的另外几件。蛋白石之声圣杯、元素防护披风，以及我们历史中更黑暗的一件——疯癫女王之戒，都已落入辛迪加之手。\n\n我不信任他们会看管好这些圣物，它们也不属于这些篡位者，因此我想请你代我们夺回它们。有人看见那件披风在靠近北fold庄园一带活动的一名狂妄的辛迪加佣兵手中，而圣杯和戒指多半仍在要塞的城墙之内。",dEN="It is the solemn duty of the Caretakers to protect the artifacts of Stromgarde's history. In times like these where our history is crumbling around us, that duty is more important than ever.\n\nOur most valued relic, the blade Trol'kalar, remains safe within this crypt, but alas, we have proven inadequate at protecting several others within the keep. The Chalice of Opal Voices, the Cloak of Elemental Protection, and a darker piece of our history, the Ring of the Mad Queen, have fallen into the Syndicate's hands.\n\nI do not trust them to care for these relics, nor do they belong to these usurpers, and so I would ask you to reclaim them in our stead. The cloak has been spotted in the hands of an arrogant Syndicate mercenary operating closer to Northfold Manor, but the Chalice and Ring are likely still within the walls of the keep.",o="为守护者取回蛋白石之声圣杯、元素防护披风和疯癫女王之戒。",oEN="Recover the Chalice of Opal Voices, the Cloak of Elemental Protection, and the Ring of the Mad Queen for the Caretakers",p="你找到那些圣物了吗？",pEN="Have you found the relics yet?",c="戒指裂了，里面的力量已经黯淡……\n\n辛迪加根本不在乎历史，我早该料到会这样。别自责，我知道这不是你干的。\n\n疯癫女王西贝尔王后，并不是我们引以为傲的一段历史。她是在阿拉索帝国开始分裂后不久即位的一位女王，为了扭转那些已迁往新土地之人的心智、让帝国重归往日荣光，她深入大地深处，钻研黑暗力量。\n\n她当然失败了。最终，她自己的儿子背叛了她，不久后便远走他乡，把激流堡留给了托尔贝恩家族。我们并不以她为荣，她的所作所为不可饶恕，但这终究是我们的历史，我不希望我们遗忘它。\n\n尽管如此，即便其中一件已受损，这些文物还是因你而失而复得。为此，守护者将永远感激你，<name>。",cEN="The ring is cracked, the power within it has dimmed...\n\nThe Syndicate cares nothing for history, I should have expected something like these. Do not fret, I know this was not your doing.\n\nQueen Sybell, the Mad Queen, is not a piece of history we pride ourselves in. A queen who reigned shortly after the Empire of Arathor had begun to break apart, she delved into dark powers from deep within the earth in a desperate attempt to twist the minds of those who had left for new lands and restore the empire to its former might.\n\nShe failed of course. Ultimately, her own son turned on her, and left not long after, leaving Stromgarde to the Trollbane family. We hold no honor for her, her actions were unforgiveable, but it is our history nonetheless, and I do not wish us to forget it.\n\nStill, damaged though one may be, the artifacts are recovered thanks to you. For that, the Caretakers will always be grateful, <name>."}
Q[255085]={d="我在奥术上摸索过一阵子。我不是什么大法师，只会些帮我干活——比如洗碗之类——的简单戏法，从没学过能用来打架的东西。\n\n不过，眼下这种局面下，还有一个法术我想学，以我对魔法技艺的理解，它应该够简单。可惜激流堡从来就没多少法师，在我们还守着的那片街区里，我怎么也找不到一本讲这个的书。\n\n可我们的士兵跟辛迪加里的不少施法者交过手。看这地方其他地方破败成那样，我猜他们把不少法术书随手丢在了能放下的地方。\n\n你下次出去时，能不能把能找到的都捡回来？筛挑选拣的活儿我自己来干。",dEN="I've dabbled in the arcane for a while now. I'm no grand mage, I only know simple cantrips that help with my work, cleaning dishes and the like. Never even anything to use in a fight.\n\nStill, with the situation as it is, there's another spell I'd like to learn, it should be simple enough even for my understanding of the magical arts. Unfortunately, Stromgarde has never had many mages, and I can't find a book on it anywhere in the remaining district we're holding onto.\n\nOur soldiers have been fighting quite a few spellcasters amongst the Syndicate, though. With how poor repair the rest of the place is in, I would guess they've left a lot of their spellbooks just lying around wherever they can set them down.\n\nWould you be able to pick up what you can find and bring them back here next time you go out? I'll do the work of sifting through them myself.",o="在激流堡要塞内收集辛迪加的法术书。",oEN="Collect Syndicate Spellbooks from within Stromgarde Keep",p="到目前为止，你在要塞里找到法术书了吗？",pEN="Found any spellbooks in the keep so far?",c="哦，你确实弄到法术书了。好，这得花点时间，让我看看……\n\n召唤元素，这个我用不着。造水术，这个我已经会了。啊哈！造食术，他们真有这一本！\n\n我们失去了所有的农场，而这里又没有多少地可以耕种。补给已经快见底了，再这样下去，我们就得开始配给了。\n\n我们可以去抢辛迪加，但多几桶也解决不了问题。可要是我学会这个法术，哪怕只是达拉然孩子学做的松饼，我也能在法力耗尽前不断变出来。艾琳不喜欢这种取巧的法子，但眼下是危急关头，我相信她会理解的。\n\n我该去研习了。谢谢你。",cEN="Oh, you certainly do have the spellbooks. Alright, this will take a bit, let me see...\n\nConjure Elemental, I don't need that. Conjure Water, I already know that one. Ahah! Conjure Food, they did have it!\n\nWe've lost every single one of our farms, and we don't exactly have land to grow much here. Our supplies are already running low, so we're going to have to start rationing if this goes on much longer.\n\nWe could rob the Syndicate, but a few more barrels won't solve anything. If I learn this spell, however, even if it's just the muffins Dalaran children learn to make, I can conjure up as many as my supply of mana lasts for. Elling isn't fond of shortcuts like that, but it's desperate times, so I'm sure she'll understand.\n\nI should get to studying. Thank you."}
Q[255086]={d="<那名卫兵正手忙脚乱地翻着一本模样古怪的日记。过了好一会儿，他才终于注意到你。>\n\n啊！你好，我想我们没见过面。我们终于找到外来的援手了吗？\n\n就你一个？嗯，多一双手总比没有强。如果你想出一份力，我正担心我的一位战友。她昨天举止反常，被撤下岗位去休息了。后来……嗯，长话短说，我一直在担心，而现在我找到了她这几天写的东西。\n\n满篇都是胡言乱语，说影子在跟她说话。我得留在这里，以防被叫去守路障，但也许你可以去她家看看她？她叫斯蒂芬娜，就住在铁匠铺旁边。",dEN="<The guard is frantically sifting through the pages of an odd-looking journal. It takes a while before he finally notices you.>\n\nAh! Hello, I do not believe we've met before. Did we finally manage to find outside assistance?\n\nJust you? Well, one extra set of hands is better than none. If you're looking to pitch in, I'm worried about a fellow soldier of mine. She was acting strange yesterday and got taken off duty to rest. Now...well, long story short, I was still worried, and now I've found the things she's been writing the past few days.\n\nIt's utter madness about shadows speaking to her. I need to remain here in case I get called to man the barricade, but maybe you could go to her home and check in on her? Her name is Stephana, she lives next to the smithy.",o="去看看举止反常的激流堡士兵斯蒂芬娜·弗莱斯。",oEN="Check on Stephana Fryth, the Stromgarde soldier who has been acting strangely.",p="早在要塞陷落之前我就认识斯蒂芬娜了。我忍不住担心，这件事总让我觉得不对劲……",pEN="I've known Stephana since before the keep fell. I can't help worrying, something about this feels off...",c="她死了？就这样？\n\n斯蒂芬娜，为什么？！就在几天前，你还说我们俩都会看到激流堡被夺回的那一天。要是我当时去了，哪怕因此成了逃兵……\n\n你就一点办法都没有吗？你难道不能把她手里的刀夺下来！她显然不该拿着那东西！\n\n对不起……我想一个人待一会儿。",cEN="She's dead? Just like that?\n\nStephana, why?! Just a few days ago, you said we'd both see the day Strom was reclaimed. Maybe if I'd gone, even if it made me a deserter...\n\nWas there nothing you could have done? Couldn't you grab the knife out of her hand! Clearly she shouldn't have had it!\n\nI'm sorry...I'd like to be alone for a bit."}
Q[255087]={d="你是来援助斯托姆王国的？\n\n作为王子，向外人求助令我自尊受挫，但我知道此刻不能拒绝盟友，因此，我，加林·托尔贝恩王子，感谢你的援助。辛迪加是我们在这里最大的敌人。他们占据着要塞的大部分，还在不断争夺我们仅存的最后一片街区。\n\n然而，这场战斗中还有第三股势力。石拳食人魔满足于控制旧阿拉索区，但别搞错了，食人魔是野蛮的家伙，不会安分太久。\n\n我的人都在焦虑地等待食人魔决定进攻的那一刻。尽管我不愿承认，我们根本没有两线作战的实力，但既然有你在此，也许你能逼他们舔舐伤口，暂时退出这场争斗。",dEN="You are here to aid the kingdom of Strom?\n\nIt pains my pride as prince to ask for outside aid, but I know we cannot turn down allies right now, and so I, Prince Galen Trollbane, am grateful for your aid. The Syndicate is our greatest enemy here. They hold most of the Keep and continue to vie for the last district we still hold claim to.\n\nHowever, there remains a third faction in this battle. The Boulderfist Ogres remain content to keep their grasp on the old Arathor District, but make no mistake, ogres are brutes that will not settle for long.\n\nMy men all wait anxiously for when the ogres decide to attack. Though I am loathe to admit it, we are in no state to fight a war on two fronts, but since we have you, perhaps you might force them to lick their wounds and stay out of this fight a while longer.",o="杀死石拳巨槌食人魔和石拳萨满。",oEN="Slay Boulderfist Maulers and Boulderfist Shamans.",p="斯托姆的每一个敌人都将倒下！",pEN="Every enemy of Strom shall fall!",c="那些食人魔真的是你一个人打败的？\n\n哈！我还以为多一个人也起不了多大作用。\n\n也许你终究能扭转局面。干得好，士兵。你先解散吧，让你去守路障太浪费了。何不去看看还有谁需要帮忙？",cEN="You actually defeated all those ogres yourself?\n\nHah! And here I didn't think one more person would make much difference.\n\nYou might be able to turn this around afterall. Good work, soldier. You're dismissed for now, it'd be a waste to put you on barricade duty. Why don't you see if anyone else needs help with anything."}
Q[255088]={d="我听说了那位可怜的士兵斯蒂芬娜的事。\n\n这里大多数人认为，她只是日复一日守着日渐缩小的领土，压力太大，精神崩溃了。历史上精神崩溃的士兵，她不会是第一个……\n\n不过，这件事总让我觉得不太对劲。据她的朋友埃斯德拉斯说，她忠诚而坚定。这并不代表她不可能强撑出一副坚强的样子，但那些关于影子的说法让我想起了西贝尔王后的故事。\n\n我认为我们至少该为她查一查是否有外力导致了这一切。我把我们这里的一件圣物借给你——真视之镜。如果有什么东西藏在影子里，或者出现了没有源头的影子，它应该能让你看见。\n\n我的职责是守护我们的历史，所以我除了给你建议什么也做不了。如果出现任何真正危险的迹象，请你直接告知加林王子。",dEN="I heard about what happened to that poor soldier, Stephana.\n\nMost around here believe her mind just snapped from the stress of holding down our dwindling territory day in and day out. I wouldn't be the first in history that a soldier has broken down under stress...\n\nStill, something about this does not feel quite right. According to her friend, Esdras, she was loyal and resolute. That doesn't mean she couldn't have been putting on a strong front, but that talk of shadows makes me think of Queen Sybell's story.\n\nI believe we owe it to her to at least investigate for any external factors that may have caused this. I will let you borrow one of our relics here, the Lenses of True Sight. If anything is hiding in the shadows, or there are shadows with no clear source, these should allow you to see them.\n\nMy duty is to our history, so I can do nothing besides advise you. If there is any sign of actual danger, I would ask that you make it known to Prince Galen directly.",o="使用真视之镜在激流堡要塞中搜寻位置异常的影子。",oEN="Use the Lenses of True Sight to search for out of place shadows in Stromgarde Keep.",p="我听说阿拉里克让你去调查弗莱斯那件事。我宁愿你专心对付更明显的威胁，但她是个好士兵，而阿拉里克一向忠于职守，所以如果你愿意，就继续查下去吧。",pEN="I hear Alaric has you investigating that incident with Fryth. I'd rather you focus on the more obvious threats, but she was a good soldier, and Alaric has always been faithful in his duties, so proceed in this if you wish.",c="影子里的低语？！难道整个艾泽拉斯都在密谋对付斯托姆，辛迪加和石拳还不够吗？\n\n不过，自你到来之后，我听到的全是对你的赞誉，而阿拉里克从我小时候起就忠心耿耿。如果你们二人都说这是真实的威胁，那作为王子，对此视而不见就是我的愚蠢。",cEN="Whispers in the shadows?! Must all of Azeroth scheme against Strom, that the Syndicate and the Boulderfist are not enough?\n\nStill, I've heard nothing but praise for you since you arrived, and Alaric has served faithfully since I was a boy. If both of you claim this is a legitimate threat, then as prince, it would be folly of me to turn a blind eye."}
Q[255089]={d="看了你目前了解到的情况，我认为这可能只是我们早已熟知的某个危险的一部分。\n\n我手下有几个人报告说，辛迪加里有个女人，穿着古怪，独自用一种他们听不懂的语言喃喃自语。她从不亲自参战，但所有人都觉得她令人不安。\n\n因为她从未出现在我们面对过的任何一次进攻中，我至今没把她放在心上，但现在，我开始觉得她也许在以自己的方式对付我们。\n\n无论如何，她显然站在辛迪加一边。除掉她，也许这一切就会结束。",dEN="Seeing what you have learned thus far, I believe this may simply be a part of a danger we are already well aware of.\n\nSeveral amongst my men have reported a woman amongst the syndicate, dressed in strange garb and muttering to herself in a language they do not recognize. She never joins the fight herself, but they all find her unsettling.\n\nBecause she has never been in any attack we've faced, I've brushed her off thus far, but now, I am beginning to think she might be working against us in her own way.\n\nShe is clearly with the Syndicate anyways. Take her down, and perhaps this will all be put to an end.",o="在激流堡要塞杀死辛迪加幽影织者。",oEN="Slay the Syndicate Wraithweaver in Stromgarde Keep.",p="即便现在，你也能感知到我？真有意思……",pEN="You can perceive me, even now? How intriguing...",c="这么说她也死了，只剩你站在她之上。\n\n确实非常有意思。\n\n你希望斯托姆王国重归它应有的荣光，对吧？我是斯托姆的盟友，也许我甚至可以说，我是它唯一真正的盟友。还有谁真正在乎它的复兴？还是说他们只是一群可悲的野狗，为残羹冷炙争斗不休？",cEN="So she, too, has died, leaving only you to stand above her.\n\nVery intriguing indeed.\n\nYou wish for the Kingdom of Strom to be restored to its rightful glory, no? I am an ally of Strom, perhaps I might even say I am the only ally it truly has. Does anyone else truly care for its restoration, or are they just pathetic dogs, fighting over scraps?"}
Q[255090]={d="你在杀死斯托姆的敌人，那就继续吧，我忠诚的臣民。\n\n还有一个像你刚才砍倒的那样的女人，在北边的一处农庄游荡。她毫无用处，仍在与斯托姆为敌。她的心智早已崩溃，如今轮到她的身体了。\n\n……嗯，对，这样最好。有时伤口必须先烧灼，才能愈合。事情自会照其应有的样子发生。\n\n别在意我。你总不会因为不信任我，就放过一个辛迪加成员吧。他们都是毫无价值的猪猡，这点我相信我们能达成一致。",dEN="You are killing the enemies of Strom, so let us continue with that, my loyal subject.\n\nThere is another like the one you cut down, who wanders a farmstead to the north. She is useless, she still fights against Strom. Her mind has long since broken, now it is her time her body breaks in turn.\n\n...Hmm, yes, this is best. Sometimes a wound must be cauterized before it can heal. Events shall occur as they will.\n\nPay me no mind. Surely you would not spare a member of the Syndicate because you are distrustful of myself. They are all worthless swine, on that I'm certain we can agree.",o="在通往北金庄园的路上杀死疯癫的萨拉纳斯。",oEN="Slay Thalanas the Mad on the road to Northgold Manor.",p="你听说了另一个辛迪加成员？那你顺便把那个也处理掉吧。",pEN="You heard about another Syndicate member? Then you might as well take care of that as well.",c="你回来了。看到至少你还平安，我心里多少有些安慰。\n\n要是你当时没有离开要塞那么远，我们或许还有一线机会。\n\n不是辛迪加，也不是石拳。最终冲破我们路障的是部落，他们杀死了我们的国王，以及每一个挡在他们面前的士兵。\n\n而更令我蒙羞的是，他们还砍倒了我的守护者同僚，几乎也杀了我。我本该与他们同死，但我们所剩无几，斯托姆需要我。\n\n他们还拿走了瓦尔考尔的印记，所以我想，在确定合适的继承人、或者达纳斯归来之前，我就是我们的摄政王。",cEN="You've returned. It brings me some measure of peace to see that you, at least, are safe.\n\nIf only you had not gone so far from the keep right then, we might have stood a chance.\n\nIt was not the Syndicate or the Boulderfist. In the end, it was the Horde that broke past our barricade, killed our king and every soldier that stood in their way.\n\nAnd then, to my even greater shame, they cut down my fellow Caretakers, and nearly killed me as well. I should have died with them, but with so few of us left, Strom needs me.\n\nThey had Valorcall's sigil too, so I suppose until a proper succession can be determined, or Danath returns, I am our Regent."}
Q[255091]={d="你的努力拖住了我们的敌人，这大概也是幸存者仍留在这里的唯一原因，但辛迪加趁我们虚弱来收拾我们，只是时间问题。\n\n无论如何，这场战斗如今已毫无意义。我们失去了统治者，也失去了历史。继续硬撑毫无结果，即便我们能再多撑一阵。\n\n辛迪加要的只是要塞和其中的财物。虽然还有其他文物留存……我或许是个守护者，但如今我也是我们的领袖，人民必须放在第一位，所以我已决定交出剩余的街区和我们尚存的贵重物品，换取众人的性命。\n\n我要去安置我们的死者了，请把我作为摄政王的第一道、也是最后一道命令传达给幸存者。",dEN="Your efforts set our enemies back, and that is likely the only reason the suvivors still remain here, but it is only a matter of time before the Syndicate comes to finish us off while we are weak.\n\nThis battle is meaningless now anyways. We've lost our ruler and our history. Trying to hold off further is fruitless, even if we somehow kept the fight going a while longer.\n\nThe Syndicate only wants the fortress and its valuables. Though other artifacts remain...I may be a Caretaker, but I am also our leader now, the people must come first, so I have decided to surrender the remaining district and anything of value we still possess in exchange for our lives.\n\nI need to tend to our dead, please pass my first and final command as Regent to the survivors.",o="将阿拉里克的决定告知激流堡余下的居民。",oEN="Inform the remaining people of Stromgrade of Alaric's decision.",p="这是个艰难的决定，但我不能再让更多人白白死在一场注定失败的战斗里。",pEN="It is a difficult decision to make, but I cannot sacrifice anymore lives on a doomed battle.",c="你谈过的每一个人都想继续战斗？连老怀恩也是？我本以为她一定想把孩子们送出这里，但她说得有道理。辛迪加毫无荣誉可言，他们已经证明了这一点。\n\n至于其他人，我绝不会责怪他们想保卫家园、为王子复仇。\n\n如果这就是人民的意愿，那我的第一个举动若是与他们作对，我就太不称职了。我的人民已准备好战死，那么我就与他们并肩而立，与他们一同赴死。\n\n斯托姆也许不是你的家乡，但你是一位强大的<class>，如果你如今也愿意站出来战斗，我们也许仍有希望。",cEN="Every single person you spoke to wants to keep fighting? Even old Wyne? I thought for certain she'd want to get the children out of here, but she has a point. The Syndicate has no honor, they've already proven that.\n\nAs for the others, I will never fault them for wanting to defend their home, and avenge their prince.\n\nIf that is the will of the people, I would be a poor regent if my first act were to oppose them. My people are prepared to die fighting, and so I shall stand with them, and die with them.\n\nThough Strom may not be your home, you are a strong <class>, if you too are willing to stand and fight even now, there may yet be hope for us all."}
Q[255092]={d="我们无法让死者复生，但我们也许还能夺回托尔卡拉。如果要继续战斗，这应当是我们的首要任务。\n\n我不知道部落把它带去了哪里，但也许他们知道。进攻落锤镇太冒险了，不过我们东边有一座他们占着的农场。\n\n那里的一些士兵可能知情。再带上我们的一件圣物，怜悯之锤，它能让虚弱的敌人失去行动能力。\n\n用它一直查到有人知道有用的情报为止，而且要快。我怀疑要不了多久，那把剑就会被送到我们难以触及的地方。",dEN="We cannot bring back our dead, but we may still be able to recover Trol'kalar. If we are to keep fighting, that should be our first task.\n\nI do not know where the Horde took it, but perhaps they do. An attack on Hammerfall would be too risky, but there is a farm to our east they hold claim to.\n\nSome of the soldiers there may know. Take another of our relics, the Mace of Mercy, it has the power to incapacitate a weakened foe.\n\nUse it until you find one that knows something useful, and quickly now. I doubt we have much time before the blade is taken somewhere we cannot easily reach it.",o="在戈谢克农场审问落锤镇步兵，直到找出知道激流堡遇袭真相的人。",oEN="Interrogate Hammerfall Grunts at Go'shek Farm until you find one that knows the truth about the attack on Stromgarde.",p="农场离落锤镇不近，但托尔卡拉失窃的消息多半还是传过去了。",pEN="The farm is a fair distance from Hammerfall, but it is likely news about Trol'kalar's theft has traveled nonetheless.",c="下令进攻的是一个叫曾古的巨魔？那么阻止他逃脱就该是我们的首要任务。\n\n你不在的时候还有一件好消息。",cEN="A troll named Zengu ordered the attack? Then preventing his escape should be our first priority.\n\nThere is one more piece of good news from while you were away."}
Q[255093]={d="你离开后不久，瓦尔考尔中尉跌跌撞撞地穿过路障回来了，他被部落打得半死，只为夺取他的印记。\n\n但他还活着，这对我们所有人来说都是天大的好消息。他一直是我们最出色的人之一，所以才会被托付那枚印记。\n\n你该去见见他。他在谋略上一向远胜于我，也许他能帮忙找到曾古。",dEN="Lieutenant Valorcall strumbled through the barricade not long after you left, beaten and left for dead by the Horde to claim his sigil.\n\nBut the fact that he still lives is wonderfull news for us all. He has always been one of our best, that is why he was entrusted with the sigil.\n\nYou should meet him. He has always been far better at strategy, perhaps he will be able to help find Zengu.",o="与瓦尔考尔中尉交谈。",oEN="Speak with Lieutenant Valorcall.",c="<瓦尔考尔痛得直咧嘴。他最重的伤似乎刚愈合不久，但显然仍在受着伤痛的折磨。即便如此，看到你走近，他还是露出灿烂的笑容。>\n\n哎呀，这不是<name>吗？我回来之后听到的全是对你的赞誉。\n\n……还有那些惨剧，不过我想今天已经说得够多了。听起来，要塞至今还能屹立，都得感谢你？\n\n等我们不用再为性命拼杀的时候，我们该坐下来喝一杯。",cEN="<Valorcall winces in pain. The worst of his wounds seem freshly healed, but he is clearly still suffering from his injuries. Even so, he puts on a wide smile as you approach.>\n\nWell, if it isn't <name>? All I've heard since I returned is your praises.\n\n...That, and all the tragedy, but I think there's already been enough talk of that this day. It sounds like we have you to thank for the fact that the Keep still stands at all?\n\nWe should sit down and have a drink sometime, once we're done fighting for our lives."}
Q[255094]={d="没想到他们这么轻易就偷袭得手，但事已至此。\n\n这一切背后的主使是一个独行的巨魔？我怀疑他会雇那些同样的冒险者护送自己，我们见过他们，那太引人注目了。\n\n也就是说，他多半是一个人在偷偷溜走。离开阿拉希有两条路，西边的索拉丁之墙，或者南边的萨多尔大桥。\n\n西边是显而易见的选择，走得够远他就能到幽暗城。而他也一定料定我们会这么想。所以我相信他会走萨多尔大桥。我们会把所有人力都派去墙边截他，而他则偷偷穿过去到湿地，那是我们绝不会想到去搜查的地方，多半还会再雇些人从那里护送他回到部落领地。",dEN="Never thought they'd get the jump on me so easily, but what's done is done.\n\nThe one behind this all was a lone troll? Doubt he'd hire those same adventurers to escort him, we've seen them, so they'd draw attention.\n\nThat means he's probably sneaking out all on his own. There's two ways out of Arathi, Thoradin's Wall to the west, or Thandol Span to the south.\n\nWest is the obvious choice, make it far enough and he'll get to the Undercity. And he'd be counting on us to know that too. That's why I'm sure he's crossing Thandol Span. We'll send all our people to catch him at the wall, while he sneaks across to Wetlands where we'd never think to look, and probably hire someone else to help get him back to Horde territory from there.",o="在萨多尔大桥拦截曾古并夺回托尔卡拉。",oEN="Intercept Zengu at Thandol Span and recover Trol'kalar.",p="阴影深眠于这片土地之下。你听不见它们吗？\n\n终有一日，你会听见，而当你听见时，你就会明白，它们从不沉默。",pEN="Shadows rest deep beneath this land. Can you not hear them?\n\nIn time, you will hear, and when you do, you shall realize that they are never silent.",c="我们又见面了，我的臣民。\n\n而且你手里拿着伊格纳乌斯遗志之剑。他的子孙如今受人敬奉，正如当年的索拉丁一族。正如当年的我。\n\n他们只是白白糟蹋了一个曾经伟大的王国，但这无可挽回。其他人相信他们可以分裂出去，寻找更肥沃的土地，构筑自己的权力幻梦，哪怕这么做让古老的帝国分崩离析。\n\n但尽管过去了那么多年，我终于还是苏醒了过来，而在我触及的所有人当中，只有你没有崩溃。",cEN="We meet again, my subject.\n\nAnd you have the blade of Ignaeus's legacy. His children are now revered as Thoradin's once were. As I once was.\n\nThey have only squandered a once great kingdom, but it cannot be helped. Others believed they could break apart, find greener lands and form their own illusions of power, even if doing so allowed the empire of old to crumble.\n\nBut though many years passed, I have finally awakened, and of all those I reached, only you did not break."}
Q[255095]={d="我王国之内的一切，按权属都归我所有。你是唯一配得上的容器，而你也属于我。\n\n投降吧，作为感谢，我会允许你继续作为我的顾问存在。\n\n但我必须回去。叛徒们会屈膝臣服。阿拉索将被重建。我所需要的，只是一具能再次行走于艾泽拉斯的躯体。\n\n它是我的。把它交给我。",dEN="All within my kingdom is mine by right. You are the one worthy vessel, and you too are mine.\n\nSurrender, and as gratitude, I shall allow you to persist as my advisor.\n\nBut I must return. The traitors will bend, and serve. Arathor will be reformed. All I need is a body with which to walk Azeroth once more.\n\nIt is mine. Give it to me.",o="抵抗西贝尔王后。",oEN="Resist Queen Sybell.",p="你夺回托尔卡拉了吗？",pEN="Were you able to recover Trol'kalar?",c="托尔卡拉！它真的被夺回来了！\n\n西贝尔王后还活着？\n\n<守护者沉默了许久。>\n\n她是索拉丁血统的最后一位女王。她的儿子法尔迪尔将她击倒后，扬帆南下建立了暴风城王国，而托尔贝恩家族则在激流堡登上了王位。\n\n我一直以为西贝尔只是远古历史中的一段往事。尽管我们与其他王国或许有分歧，但以武力奴役他们的心智，绝不是我希望看到的斯托姆复兴方式。\n\n不过，疯癫女王的事暂且放下吧，你击败了她，我们只能希望她这次是真正死去了。夺回托尔卡拉可是值得庆祝的大事！",cEN="Trol'kalar! It has truly been reclaimed!\n\nQueen Sybell still persisted?\n\n<The caretaker is silent for a while.>\n\nShe was the last queen of Thoradin's bloodline. After her son, Faldir, struck her down, he sailed to the south and founded the nation of Stormwind, and the Trollbane family took the throne here at Strom.\n\nI had always assumed that Sybell was just a piece of ancient history. Though we may have our differences with the other kingdoms, enslaving their minds by force is not how I wish to see Strom restored.\n\nBut let us leave the matter of the mad queen aside for now, you defeated her, and we can only hope she has found true death this time. The recovery of Trol'kalar is a matter that calls for celebration!"}
Q[255096]={d="哎呀，这不是那位夺回托尔卡拉的英雄吗？！干得漂亮！\n\n阿拉里克把摄政之位交给了我。看来他宁愿回他的墓穴去。\n\n……我们两个本来都不该被考虑担任这个位子，但如今是危急时刻。托拉斯的侄子达纳斯才是加林不在后的合法王位继承人，可他已在黑暗之门彼端失踪多年。\n\n除了战场，我从来不太在行，但如果人民要我领导他们，我不打算让他们失望。看来那杯酒还得再等一阵子了。\n\n我们走走吧，对我的伤有好处，而且有件事我得跟你谈谈。",dEN="Why if it isn't the hero who recovered Trol'kalar?! Fine work out there!\n\nAlaric has passed the regency onto me. Seems like he'd rather go back to his crypt.\n\n...Neither of us should have even been considered for this, but these are desperate times. Thoras's nephew, Danath, is the rightful heir to the throne with Galen gone, but he's been lost behind the dark portal for many years now.\n\nI've never been much good outside a battlefield, but if the people want me to lead them, I don't plan on letting them down. Guess that drink will have to wait a bit longer.\n\nLet's walk a bit, it'll do good for my wounds, and there's something I need to talk to you about.",o="与瓦尔考尔中尉同行。",oEN="Walk with Lieutenant Valorcall.",p="你有封信要给我？",pEN="You have a letter for me?",c="激流堡王国想重新加入联盟？\n\n我相信你知道这不是我一个人能决定的事，联盟的其他领袖也需要批准。\n\n话虽如此，激流堡在阿拉希战线上已经帮了我们大忙，所以我确信不会有人反对。尽管他们已被削弱，但我们的行列中多一个王国，对我们来说是大有益处的。\n\n至于他们请求的士兵，我们本已捉襟见肘，但我会尽量召集人手加入对抗辛迪加的战斗。他们需要的可不只是士兵，还有各种资源。如果你有什么富余的，不如回去一趟，看看他们缺什么。\n\n为了联盟！",cEN="The Kingdom of Stromgarde wishes to rejoin the Alliance?\n\nI'm sure you know this is not my decision alone to make, the other leaders of the Alliance will need to approve as well.\n\nThat said, Stromgarde has already been of great aid to us on the Arathi front, so I am sure there will be no objections. Weakened though they are, counting another kingdom amongst our ranks would be a great boon to us.\n\nAs for the soldiers they requested, we are already stretched thin, but I will rally who I can to join the fight against the Syndicate. They'll need resources beyond just soldiers. If you have anything to spare, you should go back there and find out what they're short on.\n\nFor the Alliance!"}
Q[255097]={d="似乎出了点小差错。我从达纳苏斯进口的这批新书里，有一本是我早就有的。\n\n平时我会亲自送回去，但近来哨兵来得太频繁，我觉得现在没法把法尔奈一个人留下。\n\n你能替我把书送回去吗？我是从金蕾拉那里拿到的，她一般在工匠区的图书馆里。",dEN="There seems to have been a bit of a mistake. One of these new books I imported from Darnassus is a copy of a text I already had.\n\nNormally I'd take it back myself, but with the Sentinels coming by so much recently, I don't feel I can leave Farnae on her own right now.\n\nWould you be able to take the book back for me? I got it from Kynrela, she's usually at her library in the Craftsmen Terrace.",o="把瑟莱莎的书交给角鹰兽管理员凯拉伊斯·月羽。",oEN="Bring Thelaesa's Book to Caylais Moonfeather the hippogryph master.",p="你看起来像是有急事。那你可来对地方了！",pEN="You look like you're in a hurry. Well, then you came to the right place!",c="你要把这本书送到达纳苏斯？没问题，你可以骑我的一只角鹰兽去！",cEN="You have to get this book to Darnassus? That's not a problem, you can take one of my hippogryphs!"}
Q[255098]={d="付一点小钱，你就可以骑角鹰兽飞往达纳苏斯，把瑟莱莎的书交给金蕾拉。没有比这更快的办法了。\n\n如果觉得可以，等你准备好出发时再和我说一声。我会收一点费用，但相信我，这绝对值得！",dEN="For a small fee, you can take a hippogryph to Darnassus, so you can deliver Thelaesa's book to Kynrela. You won't get there faster any other way.\n\nIf that sounds acceptable, then just speak to me again when you're ready for the ride. I'll charge you a little, but trust me; it'll be worth it!",o="向角鹰兽管理员凯拉伊斯·月羽购买一次角鹰兽飞行，然后把瑟莱莎的书交给达纳苏斯工匠区的博学者金蕾拉。",oEN="Buy a hippogryph ride from the hippogryph master Caylais Moonfeather, then bring Thelaesa's Book to Lorekeeper Kynrela, in the Craftsmen Terrace of Darnassus.",p="你好。你是在找我吗？",pEN="Hello. Are you looking for me?",c="你有一本瑟莱莎那里的重复的书？好，让我看看。\n\n她的藏书近来相当齐全，所以我并不意外，不过这本本来就是误装进这批货里的，那正好。",cEN="You have a duplicate book from Thelaesa? Alright, let me see.\n\nHer library is quite well stocked these days, so I can't say I'm surprised, but this one actually made it into the shipment by mistake anyways, so it's just as well."}
Q[255099]={d="我可不想让你空手回去。\n\n我最近多收到了一本《第二次大战的余波》。因为大家通常就在图书馆里读它，它一直只是在积灰。\n\n你何不把它带回去给瑟莱莎？就当是谢你把另一本书送回来。\n\n你该去找鲁瑟兰村的维斯普里斯图斯。既然你已经见过凯拉伊斯，他会让你骑角鹰兽飞回她在奥伯丁的站点。",dEN="I'd hate to send you back empty handed.\n\nI got an extra copy of Aftermath of the Second War in recently. Since people usually end up just reading it here in the library, it's just been collecting dust.\n\nWhy don't you bring it back to Thelaesa? Consider it a favor for sending the other book back to me.\n\nYou should go talk to Vesprystus, in Rut'theran Village. Since you've already met Caylais, he'll let you take a hippogryph back to her stop in Auberdine.",o="把金蕾拉的书交给角鹰兽管理员维斯普里斯图斯。",oEN="Bring Kynrela's Book to Vesprystus the hippogryph master.",p="要出门？你该考虑骑一只我的角鹰兽。",pEN="Going somewhere? You should think about taking one of my hippogrpyhs.",c="你要把书送到奥伯丁？你以前去过奥伯丁吗？去过的话就没问题，朋友。我有的是训练过这条航线的角鹰兽！",cEN="You're taking a book to Auberdine? Have you been to Auberdine before? If so, then it's no problem, my friend. I have plenty of hippogrphs trained to fly that route!"}
Q[255100]={d="奥伯丁的角鹰兽管理员是凯拉伊斯·月羽。如果你以前和她说过话，就可以骑我的一只角鹰兽去她那里。\n\n有个常识值得记住：角鹰兽总是被训练飞往各自的首都城市，但只有在你去过某个偏远管理员那里之后，它们才会载你飞过去。\n\n你已经去过凯拉伊斯那里了，所以等你准备骑角鹰兽去奥伯丁时，再和我说一声就行。到了那里，你就可以把金蕾拉的书交给瑟莱莎。",dEN="The hippogrpyh master in Auberdine is Caylais Moonfeather. If you've spoken to her before, then you can take one of my hippogrphs to her.\n\nThat's a good lesson to know: hippogrpyhs are always trained to fly to their capital city, but they'll only take you to a remote hippogrpyh master after you've already been there.\n\nYou've already been to Caylais, so just speak with me again when you're ready to take a hippogrpyh to Auberdine. Once there, you can deliver Kynrela's book to Thelaesa.",o="向角鹰兽管理员维斯普里斯图斯购买一次飞往奥伯丁的角鹰兽飞行，然后把金蕾拉的书交给奥伯丁的博学者瑟莱莎。",oEN="Buy a hippogryph ride to Auberdine from the hippogryph master Vesprystus, then take Kynrela's Book to Lorekeeper Thelaesa at Auberdine.",p="你已经回来了？金蕾拉收下书了吗？",pEN="You're back already? Did Kynrela take the book?",c="她让你带回来另一本书作为回礼？\n\n她一向体贴周到。我现在已经收藏了相当一批关于我们历史的典籍，但涉及其他种族的部分还比较有限，既然我们已经加入联盟，多了解我们的新盟友对我们大家都有好处。我很乐意把这本书放上书架。",cEN="She sent another book with you in return?\n\nShe's always been very thoughtful. I have a good collection of tomes relating to our history now, but anything beyond our own people is a bit limited, and now that we've joined the Alliance, it would do us all well to learn more about our new allies. I'd be happy to add this to the shelves."}
Q[255101]={d="<这封信以繁复的龙语文字写成。除了最下方的一行，你一个字也看不懂。>\n\n<name>，如果你读到这封信，那么我的进攻多半已经失败。若真如此，你至少已经走到了我走到的地方，这意味着希望尚未完全破灭。\n\n在尖塔入口附近找到诡计宝珠，用它去见我妹妹。她会知道该怎么做。\n\n瓦拉斯塔兹",dEN="<The letter is written in intricate Draconic script. You cannot make sense of a single word written on it, except for the very bottom.>\n\n<name>, if you are reading this, then my attack has likely failed. If so, you have at least made it as far as I did, meaning all hope is not yet lost.\n\nSeek out the Orb of Subterfuge near the entrance of the spire, and use it to reach my sister. She will know what to do.\n\nVaelastrasz",o="在黑石山使用诡计宝珠，然后把瓦拉斯塔兹的密信交给湿地格瑞姆巴托附近红玉磨砺会的拉莱斯塔萨。",oEN="Use the Orb of Subterfuge in Blackrock Mountain, then bring Vaelastrasz's Missive to Ralestrasza at the Ruby Attrition near Grim Batol in Wetlands.",p="怎么了，<race>？你带来了什么消息？",pEN="Yes, <race>? What news do you bring?",c="<拉莱斯塔萨一言不发地读完密信。直到读完之后，她才终于开口。>\n\n瓦拉斯塔兹被奈法利安腐化了，你完全是出于仁慈才不得不杀了他。你知道这故事听起来有多荒谬吗？\n\n你真该庆幸我哥哥特意写明，如果他失败了我该信任你，否则我现在就把你交给奥米克萨。倒不是说我信得过一个无视我的忠告、一头冲进黑石心脏的蠢货的判断。鲁莽的白痴……\n\n你对抗奈法利安的努力有目共睹，尽管我为我哥哥的死而痛苦，但忽视你的潜力会让更多人丧命。所以我愿意正式欢迎你加入红玉磨砺会。不，这远远不够，但我们只能将就了。我哥哥或许已经不在了，但奈法利安要付出十倍的代价。",cEN="<Ralestrasza reads the missive without giving you so much as a word. Only when she has finished does she finally speak.>\n\nVaelastrasz was corrupted by Nefarian, and you had absolutely no choice but to kill him out of mercy. Do you have any idea how utterly ridiculous that story sounds?\n\nYou are very, very lucky my brother thought to specify that I should trust you if he were to fail, or I would be handing you over to Aumixsar right now. Not that I trust the judgment of a fool who went rushing into the heart of Blackrock, heedless of my advice. Reckless idiot...\n\nYour efforts against Nefarion are clear, and though I am bitter over my brother's passing, ignoring your potential would risk many more lives. So I would like to officially welcome you to the Ruby Attrition. And no, it is not nearly enough, but we will simply have to make do. My brother may be gone, but Nefarion will suffer tenfold."}
Q[255102]={d="……还没到？\n\n哦，嘿，就是你！也许你能弄清楚这件事。\n\n有人要来卖给我们一批新零件。而且不是普通零件，不，他是个德莱尼。听说过他们吗？蓝皮肤、长角、来自完全另一个星球？对，你当然听说过……\n\n他们的技术跟我们的简直是天壤之别，字面意义上的，但这正是深挖它的理由！德莱尼的技术有太多新东西值得我们学习。\n\n所以他才迟迟不到，让我有点恼火！真希望他没有遇到海难之类的，那些可怜的零件，沉进海里……当然还有巴拉尔！总之，你能去米奈希尔港一趟，确认他的船平安到了吗？顺便催他快点过来？",dEN="...Still not here?\n\nOh, hey, you! Maybe you could figure this out.\n\nWe've got someone coming to sell us some new components. And not just any components, no, he's a Draenei. Ever heard of them? Blue, horns, came from another planet entirely? Right, of course you have...\n\nThey're tech must be worlds apart from ours, literally, but that's all the more reason to dig into it! We've got so many new things to learn from Draenei tech.\n\nThat's why I'm just a bit annoyed he's still not here yet! Really hope he didn't get shipwrecked or something, all those poor parts, lost at sea...and Baraal, of course! Anyways, could you head over to Menethil Harbor, make sure his ship got here safely? Maybe tell him to hurry it up getting over here?",o="在米奈希尔港找到工匠巴拉尔，弄清他为何还没抵达丹奥加兹。",oEN="Find Artificer Baraal in Menethil Harbor and learn why he hasn't reached Dun Algaz yet.",c="给丹奥加兹的侏儒送零件？不，我完全不记得有这回事。\n\n我只是来这里……\n\n<那个德莱尼揉了揉头。>\n\n你确定那些侏儒提到了我？还提了我的名字？而且我带着给他们的货在这里？\n\n……我信你。其他种族分享我们的知识，是我来到这里之后一直想做的事。其实更早以前就想，只是兽人不太愿意接受……\n\n还有，我忘了自己究竟是为什么来这里的。花好几天跨海到另一块大陆？如果只是观光，我会去更大的城市。所以我很确定，我的记忆被人动过手脚。",cEN="Components for the gnomes at Dun Algaz? No, I don't remember anything about that.\n\nI was just here to...\n\n<The draenei rubs his head.>\n\nYou're sure those gnomes mentioned me? By name? And I was here with a delivery for them?\n\n...I believe you. Sharing our knowledge with other races is something I've wanted to do since arriving here. Before, really, but the orcs weren't as receptive...\n\nAlso, I forgot why I actually went here. On a several day journey to another continent? If it was just sight seeing I'd have gone to one of the bigger cities. So I'm fairly sure my memories were altered."}
Q[255103]={d="军团以前就试过这种手段，纳斯雷兹姆相当擅长这类把戏，不过我看不出军团为什么要插手去偷几个零件……\n\n不管怎样，拿着这枚戒指，这是我一直在做的、用来抵御军团心灵诡计的东西，对付别的东西大概也管用。如果我真带着几箱零件，我想我会把它们留在码头，直到安排好马车。\n\n你要是赶紧过去，也许还能找到。我本想一起去，但不管那是什么，它已经得手过一次，我去恐怕帮不上什么忙。",dEN="The Legion has tried things like this before, Nathrezim are quite proficient in this sort of trick, though I don't see why the Legion would intervene to steal a few parts...\n\nStill, take this ring, it's something I'd been working on to protect against the Legion's mind tricks, it'd probably still work on something else. If I did have boxes of parts with me, I assume I would have left them at the dock until I arranged a wagon.\n\nIf you hurry over there, you might still find them. I'd go with, but whatever it was already got me once, so I doubt I'd be much help.",o="找到工匠巴拉尔丢失的零件。",oEN="Locate Artificer Baraal's missing parts.",p="你怎么又回来了？快到码头去！",pEN="What are you doing back here? Get down to the docks!",c="一个血精灵法师？我为什么不意外呢？\n\n早在我们来到这里之前，他们对我族来说就只是一根刺。没想到会有一个跟着我到这里来，但这就是我不常戴这枚戒指的下场。\n\n别操心把箱子搬回来了，那肯定不是一个人能搬动的。我自己来处理。",cEN="A blood elf mage? Why am I not surprised?\n\nThey've been nothing but a thorn to my people since before we got here. Didn't think one would follow me out here, but that's what I get for not wearing this ring more often.\n\nDon't worry about bringing the boxes back, I'm sure it's too much for one person to carry. I'll get it sorted out."}
Q[255104]={d="大概还得再过几天。我的脑子还是一团乱，而且我得安排好交通工具。另外我忘了我们之前约定的具体内容，所以还得再谈一次。\n\n比起金币，我更感兴趣的是知识交流，因为我对这个世界的种种发明还知之甚少。我猜我们之前约定的也是类似的东西。\n\n既然你和那些侏儒有联系，能不能先去一趟，把情况告诉他们？",dEN="It'll probably be a couple more days. My head's still a mess, and I need to get transportation arranged. And I forgot the specifics of the deal we'd arranged, so that will have to be discussed again.\n\nI'd be more interested in an exchange of knowledge than gold, as I still know little about this world's innovations. I assume we arranged something like that before as well.\n\nSince you're in contact with the gnomes, could you go on ahead and let them know the situation?",o="告知丹奥加兹的侏儒，巴拉尔很快就会与他们见面。",oEN="Inform the gnomes at Dun Algaz that Baaral will be meeting with them soon.",c="一个能改写记忆的法师，这答案我可没料到！光是想想就够吓人的了！\n\n<El gnomo tiembla>\n\n不过我想，结局好就一切都好。除了那两天的等待有点难熬，但迟来总比不来强。很高兴我派你去了那儿！",cEN="A memory altering mage, now there's an answer I didn't expect! Just the thought alone is horrifying enough!\n\n<The gnome shivers>\n\nBut all's well that ends well I guess. Aside from that couple day wait, but better late than never. Glad I sent you over there!"}
Q[255105]={d="<你走近时，机器人疯狂地闪烁着，像是在拼命引起你的注意。>\n\n<它指了指自己，然后又指向远处，发出一阵烦人的哔哔声。这很难听懂，但在你反复确认之后，你大致明白了它的意思。还有另一个机器人不见了，就在西北方；你向它复述这一点时，它用那颗过大的脑袋做了个点头的动作，看来你理解得没错。至少四处查看一下应该没坏处。>",dEN="<The bot flashes wildly as you approach, as if trying to get your attention.>\n\n<It points at itself, then off in the distance, playing an annoying beeping noise. It's difficult to understand, but after a few more clarifications, you think you get what it's trying to tell you. Other robot missing, to the north-west; repeating that back to it causes it to make a nodding motion with its oversized head, so that seems to be correct. It probably wouldn't hurt to at least take a look around.>",o="在塞尔根石找到失踪的机器人。",oEN="Locate the missing bot at Thelgen Rock.",p="警报！为了您自—自身的安全，请立即撤离该区域。当前区—区域已遭蜘—蜘蛛类生物入侵。",pEN="Alert! For your own s-safety, please evacuate the area immediately. Current area h-has been infested with a-a-arachnids.",c="警报！为了您自身的安全，请立即撤离该区域。\n\n当前区—区域已遭蜘—蜘蛛—蛛—类生物入侵。\n\n请—请—请立—立—立—立—立—立—立—立\n\n<也许从机器人的电路上清掉一些蛛网，就能解决这些故障。>",cEN="Alert! For your own s-safety, please evacuate the area immediately.\n\nCurrent a-area has been i-infested with a-a-archni-i-ids.\n\nP-p-please e-e-e-e-e-e-e-e\n\n<Maybe removing some of the webbing from the bot's circuits would solve the malfunctions.>"}
Q[255106]={d="系统运行效率已恢复至：百分之九十三。\n\n正在处理积压指令：扯断蛛网。\n\n<机器人在自己面前疯狂地挥动。幸好你及时向后退了一步。>\n\n正在处理积压指令：警示倒霉的平民——为了您自身的安全，请立即撤离该区域。当前区域已遭蜘蛛类生物入侵。\n\n正在处理积压指令：致命捕获响应——启动自毁程序。距自毁还有十分钟。\n\n积压指令处理完毕。感谢您的协助，倒霉的平民。请尽快将我送回我的制造者处进行进一步维护。由于我的腿部已严重受损，若您的条件允许，最优方案是由您将我搬运至该处。",dEN="System operational efficiency restored to: Ninety three percent.\n\nProcessing backlogged commands: Tear webbing.\n\n<The bot swings wildly in front of itself. Fortunately, you're able to step back in time.>\n\nProcessing backlogged commands: Warn hapless civillian - For your own safety please evacuate the area immediately. Current area has been infested with arachnids.\n\nProcessing backlogged commands: Fatal capture response - Initiating self-destruct sequence. Ten minutes until self-destruct.\n\nBacklog processing complete. Thank you for your assistance, hapless civillian. Please return me to my creators for further maintenance at your earliest convenience. As my legs have sustained substantial damage, it would be optimal for you to carry me there if this course of action is within your means.",o="在机器人自毁之前，把它送到丹奥加兹的工程师那里。",oEN="Bring the bot to the Dun Algaz Engineer before it self-destructs.",p="哦？你有什么要给我的吗？",pEN="Oh? Do you have something for me?",c="RH-7，你上哪儿去了？！我不是说过你必须在维护时间之前回来吗？！\n\n他又自己跑出去惹麻烦了？唉，真不愧是他。行了，今晚没你的油喝了……算了，反正我得把这些蛛网全都清掉。不过这一整周你都归到齿轮维护岗去，听见没有？\n\n……哦，对了，自毁程序。你干嘛不直接关掉它？那又不难，你只要按三下蓝色按钮，再按一下紫色按钮，接着按两下绿色按钮，而且无论如何都千万别按红色按钮。这就是标准流程，真的。\n\n<她迅速照着自己说的步骤操作起来。>\n\n不过，至少你在它炸掉之前把他带回来了，谢了。",cEN="RH-7, where have you been?! Haven't I told you you're supposed to be back by maintenance time?!\n\nHe wandered off and got himself in trouble again? Well isn't that just like him. That's it, no oil for you tonight...actually nevermind, I need to get all this webbing out anyways. But you'll be on cog maintenance duty for the whole week, you hear?\n\n...Oh, right, the self-destruct. Why didn't you just turn it off? It's not that hard, you just press the blue button three times, then the purple button once, followed by pressing the green button twice, and never under any circumstances press the red button. Standard procedure, really.\n\n<She quickly followers her own instructions.>\n\nStill, I guess you did bring him back here before it went off at least, so thanks for that."}
Q[255107]={d="还没到南海镇，我们就在路上遭到了强盗的伏击。承蒙圣光眷顾，我们大多数人保住了性命，但这只是因为埃德蒙——愿圣光保佑他——留下来为我们断后。\n\n我的同伴们还在养伤，以我们现在的状况，我不敢再拿他们的性命去冒险。如果他还活着，他现在需要的不是复仇，而是一只有力的手，把他平安带回家。\n\n去敦霍尔德城堡找到埃德蒙·克雷斯特法尔，把他从那个鬼地方救出来，等他安全之后再回来见我。",dEN="Bandits fell upon us on the road before we reached Southshore. By the grace of the Light, most of us escaped with our lives, but only because Edmund, light bless him, stayed behind to cover our retreat.\n\nMy fellows are still recovering from their own wounds and I dare not risk their lives in our current state. If he still lives, then what he needs now is not vengeance, but a steady hand to bring him safely home.\n\nFind Edmund Crestfall in Durnholde Keep, free him from that wretched place, and return to me once he is safe.",o="在敦霍尔德城堡找到埃德蒙·克雷斯特法尔。",oEN="Locate Edmund Crestfall within Durnholde Keep.",p="拜托，别在这里闲晃。我们需要你的帮助。",pEN="Please, don't loiter. We need your help.",c="是希斯派你来的？圣光在上，我就知道我的朋友们不会抛下我！\n\n我还没被打垮，<name>，尽管这帮狗东西想方设法要让我崩溃。\n\n我还能打，但我需要你的力量，帮我们杀出一条路离开这里。",cEN="Heath sent you? By the light, I knew my friends would not abandon me!\n\nI am not beaten yet, <name>, though these dogs have done their best to see me broken.\n\nI can still fight, but I will need your strength to cut our way out of this place."}
Q[255108]={d="眼下避难谷地更安全，但我们的大部分兵力还留在城堡里，努力守住我们对家园的所有权。\n\n从我收到的报告来看，情况不太妙，但他们仍坚守着手中最后一个城区。如果你想帮我们，就该去那儿找加林王子，他比我更清楚该怎么做才能夺回激流堡。",dEN="Refuge Pointe is safer for the moment, but most of our forces are still in the Keep, trying to hold claim on our home.\n\nFrom the reports I've gotten, it isn't going very well, but they're holding their ground in the last district they still have. If you want to help us, you should go there and find Prince Galen, he'll know better than I what needs to be done to take back Stromgarde.",o="在激流堡与加林·托尔贝恩王子会面。",oEN="Meet with Prince Galen Trollbane in Stromgarde Keep.",c="尼尔阿斯是个好士兵，她派你来是对的。\n\n眼下我们能得到任何援助都用得上。\n相关",cEN="Nials is a good soldier, and she was right to send you.\n\nWe can use any aid we can get right now.\nRelated"}
Q[255109]={d="就算我们能打通前往南海镇的路，要是能多一条补给线，我们的处境也会安全得多。\n\n东边住着一家蛮锤矮人。我们过去常从他们那儿运些粮食。他们一向置身战事之外，所以也从不在意我们脱离联盟，但我们已经很久没有他们的消息了。\n\n这虽然远比不上一条像样的补给线，但只要能让他们供应些粮食，辛迪加想饿死我们就没那么容易了。你看能不能去问问他们？",dEN="Even if we're able to get through to Southshore, we'd be a lot less vulnerable if we had a second supply route.\n\nThere's a family of Wildhammers to the east. We used to bring in some food from them. They always stayed out of the war, so they never minded us leaving the Alliance, but it's been a while since we've heard from them.\n\nIt'd hardly make up for a proper supply route, but if we could get some food coming from them, it'd make it harder for the Syndicate to starve us. Think you could go check with them?",o="在阿勒斯通庄园与农夫萨尔交谈。",oEN="Speak with Farmer Sal at Alestone Estate",c="恐怕我们现在实在没条件谈什么补给交易。\n\n不过你看起来挺结实，也许你能帮上我们。等我们不用再为性命担惊受怕的时候，再来谈这笔生意吧。",cEN="Afraid we ain't in any shape for a supply deal right now.\n\nYe look tough though, maybe ye can help us out. When we ain't fearin' for our lives, we can talk out a deal."}
Q[255110]={d="在联盟腹地这么深的地方，我们得不到多少补给。猎物倒是不少，可自己打猎充饥会耽误正事。\n\n听说东边不远有几个蛮锤矮人经营着一座农场。他们不掺和这场战争——倒不是我信得过矮人——但在这地界我们也没别的更好选择。也许你能跟他们谈成点什么。",dEN="We aren't getting many supplies this deep in Alliance territory. Plenty of wildlife to hunt, but hunting our own food is a distraction from the fight.\n\nTurns out there's some Wildhammer dwarves running a farm a bit to the east. They're staying out of the war, not that I'd trust dwarves anyways, but we don't have better options out here. Maybe you can work something out with them.",o="在阿勒斯通庄园与农夫萨尔交谈。",oEN="Speak with Farmer Sal at Alestone Estate",c="恐怕我们现在实在没条件谈什么补给交易。\n\n不过你看起来挺结实，也许你能帮上我们。等我们不用再为性命担惊受怕的时候，再来谈这笔生意吧。",cEN="Afraid we ain't in any shape for a supply deal right now.\n\nYe look tough though, maybe ye can help us out. When we ain't fearin' for our lives, we can talk out a deal."}
Q[255111]={d="如果暴风城不打算再派援军，那也好，我们还有别的地方可以求助。\n\n红法师塔的法师们一直置身于这场冲突之外，但前些日子巨龙袭击时，他们中的一位大法师曾保护过湖畔镇。圣光在上，我们现在真需要米娜维亚……\n\n唉，她在那之后不久就失踪了，可要是湖畔镇陷落，下一个就轮到他们头疼了，所以也许会有别人同情我们。我想你应该愿意跑一趟，去跟他们谈谈吧？我觉得他们对我可不会太客气。",dEN="If Stormwind won't send more aid then fine, there's other places we can turn.\n\nThe mages of the Red Mage Tower have stayed out of the conflict, but one of their archmages protected Lakeshire during the dragon attack a while back. Light knows we could use Minervia right now...\n\nWell, she disappeared soon after that, but it'll be their problem next if Lakeshire falls, so maybe some others will be sympathetic to us. I don't suppose you'd be willing to travel up there and talk to them? I don't think they'd be all that welcoming to me.",o="代表伊迪莉娅·所罗门女士，在红法师塔与探灵者赫斯特洛会面。",oEN="Meet with Ley-Tracker Hestlor at the Red Mage Tower on behalf of Lady Idelia Solomon.",c="那个鲁莽的蠢货伊迪莉娅又爬回来求我们帮忙了，是吧？\n\n哦？她甚至连解释一下为什么派你来跟我们谈、而不是自己上这儿来的意思都没有？真是好大的脸。",cEN="That reckless idiot Idelia is crawling back to us for help, is she?\n\nOh? She didn't even feel the need to explain why she sent you to talk to us instead of going up here herself? Isn't that rich."}
Q[255112]={d="不过，我想这个请求是为了整个湖畔镇，而不只是为了她自己……\n\n我们大多数人都不擅长战斗。要是兽人真打上来，我们就从多里安和赛拉斯的传送门逃走，然后把门关在身后。最有可能出手相助的是阿莱克斯，可她只是个新手。\n\n<Hestlor suspira>\n\n我想是米娜维亚让镇上的人对我们产生了误解。如果士兵们把装备带上来，维里丹可以把它们全部附魔，而我的追踪术也能察觉到兽人是否在进行什么特别危险的仪式。这就是我们能拿出的全部了。",dEN="Still, I suppose the request is for all of Lakeshire, not just herself...\n\nMost of us aren't specialized in combat. If the orcs did get up here, we'd escape through Dorian and Silas's portal and close it behind us. Alex is the most likely to help, but she's only a novice.\n\n<Hestlor sighs.>\n\nI think Minervia gave the town a skewed perception of us. If the soldiers bring their equipment up here, we'll Veridan can enchant it all, and my own tracking will detect if the orcs are in the process of any particularly dangerous rituals. That's the best we can offer.",o="带着赫斯特洛的答复回去见伊迪莉娅·所罗门女士。",oEN="Return to Lady Idelia Solomon with news of Hestlor's response.",c="附魔和法术追踪，但没有直接援军？好吧，比我预想的要好。我会通知驻守在这里的卫兵，让他们尽快去一趟塔里。\n\n……我想我该给你个解释。我年轻时一心想当法师；大概是太想了吧。我急于证明自己，开始钻研那些超出我能力范围的法术。头几个还算说得过去，但最终报应还是落到了我头上，也落到了我周围整座塔的人头上。\n\n说实话，我能活下来简直是奇迹。当然，法术的反噬烧毁了我施法的能力——反正我在那儿也当不成学徒了，所以也许我根本没法另寻出路反倒是件好事。\n\n最后一切都还好。否则我就不会遇到我丈夫，也不会有我的孙辈了。",cEN="Enchanting and spell tracking, but no direct reinforcement? Very well, it's better than I would have gotten. I'll let the guards on standby here know to make a trip to the tower as soon as they can.\n\n...I suppose I do owe you an explanation. I was an aspiring mage in my youth; a bit too aspiring, I suppose. I was eager to prove myself, and started delving into spells beyond my means. The first couple were reasonable enough, but eventually it caught up to me, and the rest of the tower around me.\n\nIt was honestly a miracle I survived. Of course, the backlash burned out my ability to use magic, not that I had any future left as an apprentice there regardless, so perhaps it's just as well I couldn't turn to some other path.\n\nIt all worked out in the end. I wouldn't have met my husband otherwise, or have my grandkids."}
Q[255113]={d="这些日子打猎太危险了，而西部荒野运来的粮食也断了。湖畔镇的人一向吃很多鱼，可湖里的鱼不够我们光靠它过活。\n\n没有食材，我没法给家人做饭，不过我有个主意，也许你能帮上忙。当地的豺狼人越来越大胆了，我分不清他们是跟兽人结了盟，还是根本不在乎。不管怎样，他们猎了很多猎物。我敢打赌他们甚至还有多余的，你懂我的意思。",dEN="It's too dangerous to hunt these days, and the shipments of grain from Westfall stopped. We've always eaten a lot of fish in Lakeshire, but there aren't enough fish in the lake to live on just that.\n\nI can't cook for my family without food to cook, but I do have an idea you might be able to help with. The local gnolls have only gotten bolder, I can't tell if they're allied with the orcs or just don't care. Either way, they've been hunting plenty. I'll bet they've even got some to spare, if you know what I mean.",o="为卢卡·廷德尔在赤脊山一带的豺狼人营地收集豺狼人食物补给。",oEN="Collect Gnoll Food Supplies from gnoll camps around Redridge for Luca Tyndall.",p="豺狼人是好猎手，这是我能说他们的唯一好话。但愿他们手边有些新鲜肉。",pEN="Gnolls are good hunters, that's the only good thing I can say about them. Hopefully they have some fresh meat laying around.",c="豺狼人……就吃这个？\n\n让我看看，这是……狼蛛，我很确定。真可爱。\n\n至少我在这儿看到了些野猪。也许我能想办法把剩下的这些做得对我们人类可口一点。总比饿死强，谢了。",cEN="That's what the gnolls...eat?\n\nLet's see, this is...tarantula, I'm pretty sure. Lovely.\n\nI see some boar in here at least. Maybe I can figure out a way to make the rest of this palatable for us humans. It's better than starving, so thanks."}
Q[255114]={d="愿圣光保佑你，善良的旅人！\n\n如果你要深入荒野，也许能以圣光之名帮个小忙？\n\n湖畔镇曾有一件古老的圣物，泰伦纳尔圣杯。那是件美丽的东西，我的描述根本配不上它。前些时候它被暗影隐藏豺狼人部族抢走了，而我们没有能力把它夺回来。\n\n但如果你在旅途中碰巧遇见它，我恳求你把它带回我的礼拜堂。",dEN="May the Light bless you, good traveler!\n\nIf you're venturing into the wilds, perhaps you could do a small favor in the Light's name?\n\nWe once had an old relic here at Lakeshire, the Chalice of Tyrenel. A beautiful thing, my descriptions could hardly do it justice. It was taken by the Shadowhide gnoll clan a while back, and we have not the means of recovering it.\n\nBut if you, perhaps, stumble upon it in your journey, I implore you to bring it back to my chapel.",o="为诺里斯神父找回泰伦纳尔圣杯。",oEN="Recover the Chalice of Tyrenel for Father Norice.",p="泰伦纳尔圣杯在这座礼拜堂里供奉了好几代。我们不能容许它就此失落。",pEN="The Chalice of Tyrenel has sat in this chapel for generations. We cannot allow it to be lost.",c="它依然完好无损！你真是深受圣光庇佑！\n\n从今往后，我会确保它在这里安然无恙。它本就不该被偷走，可我……啊，那不重要。\n\n以圣光之名，我感谢你，善良的旅人。",cEN="It is still intact! You are truly blessed by the Light!\n\nI shall ensure it is safe here from now on. It should never have been stolen, but I...ah, that is not important.\n\nIn the Light's name, I thank you, good traveler."}
Q[255115]={d="-正在重新配置，暂时闲置-",dEN="-Being reconfigured, unused for now-"}
Q[255116]={d="没有多少货物运进来，我们几乎缺所有能用的补给。其中许多都没有立即可行的解决办法，但石堡陷落之前，湖畔镇一直有座不错的伐木场。它离黑石部族太近，处境危险，不过他们也并没有真正控制住那里。\n\n报告说阿勒斯磨坊里爬满了蜘蛛。你看能去把它们清理掉吗？",dEN="Without many shipments coming in, we're low on just about every form of supplies we could use. There isn't an immediate solution to many of them, but Lakeshire has always had a good lumber mill until Stonewatch fell. It's dangerously close to the Blackrocks, but they aren't actually holding it down either.\n\nReports say Alther's Mill is infested with spiders. Think you could clear them out?",o="杀死阿勒斯磨坊周围的大狼蛛，帮助湖畔镇的居民夺回这片区域。",oEN="Slay Greater Tarantulas around Alther's Mill to help the people of Lakeshire reclaim the area.",p="就算我们能抽出几个卫兵去办这事，我想他们也宁愿去打兽人，而不是去对付巨型蜘蛛。",pEN="Even if we could spare some guards for it, I think they'd rather fight the orcs than deal with giant spiders.",c="难得听到点好消息，真好。\n\n阿勒斯磨坊离石堡那么近，可不是个容易守住的地方，但我敢肯定我丈夫宁愿不要一味采取守势。",cEN="It's nice to hear some good news for once.\n\nAlther's Mill won't be an easy position to hold, being close to Stonewatch and all, but I'm sure my husband would rather not stay entirely on the defensive."}
Q[255117]={d="眼下我们还有些富余的木料，但码头和桥都要修，我看这点存货撑不了多久。\n\n我听说有人在谈论收复阿勒斯磨坊，可那对眼下的我没什么帮助。要我说，那主意本来就疯了，那儿离兽人的要塞太近了。\n\n不过，当初撤离得很匆忙。我敢打赌那边还扔着不少好木板。你要是给我弄些来，我出的金币可比你在暴风城卖掉它们赚得多。",dEN="We've got some wood to spare for now, but between the dock repairs and the bridge, I don't see our supply lasting long.\n\nI hear there's been talk about reclaiming Alther's Mill, but that doesn't help me very much right now. If you ask me, that idea's insane anyways, it's too close to the orcs' stronghold.\n\nStill, it was evacuated in a hurry. I'll bet there's plenty of good planks just lying around there. I've got good gold if you bring me some, more than you'll get selling it off in Stormwind.",o="为工头奥斯洛在阿勒斯磨坊收集木板。",oEN="Collect Wood Planks from Alther's Mill for Foreman Oslow.",p="你最好多找些来，谁知道在袭击停止之前我还需要多少。",pEN="You best find a good amount, who knows how many more I'll need before the attacks stop.",c="不错。这些是好木板，你眼力不错。\n\n也许他们真能把磨坊夺回来，不过至少眼下这些应该够用了。",cEN="Not bad. These are good planks, you have a fine eye.\n\nMaybe they really will manage to take the mill back, but this should be enough for now at least."}
Q[255118]={d="这些新来的人一直向我要水，可我觉得我们的井水对活人来说已经不太合适了。\n\n我也不能就这么让他们渴死。我们正东边有条河，那水应该好一些。在……这一切之前，我一直觉得瀑布脚下的水味道最好。\n\n我不放心让我这身子骨安然无恙地下山，可你看起来还撑得住一些。也许你能帮他们打一桶水回来？",dEN="These new arrivals have been asking me for water, but I don't think our well would be very good for the living anymore.\n\nI can't just let them die of thirst either. There's a river just to the east of us that should be better. Back before...all this, I always thought it tasted best at the base of the waterfall.\n\nI don't trust my body to make it down the hill in one piece, but you seem like you're holding together a bit better. Maybe you could fill a bucket up for them?",o="为莫妮卡·森古兹从瀑布底部取水。",oEN="Fetch water from the base of the waterfall for Monika Sengutz.",p="我想你还没办完吧……？",pEN="I don't suppose you've finished already...?",c="看见没？要是换了我，那只乌龟多半会把我吃了。也许也不会……我怀疑连野狗都懒得碰这身腐肉。\n\n我真该去找一趟外科医生……看看能不能弄到些更新鲜的部件。",cEN="See? If that had been me, that turtle probably would’ve eaten me. Or perhaps not… I doubt even the wild dogs would bother with this rotten flesh.\n\nI really should pay the surgeon a visit… see about acquiring some fresher parts."}
Q[255119]={d="我猜你觉得我们这些亡灵不在乎喝被污染的井水，是吧？说实话，我们大多数人宁愿避开它……那会勾起不愉快的回忆。\n\n碰巧的是，对我们这类人来说最好的水是海水。盐能帮我们保持干燥。\n\n相信我，一座住满干爽亡灵的镇子，闻起来可比住满……湿漉漉亡灵的要好得多。\n\n去河海交汇的地方给我打一桶水来，那正好合用。去的路上尽量离南海镇远点。",dEN="I suppose you think us undead don’t mind using tainted well water, don’t you? Truth is, most of us prefer to avoid it... brings back unpleasant memories.\n\nAs it happens, the best water for our kind is seawater. The salt helps dry us out.\n\nTrust me, a town full of dry undead smells far better than one full of… moist ones.\n\nFetch me a bucket from where the river meets the ocean, that’ll do nicely. And do try to steer clear of Southshore while you’re at it.",o="为莫妮卡·森古兹从河口取回海水。",oEN="Fetch ocean water from the mouth of the river for Monika Sengutz.",p="我差点就忍不住要问你，在南海镇有没有见到什么我可能认识的人……可转念一想，也许还是不知道为好。",pEN="I'm almost tempted to ask if you saw anyone I might've known in Southshore... but then again, I'm probably better off not knowing.",c="嗯，你没洒掉太多。拎着那桶水到处走可不容易……这我清楚。\n\n谢谢你的帮忙。你可真是让我大出血了。\n\n我说这话是字面意思。",cEN="Well, you didn’t spill too much of it. Carrying that bucket around isn’t easy... I should know.\n\nThanks for the help. You’re really saving me an arm and a leg here.\n\nAnd I do mean that quite literally."}
Q[255120]={d="那么，还记得我说过我们大多数人都不碰瘟疫之水吗？嗯……有那么一小撮可疑的家伙却对它爱得不行。瘟疫使者莱登恰好就是其中之一。别问我为什么，我那口不起眼的井显然配不上他高雅的品味。\n\n不，他坚持要直接取自瘟疫之地的样本。\n\n不过，他还没疯到派我横穿整个洛丹伦去源头取水……但他的架子够大，非要我从达隆米尔湖汇入希尔斯布莱德河的地方取。\n\n愿意再帮一位女士一次忙吗？",dEN="So, remember how I said most of us avoid plague water? Well… a small, questionable few absolutely adore it. Plaguemaster Lydon happens to be one of them. Don’t ask me why, my modest well clearly isn’t up to his refined tastes.\n\nNo, he insists on samples straight from the Plaguelands.\n\nNow, he’s not quite mad enough to send me all the way across Lordaeron to fetch it from the source… but he is entitled enough to demand it from where Darrowmere Lake feeds into the Hillsbrad River.\n\nCare to help a lady out, one last time?",o="从西瘟疫之地边界的达隆米尔湖瀑布取一桶被瘟疫污染的水。",oEN="Fetch a bucket of plagued water from the Darrowmere Lake waterfall on the border of Western Plaguelands.",p="你去取水了吗？光是想到这样一趟路，我的骨头就疼……",pEN="Have you gone and fetched the water yet? My bones ache just thinking about such a trip...",c="<Monika mira hacia el agua, con una expresión de asco>\n\n我甚至不确定自己能不能受得了这个……而这话已经说明很多了。\n\n更别提最糟的部分了……很大一部分水直接顺流而下，流向下一道瀑布……正是我派你去为那些精灵取干净水的地方。\n\n……唉，算了。那不是我的问题。",cEN="<Monika glances down at the water, her expression twisting in disgust.>\n\nI’m not even sure I could stomach this… and that’s saying something.\n\nNot to mention the worst part... A good portion of it flows straight downstream, to the next waterfall… the very same place I sent you to fetch clean water for those elves.\n\n…Ah well. Not my problem."}
Q[255121]={d="啊，一盘美味的鱼……烤得恰到好处，用上了我所有最好的香料，鱼皮下还藏着一只火焰元素的命火。\n\n要是这都烫不烂他们的嘴、给那些傲慢的小鬼一个教训，那……再往下做恐怕就要让银月城和亡灵之间的关系紧张了。\n\n我不想给黑暗女士惹麻烦……所以我的参与就到此为止。不过我承认，我挺想看看他们的表情……",dEN="Ah, a lovely plate of fish... crisped to perfection, seasoned with all my finest aromatics, and the lifespark of a fire elemental slipped beneath the skin.\n\nIf this doesn't scorch their mouths and teach those snooty brats a lesson, well... anything more will probably create strain the relations between Silvermoon and the Forsaken.\n\nI do not wish to cause the Dark Lady any problems... so this is as far as my involvement shall go. Though I will confess, I'd quite like to see their faces...",o="把德拉克的饭菜送到塔伦米尔旅店的艾佛莫恩姐妹手中。",oEN="Deliver Derak's meal to the Evermorne sisters in the Tarren Mill inn.",p="嗯嗯……！那香味是什么，这么好闻？",pEN="Mmmm...! What's that delicious smell?",c="哦，这看起来太棒了！也许只是我的肚子在说话，但我觉得希瑞妮娅的厨艺可能真变好了。\n\n也许是因为我们谁都没别的选择，逼得她进步，不再什么都往上乱喷火了？这堆烂事里总算有件好事……\n\n维内斯拉！看来我们难得能吃上一顿像样的饭了。",cEN="Oh, this looks incredible! Maybe it's just my stomach talking, but I think Cirenia might have actually gotten decent at cooking.\n\nMaybe none of us having other options forced her to improve and stop blasting far too much fire at everything? At least one good thing would've come out of all this...\n\nVenesra! It looks like we actually get to have a decent meal for once."}
Q[255122]={d="这地方满是隐藏的秘密。当然，我一个人到处乱逛太危险了，而亡灵对巨魔的历史又没什么兴趣。\n\n要是你愿意帮忙，河上游有片废墟，所有人——连野兽都——都绕着它走。也许有什么东西在守着那地方，但我敢肯定里面满是器物和遗物，我早就想弄到手了。\n\n能拿多少拿多少，都给我带回来。",dEN="Dis place be full of hidden secrets. 'Course, it be too dangerous to go wanderin' out on my own, and de Forsaken ain't showin' much interest in troll history.\n\nIf you be willin' to help, there be ruins up the river that everyone, even the beasts be ignorin'. Maybe there's somethin' protectin' the place, but I'm sure it be full of artifacts and relics I'm eager to get my hands on.\n\nGrab whatever you can find an' bring it back to me.",o="为拉克提尔从河上游的废墟中收集巨魔遗物。",oEN="Collect Troll Relics from the ruins up the river for Rak'til.",p="你找到什么了吗，老兄？",pEN="You found anything yet, mon?",c="原来那是些灵魂……\n\n要我是个更好的巨魔，我会说我们该想办法让它们的灵魂安息。可是……那可能就意味着我得放弃这些新到手的遗物。\n\n我想它们不会介意让我再多留一阵子吧，嗯，老兄？",cEN="So it were spirits...\n\nIf I was a bettah troll I'd say we should find a way to put their souls to rest. But... that might involve me giving up my new relics.\n\nI don't think they'd mind if I kept 'em for a little longer, eh mon?"}
Q[255123]={d="这群小家伙最近不太高兴。我给它们喂了不少牛血，可它们的口味显然更……刁钻。\n\n有一次我让它们去对付几只从奥特兰克往南跑得太远的雪怪，自那以后，别的东西就再也满足不了它们了。\n\n它们还小，我也还没准备好放它们独自去猎杀那么危险的猎物，所以在我彻底失控之前，换个办法怎么样？拿上我平时给还不能自己进食的幼崽用的那支注射器，你亲自去从雪怪身上采血。带回来，至少我还能有点东西安抚它们。",dEN="The colony has been unhappy as of late. I feed them plenty of cow blood, but they've proven to have a more...exotic palette.\n\nI set them upon some yetis that came too far south from Alterac once, and ever since, nothing else will quite satisfy them.\n\nThey're still juvenille, and I'm not ready to send them out hunting such dangerous prey on their own quite yet, so how about another plan then, before I lose control completely? Take the syringe I usually use for the young who can't yet feed themselves, and use it to collect blood from the yetis yourself. Bring it back here, and at least I'll have something to appease them.",o="使用法兰格的注射器从被杀死的雪怪身上采集血液，交给法兰格·伍德玛格。",oEN="Use Farlang's Syringe to harvest blood from slain yetis for Farlang Woodmarg.",p="能采多少采多少，你会惊讶于它们有多能喝。",pEN="Get as much as you can gather, you'd be surprised how much they can drink.",c="哦，这相当多了。干得好。\n\n我迟早得想个更好的办法，但至少这能让我在不得不为此太操心之前争取些时间。等这些用完的时候，也许它们就准备好来一场像样的狩猎了。",cEN="Oh, that's quite a lot. Good work.\n\nI'll need to figure out a better solution sooner or later, but this will at least give me some time before I have to worry too much about it. By the time this all runs out, maybe they'll be ready for a proper hunt."}
Q[255124]={d="啊，你看起来很壮实。正是我需要的。\n\n这两只可是我最得意的作品，不过我还在改进它们的战斗能力。你看，它们的手臂动作还有点太僵硬，发力也不够……啊，你已经听烦了。你是那种人，行吧。\n\n既然它们已经活起来了，就得进食，但总得有人先替它们去杀。明白我为什么现在跟你说这些了吗？先从这边的贪吃鬼开始吧，它几乎什么都吃，所以你就去宰塔伦米尔附近的本地野兽。反正那儿的野兽少点也好。",dEN="Ah, you look strong. Just what I needed.\n\nThese two here are my finest work, but I'm still working on their ability to fight. See, their arm motions are a bit too rigid and they aren't putting enough force into...ah, you're bored already. One of those types, fine then.\n\nNow that they're active, they need to feed, but someone has to do the killing for them first. See why I'm telling you this now? Start with Glutton here, he'll eat just about anything, so I'd just stick the local wildlife near Tarren Mill. We could do with less of it anyways.",o="把贪吃鬼带出希尔斯布莱德，杀死 10 只灰熊、苔藓爬行者和饥饿的山地狮来喂它。",oEN="Take Glutton out of Hillsbrad and feed him by slaying 10 Grey Bears, Moss Creepers, and Starving Mountain Lions.",p="贪吃鬼看起来吃饱了吗？没有？那就接着干吧，我还有活要干。",pEN="Does Glutton seem like he's had enough yet? No? Well, keep at it then, I've got work to do.",c="贪吃鬼看上去相当满足。你到底猎了多少只？\n\n十只？！那完全没有必要。一只憎恶吃两头熊就能轻松活下来。\n\n不过这得怪我，不该以为你早就知道。至少它看起来壮了些，也许你的路子是对的。",cEN="Glutton looks quite satisfied. How many did you hunt anyways?\n\nTen?! That's entirely unnecessary. An abomination can survive on a couple bears easily.\n\nBut that's on me for assuming you'd know that already. He does look stronger at least, maybe you were onto something."}
Q[255125]={d="好了，下一个是吞食者。它只吃更强壮的野生动物。塔伦米尔附近没什么合它口味的，所以你得多带它走远一些。\n\n顺便也让它吃上十只，我正好试试这到底有没有什么用处。",dEN="Alright, next is Gorger. He'll only eat stronger wildlife. Nothing near Tarren Mill is quite to his tastes, so you'll have to take him out a bit more.\n\nJust have him eat another ten as well, I might as well test if this does anything useful.",o="把吞食者带出希尔斯布莱德，杀死 10 只年长的灰熊、巨型苔藓爬行者和凶猛的山地狮来喂它。",oEN="Take Gorger out of Hillsbrad and feed him by slaying 10 Elder Grey Bears, Giant Moss Creepers, and Feral Mountain Lions.",p="它们在试图冲到地面时把身体损坏得太严重了。",pEN="They've damaged too much of their bodies trying to get out to the surface.",c="你应付得不错。你会是个好助手。\n\n不过，我当然相信你马上就要跑掉了。行吧，去吧，我还有几项测试要做。",cEN="You handled yourself well. You'd make a fine assistant.\n\nBut of course I'm sure you're running off. Well, go on then, I've got some tests to perform."}
Q[255126]={d="我们这条路不是给胆小鬼走的。只有意志坚不可摧、力量强大无比的人，才能登上高塔，协助我们完成神圣的使命。\n\n你不属于我们。要是由我来决定，你永远都不会是。\n\n但我不是你的审判者。\n\n如果你真的一心想要加入……如果你渴望暗影的知识，那就去墓地，把这瓶喝下去。然后……你就会明白了。",dEN="Ours is no calling for the faint of heart. Only those of unyielding will and formidable power may ascend the tower and assist in our sacred mission.\n\nYou are not among us. And if it were my decision, you never would be.\n\nBut I am not your judge.\n\nIf you truly seek entry… if you crave the knowledge of shadow, then go to the graveyard and drink this. Then... you will understand.",o="在塔伦米尔墓地喝下那瓶毒药，向暗影法师证明你的资格。",oEN="Drink the bottle of poison in the Tarren Mill graveyard and prove yourself worthy to the Shadowmages.",p="别来烦我。",pEN="Don't bother me.",c="啊……现在我从你眼里看出来了。\n\n你已经感受过了，不是吗？死亡的冰冷拥抱、恐惧，还有那无可避免的宿命压得人喘不过气——因为它终有一天会再次来找你。\n\n这是我们都有的感受，也是我们愿意不惜一切代价去逃避的东西。而现在……你也怕它了，就像我们一样。\n\n进来吧。",cEN="Ah… I see it in your eyes now.\n\nYou’ve felt it, haven’t you? The cold embrace of death, the terror, the crushing weight of its inevitability as it will one day come for you again.\n\nIt is a feeling we all share, and one we would do anything to escape. And now… you fear it, just as we do.\n\nEnter."}
Q[255127]={d="虽然黑暗女士给我们的经费充足，但我们的研究依旧……耗资巨大。而到目前为止，它几乎没结出什么果实。\n\n结果就是，卫兵们越来越不愿意给我们送来新鲜的实验体。他们带来的活人都留给我们做更深层的灵魂探索。但你会有不同的用途。\n\n拿上这个容器。往北走，到那些连我们的卫兵都很少踏足的群山里。你会在那儿找到躲藏的人类。干掉他们。然后对刚死不久的人使用这个容器。\n\n我对你的发现……非常感兴趣。",dEN="Though we are well-funded by the Dark Lady, our research remains… costly. And as yet, it has borne us little fruit.\n\nAs a result, the guards grow increasingly reluctant to deliver us fresh subjects. The living they bring are reserved for our deeper explorations of the soul. But you shall have a different purpose.\n\nTake this vessel. Travel north, to the mountains where even our guards seldom tread. There, you will find humans in hiding. End them. And use the vessel upon the freshly departed.\n\nI am… most interested in what you will uncover.",o="在斯坦恩布莱德对死去的人类使用贝加蒙特·莱斯特恩的精华提取器。",oEN="Use Bergamont Lestern's Essence Extractor on dead humans in Strahnbrad.",p="大声点，你发现了什么？",pEN="Speak up, what have you found?",c="太妙了……眼下这些够用了。\n\n我得承认，你正逐渐成为一个有用的小棋子。也许你终究会成为我们事业的一项资产。",cEN="Marvelous… this will suffice for now.\n\nI must admit, you are proving to be a useful little pawn. Perhaps you will become an asset to our cause after all."}
Q[255128]={d="法师大人已经尽力而为了，可这些人类的魔法实在太弱了。要不是怕惹怒银月城，我猜噬魂者早就把我和我的精灵商队视作维持这些缚灵供她研究的上好燃料了。\n\n那种下场我巴不得避开。\n\n可需要就是需要，为了银月城的利益，这样的欲望必须得到满足。不过我本人还没准备好献出自己或家人的性命。所以，拿着这支虹吸器，用它从山里的食人魔法师身上抽取奥术能量。\n\n办成这件事，我就欠你一份人情。",dEN="The magister is doing what he can, but these humans possess such feeble magic. If it were not for the risk of drawing Silvermoon’s ire, I suspect the Soulcleaver would have already deemed us, and my elven caravan, fit as fuel to sustain these bound spirits for her research.\n\nA fate I would very much prefer to avoid.\n\nNeeds are needs however, and such desires must be met, for the good of Silvermoon. Yet I for one am not quite ready to lay down my own life, nor that of my family. So here, take this siphon and use it to draw the arcane from the ogre spellcasters in the mountains.\n\nDo this, and I will be in your debt.",o="使用女祭司的奥术虹吸器，从奥特兰克山脉的食人魔法师身上抽取魔法。",oEN="Using the Priestess' Arcane Siphon, extract magic from the ogre mages in Alterac Mountains.",p="替女祭司跑腿跑得开心吗？",pEN="Having fun with the priestess' errands?",c="哎呀呀……这是什么？给我们灵魂锚点的礼物？真是体贴。\n\n简直就像女祭司觉得我会绝望到开始拿自己人当燃料似的。\n\n拜托。好像我会那么蠢一样。那种程度的背叛毫无疑问会要了我的命。我还以为女祭司比这更有洞察力。\n\n不过……\n\n恐惧总会蒙蔽人的判断。既然现在细想起来……也许她的担忧并非全无道理。",cEN="Oh my… what do we have here? A gift for our soul anchors? How thoughtful.\n\nIt's almost as if the Priestess believes I might grow desperate enough to begin using our own people as fuel.\n\nPlease. As if I would be so foolish. Treason of that magnitude would ensure my death without question. I had thought the Priestess more perceptive than that.\n\nStill…\n\nFear has a way of clouding judgment. And now that I consider it… perhaps her concerns are not entirely without merit."}
Q[255130]={d="我必须逃离这个地方，把这些恐怖行径的真相带给会采取行动的人，带给有足够力量制止这场疯狂的人！\n\n去找我牢房的钥匙；走廊尽头左手边有一间审讯室，囚犯会被带到那里处理，用于实验。\n\n钥匙应该就在那儿。快！",dEN="I must escape this place and bring word of these horrors to someone who will act, someone with power enough to stop this madness!\n\nFind the key to my cell, there is an interrogation chamber down the hall on the left where prisoners are taken and processed for experiments.\n\nThe keys will be kept there. Hurry!",o="在审讯室里寻找钥匙。",oEN="Look for the key in the interrogation chambers.",p="你在审讯室里找到钥匙了吗？",pEN="Did you find the key in the interrogation chambers?",c="我本以为钥匙一定在那儿……可你找到的却是被杀害的队长。\n\n他是个好人。这恰恰证实了我的担忧：这座设施里正在发生某种污秽之事。先是我被囚禁，如今队长又死了……你还说狼人跑出来了？\n\n以黑暗女士之名……这里到底出什么事了？！",cEN="I was certain the key would be there... yet instead you find the Captain murdered.\n\nHe was a good man. This only confirms my fears that something foul is unfolding within this facility. First my imprisonment, now the Captain's death... and you claim the Worgen are loose?\n\nBy the Dark Lady... what in the hells is going on here?!"}
Q[255131]={d="疫谷的每一只狼人本该都被关在笼中、严加束缚。它们被带到这里，是为了让皇家药剂师协会研究这种诅咒……去理解它，甚至也许控制它。但听你说了这些之后，很显然这里有人想要的远不止简单的研究。\n\n不过，只要我还被困在这间牢房里，这些就都不重要。\n\n东侧的密室有时用来存放没收来的物品。也许你会在那儿找到它。",dEN="Every Worgen in Blighthollow was meant to remain caged and restrained. They were brought here so the Royal Apothecary Society could study the curse... to understand it, perhaps even control it. But after what you've told me, it is clear someone here seeks far more than simple research.\n\nStill, none of this matters if I remain trapped in this cell.\n\nThe eastern chambers are sometimes used to store confiscated belongings. Perhaps that is where you will find it.",o="在东侧密室中寻找钥匙。",oEN="Look for the key in the eastern chambers.",p="告诉我你在东侧密室里找到钥匙了。",pEN="Tell me you found the key in the eastern chambers.",c="该死……还是没有钥匙。\n\n你说死灵法师？！\n\n以黑暗女士之名……我就知道有什么不对劲！\n\n如果真有死灵法师在这里肆意横行，用未经许可的仪式亵渎尸体，那我被囚禁就不再是最要紧的事了。\n\n任何忠于亡灵的仆从，无论疯没疯，都不会堕落到这种地步。强迫他人承受亡灵诅咒……那是不可言说的罪行。",cEN="Damn it... still no key.\n\nNecromancers you say!?\n\nBy the Dark Lady... I knew something wasn't right!\n\nIf necromancers are truly running rampant through this place, defiling corpses with unsanctioned rituals, then my imprisonment is no longer the greatest concern.\n\nNo loyal servant of the Forsaken, mad or otherwise, would stoop to such depravity. To force another into the curse of undeath... it is an unspeakable crime."}
Q[255132]={d="我早该料到会这样。自从那些不稳定分子之间掀起暴动、结成同盟之后，事情就变得越来越可疑。他们告诉我们已经处理掉了。看来我们错了。\n\n这只能说明一件事。这座设施已经被那些假装是我们一员的人从内部渗透并腐化了！我清楚幕后是谁。一共四个，每一个都只痴迷于在这些高墙之内爬上高位。找到他们，处决他们！\n\n钥匙应该在他们其中一人手上！\n\n去吧……现在就去！",dEN="I should have seen this coming. Ever since the revolts and coalitions that formed among the unstable ones, things became increasingly suspicious. We were told they had been dealt with. It seems we were wrong.\n\nThis can only mean one thing. This facility has been infiltrated and corrupted from within by those who pretended to be one of us! I know exactly who's behind this. Four of them, each obsessed with nothing but reaching a position of high authority within these walls. Find them and execute them!\n\nOne of them should have the key!\n\nGo... Now!",o="杀死高阶死灵法师瓦尔德里斯、首席科学家塞里克斯、药剂大师伊沃娜和指挥官费斯图斯。",oEN="Kill High Necromancer Valdris, Lead Scientist Serix, Master Chemist Ivona, and Commander Festus.",p="那些叛徒受到应有的惩罚了吗？",pEN="Have those traitors been dealt with?",c="那些叛徒被解决掉，我很高兴，可一想到他们当中竟没有一个人有我牢房的钥匙，我忍不住有些失望……",cEN="I'm glad those traitors have been dealt with, yet I can't help but feel some measure of disappointment that not one of them had the key to my cell..."}
Q[255133]={d="这很糟，糟透了！\n\n我早该知道留在疫谷的那些人都已经腐化了。\n\n我在这座设施里巡逻了这么多年。我从没想过它会被从内部渗透。我保护了他们所有人。连我怀疑过的人也一样。一直以来他们都在利用我们，这些年一直在假装为亡灵效力。果然和我怀疑的一样！\n\n这座设施里的每一个死灵法师、每一个药剂师、每一个审讯官和卫兵都背叛了亡灵！\n\n把他们全都找出来，不用留情。全部杀光。",dEN="This is bad, real bad!\n\nI should have known the ones who remained in Blighthollow were corrupted.\n\nI have spent years patrolling this facility. Never could I have imagined for it to be infiltrated from within. I protected all of them. Even the ones I was suspicious of. All this time they were using us, pretending to be serving the Forsaken for all these years. Just as I suspected!\n\nEvery necromancer, every chemist, every interrogator and guard in this facility have betrayed the Forsaken!\n\nFind them all and show them no mercy. Kill them all.",o="杀死 4 名疫谷死灵法师、4 名疫谷审讯官、6 名疫谷药剂师和 10 名疫谷卫兵。",oEN="Slay 4 Blighthollow Necromancers, 4 Blighthollow Interrogators, 6 Blighthollow Chemists, and 10 Blighthollow Guards.",p="疫谷那些腐化的部队都死了吗？",pEN="Are the corrupted forces of Blighthollow dead?",c="想想看……我曾把这些人当作同志交谈。有些人我甚至当成了朋友。\n\n一直以来，我不过是个被人摆布的傻瓜。\n\n也许我从未真正了解过他们中的任何一个。",cEN="And to think... I spoke with these people as comrades. Some, I even considered friends.\n\nAll this time, I was nothing but a manipulated fool.\n\nPerhaps I never truly knew any of them."}
Q[255134]={d="我不明白。总得有人拿着那把钥匙。它不可能就这么凭空消失了！\n\n除非……是编年史官！\n\n我不敢相信。我们所有人都信任他，连希尔瓦娜斯本人也是。\n\n他是记录保管者，负责监管疫谷内的报告和事件，并把它们回报给幽暗城的皇家药剂师协会。\n\n这一切一定都是他干的！\n\n钥匙在他手上。把钥匙给我拿来，也把他的脑袋给我带来。",dEN="I do not understand. Someone has to have that key. It cannot have simply disappeared!\n\nUnless... The Chronicler!\n\nI can't believe it. He was trusted by all of us, including Sylvanas herself.\n\nHe is the keeper of records who watched over the reports and happenings within Blighthollow, relaying them back to the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity.\n\nHe must be the one behind all of this!\n\nHe'll have the key. Bring it to me, and bring me his head as well.",o="杀死编年史官哈维，取回疫谷牢房钥匙。",oEN="Slay Chronicler Harvey and retrieve the Blighthollow Cell Key.",p="钥匙到手了吗？告诉我，编年史官手里有钥匙。",pEN="Do you have the key? Tell me The Chronicler had it.",c="钥匙！\n\n蒙黑暗女士恩典……你真的找到它了！\n\n终于……我自由了！\n\n在我离开之前，有件事你必须知道。",cEN="The key!\n\nBy the grace of the Dark Lady... you actually found it!\n\nFinally... I am free!\n\nBefore I leave there is something you need to know."}
Q[255135]={d="这些墓穴最初是亡灵的复活之所，后来被改作他用，不仅用来研究狼人诅咒，还用来研制一种新毒药。我们都在为同一个目标努力。制造一件对付联盟的生物武器。把最恶毒的毒素与我们能找到的最凶残的狼人融合在一起。他们管它叫腐喉。\n\n这里复活起来的许多亡灵都不稳定，拒绝认同我们的目标。腐喉本是要成为黑暗女士的毁灭工具，但如今我看得很清楚，他们中有一些人隐瞒自己的意图，只是为了爬上权力高位，然后拿腐喉来对付我们。\n\n腐喉还在下面，就在设施深处。要是它离开这些高墙，后果将不堪设想。\n\n无论付出什么代价，都一定要把那头憎恶解决掉。",dEN="These crypts began as a place of resurrection for the Forsaken but were later repurposed not only to study the Worgen curse, but also to develop new poison. We were all working toward the same goal. To create a biological weapon against the Alliance. A fusion of the most vile toxins with the most relentless Worgen we could find. They called it Rotmaw.\n\nMany of the Undead raised here were unstable and refused to align themselves with our goals. Rotmaw was meant to be the Dark Lady's instrument of devastation, but it is clear to me now that some of them were keeping their intentions a secret only to gain high positions of power and use Rotmaw against us.\n\nRotmaw is still down there, deep within the facility. If it leaves these walls, the catastrophe will be unfathomable.\n\nWhatever the cost, make sure you put that abomination down.",o="杀死腐喉，然后向墓室的药剂师霍尔姆复命。",oEN="Slay Rotmaw and report to Apothecary Holm in The Sepulcher.",p="腐喉死了吗？",pEN="Is Rotmaw dead?",c="你回来了……\n\n<他一边听一边睁大了眼睛，缓缓摇了摇头。>\n\n这已经远远超出了背叛。一想到他们要是把黑暗女士的生物武器放到我们头上会是什么后果，我就不寒而栗。\n\n我试图救治的那名卫兵没能活下来。他们注进那头畜生血管里的毒药早已注定了他的命运。",cEN="You've returned...\n\n<His eyes widen as he listens, and he slowly shakes his head.>\n\nThis goes far beyond betrayal. I shudder to imagine what would've happened if they unleashed the Dark Lady's biological weapon onto us.\n\nThe guard I attempted to treat did not survive. Whatever poison they pumped into that beast's veins ensured his fate."}
Q[255136]={d="这对皇家药剂师协会来说可不是好兆头。我会把这些发现呈报给黑暗女士本人，尽管我猜这样的真相会在幽暗城掀起波澜。\n\n把这本日志带到塔伦米尔，交给药剂师莱登。他的手段也许比我还阴暗，但他对黑暗女士的忠诚从未动摇过。\n\n这种背叛绝不能听之任之……我也无意保持沉默。",dEN="This bodes ill for the Royal Apothecary Society. I will bring these findings before the Dark Lady herself, though I suspect such revelations will send tremors through the Undercity.\n\nTake this journal to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. His methods may be darker than my own, but his loyalty to the Dark Lady has never wavered.\n\nThis betrayal cannot be allowed to stand... and I have no intention of remaining silent.",o="把疫谷卫兵日志带给塔伦米尔的药剂师莱登。",oEN="Bring the Blighthollow Guard Logbook to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",p="你带来疫谷的消息了？让我看看这本日志。",pEN="You have brought news from Blighthollow? Let me see this journal.",c="所以疫谷那些蠢货居然造出了这么件了不起的武器……却因为自己的无能白白糟蹋了它，逼得你不得不把那东西解决掉？\n\n多么可惜的浪费……\n\n不过，你把这事告诉我做得好。也许他们的研究里还有什么可以挽救，等黑暗女士得知这场灾祸时，多少能缓和一下冲击。\n\n毕竟，药剂师的工作从来就没有真正完成的时候。",cEN="So the fools at Blighthollow managed to create such a magnificent weapon... only to squander it through their own incompetence, forcing you to put the creature down?\n\nWhat a tragic waste...\n\nStill, you have done well to bring this to my attention. Perhaps there is something yet to salvage from their research, something that may soften the blow when the Dark Lady learns of this disaster.\n\nThe work of the Apothecaries is never truly finished, after all."}
Q[255138]={c="你找到他了？谢谢你告诉我他平安无事。我很感激你，<class>。\n\n别害怕。",cEN="You found him? Thank you for letting me know that he is safe. I appreciate you, <class>.\n\nDon't be afraid."}
Q[255139]={c="汪！汪！<El perro te mira felizmente como si esperara algo>",cEN="Woof! Woof! <The dog looks at you happily as if it expects something>"}
Q[255140]={d="南海镇的许多守军都东去了，去保护蔚蓝矿洞里的矿工。\n\n身为圣光的女祭司，我无法忍受袖手旁观，眼看着那么勇敢的灵魂去冒生命危险。可我知道我的职责在这里，维持希望，让民众安心。\n\n不过，我已经做了力所能及的事。我准备了一瓶圣油，用来帮助我们的士兵。\n\n你愿意把它带到矿洞去，确保我们的守军得到圣光的祝福吗？",dEN="Many of Southshore’s defenders have gone east, working to protect the miners in the Azurelode Mine.\n\nAs a priestess of the Light, I cannot bear to stand idle while such brave souls risk their lives. Yet I know my duty lies here, keeping hope alive and the people calm.\n\nStill, I have done what I can. I’ve prepared a flask of holy oil to aid our soldiers.\n\nWill you take it to the mine, and see that our defenders receive the Light’s blessing?",o="用圣光武器油为蔚蓝矿洞的 10 名希尔斯布莱德哨兵或希尔斯布莱德守军施加祝福。",oEN="Empower 10 Hillsbrad Sentries or Hillsbrad Defenders at the Azurelode Mine with Holy Weapon Oil.",p="我们在矿洞里的守卫情况如何？",pEN="How fares our guardians in the mines?",c="哦……听你这么说我就放心了。我很庆幸自己的努力帮上了忙。\n\n我祈祷他们能有更多人早日归来……而且是带着胜利归来。\n\n请收下这个，作为我谢意的表示。这一切你起了关键作用。",cEN="Oh… that is a relief to hear. I’m grateful my efforts were of some help.\n\nI pray more of them return to us soon… and with victory in hand.\n\nPlease, take this as a token of my gratitude. You’ve been instrumental in all of this."}
Q[255141]={d="二十……四十……六十——圣光在上，还是不够！\n\n你，冒险者。\n\n如果你在找活干，我这儿正有个合适的任务。我们已经抽调了一部分民兵去守卫蔚蓝矿洞，可不管我们派多少卫兵过去，矿工们还是怕得不敢干活。\n\n南海镇承受不起矿产短缺。\n\n去矿洞，亲自确保工人们能重新回到岗位上。",dEN="Twenty… forty… sixty- Light damn it, it’s still not enough!\n\nYou there, adventurer.\n\nIf you’re looking for work, I have just the task. We’ve already diverted part of the militia to secure the Azurelode Mine, but no matter how many guards we send, the miners are still too frightened to do their jobs.\n\nSouthshore cannot endure a shortage of minerals.\n\nGo to the mine and see to it, personally, that the workers can return to their duties.",o="从蔚蓝矿洞的希尔斯布莱德矿工那里回收 15 块蔚蓝矿石。",oEN="Reclaim 15 chunks of Azurite Ore from Hillsbrad Miners in the Azurelode mine.",p="那些石头可不会自己把自己挖出来，你知道的……",pEN="Those rocks aren't going to mine themselves you know...",c="你回来了，还带回了这么一大堆……！\n\n我说不清哪件事更让人佩服……是你居然安抚住了矿工，让他们肯干活了，还是你连辆推车都没有就把那么多石头运了回来。\n\n不管怎样，活干得漂亮就该有像样的报酬。",cEN="You've returned, and with quite the haul...!\n\nI’m not sure which is more impressive... that you managed to steady the miners enough to do their work, or that you hauled all that stone back here without so much as a cart.\n\nEither way, a job well done deserves a proper reward."}
Q[255142]={d="心里装着这么多事，我很难集中精神。不过……也许我能借你去办一件更私人的差事？\n\n达拉然升空时，肯瑞托的一些成员留了下来，负责缓解陨石坑里残留的奥术扰动。其中有我昔日的导师，大法师安斯雷姆·符文编织者。\n\n尽管他才华横溢，却总爱走……捷径。而南海镇现在最不需要的，就是不稳定魔法渗进这片地区。\n\n把这张便条带给他，务必确认他的工作是在按规矩进行。",dEN="With so much on my mind, I find it difficult to concentrate. Still… perhaps I might borrow you for a more personal errand?\n\nSome members of the Kirin Tor remained behind to mitigate the arcane disturbances left in the crater when Dalaran took to the skies. Among them is my old mentor, Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver.\n\nFor all his brilliance, he has always had a tendency to take… shortcuts. And the last thing Southshore needs right now is unstable magic seeping into the region.\n\nTake this note to him, and make certain his work is being done properly.",o="把顾问贝尔维尤那封封蜡精美的便条交给奥特兰克山脉达拉然巨坑附近的大法师安斯雷姆·符文编织者。",oEN="Deliver Advisor Belview's Elegantly Sealed Note to Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver near the Dalaran Crater in Alterac Mountains.",p="嗯？这是什么……？",pEN="Hmm? What's this...?",c="这笔歪歪扭扭的字我认得出来。\n\n所以……小贝尔维尤信不过我，觉得我干不好自己的活。\n\n我虽然有时看着散漫，可毕竟还在达拉然的六人议会里占着一席。本以为他会对长辈多几分尊重……",cEN="I’d recognize this loopy handwriting anywhere.\n\nSo… young Belview doesn’t trust me to do my work properly.\n\nLax as I may sometimes appear, I still hold a seat on the Council of Six in Dalaran. One would think he’d show a bit more respect for his elders…"}
Q[255143]={d="就目前的情况看，贝尔维尤担心达拉然巨坑的余波并非全无道理。\n\n我们已经立起一道奥术屏障，把最糟糕的部分困住，防止那些显现物扩散到洛丹伦其他地区。可维持屏障的守护石往往会引来附近生物不必要的注意。\n\n它们时不时需要加固……看来我这位学徒替我举荐了你。",dEN="As it is, Belview isn’t entirely wrong to be concerned about the lingering effects of the Dalaran Crater.\n\nWe’ve established an arcane barrier to contain the worst of it, preventing those manifestations from spreading into the rest of Lordaeron. However, the wardstones maintaining that barrier tend to attract unwanted attention from nearby creatures.\n\nThey require reinforcement from time to time… and it seems my apprentice has volunteered you for the task.",o="用充能水晶加固北、南、东、西四侧的奥术屏障。",oEN="Reinforce the Arcane barrier at the North, South, East, and Western edges with the Energy Infused Crystal.",p="那么，办好了吗？",pEN="Is it done then?",c="啊哈……没错！\n\n我在这儿就能看见那道光，干得漂亮。\n\n要是我手下的法师有你这股敢闯进巨坑的魄力，哪怕只有一分，我们这儿说不定真能推动点实际进展……",cEN="Aha… yes!\n\nI can see the glow from here, excellently done.\n\nIf only my own mages had even a fraction of your willingness to venture so boldly into the crater, perhaps we’d actually get some real work done around here…"}
Q[255144]={d="体力活从来就不是法师该干的事……可我们的工人慢得实在离谱。\n\n这片区域越早清理干净，我就越早能回去处理更重要的事务。\n\n他们口口声声说补给不够用，可我看到的只是碎石堆里散落着各种可用材料。只需要一个有眼力的人，把真正没用的和还能救回来的分开。\n\n翻检废墟，把一切能在重建中用得上的值钱东西回收回来。",dEN="Manual labor has never been a task suited to a mage… and yet our laborers are extraordinarily slow.\n\nThe sooner this area is properly cleared, the sooner I may return to matters of greater importance.\n\nThey insist they are low on supplies, yet all I see is potential material scattered through the rubble. It only requires someone with discernment to separate what is truly useless from what can be salvaged.\n\nSift through the debris and recover anything of value that can be reused in our restoration efforts.",o="在废墟堆中寻找可回收的材料，交给达拉然巨坑周围的达拉然工人。",oEN="Sift through the rubble piles for salvageable materials and deliver them to Dalaran Workers around the Dalaran Crater.",p="你看起来脏兮兮的，我猜翻找进行得挺顺利？",pEN="You look filthy, I suppose the scrounging is going well?",c="感谢你的努力，希望这能帮着加快些进度。\n\n就目前而言，除了等着看事情怎么发展，我也做不了太多。\n\n不过……我想，今天我是被迫要练练耐心这门美德了。",cEN="I appreciate your efforts, hopefully this will help speed things along.\n\nAs it stands, there is little more I can do but wait and see how matters unfold.\n\nStill… I suppose patience is a virtue I am being forced to practice today."}
Q[255145]={d="魔法既可以是奇妙的东西……也可以是怪物。\n\n在稳健的手中，它会化为美、实用与无限的可能。落到心怀恶意的人手里，它会带来难以估量的毁灭。\n\n可若是失去控制，它就会变成完全不同的东西。怪异而多变……往往充满暴力，连最精湛的法师也无法掌控。\n\n除掉这样一头异物本在我的职责清单上……不过也许你可以代我处理掉它。它就在巨坑的东侧边缘——当然，如果你愿意的话。",dEN="Magic can be both wonderful… and monstrous.\n\nIn steady hands, it becomes beauty, utility, and limitless possibility. In the hands of the malicious, it brings untold devastation.\n\nBut left unchecked, it becomes something else entirely. Strange, volatile things... often violent, and beyond the control of even the most accomplished wizards.\n\nTo bring down such an abomination was on my list of duties… but perhaps you could deal with it on my behalf. It’s located on the eastern edge of the crater, if you'd be so kind, of course.",o="摧毁达拉然巨坑东侧的奥术异常体。",oEN="Destroy the Arcane Anomaly on the eastern edge of the Dalaran Crater.",p="还有那么多差事没办完……唉，我多希望能回到达拉然……",pEN="So many tasks to finish... oh how I wish to return to Dalaran....",c="那么……它被拆掉了？\n\n你证明了自己是个相当顽强的对手。\n\n告诉我，你有没有想过加入肯瑞托？你甚至可以当我的学徒……只要你别像贝尔维尤那样，过了这么多年还盯着我不放。\n\n再想想……也许不值得费这个劲。",cEN="So… it’s been dismantled?\n\nYou’ve proven yourself quite the hardy adversary.\n\nTell me, have you ever considered joining the Kirin Tor? You could even serve as my apprentice… provided you don’t watch over me the way Belview still does, even all these years later.\n\nOn second thought… perhaps it isn’t worth the trouble."}
Q[255146]={d="既然这里现在大体上已经控制住了，你也亲眼看到了……你介意回去找我那位过分热心的学徒，让他放心，说这里一切都在我掌握之中吗？\n\n说真的，被自己的学徒这样纠缠……\n\n<大法师重重叹了口气。>",dEN="With everything here now relatively under control, as you’ve seen for yourself… would you mind returning to my rather overzealous apprentice and assuring him that I have things well in hand?\n\nTruly, to be pestered so by one’s own apprentice…\n\n<The Archmage sighs heavily.>",o="回到南海镇找顾问贝尔维尤，告诉他你在达拉然巨坑所做的事。",oEN="Return to Advisor Belview in Southshore and tell him of your work in the Dalaran Crater.",p="大法师说了什么？",pEN="The Archmage said what?",c="哦……真是好大的胆子！\n\n我真有点想直接传送上去，亲自数落他一顿！\n\n话虽如此……就算他利用你替他分担了工作，我也很感激大法师维持住了屏障，而且事情确实在推进。\n\n也许至少眼下，我可以把全部注意力重新放回南海镇了。\n\n谢谢你，冒险者。",cEN="Oh… the nerve!\n\nI have half a mind to teleport up there and give him a piece of my thoughts myself!\n\nThat said… even if he did use you to offload his own work, I am grateful the Archmage has maintained the barrier and that progress is being made.\n\nPerhaps, for now at least, I can redirect my full attention back to Southshore.\n\nThank you, adventurer."}
Q[255147]={d="奥尔森叔叔当年只花了一枚铜币就买下了他那座农场。当然，他得到的就是他出的那个价。那片地比我如今还死气沉沉，谷仓离塌下来压死里面所有人只差一根烂梁，房子上的洞多到你干脆睡在外面也一样。\n\n我小时候喜欢去那儿做客，感觉像一场冒险。等我意识到那地方有多糟的时候，他已经把它修得挺像样了。就奥尔森叔叔修东西的水平而言算是挺像样了——他那么抠门。可惜他没能被复活，我都能听见他说话……\n\n\"胳膊腿儿不都还能动吗？就因为长得不好看，犯得着闹腾吗。\"\n\n……唉，我最后听说的是农场被占了，大概又变回从前那副样子了。我知道这想法很傻，可想到他花过的那些功夫，心里就是不舒服。你看能不能至少把那些食尸鬼和骷髅清掉？放心，我付的肯定不止一枚铜币。",dEN="Uncle Olsen bought his farm for nothing but a single copper coin. 'Course, he got what he paid for. The land was more dead than I am now, the barn was one rotted beam away from crushing everyone inside, the house had so many holes you may as well have just been sleeping outside.\n\nI liked visiting as a little girl, it felt adventurous. By the time I realized how awful it was, he'd already gotten things fixed up rather nice. As nice as Uncle Olsen fixed up anything, cheapskate that he was. A shame he didn't get raised, I can just hear him...\n\n\"Arms and legs still move, don't they? No need to make a fuss just 'cause they ain't all pretty.\"\n\n...Well, last I heard, the farm's been overrun, and probably fell back into the state it used to be. I know it's silly, but it just feels wrong, after all the work he put in. Think you could at least clear the ghouls and skeletons out? I'll pay more than a copper, don't worry.",o="在奥尔森农庄消灭 6 名鸦爪袭击者和 6 名鸦爪奴隶。",oEN="Destroy 6 Ravenclaw Raiders and 6 Ravenclaw Slaves at Olsen's Farthing.",p="我敢打赌，他要是雇些人手，那地方早就能修好得多。\n\n倒不是说他真会那么干。奥尔森叔叔绝不会为自己能动手的活花钱，哪怕要花上好几年。",pEN="I'll bet he'd have gotten that place fixed up a lot faster if he brought in some hired help.\n\nNot that he ever would've. Uncle Olsen would never spend anything on work he could do himself, even if it took years.",c="我想现在这农场算是我的了。奥尔森叔叔一直独居，直到去世那天。我是唯一还去看望他的亲人，所以他把一切都留给了我。\n\n旅店的生意比那座破败的农场当年好得多，不过我想，他至少会高兴看到那地方不再有没脑子的亡灵到处乱窜。\n\n当然，他是不会承认的。他从来不是那种多愁善感的人。",cEN="I guess it's actually my farm now. Uncle Olsen lived alone until the day he died. I was the only family who actually visited still, so he'd left it all to me.\n\nThe inn business is going a lot better than that run-down farm ever did, but still, I think he'd be glad the place is at least being kept clear of mindless undead rampaging around in it.\n\nNot that he'd admit it. He never was the sentimental type."}
Q[255148]={d="登霍尔姆一家过去每周都会来这里，为那些再没有别人记得的死者献花。多么善良的灵魂。\n\n我听说如今他们的农场被叫作亡者之野。那一定是个可怕的结局。我没有感觉到他们的灵魂离去，可他们也不在那些仍在这里游荡的死者当中。\n\n我的灵魂被束缚在坟墓上，无力为他们做什么，但我的墓碑顶上有一枚小护符，还存着我的一些力量。能否麻烦你把它带到登霍尔姆农场……亡者之野……如果他们的灵魂真的还在那里，就让他们解脱吧。",dEN="The Denholm family used to come here every week to bring flowers for those of the dead who had no one else to remember them. They kind souls.\n\nI hear now their farmstead is known as the Dead Field. It must have been a horrible fate. I have not felt their souls pass on, yet they are not amongst the dead who continue to walk here.\n\nIt is beyond my means to do anything for them, bound as my soul is to my grave, but there is a small talisman atop my monument that still carries some of my power. Could I trouble you to take it to the Denholm Farmstead...the Dead Field...and set their spirits free, if they truly remain there?",o="帮助戴顿神父让登霍尔姆一家的灵魂在亡者之野得到安息。",oEN="Help Father Dayton put the spirits of the Denholm family to rest at the Dead Field.",p="登霍尔姆一家对自家的照料，就像我对这些坟墓一样用心，所以我相当肯定他们的灵魂不会离开。",pEN="The Denholm family cared for their home as much as I cared for these graves, so I am quite sure their spirits would not have left.",c="他们终于安息了吗？\n\n很抱歉你不得不在那种状态下见到他们，带着临终时的恐惧与愤怒。我可以向你保证，换作别的时候，他们绝不会试图伤害任何人。\n\n我太清楚那种连死亡都无法卸下的职责是什么滋味了。他们的家早已不复存在，留在那里只会带来更多痛苦。你可以把那枚护符放回我的坟上，我留在这里还有使命。等使命不再需要我的时候，也许我才会安息。",cEN="They are finally at peace?\n\nI am sorry you had to meet them in such a state, living the fear and anger of their dying moments. I can promise you that they would have never tried to bring harm otherwise.\n\nI know all too well the feeling of a duty that death cannot take you from. Their home has been gone for a long time, and remaining there would only bring them more pain. You can put that talisman back on my grave, I still have a purpose in remaining here. When that is no longer true, perhaps then I shall rest."}
Q[255149]={d="抛开自尊不谈……我不得不问一句，你愿意去对付这些山丘有史以来最可怕的细腿祸害吗？\n\n我叫她丝影。一头恶毒、扭曲的野兽。我循着她的踪迹找到她的巢穴时，看到的尸体多得我不愿去数。\n\n我的反应已经不如当年，现在要是对上她，多半会变成她的下一顿饭。可你……你也许能做成我做不到的事。\n\n去猎杀那头野兽，终结她在这片山丘上的恐怖统治。",dEN="Pride aside… I find myself having to ask, are you willing to take on the worst spindly menace these hills have ever known?\n\nI call her Silkshadow. A vicious, twisted beast. When I tracked her back to her lair, I found more bodies than I care to count.\n\nMy reflexes aren’t what they once were and if I faced her now, I’d likely end up as her next meal. But you… you might just succeed where I could not.\n\nHunt the beast down, and end her reign of terror over these hills.",o="在希尔斯布莱德丘陵杀死丝影。",oEN="Slay Silkshadow in Hillsbrad Foothills.",p="她的巢穴在东边，靠着那堵墙，那儿方便她伏击旅人……她可真是狡猾，对吧？",pEN="Her lair is to the east, near the wall where she can pray on travelers... she's a cunning one, isn't she?",c="圣光在上……你真的做到了。\n\n哈！我承认，我很佩服。我本该说欠你一杯酒，可既然那头野兽已经解决，我想整个南海镇都欠你一杯……还不止一杯。\n\n至于我……知道她不再在外面游荡，我终于能睡得安稳些了。\n\n是啊……好好休息一下，听起来再合适不过。",cEN="By the Light… you actually did it.\n\nHa! I’ll admit it, I’m impressed. I’d say I owe you a drink, but with that beast gone, I reckon all of Southshore owes you one... and then some.\n\nAs for me… I’ll finally sleep a little easier knowing she’s no longer out there.\n\nYes… some rest sounds just about perfect."}
Q[255150]={d="在我永远挂起长矛之前，这片山丘上还有最后一个祸害必须降服。\n\n但听我说……不要独自面对这场狩猎。这头野兽不是任何单个猎人能对付的。\n\n他们叫他高爪，是我追踪过的最庞大、最难以捉摸的山地狮。狮子很少构成威胁，至少对我来说是这样……可这一头不同。他会主动猎杀人类。营地、商队，都无所谓。对他来说，我们都是猎物。\n\n动作要快，出手要狠。你要是被他杀了，我不知道自己会做出什么。",dEN="Before I hang up my spear for good, there’s one last menace in these hills that must be brought to heel.\n\nBut heed me... do not face this hunt alone. This beast is beyond any one hunter.\n\nThey call him Highclaw, the largest, most elusive mountain lion I’ve ever tracked. Lions are rarely a problem, at least not for me… but this one is different. He actively hunts men. Camps, caravans, it makes no difference. To him, we are all his prey.\n\nBe quick, and strike swiftly. I'm not sure what I'd do if he killed you.",o="在希尔斯布莱德丘陵杀死高爪。",oEN="Slay Highclaw in Hillsbrad Foothills.",p="那么……已经办妥了？",pEN="So… it is done, then?",c="不瞒你说，我并不确定你还能回来。我心里还有一小部分在想，如果你回来了我该怎么办……我是否真的准备好挂起长矛。\n\n放下狩猎的刺激……还有守护这些人平安的职责。\n\n但现在我看清楚了，这份重担不再属于我。你把它扛得比我所能扛的更远。\n\n谢谢你，<name>ame。",cEN="I won’t lie, I wasn’t certain you’d return. And a small part of me wondered what I’d do if you did… whether I was truly ready to hang up my spear.\n\nTo leave behind the thrill of the hunt… and the duty of keeping these people safe.\n\nBut I see it clearly now, that burden no longer belongs to me. You’ve carried it further than I ever could.\n\nThank you, <name>ame."}
Q[255151]={d="我们在敦霍尔德城堡附近——至少是它残存的部分附近——遭到了一伙盗贼的袭击。\n\n我们的商队当时正沿大路运送几件遗物，本希望能击退任何挡路的窃贼。不幸的是，我们没能完成任务，至今仍在从这场遭遇中恢复。\n\n你愿意在这些窃贼毁掉如此珍贵的历史文物之前，帮我们把被抢的货物夺回来吗？",dEN="We were accosted by a band of pilferers near Durnholde Keep, or what remains of it, at least.\n\nOur company was transporting several relics along the main road, hoping we could fend off any thieves that crossed our path. Unfortunately, we failed in our mission and are still recuperating from our ventures.\n\nWould you be willing to recover our stolen goods before those thieves destroy such wondrous pieces of history?",o="从敦霍尔德城堡的辛迪加成员手中夺回 8 件被盗遗物。",oEN="Retrieve 8 Stolen Relics from the Syndicate in Durnholde Keep.",p="你找到我们货物中的什么了吗？",pEN="Did you manage to locate any of our cargo?",c="啊哈！你找到它们了……！\n\n<历史学家看了一眼那些遗物，脸色沉了下来。>\n\n哦……哦，不……",cEN="Aha! You found them...!\n\n<The Historian takes a look at the relics and his face falls.>\n\nOh... oh no..."}
Q[255152]={d="虽然普通人看着也许没什么问题，但任何行家都能看出这些可怜东西受的损伤。\n\n以它们现在的状态，我不确定它们还能经得起任何旅程而不碎成渣。\n\n你不在的时候我四处打听过，发现城里有位探险者协会的成员——那是一群赫赫有名的考古学家。要是我们有什么办法能让这些器物为接下来的旅程做好准备，也许他们能分享些诀窍给我们。",dEN="Though they may look fine to a regular person, any expert can see the damage these poor things have sustained.\n\nIn their current condition, I’m not sure they would survive any kind of journey without crumbling to pieces.\n\nWhile you were gone, I asked around and discovered that a member of the Explorer’s League is in town, a band of renowned archaeologists. If there’s anything we can do to prepare these artifacts for the journey ahead, perhaps they have some wisdom they can share with us.",o="把一捆受损的遗物带给南海镇的探险者协会代表。",oEN="Take the bundle of damaged relics to the Explorer's League representative in Southshore.",p="你那儿拿的是什么？",pEN="What do ye got there?",c="以我的胡子起誓——！是哪个穴居人摆弄过这些宝贝？！\n\n<矮人嘟囔着，用责备的眼神看着你。>\n\n手笨是没办法的事……可要是你识相的话，就该对这些东西再上心一点！",cEN="By my beard-! What kind o’ trogg handled these beauties?!\n\n<The dwarf grumbles, eyeing you accusingly.>\n\nHeavy hands can’t be helped… but ye ought tae handle these with a bit more care if ye know what’s good for ye!"}
Q[255153]={d="好了，现在过来仔细听，我不想重复第二遍。\n\n我把这些东西放进了一个加固的箱子，用我能弄到的最好的衬垫裹好了。你最好别摔它、别晃它、别倒过来放、别扔它，除了像抱着你头生子一样抱着它，别的什么都不许做。听明白了吗？！\n\n你要把它送到很南边的米奈希尔港，交给考古学家弗拉冈古特。这一侧大陆上，我认识的敢指望把这些东西修复回来的，只有他一个。",dEN="Alright, now come here and listen close, I don’t want tae have to repeat myself.\n\nI’ve placed these things in a reinforced box, cushioned as best I could manage. Ye better not drop it, shake it, turn it upside down, throw it, or do anything other than carry it like it’s your firstborn child. Got it?!\n\nYer goin' to take it to Archeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor, far tae the south. He’s the only one I know on this side o’ the continent who’d even dare hope to recover these things.",o="把装满极脆弱遗物的箱子安全送到米奈希尔港的考古学家弗拉冈古特手中。",oEN="Deliver the box of very fragile relics safely to Archeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor.",p="我没等着有什么货送来啊……",pEN="I wasn't expecting a delivery...",c="哎呀，这难道不是个惊喜吗？\n\n符文桶跟我说他要去北方看看能找到什么的时候，我可没指望他能带回来什么，除了身上那身衣服和一个空空的酒钱袋子！\n\n话虽如此，我很高兴你把这些带来了。我觉得它们连场雷雨都挺不过去，更别说坐车在乡间颠簸了。",cEN="Well, isn't this a pleasant surprise?\n\nWhen Runebarrel told me he was going up north to see what he could find, I didn't expect him to return with anything but the clothes on his back and an empty drinking fund!\n\nThat being said, I'm glad you brought these to me. I can't think of them surviving a thunderstorm much less a cart ride through the countryside."}
Q[255154]={d="我无意冒犯，但像你这样的人实在不该摆弄这么脆弱的器物。\n\n话虽如此，我很乐意把它们从你手里接过来。\n\n不过，我也不想让你空手而归……请把这枚钱币带回去，交给我买下这些宝贝的那个人，然后你就可以走了。",dEN="I mean no offense, but your type shouldn't really be handling such fragile artifacts.\n\nThat being said, I'm more than happy to take them off your hands.\n\nNow, I don’t want you to walk away empty-handed... please take this coin back to the person I’m purchasing these beauties from, and you’re free to be on your way.",o="把考古学家的付款带回南海镇，交给历史学家温德尔。",oEN="Take the Archeologist's payment back to Historian Wendell in Southshore.",p="你回来了！可是……遗物呢？",pEN="You've returned! But... where are the relics?",c="<历史学家的脸色沉了下来，但他还是点了点头，表示理解。>\n\n我明白了，可惜我无法亲自守护它们的秘密，不过，能为我们这些麻烦换回一点报酬，我还是很高兴的。\n\n最重要的是，这些器物安然无恙。\n\n也许有一天我会在展柜里见到它们……",cEN="<The Historian's face falls but he nods his head, understanding.>\n\nI see, it's unfortunate that I could not be the one to safeguard their mysteries myself, but still, I am glad to have some sort of payment for our troubles.\n\nMost importantly however, the artifacts are safe.\n\nPerhaps I'll see them on display someday..."}
Q[255155]={p="既然战局开始扭转，我终于能重新考虑些别的事了。阿拉索城区烧毁时，我们几乎失去了一切。\n\n衣物、寝具、玩具……我还能做更多，但没有布料就做不成。如果你有富余的魔纹布，我会非常感激。",pEN="Now that the tide of the battle is starting to turn, I can finally think of other matters again. We lost almost everything when the Arathor district burned.\n\nClothes, bedding, toys...I can make more, but not without fabric. If you have any Mageweave to spare, I'd be very grateful.",c="谢谢你。你真是慷慨。我一定会好好利用这些东西。",cEN="Thank you. This is very generous of you. I'll be sure to put it all to good use."}
Q[255156]={p="<name>，能在这儿见到你总是很高兴。你真露面的时候他们反倒有点害羞，可孩子们总在念叨你。\n\n我们还缺更多布料。如果你有符文布想要出手，我很乐意接手。",pEN="<name>, it's always good to see you around. They're a bit shy when you actually show up, but kids are always talking about you.\n\nWe could still use more fabric. If you have any Runecloth to part with, I'd be glad to take it off your hands.",c="这真是帮了大忙。我会尽快把全都用上。",cEN="This will be a great help. I'll be putting it all to use as fast as I can."}
Q[255157]={p="我们就快能从女儿家搬出来了，可我总觉得还需要更多布料。如果你手头有多余用不上的，这里能派上不少用场。",pEN="We're close to being ready to move out of my daughter's home, but I always seem to need more fabric. If you find yourself with more you don't need, it will find plenty of use here.",c="谢谢你一直帮助我们。但愿我能给你更多，可眼下我能给的只有感谢。希望这足够了。",cEN="Thank you for continuing to help us. I wish I could offer more, but all I can give you for now is my thanks. I hope that's enough."}
Q[255158]={p="见到你总是很高兴，<name>。总能听到你的名字——那位找回托尔卡拉尔的英雄。\n\n战斗还没结束，但我们终于占了上风。不过，路障用的木料快用完了。如果你有富余的林地木板，我很乐意收下。",pEN="Always good to see you, <name>. I hear your name a lot, the hero who recovered Trol'kalar.\n\nThe battle's not over, but we've been able to finally take the upper hand. We're running low on wood for the barricade though. If you've got any Grovewood Planks to spare, I'd be glad to take them.",c="这真是帮了大忙。有了这些，我们应该能让这道路障再多撑一阵子。\n\n但愿圣光眷顾我们，撑到不再需要它的那一天。谢谢你。",cEN="This will be a tremendous help. We should be able to make this barricade hold a while longer with this.\n\nIf the Light favors us any, longer enough to stop needing it. Thank you."}
Q[255159]={p="路障还撑得不错，不过随着战局开始转变，我也真的开始听到人们在谈论未来。这也许有点乐观，可经历了这一切，也许我们都需要一点乐观。所以我也开始琢磨这些事。\n\n等我们彻底清剿掉辛迪加，让城堡恢复昔日荣光还有一大堆活要干，我们会需要大量建筑材料。所以，万一你手头恰好有富余的林地木料，我们很快就会有更多需求。",pEN="Barricade's still holding well, but with the battle starting to take a turn, I'm starting to actually hear talk about the future. It might be a bit optimistic, but after everything, maybe some optimism is what we all need. So, I've started giving it some thought too.\n\nOnce we route out the Syndicate, we'll have plenty of other work ahead to get the keep back to its former glory, and we'll need a lot of building materials. So if you have happen to find yourself with more Grovewood to spare, we'll have plenty more need for it soon enough.",c="总有一天，我希望你能回到这里，看看一座名副其实的激流堡。\n\n谢谢你付出的一切努力。",cEN="One day, I hope you'll come back here to see a proper Stormgarde.\n\nThank you for all your efforts."}
Q[265001]={d="在你领取宝箱之前，Project-Ascension 的员工想向你致以最诚挚的感谢。\n\n你的支持对我们意义重大，让我们能够继续把飞升做得尽可能出色。\n\n你的贡献是服务器的命脉，我们的感激之情永远不够。\n\n希望你喜欢自己的购买，并享受一段美妙的游戏时光。\n\n此致，\nProject-Ascension 员工团队",dEN="Before you accept your chest, the Staff at Project-Ascension would like to extend our heartfelt gratitude.\n\nYour support means the world to us and empowers us to continue making Ascension as great as possible.\n\nYour contributions are the lifeblood of the server and our appreciation can never be overstated.\n\nWe hope you enjoy your purchase and have an amazing time playing.\n\nRegards\nThe Project-Ascension Staff",o="完成任务以领取你的赛季支持者宝箱。",oEN="Complete the quest to accept your Seasonal Supporter Chest."}
Q[265002]={d="在你领取宝箱之前，Project-Ascension 的员工想向你致以最诚挚的感谢。\n\n你的支持对我们意义重大，让我们能够继续把飞升做得尽可能出色。\n\n你的贡献是服务器的命脉，我们的感激之情永远不够。\n\n希望你喜欢自己的购买，并享受一段美妙的游戏时光。\n\n此致，\nProject-Ascension 员工团队",dEN="Before you accept your chest, the Staff at Project-Ascension would like to extend our heartfelt gratitude.\n\nYour support means the world to us and empowers us to continue making Ascension as great as possible.\n\nYour contributions are the lifeblood of the server and our appreciation can never be overstated.\n\nWe hope you enjoy your purchase and have an amazing time playing.\n\nRegards\nThe Project-Ascension Staff",o="完成任务即可领取你的赛季冒险者宝箱。",oEN="Complete the quest to accept your Seasonal Adventurers Chest."}
