Q[1650000]={d="<你感到口袋被轻轻一扯。有人悄悄塞进了一封折叠好、未署名的亲笔信。>\n\n务必谨慎。\n\n你在对抗巫妖王之战中的功绩从未被遗忘。正因如此，也因无数其他功勋，你被选中执行一项最高机密的任务。\n\n阿尔萨斯陨落后的十年和平即将终结。与部落的战争不可避免，但这并不意味着我们必须在众目睽睽之下开战。\n\n前往暴风城码头，与瓦爾迪尔交谈。他会让你了解这次行动的详情。\n\n为了王国的安全。",dEN="<You feel a tug at your pocket. Someone has slipped in a folded, unsigned handwritten letter.>\n\nBe discreet.\n\nYour service in the war against the Lich King has not been forgotten. For that, and for countless other merits, you’ve been chosen for a mission of the highest secrecy.\n\nThe ten years of peace since Arthas fell are coming to an end. War with the Horde is inevitable, but that doesn’t mean we need to fight it in plain sight.\n\nMake your way to the Stormwind Docks and speak with Valdior. He’ll bring you up to speed on the operation.\n\nFor the safety of the realm.",o="在暴风城码头寻找寄信人。",oEN="Find the sender at the Stormwind Docks.",p="人类 Grand Alliance 的子民肩上，压着多少悲伤啊。",pEN="How much sorrow weighs upon the shoulders of the people of the Grand Alliance.",c="<看到你手中的信，瓦爾迪尔唇边泛起一丝自豪的微笑。>\n\n原来你就是那种在他人沉睡时依然清醒的人。少数不愿将就于一个破碎世界的人之一，深知和平不过是那些怯于战斗者的避难所。\n\n正因如此，你才被召来。\n相关",cEN="<A proud smile tugs at Valdior’s lips as he catches sight of the letter in your hand.>\n\nSo you’re one of those who wake while others sleep. One of the few who won’t settle for a broken world, who know that peace is a shelter for those too afraid to fight.\n\nThat’s exactly why you’ve been summoned.\nRelated"}
Q[1650001]={d="请原谅我失礼；我叫瓦爾迪尔。\n\n我想你已经见过那艘被烧毁的船了。它正从阿扎尔群岛返航时遭到部落袭击；\n这只是一长串挑衅中的又一次侮辱。\n\n这些是即将到来之战的最初震颤。一场联盟若没有像你这样的士兵就无法承担的战争。\n\n我们当然有计划……但在透露任何细节之前，我希望你先花点时间：在码头走走，和人们谈谈。你会发现街上的气氛，与你此行的紧迫感如出一辙。",dEN="Pardon my manners—my name is Valdior.\n\nI assume you've already seen the burned ship. It was returning from the Azzar Archipelago when the Horde struck;\nanother insult in a long list of provocations.\n\nThese are the first tremors of the war to come. A war the Alliance cannot afford to fight without soldiers like you.\n\nWe do have a plan, of course… but before I share any details, I’d like you to take a moment: walk the docks, talk to the people. You’ll see that the mood in the streets matches the urgency that brought you here.",o="在暴风城码头聆听灾难目击者的讲述。",oEN="Listen to those witnessing the disaster at the Stormwind docks.",p="民众的呼声绝非无谓的低语；最好还是听一听。",pEN="The people's outcry is not just a mere murmur—it is best to listen.",c="现在你看清了吗？过去十年所谓的和平，不过是一场幻象。\n\n这个世界容不下我们所有人。\n\n兽人？他们已经将这座城市夷为平地一次了。那是一场屠杀。但我们该感到意外吗？他们的心脏跳动着恶魔之血。\n\n被遗忘者？说实话吧：赐予他们曾被剥夺的安葬，已经算是一种仁慈了。\n\n在部落里，你要不是野蛮人，就是恶棍。\n相关",cEN="Do you see it now? The so-called peace of the last ten years was nothing but a mirage.\n\nThere’s no room for all of us in this world.\n\nThe orcs? They've already razed this city once. It was a bloodbath. But should we be surprised? Their hearts beat with demon blood.\n\nThe Forsaken? Let’s be honest—granting them the burial they were once denied would be an act of mercy.\n\nIn the Horde, if you’re not a savage, you’re a villain.\nRelated"}
Q[1650002]={d="部落在这座城里安插了耳目。那些耳目听到了与你同样的愤怒。\n\n他们知道联盟的雄狮正从漫长的沉睡中苏醒。\n\n他们或许没探到什么出乎意料的东西，但无论如何，他们逗留得太久了。\n\n想来点实际行动吗？\n\n干掉那些多管闲事的渣滓。你会明白，向那些早已抛弃人性的怪物举起武器是多么容易。",dEN="The Horde has ears in this city. Ears that hear the same outrage you feel.\n\nThey know the lion of the Alliance is waking from its long slumber.\n\nThey may not have learned anything they didn’t suspect, but they’ve overstayed their welcome all the same.\n\nCare for a little action?\n\nCut down that meddling filth. You’ll see how easy it is to raise your weapon against monsters who long ago cast off their humanity.",o="消灭 9 名部落叛逃间谍。",oEN="Eliminate 9 renegade spies of The Horde.",p="如果部落一定要听到什么……那就让他们听到我们的怒吼。",pEN="If the Horde must hear something… let it be our roar.",c="你有着英雄的资质，<name>。你甚至算是帮了那些亡灵潜行者一个忙，让他们死了。\n\n遗憾的是，这个港口永远不够安全，不足以让我把所负的任务托付给你。\n\n我们需要一个更安静的地方。\n相关",cEN="You are made of the stuff of heroes, <name>. You’ve even done the deathstalkers a favor by killing them.\n\nSadly, this harbor will never be safe enough to trust you with the mission I’m carrying.\n\nWe’ll need a quieter place.\nRelated"}
Q[1650003]={d="<name>，你可曾有幸参观过暴风城的下水道？我猜没有；你闻起来太干净了。\n\n等我们进去之后，我再把细节告诉你。\n\n当然，自从上次那起……事件之后，港口和下水道的卫兵都异常警觉。但总有办法赢得他们的……配合，这么说吧。\n\n想要点提示吗？昨天靠岸的那艘船运来了一批阿扎尔群岛最好的烈酒。去找约翰·冈威兹，他知道怎么不引人注意地溜进货舱。弄到一箱酒瓶，足够软化卫兵的决心。",dEN="<name>, have you ever had the pleasure of visiting Stormwind's sewers? I doubt it; you smell far too clean.\n\nI'll fill you in on the details once we're inside.\n\nOf course, ever since the last... incident, the harbor and sewer guards have been unusually watchful. But there's always ways to earn their... cooperation, let's say.\n\nWant a hint? The ship that docked yesterday brought in a fine shipment of the best liquor from the Azzar Archipelago. Find John Gunwhiz, he'll know how to slip into the hold without drawing attention. Get your hands on a crate of bottles, enough to soften up the guards' resolve.",o="潜入船的货舱。",oEN="Sneak into the ship's hold.",c="<约翰·冈威兹打量着装满酒瓶的箱子，露出一丝赞许的微笑。>\n\n这才像话。\n相关",cEN="<John Gunwhiz eyes the crate full of bottles and cracks a faint, approving smile.>\n\nThat's more like it.\nRelated"}
Q[1650004]={d="<约翰·冈威兹拿起一个酒瓶，眯起眼睛读着标签，念出声来：>\n\n\"凋歌甘露。纯正阿扎尔药剂。\"啊哈。\"幸福，只在一口之遥。\"完美。\n\n<当他看到磨损标签上那位衣着清凉的精灵画像时，眼睛不由睁大了。>\n\n阿尔达拉可真会推销酒。\n\n<他猛地一拧，打开一瓶。浓烈的酒香在他重新塞上软木塞之前就扑鼻而来。>\n\n这酒够烈，足以让卫兵们满意。来，把瓶子拿上。瓦爾迪尔会在里面等你，就在下面的下水道里。",dEN="<John Gunwhiz grabs a bottle and squints at the label, reading aloud:>\n\n\"Wiltedsong Ambrosia. Pure Azzar Elixir.\" Aha. \"Happiness, one sip away.\" Perfect.\n\n<His eyelids lift as he spots the image of a scantily clad elf on the worn label.>\n\nAldara sure knows how to sell a drink.\n\n<With a fierce twist he opens a bottle. The sharp aroma of the liquor hits your nose before he corks it shut again.>\n\nThat’s strong enough to keep the guards happy. Here, take the bottles. Valdior will be waiting for you inside, down in the sewers.",o="弄到一个空箱子，收集 6 瓶阿扎尔烈酒。然后，把酒瓶交给暴风城下水道的卫兵。将阿扎尔烈酒交给暴风城下水道的卫兵。",oEN="Get a empty crate and gather 6 bottles of Azzar alcohol. Then, deliver bottles to the guards in the Stormwind Sewers. Deliver bottles of Azzar's Alcohol to the Stormwind Sewers guards.",p="别搞错了——像这样潮湿的地方，可挡不住人们想开一瓶好酒的念头。",pEN="Make no mistake—a damp place like this doesn’t take away the desire to uncork a good bottle.",c="我就知道你能做到，<name>。而且我看你已经荣幸地见过娜莉亚同志了。太好了，非常好。\n\n欢迎来到暴风城下水道，在这里，霉味与死水的气味，与那些在黑暗中如鱼得水之人的低语交织在一起。\n\n进来吧。",cEN="I knew you had it in you, <name>. And I see you’ve already had the pleasure of meeting Comrade Nalia. Excellent—very good.\n\nWelcome to the Stormwind Sewers, where the stench of mold and stagnant water mixes with the whispers of those who thrive in the dark.\n\nGo on in.\nRelated"}
Q[1650005]={d="欢迎来到下水道，<name>。你在寻找答案吗？一言既出，驷马难追：\n\n我受命组建一支小型私掠船队的船员。我们的目的地，正是你劫掠的那艘船所来自的那片被诅咒的群岛：\n\n阿扎尔。\n\n除非我想被割掉舌头，否则我只能说这么多。如果你想知道行动的细节，就得让玛拉·赤刃对你刮目相看。\n\n这么说吧，她喜欢亲自评判新兵。我警告你：她是个无情的裁判。",dEN="Welcome to the sewers, <name>. Looking for answers? A promise is a promise:\n\nI’ve been tasked with putting together the crew of a small corsair fleet. Our destination is the same cursed archipelago the ship you looted came from:\n\nAzzar.\n\nThat’s as much as I can tell you—unless I want to lose my tongue. If you want the details of the operation, you’ll need to impress Mara Crimson-Edged.\n\nLet’s just say she likes to judge new recruits personally. And fair warning—she’s a harsh judge.",o="在下水道与玛拉接头。",oEN="Contact Mara in the Sewers.",c="<玛拉眼中闪过一抹无声的赞许。>\n\n看来你是径直走进蛛网里来的。\n\n很好。\n相关",cEN="<A flicker of silent approval sparks in Mara’s eyes.>\n\nLooks like you’ve walked straight into the web.\n\nGood.\nRelated"}
Q[1650006]={d="那么……你觉得自己有用了？\n\n是的，我有件事你能应付。\n\n你大概已经猜到了，码头挤满间谍绝非偶然。有人给他们通风报信了。而我们知道那个人就在这下边。\n\n无论如何，下水道的老鼠总是清楚这座臭气熏天的迷宫里发生的一切。\n\n去逼他们。\n\n恐吓所有必要的人，直到有人崩溃，把我们需要的东西交出来。你还不至于娇气到干不了这种活，对吧？",dEN="So... Feeling useful?\n\nYeah, I’ve got something you can handle.\n\nAs you’ve probably guessed, it’s no coincidence the docks are crawling with spies. Someone tipped them off. And we know that someone is down here.\n\nOne way or another, the sewer-rats always know what’s happening in this reeking maze.\n\nLean on them.\n\nIntimidate as many as it takes until one cracks and gives us what we need. You’re not too delicate for that kind of work, are you?",o="从下水道的流浪汉那里获取必要情报。",oEN="Obtain the necessary information from the sewer vagabonds.",p="我要求你做的事并不愉快，但却必不可少。",pEN="What I ask of you is not pleasant, but it is necessary.",c="我一直知道贾齐尔在玩火，但从没想过他真有胆量做出如此鲁莽的事。\n\n<玛拉的脸沉了下来。>\n\n他背叛了我们的信任，越过了一条无法回头的界线，为部落敞开了大门。\n\n这件事绝不会没有惩罚。\n相关",cEN="I always knew Jaszir was playing with fire, but I never thought he’d have the guts to try something this reckless.\n\n<Mara's face hardens.>\n\nHe betrayed our trust. Crossed a line he can’t uncross. He opened the door to the Horde.\n\nThat won’t go unpunished.\nRelated"}
Q[1650007]={d="贾齐尔不是军情七处打交道的第一个双面间谍，也不是第一个自以为能耍弄我们却不必付出代价的人。\n\n无论部落给了他什么——黄金、承诺、恩惠——等你替我们伸张正义之后，都将变得毫无意义。\n\n你会在逃犯围栏找到他。\n\n把他的头带给我。",dEN="Jaszir’s not the first double agent the SI:7 has worked with, and not the first who thought he could play us without paying the price.\n\nWhatever the Horde gave him—gold, promises, favors—it won’t mean a thing once you’ve delivered our justice.\n\nYou’ll find him at the Fugitive’s Stockade.\n\nBring me his head.",o="杀死前成员贾齐尔，把他的头带给玛拉。",oEN="Kill the former member Jaszir and bring his head to Mara.",p="贾齐尔必须为自己的所作所为付出代价。",pEN="Jaszir must answer for his actions.",c="<你交出贾希尔的头颅，它依然温热，滴着血。玛拉单手掂了掂它，目光始终没有离开地精那毫无生气的眼睛，说道：>\n\n这就是等待我们敌人的下场。\n\n干得好。\n相关",cEN="<You hand over Jaszir’s head, still warm and dripping with blood. Mara weighs it in one hand and, without breaking eye contact with the goblin’s lifeless stare, says:>\n\nThis is the fate that awaits our enemies.\n\nWell done.\nRelated"}
Q[1650008]={d="几年前，一群暴风城地牢的囚犯挖出一条隧道逃了出去，却发现自己来到了一处比牢房更加悲惨的地方。\n\n他们在那里搭建的临时避难所至今仍窝藏着不少逃犯。其中一些是贾希尔的朋友。\n\n我怀疑他可能向他们透露过机密情报……以防万一我们察觉。\n\n你猜得到接下来是什么，对吧？\n\n我们需要传个口信。响亮而清楚。\n\n杀死几只下水道的老鼠，这世界连眼睛都不会眨一下，<name>。",dEN="A few years ago, a group of prisoners from the Stormwind dungeons managed to dig a tunnel out, only to find themselves in a place even more miserable than their cells.\n\nThe makeshift shelter they built down there still houses a fair number of fugitives. Friends of Jaszir, some of them.\n\nI suspect he may have shared sensitive intel with them... just in case we caught on.\n\nYou can guess what comes next, right?\n\nWe need to send a message. Loud and clear.\n\nThe world won’t bat an eye if you kill a few sewer rats, <name>.",o="在下水道消灭 7 名监狱逃犯。",oEN="Eliminate 7 Stockade Fugitives in the Sewers.",p="贾希尔的秘密绝不能见光。",pEN="Jaszir's secrets must never see the light of day.",c="别为他们的死失眠。任何一个有点价值的逃犯，都早就在为瓦爾迪爾和抵抗军做事了。\n\n我们做了该做的事。\n相关",cEN="Don’t lose sleep over their deaths. Any fugitive worth a damn is already working for Valdior and the Defiance.\n\nWe did what needed to be done.\nRelated"}
Q[1650009]={d="也许贾希尔比我以为的更大胆，但更聪明？绝无可能。他一定留下过某种线索，指向他在部落中的接头人。\n\n搜寻任何能揭示他所知情形的文件。我需要知道他了解得多深……以及泄露了多少。\n\n找到他的日志，或任何与他有关的东西，带来给我。",dEN="Maybe Jaszir was bolder than I gave him credit for, but smarter? Not a chance. He must’ve left some kind of trail pointing to his contact in the Horde.\n\nSearch for any documents that might shed light on what he knew. I need to know how deep his knowledge went… and how much he gave away.\n\nFind his journal, or anything tied to him, and bring it to me.",o="搜寻并收集可能影响计划的文件。",oEN="Search for and collect documents that may affect the plan.",p="你拿到贾希尔的日志和我们一直在找的文件了吗？",pEN="Do you have Jaszir’s journal and the documents we were looking for?",c="<Mara hojea los papeles de Jaszir>.\n\n管道与隧道的图纸……关于入口与出口的笔记……\n\n那该死的地精。\n\n这是我们的错——我们本该把他拴得更紧些。\n\n无所谓。这次小小背叛的后果，我会亲自处理。\n相关",cEN="<Mara flips through Jaszir’s papers.>\n\nSchematics of the pipes and tunnels… notes about the entrances and exits…\n\nThat damned goblin.\n\nThis is on us—we should’ve kept him on a shorter leash.\n\nNo matter. I’ll deal with the fallout from this little betrayal myself.\nRelated"}
Q[1650010]={d="看来上级对你的评价没错。你做得很好。\n\n你已经赢得了见我其余部下的资格。他们会把行动的完整细节告诉你。\n\n去酒馆找瓦爾迪爾。告诉他赤刃已经给予了祝福。",dEN="Looks like the higher-ups were right about you. You did well.\n\nYou’ve earned the right to meet the rest of my division. They’ll give you the full breakdown of the operation.\n\nFind Valdior at the tavern. Tell him Crimson-Edged has given her blessing.",o="向瓦爾迪爾报到。",oEN="Present yourself to Valdior.",p="瓦爾迪爾该为把你丢给玛拉处置而向你道歉。",pEN="Valdior should apologize for leaving you to your fate with Mara.",c="你来是为了寻找答案，但我的出现恐怕会带来更多疑问。\n\n别怕。我们为军情七处和联盟效力。很快，你就会明白你需要知道的一切。\n\n欢迎来到暗影，<name>。\n相关",cEN="You came looking for answers— but my presence will likely raise even more questions.\n\nFear not. We serve the SI:7 and the Alliance. Soon, you’ll understand everything you need to.\n\nWelcome to The Shade, <name>.\nRelated"}
Q[1650011]={d="我们是暗影，军情七处的一支精锐力量。我们负责联盟最微妙——也最肮脏——的工作。那些无法见光的事。\n\n眼下正在发生的事——由瓦爾迪爾领导的近海打击任务——正是遵循这一理念。对部落发起一次突然而致命的打击。\n\n但在你踏入风暴之前，你需要明白我们为何这样做……以及代价是什么。\n\n仔细听。",dEN="We are The Shade, an elite arm of the SI:7. We handle the Alliance’s most delicate—and dirtiest—work. The things that can’t be done in the light.\n\nWhat’s happening now—the offshore strike mission, led by Valdior—follows that exact philosophy. A sudden, decisive blow against the Horde.\n\nBut before you step into the storm, you need to understand why we’re doing this… and what it’ll cost.\n\nListen closely.",o="倾听这次行动背后的理由。",oEN="Listen to the reasons behind the operation.",c="让我们在部落的船只抵达阿扎尔之前就把它们击沉。\n\n既然诺森德已出局，谁赢得地精的青睐，谁就掌控北方。而若北方属于我们……部落与被遗忘者就将任凭我们处置。\n\n你说呢？很激动人心，对吧？\n\n<Valdior saca pecho con orgullo>.\n\n既然你已经知情，那就开工吧。\n相关",cEN="Let’s sink the Horde’s ships before they ever reach Azzar.\n\nWith Northrend out of the picture, whoever wins the goblins’ favor controls the North. And if the North is ours… the Horde—and the Forsaken—will be at our mercy.\n\nWhat do you say? Exciting, isn’t it?\n\n<Valdior puffs out his chest with pride.>\n\nNow that you’re in the loop, let’s get to work.\nRelated"}
Q[1650012]={d="恭喜，正式通知你：你刚刚填补了「抵抗号」前往阿扎尔的船员名单上最后一个空缺。\n\n不过……在启航之前，还有几桩尾巴要收拾。\n\n我的忠实伙伴阿拉里克——一位颇具魔法声望的高等精灵——本该处理下水道里某桩……财务事宜。你当然明白，这次行动可不会自己掏钱，总有些债要收。\n\n遗憾的是，我一直没有他的消息。能否劳烦你去确认一下一切都还顺利？",dEN="Congratulations, it’s official: you’ve just filled the last open spot on the Defiance’s crew bound for Azzar.\n\nHowever... before we set sail, there are a few loose ends to tie up.\n\nMy loyal associate Alaric—a high elf of considerable magical repute—was supposed to take care of a certain... financial matter down in the sewers. You understand, of course, this operation doesn’t fund itself, and some debts need collecting.\n\nUnfortunately, I haven’t heard from him. Would you be so kind as to make sure everything’s in order?",o="在暴风城下水道寻找阿拉里克。",oEN="Search for Alaric in the Stormwind Sewers.",c="嗯嗯……嗯嗯嗯嗯。嗯嗯嗯嗯嗯！\n\n<阿拉里克飞快地点头，眼睛睁得大大的、闪闪发亮，仿佛在绝望地试图传达某件显而易见的事。>\n\n嗯嗯嗯，嗯嗯嗯嗯。嗯……嗯嗯嗯嗯！\n相关",cEN="Mmhm... mmmhhhmm. Mmmmhmmmm!\n\n<Alaric nods rapidly, eyes wide and glittering, as if desperately trying to communicate something glaringly obvious.>\n\nMmmhmm, mmmmhhh. Mmm... mhmmmm!\nRelated"}
Q[1650013]={d="那么……你见过那个话痨精灵了？我明白了。\n\n可怜的家伙，中了沉默法术。我也许能逆转它、解除诅咒，但我需要三种半魔法成分来提取他的精华，调配出合适的解药。\n\n对我们来说幸运的是，这些都能在下水道里找到。\n\n给我带来：蟑螂汁、富含钙质的软泥，以及一片被感染的侏儒脚趾甲。",dEN="So... you’ve met this chatterbox of an elf? I see.\n\nPoor thing’s been hit with a silence spell. I might be able to reverse it and lift the curse, but I’ll need three semi-magical components to extract their essence and brew a proper antidote.\n\nFortunately for us, they can all be found right here in the sewers.\n\nBring me: Cockroach juice, Calcium-rich ooze and one infected gnome toenail.",o="取得蟑螂汁、富含钙质的黏液和被感染的侏儒指甲。然后，取得塞雷莎的药剂。",oEN="Get Cockroach Juice, Calcium-Rich Viscosity, and Infected Gnome Nail. Then, get Cereza’s potion.",p="嗯嗯嗯嗯嗯……嗯嗯！",pEN="Mmmmmmm… mmmhh!",c="<阿拉里克喝了一口药剂，立刻干呕起来，剧烈地呕吐。>\n\n真恶心！<他狠狠地向地上吐了一口。>\n\n就算在这里，一句赞美也会让你闭嘴！我不过是向几位迷人的女士说了几句好话，谁知道，我偏偏撞上了塞雷莎。一个瞪眼，一个手势，砰——被诅咒了。\n\n<阿拉里克又吐了一口，浑身发抖。>\n\n不过……谢谢你。我欠你一次。\n相关",cEN="<Alaric takes a sip of the potion and immediately gags, retching hard.>\n\nFoul! <He spits violently onto the floor.>\n\nEven here, they silence you for a compliment! I merely offered a few kind words to a group of charming ladies, and wouldn’t you know it, I crossed paths with Cereza. One glare, one gesture, and boom—cursed.\n\n<Alaric spits again, shuddering.>\n\nStill… thank you. I owe you.\nRelated"}
Q[1650014]={d="<阿拉里克在椅子上扭动，捂着肚子，一脸痛苦。>\n\n塞雷莎的药剂把我的胃彻底毁了……\n\n我不确定瓦爾迪爾有没有提过我在忙什么，但在那老巫婆夺走我的声音之前，我正要去收干涸居所的欠租，并付钱给一位名叫银溪的贵族，他正在墓穴入口附近等着。\n\n以我现在的状态，我……不太可靠。你介意替我跑一趟吗？",dEN="<Alaric writhes in his chair, clutching his stomach with a grimace of pain.>\n\nCereza’s potion has utterly wrecked my stomach...\n\nI’m not sure if Valdior mentioned what I was working on, but before the old crone snatched my voice, I was headed to collect back rent from the Dry Dwellings and repay a noble named Silverbrook, who’s waiting near the crypt entrance.\n\nIn my current state, I’m... less than reliable. Would you mind handling it for me?",o="向所有租户收取租金，并结清与那位贵族的债务。",oEN="Collect the rent payments from all the tenants and settle the debt with the noble.",p="<尸体已经失去了所有温度。>",pEN="<The corpse has lost all trace of warmth.>",c="<就在通往暴风城大教堂的墓穴正前方，一具衣着考究的人类尸体摊在地上，他的珠宝闪烁着 unmistakable 的贵族气派。毫无疑问：这就是那位贵族银溪，阿拉里克本该与他见面结清债务的人。>\n\n<凑近查看，你注意到散落的咬痕和深深的抓痕。致命伤似乎是被撕开的颈动脉。>\n\n<你琢磨着该如何处理收来的租金……但毫无疑问——那些金币对你比对一个死人更有用。>\n相关",cEN="<Right in front of the crypts that connect to Stormwind Cathedral, the body of a well-dressed human lies sprawled on the ground, his jewelry gleaming with unmistakable noble flair. There's no doubt—this is the noble Silverbrook, the one Alaric was supposed to meet to settle the debt.>\n\n<On closer inspection, you notice scattered bite marks and deep scratches. The fatal blow seems to be a torn-open jugular.>\n\n<You wonder what to do with the rent payments you've collected... but there's no question — that gold will serve you better than it will a dead man.>\nRelated"}
Q[1650015]={d="<阿拉里克的奥术投影闪烁了一下，仿佛被难以置信惊呆了。>\n\n银溪？不……不，这不可能。我怎么能这么倒霉？\n\n<影像微微变暗。>\n\n集中精神，阿拉里克。\n\n无论这是谁干的，都可能危及整个行动。对。我们得调查这些墓穴。查明发生了什么。处理这个威胁。\n\n嗯……说\"我们\"可能有点夸张。应该由你去做。你已经在下面了——至少是血肉之躯在下面。一旦你发现什么，直接回来找我。",dEN="<Alaric’s arcane projection flickers briefly, as if stunned by disbelief.>\n\nSilverbrook? No... no, this can’t be. How can I be so unlucky?\n\n<The image dims slightly.>\n\nFocus, Alaric.\n\nWhoever did this could jeopardize the entire operation. Yes. We need to investigate the crypts. Find out what happened. Deal with the threat.\n\nWell... “we” might be a stretch. You should do it. You’re already down there—at least, in the flesh. Once you find anything, come straight back to me.",o="铲除下水道墓穴中的威胁，并查明其来源。",oEN="Eradicate the threat in the Sewers' Crypts and uncover its origin.",p="你发现了什么？",pEN="What have you discovered?",c="<阿拉里克听你讲述墓穴中的见闻，越来越不安。在附近偷听的塞雷莎似乎同样心神不宁。>\n\n这比我担心的更糟。如果那个死灵法师的计划已经启动，下水道……不，整个暴风城，都可能陷入极大的危险。\n相关",cEN="<Alaric listens to your account of the crypts with growing unease. Cereza, eavesdropping nearby, seems just as disturbed.>\n\nThis is worse than I feared. If the necromancer’s plan is already in motion, the sewers—no, all of Stormwind—could be in grave danger.\nRelated"}
Q[1650016]={d="<塞雷莎翻着桌上的文件，神情阴沉。>\n\n如果他的计划是把瘟疫药剂武器化……我们没时间可以浪费了。\n\n<name>，我需要你深入下水道更深处。如果遇到任何药剂师——杀了他们。全部杀光。并在瘟疫罐被引爆之前摧毁它们。\n\n<塞雷莎用沉稳的手递给你一个空瓶。>\n\n就算它们还没有炸开，瘟疫也可能已经渗入管道。取一份水样，带给德鲁伊埃尔德林。如果我们的担忧属实……他会知道该怎么做。\n\n但愿如此。",dEN="<Cereza rifles through the papers on her table, her expression grim.>\n\nIf his plan was to weaponize blight charges... we don’t have time to waste.\n\n<name>, I need you to go deeper into the sewers. If you encounter any apothecaries—kill them. All of them. And destroy the blight canisters before they can be triggered.\n\n<Cereza hands you an empty vial with a steady hand.>\n\nEven if they haven’t gone off yet, the blight might already be seeping into the pipes. Take a water sample and bring it to Eldryn, the druid. If our fears are true... he’ll know what to do.\n\nI hope.",o="前往下水道深处，消灭药剂师，摧毁瘟疫药剂，并取得一份水样。",oEN="Head to the depths of the sewers, eliminate the apothecaries, destroy the Blight charges, and obtain a water sample.",p="暴风城的水源正处在危险之中。一小份样本就足以评估威胁的规模。",pEN="Stormwind’s waters are in danger. A small sample will be enough to assess the magnitude of the threat.",c="瘟疫……那毒药带来的从来只有苦难。你把样本带来给我是对的。让我们查清损害蔓延到了什么程度。\n相关",cEN="Blight... That poison has never brought anything but misery. You were right to bring me a sample. Let’s find out just how far the damage has spread.\nRelated"}
Q[1650017]={d="<埃尔德林仔细端详着那只瓶子。他轻轻点头，示意你跟上。>\n\n穿出这些墙壁的根系属于一棵灌注了奥术精华的树。所有树木都寄居着一个灵魂，某种心智——但这一棵……这一棵比大多数听得更敏锐。\n\n在我与它的根系沟通时，我要你把受污染的水滴几滴在根上。\n\n灵魂会感知到腐化——并权衡瘟疫的代价。",dEN="<Eldryn studies the vial carefully. With a slight nod, he gestures for you to follow.>\n\nThe roots breaching these walls belong to a tree infused with Arcane essence. All trees house a spirit, a mind of sorts—but this one… this one listens more sharply than most.\n\nWhile I commune with its roots, I want you to apply small drops of the contaminated water to them.\n\nThe spirit will sense the corruption—and weigh the cost of the blight.",o="把水样滴在奥术之树的根上。",oEN="Apply the water sample to the roots of the Arcane tree.",p="生命与奥术走着不同的道路，却都汇聚于同一个终点。",pEN="Life and the Arcane follow different paths, but both converge at the same destination.",c="<一丝疲惫的愁容打破了德鲁伊的平静。>\n\n这棵树的灵魂已经探查了下水道的深处。幸运的是，瘟疫的腐化并未扎根。\n\n然而……\n\n这种毒药它并不陌生。树木之间交换着低语……流言如同穿行小巷的商贩，顺着根系传递。我相信被遗忘者可能在暴风城附近藏有更多瘟疫。\n相关",cEN="<A wearied grimace breaks the druid’s calm demeanor.>\n\nThe spirit of the tree has probed the depths of the sewers. Fortunately, the blight’s corruption hasn’t taken hold.\n\nHowever...\n\nThis poison is not unknown to it. The trees exchange whispers... rumors that pass through their roots like traders through alleys. I believe the Forsaken may be hiding more blight near Stormwind.\nRelated"}
Q[1650018]={d="塞雷莎敏锐的直觉——以及你迅速的行动——让下水道免于瘟疫之害。但正如我所说，当我与那棵树的精华沟通时……我感到了某种令人不安的东西。\n\n这不是唯一一棵尝过被遗忘者毒药的树。\n\n如果还有另一处感染正在城中蔓延，我必须赶在它绽放之前追查到源头。\n\n把这些发现告诉塞雷莎。她会急于知道我们了解到的一切。",dEN="Cereza’s sharp instincts—and your swift action—have spared the sewers from the blight. But as I said, when I communed with the tree’s essence... I sensed something troubling.\n\nThis isn’t the only tree that’s tasted the Forsaken’s poison.\n\nIf there’s another infection spreading through the city, I must track its source before it blooms.\n\nShare these findings with Cereza. She’ll be eager to hear what we’ve learned.",o="向塞雷莎汇报埃尔德林的发现。",oEN="Report Eldryn's findings to Cereza.",c="谢谢你，<name>。如果不是你……\n\n<一阵寒意顺着老妇人的脊背爬过，她的身姿在岁月的重压下佝偻下去。>\n\n我相信德鲁伊会找到毒药的源头。在此期间，我会确保那些被解除的瘟疫罐完好无损地运出城去。\n相关",cEN="Thank you, <name>. If not for you...\n\n<A shiver runs down the old woman’s spine, her posture bending under the weight of the years.>\n\nI trust the druid will find the source of the poison. In the meantime, I’ll make sure the deactivated blight charges leave the city in one piece.\nRelated"}
Q[1650019]={d="我的得力助手是个叫拉胡德的侏儒。虽然我愿把性命托付给他……\n\n嗯，这话就我们之间说说：他偶尔会……辐射发作。事后会有点神志恍惚。\n\n这次任务，我让他负责收集、管理和运输我们的武器储备。你可以想象——我们可不是空着手去突袭部落的。\n\n你介意去看看拉胡德吗？确认一切仍在正轨上？",dEN="My right-hand man is a gnome named Lahud. And while I’d trust him with my life...\n\nWell, let’s keep this between us—he has the occasional... radioactive episode. Leaves him a little dazed.\n\nFor this mission, I put him in charge of gathering, managing, and transporting our weapons stockpile. You can imagine—we’re not storming the Horde empty-handed.\n\nWould you mind checking in on Lahud? Make sure everything’s still on track?",o="在暴风城下水道寻找拉胡德。",oEN="Look for Lahud in the Sewers of Stormwind.",c="嘿！看来我们现在是队友了，是吧？\n\n是瓦爾迪爾派你来的？他很明智。我感觉有点……头晕。\n相关",cEN="Hey there! Looks like we’re teammates now, huh?\n\nValdior sent you? Smart of him. I’m feeling a little... woozy.\nRelated"}
Q[1650020]={d="我正要去弹匠工厂取船员的武器装备，这时塞雷莎拦住了我。\n\n而且，嗯……拉胡德从不对塞雷莎说不。不，不。她为我们做了很多。\n\n你能帮我去电车坟场收集一些优质废料吗？她让我把它连同这张字条一起交给杜尔根。\n\n问题是……那地方到处都是拾荒者。更糟的是，我觉得辐射正把我的脑子像鸡蛋一样煎……",dEN="I was headed to the Bulletsmith Factory to pick up the crew’s weaponry when Cereza stopped me.\n\nAnd, well... Lahud never says no to Cereza. No, no. She’s done a lot for us.\n\nCould you help me gather some quality scrap from the tram graveyard? She asked me to bring it to Durgan along with this note.\n\nProblem is... the place is crawling with scavengers. And to top it off, I think the radiation’s cooking my brain like an egg...",o="从电车坟场收集 15 块贵重废料，交给暴风城下水道的杜尔根·弹匠。",oEN="Collect 15 Valuable Scraps from the tram graveyard and deliver them to Durgan Bulletsmith in the Stormwind Sewers.",p="欢迎来到弹匠工厂。",pEN="Welcome to the Bulletsmith Factory.",c="你是抵抗号那伙人里的？\n\n我记得你更矮……而且绿得多。\n\n<杜尔根沙哑地笑了一声，一边调了调一副小小的阅读镜，眯眼读着塞雷莎的字条。>\n\n啊，我明白了。塞雷莎……还有一笔让事情正式化的小钱。完美。\n相关",cEN="You with the Defiance crew?\n\nI remember you being shorter... and a lot greener.\n\n<Durgan barks a raspy laugh as he adjusts a pair of tiny reading specs and squints at Cereza’s note.>\n\nAh, I see. Cereza... and a little payment to make it official. Perfect.\nRelated"}
Q[1650021]={d="老家伙要武器。你带来的那些零件呢？足够完成订单还有富余。\n\n我马上开工。\n\n问题是……装配线拖拖拉拉。我不知道下面那些懒骨头怎么了，但如果我们想按时完成这批货，他们最好打起精神来。\n\n下到车间去，让他们动起来。一份点心、几句鼓励……或者狠狠踹一脚屁股；管用就行。\n\n哦，还有，完事后给我从桌上拿杯咖啡来，行吗？我也需要提提神。",dEN="The old cat wants weapons. And the parts you brought? More than enough to cover the order.\n\nI’ll get started right away.\n\nThing is... the assembly line’s dragging its feet. Not sure what’s gotten into those layabouts down there, but if we want this shipment done on time, they’d better get their act together.\n\nHead down to the floor and get them moving. A snack, a pep talk... or a good kick in the pants—whatever works.\n\nOh, and when you’re done, grab me a coffee from the table, will you? I need a little boost too.",o="用他们所要的东西唤醒工人们。然后，给杜尔根带一杯咖啡。",oEN="Wake up the workers by offering them whatever they ask for. Then, bring a coffee to Durgan.",p="我想听到机器全功率运转的轰鸣。",pEN="I want to feel the roar of the machinery running at full power.",c="干得好，把齿轮上的锈都抖掉了。订单已经跑起来了。\n\n告诉塞雷莎——或者你那位侏儒小朋友——等准备好了我们会通知他们。我们会把它放在老地方。\n相关",cEN="Nice work shaking the rust out of the gears. The order’s rolling now.\n\nTell Cereza—or your little gnome friend—that we’ll let them know when it’s ready. We’ll drop it off at the usual spot.\nRelated"}
Q[1650022]={d="「抵抗号」船员的武器装备？刚下生产线——随时可以出发。\n\n去工厂取你的货：霰弹枪、弹药、火药、炸药……你懂规矩。\n\n然后，把订单存根在会计的桌子上烧掉。总不能让任何人发现一场联盟行动在使用未登记武器，对吧？\n\n完事后在这里签上你的名字。<杜尔根粗壮的食指戳了戳桌上的一份文件。>\n\n最后一件事——直接向你的内线汇报。就是那个负责走私路线的姑娘。",dEN="The weaponry for The Defiance crew? Hot off the line—ready to go.\n\nPick up your shipment at the factory: shotguns, ammo, powder, explosives… You know the drill.\n\nThen burn the order slips on the accountants’ desks. Can’t have anyone finding out an Alliance op is using unclassified weaponry, right?\n\nJust scribble your name here when you’re done. <Durgan’s thick index finger jabs a document on the table.>\n\nAnd last thing—report straight to your mole. The girl running the smuggling route.",o="取走武器装备，销毁订单表格，完事后在杜尔根的文件上签字。",oEN="Pick up the armament, destroy the order forms, and when you're done, sign Durgan's document.",p="你拿到武器装备了吗？",pEN="Do you have the armament?",c="又是你。看来他们让你负责这批武器运输了。\n\n哦，顺便说一句；阿扎尔的酒太棒了。我迫不及待地想扬帆前往那片群岛，痛揍那些部落渣滓，再开一瓶凋歌为胜利干杯。\n相关",cEN="You again. They put you in charge of the weapons run, it seems.\n\nOh, and by the way; Azzar's booze was amazing. Can’t wait to sail for the archipelago, thrash some Horde scum, and toast the victory with another Wiltedsong bottle.\nRelated"}
Q[1650023]={d="大白天地把武器运过码头，赌注未免太大了。我们要这事悄无声息。\n\n计划是这样：把弹匠的武器藏进存放在下面下水道码头舱室里的密封板条箱，然后把它们扔进运河。水流会把它们从排水隧道带出去。\n\n「抵抗号」的码头工人会在另一头等着，悄悄把它们装上船。\n\n完事后，告诉那个侏儒一切顺利。",dEN="Hauling weapons across the docks in broad daylight would be pushing our luck. We want this quiet.\n\nHere’s the plan: stash the Bulletsmith armament in the sealed crates stored in the dock chamber down here in the sewers, and toss them into the canal. The current will carry them out through the drainage tunnel.\n\nThe Defiance’s dockhands are waiting on the other side to discreetly load them onto the ship.\n\nOnce it’s done, let the gnome know everything went smoothly.",o="把武器装备放进下水道码头舱室的密封板条箱，然后把它们扔进运河。",oEN="Place the armament in the sealed crates in the dock room in the sewers and throw them into the canal.",p="我们就要完成准备工作了！",pEN="We're about to finish the preparations!",c="货物已经在运往船上的路上了？我就知道你能办到！\n\n那么，我们这里也快完事了。\n相关",cEN="The shipment’s on its way to the ships? I knew you’d pull it off!\n\nWe’re almost done here, then.\nRelated"}
Q[1650024]={d="抵抗军的武器正在运输途中，塞雷莎的订单也在进行中……<拉胡德挠了挠他那颗绿色的大脑袋。>我想我的待办清单到此为止了！\n\n我欠你一声谢，所以……没错。谢谢！\n\n我会去码头和其他人会合，把最新情况告诉他们。你介意去告诉塞雷莎，她的委托现在已经在杜尔根·弹匠手上了吗？",dEN="The Defiance’s weapons are in transit, Cereza’s order is in motion... <Lahud scratches his large green head.> I think that wraps up my to-do list!\n\nI owe you a thanks, so... yeah. Thanks!\n\nI’ll meet up with the others at the docks and give them the update. Would you mind letting Cereza know her favor’s in Durgan Bulletsmith’s hands now?",o="与塞雷莎交谈。",oEN="Talk to Cereza.",c="可怜的拉胡德和他的头晕。至少他还明智地求助了。\n\n至于我托付给杜尔根的事……\n\n当你在下面待了像我这么多年，你就会明白联盟的根基其实有多脆弱。\n\n金字塔的底层——我们这一层——必须坚实。但它不会自己坚挺。需要力量，才能阻止它在那些使用它、榨取它的人脚下崩塌，直到什么都不剩。\n\n<塞雷莎向你露出一个罕见而真诚的微笑。>\n\n我的工作常常要流血。\n相关",cEN="Poor Lahud and his dizziness. At least he had the good sense to ask for help.\n\nAs for my request to Durgan…\n\nWhen you’ve spent as many years down here as I have, you learn just how fragile the Alliance’s foundations really are.\n\nThe bottom of the pyramid—our level—has to hold strong. But it doesn’t hold on its own. It takes force to keep it from collapsing under those who use it, exploit it, until there’s nothing left.\n\n<Cereza offers you a rare, genuine smile.>\n\nMy work often involves shedding blood.\nRelated"}
Q[1650025]={d="我……没料到会有这种规模的袭击。\n\n你在下面为我们立了大功，<name>。但我们现在还不能启航——除非收拾干净几桩尾巴。\n而我说的\"收拾\"，是指找根绳子，把我们敌人的残部吊起来。\n\n我会确保没有被遗忘者还潜伏在下水道里。你呢，穿过下方的管道前往码头，去找约翰·「枪智」，那位率领我们在「抵抗号」船员中突击队的吉尔尼斯佣兵。\n\n你会发现他和他的手下早已急不可耐。",dEN="I... didn’t see an attack of this scale coming.\n\nYou’ve done us a great service down here, <name>. But we can’t set sail just yet—not until we tie up a few loose ends.\nAnd by “tie” I mean find a rope and hang what’s left of our enemies.\n\nI’ll make sure no Forsaken are left lurking in the sewers. You, head to the docks through the lower pipe and speak to John ‘Gunwhiz’, the Gilnean mercenary leading our strike force within the Defiance crew.\n\nYou’ll find he and his men are more than eager to act.",o="沿着下方的管道离开下水道，在暴风城码头联系约翰·「枪智」。",oEN="Exit the sewers through the lower pipe and contact John 'Gunwhiz' at the Stormwind docks.",c="<约翰的双眼闪烁着掠食者般饥渴的光芒——凶猛、专注、渴望鲜血。>\n\n省下你的故事吧。德鲁伊已经告诉过我们了。我们知道部落的事。\n相关",cEN="<John’s eyes have the hungry gleam of a predator—feral, focused, itching for blood.>\n\nSpare me the story. The druid already filled us in. We know about the Horde.\nRelated"}
Q[1650026]={d="结果证明，德鲁伊的直觉和我手下的鼻子是绝配。我们刚找到了部落的基地。\n\n不过，你也能派上用场。敌人扎营在南边——沿着峭壁底部顺着海岸线走，很快就能找到他们。\n\n我的小伙子们已经出发了，一如既往地准备就绪。只要别挡他们的路，他们会欢迎你的帮助。\n\n命令很简单：杀。烧。砸。斩首。",dEN="Turns out the druid’s instincts and my men’s noses make a good team. We’ve just found the Horde’s base.\n\nStill, you can be of use. The enemy’s camped out to the south—follow the shoreline along the base of the cliffs and you’ll find them soon enough.\n\nMy boys are already on the move, ready as ever. Just stay out of their way, and they’ll welcome your help.\n\nOrders are simple: Kill. Burn. Smash. Decapitate.",o="消灭部落成员，烧毁船只，并解决海滩上部落营地的行动指挥官。",oEN="Eliminate the members of the Horde, burn the boats, and deal with the operations leader at the Horde camp on the beach.",p="不把部落从我们的海岸上彻底清除就启航，是鲁莽之举。",pEN="Setting sail without eradicating the Horde from our shores would be reckless.",c="你拥有「抵抗军」每一名成员都梦寐以求的勇气与本领\n\n目前，暴风城的海岸已经清除了部落的污秽，但这只是开始。\n\n很快，在阿扎尔的海域，我们将挥出开启终结的一击。为了兽人。为了被遗忘者。也为了任何其他蠢到与他们为伍的种族。\n相关",cEN="You’ve got the courage and skill every member of The Defiance dreams of\n\nFor now, Stormwind’s shores are clean of Horde filth, but this was just the beginning.\n\nSoon, in the waters of Azzar, we’ll strike the blow that begins the end. For the orcs. For the Forsaken. And for any other race foolish enough to stand with them.\nRelated"}
Q[1650027]={d="我的人民对狼人诅咒的记忆充满苦涩。在吉尔尼斯，我们竭尽全力遏制它、平息那份狂怒，但是……\n\n<一丝恐惧的阴影掠过德鲁伊的目光。他对狼人的恐惧几乎不亚于对被遗忘者的恐惧。>\n\n你正要去部落的营地，对吧？<他眼中突然燃起一簇决心的火花。>那我和你一起去。我的魔法可以中和瘟疫的毒性。\n\n此外……\n\n大自然与那个死灵法师之间，也有一笔账要算。",dEN="My people remember the worgen curse with bitterness. In Gilneas, we did everything we could to contain it, to calm the fury, but...\n\n<A flicker of fear darkens the druid’s gaze. He dreads the worgen nearly as much as the Forsaken.>\n\nYou’re heading for the Horde’s camp, aren’t you? <A sudden spark of resolve ignites in his eyes>. Then I’m coming with you. My magic can counteract the blight’s toxicity.\n\nBesides...\n\nNature has its own score to settle with the necromancer.",o="清除瘟疫储罐的毒性，并杀死死灵法师文瑟拉尔。",oEN="Eradicate the toxicity of the blight reservoirs and slay the Necromancer Venthral.",p="像瘟疫这样的造物，那些叛徒之一，绝不会带来任何好处；铲除这些怪物所做的一切，是我们的职责。",pEN="A creation like the blight, one of the renegades, will never bring anything good; it is our duty to eradicate everything those monsters have done.",c="我不知道埃尔德林在那个营地里看到了什么让他改变了主意，但我不会质疑。\n\n干得好，<name>。双倍的好。你不仅消除了死灵法师的威胁；\n还为我们赢得了一位强大的盟友。\n\n很快，我们就会启程前往阿扎尔群岛。而历史将传唱我们的名字。\n相关",cEN="I don’t know what Eldryn saw in that camp that changed his mind, but I won’t question it.\n\nWell done, <name>. Twice over. You didn’t just eliminate the necromancer’s threat;\nyou’ve earned us a powerful ally.\n\nSoon, we will depart for the Azzar archipelago. And history will sing our names.\nRelated"}
Q[1650028]={d="一切都准备好了。\n\n我们清除了下水道里被遗忘者的腐臭，粉碎了死灵法师的阴谋，也拯救了暴风城免于溺毙在毒药之中。\n\n但那……那只是序幕。真正的挑战在海上等着我们。\n\n船员已经集结。风向我们有利。而「自由号」也渴望着启航。\n\n准备好就告诉我，<name>……\n\n是时候改变联盟历史的走向了。\n相关",dEN="Everything’s ready.\n\nWe’ve cleansed the sewers of Forsaken rot, ruined the necromancer’s plot, and saved Stormwind from drowning in poison.\n\nBut that... That was just the prologue. The true challenge awaits us at sea.\n\nThe crew is assembled. The wind is with us. And The Liberty is eager to sail.\n\nLet me know when you’re ready, <name>...\n\nIt’s time to shift the course of Alliance history.\nRelated",o="当你准备好启程时，在暴风城港口通知瓦爾迪爾。",oEN="Notify Valdior at the Stormwind port when you are ready to depart."}
Q[1650029]={d="我们正在完成订单的最后几项细节。如果你想亲自核验，我请你为装运物资的箱子打上封条。\n\n订单一完成，我会亲自把它送到港口，我们就在那里碰头。请告知你的船长，订单正在处理中。",dEN="Estamos finalizando los últimos detalles del encargo. Si desea verificarlo personalmente, le invito a sellar las cajas que contendrán el material.\n\nUna vez completado el pedido, me encargaré personalmente de llevarlo al puerto, donde nos encontraremos. Por favor, hágale saber a su capitán que el encargo está en proceso.",o="封好箱子并通知瓦爾迪爾。",oEN="Sella las cajas e informa a Valdior.",p="我们需要确认弹匠妥善处理了武器装备。你检查过没有遗漏什么吗？",pEN="Necesitamos estar seguro que Bulletsmith ha gestionado bien el armamento ¿Has revisado que no falte nada?",c="一切都准备好了吗？\n相关",cEN="¿Todo listo?\nRelated"}
Q[1650030]={d="我们有了船、船员、武器和意志。有了这些，任何部落想运进或运出阿扎尔岛的船只，都会被我们撕碎。\n\n行动的一切都已就绪。当你<准备好/准备好了>时，来暴风城码头见我，<name>。\n\n让我们创造历史。",dEN="Tenemos los barcos, la tripulación, el armamento y la voluntad. Con estos medios, arrasaremos con cualquier barco que la Horda quiera meter o sacar de la Isla de Azzar.\n\nEstá todo preparado para la operación. Ven a verme a los muelles de Ventormenta cuando esté <listo/lista>, <name>.\n\nHagamos historia.",o="当你准备好启程时，在暴风城港口通知瓦爾迪爾。",oEN="Avisa a Valdior en el puerto de Ventormenta cuando estés listo para partir.",p="当你<准备好/准备好了>创造历史时告诉我，<name>。\n相关",pEN="Avísame que estás <listo/lista> para hacer historia, <name>.\nRelated"}
Q[1650100]={d="<你感到口袋被轻轻一扯。有人悄悄塞进了一封折叠好的、未署名的亲笔信。>\n\nThrom-Ka，同志。你可以叫我「匕首」。现在透露我的真名还为时过早。过去几个月里，联盟部署了太多间谍，再多一个，我们就得像赶苍蝇一样把他们轰走。再多的谨慎也不为过。\n\n我派了一个人在暗影裂口下方的泉水处守着。你一眼就能认出他。他是个亡灵潜行者。你知道那种类型：严肃、可靠。他会告诉你怎么找到我……只要你有这个胆量。\n\n动作快点，并确保没人跟踪你。",dEN="<You feel a tug in your pocket. Someone has slipped in a folded, unsigned handwritten letter.>\n\nThrom-Ka, comrade. You can call me ‘Dagger.’ It’s too early to reveal my real name. Over the past few months, the Alliance has deployed so many spies that one more and we’d have to swat them away like flies. No precaution is too much.\n\nI’ve got a man stationed at the Spring, below the Cleft of Shadow. You’ll spot him right away. He’s a Deathstalker. You know the type: serious, reliable. He’ll show you how to find me… if you’ve got the guts for it.\n\nHurry, and make sure you’re not being followed.",o="在奥格瑞玛使用暗影裂口的升降梯，把信给守在奥格瑞玛深处泉水处的被遗忘者凯恩德瑞斯看。",oEN="Use the elevator in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar, and show the letter to the Forsaken named Caindres, stationed at the Spring in the Orgrimmar Depths.",p="<你走近时，亡灵的手猛地伸向匕首。>",pEN="<The forsaken’s hand darts to his dagger as you approach.>",c="<直到你出示那封信，被遗忘者才把手从匕首柄上移开。随后，他点了点头。他的双眼是两轮病态的月亮，投下盛满轻蔑的昏黄光芒。>\n\n我们寄出了很多信。在你之前也有人来过。你并不特别。而你是否值得这份麻烦，还有待观察。\n相关",cEN="<The Forsaken only moves his hand away from the dagger's hilt when you show him the letter. Then, he nods. His eyes are two sickly moons, casting a yellow light heavy with disdain.>\n\nWe sent out a lot of letters. Others have come before you. You’re not special. And it remains to be seen if you’re even worth the trouble.\nRelated"}
Q[1650101]={d="赌注很大。在我能向你透露是谁给你写信、又在哪里能找到他们之前，我们必须确保没有不速之客闯进这场派对。\n\n我自己已经处理掉几个间谍，但春季区下面还潜伏着联盟特工。至少，这是我在拔他们指甲时他们招供的……\n\n<凯恩德瑞斯露出一抹阴森的偏嘴笑。>\n\n找到那些间谍并处理掉他们，好吗？",dEN="A lot is at stake. Before I can give you any details on who wrote to you or where to find them, we need to make sure that no uninvited guests crash the party.\n\nI’ve already taken care of a few spies myself, but there are still Alliance agents lurking down here in the Spring District. Or at least, that’s what they confessed while I was pulling out their nails...\n\n<Caindres gives a sinister half-smile.>\n\nFind the spies and take care of them, will you?",o="在奥格瑞玛深处的源泉区消灭七名联盟间谍。",oEN="Eliminate seven Alliance spies in the Fountain District, in the Depths of Orgrimmar.",p="你处理掉那些联盟渣滓了吗？",pEN="Have you dealt with those Alliance scum?",c="你杀了他们？\n\n<那盗贼水汪汪的眼睛扫过你。当他注意到你衣服上的血迹时，一个缓慢的笑容在他脸上蔓延开来。>\n\n很好……\n相关",cEN="Did you kill them?\n\n<The rogue's watery eyes sweep over you. As he notices the bloodstains on your clothes, a slow smile spreads across his face.>\n\nGood...\nRelated"}
Q[1650102]={d="如果杀掉他们就够了，我们早就终结这个问题了。但我们每除掉一个间谍，联盟就会再派两个来。\n\n拿着。\n\n<凯恩德瑞斯递给你一捆信件。>\n\n里面是假命令，有些自相矛盾，如果我没记错，甚至还有一两份菜谱。我们的事业靠散布假情报比靠流血获益更多。如果暴风城的间谍截获了这些信中的任何一封……他们会写出令人愉悦地混乱的报告。",dEN="If killing them were enough, we’d have put an end to this problem long ago. But for every spy we get rid of, the Alliance sends two more.\n\nHere.\n\n<Caindres hands you a bundle of letters.>\n\nThey contain false orders, some contradictory, and if I recall correctly, even a cooking recipe or two. Our cause benefits more from spreading misinformation than from spilling blood. If Stormwind’s spies intercept any of these letters… they’ll be writing some delightfully confusing reports.",o="在奥格瑞玛深处的春季区投递 5 份假命令，以迷惑联盟间谍。",oEN="Deliver 5 fake orders in the Spring District, in the Depths of Orgrimmar, to confuse the Alliance spies.",p="来吧。邮件可不会自己送出去。",pEN="Come on. The mail’s not going to deliver itself.",c="暴风城的猎犬们为了理清你散布的那些命令，耳朵都要冒烟了。祝他们好运……\n相关",cEN="Stormwind's hounds are going to blow steam out of their ears trying to make sense of all the orders you’ve spread around. Good luck with that...\nRelated"}
Q[1650103]={d="在我这一行，行动胜于言语。你觉得你的所作所为说明了什么？\n\n冷酷的效率：刺客的美德。\n\n不动声色的服从：士兵的美德。\n\n以及恰到好处的好奇心，足以让你收到一封匿名信并前来赴约。\n\n你想见\"匕首\"吗？你想知道他们为什么召你前来，又想从你身上得到什么吗？去幽影回声酒馆。靠里的那张桌子，挨着吧台。他们会问你：\"我喝了几杯啤酒？\"答案是：\"一杯也没有。\"\n\n走吧，别引人注目。",dEN="In my field, actions speak louder than words. What do you think your work says about you?\n\nCold efficiency: the virtue of an assassin.\n\nDispassionate obedience: the virtue of a soldier.\n\nAnd just enough curiosity to receive an anonymous letter and show up.\n\nDo you want to meet “Dagger”? Do you want to know why they summoned you and what they want from you? Go to the Shaded Echo Tavern. The table at the back, near the bar. They’ll ask you: \"How many beers have I had?\" The answer is: \"None.\"\n\nLeave, and keep a low profile.",o="与奥格瑞玛深处春季区幽影回声酒馆里的神秘接头人交谈。",oEN="Speak with the mysterious contact at the Shaded Echo Tavern in the Spring District, in the Depths of Orgrimmar.",c="<当你低声说出暗号时，兽人的表情转为戒备。>\n\n那么，你拿到了我的信……而凯恩德瑞斯也给了你他的认可。很好。在你之前来过几个，但没有一个像你这么有前途。\n相关",cEN="<As you whisper the password, the orc's expression shifts to one of caution.>\n\nSo, you got my letter… and Caindres gave you his approval. Good. A few have come before you, but none as promising.\nRelated"}
Q[1650104]={d="我叫卡格莎。\n\n<兽人从膝上抬起手，把一把手枪放在桌上。你意识到她从始至终都把它对准着你。>\n\n我属于碎手氏族——部落最接近情报机构的组织。或者干脆说，就是情报本身。\n\n你想知道你为什么会在这里，对吧？很好，坐下。我们正要听那位说书人讲故事。",dEN="My name is Kagtha.\n\n<The orc lifts her hand from her lap and places a pistol on the table. You realize she’s had it trained on you from the start.>\n\nI belong to the Shattered Hand—about as close as the Horde gets to having an intelligence service. Or just plain intelligence, for that matter.\n\nYou want to know why you’re here, don’t you? Good, sit down. We were just about to listen the storyteller’s tale.",o="听那位说书人讲述。",oEN="Listen to the storyteller.",p="<卡格莎皱起眉头，示意你注意听说书人。你们稍后再谈。>",pEN="<Kagtha scowls and gestures for you to pay attention to the storyteller. You’ll talk later.>",c="如你所见，旧日的仇恨难以消弭。而近年来，那些高喊「东部王国属于联盟」的声音只是越来越响。\n\n洛丹伦。被遗忘者会承受第一击。奥特兰克的霜狼氏族将是下一个。而无论血精灵的怨恨有多深……当他们发现自己被一片蓝色旗帜的海洋包围时，真的会选择骄傲而非生存吗？\n相关",cEN="As you can see, old hatreds die hard. And in recent years, the voices shouting “The Eastern Kingdoms belong to the Alliance” have only grown louder.\n\nLordaeron. The Forsaken will take the first blow. The Frostwolf Clan in Alterac will be next. And as deep as the blood elves' resentment runs… when they find themselves surrounded by a sea of blue banners, will they really choose pride over survival?\nRelated"}
Q[1650105]={d="你可曾听说过地精城市阿扎尔？过去两年里，它已经成为大海域最大的港口。\n\n谁控制了那座岛，谁就有能力在即将爆发的战争中先发制人。我的任务就是确保风向对我们有利。这就是联盟试图破坏我们行动的原因。\n\n你有能力，但你有打仗的胃口吗？\n\n我的人刚刚抓到了联盟间谍的头目。向我证明你没软弱到不敢拷问一个手无寸铁的人。让他招供。",dEN="Have you ever heard of the goblin city of Azzar? In the last two years, it’s become the largest port in the Great Sea.\n\nWhoever takes control of the island will have the power to strike the first blow in the war that’s about to break out. My mission is to make sure the winds blow in our favor. That’s why the Alliance is trying to sabotage us.\n\nYou’re capable, but do you have the stomach for war?\n\nMy men just captured the leader of the Alliance spies. Show me you’re not too soft to torture a defenseless man. Get a confession out of him.",o="痛打那名联盟间谍，直到他把知道的一切都招出来。",oEN="Beat the Alliance spy until he confesses everything he knows.",p="心里打结了吗？还是有别的什么原因让你还没开始干活？",pEN="Got a knot in your stomach? Or is there another reason you haven’t started the job yet?",c="他真的对我们大谈荣誉？<Kagtha ahoga una risa ronca>.\n\n只有不懂风险的蠢人，或是派别人替自己去送死的懦夫，才负担得起荣誉这种奢侈品。在这下面，在现实世界里，被幻想支配的人活不长久。\n\n但你从他口中问出了有趣的供词。我很惊讶军情七处对我们和我们的目标了解得这么多。\n相关",cEN="Did he really lecture us about honor? <Kagtha stifles a raspy laugh.>\n\nOnly a fool who doesn’t understand the risks, or a coward who sends others to die in his place, can afford the luxury of honor. Down here, in the real world, those ruled by fantasies don’t survive for long.\n\nBut you’ve gotten an interesting confession out of him. I’m surprised the SI:7 has learned so much about us and our goals.\nRelated"}
Q[1650106]={d="如果之前还有疑问，你刚刚把它打消了：你在战斗中很有一套。事实上，不止一套。\n\n等我收拾完这摊烂摊子，我要你去见我们最忠诚的战士之一：恐怖图腾的阿尔姆胡尔。拿着我的印章。接近他时给他看。\n\n你会在峡谷区找到他，就在河对岸、桥边哨站附近。",dEN="If there was any doubt left, you just put it to rest: you handle yourself well in a fight. More than well, actually.\n\nWhile I clean up this mess, I want you to meet one of the most committed warriors we have: Armhul of the Grimtotem. Take my seal. Show it to him when you approach.\n\nYou’ll find him in the Gorge, across the river, near the bridge outpost.",o="在峡谷区桥边的小屋旁找到阿尔姆胡尔。",oEN="Find Armhul in the Gorge district, next to the shack by the bridge.",c="Shteleo pi-ssan。是卡格莎派你来的？你有她的印章吗？\n\n<巨大的牛头人俯身查看印章，哼了一声，鼻子上的环叮当作响。他呼气时温热的气流扑在你脸上。你清楚地感到，这将是你能从他身上得到的唯一温暖。>\n\n好吧。如果你想为事业出力，我有份工作给你。\n相关",cEN="Shteleo pi-ssan. Did Kagtha send you? Do you have her seal?\n\n<The massive Tauren leans in to inspect the seal and snorts, causing the ring in his nose to jangle. The warm gust of his breath hits your face. You get the distinct feeling this will be the only warmth you'll receive from him.>\n\nAlright. If you want to be useful to the cause, I've got a job for you.\nRelated"}
Q[1650107]={d="萨尔太天真了。如果他发现我们在谋划什么，我们的脑袋就要搬家。幸运的是，我们有强大——且大胆——的靠山。\n\n女妖之王第一个表现出对流血感兴趣，你觉得意外吗？A'ke no wachi。\n\n然而，有一件事让我深感忧虑。我整天都在等着见她的一位黑暗游侠，一个叫蕾娜拉的女人。她本该带着一批武器和补给前来支援事业。如果他们抓住了她，如果她暴露了……那么，下一个就是我。\n\n我暂时还不能离开我的岗位。你能去调查一下出了什么事吗？",dEN="Thrall is naive. If he found out what we’re up to, our heads would roll. Luckily, we have powerful—and bold—patrons.\n\nAre you surprised that the Banshee Queen is the first to show interest in spilling blood? A'ke no wachi.\n\nThere’s one thing, however, that has me deeply concerned. I’ve been waiting all day to meet with one of her dark rangers, a woman named Lenara. She was supposed to arrive with a shipment of weapons and supplies for the cause. If they’ve caught her, if they’ve exposed her… Well, I’m next in line.\n\nI can’t leave my post here just yet. Could you go investigate what happened?",o="向奥格瑞玛深处大釜区的当地人打听黑暗游侠蕾娜拉的下落。",oEN="Ask locals in the Cauldron district, in the Depths of Orgrimmar, about the dark ranger Lenara.",p="<那精灵背对着你。她似乎很忙，按着一个抽泣的兽人，把那兽人的脸压在地上，手臂被痛苦地扭到背后。>",pEN="<The elf turns her back to you. She seems busy, holding down a whimpering orc whose face is pressed against the ground, his arm twisted painfully.>",c="<黑暗游侠把匕首抵在脚下兽人的喉咙上。还没来得及说你是来求和的，她的手已经摸到弓上，拉紧了弓弦。金属箭尖对准了你。>\n\n再走一步，我就杀了你。\n相关",cEN="<The dark ranger holds a dagger to the throat of the orc at her feet. Before you can say you come in peace, her hand has already reached for her bow and drawn the string tight. The metal tip of the arrow is aimed at you.>\n\nOne more step, and I'll kill you.\nRelated"}
Q[1650108]={d="今天早上，一队来自格罗玛什要塞的士兵出现在独眼维尔的老巢；你知道的，就是那种以为解决一个问题就等于解决全世界的人。\n\n我要你趁他们醉得神志不清，把这瓶镇静剂倒进他们的酒里。应该能让他们昏睡接下来的二十四小时，免得他们干扰我们的计划。\n\n女巫塞拉腊·冷影藏身于老巢的上层。她会把细节都告诉你。完事后，去找一个叫查兹利的红冠巨魔。",dEN="This morning, a group of soldiers from Grommash Hold showed up at Vil the Squint’s Den—you know, the type who think fixing one problem equals fixing the whole world.\n\nI want you to take advantage of their drunken stupor and slip this sedative into their drinks. It should knock them out for the next twenty-four hours and prevent them from interfering with our plans.\n\nThe sorceress Selara Coldshadow is hiding out in the upper level of the Den. She’ll fill you in on all the details. When you’re done, look for a red-crested troll who goes by the name Chazili.",o="前往奥格瑞玛深处大釜区尽头的独眼维尔老巢，把镇静剂倒进部落士兵的酒里。",oEN="Go to Vil the Squint’s Den, at the far end of the Cauldron district, in the Depths of Orgrimmar, and slip the sedative into the drinks of the Horde soldiers.",p="我认识你吗？",pEN="Do I know ya?",c="站住别动，不然我砍了你！哦，等等，等等；你是说阿尔姆胡尔派你来的？\n\n<这巨魔表现出的智力水平仅略高于本能。你能看出他把这些线索串起来所费的巨大力气。>\n\n那么，我猜是阿尔姆胡尔派你来给老巢里的士兵下毒的。也许你也能帮我个忙？\n相关",cEN="Hold it right there, or I'll cut ya! Oh, wait, wait; ya're sayin' Armhul sent ya?”\n\n<The troll shows a level of intelligence that's barely above instinctual. You can see the monumental effort it's taking him to connect the dots.>\n\nSo, I guess Armhul sent ya to poison da soldiers at da den. Maybe ya could help me out too?\nRelated"}
Q[1650109]={d="我和手下从码头大门进来，带着两辆装得满满当当的补给车。我怀疑是你们中的某个人给辛迪加报了信——因为他们正等着我们。\n\n我们能抢回多少算多少；其余的都被他们的打手拿走了。真是胆大包天！不到五分钟，他们就把东西挂到地下黑市上出售了。\n\n既然阿尔姆胡尔派你来了……你觉得能帮我们找回被抢的补给吗？我和我这位绿皮肤的朋友还有话要谈完。",dEN="My men and I came in through the docks gate with two carts packed to the brim with supplies. I suspect one of your own tipped off the syndicates—because they were waiting for us.\n\nWe salvaged what we could; the rest was taken by their thugs. The audacity! It didn’t take them five minutes to put it up for sale on the UnderMarket.\n\nSince Armhul sent you… think you could help us recover the stolen supplies? My green friend and I have a little conversation to finish here.",o="使用奥格瑞玛深处大釜区的中央升降梯。\n\n从地下黑市取回被抢的补给。",oEN="Use the central elevator in the Cauldron District, in the Depths of Orgrimmar.\n\nRetrieve the stolen supplies from the UnderMarket.",p="你已经找回补给了吗？",pEN="Have you recovered the supplies yet?",c="这就是……全部？\n\n<蕾娜拉抿紧嘴唇，脸上扭曲成凶猛的怒容。>\n\n这还不到他们从我们这里抢走的三分之一。\n\n<你注意到她握弓柄的手收得更紧了。片刻之后，怒意褪去，取而代之的是一种沉思般的认命。>\n\n好吧，我们凑合着用。就像我们一直做的那样。\n相关",cEN="Is this… all of it?\n\n<Lenara presses her lips together, her face twisting into a fierce scowl.>\n\nThis is less than a third of what they stole from us.\n\n<You notice how her grip tightens around the bow’s handle. A moment later, the anger fades, replaced by a contemplative resignation.>\n\nWell, we’ll make do. Like we always have.\nRelated"}
Q[1650110]={d="这场伏击让我损失了好几名优秀的战士。有几个迎来了真正的死亡。另一些在混乱中失散，我们还没找到他们。\n\n<蕾娜拉赤红的双眼如同残酷的宝石般燃烧。她的靴跟踩在那兽人的手上，骨头在重量下咯吱作响。>\n\n我要你找到我的手下。我们的猎犬巴吉斯特会帮你追踪他们。别担心，亡者之身并没有让他的嗅觉变钝。只要给他一条可循的踪迹。\n\n确保我的战士们完整地回到我身边——当然是比喻意义上的。",dEN="The ambush cost me a handful of good warriors. A few met their true death. Others were lost in the chaos, and we still haven’t found them.\n\n<Lenara’s red eyes burn like cruel gemstones. The heel of her boot presses down on the orc’s hand, bones crunching beneath the weight.>\n\nI want you to find my men. Barguist, our hound, will help you track them down. Don’t worry—the undead state hasn’t dulled his sense of smell. Just give him a trail to follow.\n\nMake sure my warriors return to me in one piece—figuratively speaking, of course.",o="寻找失踪被遗忘者的踪迹，并借助巴吉斯特追踪他们。",oEN="Find traces of the missing Forsaken and use Barguist to track them down.",p="跳蚤好痒！你要我杀什么？",pEN="Fleas tickle! What you want me to kill?",c="是精灵派你来帮忙的？\n相关",cEN="Elf sent you to help?\nRelated"}
Q[1650111]={d="蠢货们以为能治好被遗忘者的朋友，但没什么可治的——被遗忘者的朋友没有生病！\n\n朋友自由了！如果敌人想要药……我给他们准备了药！\n\n<布魯斯在自己的内脏里翻找，递给你一样看起来像油腻、搏动着的肝脏的东西。>\n\n布魯斯的药！你用它杀敌人！",dEN="Fools think can cure Forsaken friends, but there’s nothing to cure—Forsaken friends not sick!\n\nYou free friends! And if enemies want medicine… I have medicine for them!\n\n<Bruise rummages through his own guts and hands you something that looks like a greasy, pulsating liver.>\n\nBruise’s medicine! You use it to kill enemies!",o="在族长岩洞击败 12 名族长的开明者，并解救 4 名被遗忘者病患。",oEN="Defeat 12 Patriarchs’ Enlightened and free 4 Forsaken Patients in the Patriarchs' Grotto.",p="你找到我的手下了吗？",pEN="Have you found my men?",c="谢谢你救了他们。很少有人愿意冒这个险。\n\n这世界憎恶我们。我们所谓的盟友能容忍我们的唯一方式，就是把他们的厌恶淹没在居高临下的同情之海中。\n我不怪他们。看看我们吧：\n\n威克斯的下颚被撕掉了——他的舌头不过是一片流着口水、毫无用处的肉垂。索芙莉娜的双眼早已干枯，却仍挂在视神经上，像树上垂着的淫秽果实。\n\n可悲的事实是，我们是怪物。以畸形秀的标准来看，也算得上怪诞。\n相关",cEN="Thank you for saving them. Few would have taken that risk.\n\nThe world loathes us. The only way our so-called allies can tolerate us is by drowning their disgust in an ocean of condescension and pity.\nI can’t blame them. Just look at us:\n\nWickers had his lower jaw torn off—his tongue is nothing more than a drooling, useless flap. Sofrina’s eyes dried out long ago, but they still dangle from the optic nerve like obscene fruit hanging from a tree.\n\nThe sad truth is, we are monsters. Grotesque, even by a freak show’s standards.\nRelated"}
Q[1650112]={d="<一份研究日志中散落的笔记，很可能只是这短短几页之外某项更宏大研究的一部分。>\n\n<草图描绘了处于不同腐烂阶段的人类形体。在他们血肉之下，某种类似血管的东西似乎形成了一个连接肉体与灵魂的闭合回路。>\n\n<注释交织着牛头人的德鲁伊教义、兽人的萨满知识、巨魔的巫毒迷信，甚至还有熊猫人的「气」这类难以捉摸的概念。>\n\n<也许，如果你收集到这本日志更多的书页，你就能揭开族长开明者真正追求的东西。>",dEN="<Scattered notes from a research journal, likely part of a much larger study beyond these brief pages.>\n\n<The sketches depict human figures in various stages of decomposition. Beneath their flesh, something resembling veins appears to form a closed circuit linking body and soul.>\n\n<The annotations intertwine Tauren druidic principles, Orcish shamanic knowledge, Troll voodoo superstitions, and even elusive concepts such as the Pandaren Chi.>\n\n<Perhaps, if you gather more pages of this journal, you may uncover what the Patriarchal Enlightened are truly after.>",o="找到并帮助布魯斯在奥格瑞玛深处的大釜杀死五名打手。",oEN="Find and help Bruise kill five thugs in the Cauldron, in the Depths of Orgrimmar.",p="这是什么？",pEN="What is this?",c="这是什么？\n\n<蕾娜拉带着怀疑的目光审视这些笔记。>\n\n蠢货……他们居然真以为能\"治好\"我们。如果他们的药没杀死我们，他们也会动手——而不是承认自己的失败。\n相关",cEN="What is this?\n\n<Lenara examines the notes with a skeptical gaze.>\n\nFools… They actually believed they could “fix” us. If their medicine didn’t kill us, they would—rather than admit their own failure.\nRelated"}
Q[1650113]={d="这次任务有些事我认同，有些事我不认同。那些被安抚者？那就是我不喜欢的事情之一。他们让我毛骨悚然……\n\n你知道我什么意思吗？精神奴隶。被遗忘者给他们洗脑，然后像木偶一样卖掉他们。\n\n阿尔姆胡尔让我把我们抓到的联盟间谍带给她。五个可怜的傻瓜。他们现在应该已经准备好了，但我……我没那个胆量去接他们。我甚至不敢看他们的眼睛。\n\n你能去和被遗忘者谈谈，把这活干完吗？",dEN="Dere be tings ‘bout dis mission I agree wit, and tings I don’t. Da pacified ones? Dey one o’ da tings I don’t like. Dey give me da creeps…\n\nYa know what I mean? Mind slaves. Dat Forsaken brainwashes ‘em and sells ‘em like puppets.\n\nArmhul told me ta take da Alliance spies we captured to her. Five poor fools. Dey should be ready by now, but me… I ain’t got da stomach ta go get ‘em. Can’t even look ‘em in da eyes.\n\nCan ya go talk ta da Forsaken an’ finish da job?",o="在奥格瑞玛深处的露克兰塔巢穴与露克兰塔交谈，并接收那些被安抚者。",oEN="Speak with Lucranta at Lucranta's Den in the Depths of Orgrimmar, and secure the pacified ones.",c="所以是那个巨魔白痴派你来的，我猜？他带那些被抓的间谍来的时候，我就知道他有问题。我从没觉得这么被评判过！他甚至连让我开价的时间都没给。\n\n相信我，这可不便宜。\n相关",cEN="So, the troll idiot sent you, I take it? I knew something was off with him when he brought me those captured spies. I’ve never felt so judged! He didn’t even give me time to name my fee.\n\nBelieve me, this isn’t going to come cheap.\nRelated"}
Q[1650114]={d="你看，安抚这门高贵的艺术，处在炼金术、心理学和魔法的交汇点上。只要这三根支柱中有一根失灵，结果就可能……出人意料地暴力。\n\n那个巨魔带来给我的五个人类，我几乎已经处理完了，但出现了麻烦。他们对联盟的忠诚坚不可摧——我不得不把手上最后一滴噬我药剂都用了下去，可他们依旧抗拒服从！\n\n我需要调配更强的东西，但我缺少关键的原料……\n\n我把需要的一切都写在这张清单上了，包括银行职员的暗码。如果你还需要更多指示，你知道去哪儿找我。",dEN="You see, the noble art of pacification lies at the crossroads of alchemy, psychology, and magic. If even one of these three pillars fails, the results can be… unexpectedly violent.\n\nI’ve nearly finished with the five humans the troll brought me, but complications have arisen. Their loyalty to the Alliance is unshakable—I’ve had to administer every last drop of ego-phagic potion I had, and still, they resist obedience!\n\nI need to concoct something stronger, but I’m missing key ingredients…\n\nI’ve written everything I need on this list, including the code for the bank clerk. If you need any further directions, you know where to find me.",o="在奥格瑞玛深处大釜区的市场取得露克兰塔调配安抚药剂所需的原料。",oEN="Obtain the ingredients Lucranta needs to brew the pacification potion at the market in the Cauldron district, in the Depths of Orgrimmar.",p="我以为你识字，但如果你更愿意，我可以把原料念出来：观察者的视神经、海巨人之吸盘、法力浮龙碎片和元素废料。\n\n要我重复一遍吗？观察者的视神经、海巨人之吸盘、法力浮龙碎片和灵魂废料。\n\n现在，去吧。",pEN="I assumed you could read, but if you’d prefer, I can list the ingredients out loud: observer’s optic nerve, kraken sucker, mana wyrm shard, and elemental waste.\n\nShall I repeat it? Observer’s optic nerve, kraken sucker, mana wyrm shard, and spiritual waste.\n\nNow off you go.",c="好极了！我猜你现在想要报酬……一块饼干够吗，还是你更想让我扔根骨头给你？恐怕我的骨头可不在菜单上。\n\n<露克兰塔发出一阵干涩刺耳的大笑。片刻之后，她腐烂面孔上的表情转为某种令人不安的严肃。>\n\n别再犯傻了！该下厨了！\n相关",cEN="Bravo! I suppose you’re expecting a reward now—will a cookie suffice, or would you rather have me toss you a bone? I’m afraid mine aren’t on the menu.\n\n<Lucranta lets out a dry, rasping laugh. A moment later, the rotten expression on her face shifts into something unsettlingly serious.>\n\nEnough foolishness! Time to cook!\nRelated"}
Q[1650115]={d="很好，给我一点时间，然后……\n\n<就在原料爆成一团炫目的彩色云雾时，被遗忘者从大锅旁退开。>\n\n多么……奇妙。药剂完成了。一旦他们喝下，那些被安抚者就归你了——身体与灵魂。\n\n我不骗你；完善这个配方让人头疼。我的大多数老主顾想要的是……这么说吧，另一种服务；更\"精灵向\"的，如果你懂我的意思。\n\n但我做到了！我的药剂改变大脑化学的方式，超出了我在洛丹伦那些所谓的同行以为可能的程度。<她自豪地咯咯笑起来，随后表情扭曲成更阴险的样子。>人们说，笑到最后的人笑得最好。\n\n把桌上的药剂拿走，给他们服下。来吧，我想看看他们会有什么反应。",dEN="Very well, just give me a moment and…\n\n<The Forsaken steps away from the cauldron just as the ingredients erupt into a dazzling cloud of colors.>\n\nWhat… a marvel. The potion is ready. Once they drink it, the pacified will be yours—body and soul.\n\nI won’t lie to you; perfecting this recipe was a headache. Most of my regular clients are after… let’s say, a different kind of service—more “elven,” if you catch my drift.\n\nBut I did it! My potion alters brain chemistry beyond anything my so-called colleagues in Lordaeron ever thought possible. <She cackles, proud, before her expression twists into something more sinister.> They say the one who laughs last, laughs best.\n\nTake the potion from the table and administer it. Come on, I want to see how they react.",o="在奥格瑞玛深处给五名被安抚者服下药剂。",oEN="Administer the potions to five pacified ones in the Depths of Orgrimmar.",p="查兹利承认他派你处理那些被安抚者。我想……你还没有什么可汇报的？",pEN="Chazili admitted that he has tasked you with handling the pacified ones. I assume… you have nothing to report yet?",c="给你，你还带来了同伴。\n\n<卡格莎不安地动了动，这种情绪被她薄唇轻微的撇动出卖了。>\n\n干得好。说实话，我讨厌那些被安抚者。我讨厌他们所代表的东西。但当然，我不会让我的……道德指南针妨碍我的工作。\n\n<卡格莎最后向查兹利投去锐利的一瞥，随后便不再追究此事。>\n相关",cEN="Here you are, and you’ve brought company.\n\n<Kagtha shifts uneasily, a feeling betrayed by the slight curl of her thin lips.>\n\nGood work. To be honest, I hate the pacified ones. I hate what they represent. But of course, I don’t let my… moral compass get in the way of my work.\n\n<Kagtha throws a final, pointed glance at Chazili before considering the matter closed.>\nRelated"}
Q[1650116]={d="我相信你的上级会乐于得知我们的协议依然有效。我们会交付剩余的补给，并在船只启程前往阿扎尔时与大部队会合。\n\n如果联盟控制了那座岛……洛丹伦不仅会在陆地上被孤立，在海上也一样。以酋长的优柔寡断，他们会像猎杀老鼠一样猎杀我们。",dEN="I believe your superiors will appreciate knowing that our agreement is still in place. We’ll deliver the remaining supplies and join the rest of the group when the ships set sail for Azzar.\n\nIf the Alliance takes control of that island… Lordaeron will be cut off not just by land, but by sea as well. With the Warchief’s indecision, they’ll hunt us down like rats.",o="向卡格莎汇报被遗忘者盟友的状况。",oEN="Inform Kagtha of the forsaken allies' status.",c="是蕾娜拉派你来的？\n\n<卡格莎一边听你汇报，一边漫不经心地转着一把匕首。>\n\n阿尔姆胡尔担心大酋长的猎犬发现了蕾娜拉，并顺藤摸瓜找到我们。但你告诉我的情况几乎更糟。我们队伍里有老鼠，而且是最恶劣的那种。如果他们把我们出卖给萨尔，至少那还算是个原则问题。但被出卖给下面这些本地帮派……\n\n我还有活要干，<name>。是时候拔除杂草了。\n相关",cEN="Lenara sent you?\n\n<Kagtha idly twirls a dagger as she listens to your report.>\n\nArmhul feared that the Warchief’s hounds had discovered Lenara, and through her, us. But what you’re telling me is almost worse. Rats in our ranks—and the worst kind. If they’d sold us out to Thrall, at least it would’ve been a matter of principle. But to be sold out to the local gangs down here...\n\nI’ve got work to do, <name>. Time to clear out the weeds.\nRelated"}
Q[1650117]={d="只剩下一个位置要填补。\n\n你看……我为这次任务雇佣的雇佣兵法师之一刚刚丢了脑袋。字面意义上的。拜联盟所赐。\n\n不过没什么大不了，我心目中还有另一位人选：奥术师阿尔达因。听说过他吗？这家伙是个狂妄的显摆鬼，但该死，他确实很在行。我们只需要让他的女主人稍微放松一下他的皮带，好让他能陪我们走这一趟。\n\n去飞镖帮的总部。出示我的印章，要求见女爵。运气好的话，她会愿意配合。",dEN="There's just one spot left to fill.\n\nYou see... One of the mercenary mages I hired for the mission just lost his head. Literally. Courtesy of the Alliance.\n\nBut no big deal, I’ve got another candidate in mind: Arcanist Ardayn. Heard of him? The guy’s a cocky show-off, but damn, he's good at what he does. We just need to get his lady to loosen his leash enough for him to tag along on this mission.\n\nHead over to the Darts' headquarters. Flash my seal and ask to see Duchess. With any luck, she'll be willing to play ball.",o="在飞镖帮总部出示卡格莎的印章，并请求觐见女爵。",oEN="Show Kagtha’s seal in the headquarters of the Darts and ask for an audience with Duchess.",c="欢迎来到女爵的飞镖帮总部，伙计。我们可不随便让人上来的，你知道吗？希望你能意识到自己获赐了多么难得的特权，是吧？\n相关",cEN="Welcome to da Duchess' Darts headquarters, mon. We don’t be lettin’ just anyone up here, ya know. Hope ya realize da rare privilege ya been given, yeah?\nRelated"}
Q[1650118]={d="老大在等你。\n\n沿着走廊向左，上楼到最顶层。女爵就在顶上。\n\n别再浪费我的时间了。",dEN="Da boss is waitin' for ya.\n\nLeft down the hall, up the stairs to the very top. Duchess at the peak.\n\nDon't waste any more of my time.",o="在奥格瑞玛深处的木冠与女爵交谈。",oEN="Speak with Duchess in the Timber Crown, in the Depths of Orgrimmar.",c="哎呀，哎呀，看看你。天哪，多英俊啊！幸亏我有我的讽刺，不然在你的魅力面前我就束手无策了。\n\n<女爵残忍地笑了。片刻之后，她松开交叉的双腿，优雅地起身，赠予你一个充满秘密的微笑。>\n\n我就知道你迟早会找到我门前。现在告诉我，这回是我哪只小宠物惹上麻烦了？嘘，不，不必说。我已经能从你脸上看出来了。\n\n你是为阿尔达因来的，对吧？\n相关",cEN="Well, well, look at you. My, my, how dashing! Good thing I have my sarcasm, or I’d be helpless before your charms.\n\n<Duchess laughs cruelly. After a moment, she uncrosses her legs and rises gracefully, gifting you a smile full of secrets.>\n\nI knew you'd find your way to my doorstep, eventually. Now tell me, which one of my little pets has found themselves in hot water this time? Shh, no, no need to say it. I can already see it written all over your face.\n\nYou’re here for Ardayn, aren’t you?\nRelated"}
Q[1650119]={d="恐怕我们有个小问题：阿尔达因正在地牢里服刑。\n\n一桩相当难堪的事件，你看。我撞见他跟试毒人在一起……品尝他绝对不该品尝的东西！现在谁来替我试吃，确保没人试图毒死我？\n\n但也许你和我能达成一项安排。\n\n碰巧我有点虫害防治的小麻烦。我在这儿开店的时候，根本不知道这些横梁上睡了多少蝙蝠。把鱼叉上的灰掸掉，替我干掉几只那些扑棱翅膀的东西，然后……谁知道呢……也许阿尔达因能全身而退。",dEN="I’m afraid we have a bit of a problem—Ardayn is currently serving time in the dungeon.\n\nA rather embarrassing incident, you see. I caught him with the food taster… tasting what he most certainly shouldn’t have! Now who’s going to test my meals to make sure no one’s trying to poison me?\n\nBut perhaps you and I can come to an arrangement.\n\nIt just so happens that I have a little pest control issue. When I set up shop here, I had no idea how many bats were napping in these rafters. Dust off the harpoons, take out a few of the flappers for me and… who knows… maybe Ardayn’ll make it out of this in one piece.",o="使用鱼叉在奥格瑞玛深处的木冠消灭 10 只蝙蝠。",oEN="Exterminate 10 bats using the harpoons in the Lignary Crown , located in Orgrimmar’s Depths.",p="我还能听见那些小飞鼠的尖叫声。\n\n你到底要不要除掉那些蝙蝠，还是让我任阿尔达因在牢房里烂掉？",pEN="I can still hear the screeching of those little flying rats.\n\nAre you going to get rid of the bats, or should I let Ardayn rot in his cell?",c="干得漂亮，真正专业人士的成色。真遗憾你这么快就要走。你本可以取代阿尔达因的……\n相关",cEN="An excellent job, the mark of a true professional. Such a shame you’ll be leaving so soon. You could have replaced Ardayn...\nRelated"}
Q[1650120]={d="<女爵打了个响指，阿尔达因笼子的钥匙便魔法般地出现在你口袋里。>\n\n带他离开这里。告诉他最好别再敢回来。诚信是我的原则……但记仇也是。",dEN="I may be frivolous, even complacent at times, but above all, I am a woman of my word. Take this.\n\n<Duchess snaps her fingers, and the key to Ardayn’s cage magically appears in your pocket.>\n\nGet him out of here. Tell him he better not dare come back. Honesty is my policy... but so is holding a grudge.",o="在奥格瑞玛深处的木冠用钥匙打开阿尔达因的笼子，并解开他的束缚。",oEN="Use the key to open Ardayn’s cage in the Timber Crown, in the Depths of Orgrimmar, and untie him.",p="<被堵住嘴的精灵绝望地咕哝着。他似乎想说：「求你了，带我离开这里。」>",pEN="<The gagged elf mumbles desperately. He seems to be trying to say, “Please, get me out of here.”>",c="<你还没解开堵嘴布，阿尔达因就开始结结巴巴地道谢，含泪的双眼恳求般地望着你。>\n\n谢谢你。谢谢你！在我之前的所有那些男人……这么说吧，当女爵玩腻了她的玩具，她就会打他们。当她打腻了，就把他们丢到一边。\n相关",cEN="<Before you even finish untying the gag, Ardayn starts babbling his thanks, his tearful eyes looking at you, pleading.>\n\nThank you. Thank you! All those other men before me... well, let’s just say, when Duchess gets bored of her toys, she hits them. And when she’s bored of hitting them, she tosses them aside.\nRelated"}
Q[1650121]={d="那么，碎手氏族需要我的效劳。\n\n<阿尔达因抬手托住下巴，摆出一副意在装作若有所思的姿态。尽管双颊凹陷、眼窝乌青，这个无赖依然保有自己的魅力。>\n\n就算你的上级会接受一个「不」字，我出去之后也没有积蓄可以依靠。而在与女爵的……<他停顿片刻，寻找合适的词>分歧之后，最聪明的做法大概是与奥格瑞玛告别一段时间。",dEN="So, the Shattered Hand requires my services.\n\n<Ardayn raises a hand to his chin in what is meant to pass as a thoughtful gesture. Despite his sunken cheeks and the bags under his eyes, the scoundrel still retains his charm.>\n\nEven if your superiors would accept 'no' for an answer, I’ve got no savings to fall back on when I get out of here. And after my… <he pauses for a moment, searching for the right word> disagreements with Duchess, the smartest move would probably be to bid Orgrimmar farewell for a while.",o="回到卡格莎身边，汇报阿尔达因可以效力。",oEN="Return to Kagtha and report Ardayn’s availability.",c="哦，我多爱看一场好戏！\n\n你知道这个区里有人饿得要死，愿意为一块面包皮去杀人吗？与此同时，上面那些人裹在丝绸和软垫里，为谁跟谁搞在一起而大惊小怪。\n\n不过嘛，法师就是法师。而我最喜欢的就是一个既吓得要死、又欠我们钱的 recruits。\n相关",cEN="Oh, how I love a good drama!\n\nDid you know there are people in this district starving to death, ready to kill for a crust of bread? Meanwhile, those up there, wrapped in silks and cushions, fussing over who’s getting it on with whom.\n\nBut hey, a mage is a mage. And there’s nothing I like more than a recruit who’s terrified and in debt to us.\nRelated"}
Q[1650122]={d="我们可能撞上麻烦了。一个大麻烦，血淋淋的。\n\n和我敲定船只交易的三位商人之一失踪了。格洛特卡。他本该在两个该死的小时前来见我签文件。你见过他吗？因为我肯定没有。\n\n我怕是最坏的情况。又是联盟的一次背后捅刀。但我需要确定。\n\n格洛特卡在这家旅店顶层租了个房间。你能上去看看吗？我不能让任何人看见我东张西望，否则他们会想从我们的绝望中捞好处。",dEN="We might have stumbled into a problem. A big, bloody one.\n\nOne of the three merchants I sealed the deal with for the ships has gone missing. Glotka. He was supposed to meet me two damn hours ago to sign the papers. Have you seen him? 'Cause I sure haven’t.\n\nI fear the worst. Another backstab from the Alliance. But I need to be sure.\n\nGlotka rents a room on the top floor of this inn. Can you go up and take a look? I can’t have anyone seeing me snooping around, or they’ll try to profit off our desperation.",o="调查奥格瑞玛深处大釜区旅店里格洛特卡的房间。",oEN="Investigate Glotka’s room at the Cauldron district inn in the Depths of Orgrimmar.",c="如果你在找格洛特卡，你来晚了。\n\n<兜帽投下的阴影在兽人脸上蒙上一层黑暗的面纱。>\n\n他们把他带走了。\n相关",cEN="If you're looking for Glotka, you're too late.\n\n<The shadow from his hood casts a dark veil over the orc's face.>\n\nThey took him.\nRelated"}
Q[1650123]={d="我一直在留意你。你的上级费尽心思掩盖行踪，但一条锁链的强度取决于它最薄弱的一环。而格洛特卡是那种总把过去拖在身后的人。\n\n我可以告诉你他们把他带去了哪里。但我要点回报：等你们启航前往阿扎尔时，给我在船上留个位置。\n\n<扎夫洛伸出一只畸形的手。犹豫片刻后，你握了上去，达成交易。>\n\n很好，我会盯着你兑现的。士兵们把格洛特卡带到了下屋顶的地牢。当然……你得先击败守卫，才能拿到打开他笼子的钥匙。",dEN="I’ve been keeping an eye on you. Your superiors have gone to great lengths to cover their tracks, but a chain is only as strong as its weakest link. And Glotka is the kind of man who’s always dragging his past behind.\n\nI can tell you where they took him. But I want something in return: guarantee me a spot on the ship when you set sail for Azzar.\n\n<Zavlor extends a disfigured hand. After hesitating for a moment, you shake it, sealing the deal.>\n\nAlright, I’ll hold you to that. The soldiers took Glotka to the dungeons in Underroof. Of course… you’ll have to defeat the guards to get the key that opens his cage.",o="在奥格瑞玛深处的下屋顶击败守卫，取回钥匙并释放格洛特卡。",oEN="Defeat the guards in the Underroof, in the Depths of Orgrimmar, to retrieve the key and free Glotka.",p="你……你不是他们中的一员。是谁派你来的？\n\n<格洛特卡飞快地扫了一眼你的武器和装束。>\n\n我明白了。你能不弄出太大动静就把我弄出去吗？",pEN="You... You're not one of them. Who sent you?\n\n<Glotka quickly scans your weapon and attire.>\n\nI see. Can you get me out of here without making too much noise?",c="这么多血……\n\n当然，你是卡格莎的打手，对吧？Ur'gora kim-ashan……我们究竟愿意走多远？\n相关",cEN="All this blood...\n\nOf course, you're Kagtha's grunt, aren’t you? Ur’gora kim-ashan... How far are we willing to go?\nRelated"}
Q[1650124]={d="谢谢你释放了我。不过……这感觉不对劲。那些士兵只是在服从命令。我希望……你没有杀他们。\n\n<格洛特卡耸了耸肩，流露出沮丧。这不是你刚把人从牢房里救出来时会期待的反应。>\n\n卡格莎会想知道我依然愿意签那些文件。经过这件事，我也没多少别的选择了。你先走吧。我需要一点时间振作起来……",dEN="I thank you for freeing me. Still... this doesn't feel right. These soldiers were just following orders. I hope... you didn’t kill them.\n\n<A shrug from Glotka shows his discouragement. It’s not the reaction you'd expect from someone you just rescued from a prison cell.>\n\nKagtha will want to know I’m still willing to sign the papers. After this, I don’t have many other options. You go ahead. I need a moment to pull myself together...",o="回到卡格莎身边，汇报格洛特卡的下落以及他愿意完成交易的意愿。",oEN="Return to Kagtha and report on Glotka’s whereabouts and his willingness to close the deal.",c="你干得很好，<name>，一如既往。你得到了我的认可。\n\n但我们不能放松警惕。在联盟间谍和……眼下这件事之间，任务岌岌可危。\n\n我们必须迅速行动，在他们有机会破坏我们的战役之前完成准备。\n相关",cEN="You’ve done a fine job, <name>, as usual. You have my recognition.\n\nBut we can’t take our foot off the gas. Between the Alliance spies and... now this, the mission is in jeopardy.\n\nWe must act quickly and wrap up preparations before they have a chance to ruin our campaign.\nRelated"}
Q[1650125]={d="Gakarah ma。给你寄那封信是个好举措。多亏了你，我们拥有所需的一切。我们的上级会很高兴。\n\n也许是时候让你见见他们了。我在下面还有活要干，尤其是考虑到我们刚刚发现的事。而你，倒可以去呼吸点新鲜空气。\n\n去码头。在岩石间找阿尔姆胡尔。告诉他，就我这边而言，事情已经差不多准备好了。",dEN="Gakarah ma. It was a good move sending you that letter. Thanks to you, we have everything we need. Our superiors will be pleased.\n\nPerhaps the time has come for you to meet them. I still have work to do down here, especially with what we've just uncovered. You, on the other hand, could use some fresh air.\n\nGo to the docks. Look for Armhul among the rocks. Tell him that, on my end, things are almost ready.",o="探索通往奥格瑞玛码头的隧道，并使用升降梯。\n\n在码头与阿尔姆胡尔交谈。",oEN="Explore the tunnel that leads to Orgrimmar’s docks and use the elevator.\n\nSpeak with Armhul at the docks.",c="下面一切都准备好了吗？\n\n<巨大的牛头人狐疑地看了你一眼。随后他向同伴们示意。>\n\n让我向你介绍我们的资助人：玛加萨，我族恐怖图腾的女族长；纳萨诺斯·凋零者，女妖之王的勇士；以及哈杜伦，银月城游侠将军。\n\n既然你来了，我有活给你。\n相关",cEN="Everything ready down there?\n\n<The massive tauren gives you a suspicious look. Then he gestures toward his companions.>\n\nLet me introduce you to our benefactors: Magatha, matriarch of my tribe, the Grimtotem; Nathanos Blightcaller, champion of the Banshee Queen; and Halduron, Ranger General of Silvermoon.\n\nSince you're here, I’ve got some work for you.\nRelated"}
Q[1650126]={d="格罗玛什要塞那些目光短浅的蠢货居然追踪到了军情七处的间谍，就在南边不远的一座海岸洞穴里。我们的线人说，加尔鲁什正在调动一支库卡隆突击队去解决他们。\n\n多亏你在旅店里和那个囚犯的那番小谈话，我们得知军情七处已经掌握了一些关于我们行动的情报。那种知识必须随他们一同死去。\n\n幸运的是，凯恩德瑞斯认为他找到了进入洞穴的办法，能让我们在库卡隆毫无察觉的情况下歼灭联盟间谍。把这些炸药带给他，帮他打通一条穿过洞穴、直抵敌方指挥官咽喉的路。\n相关",dEN="The short-sighted fools at Grommash Hold managed to track the SI:7 spies to a coastal cave, just south of here. Our contacts say Garrosh is mobilizing a Kor'kron strike team to take them out.\n\nThanks to the little chat you had with that prisoner at the inn, we know SI:7 has picked up a few details about our operation. That kind of knowledge needs to die with them.\n\nLuckily, Caindres thinks he’s found a way into the cave that'll let us wipe out the Alliance spies without the Kor'kron ever seeing us. Take these explosives to him, and help him carve a path through the cave straight to the enemy commander’s throat.\nRelated",c="干得好……我猜。\n\n联盟间谍一定感觉到了爆炸。他们现在会比以往更加紧张。\n\n他们自以为是有骄傲的幼狮。是他忠诚的一窝。但我看到的只有鼠辈；颤抖着、尖叫着，躲在自己的窝里。",cEN="Nice work… I guess.\n\nThe Alliance spies must’ve felt the blast. They’ll be more on edge than ever now.\n\nThey think themselves proud cubs of the Lion. His loyal brood. But all I see are ratlings; quivering, squealing, hiding in their burrow."}
Q[1650127]={d="就在我们说话的当口，五名联盟间谍正在前去放火烧剃刀岭的路上。\n\n什么？不，你不会去追他们。你来处理这件事。拿着。\n\n<塞拉腊把一叠卷轴和信件放进你手里。>\n\n这些文件将联盟与即将到来的大火直接联系起来。我要你把它们塞进间谍头目的胸腔里，就在洞穴深处。\n\n等库卡隆发现它们时，要阻止任何事都为时已晚。正如我们所愿。",dEN="As we speak, five Alliance spies are on their way to set Razor Hill on fire.\n\nWhat? No, you’re not going after them. You’re handling this. Here.\n\n<Selara places a stack of scrolls and letters into your hand.>\n\nThese documents link the Alliance directly to the coming fire. I want you to plant them in the spy leader’s chest, deep inside the cave.\n\nBy the time the Kor'kron find them, it'll be far too late to stop anything. Just the way we want it.",o="杀死战地指挥官迪尔肯，并把那些罪证文件塞进他的胸腔。",oEN="Kill Field Commander Dirken and plant the incriminating documents in his chest.",p="记住。把文件塞进敌方指挥官的胸腔。我们需要加尔鲁什和他的库卡隆把剃刀岭的大火归咎于联盟的破坏。",pEN="Remember. Plant the documents in the enemy commander’s chest. We need Garrosh and his Kor'kron to blame the Razor Hill fires on Alliance sabotage.",c="当加尔鲁什得知联盟是剃刀岭大火幕后黑手时，他会暴怒。现在就公然挑战萨尔对他来说还为时过早，但迟早，部落必须问自己这个问题：\n\n我们需要什么样的领袖，来回应联盟的越界？一位大酋长？还是一位和平酋长？\n相关",cEN="Garrosh will be furious when he learns that the Alliance was behind the Razor Hill fires. It’s still too early for him to openly challenge Thrall, but sooner or later, the Horde will need to ask itself this question:\n\nWhat kind of leader do we need to retaliate against the Alliance’s transgressions? A Warchief? Or a Peace Chief?\nRelated"}
Q[1650128]={d="一切都准备好了。我们的人已经控制了码头。恐怕在我们引起怀疑之前没多少时间了。必须迅速行动。\n\n我会留在这里，确保我们不留任何尾巴。你去和卡格莎谈谈。她正在格洛特卡的船上等你。\n\n如果我们不再相见……<el tauren se inclina hacia adelante y te mira intensamente>. 愿灵魂在阿扎尔群岛上指引你。",dEN="Everything is ready. Our people have taken control of the docks. I’m afraid we don’t have much time before we start raising suspicions. We must act quickly.\n\nI’ll stay behind to make sure we don’t leave any loose ends. You go speak with Kagtha. She’s waiting for you aboard Glotka’s ship.\n\nIf we don’t meet again... <the tauren leans forward and looks at you intensely>. May the spirits guide you on the Azzar Archipelago.",o="在奥格瑞玛港的码头与卡格莎交谈。",oEN="Speak with Kagtha at the docks of Orgrimmar’s port.",c="你闻到了吗？\n\n<卡格莎深深吸气，让海风充满肺腑。>\n\n希望。\n\n和平即是胜利。其他一切都是妄想。\n相关",cEN="Do you smell that?\n\n<Kagtha inhales deeply, filling her lungs with the sea breeze.>\n\nHope.\n\nPeace is victory. Anything else is delusion.\nRelated"}
Q[1650129]={d="我们拥有了所需的一切。甚至比我预想的还多。足以一声不响地把那些混蛋击沉在海上！\n\n他们想拿下阿扎尔城？我会很享受看他们尝试，而我们把他们派往群岛的船只一艘艘击沉。\n\n我们在阿扎尔的外交官只需要时间。迟早，油表财团的地精会效仿污水财团，加入部落。\n\n准备好就告诉我，<name>。夜幕一降临我们就启航。\n相关",dEN="We have everything we needed. Even more than I had anticipated. Enough to sink those bastards out at sea, without a word!\n\nThey want to take the city of Azzar? I’ll enjoy watching them try, as we sink the ships they send to the archipelago, one by one.\n\nOur diplomats in Azzar just need time. Sooner or later, the goblins of the Oilgauge cartel will follow the lead of the Bilgewater cartel and join the Horde.\n\nLet me know when you’re ready, <name>. We’ll set sail once night falls.\nRelated",o="一",oEN="One"}
Q[1650130]={d="没时间可以浪费了！\n\n跟紧我，准备战斗。如果联盟以为能打我们个措手不及……\n\n嗯，红色是部落的颜色。而这家旅店早就该刷新漆了。\n相关",dEN="No time to waste!\n\nStick close and get ready to fight. If the Alliance thought they could catch us with our pants down…\n\nWell, red is the color of the Horde. And this inn was long overdue for a fresh coat of paint.\nRelated",c="一幅画胜过千言万语。好好看看你的四周：如果我们失败，这就是等待我们的未来。\n\n<卡格莎指向那骇人的景象：血仍像喷泉一样从尚有余温的尸体中涌出。>\n\n联盟会不惜一切夺取阿扎尔群岛的控制权。而我们也会不惜一切阻止他们。",cEN="A picture’s worth a thousand words. Take a good look around: this is the future waiting for us if we fail.\n\n<Kagtha gestures toward the gruesome scene: blood still flows from warm corpses like fountains.>\n\nThe Alliance will do whatever it takes to seize control of the Azzar Archipelago. And we’ll do whatever it takes to stop them."}
Q[1650131]={d="别急。\n\n还有一件事我想了结。一个象征性的举动，真的；一桩小事，但对我个人意义重大。\n\n自从卡格莎开始谋划……不管她谋划的是什么，奥格瑞玛深处就爬满了联盟间谍。结果其中一个一路跟着你到了这里。\n\n真是胆大包天！别担心，我的人已经把他看押起来了。\n\n你愿意赏光，以我的名义执行处决吗？我的判决是：扔出窗外处死。",dEN="Not so fast.\n\nThere’s one more matter I wish to settle. A symbolic gesture, really; a trifle, but one of great personal importance.\n\nEver since Kagtha started scheming… whatever it is she's scheming, the Depths of Orgrimmar have been crawling with Alliance spies. Turns out one of them followed you all the way here.\n\nThe nerve! Don’t worry, my men already have him in custody.\n\nWould you do the honors and carry out the execution in my name? My sentence is death by defenestration.",o="把抓获的联盟间谍扔下深渊处决。",oEN="Execute the captured Alliance spy by throwing him into the abyss.",p="<女爵打了个哈欠，散发着帝王般的无聊。>\n\n哦，不，真的，别担心。你需要多少时间都可以……",pEN="<Duchess yawns, radiating imperial boredom.>\n\nOh no, really, don’t worry. Take all the time you need…",c="这算上，我们上个月已经扔出窗外处死了五名联盟间谍。\n\n嗯……严格来说，我们只扔了四个。第五个……啊，那天我心情很有创意。我决定试试变形术，把他变成了一只蝙蝠。\n\n当法术消退、他恢复人形时……\n\n<女爵用左手向下指了指。她耸了耸肩，但她的眼睛在笑。>\n相关",cEN="That makes five Alliance spies we’ve defenestrated this past month.\n\nWell… technically, we only threw four of them. The fifth… Ah, that was on a day I was feeling creative. I decided to try a polymorph spell and turned him into a bat.\n\nWhen the spell wore off and he returned to human form…\n\n<Duchess gestures downward with her left hand. She shrugs, but her eyes are smiling.>\nRelated"}
Q[1650132]={d="算术很简单。\n\n军情七处对我们的计划了解得太多了。\n\n一个都不能活。如果库卡隆抓到一个哪怕只知道最细微细节的间谍，只要一点审讯，大酋长和他的核心圈子就能弄清我们在谋划什么。\n\n凯恩德瑞斯会帮你解决他们。很合适，不是吗？把你卷进这件事的人，正是帮你终结它的人。",dEN="The math is simple.\n\nSI:7 has learned too much about our plans.\n\nNot a single one can be allowed to live. If the Kor'kron capture even one spy who knows the barest detail, a bit of questioning is all it’ll take for the Warchief and his inner circle to figure out what we’re up to.\n\nCaindres will help you finish them off. Fitting, isn’t it? That the one who brought you into this is the one who’ll help you end it.",o="在奥舒苟尔洞穴杀死十名联盟间谍。",oEN="Kill ten Alliance spies in the Oshu’gol Caverns.",p="那些间谍。一个都别留。",pEN="The spies. Leave none alive.",c="干得好。除非他们能让死人复活，否则我们的秘密安全了。\n相关",cEN="Good work. Unless they’re raising the dead, our secrets are safe.\nRelated"}
Q[1650236]={d="哦……你好！不知道你有没有注意到，但是……你看见过上面过山车上那些可怜的拧螺母工人吗？他们整天不停地拧螺栓和螺钉，就为了让轨道不散架！他们从黎明干到黄昏，而且……而且……太危险了！我忍不住替他们担心。\n\n我一直在为他们准备一些清凉的瓶装水，你知道的，能帮他们撑下去的东西……但，唉，不幸的是，我有严重的恐高症。你能不能……？我是说，如果不算太麻烦的话……你能把这些瓶子带给他们吗？交给轨道上的工人。我相信他们会感激的，更重要的是，这会让他们知道有人在乎他们。\n\n你说呢？你能帮我这个忙吗？",dEN="Oh... hello! I don't know if you've noticed, but… have you seen those poor nut-tighteners up there on the roller coaster? They spend all day tightening bolts and screws non-stop, just to keep the tracks from falling apart! They work from dawn till dusk, and… and… it's so dangerous! I can't help but worry about them.\n\nI've been preparing some refreshing water bottles for them, you know, something to help them keep going… But, ah, unfortunately, I have a terrible fear of heights. Could you please…? I mean, if it's not too much trouble… could you take these bottles to them? Give them to the workers on the tracks. I'm sure they'd appreciate it, and more importantly, it would let them know that someone cares about them.\n\nWhat do you say? Could you help me with this?",o="把 10 瓶\"塞尔玛的清凉之水\"分发给过山车上的拧螺母工人。",oEN="Distribute 10 \"Selma's Refreshing Water\" bottles to the nut-tighteners on the roller coaster.",p="那些拧螺母工人看起来渴坏了。你把我给你的瓶子都发完了吗？",pEN="The nut-tighteners look parched. Have you managed to hand out all the bottles I gave you?",c="你真是救星！那些拧螺母工人确实需要休息一下，哪怕只是喝点清水润润嗓子。\n\n拿着，这是给你的小谢礼，感谢你这样的好手。还有，别忘了自己也多喝水！",cEN="You're a lifesaver! Those nut-tighteners really needed a break, even if it was just to wet their whistles with some fresh water.\n\nHere, take this as a little thank you for being such a champ. And hey, don't forget to stay hydrated yourself!"}
Q[1650238]={d="嘿，你！对，就是你！过来一下，行吗？\n\n<布里达双手交叠在胸前，露出狡黠的笑容。>\n\n你想享受一名嘉年华工作人员能提供的所有好处吗？是啊，我可以帮你这个忙。一个忙换一个忙，你知道规矩的。你是联盟的人，对吧？\n\n地精们爱吹嘘阿扎尔是附近最自由的港口，但那些税收讲的却是另一个故事。对我们来说幸运的是，总有人走私。\n\n<布里达递给你一张卷轴，上面列着名字和货物。>\n\n这就是你需要的全部了。你会在暴风城的贸易区找到他们。等你买齐了所有东西，来阿扎尔集市找我。",dEN="Hey, you! Yes, you! Come here for a sec, will ya?\n\n<Bridda clasps her hands at her chest and flashes a cunning grin.>\n\nWould you like to enjoy all the perks a carnival worker can offer you? Yeah, I could help with that. A favor for a favor, you know how it goes. You're with the Alliance, right?\n\nThe goblins love to brag about how Azzar's the freest port around, but those taxes tell a different story. Lucky for us, there's always smuggling.\n\n<Bridda hands you a scroll with a list of names and goods.>\n\nThat's all you need. You'll find them in Stormwind, in the Trade District. Once you've bought everything, come find me at the Azzar Faire.",o="在暴风城贸易区购齐清单上的物品，带到阿扎尔集市交给布里达。",oEN="Get the listed goods in Stormwind’s Trade District and bring them to Bridda at the Azzar Faire.",p="你拿到补给了吗？我需要的东西都在暴风城贸易区有售。你很容易就能弄到，相信我。",pEN="Do you have the supplies? Everything I need is sold in the Trade District in Stormwind. It will be easy for you to get it, trust me.",c="等一下，我只想确认……好，完美。真是好一批货！\n\n有了符文线、地狱石和传送门符文，我就能做出一件了不起的东西。不过，我还需要成百上千的符文、线和石头。也许甚至上千。我还需要你继续把它们偷偷带进集市——一天一个应该不会引起怀疑。\n\n这是你的报酬。希望我们能把这桩小交易继续下去！",cEN="Hold on a sec, just wanna make sure… Alright, perfect. What a haul!\n\nWith the rune thread, infernal stone, and portal rune, I'll be able to whip up something fantastic. Though, I'm gonna need hundreds more runes, threads, and stones. Maybe even thousands. I'll still need you to sneak them into the faire—one a day shouldn't raise any eyebrows.\n\nHere is your reward. Hope we can keep this little arrangement going!"}
Q[1650239]={d="嘿，你！对，就是你！过来一下，行吗？\n\n<布里达双手交叠在胸前，露出狡黠的笑容。>\n\n你想享受一名嘉年华工作人员能提供的所有好处吗？是啊，我可以帮你这个忙。一个忙换一个忙，你知道规矩的。你是部落的人，对吧？\n\n地精们爱吹嘘阿扎尔是附近最自由的港口，但那些税收讲的却是另一个故事。对我们来说幸运的是，总有人走私。\n\n<布里达递给你一张卷轴，上面列着名字和货物。>\n\n这就是你需要的全部了。你会在奥格瑞玛的力量谷找到他们。等你买齐了所有东西，来阿扎尔集市找我。",dEN="Hey, you! Yes, you! Come here for a sec, will ya?\n\n<Bridda clasps her hands at her chest and flashes a cunning grin.>\n\nWould you like to enjoy all the perks a carnival worker can offer you? Yeah, I could help with that. A favor for a favor, you know how it goes. You're with the Horde, right?\n\nThe goblins love to brag about how Azzar's the freest port around, but those taxes tell a different story. Lucky for us, there's always smuggling.\n\n<Bridda hands you a scroll with a list of names and goods.>\n\nThat's all you need. You'll find them in Orgrimmar, in the Valley of Strength. Once you've bought everything, come find me at the Azzar Faire.",o="在奥格瑞玛力量谷购齐清单上的物品，带到阿扎尔集市交给布里达。",oEN="Get the listed goods in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength and bring them to Bridda at the Azzar Faire.",p="你拿到补给了吗？我需要的东西都在奥格瑞玛的力量谷有售。你很容易就能弄到，相信我。",pEN="Do you have the supplies? Everything I need is sold in the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar. It will be easy for you to get it, trust me.",c="等一下，我只想确认……好，完美。真是好一批货！\n\n有了符文线、地狱石和传送门符文，我就能做出一件了不起的东西。不过，我还需要成百上千的符文、线和石头。也许甚至上千。我还需要你继续把它们偷偷带进集市——一天一个应该不会引起怀疑。\n\n这是你的报酬。希望我们能把这桩小交易继续下去！",cEN="Hold on a sec, just wanna make sure… Alright, perfect. What a haul!\n\nWith the rune thread, infernal stone, and portal rune, I'll be able to whip up something fantastic. Though, I'm gonna need hundreds more runes, threads, and stones. Maybe even thousands. I'll still need you to sneak them into the faire—one a day shouldn't raise any eyebrows.\n\nHere is your reward. Hope we can keep this little arrangement going!"}
Q[1650271]={d="准备好再次押注那只获胜的蜗牛了吗？\n\n你知道怎么玩的！只要仔细观察那些蜗牛，相信你的直觉，挑出你相信会第一个冲过终点线的那只。\n\n一旦你下定决心，来找我，告诉我你要押哪只蜗牛。如果你的蜗牛赢了，你会带走一份丰厚的奖励！\n\n没有花招，没有伎俩。那么，你还在等什么？选好你的蜗牛，下好你的注，愿好运永远站在你这边！",dEN="Ready to bet again on the winning snail?\n\nYou know how it goes! Just watch the snails closely, trust your gut, and pick the one you think will cross the finish line first.\n\nOnce you've made up your mind, come see me and tell me which snail you're betting on. If your snail wins, you'll walk away with a generous reward!\n\nNo tricks, no gimmicks. So, what are you waiting for? Pick your snail, place your bet, and may the odds be ever in your favor!",o="在阿扎尔集市押注一场蜗牛赛跑。",oEN="Bet on a snail race at the Azzar Faire.",p="嘿！你下注了吗？如果下了，就到地下去，为你那黏糊糊的赛手加油。祝你好运！",pEN="Hey! Have you placed your bet yet? If so, head down to the underground and cheer on your slimy racer. Good luck!",c="好运对你的投注微笑了吗？\n\n作为参与并给这场蜗牛赛跑一个机会的答谢，请收下这份奖励。\n\n祝你未来的投注好运！\n相关",cEN="Did luck smile on your bet?\n\nAs a thank you for participating and giving this snail race a shot, accept this reward.\n\nGood luck with your future bets!\nRelated"}
Q[1650273]={d="我就知道你会回来玩我的游戏，翁卡翁卡！你大概还记得，你在这个小游戏上花的每一枚代币，都能帮助这个濒危物种在艾泽拉斯继续生存下去，对吧？\n\n让我快速提醒你目标，虽然你已经知道怎么玩了：骑上一只翁卡坐骑，探索帐篷，在时间耗尽前救出走失的翁卡。但要小心陷阱！\n\n去玩吧，展现你的担当，尽可能多地救出翁卡。救得最多的人获胜！",dEN="I knew you'd be back to try my game, Wonka Wonka! You probably remembered that every token you spend on this mini-game helps this endangered species continue to survive in Azeroth, right?\n\nLet me quickly remind you of the goal, though you already know how it works: hop on a wonka mount, explore the tent, and rescue the lost wonkas before time runs out. But watch out for traps!\n\nPlay, show your commitment, and save as many wonkas as you can. Whoever rescues the most, wins!",o="完成一局翁卡翁卡！游戏。",oEN="Complete a Wonka Wonka! game.",p="别担心，你的贡献也有助于为翁卡们保持稳定供应的鲜嫩香甜的香蕉。进来吧，好好利用它们！",pEN="Don't worry, your contribution also goes toward keeping a steady supply of tender, sweet bananas ready for the wonkas. Come on in and put them to good use!",c="你看到这有多刺激了吗？每一局都重要，多亏你对这游戏的投入，这些小家伙们有了重新快乐飞翔的机会……当然，是在帐篷里。\n\n所以，如果你要在哪里花掉你的代币，一定要选这里，在这里乐趣与善举融为一体。不管你的成绩如何，你都是一件重要事业的一部分，我的朋友！\n相关",cEN="Did you see how exciting it is? Every game matters, and thanks to your investment in the game, these little ones have a new chance to fly happily... inside the tent, of course.\n\nSo, if you're going to spend your tokens somewhere, make sure it's here, where fun and a good cause come together. No matter how you did, you're part of something important, my friend!\nRelated"}
Q[1650274]={d="哦……嘿，你回来了！是这样，我一直在下面盯着那些拧螺母工人，而且……我不想唠叨，但过山车那队人看起来还是彻底累垮、渴得不行。他们干得太辛苦了，而且，说实在的，他们这活儿基本就是一张通往危险谷的单程票！天哪……\n\n所以我在想——如果不算太麻烦的话——也许你可以，你知道的，顺路过去再放几瓶清凉的水？我只是不想让他们觉得在外头是孤军奋战……因为他们不是。我们支持他们，对吧？\n\n所以……如果你有空，能不能……也许再帮他们一次？求求你了？",dEN="Oh… hey there, you're back! So, I've been keeping an eye on those nut-tighteners from down here, and… I don't want to be a nag, but the roller coaster crew still looks totally wiped out and parched. They're working so hard, and, let's be real, their job's pretty much a one-way ticket to Dangerville! Yikes…\n\nSo, I was thinking—if it's not too much trouble—maybe you could, you know, swing by and drop off some more refreshing water bottles? I just don't want them thinking they're on their own out there… because they're not. We've got their backs, right?\n\nSo… if you've got a sec, could you… maybe help them out again? Pretty please?",o="把 10 瓶\"塞尔玛的清凉之水\"分发给过山车上的拧螺母工人。",oEN="Distribute 10 \"Selma's Refreshing Water\" bottles to the nut-tighteners on the roller coaster.",p="那些拧螺母工人看起来渴坏了。你把我给你的瓶子都发完了吗？",pEN="The nut-tighteners look parched. Have you managed to hand out all the bottles I gave you?",c="你真是救星！那些拧螺母工人确实需要休息一下，哪怕只是喝点清水润润嗓子。\n\n拿着，这是给你的小谢礼，感谢你这样的好手。还有，别忘了自己也多喝水！",cEN="You're a lifesaver! Those nut-tighteners really needed a break, even if it was just to wet their whistles with some fresh water.\n\nHere, take this as a little thank you for being such a champ. And hey, don't forget to stay hydrated yourself!"}
Q[1650275]={d="嘿，你！再去你阵营的首都跑一趟小差事怎么样？\n\n走私从不过时，而在我的杰作完成之前，我会需要大量材料。\n\n<布里达递给你一张卷轴，上面列着名字和货物。>\n\n这就是你需要的全部了。你会在暴风城的贸易区找到他们。等你买齐了所有东西，来阿扎尔集市找我。",dEN="Hey, you! How about taking another little trip to your faction's capital?\n\nSmuggling never goes out of style, and I'm going to need a ton of materials before my masterpiece is finished.\n\n<Bridda hands you a scroll with a list of names and goods.>\n\nThat's all you need. You'll find them in Stormwind, in the Trade District. Once you've bought everything, come find me at the Azzar Faire.",o="在暴风城贸易区购齐清单上的物品，带到阿扎尔集市交给布里达。",oEN="Get the listed goods in Stormwind’s Trade District and bring them to Bridda at the Azzar Faire.",p="你拿到补给了吗？我需要的东西都在暴风城贸易区有售。你很容易就能弄到，相信我。",pEN="Do you have the supplies? Everything I need is sold in the Trade District in Stormwind. It will be easy for you to get it, trust me.",c="等一下，我只想确认……好，完美。又是好一批货！我不该怀疑你；你在这方面很有天分。但是，你知道的……有备无患。\n\n有了符文线、地狱石和传送门符文，我就能做出一件了不起的东西。不过，我还需要成百上千的符文、线和石头。也许甚至上千。我还需要你继续把它们偷偷带进集市——一天一个应该不会引起怀疑。",cEN="Hold on a sec, just wanna make sure… Alright, perfect. Another great haul! I shouldn't doubt you; you've got a knack for this. But, you know… better safe than sorry.\n\nWith the rune thread, infernal stone, and portal rune, I'll be able to whip up something fantastic. Though, I'm gonna need hundreds more runes, threads, and stones. Maybe even thousands. I'll still need you to sneak them into the faire—one a day shouldn't raise any eyebrows."}
Q[1650276]={d="嘿，你！再去你阵营的首都跑一趟小差事怎么样？走私从不过时，而在我的杰作完成之前，我会需要大量材料。<布里达递给你一张卷轴，上面列着名字和货物。>这就是你需要的全部了。你会在奥格瑞玛的力量谷找到他们。等你买齐了所有东西，来阿扎尔集市找我。",dEN="Hey, you! How about taking another little trip to your faction's capital?Smuggling never goes out of style, and I'm going to need a ton of materials before my masterpiece is finished.<Bridda hands you a scroll with a list of names and goods.>That's all you need. You'll find them in Orgrimmar, in the Valley of Strength. Once you've bought everything, come find me at the Azzar Faire.",o="在奥格瑞玛力量谷购齐清单上的物品，带到阿扎尔集市交给布里达。",oEN="Get the listed goods in Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength and bring them to Bridda at the Azzar Faire.",p="你拿到补给了吗？我需要的东西都在奥格瑞玛的力量谷有售。你很容易就能弄到，相信我。",pEN="Do you have the supplies? Everything I need is sold in the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar. It will be easy for you to get it, trust me.",c="等一下，我只想确认……好，完美。又是好一批货！我不该怀疑你；你在这方面很有天分。但是，你知道的……有备无患。\n\n有了符文线、地狱石和传送门符文，我就能做出一件了不起的东西。不过，我还需要成百上千的符文、线和石头。也许甚至上千。我还需要你继续把它们偷偷带进集市——一天一个应该不会引起怀疑。",cEN="Hold on a sec, just wanna make sure… Alright, perfect. Another great haul! I shouldn't doubt you; you've got a knack for this. But, you know… better safe than sorry.\n\nWith the rune thread, infernal stone, and portal rune, I'll be able to whip up something fantastic. Though, I'm gonna need hundreds more runes, threads, and stones. Maybe even thousands. I'll still need you to sneak them into the faire—one a day shouldn't raise any eyebrows."}
Q[1660000]={d="<一个女人迎上前来，明显焦躁不安。她眼中闪过愤怒与忧虑交织的锐利神色。>\n\n抱歉，我不是故意要闹出动静的，但是……我那个该死的哥哥，总是埋头在他的书里！我在外面站了老半天，扯着嗓子喊，一点用都没有。守卫已经又一次警告我\"扰乱修道院的安宁\"了。\n\n你介意进去一趟，必要时揪着他的耳朵把他拖出来吗？我们的母亲已经弥留，我走了很远的路来带他回去，好让他能道别。这个不知感恩的混蛋。",dEN="<A woman greets you, visibly agitated. A sharp mix of anger and worry flashes in her eyes.>\n\nSorry, I didn’t mean to make a scene, but… that blasted brother of mine, always buried in his books! I’ve been out here forever, yelling my lungs out, and nothing. The guards have already warned me about “disturbing the abbey’s peace” one more time.\n\nWould you mind going in there and dragging him out by the ears if you have to? Our mother’s on her deathbed, and I’ve traveled a long way to fetch him so he can say goodbye. The ungrateful wretch.",o="与比安卡·斯帕达的哥哥、修士莫罗伊交谈。",oEN="Speak with Seminarian Moroi, brother of Bianca Spada.",c="顺便问一下，是我姐姐派你来的吗？\n\n我已经告诉过她现在不是好时候；不过说实话，跟她打交道从来没有好时候。\n\n总之，我正处在某项发现的中间，它……让我完全沉浸其中。也许你有兴趣搭把手？",cEN="Did my sister send you, by any chance?\n\nI already told her this isn’t a good time; although honestly, there’s never a good time to deal with her.\n\nAnyway, I’m in the middle of a discovery that… has me completely absorbed. Maybe you’d be interested in lending a hand?"}
Q[1660001]={d="来吧，看看。\n\n<莫罗伊指向吸引他注意的那本书：一本薄薄、破旧的手稿，跟它的读者倒有几分相似。>\n\n我在图书馆里偶然发现的；它不在修道院的记录中。我想它是某种关于一位被指控为异端的老修女的编年史。匆忙之中，我把好几页弄丢了。我一直在试着把它们拼回去，但还缺一些。\n\n你能在修道院里转转，把我丢的书页找回来吗？这是一本禁书；如果被人发现我在不该插手的地方乱翻，他们会把我送回家……送到我姐姐那儿。\n\n行行好，可以吗？",dEN="Go on, take a look.\n\n<Moroi gestures toward the book holding his attention: a thin, battered manuscript, not unlike its reader.>\n\nI stumbled across it in the library; it’s not listed in the abbey’s records. I think it’s some sort of chronicle about an old abbess accused of heresy. In my haste, I’ve misplaced several pages. I’ve been trying to piece them back together, but some are still missing.\n\nCould you have a look around the abbey and recover the pages I lost? This is a banned book; if anyone finds out I’ve been poking my nose where it doesn’t belong, they’ll ship me back home… to my sister.\n\nDo me a mercy, will you?",o="找回莫罗伊那份未登记手稿中散落在修道院各处的遗失书页。",oEN="Recover the missing pages from Moroi’s unclassified manuscript, scattered throughout the abbey.",p="你找到那些书页了吗？",pEN="Have you found the pages?",c="那么，我们这儿有什么？\n\n<莫罗伊急切地查看你带来的书页。>\n\n这填补了几处空白：那位被指控为异端的修女受宗教裁判所审判并被逐出教会。难怪教会想把整件事从记录中抹去。他们忘了烧掉这本书，几乎算是个奇迹。\n\n这让人不禁想问，她到底做了什么才招来这样的惩罚，对吧？",cEN="Well, what do we have here?\n\n<Moroi eagerly inspects the pages you’ve brought him.>\n\nThat clears up a few gaps: the abbess accused of heresy was tried by the Inquisition and excommunicated. No wonder the Church wanted the whole thing wiped from the records. It’s almost a miracle they forgot to burn this book.\n\nMakes you wonder what she did to earn such a punishment, doesn’t it?"}
Q[1660002]={d="去一趟审判那位修女的地牢，也许能揭开一些线索……\n\n根据书上的说法，如今已被废弃的北郡镇有一处通往宗教裁判所地牢的秘密入口。\n\n我会在你的地图上标出来，但要小心行事。已经很多年没人踏足那个地方了……我宁愿不去想象什么样的害虫占据了它的废墟。",dEN="A visit to the dungeon where the abbess was tried might shed some light…\n\nAccording to the book, the now-abandoned town of Northshire held a secret entrance to the Inquisitorial Dungeon.\n\nI’ll mark it on your map, but tread carefully. No one’s set foot in that place for years… I’d rather not imagine what vermin have claimed its ruins.",o="找到秘密宗教裁判所地牢的地窖入口。",oEN="Locate the cellar entrance to the Secret Inquisitorial Dungeon.",p="道路已经封闭……",pEN="The way is shut…",c="道路已经封闭，凡人。\n\n这座地牢是亡者的家园，而亡者守护着它。\n\n生时为狱卒，死后为囚徒……我们所有人，都是她诅咒的受害者。\n\n道路已经封闭。",cEN="The way is shut, mortal.\n\nThe dungeon is home to the Dead, and the Dead keep it so.\n\nJailers in life, prisoners in death… all of us, victims of her curse.\n\nThe way is shut."}
Q[1660003]={d="道路已经封闭。修女诅咒了那些审判她的人，把他们束缚成不得安息的游魂。\n\n那些死去的人仍被她的力量锁链束缚。他们从她身上剥夺的尊严与财物变成了镣铐。一句简单的祈祷。一声真诚的恳求。那就足够了……\n\n直到有人净化修女散落在地牢各处的圣物，他们才能得到安息。\n\n但亡者把它们看守得很好。因此，道路依旧封闭。",dEN="The way is shut. The abbess cursed those who judged her, binding them to wander as restless spirits.\n\nThose who died are still chained by her power. The dignity and belongings they stripped from her became shackles. A simple prayer. A sincere plea. That would be enough...\n\nThey’ll find no rest until someone purifies the abbess’s relics, scattered throughout the dungeon.\n\nBut the Dead guard them well. And so, the way remains shut.",o="净化散落在秘密宗教裁判所地牢中的前修女遗物。",oEN="Purify the belongings of the former abbess, scattered throughout the Secret Inquisitorial Dungeon.",p="道路依旧封闭，凡人……\n\n一个永恒的灵魂暗夜。",pEN="The way is still shut, mortal...\n\nAn eternal Dark Night of the Soul.",c="诅咒……\n\n道路已经打开。我能感觉到；一道温暖的光正召唤我的灵魂前往别处。\n\n<女祭司看起来比之前更清醒、更有意识。>\n\n我曾被称为阿尔玛修女，北郡修道院的女祭司。\n\n你下来这里寻求知识。你不是第一个。但我相信你会是最后一个。\n\n很好。我会告诉你关于西蒂斯的事。",cEN="The curse…\n\nThe way has opened. I can feel it; a warm light calling my spirit elsewhere.\n\n<The priestess seems more awake, more aware than before.>\n\nI was once called Sister Alma, priestess of Northshire Abbey.\n\nYou came down here seeking knowledge. You’re not the first. But I trust you’ll be the last.\n\nVery well. I will tell you about Sitis."}
Q[1660004]={d="西蒂斯曾是……一场风暴。她的教义不合正统；甚至危险。许多学生因她而离开教会。\n\n所以，当宗教裁判法庭传唤我作证时，我同意出面指证她。\n\n我得知她在瀑布上方一座旧宅邸里与她最亲近的圈子举行秘密集会。在那些集会上，西蒂斯谈论圣光、生命、死亡……\n\n以及暗影的本质。\n\n她的异端至今仍玷污着那片土地。但如果你去那里，务必小心；她从不缺追随者，而宗教裁判所从未把他们全部抓获……",dEN="Sitis was... a storm. Her teachings were unorthodox; dangerous, even. Many students left the Church because of her.\n\nSo when the inquisitorial court summoned me to testify, I agreed to speak against her.\n\nI had learned she was holding secret gatherings with her closest circle at an old manor above the waterfall. In those meetings, Sitis spoke of the Light, of life, of death...\n\nAnd of the nature of the Shadow.\n\nHer heresy still stains that land. But beware if you go there; she had no shortage of followers, and the Inquisition never caught them all...",o="找到通往瀑布顶端的隐秘路径，直面北郡前修女的罪孽。",oEN="Find the hidden path leading to the top of the waterfall and confront the sins of the former abbess of Northshire.",p="你了解到什么了吗？",pEN="Learned anything?",c="莫罗伊专注地听你讲述。\n\n人们说笔比剑更有力，而西蒂斯……这名字取得真贴切。它的意思是\"渴\"。从你告诉我的来看，她是一个渴求真相与知识的女人。\n\n我实在不觉得那算是罪。\n\n这是我的计划，<name>：我会和姐姐一起走，向母亲道别，而在回修道院的路上，我会去你提到过的那个地方看看，就是西蒂斯举行她最大胆集会的所在。\n\n\"除无知外，别无黑暗。\"我感谢你的警告，但在我揭开真相之前，我的心无法安歇……无论你提到的风险有多大。相关",cEN="<Moroi listens to your account intently.>\n\nThey say the pen is mightier than the sword, and Sitis... fitting name. It means “thirst.” From what you’ve told me, she was a woman thirsty for truth and knowledge.\n\nI hardly think that’s a sin.\n\nHere’s my plan, <name>: I’ll go with my sister, say my goodbyes to my mother, and on my way back to the abbey, I’ll stop by that place you spoke of, where Sitis held her most daring gatherings.\n\n“There is no darkness but ignorance.” I thank you for the warning, but my mind won’t rest until I uncover the truth... no matter the risks you’ve mentioned."}
Q[1660005]={d="我需要……帮助。\n\n<士兵的声音沙哑断续，被痛苦哽住。每一次皱眉都是一道新伤。>\n\n我奉命找到鱼人村落，消除他们的威胁。但如你所见，这条路对我并不友善。更糟的是：通往上游河流的唯一小径，正好穿过那座塔。\n\n<他虚弱地朝那座隐现的废墟建筑点了点头。>\n\n而你……也许能在我失败的地方成功。\n\n处理盘踞在那座塔里的迪菲亚，削减瀑布上方鱼人的数量，你就是在帮我一个整个王国都会感谢你的忙。",dEN="I need… help.\n\n<The soldier’s voice comes ragged, choked with pain. Each grimace is a fresh wound.>\n\nI was ordered to find the murloc village, to cut off their threat. But, as you can see, the road has not been kind to me. And worse yet: the only path to the upper river runs straight through that tower.\n\n<He nods weakly toward the looming, ruined structure.>\n\nYou, though… you might succeed where I could not.\n\nDeal with the Defias infesting the tower, thin the ranks of the murlocs above the falls, and you’ll be doing me a favor the whole kingdom will thank you for.",o="击败潜伏在废墟之塔中的迪菲亚，并削减瀑布顶端、绳索桥对面暗井鱼人的数量。",oEN="Defeat the Defias lurking in the ruined tower and thin the ranks of the Shadewell murlocs atop the waterfall, across the rope bridge.",p="别为我担心；我跟不上了，但我还能守住阵地。",pEN="Don’t worry about me; I can’t follow, but I can still hold my ground.",c="你做到了……<他喘着气。>\n\n我如此自豪地穿着这身军装，却不得不求助于军队之外的人，这让我羞愧。\n\n本该是我的职责去完成它，但如你所见，我连跛着走回修道院的力气都没有了。\n\n暴风城欠你一声谢，<class>……我也一样。",cEN="You did it… <he gasps for breath.>\n\nIt shames the uniform I wear with such pride that I had to turn to someone outside the army.\n\nIt should have been my duty to see it done, but, as you can see, I haven’t the strength to even limp back to the Abbey.\n\nStormwind owes you thanks, <class>… and so do I."}
Q[1660006]={d="啊，一位旅行者！只看你的装束我就知道你来自远方。\n\n靠近些，看。我这刚出生的孩子患有一种没有治疗师能治好的病。他时日无多了。但他的哥哥拒绝接受这一点。\n\n在路上某处，他听说了某个\"集会\"的传言，声称能治愈一切疾病。格雷尔宾像溺水者抓住浮木一样抓住这份希望，动身去寻找他们。\n\n那是两周前的事了。他还没回来，更糟的是，风现在从我最末次看到他离去的方向带来难看的黑烟。我怕是最坏的情况。\n\n求你……跟随他的脚步，把他带回来给我。神明已经判定我必须失去一个儿子。我不会两个都失去。",dEN="Ah, a traveler! One look at your garb and I knew you’d come from afar.\n\nCome closer, look. This newborn of mine suffers from an illness no healer has managed to cure. He has little time left. But his older brother refuses to accept that.\n\nSomewhere along the way, he heard whispers of a “congregation” claiming to have a cure for all ailments. Grelbin clung to that hope like a drowning man to driftwood, and left to find them.\n\nThat was two weeks ago. He hasn’t returned yet, and worse, the wind now carries an ugly black smoke from the direction I last saw him go. I fear the worst.\n\nPlease… follow in his footsteps, and bring him back to me. The gods have already judged that I must give up one son. I won’t lose them both.",o="跟随格罗尔德哈之子格雷尔宾的脚步，调查黑烟的来源。",oEN="Follow in the footsteps of Grelbin, son of Groldha, and investigate the source of the smoke.",p="<这只地精毫无疑问地、不可逆转地死了。>",pEN="<The goblin is, beyond any doubt, irreversibly dead.>",c="<这只地精从火箭残骸中爬出了他能爬的最远距离，直到力气耗尽，最后一声呼噜作响的呼吸从他烧焦的喉咙里逸出。>\n\n<尽管坠毁把他的双腿压成了血淋淋的肉酱，一沓文件仍从他烧焦、磨破的裤袋里支棱出来。>",cEN="<The goblin had crawled from the wreckage of the rocket as far as he could before his strength gave out and his final, rattling breath escaped his scorched throat.>\n\n<Though the crash had reduced his legs to bloody pulp, a wad of papers still juts from the pocket of his scorched, threadbare trousers.>"}
Q[1660007]={d="<在搜刮尸体之前，你推断这只地精不会介意口袋里的文件。>\n\n<翻阅这些文件，你拼凑出这只地精属于一支被派去寻找冷脊山脉中一群神秘苦修者的队伍；正是格罗尔德哈之子格雷尔宾前去寻找的同一群人。>\n\n<在文件中，你找到一张地图，标出了一条沿山而上前往苦修者隐秘领地的小路。>",dEN="<Before looting the body, you reason that the goblin won’t be missing the papers in his pocket.>\n\n<Thumbing through them, you piece together that the goblin was part of a crew sent to locate a mysterious group of ascetics in the Coldridge Mountains; the very same group Grelbin, Groldha’s son, went searching for.>\n\n<Among the papers, you find a map marking a path up the mountain to the ascetics’ hidden domain.>",o="沿着山路前行，找出那个神秘团体的位置。",oEN="Follow the mountain path to uncover the location of the mysterious group.",p="你到底是谁？",pEN="And just who in blazes are you?",c="以我的胡子起誓……！我差点一枪打穿你。差点把我吓死。\n\n来，坐下。<矮人热情地朝一只凳子示意，那是你在这片冰封荒原上能找到的唯一温暖。>\n\n你在找格罗尔德哈的儿子，是吧？可怜的女人。他是最新一个加入那帮疯子行列的新兵。",cEN="By my beard…! I nearly put a bullet through you. Nearly scared the life out of me.\n\nHere, have a seat. <The dwarf gestures warmly toward a stool, the only warmth you’ll find in this frozen wasteland.>\n\nLooking for Groldha’s boy, are you? Poor woman. He’s the latest recruit to join those lunatics’ ranks."}
Q[1660008]={d="前面就是光辉镇的大门，那教派渣滓的老鼠窝。他们自称\"光辉者\"。我已经监视他们一个月了。\n\n他们相信，沐浴在那场摧毁诺莫瑞根的辐射中，会赐予他们某种启示，或天知道什么东西。\n\n他们很危险；既是异端，也是叛党。他们的首领已经自封为王，你信不信。而我有命令要看他被处决。\n\n既然你来了……我有个主意。\n\n沿着路走，侦查前方的森林，砍倒几个那样的狂信徒。给我带些他们盔甲的碎片回来。我有个点子……你会看到的！",dEN="Up ahead are the gates to Radiance Town, a rat’s nest of that sect’s rabble. They call themselves “The Radiants.” I’ve been keeping watch on them for a month now.\n\nThey believe bathing in the same radiation that devastated Gnomeregan will grant them some kind of revelation, or Light knows what.\n\nThey’re dangerous; heretics as well as rebels. Their leader’s crowned himself king, if you can believe it. And I have orders to see him executed.\n\nNow that you’re here… a plan comes to mind.\n\nFollow the road, scout the forest ahead, and cut down a few of those zealots. Bring me back some pieces of their armor. I’ve got an idea… you’ll see!",o="杀死光辉者狂信徒，收集他们的盔甲碎片。把它们交给阿拉斯洛，好让他制作一套伪装。",oEN="Slay Radiant fanatics and collect their armor pieces. Deliver them to Arathror so he can craft a disguise.",p="暖和过来了吗？没有什么比一场痛快的打斗更能抵御山中的严寒了！",pEN="Warmed up yet? Nothing like a good brawl to survive the mountain cold!",c="嗯，这能用……\n\n注意，不太合你的尺码，但总比合我的身。光是我这鼻子就塞不进那么小的头盔。",cEN="Aye, this’ll do…\n\nNot quite your size, mind, but it’ll fit you better than me. My nose alone wouldn’t fit in a helmet that small."}
Q[1660009]={d="我和光辉者打过太多次照面了；他们一眼就能认出我。可你……你是新面孔。一张陌生的脸。\n\n嗯，我想这套伪装能过关。准备好就告诉我，我帮你穿上。不，不是那样，别犯傻。\n\n一旦伪装好，就低下头。不引人注目地穿过村子到另一头，找到他们所谓的国王。大多数教派一旦失去强势的领袖就会土崩瓦解。\n\n如果这也是其中之一，你也许正好来得及救下格罗尔德哈的儿子，不让他丧失心智。",dEN="I’ve had too many run-ins with the Radiant; they’d spot me in a heartbeat. You, though… you’re new. An unknown face.\n\nAye, I think this disguise will pass. Let me know when you’re ready and I’ll help you into it. No, not like that, don’t be daft.\n\nOnce you’re disguised, keep your head down. Cross the village to the far side without drawing attention, and find their so-called king. Most cults fall apart without a strong leader.\n\nIf this is one of them, you might just be in time to save Groldha’s son from losing his mind.",o="在准备好穿上伪装时告诉阿拉斯洛。然后潜入光辉镇，杀死教派领袖「光辉陛下」。",oEN="Tell Arathror when you’re ready to don the disguise. Then infiltrate Radiance Town and slay the cult leader, His Radiant Majesty.",p="回到铁炉堡了？还没带回我的儿子……我猜你没能找到他。哎呀，我好苦命啊！",pEN="Back in Anvilmar? And without my son… I take it you didn’t find him. Oh, woe is me!",c="你回来了！我本想告诉你，但不知道去哪里找你：你走后不久格雷尔宾就回来了。你简直不会相信……他带回了听说过的那个\"奇迹疗法\"。\n\n我还不能说小家伙的健康有所好转，但这场冒险是值得的。\n\n可惜格雷尔宾现在不在；没有什么比把你们互相介绍更让我骄傲的了。我那儿子……像他父亲一样强壮、勇敢，也一样固执。\n\n他回集会去了。说他在那些学者中交到了很好的朋友。也许，如果他回来时你还在铁炉堡，你会亲自见到他……",cEN="You’re back! I wanted to tell you, but didn’t know where to find you: Grelbin returned not long after you left. And you won’t believe it… he brought that “miracle cure” he’d heard about.\n\nI can’t yet say it’s improved the little one’s health, but the risk was worth it.\n\nIt’s a shame Grelbin isn’t here now; nothing would make me prouder than to introduce you. That son of mine… strong, brave, and stubborn as his father was.\n\nHe’s gone back to the congregation. Says he’s made great friends among those scholars. Perhaps, if you’re still in Anvilmar when he returns, you’ll meet him yourself…"}
Q[1660010]={d="如果你能溜进光辉镇……有件事我可能需要你帮忙。\n\n我一直在试图弄懂辐射是如何运作的，寻找抵消其影响的方法。为此……我造了这个：\n\n<雷德娜给你看了一件只是隐约像步枪的装置。>\n\n杀死一些辐射软泥怪，然后扣动这宝贝的扳机。它会吸取软泥的精华，运气好的话，能让我分离出诱变剂。",dEN="If you can sneak your way into Radiance Town… there’s something I could use your help with.\n\nI’ve been trying to understand how radiation works, looking for a way to counter its effects. For that purpose… I built this:\n\n<Redna shows you a contraption that only vaguely resembles a rifle.>\n\nKill a few radioactive slimes, then pull the trigger on this beauty. It’ll siphon the essence out of the slime and, with luck, let me isolate the mutagen.",o="杀死光辉镇的辐射软泥怪，并对它们的尸体使用污染提取器来采集诱变剂。",oEN="Slay radioactive slimes in Radiance Town and use the Contamination Extractor on their corpses to harvest mutagen.",p="有了这些诱变剂样本，我就离揭开辐射之谜更近一步了。",pEN="With those mutagen samples, I’ll be one step closer to unraveling the mystery of radiation.",c="成功了。有意思。说实话，我并不完全确定它不会在你手里炸开。\n\n<雷德娜用因辐射而脱落了指甲的手指挠了挠斑秃的头皮。随后她扶了扶翠绿色的护目镜，那让她看上去像只变色龙，透着诡异。>\n\n用我手头这些简陋工具分析样本需要一些时间。但我会把这件事查个水落石出。而等我做到了，我会拿一把鹤嘴锄，挖得更深。\n\n我会找到解药。",cEN="It worked. Interesting. To be honest, I wasn’t entirely sure it wouldn’t blow up in your hands.\n\n<Redna scratches at her scalp, patchy with bald spots, using fingers stripped of nails by radiation. Then she adjusts her emerald-green goggles, which give her the uncanny look of a chameleon.>\n\nIt’ll take me some time to analyze the samples with the crude tools I’ve got here. But I will get to the bottom of this. And when I do, I’ll take a pickaxe and dig even deeper.\n\nI’ll find a cure."}
Q[1660011]={d="新来的？\n\n原谅我；也许我以前碰见过你，但我的记忆……闪闪烁烁，时有时无，像一盏将熄的灯泡。\n\n无论朋友还是陌生人，我可能需要你帮忙。<拉胡德憋住一声负疚的轻笑，显然很尴尬。>别以为我想逃避职责；我本打算做的，真的！但后来我头晕了……\n\n<侏儒咽回一个嗝，猛地挺直身子，抽搐着，仿佛抓到了带电的电线。>\n\n你只需要给镇上的一些居民喷洒一点受祝福的辐射。你知道的，他们每周的剂量。替我做了这个，我将永远感激你！",dEN="New around here?\n\nForgive me; might be I’ve run into you before, but my memory… it flickers, in and out, like a dying bulb.\n\nFriend or stranger, I could use your help. <Lahud stifles a guilty little giggle, clearly embarrassed.> Don’t think I’m trying to weasel out of my duty; I meant to do it, truly! But then I got woozy…\n\n<The gnome swallows back a burp and jerks upright, twitching as if he’d grabbed a live wire.>\n\nAll you need to do is spray a bit of blessed radiation on some of the townsfolk. You know, their weekly dose. Do this for me and I’ll be forever in your debt!",o="使用辐射喷雾器给辐光镇的居民喷洒辐射。",oEN="Use the Radiation Sprayer to douse Radiaville’s townsfolk with radiation.",p="你……做完了……？",pEN="You’re… done…?",c="<发作越来越严重了。侏儒几乎连一只眼睛都睁不开。>\n\n你做完了？好极了……\n\n<一缕胆汁挂在他嘴边。你不在的时候他一直在呕吐。>\n\n自从我加入这一伙……病症只是越来越深。这说不通……对吧？",cEN="<The fits have grown worse. The gnome can barely keep one eye half open.>\n\nYou’re done? Splendid…\n\n<A string of bile hangs from his mouth. He’s been vomiting in your absence.>\n\nEver since I joined this lot… the sickness has only deepened. It doesn’t make any sense… does it?"}
Q[1660012]={d="<精灵彬彬有礼地点头致意。>\n\n请原谅我。我走了很远的路，这里似乎没人愿意帮我。也许……你可以？\n\n我一直在寻找我的妹妹艾尔蒂娜。大约半年前，她受邀加入一个秘密的德鲁伊圈子，连再见都没说就走了。她再也没有回来。\n\n我一路追寻她的足迹来到此地，来到暗影谷……但我只是个商人。我连刀都握不稳！而通往那片隐秘德鲁伊林地的路戒备森严，十分危险。\n\n你愿意替我走那一趟，确认我妹妹还活着吗？",dEN="<The elf greets you with a respectful bow of the head.>\n\nForgive me. I’ve come a long way, and no one here seems willing to help me. Perhaps… you could?\n\nI’ve been searching for my sister, Elydna. About half a year ago, she was invited to join a secret druidic circle, and left without even saying goodbye. She never returned.\n\nI managed to trace her steps here, to Shadowglen… but I’m just a merchant. I can barely hold a blade! And the path leading to this hidden grove of druids is well-guarded, and dangerous.\n\nWould you walk that road for me, and make sure my sister still lives?",o="走过腐尸小径并击败它的守卫。",oEN="Walk the Carrion Path and defeat its guardians.",p="<精灵向你露出一口黄色参差的牙齿。这就足够当作警告了。>\n\n只有活着走过腐尸小径的人，才受欢迎进入秃鹫教派的巢穴。",pEN="<The elf shows you a mouthful of yellow, jagged teeth. Let that be warning enough.>\n\nOnly those who survive the Carrion Path are welcome in the Nest of the Vulture’s Cult.",c="站住。\n\n我能感觉到你。我知道你在那里。而且我知道你不是我们中的一员。\n\n是什么事让你来到秃鹫教派鹰巢？",cEN="Stop.\n\nI can feel you. I know you’re there. And I know you’re not one of us.\n\nWhat business brings you to the Vulture Cult Eyrie?"}
Q[1660013]={d="那么……你不是自愿来此，而是出于……\"利他之心\"。<这个词透着轻蔑，仿佛他认为这更像弱点而非美德。>\n\n我受誓言约束；我不能谈论我们的成员。你必须去向我们的女主、我们的导师、我们的引路人——艾吉娅女士——恳求。她会决定如何处置你，以及你是否会分享艾尔蒂娜的命运。\n\n你会在里面的大厅里找到艾吉娅女士。",dEN="So… you’re not here of your own will, but out of… “altruism.” <The word drips with disdain, as though he thinks it more weakness than virtue.>\n\nI am bound by oath; I cannot speak of our members. You must beg before our lady, our teacher, our guide: Lady Aegya. She will decide what to do with you, and whether you’ll share in Elydna’s fate.\n\nYou’ll find Lady Aegya further inside, in the hall.",o="与秃鹫教派领袖艾吉娅女士交谈，询问萨里尔的妹妹艾尔蒂娜的下落。",oEN="Speak with Lady Aegya, leader of the Vulture’s Cult, and ask what became of Thariel’s sister, Elydna.",p="<艾吉娅空洞的眼窝锁定你，那目光比任何刀刃都切得更深。>",pEN="<The empty sockets of Aegya’s eyes fix on you with a gaze that cuts deeper than any blade.>",c=" communion 是任何入门者最神圣的时刻。在她的 communion 中，艾尔蒂娜将押上自己的性命。她必须为自己成为秃鹫德鲁伊的权利而战……否则就会沦为献祭的腐肉。\n\n但还有……准备工作要做。如果你出于对她兄长的怜悯，想要看她活着通过仪式，那么……也许你能派上用场。相关",cEN="Communion is the most sacred moment for any initiate. In hers, Elydna will stake her very life. She must fight for her right to stand as a Druid of the Vulture… or else end as sacrificial carrion.\n\nBut there are still… preparations to be made. If what you seek, out of pity for her brother, is to see her survive the rite, well… perhaps you can be of use."}
Q[1660014]={d="大秃鹫反复无常，但他记得那些匍匐乞求的人。有了合适的祭品……也许他会在艾尔蒂娜的 communion 中对她另眼相看。\n\n<艾吉娅女士歪斜的笑容暗示的恰恰相反。>\n\n进入我们称作月光骸骨堂的墓穴，从那些在腐臭走廊里腐烂的尸体上取五块上好的肉给我。\n\n不过要小心。我们让那些尸体发酵，好让它们的滋味更讨大秃鹫的喙喜欢。而腐烂，如你所知，会引来各种害虫……",dEN="The Great Vulture is fickle, but he remembers those who crawl and beg. With the right offering… perhaps he’ll look kindly on Elydna during her communion.\n\n<Lady Aegya’s crooked smile suggests the exact opposite.>\n\nGo into the barrow we call the Moonlit Ossuary and bring me five cuts of good meat from the corpses that rot within its rancid halls.\n\nBe careful, though. We leave their bodies to ferment, that their taste might better please the Great Vulture’s beak. And rot, as you well know, draws all manner of vermin…",o="在秃鹫教派鹰巢内的月光骸骨堂收集五块上好的肉。",oEN="Gather five cuts of good meat from the Moonlit Ossuary within the Vulture Cult Eyrie.",p="时间紧迫，大秃鹫越来越不安分。即便此刻，他也在你头顶盘旋，注视着你……",pEN="Time is short, and the Great Vulture grows restless. Even now he circles overhead, watching you…",c="啊……我几乎能尝到它了。你带来了五块？是的……完好无损。我不知道你是怎么忍住不偷咬一口的。\n\n<艾吉娅用舌头舔过嘴唇，缓慢而淫猥：一条覆满黏液的黑色蛞蝓。>\n\n大秃鹫……今晚要大快朵颐了。",cEN="Ahh… I can almost taste it. And you’ve brought five? Yes… intact. I don’t know how you resisted sneaking a bite.\n\n<Aegya runs her tongue across her lips, slowly and obscenely: a black slug slick with slime.>\n\nThe Great Vulture… will feast tonight."}
Q[1660015]={d="只剩下最后一步。\n\n你采集的肉滴着腐化，但太干了。大秃鹫喜欢他的祭品湿润，好让它们沾湿他残酷的喙。\n\n把这些肉带到我们的月井去。你所认识的艾露恩的面貌只是众多面貌之一。早在与玛洛恩同床之前，她就将大秃鹫带上了她的床。直到今日，她仍真心爱着他。\n\n在月井的水中祝福这些肉，并杀死任何从深处升起的暗影。只有到那时，艾尔蒂娜才算为她的 communion 做好了准备。",dEN="One last step remains.\n\nThe flesh you’ve gathered drips with corruption, but it’s too dry. The Great Vulture likes his offerings moist, so they wet his cruel beak.\n\nTake this meat to our Moonwell. The face of Elune you know is only one among many. Long before she laid with Malorne, she took the Great Vulture to her bed. Still today, she loves him true.\n\nBless the flesh in the Moonwell’s waters and slay whatever shadow rises from its depths. Only then will Elydna be ready for her communion.",o="把采集到的肉带到月井，在井水中将其圣化。",oEN="Carry the gathered flesh to the Moonwell and sanctify it in the waters.",p=" communion 即将开始。你还没有圣化祭品的肉吗？",pEN="The communion is about to begin. You have yet to sanctify the flesh of tribute?",c="腐烂的血肉……已被圣化。大秃鹫会细细品味这份祭品。\n\n时候到了。艾尔蒂娜·翼击的 communion 开始了。",cEN="Rotten flesh… sanctified. The Great Vulture will savor this offering.\n\nThe time has come. Elydna Wingstroke’s communion begins."}
Q[1660016]={d="这里。\n\n<吉尔盖恩摸索着你的双手，把圣化过的肉重新按进你的掌心。>\n\n把它放进巢里，和艾尔蒂娜为取悦大秃鹫收集的其他祭品放在一起。\n\n你获赐了极大的荣耀，你意识到了吗？参与我们中一员的 communion。艾尔蒂娜迫不及待想见你。我想你也一样急切地想见她。",dEN="Here.\n\n<Gilgaen gropes at your hands and presses the sanctified flesh back into your palms.>\n\nLay it in the nest, with the other offerings Elydna has gathered to please the Great Vulture.\n\nYou’ve been granted a great honor, do you realize? To share in the communion of one of our own. Elydna can’t wait to meet you. I imagine you’re just as eager to meet her.",o="把圣化的肉放在大秃鹫巢中的碗里。然后，帮助艾尔蒂娜完成她的 communion。",oEN="Place the sanctified flesh upon the bowl in the Great Vulture’s nest. Then, aid Elydna in completing her communion.",p=" communion 即将开始。你还没有圣化祭品的肉吗？",pEN="The communion is about to begin. You have yet to sanctify the flesh of tribute?",c="一场壮丽的战斗。大秃鹫很满意。\n\n哦，别告诉我你怜悯艾尔蒂娜。艾吉娅嘲弄地撅起嘴。我没警告过你 communion 的风险吗？\n\n你要么胜出，作为我们中的一员崛起……要么失败，只能在月光骸骨堂中腐烂。\n\n艾尔蒂娜有过她的机会。你只是证明了更强。把你自己的\"communion\"当作一次成功吧。从此刻起，你可以选择：加入我们……或者离开。",cEN="A sublime fight. The Great Vulture is pleased.\n\nOh, don’t tell me you pity Elydna. <Aegya pouts mockingly.> Didn’t I warn you of the risks of the communion?\n\nYou either triumph, and rise as one of us… or you fail, only to rot in the Moonlit Ossuary.\n\nElydna had her chance. You simply proved the stronger. Consider your own “communion” a success. From this moment, you may choose: join us… or walk away."}
Q[1660017]={d="一位访客……我们很少欢迎陌生人来到我们中间，理由充分：我们的习俗在数千年前就被取缔了。\n\n有时我想，确实该被取缔……艾吉娅女士愿意做那些连萨特都会战栗的事。你知道我在说什么吗？精灵孩童，被当作祭品献上；无人会想念的战争孤儿。\n\n帮我救救他们。去大巢穴，在腐尸中搜寻。通过你，我将引导我的力量，把他们变成美丽的蝴蝶。\n\n我给这顶花冠施了魔法；它的芬芳将……无法抗拒。无论你领向何处，他们都会跟随。\n\n把他们带到这里。剩下的我来处理。",dEN="A visitor… Rarely do we welcome strangers among us, and with good reason: our practices were outlawed millennia ago.\n\nAt times I think, rightly so… Lady Aegya is willing to do things that would make even a satyr shudder. Do you know of what I speak? Elf children, offered up as tribute; war orphans no one would miss.\n\nHelp me save them. Go to the Great Nest and search among the carrion. Through you, I will channel my power and turn them into beautiful butterflies.\n\nI have enchanted this flower crown; its fragrance will be… irresistible. They will follow wherever you lead.\n\nBring them here. I will see to the rest.",o="在大巢穴中引导艾尔蒂娅的力量作用于新生者，将他们变成蝴蝶。然后，把蝴蝶引回艾尔蒂娅身边。",oEN="Channel Eldya’s power over the newborns in the Great Nest to transform them into butterflies. Then guide the butterflies back to Eldya.",p="你及时赶到了吗？他们还活着吗？",pEN="Did you reach them in time? Were they still alive?",c="<精灵深吸一口气，捕捉着那花冠的芬芳。>\n\n他们跟来了。很好。\n\n大秃鹫教会了我们许多道理，但把如此稚嫩的生命献祭给它那残忍的喙……那是我永远无法原谅自己的堕落。\n\n无论付出什么代价，我都会确保这些孩子安然无恙。",cEN="<The elf breathes in, catching the scent of the flower crown.>\n\nThey followed. Good.\n\nThe Great Vulture teaches many lessons, but to sacrifice such tender lives to the cruelty of its beak… that is a depravity I could never forgive myself.\n\nWhatever it takes, I will see these children safe."}
Q[1660018]={d="亡者的灵魂不得安宁。他们用梦境与幻象折磨我们，已经击垮了我们许多同胞。我曾向元素寻求指引，但……他们不会回应我。\n\n拿着这个。\n\n<埃斯格拉莫把一块石头放进你手中，它比那不起眼的外表要沉重得多。>\n\n这是一枚护身符。前往破碎者与受折磨者所在之处，用这块石头的力量抽取他们不安灵魂的碎片。尽可能多地收集，然后交给泽布戈罗的女巫。她是一位力量可怖、智慧深邃的巫女。\n\n我相信她清楚该怎么做。",dEN="The spirits of the dead are restless. They torment us with dreams and visions that have already broken many among us. I have sought counsel with the elements, but… they will not answer me.\n\nTake this.\n\n<Esgramor places in your hand a stone far heavier than its modest size would suggest.>\n\nIt is a warding amulet. Go to the broken, to the tormented, and use the stone’s power to draw forth fragments of their unresting spirit. Gather what you can and bring them to the witch of Zeb’Goro. She is a sorceress of dreadful power and deep wisdom.\n\nI trust she will know what must be done.",o="使用不起眼的石头，从躁动不安的兽人与巨魔身上抽取灵魂躁动的样本，并将你的发现呈交给泽布戈罗的女巫。",oEN="Use the Unremarkable Stone to extract samples of spiritual unrest from the restless orcs and trolls, and present your findings to the witch of Zeb'Goro.",p="你想要什么，陌生人？",pEN="What ya want, stranger?",c="我不记得你的脸。但你带来的东西让我汗毛倒竖……\n\n你说的那个……\"灵魂躁动\"？哈！这么说，是埃斯格拉莫派你来的。女巫早就知道笼罩试炼谷的诅咒了。此刻，她正在筹备一场仪式来解决它。\n\n嗯……<El troll inclina la cabeza, evaluándote.>\n\n既然你已经走到这里，或许你能在仪式上搭把手。",cEN="I don’ recall ya face. But ya bringin’ somethin’ dat make me skin crawl…\n\nDis… “spiritual unrest,” ya say? Hah! So Esgramor be sendin’ ya. Da Witch already be knowin’ of da curse hangin’ ova da Valley o’ Trials. Even now, she be workin’ a ritual to fix it.\n\nHrmm… <The troll tilts his head, sizing you up.>\n\nSince ya come dis far, maybe ya can lend a hand wit’ da ritual."}
Q[1660019]={d="就在附近，我们发现了一处世界之间的帷幕十分薄弱的洞穴。那是一处力量之地，盘踞着化作野兽形态的灵魂。\n\n女巫派她的学徒去收集仪式所需之物：一条蛇、一只蝙蝠和一只蜘蛛的灵魂精华。但她再也没回来。也许她已经死了。\n\n<斯瓦莉把一尊小小的巨魔神像按进你手里，它由骨头雕成，嵌着一颗血红色的宝石。\n\n一道强大的法术守护着洞口。你需要这个才能穿过屏障，抵达另一边。如果安贾莉已经死了……你能否替她完成她未竟之事？",dEN="Nearby, we found a cave where the veil ‘tween worlds runs thin. A place o’ power, haunted by spirits dat take de form o’ beasts.\n\nDa Witch sent her apprentice to gather what be needed for da ritual: da spirit essence of a serpent, a bat, an’ a spider. But she never returned. Could be she already dead.\n\n<Swa’li presses into your hand a small troll idol, carved from bone and set with a blood-red gem.>\n\nA mighty spell wards de cave’s entrance. You’ll be needin’ dis to cross de barrier an’ reach de other side. If Anjali be dead… can we count on you to finish what she began?",o="使用斯瓦莉给你的护身符，穿过守护着阴暗巢穴入口的魔法屏障。",oEN="Use the amulet given to you by Swa’li to break through the magical barrier guarding the entrance to the Sinister Lair.",p="<那女巨魔倒在血泊中，气息奄奄，仿佛吊着一根承受不住重量的细线。>",pEN="<The troll lies broken, her life hanging by a thread that bears too heavy a weight.>",c="他们派你来……确认我死了。哈……\n\n<El trol yace desplomado en el suelo, cada respiración es un gemido entrecortado.>\n\n那护身符……没用。没有完全奏效……这洞穴的魔法把我从里到外撕碎了。那是个陷阱。女巫一定看穿了我的野心……\n\n但他们没料到，我会像水蛭一样死死抓住性命。我不会死在这里！\n\n靠近些……<su voz baja hasta convertirse en un susurro>。我全都告诉你。",cEN="Dey send you… to make sure I be dead. Ha…\n\n<The troll lies crumpled on the ground, each breath a ragged moan.>\n\nDe amulet… it didn’t work. Not all de way… De magic o’ dis cave tore me apart, inside an’ out. Was a trap. De Witch must’ve seen through my ambitions…\n\nBut dey didn’t count on me clingin’ to life like a leech. I will not die here!\n\nCome closer…<her voice falls to a whisper>. I tell you everyt’ing."}
Q[1660020]={d="女巫……不是你的盟友。我不知道她全部的计划，但我知道这一点：她不会解决灵魂的问题。\n\n因为正是她造成了这一切。\n\n她一直在召唤亡者的灵魂，把它们从安息中拽出，当作仪式的燃料焚烧。她唯一还缺的，就是这处洞穴里的灵魂精华。所以绝不能让它们落到她手里。\n\n但如果你把它们带给我……\n\n我的伤很重，但我的决心从未如此坚定。我想我能扭转这些精华的力量，削弱女巫的巫毒。",dEN="De Witch… she not your ally. I don’t know all what she be plannin’, but I know dis: she won’t mend de troubles o’ de spirits.\n\n’Cause she de one who caused dem.\n\nShe been callin’ up de souls o’ de dead, tearin’ dem from deir rest, burnin’ dem as fuel for her ritual. All she still be needin’ are de spirit essences from dis cave. Dat why she mus’ not claim dem.\n\nBut if you were to bring dem to me instead…\n\nMy wounds be grave, but my resolve never been stronger. I believe I could bend de power of de essences to weaken de Witch’s Voodoo.",o="收集盘踞在阴暗巢穴中的野兽的灵魂精华。你需要一份蜘蛛的、一份蝙蝠的和一份蛇的。",oEN="Gather the spiritual essences of the beasts haunting the Sinister Lair. You will need one from a spider, one from a bat, and one from a serpent.",p="女巫会为她的背叛付出代价。",pEN="The Witch will pay for her betrayal.",c="这些精华……！\n\n<A pesar de sus graves heridas, el trol hace un esfuerzo por incorporarse a medias, con el torso temblando por el esfuerzo.>\n\n三道神圣的印记，与阴暗三神系的洛阿相连：丹巴拉，智慧与阴谋的蛇神；希尔雷克，黑夜与秘密的蝙蝠神；还有埃洛莎·诺·沙德拉，命运与欺瞒的蜘蛛女神。\n\n换作从前，你交到我手中的这份力量足以杀死女巫。但……<el trol esboza una sonrisa de cansancio>我只能满足于削弱她那黑暗的巫毒了。",cEN="De essences…!\n\n<Despite her grievous wounds, the troll makes an effort to raise herself halfway, her torso trembling with the effort.>\n\nThree sacred signs, bound to de loa of de Siniestra Triad: Dambala, de serpent god of wisdom an’ intrigue; Hir’eek, de bat god of night an’ secrets; and Elortha no Shadra, de spider goddess of fate an’ deceit.\n\nIn anoder time, dis power you placed in my hands would be enough to slay de Witch. But… <the troll gives a weary smile> I must content meself wit weakenin’ her dark voodoo."}
Q[1660021]={d="这些精华的力量不足以阻止女巫。\n\n你必须亲自面对她。\n\n但首先……还有元素的问题。\n\n女巫知道谷中的灵魂会起身反抗她，所以在开始仪式前，她命令我把它们束缚起来，困在一道力量法阵中，使它们无法干涉。\n\n在回去找萨满、直面女巫之前，你必须先释放它们。走出洞穴后，沿着向右蜿蜒穿过岩石的小路走。走到尽头，你会找到那道力量法阵。",dEN="De power of de essences won’t be enough to stop de Witch.\n\nYou will have to face her yourself.\n\nBut first… dere be de matter of de elementals.\n\nDe Witch knew de spirits o’ de valley would rise against her, so before she began de ritual, she bid me bind dem—trap dem in a circle o’ power, so dey could not interfere.\n\nBefore you return to de shaman an’ confront de Witch, you must set dem free. When you leave de cave, follow de path dat winds to de right, through de rocks. At its end, you will find de circle of power.",o="释放洞穴旁的元素。然后与埃斯格拉莫交谈，告诉他希尔苏塔真正的意图。",oEN="Free the elementals next to the cave. Then, speak with Esgramor and tell him of Hirsutta’s true intentions.",p="你回来了。我一直在等你。",pEN="You’ve returned. I was waiting.",c="我真是个傻瓜。当我寻求元素指引却只换来沉默时，我就该知道有更黑暗的东西在作祟。\n\n结果，我反倒派你去求助于那个女巫——讽刺的是，她正是灵魂不安的根源。\n\n但要挫败她的计划还不算太晚，无论那计划是什么。希尔苏塔已经为自己树了三个危险的敌人。",cEN="I was a fool. I should have known something darker was at work when I reached out to the elementals… and was met with silence.\n\nInstead, I sent you to seek the aid of the witch who, ironically, was the very cause of the spirits’ unrest.\n\nBut it is not yet too late to thwart her designs, whatever they may be. Hirsutta has made three dangerous enemies."}
Q[1660022]={d="就在我们说话的此刻，一阵战栗正掠过试炼谷。安贾莉与希尔苏塔陷入了意志的碰撞；尽管安贾莉拥有三份精华的力量，她仍在女巫面前节节败退。\n\n<萨满闭着眼睛说话，仿佛两位女巫之间的争斗属于一个看不见的世界。>\n\n必须现在动手，否则就永远没有机会了。\n\n我会与元素沟通，设法打断女巫的专注。在此期间……你已经积累了一些实战经验。杀出一条通往她巢穴的血路，趁还来得及，了结她。",dEN="Even as we speak, a shudder runs through the Valley of Trials. Anjali and Hirsutta are locked in a clash of wills; and though Anjali holds the power of the three essences, she is losing ground to the Witch.\n\n<The shaman speaks with his eyes closed, as though the struggle between the two sorceresses belongs to a world unseen.>\n\nIt must be done now, or never.\n\nI will commune with the elements and try to break the Witch’s focus. In the meantime… you have already gained some measure of field experience. Fight your way to her lair, and end her before it is too late.",o="直面女巫希尔苏塔，终结她黑暗的仪式。",oEN="Confront Hirsutta the Witch and put an end to her dark ritual.",p="灵魂越来越不安了。\n\n我们必须立刻阻止女巫！",pEN="The spirits grow restless.\n\nWe must stop the Witch now!",c="结束了。希尔苏塔死了。\n\n灵魂们再度安息。我想，女巫原本打算把所有在此倒下的兽人与巨魔的灵魂束缚起来，用它们锻造出一尊扭曲的黑暗诸神化身。\n\n丹巴拉并非狡诈与智慧的洛阿，而是背叛的洛阿。\n\n希尔雷克并非秘密与黑夜的洛阿，而是饥渴与鲜血的洛阿。\n\n而沙德拉……她不是命运的编织者，而是刺客，是骗子。\n\n想象一下，她的仪式会孕育出怎样的憎恶之物……",cEN="It is done. Hirsutta is dead.\n\nThe spirits rest once more. I believe the Witch sought to bind the souls of every orc and troll who fell here, and forge from them a twisted avatar of her dark gods.\n\nDambala is not the loa of cunning and wisdom, but of betrayal.\n\nHir’eek is not the loa of secrets and night, but of thirst and blood.\n\nAnd Shadra… She is no weaver of fate, but a murderer, a liar.\n\nImagine what sort of abomination her ritual would have birthed…"}
Q[1660023]={d="女巫的追随者或许根本不知道仪式的真正目的。无论如何，我们不能让他们挡在我们与希尔苏塔之间。\n\n你明白……对吧？\n\n<兽人的脸色阴沉下来。与你即将被要求做的事相比，他搭在你肩上的那只手带来的安慰微不足道。>\n\n换句话说：在抵达她面前之前，你得杀穿不止一小撮战士；他们大多是无辜的，至死都以为你才是这个故事里的恶人。",dEN="It’s possible the Witch’s followers don’t even know the true purpose of the ritual. One way or another, we cannot allow them to stand between us and Hirsutta.\n\nYou understand… don’t you?\n\n<The orc’s face darkens. The hand he sets on your shoulder offers little comfort compared to what he is asking of you.>\n\nIn other words: you’ll have to cut through more than a few warriors before you reach her; innocents, mostly, who will die believing you were the villain of this tale.",o="击败守卫着通往希尔苏塔之路的巫毒信徒。",oEN="Defeat the voodoo devotees guarding the path that leads to Hirsutta.",p="但愿我能用几句安慰的话语减轻你的负担。",pEN="If only I could ease your burden with a few words of comfort.",c="<兽人点了点头。这个微小的动作，便是两人约定不再提起此事的全部。>",cEN="<The orc nods. The small gesture is all it takes to agree never to speak of it again.>"}
Q[1660024]={d="你好。\n\n我是安东，遗产联盟引以为傲的一员。奉女王之命，我的组织承担起一项王室职责：编目、收回并修复洛丹伦的文化遗产，使其能为被遗忘者所用。\n\n离这儿不远，向西有条小路蜿蜒爬上山坡，通往凯恩家族的产业。\n\n我会把同僚营地的位置标在你的地图上。他们正需要多一双手；即便在洛丹伦陷落之前，就有传闻说那座宅邸受了诅咒……全因某个女巫。",dEN="Greetings.\n\nI’m Anthon, proud member of the Heritage League. By order of our queen, my organization has taken on the royal duty of cataloguing, reclaiming, and restoring the cultural legacy of Lordaeron so it may serve the Forsaken.\n\nNot far from here, the road winds west, up the hill, to the Cain family estates.\n\nHere, I’ll mark on your map the location of my colleagues’ camp. They could use an extra hand; even before Lordaeron’s fall, there were rumors the manor was cursed… all because of a certain witch.",o="在遗产联盟营地与里塞尔·凯恩交谈。",oEN="Speak with Riscell Cain at the Heritage League camp.",c="是安东派你来的？他上次带来的那个被遗忘者惹的麻烦比他的用处还大……不过你的筋骨似乎保养得更好些。也许你终究能为我们做点有用的事。\n\n容我自我介绍：\n\n我是里塞尔·凯恩。没错；严格说来，我是这片土地最后一位在世的合法继承人……至少本该是。\n\n即便如此，我仍觉得它们是我的责任。所以我加入了遗产联盟，决心帮助重建家族的产业，让它为新秩序效力。",cEN="Anthon sent you? The last Forsaken he dragged in caused more trouble than he was worth… but your tendons seem better preserved. Perhaps you can actually do something useful for us after all.\n\nAllow me to introduce myself:\n\nI am Riscell Cain. Yes; technically the last living heir with a claim to these lands… or at least, I would have been.\n\nStill, I feel they remain my responsibility. So I joined the Heritage League, determined to help restore my family’s estate and place it in service to the New Order."}
Q[1660025]={d="靠我们自己，已经取得了不小的进展，但前头还有许多工作。\n\n我就直说了。我的父母在瘟疫降临前几年去世，但他们的墓穴遭到了我几乎不敢启齿的亵渎与羞辱。以至于他们的灵魂如今仍在生前走过的走廊里徘徊；困惑着，受着折磨。\n\n下到家族墓穴，我的先辈安葬在那里，为他们的灵魂念一段简短的祈祷。这应当能把他们的灵魂引回遗骸……在那里，你可以与他们交战，把他们送往彼岸——那才是他们该去的地方。",dEN="We’ve made good progress on our own, but there’s still a great deal of work ahead.\n\nI’ll get straight to it. My parents died a few years before the Scourge came, yet their crypt suffered desecrations and humiliations I can hardly bring myself to name. So much so that their spirits now haunt the halls they once walked in life; confused, tormented.\n\nGo down into the family crypt, where my ancestors lie buried, and offer a brief prayer for their souls. That should draw their spirits back to their remains… where you can face them and send them on to the afterlife, where they belong.",o="在凯恩家族墓穴中净化里塞尔亡故亲属的遗骸，将他们的灵魂送回彼岸。",oEN="Purify the remains of Riscell’s deceased relatives in the Cain Family Crypt, and send their spirits back to the Afterlife.",p="你净化了我家人的遗骸吗？真希望我姐姐的名字也在那些壁龛之中……",pEN="Have you purified my family’s remains? If only my sister’s name were among those niches…",c="你说狗头人？最下等的货色；破坏者、食腐者、小毛贼。让他们烂掉吧！我会亲自确保他们的洞穴被瘟疫闷死。\n\n至于你的工作……我印象深刻。我们派驻宅邸的死亡猎手报告说，灵魂已不再游荡于那些走廊与厅堂。\n\n你知道这意味着什么吗？我们准备好下一步行动了。",cEN="Kobolds, you say? The lowest sort; vandals, scavengers, petty thieves. Let them rot! I’ll personally see their burrows choked with blight.\n\nAs for your work… I’m impressed. Our deathstalker stationed in the manor reports the spirits no longer wander its halls and chambers.\n\nDo you know what that means? We’re ready for our next move."}
Q[1660026]={d="灵魂的事处理完，还有另一件事……一件远超我同僚能力范围的事。\n\n我的姐姐普丽西拉——愿她的名字受诅咒——把这座宅邸变成了巫术的巢穴。她最恶劣的实验被封存在地下室里，而那把钥匙，我们刚刚发现，断成了三截，如今分别由旧日的管家、女仆和马夫保管。三个没脑子的空壳，一个不剩。\n\n杀了他们，取回钥匙碎片。埃克桑格会把它重新锻好，让你能打开地下室……来一次彻底的大扫除。",dEN="With the spirits dealt with, there’s another matter… one far beyond the abilities of my colleagues.\n\nMy sister Priscilla, curse her name, turned the manor into a den of witchcraft. Her worst experiments were sealed away in the basement, whose key, we’ve just found out, was broken into three pieces, now held by the former majordomo, the maid, and the stablemaster. Brainless husks, the three of them.\n\nKill them and recover their fragments of the key. Exsangue will reforge it so you can open the basement and… give it a thorough cleaning.",o="取回宅邸的管家、女仆和马夫手中的钥匙碎片。",oEN="Retrieve the key fragments held by the manor’s majordomo, maid, and stablemaster.",p="你拿到钥匙碎片了吗？别告诉我我们把它弄得太难了……",pEN="Got the key fragments? Don’t tell me we made it too hard for you…",c="钥匙碎片你拿到了？\n\n太好了，我开始不耐烦了。\n\n给我一点时间……",cEN="You have the key fragments?\n\nSplendid, I was beginning to get impatient.\n\nJust give me a moment…"}
Q[1660027]={d="好了。\n\n<Exsangue te entrega la llave, reconstruida a partir de los restos dentados de la original. Retorcida, astillada... su capacidad para sujetar sigue siendo tan dudosa como lo que sea que aguarde tras esa puerta>\n\n你处理……那下面被关着的东西时，我会确保没有游荡的尸体惊扰你。\n\n不止一次，我仿佛听到一声哀号，接着是咕嘟声和尖叫。小心点。",dEN="Done.\n\n<Exsangue hands you the key, pieced together from the jagged remnants of the original. Twisted, splintered… its ability to hold remains as doubtful as whatever waits behind that door.>\n\nI’ll make sure no shambling corpse sneaks up on you while you deal with… whatever’s been locked away down there.\n\nMore than once, I’ve thought I heard a wail, followed by gurgling and screams. Tread carefully.",o="使用钥匙进入地下室，击败里面的生物。",oEN="Use the key to access the basement and defeat the creature within.",p="我相信你已经办妥了。否则，你也不会这么自然地站在这儿跟我说话……对吧？",pEN="I trust you’ve done the job. Otherwise, you wouldn’t be standing here so casually, talking to me… right?",c="<Riscell sacude la cabeza lentamente mientras relatas lo que has visto.>\n\n那个生物……我听过传闻，但即便是对我姐姐而言，那些传闻也荒诞得令人难以置信。\n\n想想看，普丽西拉竟与一个恶魔来往……还生下了那\"东西\"。\n\n无论如何，你为遗产联盟立下了大功，也在此过程中恢复了我家族姓氏的尊严。我向你致以\"永恒\"的感激。",cEN="<Riscell shakes his head slowly as you recount what you’ve seen.>\n\nThat creature… I’d heard the rumors, but even for my sister, they seemed too grotesque to believe.\n\nTo think Priscilla consorted with a demon… and bore that “thing”.\n\nIn any case, you’ve done the Heritage League a great service, and restored the dignity of my family name in the process. You have my “undying” gratitude."}
Q[1660028]={d="你知道遗产联盟是怎么获得经费的吗？\n\n我们的女王允许我们留下所缴获财宝的一部分。因此，迄今为止，我们修复的宫殿远比堡垒多。\n\n陷落之前，凯恩家是王国最富有的家族之一。我敢打赌，那座宅邸里还有不少值得搜刮的东西。\n\n去看看吧，好吗？\n看你能找到什么，我们或许能谈笔交易。\n\n但要小心。那座宅邸昔日的女主人，里塞尔的姐姐……这么说吧，那地方闹鬼。",dEN="Do you know how the Heritage League funds itself?\n\nOur Queen allows us to keep a share of the treasures we recover. Which is why, up to now, we’ve restored far more palaces than fortresses.\n\nBefore their fall, the Cains were among the wealthiest families in the realm. I’d wager there’s still plenty in that manor worth laying hands on.\n\nGive it a look, will you? Depending on what you find, we might strike a deal.\n\nBut take care. The former lady of the manor, Riscell’s sister… Let’s just say the place is haunted.",o="探索凯恩家族的宅邸，取回任何残留的贵重物品。然后把它们交给斯里斯。",oEN="Explore Cain Family Manor and recover whatever valuables remain. Then bring them to Thris.",p="你在里面找到什么值钱的东西了吗？",pEN="Did you find anything of value in there?",c="<如果贪婪有颜色，那一定是这个亡灵眼中的黄色。>\n\n一幅大胆的画作……一颗水晶球（多半被诅咒了），一件得先估价才能庆祝的首饰，还有一枚家族印章，我敢打赌它的价值纯粹是情感上的。\n\n其实也没多少。<Ella se encoge de hombros como si no fuera nada. Pero sus ojos... dicen lo contrario.>\n\n我怀疑这些东西换不了多少钱，但总比没有好。至于那枚家族印章……就当帮里塞尔一个忙，我们自己留下吧。你知道翻出旧日回忆会有多痛……",cEN="<If greed had a color, it would be the yellow of this forsaken’s eyes.>\n\nA saucy painting… a crystal ball (likely cursed), a jewel we’d need appraised before celebrating, and a family signet whose worth, I’d wager, is purely sentimental.\n\nNot much, really. <She shrugs as if it were nothing. But her eyes… they say otherwise.>\n\nI doubt I’ll fetch much for these, but it’s better than nothing. As for the family signet… let’s do Riscell a favor and keep it. You know how painful it can be to dredge up old memories…"}
Q[1660029]={d="你注意到了，对吧？我在这儿几乎跟不上节奏。而这些可怜虫总能想出新的法子惹麻烦。\n\n我认识一个人，也许能帮上忙……只要我们能弄到合适的材料。\n\n我得留在这儿守着营地。但你……你已经证明了自己懂得照顾自己。\n\n杀掉在产业周围游荡的生物：僵尸、食尸鬼、熊……别费心把它们的遗留物带回来；它们的器官很不稳定，处理不当可能会腐坏……或者更糟。等这一切结束后，我会亲自从它们的尸体上提取我们所需之物。",dEN="You’ve noticed, haven’t you? I can barely keep up here. And these wretches keep finding new ways to get themselves in trouble.\n\nI know someone who could lend us a hand… if we can get the right ingredients.\n\nI must remain here, protecting the camp. But you… you’ve already proven you can handle yourself.\n\nKill the creatures prowling around the estate: zombies, ghouls, bears… Don’t bother hauling back what they leave behind; their organs are volatile, and if not handled properly they could spoil... or worse. I’ll take care of extracting what we need from their bodies once this is all over.",o="杀掉在凯恩宅邸周围游荡的生物：僵尸、食尸鬼和熊。",oEN="Slay the creatures prowling Cain Manor: zombies, ghouls, and bears.",p="你采购完了吗？",pEN="Done with the shopping yet?",c="你回来了。而且一路留下了不少尸体。\n\n很好。\n\n<El no-muerto sonríe ante la idea de lo que podrá cosechar de los cuerpos.>\n\n有了这些，再加一道电火花，我认识的那个亡灵就能给我们缝出一个朋友。你知道的，一个能搭把手的。两只也行。三只也行。我指的是那种鼓鼓囊囊的大家伙——我们称之为\"憎恶\"。",cEN="You’re back. And you’ve left quite the trail of corpses behind you.\n\nGood.\n\n<The forsaken grins at the thought of what he’ll be able to harvest from the bodies.>\n\nWith this, and a spark of electricity, the forsaken I know can stitch us together a friend. You know, someone to lend a hand. Or two. Or three. I’m talking about one of those great bloated things we call “Abominations”."}
Q[1660030]={d="<El tauren te analiza con una mirada pausada y juiciosa>.\n\n强壮。体格不错。有胆量。\n\n<Tras una breve pausa, asiente, convencido>.\n\n不错。你或许能派上用场。\n\n这片平原的另一头有座孤零零的小屋，是我尊贵女主人的流放之所。\n\n她是……一位严厉的审判者。但也慷慨。杀掉七个石爪部族的劫掠者，把他们的鬃毛作为凭证带给她。她会给你丰厚的报酬。而如果她认为你配得上……\n\n她会把最崇高的使命托付给你。",dEN="<The tauren sizes you up with a measured, judging gaze.>\n\nStrong. Well-built. Brave.\n\n<After a moment’s pause, he nods, convinced.>\n\nYes. You might prove useful.\n\nAcross this plain stands a lone cabin, the place of exile for my noble lady.\n\nShe is… a harsh judge. But generous. Slay seven Grimtotem Marauders and bring her their manes as proof. She will reward you well. And if she deems you worthy…\n\nShe will entrust you with the noblest of purposes.",o="在红云台地杀死七名石爪劫掠者，取下他们的鬃毛作为凭证，交给红角女士的女主人。",oEN="Slay seven Grimtotem Marauders in Red Cloud Mesa, take their manes as proof, and deliver them to Lady Redhorn’s mistress.",p="我召见过你吗？滚出我的视线！",pEN="Did I summon you here? Begone from my sight!",c="这可不是寻常的礼物……七缕鬃毛，来自七名战士。值得尊敬的壮举。\n\n我猜是我忠心的红角派你来的。如果是这样，接受你的效劳将是我的荣幸。",cEN="This isn’t just any gift... Seven manes, from seven warriors. A feat worth respect.\n\nI take it you were sent by my loyal Redhorn. If that is so, then it will be my honor to accept your service."}
Q[1660031]={d="我是莫里加·空蹄，暴君马尔戈姆·空蹄之女，三图腾的领主。\n\n我并非一直住在这里。曾经，我试图把三图腾从我父亲的暴政下解放出来。我失败了。我的同伴为那次失败付出了性命，所有追随我起义的人也一样。\n\n而我……我父亲没有处决我的胆量。他把我流放到了这里。\n\n但他不知道的是，我仍有盟友；村内村外都有。而你，陌生人，就是我联络他们的途径。\n\n沿着蜿蜒上山的小路走，去找智者诺乔尔。把这枚戒指交给他。你什么都不必多说。",dEN="I am Morriga Hollowhoof, daughter of the tyrant Malgorm Hollowhoof, lord of Three Totems.\n\nI have not always lived here. Once, I sought to free Three Totems from my father’s tyranny. I failed. My mate paid for that failure with his life, as did all who followed me in rebellion.\n\nI, however… my father lacked the courage to execute. Instead, he cast me out here.\n\nBut what he does not know is that I still have allies; both within the village, and beyond it. And you, stranger, will be my way of reaching them.\n\nFollow the path winding up the mountain, and seek out Sage Nauchol. Take him this ring. You’ll need say no more.",o="沿石爪山小径前往硬盆地，把莫里加·空蹄的戒指给智者诺乔尔看。",oEN="Follow the Grimtotem Mountain Path to Hard Basin and show Morriga Hollowhoof’s ring to Sage Nauchol.",p="什么事？",pEN="Yes?",c="这枚戒指……\n\n<那牛头人沉默了良久。他的目光不安地闪动，像草丛间的蚱蜢。>\n\n你知道这意味着什么吗？莫里加选中了你做她的勇士。我很好奇她究竟在你身上看到了什么……那是我看不到的。\n\n嗯。无所谓。我们有活要干。",cEN="This ring…\n\n<The tauren falls silent for a long while. His gaze flickers restlessly, like a grasshopper in the brush.>\n\nDo you know what this means? Morriga has chosen you as her champion. I wonder what she saw in you… that I cannot.\n\nHm. No matter. We have work to do."}
Q[1660032]={d="如果你已经与马尔戈姆的十五名战士交过手并活了下来，也许你有机会对抗暴君本人。但不可能对抗整整一个村子。\n\n我们需要一套伪装；把你打扮成我们中的一员。\n\n莫里加起义之后，她倒下的战士被剥夺了葬礼仪式的荣誉。他们的尸身仍散落在草丛与泥沼之间，任由食腐者处置。他们的遗物不会有人惦记，而秃鹫会感谢你让它们啃得只剩骨头。\n\n只有那些至死忠于马尔戈姆的人才得到了仪式。在他们的尸体上，你找不到盔甲，而是更宝贵的东西：那枚标记他们是暴君选民的身份项坠。",dEN="If you have faced fifteen of Malgorm’s warriors and lived, perhaps you have a chance against the tyrant himself. But not against an entire village.\n\nWe’ll need a disguise; to dress you as one of our own.\n\nAfter Morriga’s rebellion, her fallen warriors were denied the honor of funeral rites. Their bodies still lie scattered in the grass and muck, left to carrion. Their belongings won’t be missed, and the vultures will thank you for stripping them bare.\n\nOnly those who died loyal to Malgorm were given the rites. From their corpses you won’t find armor, but something far more valuable: the pendant that marks them as the tyrant’s chosen.",o="收集三图腾战士的护甲碎片和身份项坠，完成你的伪装。",oEN="Gather pieces of armor and the identifying pendant of Three Totems warriors to complete your disguise.",p="你还没带来伪装所需的东西吗？\n\n也许你已经击败了十五名战士，但你不可能在整座村子联手对抗下活下来。",pEN="Still haven’t brought what we need for the disguise?\n\nYou may have bested fifteen warriors already, but you will not survive an entire village united against you.",c="伪装所需的东西你都带来了吗？",cEN="Do you bring all we need for the disguise?"}
Q[1660033]={d="你会在村子的尽头、山丘顶上那座最大的小屋里找到马尔戈姆·空蹄。\n\n走向他时，把头抬起来。不要与任何人对视。要自信。骄傲。甚至傲慢。他的战士就是这样行事的。他本人也是如此。",dEN="You’ll find Malgorm Hollowhoof at the far end of the village, atop the hill, in the largest cabin of them all.\n\nAs you walk to him, keep your head high. Do not meet any gaze. Be confident. Proud. Arrogant, even. That is how his warriors behave. That is how he is.",o="当你准备好伪装后与诺乔尔交谈，然后潜入三图腾，杀掉马尔戈姆·空蹄。",oEN="Speak with Nauchol when you are ready for the disguise, then infiltrate Three Totems and slay Malgorm Hollowhoof.",p="又是你……不祥之兆。你找到诺乔尔了吗？你被发现了吗？",pEN="You again… an ill omen. Did you find Nauchol? Were you discovered?",c="我父亲……死了吗？\n\n<莫里加的眼睛湿润了。她的目光或许是悲痛……或许是解脱。多半，是一滴两者兼有的泪。>\n\n这意味着我可以回三图腾了。\n\n然后收拾残局。\n\n<莫里加的泪水消失在她微笑的酒窝里。突然间，她看起来不再那么和善了。>\n\n按我的方式来收拾。",cEN="My father… is dead?\n\n<Morriga’s eyes grow wet. Her look might be sorrow… or relief. Likely, a tear of both.>\n\nThat means I can return to Three Totems.\n\nAnd set things right.\n\n<Morriga’s tears vanish into the dimples of her smile. Suddenly, she no longer seems so gentle.>\n\nSet them right—my way."}
Q[1660034]={d="我就不让你生出一点怜悯吗？<鬣狗皱起鼻子，那模样几乎像是在撅嘴。>那么……孤独。格格不入。就像莫里加一样。\n\n她有你在身边真是幸运。可我呢？\n\n<那副嘴脸化作一个笑容，一排排锯齿闪着光。>\n\n我们来玩个游戏。进村去，把我的祝福引导穿过他们的图腾。守护图腾的灵魂会暴怒，但你和我可以拿它们取乐。\n\n为我做这件事……也许幸运也会对你露出獠牙。",dEN="Don’t I stir a bit of pity in you? <The hyena scrunches its muzzle into something that almost resembles a pout.> So… alone. Out of place. Just like Morriga.\n\nShe’s lucky to have you. But what about me?\n\n<The pout stretches into a grin, rows of jagged teeth glinting.>\n\nLet’s play a game. Go into the village and channel my blessing through their totems. The spirits guarding them will be furious, but you and I will have ourselves a laugh at their expense.\n\nDo this for me… and perhaps fortune will bare its teeth for you as well.",o="把大鬣狗的祝福引导进村中的图腾，并击败守护它们的灵魂。",oEN="Channel the Great Hyena’s blessing into the village totems and defeat the guardian spirits that protect them.",p="<祭坛前盘踞着一头轮廓朦胧的生物，几乎看不见，仿佛它并不完全属于血肉世界。>",pEN="<Before the altar looms a creature of hazy outline, barely visible, as though it does not belong fully to the world of flesh.>",c="<鬣狗又嗥又叫又哭，仿佛她交给你的差事是世上最好笑的笑话。>\n\n干得好……哦，干得太好了！\n\n村里的灵魂乱成了一团。他们活该；他们让我蒙受的羞辱，那场流放……\n\n我的笑容就是幸运的笑容。现在……好好享受吧。",cEN="<The hyena howls and laughs and weeps all at once, as though the task it set you was the greatest jest ever told.>\n\nWell done… oh, very well done!\n\nThe village spirits are in an uproar. They earned it; the humiliation they dealt me, the exile…\n\nMy smile is the smile of fortune. Now… enjoy it."}
Q[1660035]={d="指引舒哈洛的灵魂众多。有些更为人所知，受所有部族崇敬与膜拜。另一些……\n\n在山间小径的尽头，硬盆地的一角，矗立着一根孤零零的图腾，供奉着大鬣狗之灵。我的守护神。\n\n即便在流放之中，我也欠她良多。这些漫长的岁月里，她的智慧一直指引着我。\n\n以我的名义给她带一份供品去。骨头；我敌人的骨头，以及那些遗骸散落在路旁的大兽之骨。\n\n若想扳倒我父亲——那个暴君，我们需要她的祝福。",dEN="Numerous are the spirits who guide the Shu’halo. Some are more popular, well-known, and revered by all the tribes. Others…\n\nAt the end of the mountain path, in a corner of Hard Basin, stands a solitary totem honoring the spirit of the Great Hyena. My patroness.\n\nI owe her much, even in exile. Her wisdom has guided me through these long years.\n\nTake her an offering in my name. Bones; the bones of my enemies, and of the great beasts whose remains line the path.\n\nWe will need her blessing if we are to bring down my father, the tyrant.",o="沿着山间小径收集骨头，并在硬盆地的大鬣狗祭坛献上。",oEN="Gather bones along the mountain path and offer them at the Great Hyena’s altar in Hard Basin.",p="<祭坛前盘踞着一头轮廓朦胧的生物，几乎看不见，仿佛它并不完全属于血肉世界。>",pEN="<Before the altar looms a creature of hazy outline, barely visible, as though it does not belong fully to the world of flesh.>",c="<你靠近时，鬣狗之灵龇出了牙。你分不清那是警告还是笑声。>\n\n莫里加，对吧？\n\n<一阵锯齿般疯狂的笑声掠过你的颅骨>\n\n我很满意。那个牛头人总能逗我开心。她从不厌烦为我效劳。\n\n很好。她的剩饭我就收下了。",cEN="<The spirit of the hyena bares its teeth as you approach. You cannot tell if it is warning, or laughter.>\n\nMorriga, is it?\n\n<A jagged, manic laugh rakes through your skull.>\n\nI am pleased. That tauren always finds a way to amuse me. She never tires of serving.\n\nVery well. I’ll take her scraps."}
Q[1660036]={d="<在一阵残酷死亡的抽搐与痉挛之后，那鱼人瘫倒在潮湿的泥土上，丢下一颗圆球，滚到你脚边停住。>\n\n<凑近细看，你发现它不是寻常的宝石；而是一颗眼球。它滑腻的表面映出模糊的影像，与你周围的世界并不相符。仿佛……仿佛它正向你展示即将发生之事。>\n\n<也许你该杀掉其他先知，检查一下他们那些怪异的瞎眼。>",dEN="<After the spasms and convulsions of a brutal death, the murloc slumps into the wet earth, dropping a sphere that rolls to a stop at your boots.>\n\n<On closer inspection, you realize it’s no common jewel at all; it’s an eyeball. Its slick surface reflects vague images that do not match the world around you. It’s as if… it’s as if it shows you what’s yet to come.>\n\n<Perhaps you should strike down the other oracles and examine their strange, blind eyes.>",o="从游荡在幽泉的鱼人先知身上收集三颗神谕宝珠。",oEN="Collect three Prophet’s Oracular Orbs from the murloc oracles roaming the Shadewell Spring.",p="孩子，我能帮你什么吗？",pEN="Can I help you with something, child?",c="<El sacerdote escucha atentamente mientras relatas los sucesos>\n\n一个有趣的发现。\n\n说来奇怪……几乎所有被我们赋予幻象的圣徒，都患有某种失明。\n\n总之，<lanza los ojos de murloc al cubo de la basura>只有圣光知道未来会如何。\n\n你自以为从这些异端生物身上看到的任何东西，都不过是幻象。鱼人是人类精神的耻辱。你最好让这份好奇心就此安息。",cEN="<The priest listens intently as you recount the events.>\n\nAn interesting discovery.\n\nIt is curious… almost every saint to whom we ascribe visions suffered some form of blindness.\n\nIn any case <he tosses the murloc eyes into the waste bin> only the Light knows what the future holds.\n\nWhatever you think you saw in these heretical creatures was nothing but deception. Murlocs are an insult to the human spirit. Best you put this curiosity of yours to rest."}
Q[1660037]={d="洞穴里的人不是唯一受不安灵魂折磨的。在泽布戈罗，我们也遭遇了同样的事。在女巫的仪式解决它之前，我们只能勉强应付。\n\n既然你来了，我就问问你。\n\n有些蒂基面具开始不停地唠叨。起初我们吓坏了。后来我们笑了。但现在……它们已经唠叨了好些天，一刻不停。\n\n去砸碎几个。让它们闭嘴。",dEN="De cubil folk ain’t de only ones sufferin’ from de spirits’ unrest. In Zeb’Goro, we face de same trouble. ’Til de Witch’s ritual set it right, we deal wit’ it how we can.\n\nSince ya here, I be askin’ ya.\n\nSome o’ de Tiki masks done started jabberin’ nonstop. At first it scare us. Den we laugh. But now… dey been yammerin’ for days, and dey don’t stop.\n\nSmash a few. Make dem hush.",o="摧毁泽布戈罗一带会说话的蒂基面具。",oEN="Destroy the talking Tiki Masks around Zeb’Goro.",p="我相信你已经砸碎了其中一些面具。",pEN="I be trustin’ ya done broken some o’ dem masks.",c="终于！安静了！宝贵的安静！我几乎忘了那是什么声音。\n\n希望那些面具没给你添太多麻烦。灵魂反复无常，有时凶暴……但大多数时候无害。\n\n只不过它们太爱说话了。偏偏从来没什么值得一听的内容。",cEN="At last! Silence! Blessed silence! I near forgot what it sound like.\n\nHope dem masks din’t give ya too much trouble. Spirits be fickle, sometimes violent… but mostly harmless.\n\nDey do love ta talk, tho. Jus’ never got nothin’ worth sayin’."}
Q[1660038]={d="火焰之饥的奴隶，永不满足地索要更多书籍来吞噬。当再没有亵渎之物可烧时，它们便扑向神圣的典籍。\n\n烈火在他空洞的眼窝中燃烧；他已没有眼泪可流。\n\n唯有死亡才能让那受诅的审查官得到解脱……",dEN="Slave to the hunger of the flames, always demanding more books to devour. When there were no more blasphemies left, they turned on the sacred texts instead.\n\nThe fire burns in his hollow sockets; there are no more tears left to shed.\n\nOnly death can release the Cursed Censor…",o="在秘密审判地窟中击败受诅的审查官。",oEN="Defeat the Cursed Censor in the Secret Inquisitorial Dungeon.",p="你既给了审查官死亡，也给了他自由吗？",pEN="Have you granted the censor both death and freedom?",c="没有谁来满足它的欲望，火焰便无法永远燃烧下去。\n\n杀了它，你就解放了它。如今烈焰只能舔舐它的骸骨，直到两者同归尘土与灰烬。\n\n但这些殿堂里可不只有尘土与灰烬……挑选你的奖赏吧，凡人。",cEN="The fire cannot burn forever without someone to indulge its whims.\n\nBy killing him, you’ve set him free. Now the flames must content themselves with licking his bones until both are dust and ash.\n\nBut these chambers hold more than dust and ash… Choose your reward, mortal."}
Q[1660039]={d="你见过那位流放者雷德娜了吗？\n她就在我们正上方的山丘上扎了营。\n\n我上次与她交谈时，她说了一句我始终无法忘怀的话：\n「比说谎者更凶猛地捍卫谎言的，是那个信了谎言的蠢货。」\n\n那个被称作「陛下之右手」的家伙就是活生生的证明。他不是普通的追随者；雷德娜发誓说他比他的主子更残忍、更暴虐、更狂热。\n\n如果你有足够的决心，就在穿越光辉镇时杀了他。然后去告知雷德娜。她和他之间……有笔旧账。",dEN="Have you run into the exile, Redna?\nShe pitched her camp on the hill just above us.\n\nLast time I spoke with her, she said something I haven’t been able to shake off:\n“The only one who’ll defend a lie fiercer than the liar is the fool who believed it.”\n\nThe one they call “The Right Hand of His Majesty” is living proof of that. He’s no ordinary follower; Redna swears he’s crueler, more despotic, and more fanatical than his master.\n\nIf you’ve the steel for it, cut him down while you’re making your way through Radiance Town. Then, report to Redna. She and him had… unfinished business.",o="在光辉镇击败陛下之右手。",oEN="Defeat Right Hand of His Majesty in Radiance Town.",p="你杀了他吗？他还有呼吸吗？确保他受尽折磨！",pEN="Did you kill him? Is he still breathing? Make sure he suffers!",c="<那矮人仔细听着，几乎憋不住一个没牙的笑。>\n\n你杀了那混蛋？\n\n<他麻风般的脸亮了起来。>\n\n你给了他应得的下场。作为回报，我会给你应得的东西：一份配得上你带给我的满足感的奖赏。",cEN="<The dwarf listens closely, barely able to contain a toothless grin.>\n\nDid you kill that bastard?\n\n<Her leprous face lights up.>\n\nYou gave him what he had coming. In return, I’ll give you what you deserve: a reward worthy of the satisfaction you’ve given me."}
Q[1660040]={d="你要进那骸骨殿去吗？\n\n<那精灵狐疑地看着你，掂量你的价值，判断你是否适合这项任务。>\n\n一头由内脏与骸骨构成的怪物正滑行在骸骨殿的隧道中，渴望啃食尸体。那些虫子——愚蠢的亵渎者——不过是它的后代。\n\n杀了那东西，我确信教团会给你丰厚的报酬。",dEN="Heading into the ossuary, are you?\n\n<The elf eyes you doubtfully, weighing your worth before deciding if you’re fit for the task.>\n\nA monstrosity of entrails and bone slithers through the ossuary tunnels, ravenous for corpses to gnaw. The worms, foolish defilers, are nothing but its spawn.\n\nKill the creature and… I’m certain the cult will reward you handsomely.",o="在月华骸骨殿击败腐肉孽种。",oEN="Defeat the Rotting Flesh Spawn in the Lunar Ossuary.",p="那憎恶……死了吗？",pEN="The abomination… is it dead?",c="那憎恶……死了吗？\n\n<那精灵瞥了一眼你的装束，上面沾满了带血的黏液残渣。>\n\n憎恶死了。\n\n太好了。",cEN="The abomination… is it dead?\n\n<The elf glances over your garb, splattered with bits of bloody mucus.>\n\nThe abomination is dead.\n\nSplendid."}
Q[1660041]={d="我感觉前方有什么东西。在蜘蛛、蛇与蝙蝠的灵魂之间……还有什么在移动，将它的力量倾注进守护这处洞穴的屏障里。\n\n如果我们成功……如果我能活着离开这里……你就得杀掉那个生物，把它送回它该去的另一边。",dEN="I be feelin’ a presence up ahead. Among de spider spirit, de snake, de bat… someting else be movin’, pourin’ it power into de barrier guardin’ dis cave.\n\nIf we be succeedin’… if I be makin’ it outta here alive… ya gonna hafta strike down dat creature an’ send it back ta de other side, where it belong.",o="在阴暗巢穴中击败守门者泰克拉图。",oEN="Defeat Techla’tu, Gatekeeper, in the Sinister Lair.",p="那灵魂……我能感觉到它滑行，感觉到翅膀的拍打。那究竟是什么样的野兽？",pEN="De spirit… I can feel it slither, feel de wings beat. What kinda beast be dat?",c="从洞穴里，它正在变化……你杀掉那个守护灵魂了，是吗？\n\n很好。那或许你有机会对抗那个女巫了。而多亏了你，我也有机会了。\n\n拿着这个。一点小小的谢意。",cEN="De cave, it be changin’… ya done slain de guardian spirit, eh?\n\nGood. Maybe you be havin’ a chance ‘gainst de witch, den. An’ thanks ta you, I be havin’ one too.\n\nHere, take dis. A small token o’ me gratitude."}
Q[1660042]={d="我们是怪物。但比我们的命运更可悲的，是游荡在我们森林与田野间的野兽们的困惑与痛苦。\n\n曾几何时，我想我的心也许还会怜悯它们。但我已不再有同情心了。而且，最实际的做法就是除掉它们。\n\n尤其是凯恩家那头忠诚的老猎犬。\n\n绕到宅邸后面，找到它的坟墓，确认它真的死了。它不会是第一头嗅出主人踪迹的亡灵猎犬……然后把他吞掉。",dEN="We are monsters. But sadder still than our fate is the confused, agonized misery of the beasts that roam our woods and fields.\n\nOnce, I think my heart might have pitied them. But I’ve no pity left. And besides, the practical thing is to put them down.\n\nEspecially the old, faithful hound of the Cain family.\n\nCircle the mansion, find his grave, and make sure he’s truly dead. He wouldn’t be the first undead mastiff to catch his master’s scent… and devour him.",o="击败宅邸后方的凯恩家族猎犬。",oEN="Defeat the Hound of House Cain behind the manor.",p="我想我听到那野兽在远处嗥叫。请快点解决它。",pEN="I think I heard the beast howling in the distance. End it quickly, please.",c="那猎犬……死了吗？\n\n<那被遗忘者摇着头，满怀悲痛。>\n\n真可惜。腐化扭曲了太多心智，不冒险才是更稳妥的做法。\n\n谁知道呢……也许这条狗本可以不一样。\n\n拿着。这是你应得的。",cEN="The hound… it’s dead?\n\n<The Forsaken shakes his head, heavy with sorrow.>\n\nA shame. Rot has twisted so many minds, it’s safer not to take chances.\n\nWho knows… perhaps this dog might’ve been different.\n\nHere. You’ve earned it."}
Q[1660043]={d="也许你注意到了那个可怜的存在……那只在硬盆地上空盘旋、霸占着战场上散落腐尸的鸟。\n\n它不过是回声的回声，但它飞在上头，我困在这下面……让我牙痒。\n\n杀了它，好吗？就算不是为我，也为了奖赏。\n\n<鬣狗之灵露出一口锋利牙齿的狡黠笑容。>\n\n哦，是的……那份奖赏绝对值得。远远值得。",dEN="Perhaps you noticed that wretched presence… the bird circling over Hard Basin, lording over the carrion scattered across the battlefield.\n\nHe’s nothing but an echo of an echo, but with me stuck down here and him flying free above… it makes my teeth itch.\n\nKill him, will you? If not for me, then for the reward.\n\n<The hyena spirit flashes a sly grin full of sharp teeth.>\n\nOh yes… the reward will be worth it. More than worth it.",o="在硬盆地击败残忍的腐尸之灵。",oEN="Defeat the Cruel Carrion Spirit in Hard Basin.",p="<鬣狗嗅了嗅空气，然后把目光投向天空。>\n\n那秃鹫……你解决它了吗？",pEN="<The hyena sniffs the air, then fixes its gaze on the sky.>\n\nThe vulture… have you finished him?",c="终于！\n\n那具死尸变成了腐肉。美味。等他父亲知道我策划杀了他无数私生子中的一个，一定会暴跳如雷。\n\n又一笔账，记在我们那本漫长而血腥的账簿上。\n\n<最后一声得意的大笑，为这灵魂的呓语画上句号。>\n\n好吧，那么，承诺就是承诺。明智地挑选你的奖赏吧。",cEN="At last!\n\nThe scavenger turned to carrion. Delicious. His father will rage when he learns I conspired to kill one of his countless bastards.\n\nAnother grievance to add to our long, bloody tally.\n\n<A final, triumphant cackle ends the spirit’s rant.>\n\nWell then, a promise is a promise. Choose your reward wisely."}
Q[1660050]={d="你在这里干得不错。\n\n等你在丧钟镇办完事，去布瑞尔拜访药剂师弗莱默。他就是我之前提到的那位\"某人\"。\n\n告诉他，只要我抽得出空，就会给他送去一车他制作憎恶所需的肉。",dEN="You've done good work here.\n\nWhen you're finished at Deathknell, pay a visit to Apothecary Flemer in Brill. He's that “someone” I mentioned earlier.\n\nTell him that as soon as I'm able, I'll send a shipment of the flesh he needs for his abomination.",o="在布瑞尔与药剂师弗莱默交谈。",oEN="Speak with Apothecary Flemer in Brill.",c="<那被遗忘者用一把像破乐器似的嗓子哼着阴森的调子，注意力全在手中的实验上。>\n\n你是……？\n\n啊。\n\n好吧。我可以等，虽然我这双手从不闲着。埃里克答应我的肉，并不是让一具憎恶活过来所需的唯一材料。",cEN="<The Forsaken hums a sinister tune in a voice like a cracked instrument, his focus pinned to the experiment in his hands.>\n\nAnd you are…?\n\nAh.\n\nVery well. I can wait, though never with idle hands. The flesh Eric promised me isn't the only ingredient needed to bring an abomination to life."}
Q[1660051]={d="该怎么解释，才能让你那凡俗的脑子听懂呢？\n\n一具憎恶不只是它各部分的总和。对天灾军团而言，那秘密配方是一丝死灵魔法。而我们皇家药剂师协会，则不得不寻找……更有创意的方案。\n\n矗立在布瑞尔上方的那座塔里，长着方圆数里内我见过的最奇特的真菌。它以死亡与死灵魔法为养分长得肥硕，而它的孢子至今仍随着那种精华搏动。\n\n把你找到的每一份孢子都带给我，无论是粘在守卫者皮肉上的，还是裹在地面黏液球里的。",dEN="How to put this so a lay mind like yours might grasp it?\n\nAn abomination is more than the sum of its parts. For the Scourge, the secret ingredient was a dash of necromancy. We, of the Royal Apothecary Society, are obliged to find... more creative solutions.\n\nThe tower that looms over Brill shelters a fungal growth unlike any I've seen for miles. It fattened itself on death and necromancy, and its spores still pulse with that essence.\n\nBring me every spore you find, whether they're clinging to the hides of its wardens, or trapped in mucous globules scattered across the floor.",o="从俯瞰布瑞尔的废弃高塔的蘑菇上采集亡灵孢子。它们有两种形态：附着在生物身上，以及封装在地面的黏液球中。",oEN="Collect Necrotic Spores from the fungus in the abandoned tower overlooking Brill. They come in two forms: clinging to creatures and encapsulated in mucous globules on the ground.",p="你带来孢子了吗？",pEN="Did you bring the spores?",c="<那被遗忘者以行家的眼光检视样本；一旦达到他的标准，他便眯起眼睛，冷淡而耐心，露出一丝居高临下的浅笑。>\n\n干得不错，出乎我的意料。\n\n这些孢子散发着死灵能量。在它们的潜力能为科学所用之前，还需要一段漫长的培育过程……\n\n但有了这些，再加上另外一些零件，你很快就会看到：我这具造物死去的血肉，由这双巧手缝补拼合，将会抽搐着活过来！",cEN="<The Forsaken inspects the samples with a clinician's eye; once they meet his standard, his gaze narrows, coldly patient, and a thin, condescending smile appears.>\n\nGood work, much to my surprise.\n\nThe spores radiate necrotic energy. A long curing awaits before their potential can be bent to the service of science…\n\nBut with this, and a few other pieces, you'll see soon enough: the dead flesh of my construct, stitched and patchworked by these expert hands, will spasm into life!"}
Q[1660052]={d="凿子、锤子、角尺、圆规……这些我们石匠工会多得是。剑、弓、法杖、斧头？我们连该抓哪一头都不知道。至于你嘛……\n\n往东，沿着明水湖岸构筑工事的一伙叛军拒绝了黑暗女士的旨意；一群头脑简单的蠢货，以为活人会张开双臂迎接他们。\n\n我的弟弟就在其中。如果我等着塞弗伦法官派他的死亡猎手去，消息就会走漏；我的名声会被玷污，我作为工会会长那无可挑剔的地位也会随之受损。\n\n解决那些叛军。一个都别留。最重要的是，确保我弟弟逃不掉。",dEN="Chisels, hammers, squares, compasses... that's what we have in abundance here, the Masons' Lodge. Swords, bows, staves, axes? We wouldn't even know which end to hold. You, on the other hand...\n\nEast of here, dug in along Brightwater Lake, a band of rebels has rejected the Dark Lady's rule; simple-minded fools who think the living will greet them with open arms.\n\nMy brother is among them. If I wait for Magistrate Sevren to send his Deathstalkers, word will get out; my name stained, and with it my spotless standing as head of the lodge.\n\nPut the rebels down. Leave none alive. And above all, make certain my brother does not walk away.",o="找到沿明水湖岸构筑工事的被遗忘者叛军，并将他们全部消灭。",oEN="Find the Forsaken Rebels entrenched along the shores of Brightwater Lake and put them down.",p="你已经……你懂的……处理了那件事吗？",pEN="Have you… you know… taken care of that matter?",c="办妥了吗？你解决掉那帮叛徒了吗？\n\n<当你确认他弟弟的死讯时，一丝笑意掠过德尔卡德·萨丁的脸。>\n\n很好。现在再没人会知道阿尔里克差点给我们家族名声带来的耻辱了。\n\n他从不接受自己是什么：一个被遗忘者。但当一个问题无解时，它就不再是问题，而变成了另一样东西：一个必须面对的现实。",cEN="Is it done? Have you cleared out that traitorous rabble?\n\n<A flicker of a smile crosses Delcard Sading's face as you confirm his brother's death.>\n\nGood. Now no one will ever know the shame Alric nearly brought upon our family name.\n\nHe never accepted what he was—Forsaken. But when a problem has no solution, it ceases to be a problem and becomes something else: a reality to be faced."}
Q[1660053]={d="<阿尔里克·萨丁与血色十字军一个叫贝尔蒙特的人之间的往来信件。>\n\n<看来叛军与十字军已联络了一段时间，并即将打开他们栅栏的大门以示善意。>\n\n<那些人类的营地标记在北边。有必要去短暂拜访一下……提醒他们，谁才是这片土地的主人。>",dEN="<Correspondence exchanged between Alric Sading and a certain Belmont of the Scarlet Crusade.>\n\n<It seems the rebels had been in touch with the crusaders for some time, and were about to throw open the gates of their palisade as a token of goodwill.>\n\n<The humans' camp is marked to the north. A brief visit is in order... to remind them who holds lordship over these lands.>",o="找到血色十字军的营地，消灭他们的特工。",oEN="Find the Scarlet Crusade camp and put down their agents.",p="<德尔卡德缓缓摇头，仿佛在自言自语。>",pEN="<Delcard shakes his head slowly, as if to himself.>",c="我弟弟和那些叛军一直在与血色十字军联络……还打算邀请他们进来？\n\n<德尔卡德发出一阵沙哑的大笑，笑松了一颗牙；那牙啪地一声打在墙上。>\n\n好吧。看来我白把你拖进这摊事了。他们反正都要死；不是死在你的手上，就是落入十字军之手。\n\n多天真啊。毕竟，他们从来就算不上什么威胁。",cEN="My brother and the rebels were in contact with the Scarlet Crusade… and they were going to invite them in?\n\n<Delcard lets out a hoarse cackle that knocks a tooth loose; it clacks off the wall.>\n\nWell. Seems I dragged you into this for nothing. They were going to die either way; by your hand, or at the crusaders' mercy.\n\nHow naive. They were never a threat, after all."}
Q[1660054]={d="<看来你是少数有好奇心、愿意听听女妖之王布道的灵魂之一。>\n\n<也许她真有什么值得分享的东西。>",dEN="<Looks like you're one of the rare curious souls ready to hear a banshee's sermon.>\n\n<Perhaps she has something worth sharing.>",o="远离喧嚣与匆忙，稍作停留，听暗影祭司阿莎拉说上一会儿。",oEN="Take a moment from the noise and haste and stay a while to listen to Dark Priestess Ashara.",c="好奇心并不属于我们在遗忘之影教派中奉行的三美德之一。\n\n但它是它们的前厅。",cEN="Curiosity is not one of the Three Virtues we keep in the Cult of the Forgotten Shadow.\n\nBut it is their antechamber."}
Q[1660055]={d="你一整天都在修道院进进出出，可我到现在也没见到我弟弟的影子。\n\n我猜你没能把他从那状态里拉出来。好吧……值得一试。\n\n<他漫长而疲惫的叹息说明了一切。>\n\n你还要再出去吗？也许你能再帮我一个忙。去修道院的路上，我把一名女仆留在了闪金镇，带着一长串要采购的材料；给我母亲用的药。\n\n她叫杜尔西内娅。你能找到她，告诉她我会迟到吗？",dEN="You've been in and out of the abbey all day, yet I still haven't seen my brother anywhere.\n\nI take it you couldn't snap him out of it. Well... worth a try.\n\n<Her long, weary sigh says enough.>\n\nHeading out again? Maybe you can do me one more favor. On the way to the abbey I left one of my maids in Goldshire with a long list of ingredients to buy; medicine for my mother.\n\nHer name is Dulcinea. Could you find her and let her know I'll be late?",o="在闪金镇找到比安卡的女仆杜尔西内娅。",oEN="Find Dulcinea, Bianca's maid, in Goldshire.",c="是比安卡夫人派你们来的吗？\n\n<杜尔西内娅笨拙地行了个礼。>\n\n那她要迟到了……我发誓，她那个弟弟就是个麻烦精。\n\n不管怎样，她母亲的药不能等。你愿意帮我跑跑腿吗？",cEN="Did my lady Bianca send you?\n\n<Dulcinea dips into an awkward curtsy.>\n\nSo she’ll be delayed… I swear, that brother of hers is nothing but trouble.\n\nEither way, her mother’s medicine can’t wait. Would you be so kind as to help me with my errands?"}
Q[1660056]={d="阿格里娅·斯帕达女士是一位被岁月围困的妇人。近来她饱受一连串病痛折磨，卧床不起。\n\n只有一样东西能让她舒缓：她的炼金大师调制的药剂。\n\n我已经收集了一些材料，但清单又长又苛刻。我们还需要埃尔格里斯花瓣、敦卡兹烈酒浓缩液、南瓜汁和一颗鱼人眼球。\n\n去市场转一圈吧。等你全都弄到手，就到我家夫人的宅邸报个信。我不敢独自走那些路，可你……你可不是一般人，对吧？",dEN="Lady Agria Spada is a woman besieged by age. Of late she's borne a litany of ailments that keep her to her bed.\n\nOnly one thing eases her: the draught brewed by her master alchemist.\n\nI've gathered a few ingredients, but the list is long and fussy. We still need Elgris Blossom Petals, Dun Kazad Liquor Concentrate, Pumpkin Juice, and a Murloc Eyeball.\n\nTake a turn through the market. Once you've got the lot, report to my lady's manor. I don't dare the roads alone, but you... you're made of sterner stuff, aren't you?",o="在闪金镇的市场购买药剂材料：埃尔格里斯花瓣、敦卡兹烈酒浓缩液、南瓜汁和一颗鱼人眼球。",oEN="Buy the potion's ingredients at the Goldshire market: Elgris Blossom Petals, Dun Kazad Liquor Concentrate, Pumpkin Juice, and a Murloc Eyeball.",p="什么事？您来斯帕达庄园有何贵干？",pEN="Yes? What business brings you to the Spada estate?",c="又一个跑腿的？\n\n我不知道比安卡夫人和莫罗伊自以为在玩什么把戏，但他们的母亲，我的阿格里娅夫人，没多少时间了……\n\n<阿尔迪娅怜悯地看着那位老妇人。她裹在一层层被单和披肩里，看起来已经半截入土。>\n\n材料……你带了吗？很好。我会确保它们送到炼金师手上。",cEN="Another errand-runner?\n\nI don’t know what Lady Bianca and Moroi think they’re playing at, but their mother,my lady Agria, doesn’t have much time left…\n\n<Aldia gives the old woman a pitying look. Swaddled in layers of sheets and shawls, she looks half-buried already.>\n\nThe ingredients… Do you have them? Good. I’ll see they’re handed to the alchemist."}
Q[1660057]={d="嗯……\n\n<管家投来一道漫长而审视的目光。>\n\n在你走之前……我还需要你帮我处理另一件事。\n\n我长久以来都觉得，我家夫人的病痛不是肉体上的，而是魔法上的。一道诅咒。\n\n一切从一面破碎的镜子开始。而你知道人们怎么说。无论我收拾得多仔细，碎片仍不断出现；玻璃的碎块藏在宅邸和庭院各处。\n\n能麻烦你处理一下吗？",dEN="Hm...\n\n<The majordomo gives you a long, measuring look.>\n\nBefore you go... I need your help with one more matter.\n\nI've had the sense for some time that my lady's ailments aren't physical, but magical. A curse.\n\nIt started with a broken mirror. And you know what they say. However thorough I've been, shards keep turning up; bits of glass tucked around the manor and the grounds.\n\nWould you kindly deal with them?",o="检查那些被阿尔迪娅·克雷永归咎于折磨阿格里娅·斯帕达女士的诅咒的碎镜片。",oEN="Inspect the broken mirror shards that Aldia Crayon blames for the curse afflicting Lady Agria Spada.",p="你找到镜子的碎片了吗？",pEN="Did you find the mirror shards?",c="这么说我的直觉没错。\n\n衰老无药可医，但诅咒破除之后，至少阿格里娅女士那些可怕的疼痛应当会减轻。\n\n<他说话时，岁月的痕迹清晰可见：一张枯槁的脸上刻着深沟，双眼湿润而疲惫；他比自己所侍奉的那位夫人年轻不了多少。>\n\n感谢你尽职的效劳。",cEN="So my instincts were right.\n\nThere’s no cure for old age, but with the curse broken, at least Lady Agria’s terrible pains should ease.\n\n<As he speaks, the years show: furrows cut deep in a lean face, watery eyes spent; he’s hardly younger than the lady he serves.>\n\nThank you for your diligent service."}
Q[1660058]={d="低语。他们以为没人察觉，可我睡觉时耳朵贴着地面！哈！\n\n他们挖啊挖啊挖。他们会在你最意想不到的时候发动袭击……除非你先动手。\n\n狗头人，狗头人，还是狗头人。就在我们脚下！当心你的脚下。留神你的步子！\n\n找到它们的洞穴，放火烧掉。碾碎它们。用一把又大又重的锤子！\n\n<她自顾自地笑着，然后直勾勾地盯着虚空。>",dEN="Whispers. They think no one's noticed,but I sleep with my ear to the floor! Ha!\n\nThey dig and dig and dig. They'll strike when you least expect it... unless you do something first.\n\nKobolds and kobolds and more kobolds. Under our feet! Watch where you step. Mind your footing!\n\nFind their warrens and set them alight. Crush them. With a big, heavy hammer!\n\n<She laughs to herself, then stares into the middle distance.>",o="搜寻并摧毁闪金镇一带的狗头人巢穴。",oEN="Find and destroy the kobold warrens around Goldshire.",p="别让那些害虫活下来一个，否则闪金镇会在它们的隧道下坍塌。",pEN="Leave none of those vermin alive, or Goldshire will cave in under their tunnels.",c="<疯癫的克拉拉右手举着一个苹果，像在欣赏自己最珍贵的财产。\n\n闪金镇就像这个苹果。\n\n<她缓缓转动它，露出一个咬痕；里面——尽管外表光鲜——已经腐烂，爬满了虫。>",cEN="<Clara the Mad holds an apple in her right hand, admiring it as if it were her most prized possession.>\n\nGoldshire is like this apple.\n\n<Slowly, she turns it to show a bite; inside—despite appearances—it’s rotten, worm-eaten.>"}
Q[1660059]={d="欢迎。\n\n我是索姆——哈文德·索姆——闪金镇镇长，代表布鲁克领主及其家族行事。\n\n你或许注意到了这座大厅阴影下那座临时营地。近来，闪金镇收容了无数来自西部荒野的难民。有时我担心这已超出我们的能力……\n\n即便如此，只要他们还在挨饿，我就不会背过身去。到镇子的田野里走一圈，每样收成各取一些，送到营地去。我准许你这么做，布鲁克领主自然也一样。",dEN="Welcome.\n\nI am Thorm—Harvend Thorm—mayor of Goldshire, serving on behalf of Lord Bruk and his house.\n\nYou may have noticed the makeshift camp in the shadow of this grand hall. Of late, Goldshire has taken in countless refugees out of Westfall. At times I fear it's beyond our means...\n\nEven so, I won't turn away while they go hungry. Walk the village fields and take a little from each harvest to bring to the camp. You have my leave—and, by extension, Lord Bruk's.",o="从闪金镇周围的农场采集甜瓜、南瓜和苹果。然后把它们交给难民首领埃尔多·锤手。",oEN="Gather Melons, Pumpkins, and Apples from the farms around Goldshire. Then deliver them to Eldor Hammer, leader of the refugees.",p="我能帮你什么吗？",pEN="Can I help you?",c="我的人民不会忘记闪金镇的善意。\n\n我相信总有一天我们会全数偿还。",cEN="My people won’t forget Goldshire’s kindness.\n\nI trust that one day we’ll repay it in full."}
Q[1660060]={d="说起来，在村子的历史上，我算是这儿最权威的人了。想来一段简短的课吗？\n\n<这位老巫师看起来急于开口，几乎是迫不及待。>\n\n<也许他真有什么值得分享的东西。>",dEN="As it turns out, I'm the leading authority around here when it comes to the village's history. Care for a short lesson?\n\n<The aging sorcerer seems eager, almost desperate, to talk.>\n\n<Perhaps he has something worth sharing.>",o="远离喧嚣与匆忙，稍作休息，听阿利斯卡·伦德说上一会儿。",oEN="Take a moment from the noise and haste and stay a while to listen to Aliscar Lend.",c="希望我没让你太无聊！",cEN="I hope I didn’t bore you too much!"}
Q[1660061]={d="试炼谷名副其实，朋友。\n\n我的位置在这里，但道路在召唤你。我想我大致能猜到接下来你会去哪里。\n\n我在剃刀岭认识一位智者，他或许用得上你的帮助。他叫卡拉加。去找他，顺便把希尔苏塔、那场仪式，以及你挫败她计划的英勇事迹都告诉他。",dEN="The Valley of Trials lived up to its name with you, friend.\n\nMy place is here, but the road's calling you. And I think I've a fair guess where you'll head next.\n\nI know a sage in Razor Hill who could use your help. His name is Karagar. Find him, and while you're at it, tell him everything about Hirsutta, the ritual, and your heroic intervention to foil her plans.",o="在剃刀岭与卡拉加交谈。",oEN="Speak with Karagar in Razor Hill.",c="<那老兽人眯着眼听你讲述试炼谷的经历。>\n\n我从不喜欢那个希尔苏塔。也从不信任她的巫毒。时间证明我是对的。\n\n你能击败她真是万幸。但我担心她那野心的余波不会很快消散。她仪式的后果甚至在这里、在棘齿城都能感受到。",cEN="<The old orc listens to your account of the Valley of Trials with a half-lidded stare.>\n\nI never liked that Hirsutta. And I never trusted her voodoo. Shame time proved me right.\n\nIt's a blessing you managed to bring her down. But I fear the echo of her ambition won't die quickly. The consequences of her ritual are reverberating even here, in Razor Hill."}
Q[1660062]={d="希尔苏塔释放的力量引来了那些永远饥渴的纳迦，它们游荡在杜隆塔尔的沿海。\n\n你曾遇见过它们吗？精灵与毒蛇的混种。它们从海中爬出，占据了东边一处海滨洞穴的废墟。\n\n我怀疑它们并不清楚究竟是什么引发了它们所感受到的那股激增，但它们来此就是为了探究其本质。迟早，它们会成为麻烦。\n\n除非你先下手为强。",dEN="The powers Hirsutta loosed drew the eye of the ever-hungry naga that prowl Durotar's shores.\n\nEver crossed paths with one? Elf-and-serpent hybrids. They've slithered out of the sea and holed up in the ruins of a coastal cave, east of here.\n\nI doubt they know exactly what sparked the surge they sensed, but they're here to probe its nature. Sooner or later, they'll be a problem.\n\nUnless you see to them first.",o="击败杜隆塔尔海岸裂痕废墟洞穴中的纳迦。",oEN="Defeat naga in Rivenruin Cave on the Durotar coast.",p="<老人闭上双眼，那姿态透着深沉的专注与无尽的耐心。>",pEN="<The elder closes his eyes, a gesture of deep focus and endless patience.>",c="<尽管老兽人的双眼仍然闭着，他依旧感知到了你的存在。>\n\n纳迦已经死了。\n\n我从大地中感知到了；你每走一步，它都在我耳边低语。水也告诉了我，它被它们的血染红了。\n\n我向你致谢，<class>。",cEN="<Though the old orc's eyes remain shut, he senses your presence all the same.>\n\nThe naga are dead.\n\nI felt it in the earth; it whispered every step you took into my ear. The water told me too, reddened by their blood.\n\nYou have my thanks, <class>."}
Q[1660063]={d="你是为纳迦而来的？\n\n太好了！\n\n你看，我一直在洞穴废墟里翻找，收集精灵遗物打算拿去拍卖行转卖（你会惊讶那些古董值多少钱），这时第一只纳迦出现了。\n\n我只得拔腿就跑！而且，你可以想象，我几乎什么都没来得及抓。\n\n既然你反正要进那洞穴，能不能顺便帮我捡些遗物回来？我拍卖所得分你一份！",dEN="You here about the naga?\n\nPerfect!\n\nSee, I was poking around the cave ruins, scooping up elven relics to flip at auction (you'd be amazed what those antiques fetch) when the first naga showed up.\n\nI had to hightail it! And, as you can imagine, I barely grabbed a thing.\n\nSince you're heading into the cave anyway, mind picking up a few relics for me? I'll cut you in for a percentage of whatever I pull at the Auction House!",o="从杜隆塔尔裂痕废墟洞穴的废墟中找回上古精灵遗物。",oEN="Recover Elven Relics of Old from the ruins in Rivenruin Cave, Durotar.",p="想象一下我们能赚多少钱！",pEN="Just imagine the money we can make!",c="<看到你拖着那些精灵遗物走来，地精的眼睛像得到糖果的孩子一样亮了起来。>\n\n太棒了！妙极了！了不起！\n\n我要靠这个发大财了。至少……<他没说完一个数字就住了口。他抿起嘴唇，假装凑近细看。>\n\n也许我有点得意忘形了。看看这个，品相糟糕透顶！没人会为这么破烂的东西付一枚金币……\n\n算了。我不能说我言而无信。这是你辛苦一趟的一点报酬……象征性的，当然。",cEN="<The goblin's eyes light up like a kid handed candy when he sees you hauling in the elven relics.>\n\nSplendid! Wonderful! Phenomenal!\n\nI'm gonna make a killing on this. At least… <he cuts himself off before naming a number. He puckers up and pretends to take a closer look.>\n\nMaybe I got a little carried away. Look at this, the condition's awful! No one's paying top coin for something this beat-up…\n\nAnyway. Can't say I don't keep my promises. Here's a little payment for the effort… symbolic, of course."}
Q[1660064]={d="你是新来棘齿城的？\n\n我叫迪尔格兰；是这座矿里干活的苦工的工头。\n\n想挣几个铜板吗？\n\n我需要有人把这只水罐装满，带进矿里给我的苦工们解渴。\n\n你肯定也注意到了，这不用什么专家——杜隆塔尔缺水。但镇子外路边就有几个水洼，还算能喝。",dEN="New to Razor Hill?\n\nName's Dirgran; foreman over the peons working this mine.\n\nWant to earn a little coin?\n\nI need someone to fill this pitcher and head into the mine to slake my peons' thirst.\n\nYou've noticed, I'm sure, doesn't take a keen eye, that water's scarce in Durotar. But there are a few pools just outside town, by the road, still fit to drink.",o="在剃刀岭外用任一水洼装满水罐，然后给矿里的苦工们喝水。",oEN="Fill the pitcher with water from one of the pools outside Razor Hill, then give the mine peons a drink.",p="我倒不介意来一口凉水……",pEN="I wouldn't mind a swig of cold water myself…",c="别问我为什么，但我敢发誓里面比外面还热。\n\n几乎每天都有苦工晕倒。\n\n他们会感激你带来的凉水。",cEN="Don't ask me how, but I'd swear it's hotter in there than out here.\n\nHardly a day goes by without a peon keeling over.\n\nThey'll be grateful for the cool water you brought them."}
Q[1660065]={d="坐下吧，别客气。够两个人坐。\n\n<老兽人做了个欢迎的手势，低声嘟囔着，仿佛在自言自语。>\n\n<也许他真有什么值得分享的东西。>",dEN="Sit down, don't worry. There's room for both of us.\n\n<The old orc gestures in welcome, murmuring as if to himself.>\n\n<Perhaps he has something worth sharing.>",o="远离喧嚣与匆忙，稍作休息，听巴加穆尔·天牙说上一会儿。",oEN="Take a moment from the noise and haste and stay a while to listen to Bagamul Skyfang.",c="谢谢你的陪伴，<class>。\n\n很少有人愿意费心听这个老兽人说话。",cEN="Thank you for the company, <class>.\n\nFew bother to listen to this old orc."}
Q[1660066]={d="你是要翻过这些围墙，去血蹄村吗？\n\n我一直在望着那个方向的地平线，我敢发誓风里带着烟；一股烧焦的味道。\n\n这并不奇怪；即便在莫高雷这里，牛头人也不缺敌人。\n\n去拜访安穆斯·灰眼吧，就在上面那片台地。她是我们当中最有智慧的人，独自照看着山顶的神殿。\n\n我们常去找她，取她为仪式祝福的圣水。如果血蹄村正面临危机，他们会比任何时候都更需要那些祝福。",dEN="Headed to Bloodhoof Village, beyond these walls?\n\nI've been watching the horizon that way, and I'd swear the wind was carrying smoke; a scorched tang to it.\n\nIt wouldn't be strange; even here in Mulgore, the tauren are not without enemies.\n\nPay a visit to Ammus Grey-Eye, up on the mesa. She's the wisest among us and tends the sanctuary at the summit alone.\n\nWe usually go to her for the water she blesses for our rites. If Bloodhoof Village faces a crisis, they'll need those blessings more than ever.",o="在伊里斯神殿山顶与安穆斯·灰眼交谈。",oEN="Speak with Ammus Grey-Eye at the summit of the Iris Sanctuary.",c="哦，一张新面孔。\n\n<老人用覆着灰毛的双手轻抚你的脸颊，温柔地笑着。>\n\n你是为血蹄村的火来的，对吧？我曾警告过村里那位萨满，他嗜火成性中潜藏的危险。\n\n他没听。",cEN="Oh, a new face.\n\n<The elder cups your cheeks with hands furred in grey and smiles, tenderly.>\n\nYou’re here about the fire in Bloodhoof Village, aren’t you? I warned the village shaman of the dangers tucked inside his fondness for flame.\n\nHe did not listen."}
Q[1660067]={d="这座神殿是为纪念大地之母与天空之父而建。下雨时，中央那块中空的石头会接住云朵慷慨赐予的雨水。\n\n随后，我会依照全套仪式为它祝福。\n\n用洗涤图腾基座的水装满一只圣水罐，把它带给血蹄村的智者穆德伦。有了它，他就能安抚暴怒的元素，恢复村子的灵魂和谐。\n\n我不知道这是否能弥补阿尔杜诺的鲁莽，但它能减轻其后果。",dEN="This sanctuary was raised in honor of the Earthmother and the Sky-Father. When it rains, the hollowed stone at its heart gathers the water the clouds so generously bestow.\n\nThen, with all due ceremony, I bless it.\n\nFill an amphora with the water that washes the totem's feet, and carry it to Sage Muudren in Bloodhoof Village. With it, he can soothe the roused elements and restore the village's spiritual harmony.\n\nI do not know if it will mend Ardunno's rashness, but it will help to soften its effects.",o="用伊里斯神殿的圣水装满圣水罐，把它带给血蹄村的智者穆德伦。",oEN="Fill the amphora with the blessed water of the Iris Sanctuary, and bring it to Sage Muudren in Bloodhoof Village.",p="又一个牛头人小伙子。这村子满是前途无量的战士。",pEN="Another young tauren. This village teems with promising warriors.",c="这是……\n\n<望着那罐由安穆斯·灰眼祝福过的圣水，那牛头人的目光因感激而温暖起来。>\n\n你能感受到这些水散发的力量吗？很少有人能完全感受到。它就像对灵魂的爱抚；漫长喧嚣的一天之后的一片寂静。\n\n这些水会帮我恢复被阿尔杜诺扰乱了的元素平衡。不过，我仍然需要你的帮助。",cEN="This is…\n\n<The tauren’s gaze warms with gratitude as he regards the amphora of water blessed by Ammus Grey-Eye.>\n\nCan you feel the power these waters give off? Few can, fully. It’s like a caress to the spirit; a hush after a long, noisy day.\n\nThese waters will help me restore the elemental balance Ardunno disturbed. Even so, I will still need your help."}
Q[1660068]={d="阿尔杜诺就是引发那场大火的萨满。他死于自己的愚蠢，而我们运气不错，火焰没有蔓延出他的小屋。\n\n即便如此，他在死前不久召唤出的元素仍游荡在烧焦的废墟之间。你知道我说的是哪种：那些自身血肉即是火焰的暴怒之灵。\n\n四大元素中，最不稳定的一种。\n\n我将把圣水的祝福赐予你。用它削弱你遇到的火元素，把它们赶出这个村子，赶出这个世界，送回它们被囚禁的位面。",dEN="Ardunno was the shaman who set the blaze. He died of his own foolishness, and, luck for us, the flames did not spread beyond his hut.\n\nEven so, the elementals he summoned moments before his death still wander among the charred remains. You know the kind I mean: wrathful spirits whose very flesh is fire.\n\nOf the four elements, the most volatile.\n\nI will lay the blessing of these waters upon you. Use it to weaken the fire elementals you find and banish them from this village, from this world, back to their prison-plane.",o="引导祝福以削弱游荡在阿尔杜诺小屋周围的火元素，并将它们驱赶回元素位面。",oEN="Channel the blessing to weaken the fire elementals prowling around Ardunno's hut and banish them back to their elemental plane.",p="你把火焰熄灭了吗？",pEN="Have you quenched the flames?",c="水的祝福正在消退，但它已完成了使命。\n\n你安然无恙地回来了。\n\n很少有人能说自己在面对火之灵后还能活着讲述经过。\n\n你为血蹄村立下了大功，<class>。",cEN="The water’s blessing fades, but it has done its work.\n\nYou return unharmed.\n\nFew can say they’ve faced spirits of fire and lived to tell it.\n\nYou have done Bloodhoof Village a great service, <class>."}
Q[1660069]={d="年轻的<race>，我的名字是埃姆尼尔，血蹄部族的先祖母。\n\n几个世纪前，在子孙后代占据这片土地之前很久，我便穿过了帷幕。那时他们把我的骨灰带到这里撒下；并在我身后竖起了你所见的这根巨大图腾。\n\n阿尔杜诺，那个心性如火、鲁莽、始终钟爱火焰的人，守护着仪式的熏香；但随着他的死，神圣的香烟消散了，我与生者国度的联系也随之而去。\n\n你能否出于荣誉，重新点燃这芬芳，补上神圣的熏香？",dEN="Young <race>, my name is Emnil, ancestress of the Bloodhoof.\n\nI crossed the veil centuries ago, long before the children of my children laid claim to these lands. Then they brought my ashes and scattered them in this place; and they raised behind me the great totem you behold.\n\nArdunno, fiery of spirit, reckless, ever enamored of the flame, kept the ritual incense; but with his death the sacred smoke grows thin, and with it my bond to the realm of the living.\n\nWill you, out of honor, rekindle the fragrance and replenish the sacred incense?",o="为先祖埃姆尼尔的祭坛取得熏香。你需要草原鼠尾草和科多兽油脂。",oEN="Obtain incense for Ancestor Emnil's altar. You will need Prairie Sage and Kodo Tallow.",p="袅袅青烟正在消散。熏香几乎耗尽了……",pEN="The curling smoke grows faint. The incense is nearly spent…",c="熏香重新旺盛地燃烧起来。因为这一举动，我的尊严得以恢复。\n\n我子孙的子孙仍将得到我的祝福；在日子变得黯淡时，带着希望与鼓励的话语。",cEN="The incense burns with renewed vigor. By this act, my dignity is restored.\n\nThe children of my children shall yet receive my blessing; in hope, and in words of heartening when the days grow dark."}
Q[1660070]={d="<这位年迈的牛头人女性与神殿领袖的描述相符，据说她是同族中最有智慧的人之一。>\n\n<也许她真有什么值得与你分享的东西。>",dEN="<The elder Tauren fits the description of the sanctuary leader, reputed to be among the wisest of her kind.>\n\n<Perhaps she has something worth sharing with you.>",o="远离喧嚣与匆忙，稍作休息，听安穆斯·灰眼说上一会儿。",oEN="Take a moment from the noise and haste and stay a while to listen to Ammus Grey-Eye.",c="在这里歇一会儿吧，就在悬崖边上。安静地；有时，言语只会抓伤真相。\n\n感受这一刻。趁它还在，留住它。\n\n品味生命本来的样子：一种既胜过血肉、也胜过言语的力量。",cEN="Rest here a while, on the very edge of the cliff. In silence; at times, words do no more than paw at the truth.\n\nFeel this moment. Keep it, for as long as it lasts.\n\nTaste Life as it is: a force that outstrips flesh and speech alike."}
Q[1660071]={d="等等。\n\n还有别的事。<萨里尔的声音紧绷；话从他唇间挤出来时彼此磕碰。>\n\n那个教团。那些把我姐姐引去的疯子。必须做点什么。\n\n我会留在奥达希尔，向特纳隆·风暴之握汇报这个教团。你去达纳苏斯，把一切都告诉塔隆凯·捷根。\n\n他们两人联手，会知道如何终结这一切。",dEN="Wait.\n\nThere's something else. <Thariel's voice comes out tight; the words stumble off his lips.>\n\nThat cult. The lunatics who lured in my sister. Something must be done.\n\nI'll stay here in Aldrassil and report the cult to Tenaron Stormgrip. You head to Dolanaar and tell Tallonkai Swiftroot everything.\n\nBetween them, they'll know how to shut this down.",o="在多兰纳尔与塔隆凯·捷根交谈。",oEN="Speak with Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.",c="是的，<class>，什么事让你来到多兰纳尔？\n\n<德鲁伊全神贯注地听你讲述。随着你的故事展开，他的脸色阴沉下来，眼角的皱纹愈发深刻。>\n艾吉娅……一个我曾希望再也不会听到的名字。这么说，他们在这儿了。在泰达希尔。\n\n真是胆大包天……\n\n忘掉那个教团吧，<name>，安心休息。我会亲自处理，把他们连根拔起。",cEN="Yes, <class>? What business brings you to Dolanaar?\n\n<The druid gives your account his full attention. As your tale unfolds, his face darkens and the lines at the corners of his eyes deepen.>\n\nAegya… A name I'd hoped never to hear again. So they're here, then. In Teldrassil.\n\nThe audacity…\n\nForget the Cult, <name>, and rest easy. I'll see to dismantling them myself."}
Q[1660072]={d="你在秃鹫教团手中活了下来，这足以证明你的价值。\n\n在我们上方，高踞于悬崖之上的，是瑟伦迪翁神殿，哨兵们在那里磨砺胆识。\n\n她们会欢迎像你这样能考验她们的人。这也许能让你头脑清醒，说不定你还能从她们身上学到一两招。\n\n向她们发起挑战，然后向她们的领袖阿德里莉娅·灵锻汇报。告诉她，我需要她的哨兵出手对付教团的威胁。",dEN="You survived the Vulture Cult, and that more than proves your worth.\n\nAbove us, perched on the cliff, stands the Theren-Dion Sanctuary, where the Sentinels test their mettle.\n\nThey'll welcome someone like you putting them through their paces. Might clear your head, and you might pick up a thing or two from them.\n\nChallenge them to a bout, then report to their leader, Adrilia Soultemper. Tell her I'll need her Sentinels to move on the cult threat.",o="在瑟伦迪翁神殿与哨兵们交谈，向她们发起决斗，帮助她们训练。",oEN="Speak with the Sentinels at Theren-Dion Sanctuary and challenge them to duels to aid their training.",p="什么事，<class>？",pEN="Yes, <class>?",c="这么说，秃鹫教团……\n\n<她的双眼是记忆的深井。在最深处，一桩古老的怨恨正在发酵。>\n无论塔隆凯有多无礼，我都会让我的哨兵们做好准备。他忘了，在政治上——一如在宗教、战争以及几乎所有要紧的事上——发号施令的都是女人。",cEN="So, the Vulture Cult…\n\n<Her eyes are deep wells of memory. Far below, an ancient rancor ferments.>\n\nI'll ready my Sentinels, impertinence or no from Tallonkai. He forgets that in politics—as in religion, in war, and in nearly everything that matters—it's the women who give the orders."}
Q[1660073]={d="秃鹫教团的逼近，解释了我们近来一直面对的一个问题。\n\n卡利姆多大陆的食腐鸟类很少会飞到泰达希尔的枝干上；然而最近，数十只已在这座神殿周围的岩石上落了脚。\n\n在你回多兰纳尔之前，帮我手下的哨兵们减轻这一威胁。摧毁秃鹫蛋，并准备好迎接双亲的怒火。\n\n然后，再来向我汇报。",dEN="The Vulture Cult's nearness explains a problem we've been facing of late.\n\nIt's rare for the carrion birds of mainland Kalimdor to reach Teldrassil's boughs; yet lately, dozens have settled on the rocks around this sanctuary.\n\nBefore you return to Dolanaar, help my Sentinels blunt their threat. Destroy the vulture eggs and be ready for the parents' fury.\n\nThen report back to me.",o="摧毁多兰纳尔附近瑟伦迪翁神殿一带的秃鹫蛋。",oEN="Destroy Vulture Eggs around the Theren-Dion Sanctuary near Dolanaar.",p="你处理掉那些秃鹫了吗？",pEN="Have you dealt with the vultures?",c="完成了吗？\n\n干得好。我的哨兵会处理剩下的，然后她们就准备好进攻秃鹫教团的巢穴，把艾吉娅女士绳之以法，一劳永逸。",cEN="Is it done?\n\nGood work. My Sentinels will see to the rest, and they'll be ready to strike the Vulture Cult's nest and bring Lady Aegya to justice, once and for all."}
Q[1660074]={d="Ishnu-alah，<class>。\n\n泰达希尔近来变得危险，多兰纳尔也不例外。\n\n从这里往西南，大地裂开，露出世界之树树干那广袤的核心。我的姐妹们在那里发现了一窝白蚁，正勉力守住防线……但我们人手太少，每杀死一只白蚁，就有两只溜出来占据它的位置。\n\n帮我们遏制白蚁的威胁，我会确保你得到与那下面所要冒的风险相称的完整报酬。",dEN="Ishnu-alah, <class>.\n\nTeldrassil has grown dangerous of late, and Dolanaar is no exception.\n\nSouthwest of here, the earth yawns open to bare the vast heartwood of the World Tree's trunk. My sisters have found a termite colony there and are holding the line... but we're too few, and for every termite we kill, two more scuttle in to take its place.\n\nHelp us stem the termite threat, and I'll see you're rewarded in full for the risk you'll take down there.",o="进入多兰纳尔附近的泰达希尔树皮之下，击败盘踞在深处的白蚁。",oEN="Enter the bark of Teldrassil near Dolanaar and defeat the termites infesting its depths.",p="你解决掉那些白蚁了吗？它们给你添了很多麻烦吗？",pEN="Have you finished off the termites? Did they give you much trouble?",c="打得漂亮，<class>。\n\n我的姐妹们满怀钦佩地认可你的功绩……还带着一丝嫉妒。\n\n我们哨兵会负责清剿余下的。",cEN="Well fought, <class>.\n\nMy sisters acknowledge your merits with admiration… and a touch of envy.\n\nWe Sentinels will see to exterminating the rest."}
Q[1660075]={d="<看着她，你确信即便泰达希尔本身轰然燃起熊熊烈火，阿莱娜也不会皱一下眉头。>\n\n<也许她有什么值得分享的东西。>",dEN="<Gazing at her, you're certain that Teldrassil itself could go up in roaring flame and Alenna would not be moved.>\n\n<Perhaps she has something to share.>",o="远离喧嚣与匆忙，稍作休息，听阿莱娜·语枝说上一会儿。",oEN="Take a moment from the noise and haste and stay a while to listen to Alenna Whisperbough.",c="<阿莱娜的目光黯淡下来。看来多兰纳尔的美景，也不足以驱散那个教团之名所唤起的恐惧。>",cEN="<Alenna’s gaze darkens. It seems the beauty of Dolanaar isn’t enough to chase off the dread conjured by that cult’s name.>"}
Q[1660076]={d="<El enano te saluda desde lejos para llamar tu atención; primero con grandes movimientos de brazos, luego empieza a dar saltitos en el sitio.>\n\n幸会！我看到你收拾了格罗尔达。我猜你在安威玛尔不会待太久……\n\n如果是这样，而你的脚又把你带向卡兰诺斯，我有一封信得送到。\n\n去旅店找艾玛，告诉她安威玛尔那边的商谈有了成果。他们要一车我们最好的啤酒；如果这能说动他们，我们就有长期主顾了。先祖在向我们微笑，<class>！",dEN="<The dwarf waves from afar to catch your eye; big sweeping arms at first, then he starts hopping in place.>\n\nWell met! I saw how you handled Groldha. I'm guessing you won't be lingering in Anvilmar much longer...\n\nIf that's the case and your feet carry you to Kharanos, I've a message that needs delivering.\n\nFind Eyma at the inn and tell her the talks in Anvilmar bore fruit. They want a shipment of our best ale; if it wins them over, we've got ourselves regular buyers. The ancestors smile on us, <class>!",o="在卡兰诺斯的雷酒酿酒厂与艾玛·雷酒交谈。",oEN="Speak with Eyma Thunderbrew at the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos.",c="<当你提到诺尔希和他要你送的口信时，那女矮人探究的眉头舒展开来。>\n\n是好消息，<她说，语气却没什么热情。>\n\n我会尽快安排那批货备好。",cEN="<The dwarf woman’s inquisitive brow softens when you mention Norhi and the message he asked you to deliver.>\n\nThat’s good news, <she says, without much enthusiasm.>\n\nI’ll see to it the shipment’s ready as soon as possible."}
Q[1660077]={d="诺尔希一定是在你身上看出了什么，才会把那个口信托付给你。\n\n既然你来了，也许你能搭把手。\n\n走出旅店往左看；你会看到酿酒厂的啤酒花田。一种特殊的啤酒花品种，用来酿全丹莫罗最好的啤酒。\n\n今天我们客人多得忙不过来。你介意去采些啤酒花给我吗？我知道这不是英雄该干的活。但它给钱，而且给得不少。",dEN="Nori must've seen something in you, to trust you with that message.\n\nSince you're here, maybe you can lend a hand.\n\nStep out of the inn and look left; you'll see the distillery's hop yard. Special strain of hops, for the finest brew in all Dun Morogh.\n\nWe're swamped today with customers. Would you mind picking hops and bringing them back to me? Hardly hero's work, I know. But it pays, and it pays well.",o="在卡兰诺斯雷酒酿酒厂的土地上采收七份雷酒啤酒花。",oEN="Harvest seven Thunderbrew Hops from the Thunderbrew Distillery grounds in Kharanos.",p="你有兴趣吗？",pEN="Got the hops?",c="嗯……<艾玛深吸你采来的啤酒花的香气；闭上了眼睛。\n\n醉人。\n\n希望那些野兽没给你添太多麻烦。照这样下去，我得雇个人来巡逻这片地了。",cEN="Hm… <Eyma inhales the aroma of the hops you gathered; her eyes flutter shut.>\n\nIntoxicating.\n\nI hope the wildlife didn’t give you too much grief. At this rate I’ll have to hire someone to patrol the grounds."}
Q[1660078]={d="小心！那条隧道已经好几天没法通行了。\n\n我的发明，我亲手打造的自动机械<他把双手在你面前挥舞，姿态滑稽多过悲惨>，背叛了我。它们反过来对付我了！\n\n现在它们攻击任何靠近的东西。它们已经害死了一条命，更糟的是，它们毁了我的名声！\n\n别进那条隧道，除非……<los ojos del gnomo adquieren un brillo oportunista>\n\n现在仔细看你，你不像其他人。也许你能从它们手里活下来。毁掉它们……对！进去，把它们拆了，把零件带给我。",dEN="Careful! The tunnel's been impassable for a few days now.\n\nMy inventions, the automata I built with these very hands <he shakes them in your face, more comic than tragic>, have betrayed me. They've turned on me!\n\nNow they attack anything that wanders close. They've already claimed a life and, worse yet, they've wrecked my reputation!\n\nDon't go into that tunnel unless... <the gnome's eyes take on an opportunistic glint>.\n\nYou're not like the others, now that I look at you. You might just survive them. Destroy them... That's it! Go in there, take them apart, and bring me their parts.",o="击败堵塞卡兰诺斯隧道的失控自动机械，并从它们的残骸中回收可重复使用的机械零件。",oEN="Defeat Out-of-Control Automata clogging the Kharanos tunnel and recover Reusable Mechanical Parts from their remains.",p="那边情况怎么样？",pEN="How are things in there?",c="你活下来了！\n\n还救回了不少零件。\n\n<伊科拉斯咳了一声，挥手驱散从洞口飘出的细细烟柱，动作透着不安。>\n\n有了这些，再去酿酒厂灌几杯烈酒，我想我就能找回灵感（和胆量），投入下一个项目：第二代自动机械，比第一批更强壮、更听话。\n\n谢谢你！",cEN="You survived!\n\nAnd you salvaged no small number of parts.\n\n<Ikoras coughs and bats away the thin plume of smoke puffing from the cave mouth, fidgeting as he does.>\n\nWith these, and a couple of stiff drinks at the distillery, I think I’ll recover the inspiration (and the nerve) to plunge into my next project: a second generation of automata, stronger and more obedient than the first batch.\n\nThanks!"}
Q[1660079]={d="<那矮人把一支火枪夹在膝间，用通条捅进枪管；一推、一转、一拔，直到污垢松动飞了出去。>\n\n抱歉，我没注意到有观众。\n\n想打几发吗？靶子总是渴望着铅弹；运气好的话，我们能引来哪位买家。\n\n这么多弹药可不会自己卖出去。",dEN="<The dwarf braces a blunderbuss between his knees and runs a rod down the barrel; push, twist, pull, until the grime comes loose and spatters out.>\n\nSorry, didn't notice I had an audience.\n\nFancy putting a few rounds downrange? Targets are always hungry for lead; with luck, we'll catch a buyer's eye.\n\nAll this ammunition isn't going to sell itself.",o="在卡兰诺斯上方山脊的练习靶场上试射戈纳恩的火枪和弹药。",oEN="Test Gornarn's Blunderbuss and ammo on the practice targets up on the ridge above Kharanos.",p="别担心靶子。尽管放开了打！",pEN="Don't worry about the target. Blast 'em good!",c="以我母亲的胡子起誓！那可真是一场好戏！\n\n你亲眼看到了，是吧？我只卖最好的装备。\n\n帮我个忙，替我宣传宣传，好吗？干这行，口碑胜过一切。",cEN="By my mother’s beard! Now that was a show!\n\nYou saw it with your own eyes, eh? I sell only the finest kit.\n\nDo me a favor and spread the word, will you? In this line of work, nothing beats word of mouth."}
Q[1660080]={d="掘墓人疲惫的眼神诉说着漫长的一天与铁锹为伴。那墓窟让你印象深刻的不是它的深度，而是四壁泥土干净光洁的收尾。\n<La mirada de cansancio del sepulturero habla de un largo día con la pala. El foso no te impresiona tanto por su profundidad como por el acabado limpio y pulido de sus paredes de tierra>\n<Tal vez tenga algo que valga la pena compartir>",dEN="<The gravedigger's weary look tells of a long day at the shovel. The pit impresses you not so much by its depth as by the clean, polished finish of its earthen walls.>\n\n<Perhaps he has something worth sharing.>",o="远离喧嚣与匆忙，稍作休息，听掘墓人诺努伊德说上一会儿。",oEN="Take a moment from the noise and haste and stay a while to listen to Gravedigger Nonuid.",c="谨慎选择你的敌人，<class>。\n\n许多矮人路过卡兰诺斯时都想铸就一段传奇……最后却落进了这些壁龛中的一个。",cEN="Choose your enemies with care, <class>.\n\nPlenty of dwarves pass through Kharanos eager to forge a legend… only to end up dropped into one of these niches."}
Q[1660081]={d="我没什么好忏悔的。你为什么还打我？我没什么好忏悔的，我发誓……！\n\n<又一声痛苦的尖叫，接着是长久的沉默。终于，他似乎察觉到了你的存在。>\n\n那个忏悔者。杀了他！我受不了了……他是个拷问者。一个杀人犯。一个比他手下那些生物更可怕的怪物。\n\n让我们安息吧。除掉他。",dEN="I have nothing to confess. Why do you keep beating me? I have nothing to confess, I swear...!\n\n<Another agonized scream, followed by a long silence. At last, he seems to register your presence.>\n\nThe Confessor. Kill him! I can't take any more... He's a torturer. A murderer. A monster worse than the creatures at his mercy.\n\nGive us peace. Get rid of him.",o="在普通难度下杀死审判忏悔者康拉德。",oEN="Slay Inquisitorial Confessor Konrad on Normal difficulty.",p="<一声痛苦的叹息，是那可怜幽灵幽灵般的唇间唯一逸出的声音。>",pEN="<An agonized sigh is the only sound to leave the poor ghost’s spectral lips.>",c="死了？而且……你说我也死了？\n\n可是……不。这一定是个玩笑。又一个为折磨我们而设的把戏。\n\n你怎么能说你杀了他……可我仍能听见他的叫喊，仍能感觉到他的殴打？\n\n<那幽灵嗥叫到声嘶力竭，随后在一线微弱的气力中迟疑：>\n\n为什么我逃不出这折磨？",cEN="Dead? And… you say I am, too?\n\nBut… no. This must be a joke. Another trick devised to torture us.\n\nHow can you say you killed him… if I can still hear his screams and feel his blows?\n\n<The ghost howls until his voice is spent, then wavers in a thread of strength:>\n\nWhy can’t I escape this torment?"}
Q[1660082]={d="求求你。求求你……\n\n<那幽灵呻吟着，牙缝间喃喃自语，迷失在它被教会囚禁那段时间的回忆里。>\n\n<你意识到这地方受了诅咒。而如今徘徊于此的幽灵——囚徒与狱卒都一样——已经被困在这里太久了。>\n\n够了。够了。够了……\n\n<净化这座地牢，让每一个在其走廊中游荡的生物——不论是否幽灵——都得到安息，将是一种仁慈之举。>",dEN="Please. Please...\n\n<The ghost moans and mumbles under his breath, lost in memories of the time he was captive of the Church.>\n\n<This place, you realize, is cursed. And the ghosts who haunt it now—prisoners and jailers alike—have been trapped here far too long.>\n\nEnough. Enough. Enough...\n\n<It would be an act of mercy to purge the dungeon and lay to rest every creature, ghost or not, that wanders its halls.>",o="在普通难度下杀死盘踞审判大厅的亡灵。",oEN="Slay the undead that dwell within the Vaults of Inquisition on Normal difficulty.",p="<一声痛苦的叹息，是那可怜幽灵幽灵般的唇间唯一逸出的声音。>",pEN="<An agonized sigh is the only sound to leave the poor ghost’s spectral lips.>",c="为什么？\n\n<那幽灵呻吟着，仿佛仍在挨打。尽管审判地窟如今一片寂静，它的痛苦并未因你的离去而减轻；恰恰相反。>\n\n沉沦了。我们下面有数百人，像牲口一样挤作一团。我们做错了什么，要遭这样的罪？\n\n哦，母亲……",cEN="Why?\n\n<The ghost whimpers, as if he were still being beaten. Despite the hush now filling the inquisitorial dungeon, his agony has not lessened in your absence—if anything, the opposite.>\n\nHundreds. There are hundreds of us down here, packed like stable animals. What have we done to deserve this?\n\nOh, Mother…"}
Q[1660083]={d="那三个无礼之徒比我们想的更狡猾。\n\n我的主人邦桑迪憎恨亡灵，正因如此，他们派了一个去看守他那头奇美拉幼体。\n\n沃尔辛是他的名字；一个血巨魔，他们口中的嗜血狂战士。\n\n我的魔精对付这种东西毫无用处。放倒他，我会给你应得的报酬。",dEN="Da Upstart Three were craftier than we thought.\n\nMy master Bwonsamdi be hatin' da undead, and for dat very reason dey set one to guard their chimeric whelp.\n\nVol'zeen be his name; a dire troll, a blood-mad berserker, as dey be callin' him.\n\nMe mojo be worthless against a t'ing like dat. Bring it down, and I'll see ya paid in kind.",o="在普通难度下击败可怕的亡灵巨魔沃尔辛。",oEN="Defeat Vol'zeen, the dire undead troll on Normal difficulty.",p="<那巨魔闭着双眼，用长着利爪的细长手指描画着怪异的符文与图样。他似乎沉浸在某种黑暗仪式中。>",pEN="<The troll keeps his eyes closed as he traces strange glyphs and patterns with long, taloned fingers. He seems absorbed in some dark ritual.>",c="啊，那野兽倒下了！我能感觉到。又少了一个异类。\n\n你在这中间地带干得值得称道。我很满意，我的主人也是。\n\n现在我的工作开始了……把这烂摊子收拾干净，把地毯抖一抖。",cEN="Ah, da beast be fallen! I can feel it. One less aberration.\n\nYa done commendable work in dis in-between place. I be satisfied, and so be my master.\n\nNow my work begins… clean dis mess and shake out da mat."}
Q[1660084]={d="尽管希尔苏塔的仪式被毁了，她试图从血肉世界召唤出的那个生物仍强行把自己的一部分挤进了这片中间地带。\n\n那是一头畸形的奇美拉。若真有憎恶之物，它便是。\n\n希尔雷克、丹巴拉和沙德拉污染了这条通往彼界的道路。不知怎的，我相信它的性命与游荡在这些洞穴中的蜘蛛、蛇和蝙蝠之灵系于一处。\n\n把它们全部杀掉。\n\n我的主人邦桑迪会慷慨相报。",dEN="Though Hirsutta's ritual was spoiled, da creature she tried to call from da world o' flesh managed to force a part o' itself into dis in-between.\n\nIt be a monstrous chimera. An abomination if ever there was.\n\nHir'eek, Dambala, and Shadra infested dis path to da Other Side. Somehow, I be thinkin' its life be tied to da spirits of spider, serpent, and bat wanderin' dese caverns.\n\nSlay dem all.\n\nMy lord Bwonsamdi will be generous.",o="在普通难度下击败通往彼界之路上的蝙蝠、蜘蛛和嘶鸣者。",oEN="Defeat the bats, spiders, and hissers on the Road to De Other Side on Normal difficulty.",p="<那巨魔闭着双眼，用长着利爪的细长手指描画着怪异的符文与图样。他似乎沉浸在某种黑暗仪式中。>",pEN="<The troll keeps his eyes closed as he traces strange glyphs and patterns with long, taloned fingers. He seems absorbed in some dark ritual.>",c="阴暗三神系会久久记住这次失败——这份屈辱。\n\n你做得很好，把它们的子嗣之灵送回了它们父辈那里。",cEN="Da Sinister Three be rememberin’ dis defeat for a long time—dis humiliation.\n\nYa did good, sendin’ da spirits of their brood back to their parents."}
Q[1660085]={d="当你思量我们的提议时，记住：大秃鹫奖赏那些把食物带回巢中的人。如此，埃莉德娜生前曾拥有的物品，如今在她被夺走一切的那个人手中找到了新主人。\n\n<那精灵锋利的手——更像秃鹫的爪子而非她族人的手——握住你的手，把一枚华丽的项坠放进你掌心。>\n\n埃莉德娜的遗物之一。她的项坠。你想怎么处置都行。",dEN="As you ponder our offer, remember that the Great Vulture rewards those who bring food to the nest. Thus, the possessions that once belonged to Elydna in life now find a new owner in the one who took hers away.\n\n<The elf's sharp hands, more like a vulture's talons than those of her kin, grasp yours and place an ornate pendant in your palms.>\n\nOne of Elydna's belongings. Her pendant. Do with it as you will.",o="与萨里尔·翼击交谈，把他姐姐埃莉德娜的项坠交给他。",oEN="Speak with Thariel Wingstroke and deliver to him the pendant of his sister, Elydna.",p="<那精灵的目光游移不定，蒙着忧虑的阴云。>",pEN="<The elf's eyes wander, clouded with worry.>",c="<你摊开手，露出埃莉德娜的项坠。看到它，萨里尔痛苦的表情稍稍缓和。>\n\n我想……既然连凭吊的遗体都没有，这个也只能凑合了。\n\n<他用颤抖的双手接过项坠，按在胸口。>\n\n埃莉德娜……究竟是什么疯病让你加入了那些堕落之徒？",cEN="<You open your hand, revealing Elydna's pendant. At the sight of it, Thariel's grief-stricken expression eases ever so slightly.>\n\nI suppose... in the absence of a body to mourn, this will have to do.\n\n<He takes the pendant with trembling hands and presses it to his chest.>\n\nElydna... what madness drove you to join those degenerates?"}
Q[1660086]={d="出事了，出大事了！糟糕透顶！\n\n<疯癫的克拉拉神经质地绞着自己湿漉漉的双手。>\n\n门又开了。封印破了。会不会是我的姐妹们？不可能。我不会再回北郡了。绝不！\n\n<疯癫的克拉拉的目光刺穿你，狂野、狂热。>\n\n你去做！让那声音闭嘴！我把我的那点东西都给你！他们撒谎：说什么「圣光会保护我们」。哈！现在他们都死了。全都死了！除了她。除了她！\n\n<克拉拉自顾自地笑了，随后目光涣散地望向虚空。>",dEN="Something's wrong, wrong! Terribly wrong!\n\n<Clara the Mad wrings her clammy hands in a nervous frenzy.>\n\nThe door has opened again. The seal is broken. Could it have been my sisters? Impossible. I'm not going back to Northshire. No!\n\n<Clara the Mad's gaze pierces through you, wild, feverish.>\n\nYou do it! Silence the Voice! I’ll give you what little I have! They lied: “The Light will protect us,” they said. Ha! Now they're all dead. All of them! Except her. All but her!\n\n<Clara laughs to herself before her eyes drift into the void.>",o="在普通难度下深入审判宝库，击败欺诈者的化身。",oEN="Venture into the Vaults of Inquisition and defeat the Presence of the Deceiver on Normal difficulty.",p="<疯癫的克拉拉双手捂住耳朵。她睁得极大、一眨不眨的眼睛死死盯着你。>",pEN="<Clara the Mad covers her ears with both hands. Her eyes, wide and unblinking, fix upon you.>",c="你……让她的声音沉默了……\n\n<克拉拉爆发出一阵狂笑。>\n\n当然！真正的威胁是你。就是你！\n\n走开。我不想你靠近我。滚！拿着这个，别靠近我！",cEN="You've... silenced her voice...\n\n<Clara bursts into manic laughter.>\n\nOf course! The real threat is you. It's you!\n\nGo. I don’t want you near me—out! Take this and stay away from me!"}
Q[1660087]={d="<尽管老人的双眼依旧闭着，他额头上的沟壑却流露出连灵魂也无法掩藏的忧虑。>\n\n女巫希尔苏塔的回声仍在世界的帷幕间震颤。她栖居于一处夹缝位面，生者与亡者在那里融为一体。无论她在编织什么，她的巫毒之力并未随死亡而消退。\n\n这片土地上有一道敞开的伤口，一道通往彼界的裂隙。那道门槛必定藏在试炼谷的阴暗巢穴之中——希尔苏塔的名字最后一次被念出的地方。\n\n阻止她正在召唤的一切……趁她的腐化尚未吞噬那层仍守护着我们现实的脆弱界限。",dEN="<Though the old man's eyes remain closed, the furrow in his brow reveals a worry even the spirits cannot hide.>\n\nThe echo of Hirsutta, the Witch, still trembles between the veils of the world. She dwells in an interstitial plane, where the living and the dead blur into one. Whatever she is weaving, her voodoo power has not waned with death.\n\nThere is an open wound upon this land, a rift leading to the Other Side. That threshold must lie hidden within the Sinister Lair, in the Valley of Trials, where the name Hirsutta was last spoken.\n\nStop whatever she is conjuring... before her corruption devours the fragile boundary that still shields our reality.",o="深入通往彼界之路，在普通难度下击败奇美拉胚胎。",oEN="Venture into the Road to De Other Side and defeat the Chimeric Embryo on Normal difficulty.",p="你找到通往彼界的门了吗？",pEN="Have you managed to find the gateway to the Other Side?",c="<老兽人仍保持着你离开时的姿势，但他此刻的存在散发着宁静与平和。>\n\n希尔苏塔的回声已永远沉寂。\n\n然而你的功绩，将回响在剃刀岭的城墙之外，回响在灵魂铭记勇者之地。\n\n谢谢你。",cEN="<The old orc remains in the same position you left him, but now his presence radiates serenity and peace.>\n\nThe echo of Hirsutta has fallen silent forever.\n\nYour deeds, however, will echo beyond the walls of Razor Hill, in the place where the spirits keep the memory of the brave.\n\nThank you."}
Q[1660088]={d="出事了，出大事了！糟糕透顶！\n\n<疯癫的克拉拉神经质地绞着自己湿漉漉的双手。>\n\n门又开了。封印破了。会不会是我的姐妹们？不可能。我不会再回北郡了。绝不！\n\n<疯癫的克拉拉的目光刺穿你，狂野、狂热。>\n\n你去做！让那声音闭嘴！我把我的那点东西都给你！他们撒谎：说什么「圣光会保护我们」。哈！现在他们都死了。全都死了！除了她。除了她！\n\n<克拉拉自顾自地笑了，随后目光涣散地望向虚空。>",dEN="Something's wrong, wrong! Terribly wrong!\n\n<Clara the Mad wrings her clammy hands in a nervous frenzy.>\n\nThe door has opened again. The seal is broken. Could it have been my sisters? Impossible. I'm not going back to Northshire. No!\n\n<Clara the Mad's gaze pierces through you, wild, feverish.>\n\nYou do it! Silence the Voice! I’ll give you what little I have! They lied: “The Light will protect us,” they said. Ha! Now they're all dead. All of them! Except her. All but her!\n\n<Clara laughs to herself before her eyes drift into the void.>",o="集结一支完整的五人冒险小队，深入危险的审判大厅，在普通难度下击败欺诈者的化身。",oEN="Assemble a full party of five adventurers, descend into the perilous Vaults of Inquisition, and defeat the Presence of the Deceiver on Normal difficulty.",p="<疯癫的克拉拉双手捂住耳朵。她睁得极大、一眨不眨的眼睛死死盯着你。>",pEN="<Clara the Mad covers her ears with both hands. Her eyes, wide and unblinking, fix upon you.>",c="你……让她的声音沉默了……\n\n<克拉拉爆发出一阵狂笑。>\n\n当然！真正的威胁是你。就是你！\n\n走开。我不想你靠近我。滚！拿着这个，别靠近我！",cEN="You’ve... silenced her voice...\n\n<Clara bursts into manic laughter.>\n\nOf course! The real threat is you. It’s you!\n\nGo. I don’t want you near me—out! Take this and stay away from me!"}
Q[1660089]={d="<尽管老人的双眼依旧闭着，他额头上的沟壑却流露出连灵魂也无法掩藏的忧虑。>\n\n女巫希尔苏塔的回声仍在世界的帷幕间震颤。她栖居于一处夹缝位面，生者与亡者在那里融为一体。无论她在编织什么，她的巫毒之力并未随死亡而消退。\n\n这片土地上有一道敞开的伤口，一道通往彼界的裂隙。那道门槛必定藏在试炼谷的阴暗巢穴之中——希尔苏塔的名字最后一次被念出的地方。\n\n阻止她正在召唤的一切……趁她的腐化尚未吞噬那层仍守护着我们现实的脆弱界限。",dEN="<Though the old man's eyes remain closed, the furrow in his brow reveals a worry even the spirits cannot hide.>\n\nThe echo of Hirsutta, the Witch, still trembles between the veils of the world. She dwells in an interstitial plane, where the living and the dead blur into one. Whatever she is weaving, her voodoo power has not waned with death.\n\nThere is an open wound upon this land, a rift leading to the Other Side. That threshold must lie hidden within the Sinister Lair, in the Valley of Trials, where the name Hirsutta was last spoken.\n\nStop whatever she is conjuring... before her corruption devours the fragile boundary that still shields our reality.",o="集结一支完整的五人冒险小队，穿越凶险的通往彼界之路，在普通难度下击败奇美拉胚胎。",oEN="Assemble a full party of five adventurers, journey into the treacherous Road to De Other Side, and defeat the Chimeric Embryo on Normal difficulty.",p="你找到通往彼界的门了吗？",pEN="Have you managed to find the gateway to the Other Side?",c="<老兽人仍保持着你离开时的姿势，但他此刻的存在散发着宁静与平和。>\n\n希尔苏塔的回声已永远沉寂。\n\n然而你的功绩，将回响在高岩的城墙之外，回响在灵魂铭记勇者之地。\n\n谢谢你。",cEN="<The old orc remains in the same position you left him, but now his presence radiates serenity and peace.>\n\nThe echo of Hirsutta has fallen silent forever.\n\nYour deeds, however, will echo beyond the walls of Highrock, in the place where the spirits keep the memory of the brave.\n\nThank you."}
